INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(75,'02/16/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I tried to dispute due to the fact I have never lived in any other state besides California, yet, on my credit report shows an account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of Georgia. I can prove through utility bills and rental lease that I was not in Georgia at the time of said account was being used in my name. The company did nothing to further investigate my claim, but decided it was an accurate account.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',8.0,8.0,'a credit report shows an account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of Georgia. the company did nothing to further investigate my claim.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(76,'02/16/2019','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','An outside source hacked my Wells Fargo business account and made two withdrawals as payroll deductions -- {$2000.00} & {$5000.00} -- one day apart. When I realized what had happened, I contacted the fraud department of the bank, explained that I hadn''t made these withdrawals -- I''m only a one person company and don''t have a payroll process in place ; I make a distribution from my company when I need it.

Within a day or so, the {$2000.00} withdrawal was returned -- the last withdrawal -- and when a week passed and I didn''t see the return of the {$5000.00}, I followed up with the bank ''s fraud department. I was informed that even though they were able to retrieve the last withdrawal they didn''t pursue attempting to retrieve the initial {$5000.00} because I didn''t inform them within a 24 hour period after the withdrawal that this has transpired. I was stunned to hear this since they realized this was fraud, knew the source of the funds, that they didn''t pursue because this transaction was outside of the 24 hour period. Some additional information -- Wells Fargo ''s entire system was down for a number of days when these transactions occurred, and this information wasn''t even available to me until Sunday -- the day I filed the claim. 

I subsequently filed a report with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] police of this fraud and how the bank responded to this. The officer taking the information was as confused as I why if the bank knew where the money was and that this was obviously a fraudulent transaction, that would not pursue getting the money back because it fell outside of their 24 hour policy. 

I was informed by the fraud department that they would record my disagreement with their resolution and respond within 120 days. I am semi-retired ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and have a very small [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] company and {$5000.00} is a great deal of money to me. Suffice it to say that while I don''t expect to hear back from them, that I wanted to record their actions to the appropriate organization for further review.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a source hacked my Wells Fargo business account and made two withdrawals as payroll deductions. the bank''s fraud department'' contacted the fraud department and said');
