INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(111,'02/08/2019','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','I have a Visa with Capital One that had fraudulent charges on, which they took care of. They closed the account and issued a new card. When I received the new card, I put it in my safe and did not activate it. I started receiving phone calls from Capital One telling me that my account was delinquent on a card that I had not activated and had no previous balance. I looked online at the ''charges '' and the same fraudulent charges were being applied to my new, inactive card. Once again, Capital One reversed the charges, closed the account, and issued a new card. They also said that they would block any and all transactions from the companies that were charging my card with fraudulent charges. I received the new card and once again, it is being charged by those same companies for services I have never used nor authorized. Those companies are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I want to know how an account that has never been activated can have charges on it and how is my account information being shared? I am the only person with access to that card and have not given it to anyone. The fraud has to be initiating inside Capital One. I want answers. There is no reason those charges, which amounted to THOUSANDS of dollars should have ever been allowed on my account.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a Visa with capital One had fraudulent charges on a card that I had not activated. when I received the new card, I put it in my safe and did not activate it');
