INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(123,'02/06/2019','Debt collection','Medical debt','False statements or representation','The debt collection company, Commonwealth Financial Systems,  has managed to dupe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  into posting a very old collection amount ( opened [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- {$1000.00} ) as if it was just opened. For the last 3 years ive lived in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and they are NOW showing the account as " opened in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''''. This account was started in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would have had to have been in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for such an account to be valid. It''s already bad enough that consumers have to be treated as deliquent on debts that, if paid by an insurance company or medicaid, would have been discharged at 5 or 10 percent of the actual bill. Think of the money we lose while trying to build credit, because we are stuck with the option of credit cards and loans with huge percentage rates directly related to open accounts of little or no substanence. There is also a second similar account of {$340.00}, for which they did the exact same thing.','Commonwealth Financial Systems, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'debt collection company, Commonwealth Financial Systems, has duped debt collectors into posting a very old collection amount. the account was started in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
