INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(142,'02/01/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','These issues are with 2 of the 3 major credit reporting agencies [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and Experian. Each month for the past 18 months I have disputed 3 medical collection accounts on my credit reports. I have asked them to verify that these are in fact my accounts which are not. I keep getting a generic electronic statement stating the accounts have been verified. But by what means? I have requested to know who they spoke to, producing any signatures of mine, as well as any contracts, as well as what these medical charges are for. It has been very frustrating for me in the fact that these are the only derogatory items on my reports. Previously upon request, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  removed them from my report. I have had no success with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and Experian. The collection agency is : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  The amounts are : {$1500.00} {$1000.00} {$1300.00} I can produce correspondence if needed as I currently don''t have the ability to upload documents. Any assistance regarding this would be appreciated as I would like to apply for a home mortgage in the next 90 days. Thank you.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a total of 3 medical collection accounts have been disputed each month. the accounts are not my accounts. the collection agency is : [COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(143,'02/01/2019','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Trouble using your card','On XX/XX/2019, I paid {$1600.00} on my card ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That was OVER half of the balance due. In a effort to decrease my debt to income ratio. I was shocked when on XX/XX/2019, I saw on my credit report that my credit limit was decreased {$1500.00}! To be clear, the credit limit decrease hit my credit report BEFORE the debt decrease has even hit my credit report. But that''s not even the issue, I want my credit limit raised back to what it was. Clearly, I have the means to pay ( and has always paid ) and I feel betrayed by Synchrony that I can pay you all a lump sum and you all would decrease my limit in the same month so now I am back to where I started, with a high balance card with only {$46.00} to spend. If this complaint does not lead to my limit increased, I will simply cancel not only this card that I have with Synchrony but I will also cancel ALL of the cards I have with Synchrony ( I have at least 3, which I use all of the time ). I''m FED up and feel as if I wasted {$1600.00} and also my hard work has been wasted as well. If I knew I would have ended up with a high balance card anyways, I would have just paid the minimum balance and used that {$1600.00} to pay off other cards/bills.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'on XX/XX/2019, I paid $1600.00 on my card ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was OVER half of');
