[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is the master servicer of my VA loan','Dovenmuehle Mortgage, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a veteran of my mortgage in XX/XX/2018, I have missed the payments. I have repeatedly attempted faxed and/or emailed my documents to');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(162,'01/28/2019','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','To Whom It May Concern : My complaint is against this mortgage company : MB Financial, mbmortgage.com,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] acct. # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Beginning in 2019 I decided to pay off my mortgage within 5 years. I have a 15 year loan, have paid on it 5 years and I have 10 mores year before I pay it in full. Beginning the month I paid {$2500.00} towards my principal along with my monthly mortgage payment of {$3000.00}. Thus, for the next 5 years I will be paying {$5500.00} each month in order to complete paying off my mortgage in 5 years.

I went to the MB Financial website and made the arrangements described above. 

A problem developed when I looked at my bank records and noticed that MB Financial took out the {$5500.00} from my account and also accepted my Bill Pay check of {$3000.00} that I had been making to them for the previous 5 years. I promptly called their office and explained the situation. They stated that I should have stopped payment on my automatic payment of {$3000.00} as their " system '''' could not withdraw just the additional {$2500.00} I had stipulated. I told them I understood their explanation, however I explained to them that I had only authorized them to pull out {$2500.00} from my checking account. Their website did not make clear that they would be taking out the {$2500.00} I authorized plus the normal {$3000.00} mortgage payment. 

So to resolve the issue I asked them to wire back the extra {$3000.00} they had withdraw, without my authorization. They said they could not, but that they would send me a check sometime soon. Today is XX/XX/XXXXand they still have not refunded me the extra payment. My first call to them was on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have made 7 calls so far and still do not have the {$3000.00} they pulled out without my consent. Today, I called to speak to the supervisor, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I have yet to get a call back from him. 

This " bank '''' has pulled out money from my checking account without my approval. In addition, they have not had the decency to refund me the money. I request your assistance in getting they to resolve the issue. 

Thank you for your help.','MB FINANCIAL, INC.',2.0,2.0,'MB Financial, mbmortgage.com, has a 15 year loan, paid on it 5 years. a problem developed when I looked at my bank records');
