INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(207,'01/16/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I noticed 3 inaccurate accounts on my Equifax credit profile that you maintain under my social security number, therefore this may be a result of identity theft. 
This is a violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act Section 1681b ( c ) and serious breach of my privacy rights per FCRA 604 ( A ) ( 3 ), and FCRA section 605B, which details your responsibility to block fraudulent information on my credit report that may have resulted from identity theft. I have filed my FTC and 605 B affidavit. 

( My notarized drivers license for identification and proof of residency is enclosed ). 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Incorrect High Balance Reporting/ Incomplete Account # Reporting Invalid information reporting by furnisher. The Fair Credit Reporting Act 609 ( c ) ( 4 ) requires the furnisher of this information to provide the date and amount of any checks which is based on late payment history by me. Not reporting 100 % accurate information per FCRA section 609 ( a ) ( 1 ) and the FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 7 ) ( G ) ( i ) and permanently delete this from my credit file per FCRA 623 ( b ) ( 1 )  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XXXXAccount # Please update this account to show {$0.00} balance " paid in full '''' this account does not have a {$5700.00} limit, it is paid off [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Incomplete Account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reporting and Incorrect high balance reporting NOT comply with FCRA 609 ( a ) ( 1 ) by not reporting the entire account and accurate account number, this is not reporting 100 % accurate information. Inaccurate account not in compliance with FCRA Section 623 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( C ) permanently delete this from my credit file per FCRA 623 ( b ) ( 1 )','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act Section 1681b ( c) and FCRA section 605B. this is a serious breach of my privacy rights.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(208,'01/16/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','While checking my small business credit score I noticed that there are two accounts on the report apparently grading my business credit score an F. They also have a business credit score of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as a high risk account. I have no knowledge of these accounts nor is the address of my business correct. The credit bureaus are using my home address but the account is still fraudulent and I would like this information removed. I have not had any business credit until XX/XX/2019 from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in which I could provide proof. The account is a Printing and Publishing account that is over 6 months old and has nothing to do with my business. I would like the credit bureau to provide me with a contract or written proof of some sort that this is my account. Otherwise under the Fair Credit Reporting Act I would like this account removed immediately. I am also sending this complaint to the credit bureau as well. This information is affecting how fast I build my business credit which is now a major focus of my company.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'account is a Printing and Publishing account that is over 6 months old. the account is a high risk account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(209,'01/16/2019','Debt collection','I do not know','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','I received several harassing phone calls from Collection Agencies representing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   indicating that owed {$470.00} for a debt dating back to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The first Collection Agency identified themselves as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Illinois, Representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she provided an address of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Illinois. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That called was initiated on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I informed her at that time, that I did not have an account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   much less owed them anything. 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received yet another phone call from CBE Group indicating that they were representing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in an attempt to collect a debt. They had my former name and asked for my social security number. That call was generated by phone number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and the caller refused to identify herself. She however, informed me that the telephone calls will continue until they I paid what is owed. I am a senior citizens with health conditions and find this abusive. I spoke to an Attorney who informed me that this is some type of Zombie Debt method that is used to force payment. I was also advised by the attorney that oftentimes these companies will show a payment received with a current date to continue their level of harassment and to circumvent the law. My concern is that this is not a debt that I owe and it is well over 28 years! In addition, I have learned through my research that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is defunct. I requested that they put it in writing and to date have received nothing from either collection agency.','The CBE Group, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a collection agency called me to collect a debt dating back to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. she called me to collect');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(210,'01/15/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','On XX/XX/2018, I noticed there is a Bankruptcy Dismissed on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit report. On XX/XX/18, I sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a certified letter which was received by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and signed for on XX/XX/18, asking [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to validate this reporting. On XX/XX/2018, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] replied that this reporting Bankruptcy was " obtained from local, state and federal courts though a third party vendor LexisNexis ''''. I have a copy of my LexisNexis report being frozen, and also a letter from the United States Bankruptcy Court stating that the United States Bankruptcy Court does not transmit or initiate conveyance of data to the credit reporting agencies. This letter further states, " The Court does not report bankruptcies to the credit bureaus and does not get involved in disputes regarding credit reports. Per the FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 5 ) : If the Credit Bureau can not validate the information with the Original Creditor, they must remove said information from the consumers credit file. By  stating [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] verified this information with a third party vendor is a direct violation of FCRA 623 ( a ) ( 5 ) and/or FCRA 609 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( a ).','LEXISNEXIS',2.0,4.0,'a bankruptcy dismissed on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit report. on XX/XX/18, [COMP');
