I have informed them that I came back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and as a proof I have sent them my statement from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account. In that statement they could see that I made a cash withdrawal with my ID with bank casher on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. And made some other deposits to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Please see attached document [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 

Wells Fargo opened simple claim by number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for total loss of {$9000.00}. On a first days of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they denied my claim by mentioning that they are denning my claim because I have logged in at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and there were no future transactions after my call to them! I explained them one more time that I have been at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] airport not in the city! And could not logged in because of bad internet connection and it not my fault that thief did not used my card after my call! 

After I decided to open a claim with Executive office of Wells Fargo. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have received letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Please see attached document [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) saying that they are denying my claim, saying that card was used by my me or somebody else that I have authorized! 
