I appreciate your prompt attention to this matter and await your reply. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Last four digits of SSN [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a consumer financial protection bureau has a history of grand theft. a consumer financial protection bureau has a history of theft. a consumer financial protection bureau has a history');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(253,'01/05/2019','Credit card or prepaid card','Government benefit card','Problem getting a card or closing an account','Someone had my social Security number and personal information. They are calling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and changing the address and phone number to Florida and requesting new cards in my name. I have called 15 times this week to keep changing it back. I went to social security office and reported it. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   acknowledged knowing about the breach in my account and will not stop it. They keep allowing this to happen. I have yet to receive my income. I can not pay bills, I have no phone and I have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] young children at home to feed. This is unacceptable!','Comerica',2.0,2.0,'a person had my social security number and personal information. they are calling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and changing the address and phone number to Florida. they');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(254,'01/05/2019','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Had storm claim at my home in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Checks from insurance company came in my name and Ditech ''s name ( Ditech is my mortgage company ). From the beginning, I would be given different information on the process to release the funds to fix my house each time I called. My contractor has witnessed all the phone calls with me after the first two calls for this reason. They never gave me anything in writing telling me the process but instead gave me different info each time I called. We are now over 80 % done, but they have only paid out about half of the money. It has drug on so long that things are getting tough. Contractor has fronted a lot of money for the job, and hasn''t gotten paid in the way Ditech told us they would. If she didn''t have the funds she had to spend, we would both have been in trouble. They sent a third party inspector to the house on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who told me he was reporting that well over 75 % was complete and that Ditech would send 75 % of the money. We called a few days later and they had only sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the mail ( which we had been told they would overnight it free of charge since there had been a " misunderstanding '''' because they would usually charge [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to overnight it and take it out of the claim money? ) The misunderstanding they refer to is basically anything we have been told any time we called them to get the money released. From the beginning Ditech told us they would release so much up front, then when a certain amount of work was completed we were to send in invoices showing what was purchased and done and they would disperse more funds several times and hold only 10 % in the end to be released when we scheduled an inspection to show it was at least 90 % complete. My contractor overnighted invoices, etc., to them over a month ago. We called them 2 weeks after and were told they had everything they needed and a check would be sent when it was processed, probably in the next week. After another week we called and were told a 50 % inspection would need to be done? We called the next day and were told a check would be cut in a couple of days, so we asked for a supervisor, and supervisor said they were mistaken, that they had all the documentation they needed and we needed a 50 % inspection to be done in order to release more funds to show it was at least 50 % complete? Inspector came on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and told us an inspection was to be done at 25, 50, 75, and 90 % to release funds and asked if Ditech told me that? I flipped out. He said not to worry, that he would show we were well beyond 75 % complete, and that would release 75 % of the funds, then when we called for 90 % inspection, it would release the rest. So we called couple of days later and were told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was sent in mail and they were holding the rest until 90 % inspection was done? Is there anything you can do to help us? There has to be a law against a company doing business in this way. Our county was declared in a state of emergency when this happened, but I didn''t know to sign up with FEMA because I had insurance. FEMA would have made them release the funds. I had to have a new roof, siding, windows, ceilings, walls, flooring, cabinets, stove, and I do not have countertops, kitchen sink or stove at this point. Please help us.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'contractor has fronted a lot of money for the job, and hasn''t paid out half of the money. a third party inspector sent to the house on X');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(255,'01/05/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','CFPB please investigate the reporting practices of Equifax and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] enclosed are News letter s showing cases against Equifax for misuse of reporting I have been stating that they are playing games and stalling please use my information to do this investigation enclosed I want to show a pattern of how they refuse to comply with the law and make up there own manipuliating consumer credit reports','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'CFPB please investigate the reporting practices of Equifax and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] enclosed are News letter s showing cases against Equifax for misuse of reporting ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(256,'01/04/2019','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','Inquiry [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a promotional offer to open a Citi Priority bank account and after 2 criterion had been met would receive [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Thank You points. I have a credit account with Citibank and the two requirements ( spending {$750.00} and setting up 2 months of autopay for a bill within 60 days ) seemed easy to meet so I decided to give it a try and move a small amount of funds to open an account. From day one there were problems -- first, my opening deposit received an error message online so I called in to make sure it wasn''t processed. The customer rep told me they were sure it had not been and that I could try again. When I made a second attempt that seemed to work, I shortly after ( the next day ) received a notice from my bank that there were 2 transactions initiated. I attempted to cancel one and somehow this disrupted Citibank ''s delicate and outdated system and caused my account to have a negative balance before I had even had it functioning for two days! I waited almost a week for this to be cleared up. I then changed an autopay of mine to come out of my new city account. At the end of the first month the bill came out and I had spent the {$750.00} required. I called customer service to confirm this and they told me that they could not confirm I had met the requirements but informed me that it was not as simple as setting up and auto pay " you have to add payees ''''. Let me point out very strongly this was NOT what the promotional card said. It did not explain the " setting up payees '''' is what is required to meet the autopay requirement. At this point I knew that Citibank would attempt not to award the Thank You points I had earned. I set up my aforementioned autopay as a " payee '''' and designated that {$100.00} be paid monthly -- this setup was done WELL within the two months. If conversations are recorded then Citibank has evidence of all this via my conversations with the customer service representative. I opened an inquiry about a week ago in my local branch regarding this and received a letter from Citibank dated XX/XX/28 stating that I did not meet their very cleverly vague " bill pay '''' requirements. I did meet these requirements even though I had to do my own digging and clarify the promotional card with the representative to do so. I insist on being awarded my Thank You points in entirety. I am extremely thankful I did not transfer more than a tiny amount of my funds and assets to Citibank ''s care, as I see they are very dishonest. I will make sure my dealings with their " promotions '''' are seen on social media and I will most definitely warn all of my acquaintances both business and otherwise of how I was scammed by Citibank.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'inquiry received a promotional offer to open a Citi Priority bank account. the customer rep told me that the transaction was not processed. the customer service representative told me that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(257,'01/04/2019','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','NAVIENT Courtesy Loan Forbearance due to Defense to Repayment investigation is not being applied. Navient continues to insist the Department of Education has not contacted Navient for a courtesy Forbearance although I have verified with the DoE and FSAO via FSA Borrower Defense Application : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Navient will not acknowledge this Borrower defense and continues to put me on extended holds ( 45+ minutes - 90 minutes ) then transfers again for no reason.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'NAVIENT Courtesy Loan Forbearance due to Defense to Repayment investigation is not being applied. Navient insists the Department of Education has not contacted Navient');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(258,'01/04/2019','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Applying for a mortgage or refinancing an existing mortgage','On XX/XX/2018 - I went to a local Suntrust branch to inquire about a XX/XX/2018 request from Suntrust Consumer Home Loan Specialist, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Ext [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The request stated that Suntrust was requesting a seperate signed page 2 of a Uniform Borrower Assistance Form packet. ( For Background : My husband and I were in the middle of a divorce, and he alone requested the mortgage modifications. I was opposed to them. ) I had been in contact with Suntrust multiple times over an approximate 9month period, continually notifying them that I was not in agreement with the modifications that my husband, who is a previous Suntrust EVP, was requesting. Since the UBAF did not have a place for a signature on Page 2, and since the UBAF packet is a 5 Page composite whole document, that  requires legal affirmations for the entire document to be sworn to, on page 5 of the document, I became suspicious about the odd request, especially with my husband having many friends and colleagues still employed there. The local branch representative filled out a complaint form for me concerning both my mortgage and HELOC loans. At [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Suntrust Manager with the Home Mortgage Retention group. I explained to her that I had been speaking with and e-mailing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over the past several months, notifying her that my home had not been damaged by Hurricane Irma, that my husband used the Hurricane as a way to intentionally default on the mortgage as a means to securing more favorable loan terms without it impacting his [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] since he is a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), and I was opposed to modifying the Mortgage which would add over 21k in a balloon payment to the end of the loan. I submitted a previous complaint ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) concerning this issue, however that complaint was directed towards the HELOC loan associated with the mortgage. This complaint is regarding the Mortgage which Suntrust modified in spite of the fraudulently modified signature page and in addition to my ongoing objections. My husband ''s document tampering can be clearly seen on the Suntrust Corrections agreement as well as the notarized signature page that I have attached. I have also attached proof showing that I had faxed Suntrust the original pages, long before they received and processed the fraudulently tampered documents. In spite of the fact that Suntrust had the original documents along with my objections, they continued processing the modification with the tampered documents which were very obviously altered, and even initialed by my now ex-husband. Suntrust also failed to report the illegal mortgage document tampering to authorities, leaving him to continue working in the financial industry without consequence, which places hundreds of unsuspecting clients at risk. It is disturbing that Suntrust not only refused to reverse this modification, they also have made every effort to protect their former EVP from being held responsible for knowingly engaging in financial fraud.','SUNTRUST BANKS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'suntrust requested a signed page 2 of a Uniform Borrower Assistance Form. the UBAF did not have a place for a signature on Page 2.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(259,'01/04/2019','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','this is in reference to my everyday card. i id not know so please dont say disclosures were sent that you would be travel fees. when i book a trip i dont want or need these. this is bogus. please reverse all and remove feature that allows the card to be billed when a trip is booked. what a joke. please dont tell me i was told what 20 years ago? never use d it for this so did not know please refund [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars of charges. asap i am not wasting my time calling i did not kow or authorize or need.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'i id not know so please dont say disclosures were sent that you would be travel fees. when i book a trip i dont want or need these. this');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(260,'01/03/2019','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I wrote a letter to Equifax asking them to verify two accounts on my credit report. The accounts in question were [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Their response to me was that they needed to verify my address before completing the request however in my original letter to them, I included a copy of my driver ''s license, SS Card and a recent utility bill that included my address. This address was also the address that was at the time and currently is on my credit report with Equifax. Their response included examples of items that I could send to verify my address including a Driver ''s License, Mortgage or Deed, rental lease, utility bill among numerous other examples. Again, these documents were included in my original letter to them. I called to follow up and explain that I had already sent the documents that they requested, but the agent on the phone filed an additional dispute which reset the 30 days that Equifax had to respond. This was not my request. I was only calling to ensure that Equifax received my original supporting documents. I later received an email detailing the results of my dispute. When I logged on, I read where the results were mailed to me. I called Equifax to see where the results were mailed and I was informed that they were mailed to a PREVIOUS address on my file and not the CURRENT address that was reporting on the file at that time. This is a stall tactic and it will not be tolerated. It is also a violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act. Not only did they not verify the accounts in question, they stalled the request by asking for additional verification which was already sent with the original letter and by sending the follow up to a previous address. 

Neither [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] nor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] were able verify the aforementioned accounts so they followed the standards and laws set forth by the Fair Credit Reporting Act and removed the accounts. They deserve recognition for their adherence to the FCRA and I am pleased with their thorough investigation and follow up. I, however, can not say the same for Equifax. They have already lost the trust of millions of consumers for their carelessness in the company Data Breach of XX/XX/XXXXand they are continuing to fail at thoroughly doing their job to accurately report consumer information.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts in question were. they asked for');
