INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(266,'01/02/2019','Mortgage','VA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','Ocwen mortgage company took over financing my house from GMAC. Immediately they claimed I hadn''t enough insurance. Next they were taken my insurance payments from my mortgage but didn''t pay the insurance that was due to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They claim they couldn''t reach them. They allowed my insurance to lapse by not paying [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] although they had collected the money with my mortgage payment. Next they were trying to strong arm me to accept another insurance company at a much higher rate. Once I found out they purposefully lapsed my insurance I inquired why they hadn''t simply paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] insurance. I had never paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] directly since I bought the house. Now my insurance doubled from {$1400.00} a month to {$3200.00} a month. All because they just decided not to pay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Every month now I have to pay more. This company is totally aggressive in hurting homeowners. Can they be held responsible for causing my insurance to double? Plus they continue to make me pay over my contractual agreement month after month ... My principal had hardly decreased since they took over my mortgage. They are responsible for my insurance lapsing. Can they be held responsible? Thank you','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage company took over financing my house from a mortgage company. they claimed they couldn''t reach them and allowed my insurance to lapse. they were trying to strong arm');
