INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(275,'12/31/2018','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','Wells Fargo Bank foreclosed on my home with FRAUDULENT FORECLOSURE DOCUMENTATION! 

History of Fraudulent Documentation : Wells Fargo Bank is well known and has a reputation for improperly documenting foreclosure proceedings. Wells Fargo Bank has been penalized for being dishonest with mortgage document handling and account information. 

Despite being penalized for internal errors and deceptive business practices Wells Fargo Bank has yet discovered a new way to mislead and victimize minority homeowners, and profit from aggressively foreclosing on obsolete and antiquated Predatory Loan Debts. 

Predatory and Fraudulent Loans : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is gone. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank is gone. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank is gone. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank is gone, but the 30 and 40-year predatory ADJUSTABLE RATE LOANS and the PICK-A-PAYMENT LOANS they all spawned are still poisonous and problematic for millions of homeowners whose loans are now serviced by other financial banks such as Wells Fargo. 

The banks that are gone are those that focused on niche marketing. Specifically targeting and focusing on minority borrowers with relatively low credit scores who could borrow with nothing down and without verifying income. The predatory loans made by these banks included deceptive terms with payment calculations that typically become unaffordable for mostly minority borrowers over time. 

Fraudulent, Pick-A-Payment Loan : In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Pick-A-Payment Loan NOTE was deemed illegal, fraudulent and forcefully modified pursuant to a Class Action Lawsuit filed by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Attorney [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of California. The forced modification of my illegal and predatory Pick-A-Payment Mortgage Loan NOTE, terminated all contractual obligations whereby a new modified mortgage note was created, signed for by me and fully executed as a new contract or Mortgage Loan Note attached to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Deed of Trust. 

In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Wells Fargo Bank assigned the untrue, incorrect and outdated Null and VOID, Pass, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Pick-A-Payment NOTE to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to foreclose. From XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Wells Fargo Bank and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] conducted a brutally and punishing crusade to foreclose documenting and misrepresenting the Pick-A-Payment Note as my current verified debt pursuant to the Federal Debt Collections Practices Act ( FDCPA ). 

Right to Accurate Account Information : As a consumer, I have both federal and state statutory rights that entitle me to true, current and accurate account information upon demand. Wells Fargo Bank maintains that the untrue, incorrect and outdated Null and VOID, Pass, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Pick-A-Payment NOTE which has a value equal to {$0.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Due, accurately represents the current Debt attached to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Deed of Trust. 

The act of foreclosing on obsolete, antiquated and extinct loans is illegal debt collecting pursuant to the FDCPA, and fraudulent wrongful foreclosing under the California Homeowners Bill of Rights. Lawfully and timely I disputed and informed both the bank and the trustee of the improper foreclosure documentation. However, rather than correct the foreclosure documentation, both Wells Fargo Bank and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ignored my requests and demands for accurate account information. 

Traumatizing Unlawful Foreclosure : On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Wells Fargo Bank ordered the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to foreclose despite the existence and protection of a Federal Temporary Restraining Order " TRO '''', that restrained and ordered the trustee not to offer my home for sale, and not to foreclose on my home. With knowledge of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], both Wells Fargo Bank and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] colluded and ignored the Federal TRO and sold my home to a 3rd Party Buyer. 

I was traumatized and victimized by Wells Fargo Bank and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] During the foreclosure process, their persistent misrepresentations of the Pick-A-Payment Note, and foreclosing on my home protected by a Federal [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] negligently caused me and my family to endured extreme and outrageous trauma and inflicted mental and physically punishing emotional distress. My family and I suffered the undue and harsh experience of an improperly documented foreclosure. 

Duty to Protect Homeowners and Punish Wells Fargo Bank : Lawmakers and the Courts throughout the USA can not allow property seizures or foreclosures based on backdated, incomplete, obsolete, antiquated or fraudulent documentation, no matter what the circumstances are. Otherwise, no one ''s home is safe. 

Both Wells Fargo Bank and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are Mortgage Industry professional experts who are fully aware of their statutory duty to provide true, accurate, and correct account information. Their consequences for falsely, and fraudulent misrepresenting the untrue, incorrect and outdated Null and VOID, Pass, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Pick-A-Payment NOTE as the current debt of the homeowner should be, EXTREMELY PUNITIVE. 

Wells Fargo Bank should be ordered to pay {>= $1,000,000} in damages to me and my family ; and fined more than {>= $1,000,000} per each Pick-A-Payment Loan Note that have been documented, assigned and misrepresented by the bank as the debt of other similar homeowners during foreclosure. 


Millions of Potential Minority Victims : Any homeowner who has a, or inherited a Predatory Loan such as the Pick-A-Payment Loan Note, can be a victim of the servicing bank ''s fraudulent practice of an improperly documented foreclosure.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'wells Fargo Bank has been penalized for being dishonest with mortgage document handling and account information. wells Fargo Bank has yet discovered a new way to mislea');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(276,'12/30/2018','Debt collection','Private student loan debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I have disputed this debt with ability recovery services, they have yet sent ant validation as required by 809. Validation of debts b ) Disputed debts If the consumer notifies the debt collector in writing within the thirty-day period described in subsection ( a ) of this section that the debt, or any portion thereof, is disputed, or that the consumer requests the name and address of the original creditor, the debt collector shall cease collection of the debt, or any disputed portion thereof, until the debt collector obtains verification of the debt or a copy of a judgment, or the name and address of the original creditor, and a copy of such verification or judgment, or name and address of the original creditor, is mailed to the consumer by the debt collector. Collection activities and communications that do not otherwise violate this subchapter may continue during the 30-day period referred to in subsection ( a )  unless the consumer has notified the debt collector in writing that the debt, or any portion of the debt, is disputed or that the consumer requests the name and address of the original creditor. Any collection activities and communication during the 30-day period may not overshadow or be inconsistent with the disclosure of the consumers right to dispute the debt or request the name and address of the original creditor. 
I would like also to address that Ability Recovery services is in violation of Oklahoma laws as well, Oklahoma laws requires that a business such as collection company must register with the : Oklahoma Secretary Of States and/or have a registered agent - in which Ability recovery service has not and does not, Ability Recovery service can only collect, and do business in the State of Pennsylvania, IF Ability Recovery services would like I will bring these issue up in small claims court, I would not like to file in court but they are forcing me to, so to make clear if filing in court is my last option then I will, at this time cause I have dispute with out response several times I know can file in court the same as I have done against Account Resolution Services, please find there court case attached. I will Give Ability Recovery Services Until, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to remove there trade line name before I file, but once I file I will let court make there decision, with no settlement option.','Ability Recovery Services, LLC',2.0,2.0,'ability recovery services have yet sent ant validation as required by 809. debt collector shall cease collection until debt collector obtains verification of the debt. collection activities and communications that do not');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(277,'12/30/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I tried to make a payment on my mortgage. My mortgage was previously serviced by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Carrington Mortgage services is now the servicer. The terms in which my payments are processed have changed dramatically. I have to pay fees to make payments which I did not have to do before, my payments have gone up again which did not happen before, and then if I fall behind which in my almost 10 years of paying on my mortgage has happened, life happens. When I try to make my payments Carrington shuts down avenues to make them. If I am in the 30 day late category they refuse online payments and refuse over the phone payments. I spoke at length with two representatives from Carrington Mortgage Services on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was advised that they will take my payment from through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at an additional {$8.00} charge because they were refusing my online payment and would apply it by the end of business. I made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I paid more than enough to cover the late fees. That brings me less than 30 days past due. I was assured they would apply the payment and that they process payments on Saturday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as well. Either way my payment was made before 3pm that Friday. I checked my Carrington online account and it is still not posted. This is not the first time Carrington had refused payments. I was only 1 month behind and I pay my penalty. You have people who serve their time in prison for crimes. I had an issue that arose and paid my late fee. For them to continue to penalize me and refuse my payments or not apply my payments which is the case here I feel is unacceptable. As of writing this I am officially less than 30 days past due and should be cleared on any default on my loan. I am fine with a new servicer on my loan, however I am quite offended and frustrated that I feel Carrington is not servicing my loan in the same manner it was being serviced for the almost 10 years I have had my loan. I have not signed any paperwork or agreed to any additional fees and I feel they are playing deceptive games by refusing to apply payments to try to send my loan to foreclosure. My servicer should be the one per my understanding of the law to try to help with foreclosure avoidance and refusing to apply full monthly payments, especially when such payment brings my loan back into the less than 30 days past due status I feel is fraudulent activity and I am requesting they cease and desist these perceived fraudulent activities immediately and apply any and all payments to my account and fix any damages to my credit report. I am also requesting that they go back and fix my credit for the last time they held almost 3 months of my payments in a suspense account and refused to release the payments and during that time reported negatively on my credit report.','CARRINGTON MORTGAGE SERVICES, LLC',10.0,10.0,'if I fall behind which in my almost 10 years of paying on my mortgage has happened, life happens. when I try to make my payments Carrington shuts down avenues to make');
