INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(304,'12/22/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Getting a loan','I am a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Veteran and I''m [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that is apart of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was falsely misled that my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  would of taken care of my education now i am stuck with this debt. I have attached the action suit against the school. 

On Thursday, XX/XX/2018 the Department of Education announced that theyre immediatley approving {>= $1,000,000} in Borrowers Defense to Repayment Discharges, including discharges for people who attended [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 


This email is from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and contains an update about the students claims in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcy. 

We are writing to let you know that today, the Bankruptcy judge gave final approval to the Settlement Agreement between Student Claimants and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Trustee. The court will grant the final order approving the Settlement in approximately ninety days, assuming no states or the U.S. Attorney General file an objection to the Settlement. The Students allegations against [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] included [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  use of high-pressure sales tactics to get students to enroll and remain enrolled, and that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] deceived and misled students about financial aid options and costs of attendance, job placement and salary rates, the quality of equipment and experience of instructors, the desirability of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] graduates by employers, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accreditation status, the transferability of credits, and career placement assistance. 

The full settlement can be found here, but as a quick recap, some key terms of the settlement are : Student Claimants get an approved {$1.00} billion claim in the bankruptcy. In exchange, former [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] students give up their claims against the estate of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and keep their rights to seek further relief from the Department of Education and private lenders ; Over {$500.00} million in student debt held by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is canceled and that cancellation will not be taxable ; and The Trustee returned the {$3.00} million that students paid directly to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after it declared bankruptcy ( this already happened ). 
At this point, we do not have any information about any distributions to the student class from the approved claim amount. If, at the end of the bankruptcy, there is money in the estate to pay unsecured claims, the student class will receive a proportional share based on the size of the allowed claim. Any amount distributed to the student class will be divided fairly, and the distribution must be approved by the court. 

This is a significant victory for students, but we know that there is so much more work to be done. We know that students still have billions of dollars in outstanding federal and private loan debt as result of attending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and we will continue to fight on behalf of students until all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-related debt is discharged. 

There are no other updates at this time and no action is required on behalf of class members, but as always, we will continue to provide you with any updates as they arise. 

