INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(316,'12/20/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/2018 I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to try and buy diapers and meds for my sick kids when I went to check out the total came to {$130.00} so I wrote a check and gave them my ID as well. I recently got married and my last name changed so they asked for more identification since my check and Id had different last names even tho all the other info was the same. So I gave them my debit card that had the correct last name as well and the manager requested I enter my pin for verified I did and he called the bank and verified everything and then still stated he couldnt accept my check or my debit card for the purchase so I said nevermind and left. The next morning I woke up to a charge from that exact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] store for {$530.00}!!! I called chase immediately and disputed the transaction and they issued me a temporary credit. Then on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter in the mail from chase stating they made their decision and were reversing the credit and removing the {$530.00} from my account. I called and tried to appeal this decision but because I didnt have a receipt or anything saying I canceled the transaction ( which I never authorized the transaction in the first place nor did I authorize them to charge ANYTHING to my card ) that there was nothing they could do! I spoke to 3 different managers and no one helped me. So on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they took the {$530.00} back out of my account causing me to not have the money for my kids [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gifts or to pay my cell phone and car insurance payments. I have told them I never authorized any charge from that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] let alone over {$500.00} I never spend that much. We are a lower income family on a fixed income I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] children.'