INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(321,'12/19/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Unauthorized inquiries applied to my credit file. I contacted Equifax 3x and every time I am told to contact the creditors which I have done to no avail. It is a never ending cycle of being told the same thing over and over again to no avail. It has affected me personally and I intend to pursue litigation and hold Equifax liable as they have offered me no recourse. If the inquiries are a " matter of fact '''' and the companies were doing account reviews they should be coded as " soft '''' not hard inquiries. Under no circumstances are unauthorized " hard inquiries '''' allowed to remain a fact of record. Equifax continues to tell me that and that is not true. I have attached the letter of the unauthorized inquires which has been previously sent to Equifax which they have completely ignored. You are told to contact the creditor over and over again and they know that gets no results. If the inquiries are fraudulent, then of course the companies have documentation because they think you authorized it. That does not mean its authorized. Additionally, several companies indicated they were account reviews. If they were account reviews then they should be coded as such. The companies then lie and say they will contact Equifax to remove it or code it as soft but it never happens. This has been going back and forth far too long. I will absolutely take legal action if Equifax ignores my 4th request to remove or correct inaccurate information. If the creditors have been negligent in correcting this information Equifax has a duty to remove it or correct it. This is becoming a little ridiculous. Please see the attachment below to be forwarded to Equifax. 
Thanks, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'unauthorized inquiries applied to my credit file. if the inquiries are a matter of fact '''' they should be coded as soft '''' not hard inquiries. ');
