INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(333,'12/16/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','My mortgage service provider is CMG Mortgage. I have attempted to modify my loan due to a substantial decrease in my income since the start of the original mortgage. The process has taken over three months. Before and during the process, I had to empty out my children ''s NY 529 plans just to keep up with mortgage payments ( over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] worth of funds ). The process with this lender is atrocious. I wasted numerous hours of providing documentation, multiple calls per week during the process in which the representatives either provided inaccurate information. They don''t even allow you to speak to the underwriters to make the process more efficient. They would sit on your application for 30 days causing your paystubs and bank statements to become stale. The decision makers would reject the application when they could have picked up the phone to obtain a simple answer. The decision makers weren''t even knowledgable enough to know the answers to simple follow-up items. For example, they saw deposits from a 529 plan and asked if this was an independent business arrangement. I would expect these decision makers to know the answers to these questions. Another example, they asked for two months of bank statements for a new bank account. It was a new account, and they could have seen from the statement that it was the first month of operations as the starting balance was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Finally, they stated that they sent me a " second letter '''' in which they never did. They usually publish documents to my online portal. No letter for follow-up was ever sent. They now dismissed my application for being incomplete when I called multiple times to ask what else they needed. The reps you speak to are just messengers and they don''t even speak to the underwriters or decision makers. All of this could have been completed in 30 days and if you were able to speak to someone regarding the application and any questions they had on the documentation. They also stated they never received such documentation whenever I either emailed or faxed in the documentation.','CMG MORTGAGE, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the process with this lender is atrocious. the decision makers would reject the application when they could have picked up the phone. they would sit on your application for 30 days causing');
