INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(396,'12/04/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Problem caused by your funds being low','Wells Fargo now has an overdraft policy where if your account drops below [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars, you have until the end of the same business day to deposit money to bring the account into thr positive without incurring overdraft fees. I received an email from Wells Fargo yesterday stating that my account had reaached [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars. I immediately transferred the balance ( plus {$6.00} ), from my joint account ( which is attached to that one ). Today I was notified that I had three overdraft charges because the funds hadnt posted yet. This seems like a manipulation of when specific transactions post, since there is no reason it should not have posted by now when the other transactions have. At {$35.00} each, the overdraft fees overdrafted my account again! I spoke with two customer service representatives at Wells Fargo- one who wasnt even aware of the grace period where you can deposit money into your account before the end of the business day. She offered me, at best, a courtesy of 50 % off of each overdraft fee, which she assured was the best they can do. I barely said I guess ... and then once she transferred me to a higher-up, he made it sound as though he could have had the fees reversed, but they were locked now because she put the 50 % courtesy on them. What courtesy is it to pay {$53.00} for overdrafts that I covered??? I thought Wells Fargo was sued over flaky overdraft tricks like this. Im a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and at certain times in the month my account balance is close to {$0.00}, but I am always cautious and transfer money into it immediately when I see its low. I believe Wells Fargo intentionally pushed through those three transactions before my deposits so that they could charge me three times. They should make this right and completely reverse the fees instead of pretending theyre doing me a courtesy by charging me for fake overdrafts.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'if your account drops below [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars, you have until the end of the same business day to deposit money to bring the account into th');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(397,'12/03/2018','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Communication tactics','This company contacted my employer without my permission. I have a voicemail from them attesting to that. Further, I reside in New Jersey where PD loans are illegal, and loans are capped at % 30. I have paid them over {$5000.00} on {$2300.00} loan much more than 30 %. The company has no right to contact my employer thus sharing my loan information without my permission.','WLCC',2.0,2.0,'PD loans are illegal in new jersey. a voicemail from the company attests to that.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(398,'12/03/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I do not believe that I owe this debt or what you say I owe. 
Pursuant to the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, Section 809 ( b ), Validating Debts : If the consumer notifies the debt collector in writing within the thirty -day period described in subsection ( a ) that the debt, or any portion thereof, is disputed, or that the consumer requests the name and address of the original creditor, the debt collector shall cease collection of the debt, or any disputed portion thereof, until the debt collector obtains verification of the debt or any copy of a judgment, or the name and address of the original creditor, and a copy of such verification or judgment, or name and address of the original creditor, is mailed to the consumer by the debt collector.

( emphasis added ) I respectfully request that you provide me with the following : 1. the amount of the debt ; 2. the name of the creditor to whom the debt is owed ; 3. verification or copy of any judgment ( if applicable ) ; 4. proof that you are licensed to collect debts in Florida ; 5. proof of the last payment made on the account.','Convergent Resources, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'debt collector shall cease collection until debt collector obtains verification of debt. debt collector must verify debt, or copy of judgment, or name and address of original creditor.');
