INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(401,'12/03/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','A collections account was placed on my credit report by Franklin collection services for {$40.00} in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the original creditor is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was a victim of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and canceled my services due to total loss of home after flooding. I informed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  that the equipment was damaged and couldn''t be returned. I was initially charged for the equipment cost although they were aware the equipment was damaged and couldn''t be returned. I was informed by a rep they would check the zip code of my address to ensure that area was declared a disaster area. After doing so, the equipment cost was refunded and the balance owed was {$0.00}. I didn''t use [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   services after that time. 1 year later, I have a collections reporting from them. I never received a bill or any notice of a debt owed from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I also spoke to a rep on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in regards to this issue and the rep informed me she couldn''t explain why I was billed for the {$40.00}. She also contacted the collections dept who couldn''t pull up any information either. It is an unfair practice to place a collections account on my credit without giving any notification or contacting me to rectify the situation. If I owed {$40.00}, I would have paid the amount. I was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the balance was {$0.00}. Please remove any negative marks from my credit reports immediately.','Franklin Collection Service, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a collection account was placed on my credit report by Franklin collection services. the original creditor is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. he canceled my');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(402,'12/02/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','The credit reporting agencies [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Equifax [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are in violation of reporting unverified, an unvalidated account on XX/XX/2018 information provided to them by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], MI [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act, Section 609 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), you are required by federal law to verify - through the physical verification of the original signed consumer contract - any and all accounts you post on a credit report. Otherwise, anyone paying for your reporting services could fax, mail or email in a fraudulent account. 

I demand to see Verifiable Proof ( an original Consumer Contract with my Signature on it ) you have on file of the accounts listed below. Your failure to positively verify these accounts has hurt my ability to obtain credit. Under the FCRA, unverified accounts must be removed and if you are unable to provide me with a copy of verifiable proof, you must remove the accounts from my credit eport','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'the credit reporting agencies are in violation of reporting unverified accounts. the accounts must be removed and if you are unable to provide me with a copy of verifiable proof');
