INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(415,'11/29/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I experienced a mXXXX [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and lost a great deal of our family income. I contacted my mortgage provider to see if they could offer assistance. They shown do interest of assisting me in any way until I contacted HUD, who referred me to an authoring counselor who contacted my mortgage provider. I was then contacted by my mortgage provider on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to complete a loan modification application. For 3 months I called to check the status of my application, but was always told that the underwriter was working on it. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a letter in the mail stating my application was denied. The letter didn''t clearly explain why, so I called but unable to reach my Loan Preservation Specialist. I then filed an appeal, citing the lack of due diligence given to my application and the fact that I have only been in contact with my Loan Preservation Specialist once in 4 months. I only provided proof of additional family, which included my wife ''s income and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] benefit income from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] son that we care for. After call daily to speak with a representative, I received another mailed letter on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] denying my appeal. I then went to my local branch of mortgage company and spoke with some that I enter ask with often. After explaining my situation, I was told off the record that since I have a large amount of equity in my house, the bank would make more money off my house if they foreclosed. I have been in my home for 10 years and don''t want to loss it. I [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year old that would be place in a grave position. I have the income to resume my mortgage payment, I just needs a way to regroup the arearage.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'mXXXXX is a mXXXX and lost a great deal of my family income. a mortgage provider contacted me to complete a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(416,'11/29/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','We obtained a home mortgage loan in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and refinance twice with the latest loan being initiated in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the same property with UBS. We have never had flood insurance on this property ( not required by our homeowners ) because although some of the land is in a flood zone, our dwelling is not. When requested another time for flood insurance I submitted an elevation certificate and subsequently received a letter from the Mortgage lender saying " the flood insurance requirement has been removed from our loan '''' ( see Doc. 1 ). 

This year on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a letter was sent to us by the lender saying we needed to obtain flood insurance or it would be obtained for us or we could submit documentation otherwise. They also stated our flood policy expired on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which there has NEVER been a policy in effect nor have we ever had an escrow account associated with this loan. ( this fact is important to note for later in the complaint ). A second and third letter was sent on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

The Mortgage company actually obtained a flood policy for us on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and created an escrow account for us. They also unknown or uniformed to us they backdated the coverage to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( although those months had passed and no policy has ever been in place on this property or loan ). 

I submitted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] documentation to challenge the requirement of flood insurance. the original letter that was theirs on their letterhead ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) an elevation cert of our property ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and an email stating that some of our property is in AE but the dwelling is in X. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the company responded that more docs would be required. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) We moved forward with a request by phone on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a payoff of the mortgage in order to settle the matter and not be paying for flood insurance we are not required to have and without waiting for 4-6 months on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to reply while incurring the flood insurance charges. However, they would not send it excluding the flood costs. I asked for someone in the insurance department to call me to discuss. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we received an escrow analysis statement for the first time ever. ( Doc 4 ) that showed the amounts due for the upcoming year beginning XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called and spoke to two customer service agents [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who informed me for the first time that we are actually responsible for charges on the flood insurance policy obtained on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] backdated to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This was our first knowledge they are charging us for coverage back to this date. Also, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me a letter was sent in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that an escrow account was being established. We never received this letter nor do any of our paper or online statements show any extra fees, payments or email notifications. He also told us [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had contacted them in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] saying flood was required on this property. Although, by law [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is required to let us know and we never heard this from them. I have requested a copy of this [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] notification from the mortgage company in our phone conversation today XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I also requested a copy of the supposedly expired flood insurance on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] declaration page ( we have never had a flood policy or an escrow account ). In addition, I requested a copy of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter ( which they are required to send 3 letters before obtaining insurance or an escrow account for us, I believe ). Lastly, i was unable to speak to anyone in the insurance dept or escrow department directly with the customer service agent telling me there is no phone number to be connected to. I have again requested someone from that department to call me. The agent said this is not possible, however he would request his superior in customer service to call me. 

There has been veiled information seeing as we did not know of the back dated charges, even on this new/first escrow statement received today nothing shows anything from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would not have even known of this had I not called for an explaination of the " shortage charge '''' now added today that more than doubles the cost of the annual premium for the flood insurance obtained, from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Finally, I offered we would pay this mortgage off in full tomorrow and would bear the responsibility for 1 month of flood coverage in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he said he could not remove the coverage backdated to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I need some intervention and advice. Thank you for your time.','UBS BANK USA',2.0,2.0,'mortgage lender obtained flood insurance on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the mortgage company actually obtained a flood policy for us on ');
