INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(424,'11/28/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I have an existing conventional home mortgage with Wells Fargo Home Mortgage, which has improperly applied my payments to pay down principal instead of for monthly payments. 

Five electronic cash transfers were sent to Wells Fargo for an existing mortgage that should have been applied to a monthly payment cycle ( principal+interest+escrow for tax and insurance ). The payments were correctly made using a Wells Fargo-branded payment module to the mortgage account. 

Wells Fargo mis-applied the cash transfers and applied them entirely to pay down principal and demanded additional payments to become current again on the normal monthly payments. Calls to Wells Fargo resulted in incorrect explanations and demands for additional payments. It took 11 months, false explanations, and countless calls to figure out what actually happened, at which point Wells Fargo would only reverse principal payments from the last 90 days, which covered a small fraction of the funds involved. Wells Fargo ''s own incompetence led to the delays and the mis-applied funds going beyond the 90-day window. 

In summary, Wells Fargo took in funds and mis-applied them without permission, then demanded additional payments and delayed action until they claimed they could no longer reverse the older payments. I never stipulated that the funds should be used to pay down the principal and Wells Fargo refuses to refund or credit the payments towards normal monthly payments. I have been forced to make additional payments but am now in default. 

The payments are each for {$1600.00} on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a total of {$8100.00}.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'five electronic cash transfers were sent to Wells Fargo for an existing mortgage. the payments were correctly made using a Wells Fargo-branded payment module. it took 11 months');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(425,'11/27/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Our home was flooded by Hurricane Florence and our Flood insurance company sent us a check in our names and the mortgage company Nationstar Mortgage d/b/a as Mr Cooper.

I registered my disaster claim with Mr Cooper on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and received a Tracking number and information. 

I have been asking questions for more accountability and transparency of them for how my claim check is going to be handled, such as : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Why is my claim monitored diffently then my flood Matthew disaster? I was told Fema guidelines and because of the amount of my check. Is my money going to be placed in a interest bearing acct.. I was told no. Later I am told yes. Every time I call the special disaster relief number I speak with a different person and receive conflicting information from before or new information that gives me a little bit of the BIG picture of how and where is my money being held. No accountability to me how they are governing my check and Not fully being transparent to me what I have to do to have some of my money sent to me for needed repairs as well as reimbursement of our out of pocket expenses. 

I have been asking basically the same questions over and over again and have requested this information be put in writing to me. As of this time and date I still have not received this information. 
I have been told it is on the website. Just need to register and I can read it there. NO it is not on : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] So I call back again, I am told I can find the information on MrCooper.com. NO its not there either.

I can go on and on how I get the run around from Mr Cooper servicing department.

# 1 When I send this claim check in I want to know who and where my money is being held. This money is not a payment and not escrow money.

# 2 How is the money held? Trust acct? Escrow Names on acct etc?

# 3 insured?

# 4 Can we do self contracting? What are guide lines? And Hire Contractors too!

I have been asking these questions and have asked it be put in writing and as of this date have not been given or received requested information.

This is our home. We have had an Excellent mortgage history on this loan before Mr Cooper took over and since he took over. We repaired our home after the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hurricane Matthew flood. We have continued to improve our home and will do the same to repair and improve our home after this Hurricane Florence disaster.

I feel we and any consumer deserve more respect than what I have received from Mr Cooper and full transparency and accountability for this insurance money they want to hold. Today is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].. They have had long enough time to honor my request so we can move forward to repairing our home. They have left me in limbo long enough. I request your assistance.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'my claim check was sent to me by our flood insurance company. a tracking number and information was sent to me. a number of questions have been asked for more accountability ');
