INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(428,'11/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','I created an online account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The sign-up process requires that you share your social security number with them. I initiated an online chat conversation with a customer service representative to inquire about the firm ''s underwriting standards ( loan-to-value ratios and required down payments ) for single-family investment properties. I explicitly stated during this conversation that I was not applying for a mortgage with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I did not want my credit score pulled. Within the week, my credit score had been hard pulled by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice explicitly without my consent.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the sign-up process requires that you share your social security number with them. I initiated an online chat conversation with a customer service representative.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(429,'11/27/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose prepaid card','Problem with a purchase or transfer','XX/XX/2018 I submitted a bill payment using America Express Serve in the amount of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. XX/XX/2018 it was to be delivered. All went well until, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advised to send a money order or pay in cash. They sent/mailed the check back to me. I got it and on XX/XX/2018 I filed a dispute with AMEX serve. 36 reps later, 5 migraines, and I still do not have my {$120.00}. I checked with the payment processing center number on the check they wrote and they couldn''t do much to help me but they did say the stop payment was completed on their end. I have to pay my loan with those funds and they are holding them. here is a breakdown of the timeline of me calling : XX/XX/2018 Transaction was made XX/XX/2018 was the date it would be delivered to the merchant XX/XX/2018 the original dispute was requested XX/XX/2018-was told next follow up will be the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was told that i would be followed up with the same day. An email was sent to the back office and they responded saying I will be notified when credit is made to the account XXXXanother follow up was sent to the back office and yet no reply XX/XX/2018 advised dispute in process and that i will be notified once an update/advised 10 business days and still no resolution [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] this is still in process and customer will be notified when the credit is placed on their account still no resolution [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Management above back-office would be emailed, today technically is the 10th day. so story changed again still no resolution So what it boils down to is that the back-office still did not provide any response but that " This is still in progress '''' and we will notify the customer when it is completed 36 calls were made with no resolution at all. 
I have also written their feedback site, along with tried attorneys and I am not getting any help. Can you guys give me some hope??','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2018 I submitted a bill payment using America Express Serve. XX/XX/2018 was to be delivered to the merchant XX/XX');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(430,'11/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have recently been trying to obtain a consolidation loan. I have repeatedly been denied and when I check the reasons for my denial, the responses include : Serious delinquency and too few accounts currently paid as agreed. These are false statements because I have an exceptional payment record according to my actual credit reports that I have sent for, as well as credit monitoring on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have repeatedly called all three credit bureaus asking why they keep giving these responses to the lenders I apply to but they have no answer to give me. I realize my credit score is not yet at 700, but it is not because of serious delinquency or too few accounts paid as agreed. These are most definitely false statements. I will agree that my proportion of balances to credit limits on bank/national revolving accounts is too high, however that is why I am applying for a consolidation loan. In addition, the credit report states that the proportion of loan balances to loan amounts is too high. This is also untrue as my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan has gone down from {$7000.00} to {$4500.00}. I am currently paying on a car loan, however the balance has taken a long time to move because I had to pay for GAP insurance coverage first before I could start paying on the principal. I feel these false statements are very unfair and unjust.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'I have been trying to obtain a consolidation loan. I have been denied a consolidation loan. the responses include a credit score of 700.');
