INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(448,'11/22/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/2018, I received a {$300.00} check from a gentleman for merchandise he bought from me. While the gentleman was in front of me I called his bank to verify that the account was active and the funds were available. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was the bank that the check was drawn on and they confirmed that the account was active and funds were available. Once we finished our business, I deposited the check into my Capital One 360 checking account. I check my account via the mobile app at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it stated that the first {$200.00} was made available til the check clears. At [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received an email stating that fraud prevention put a hold on my account and wanted me to call in asap. At [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called Capital One and was transferred to fraud prevention. They said that they called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was told that the check would be returned for NSF and because of that Capital One was closing my account and ending any business relationship now or in the future. I told he guy in the fraud dept that I didn''t understand why they were closing my account since I did what I was suppose to do. At this point, I asked when my money was going to be released since I do have children that I need to care for. I was told that they would be keeping the funds and waiting for the check to be returned so that they could return it to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
On XX/XX/2018, I decided to check my account to see what had happened with the check. To my surprise my account was still open and this time my over all balance & available balance was {$300.00}, but states that the funds are unavailable for withdrawal and that I needed to call in yet again. So at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called in and they transferred me to another dept that wasn''t fraud prevention. I was told that they only do out bound calls and that they could transfer me to a voicemail. I asked them to please transfer me were I did leave a voicemail. Around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I still received no call from anyone at the bank so I called in again to try and reach someone before the end of business day. The rep said that they couldn''t give me any info nor release the funds. I asked him to transfer me to someone that could do something. I was transferred to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( manager ) who was rude straight from the beginning and so I told her that I wanted to speak to someone higher than her and she stated that there is no one higher than her. So I asked her, are you telling me that you own the bank? She stated no but refused to give information to anyone higher than her. The next thing I knew the call was disconnected. 
So instead of letting myself get upset, I decided to wait to see what happens with my account since I used to work for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I know their banking policies. It''s now the first week in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and in the mail I received a statement for my account stating that it''s still open and it''s earned interest of {$0.00}. That got me a little curious, so I called Capital One again. This time I was told that It''s a ghost account and the money isn''t really there. I asked them to explain how this ghost account is earning interest on money that isn''t really there and no one had an answer for me. So yet again I asked for someone higher than the person that I was talking too and was told that there was no one else that I could talk too. By now my fuse was starting to get real short since no one could give me any answers, so I started doing my own research when time allowed me. Now it''s the beginning of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and almost 2 months since I deposited the check into my account and I''m receiving another statement stating my account has earned more interest of {$0.00}. I called Capital One again and asked to talk to someone in fraud prevention. This time they wouldn''t transfer me to the voicemail, but told me if there was any changes to my account then they would call me. I told the lady on the phone that I used to work for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and if the money is in my account then that means the check cleared. I told them what they are doing was illegal and that I wanted a date that my funds would be released. I was told that they wouldn''t be and then the agent started getting really rude. Once I got off the phone this time I started looking over Capital One ''s policy and that of the Federal Reserve under regulation CC. I found out that my funds are suppose to be released to me once the check clears the other bank and that if for any reason they are to be held longer that I''m suppose to receive written notice telling me why and a date when they will be released. I never received anything of that sort from Capital One. It''s now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 3 months since the check was deposited and I received another statement saying that my account earned more interest of {$0.00}. This time I was going to stand my ground. I called Capital One again and explained to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( manager ) that the way they are holding my money is illegal. I read her Capital One policy, the Federal Reserve regulation CC and informed her that I used to work for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] so if they were going to return the check then they would have done so already. She tried to be as helpful as she could, but she was at a loss herself. She did tell me that I could contact customer satisfaction, but they can only be emailed. I explained that with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] coming up pretty fast that I just needed my money to do something for my kids. She was completely sympathetic, but her hands were tied. I did send an email to customer satisfaction, but have heard no response as of yet.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a gentleman in the fraud dept called me to check my account to see what had happened with the check. he called his bank to verify that the account was active and funds');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(449,'11/21/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I am a victim of identity theft and I write to dispute certain information in my file resulting from th e ID Theft. I have attached the items I dispute on my credit report. The items I am disputing do not relate to any transactions that I made or authorized.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the items I dispute do not relate to transactions that I authorized.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(450,'11/21/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','I applied for a Chase [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card online. It was denied even though I have excellent credit and other credit accounts with Chase. They claim I can not prove I am me and suggested I check my credit reports. I got all three credit reports and none has any false information. I correctly answered ALL of their security questions but they continue to tell me I am not the person applying for the card. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so I have had several names and addresses over my lifetime ( birth name and a few marriages ) but the same name for 32 years, the same address for 16 years, the same phone number for 16 years, etc. I have even had the same email address for more than 20 years. There are not, and have never been, any fraud alerts on my credit reports.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'I applied for a Chase credit card online. it was denied even though I have excellent credit and other credit accounts. they claim I can not prove I am me and suggested I check');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(451,'11/21/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I got a call from Navient on XX/XX/2016 saying I qualify for loan consolidation. He told me that they would consolidate all of my federal loans into one or two trade lines. After 3 months in forbearance, they only consolidated ( 7 ) of my federal loans in the amount of {$19000.00}. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2016, Navient made ( 3 ) disbursements and ( 2 ) adjustments in the amount of {$21000.00}. This is {$2600.00} more than what they paid for my ( 7 ) federal loans in question. In addition, I had to pay a one time fee of {$790.00} to have Navient consolidate my loans. The Navient representative ''s name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and his number was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He told me that the whole point in consolidating my loans would be to reduce the amount of trade lines from my federal loans as well as lower my interest rate. The current interest rate on my loans with Navient is 4 %. ( 4 ) of the ( 7 ) federal loans that Navient paid off had interest rates lower than 4 %. I was absolutely misled into believing that consolidating my loans with Navient would save me money in the long run. This is not the case at all. Not only did my loan amount increase {$3700.00}, but i paid a one time fee of {$790.00} and my interest rate went up for ( 4 ) of the ( 7 ) loans. Navient consolidated 7 trade lines into 2 ( Subsidized and Unsubsidized ). They took advantage of me right out of college by telling me i was qualified for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] student loan forgiveness Act. None of the things that occurred above had anything to do with this Act. Instead, my loan is now bigger with a higher interest rate. I recently got word of a lawsuit against Navient which made me take a deep dive into what occurred back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2016. I now see that i was misled and taken advantage of.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'i was misled into believing that consolidating my loans with Navient would save me money in the long run. i paid a one time fee of $790.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(452,'11/21/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','Received a " Notice of Unpaid Electronic Transfer '''' from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dated XX/XX/2018 requesting payment for an alleged Check Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] written on XX/XX/2018 to Original Creditor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Store Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which is in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], GA in the amount of {$2000.00}. The above information is from the notice and includes that the check was returned as either a Stop Payment or the account the check was written on was not authorized for ACH transactions. The notice also says [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] purchased the dishonored electronic fund transfer and forwarded it to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for collection. First, I live in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], TX and was at work in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], TX on XX/XX/2018 and have never been to or in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], GA. Second, there were no supporting documents accompanying this notice such as a copy of the returned check or bank name the check was drawn on or a copy of the receipt for whatever was purchased. Third, the check sequence of my bank account checks currently in use are in the 500s, not the thousands let alone the 4000s. I am not the person these people are looking for. Lastly, upon investigating scam or fraud reports via the Internet on these two companies I found numerous consumers who have had similar experiences. And apparently, these companies do not do their due diligence verifying customer information during transactions.','First Data Corporation',2.0,4.0,'a notice of unpaid electronic transfer '''' was sent to Original Creditor. the notice also says the check was returned as either a Stop Payment or the account the check was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(453,'11/21/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  has been non-compliant with removing the unverified account SYNCB/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  which has been deleted by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have both completed their research and determined that SYNCB/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was not established by myself but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] keeps verifying this accounts. Also, when I called the company they responded that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not send them all of the verifying evidence to confirm each account is unverified.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been non-compliant with removing the unverified account. the account has been deleted by [COMPTE_ANON');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(454,'11/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Unable to get your credit report or credit score','I have already reported a Dispute with Equifax ( resolution code [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ... ( When contacting [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   provide your current file number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 

