INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(467,'11/17/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Closing on a mortgage','On XX/XX/2018, I closed on a new home in the Maryland area with Quicken Loans. The closing was originally scheduled for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but was pushed back for Friday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .To my surprise during the signing of the documents I was shocked to learn that my first payment would be due in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called the gentleman who had helped me throughout the process about this and he apologized stating that " the person servicing the loan, never changed the date and unfortunately it was an oversight ''''. That was the 1st issue. 
At the same time I was on the phone with the Quicken Loan rep trying to see if this could be resolved I signed the paperwork, only to realize that he included ESCROW on my monthly payment WITHOUT DISCUSSING THIS WITH ME! I put 20 % down and my credit score is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], why would they automatically apply that to my monthly balance and not give me the option to pay for it separately?! I called, spoke with too many uninterested and frankly unhelpful investigators at Quicken Loan whose sole purpose is to protect the organization against admitting any liability. That was the 2nd major issue. 
In XX/XX/2018 ( 3rd month in the loan ) I receive a letter stating that there is a manual disbursement on my property tax and that now I OWE QUICKEN LOANS over {$5000.00} which will be applied to my mortgage! I called and spoke to another investigator and questioned them how could this happen. I signed mortgage documents less than 3 months ago agreeing to pay {$2800.00} and now you they are trying to force me to pay {$3300.00}. As they naturally did, the investigators provided no solution and they stated that it was not their responsibility. That is the 3rd and FINAL ISSUE.

I am just one person and do not have access to the same resources that Quicken Loans has, however make no mistake, THERE IS RIGHT WAY to do things AND THERE IS WRONG way to do things. These issues could have been rectified in private if they showed a willingness to take responsibility and act accordingly, they didn''t.','QUICKEN LOANS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2018, I closed on a new home in the Maryland area. the closing was originally scheduled for XX/XX/[COMPTE_');
