INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(484,'11/14/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Unable to get your credit report or credit score','I am currently in the process of obtaining a mortgage. I signed a contract and put [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] down on the house. I have a deadline and I am endangered of losing our deposit. When the mortgage ran the three credit reports they received reports back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  but not Equifax. The report was not completed because it had a " Beacon Hold ''''. I called Equifax and they made me provide them with ID Verification which I faxed to them. I called them back two days later and they stated that I should be able to run the credit report with no problem.They stated that there were no blocks or holds on my account. So I paid to run the report again and the mortgage company got the same message. I called Equifax again and they stated that I needed to sent them another ID Verification after the agent refused to give me access to my account. I asked to speak with the supervisor who then provided access. The supervisor stated that there were no problems and to have our mortgage company contact them directly. The mortgage company contacted them the next day but was not allowed access because Equifax did not have my correct birthday. I called Equifax again and had to speak with a supervisor again because the agents would not give me access to my account. They resolved the situation and the mortgage company ran my credit again and the " Beacon Hold '''' came up again. I called Equifax again and I had to be transferred to a supervisor for access to my account. The supervisor stated that it was the third party company [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was holding the process up. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with my mortgage counselor and they instructed that I call