INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(501,'11/09/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','My original student loan balances were {$38000.00} and {$34000.00} when the loans were consolidated and I began my $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  monthly payments on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I continued making the $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] monthly payments as agreed until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], when I filed a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Plan. The loan servicer told me that I should not make any payments until the Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Plan was completed and discharged. That same advice was confirmed by my bankruptcy counsel. The Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Plan lasted 5 years, during which I repaid the majority of my unsecured debt and continued paying my mortgage and car payments outside the plan. Upon discharge of the Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Plan, Navient advised me that it had capitalized 5 years of unpaid interest, effectively doubling the amount of the unpaid principal balance. 

I am now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old, unemployed and receiving a {$2000.00} monthly social security benefit, supplemented by a small IRA fund. My wife is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and also unemployed. Neither of us have been able to find employment in our respective fields. 

Navient is demanding payments of {$1100.00} for 120 months, which will result in a total repayment of over {$150000.00}. Navient purposely advised me to stop my payments during the Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Pan so that it could charge me nearly twice what I originally owed on my student loan. I have repeatedly requested a smaller repayment amount from Navient to no avail. My IRA will be depleted before my expected lifetime expires if I am forced to make the demanded repayment amount ( s ).','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my original student loan balances were $38000.00 and $34000.00. the loan servicer told me that I should not make any payments until the');
