INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(503,'11/09/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On Tuesday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I learned of an amount I owed to US bank. I called US Bank and made a settlement with them on the condition that they fax me a settlement confirmation letter the same day. I was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at US Bank that in order for that to happen I would need to go to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and make the payment there, I was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that after making that payment I would need to call her back with a confirmation number for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   transaction. I did everything as instructed and to my surprise [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said she could not send me the fax that day, I did not receive the letter I needed after doing my part. The next day Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called back and was told that the payment would have to post before the letter could be sent even though I had taken the extra steps of going to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to make the payment. I did not receive the letter that day. On Thursday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called back and was told that payment still had not posted. I did not received the letter that day either. It is now XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and although I have been told that the payment has posted I still have not received the letter I so desperately need and was promised. US Banks policies are deceitful in this regard and I would not have taken the extra step of going to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to make this payment if I had known they would not be faxing the letter I still need. The manager of this department of US Bank, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], remains unresponsive after sending several voicemails and emails.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a settlement confirmation letter was sent to me on a day of faxing. the letter was sent to me by a bank manager. the letter was sent to me on');
