INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(511,'11/08/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I wrote to Equifax asking them to verify an account ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). They never verified the account and in fact responded that the account was not found on my credit report although I have proof that it was and still is reporting. I wrote a second letter in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] asking them to verify the account and included my current credit report with the account circled to show that the account is reporting and they responded " Please be specific with your concerns by listing the account names, numbers and the nature of the dispute. Please be advised that a 7 years extended fraud alert is currently reporting on your credit file. '''' This is bogus because as you can see in the attached letter to Equifax, I was very specific and listed the name of the alleged creditor ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), account number ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), and the nature of my dispute ( PLEASE VERIFY AND PROVIDE METHOD OD VERIFICATION ). I am convinced that they can not verify this account, thus they continue to send me dunning letters. This is a direct violation of the FCRA and my Consumer Rights and I want this account thoroughly investigated with verification and the method ( s ) by which they verified. If they can not do that, it needs to be removed. I have perfect credit with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have never had reporting problems with them. Equifax already has proven themselves to be untrustworthy among consumers and businesses alike with their data breach last year and I am convinced that they are not doing the right thing and it needs to be brought to light.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a 7 years extended fraud alert is currently reporting on your credit file. I wrote to Equifax asking them to verify an account. they never verified the account and responded that the account');
