INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(536,'11/02/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','My credit score dropped from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with Transunion ( 62 points ) and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( 40 points ) in the matter of two days as a result of paying off a credit card account balance ( which was normally paid off on a monthly basis ) and closing that business credit card account for an entity that was being terminated. I was shocked, and contacted via telephone both Transunion and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for an explanation of such a drastic decline. Both agencies could or would not supply an answer to my question. Both agencies transferred me to different departments for more information. Again, could not get an answer to my simple question of why, for closing an account that was no longer required, my credit score ( which effects even my insurance rates ) dropped so much. The answers where the same form both agencies, they said in essence : " many factors go into determining your credit score and we can not divulge how the score is determined. '''' This answer is unacceptable. These agencies set benchmarks for banks, insurance companies, lenders, credit companies to determine what credit worthiness you deserve and your credit score determines what rate you may pay moving forward, even regarding car and house insurance rates. 

