INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(540,'11/01/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Our loan was transferred from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to Flagstar Bank in XX/XX/2018. I called the bank to see where we needed to send our payments. The representative I spoke with told me that we had a 60 day grace period during which we didnt have to make our payments because there would be no late fee or penalties. I asked multiple times if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments would be due when it came [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he assured me they wouldnt. He also assured me that we wouldnt be penalized for those payments later on, none of that information was correct. We are now two payments behind and have been trying to play check up ever since. This all couldve been avoided if we had been given correct information to begin with. Weve had our mortgage for three years with no issues at all but weve literally had problems nonstop since the day our loan was transferred. Im beyond fed up. We are now charged a fee monthly on our bank accounts at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] since our mortgage isnt with them anymore which isnt fair at all because we had no say in this transfer. " Consumers should not be collateral damage in the mortgage servicing transfer process, '''' said Consumer Financial Protection Bureau Director [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Well we definitely feel like collateral damage to say the least.','FLAGSTAR BANK, FSB',2.0,2.0,'a representative told me that we had a 60 day grace period. he assured me that we wouldn''t be penalized for those payments later on. we are now two');
