INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(544,'11/01/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Waypoint Resource Group reported me as a delinquent debtor on my credit reports in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] without ever contacting me to inquire about the ( erroneous ) debt of {$430.00} They got the collection assignment from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for service to a residence in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] between XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] andXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I have lived in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Pennsylvania since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]! This account was fraudulently put in my name. When I contacted Waypoint this past spring to inform them that the debt wasn''t mine they refused to remove the bad debt report from my credit record and said I would have to take it up with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  without providing any information about the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account. I, again, called Waypoint in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of this year and insisted that they research the bad debt. They gave me a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  phone number and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gave me an account number. I, then, filed a fraud report with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  but purposely left off my Social Security number ( which they really don''t need to resolve this issue as they had the account number, my PA driver ''s license, my address and my phone number ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  called to say they would not process my fraud claim without a full SS #. I offered to give it to them over the phone. They refused, and said I could fax it to them. My fax doesn''t work, so I mailed it to them. They then refused to process it bc it wasn''t on their " fraud form ''''. I have resubmitted a complete fraud form by registered mail to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  but it is clear to me all their privaricating is simply to delay processing my fraud claim and their data collection is solely meant to get my current personal information so their collection agency can harass me. This was proven out because Waypoint, who had never sent me a single piece of mail in the interim four years, immediately sent me a collection notice. How is it legal for a collection agency to defame one ''s credit rating to a credit rating agency without EVER contacting a person for collection or to determine whether the claim is, in fact, genuine? And how can [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   claim I owe them money when I haven''t had their service since I moved to PA in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]!!','Waypoint Resource Group, LLC',2.0,4.0,'Waypoint Resource Group reported me as a delinquent debtor on my credit reports in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] without');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(545,'10/31/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I have a mortgage on my home with Caliber Home Loans, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], OK. I have been trying for several years to get a loan modification application approved to get my mortgage payments lowered and a better interest rate. The VA is also on the mortgage as my husband was a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  veteran. Unfortunately, my husband passed away in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the mortgage is in his name ONLY. Caliber sent me a loan modification agreement with a letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The agreement had signature lines for my husband ''s name only. Caliber had already supposedly put the account in my name as " Successor of Interest '''' for the mortgage. My husband passed away [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called Caliber to ask them about my husband ''s name being on the signature line of the loan mod agreement. The representative I spoke to did NOT have a copy of the agreement on his computer, but told me to just cross out my husband ''s name and sign my name on the agreement. I signed the agreement in front of a Notary Public and then mailed the agreement to Caliber in the overnight mail. I did not hear from Caliber and called them on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The Caliber representative informed me that the agreement was dated for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Caliber was NOT going to accept the agreement and they were proceeding with the Sheriff ''s sale of my property. I spoke to a VA representative on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who is servicing this account. That rep informed me that she could see on her computer records that Caliber had APPROVED the loan modification application in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and again in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I never received this approval from Caliber nor did I receive an agreement from Caliber. My husband was still living in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] so he would have been the one to sign the agreement, but we did NOT receive that agreement. This is a super mess and has been ever since we started doing business with Caliber Home Loans several years ago. I have submitted NUMEROUS loan mod applications over the years and Caliber holds onto the documents long enough for them to become outdated, and then they request new, updated documents so I have to start the loan mod application all over again. I have over twenty-five ( 25 ) years '' experience in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  field and am currently [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I keep very good records of everything which has taken place during this process. We had asked for a modification when my husband retired and I was not working. I have been [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for the last four ( 4 ) years and am able to make my mortgage payments on time each and every month. But Caliber has never been interested in that fact. They prefer to play games and keep me on a merry go round and in suspense as to whether or not I will be able to keep my home. I did a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] search on Caliber Home Loans and a large number of lawsuits and class action lawsuits popped up where customers have sued Caliber for many of the same issues I am having with them. The rep at the VA suggested I file a complaint with you so that maybe you can investigate this terrible mess and possibly help me to keep my home. Thank you for your assistance, have a great day and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bless You! [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Caliber Home Loans, Inc.',4.0,4.0,'a mortgage on my home with Caliber Home Loans, OK, is on the mortgage. my husband passed away in XX/XX/[COMPTE_AN');
