INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(554,'10/30/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','The only reason that Im reaching out the CFPB is because I was taken off a repayment plan unilaterally without my knowledge and then illegally penalized by having to jump though more hoops and being reported negatively on my credit report. This applies to myself and the co-signer, which in this instance is my ill mother whom Navient knows. 

As a result of a lot of hard work and negotiation with Navient. I was approved to have a certain payment and contractual terms for the duration of my loans. Navient removed me from these payments based on subjective measures that were not at any time part of the agreed terms and refused to place me back on the the automatic repayment plan that I was on. Its not if I made my payments on time since my payments were in auto debit, but why Navient took me off of this contract and refuses to fix it, fairly. 

I hope this makes sense and you can see whats happening. If not, I can most definitely speak to you in person and articulate this differently. 

The office of the advocate has mistreated me and not responded to me on getting any traction to fix this. 

