INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(587,'10/23/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my FHA mortgage was transferred from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to Carrington Mortgage. Since the transfer, I have made both the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( online payment ) and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( telephone payment with bankruptcy representative ) payments to Carrington Mortgage. However, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a monthly statement from Carrington showing that my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment had not been applied to my account. It was being held in a " suspense '''' account. The statement also indicated that I owed {$10000.00} due XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I immediately called Carrinton and was transferred to a bankruptcy representative who stated that something happened with my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment and caused it to be sent to a " suspense account ''''. She said she would put in an order to have it applied to the account. However, she also stated that Carrington could not find my payment ledgers from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and because of that, they had no record that I had made payments from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That''s why they were billing me for the {$10000.00}. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was told Carrington had received the payment ledgers along with all of the other loan documents during the transfer. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] also faxed a copy to their bankruptcy department ( addressed to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 

