INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(610,'10/18/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Virtual currency','Fraud or scam','Hello! 

I have been a Chase Bank user since my parents let me get a debit card in High School. While I have had mostly amazing experiences with Chase Bank, today was really hard for me and it makes me think twice about Chase and the fraud protection they offer to their customers. Or, lack there of. 

On the morning of Thursday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I went to go buy tickets for my favorite artist, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who would be performing on Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Utah. When I went to the website to try to buy tickets, I noticed they were sold out. This scared me, because I knew I couldn''t miss the show. So I proceeded to go on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to see if there was anyone selling tickets. Having been scammed by a scam artist one other time, I was trying to be extra careful when looking for tickets. My boyfriend [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and my friend [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] both wanted to go as well, and trusted me to find the tickets. I came across a girl named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who seemed to have a decent profile and I texted the number she included in her post. I will attach our texting conversation in this thread. I told her I was looking for 3 tickets for me and two of my friends. She told me she had 4, and could sell me 3, for {$45.00} each. I told her I recently was scammed and didn''t want another experience like that, and she proceeded to send me the ticket confirmation email as proof. I believed her. I asked my boyfriend and my friend to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] me {$45.00} each, and they did. The girl wanted me to pay her via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which is something that Chase Quick Pay owns. I had her email, and her phone number, so I thought even if this was a scam, I would be okay, since Chase has all of their information. Right? Wrong. I paid the girl, and she told me she was sending me the tickets. Well, they never came. I never got them. I called the girl, call rejected. She blocked me. She deleted her [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so I wouldn''t find her. 

I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], sobbing. {$130.00} down the drain. How do people do this to others? Is this what they do with their lives? Does this make people happy? When I told them what happened, the lady over the phone said " There''s nothing we can do. '''' I''m sorry, what? You literally have a phone number AND and email attached to this person ''s account, and you can''t track them down and flag them? It was just a simple NO. How could Chase Quick Pay own [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and work with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if they can''t find a way to track down scammers? I am not putting up with this.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a girl named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was scammed by a scam artist. she told me she had 4 tickets and could sell me 3, for ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(611,'10/18/2018','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Personal line of credit','Charged fees or interest you didn''t expect','Dear Sir or Madam, I did not receive my student loan for XX/XX/XXXX8. I received checks in the mail that said sign it and the money is yours. I was in a rough spot and still am but I needed the money to keep going to school. I have contacted the loan institutions and asked for a lower payment and interest charge. They ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) are currently charging me 48 % and 79 % interest, respectively. 
