INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(628,'10/16/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose prepaid card','Problem with a purchase or transfer','I have an American Express Serve prepaid card. I have direct deposits made on a regular basis. Four recent deposits have failed to show up on my balance even after the payment was processed by the issuer. I called their customer service number, but the call was not picked up after being on hold for over thirty minutes. 
I found out from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and other social media that thousands of people have been waiting for direct deposits from this and the Bluebird card ( also issued by Amex in conjunction with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ). I am broke and desperate for answers.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'prepaid card issued by american Express Serve. four deposits failed to show up on balance even after payment was processed.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(629,'10/15/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','This all happened between XX/XX/2018 and XX/XX/2018. 

I am writing to dispute the amount of {$12000.00} on account ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This letter will also clarify the verbal communication I had with Chase Credit Card Service and submit new finds regarding this matter. 


Please note new Information regarding my case : That in-addition there is new information that has come to light. The employee of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had allegedly perpetrated this fraudulent transaction apparently to least 30 other victims, not including myself. According to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] president, this person may have stolen possibly as much as {$80000.00} since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of last year. Below is the event leading up to this point. 


I am disputing this amount for the following reasons : I am a victim of a very creative credit card fraud, designed to appear as if the transaction was a legal sale using my credit card information and electronic signature on file. ( Bait and switch credit card processing ). 


I entered into a signed contract with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to replace my roof for {$18000.00}. {$9000.00} down, the balance of {$9000.00} at the end of the job. ( A copy of the contract is attached ) I used my Chase Credit Card ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as the source for a " One Time Payment '''' for the down payment. Transaction process by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the employee of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] signee on contract attached. 

I gave my credit card information and signed a tablet with this employee from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] At my home. 


I visited [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  office, I met [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who represented himself as the President/Owner of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the office to discuss the job and contract. After investigating [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] informed me that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] processed my card but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not understand what happened to the money. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charged my credit card and used my electronic signature on file ( intended for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to commit credit card fraud for {$12000.00} from my credit card. 


I am not sure if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is part of this fraud but they claim even though [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is an employee, they never received the funds in their account. 


At no time did I give my permission ( in writing or verbally ) or intended to have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] use my information and electronic signature for his personal use in any capacity. I was lead to believe by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that my deposit would safely be processed via the tablet after I signed the contract. 


I do not know who this company is that have charged the {$12000.00}. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have also stated they do not know whom this company is that withdrew these funds. I have no agreement or contract with the person ( s ) / company that have taken these funds with my stolen information. It is standard industry business practice that there should have been a contract or document of some sort detailing the work to be performed for this type and size of the transaction, however, no one knows whom these people are that charged my card. 


It is not reasonable to believe that I would have to know that an employee in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] office having access and or entrusted with customers credit card information would have used my information to withdraw these funds for his personal use or to sell my information to be used by someone not intended for. 


This transaction, without doubt, rises to the level of fraud by these individuals. Based on The Fair Credit Billing Act ( FCBA ) I am requesting that the amount is corrected to reflect this fraud and that any finance and other charges related to the disputed amount be credited as well, and that I receive an accurate statement. Enclosed are copies of the contract and supporting documents supporting my position. Please investigate this matter and correct the billing error as soon as possible.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a credit card fraud victim is a victim of a very creative credit card fraud. a credit card fraud victim is suing the company for a ''one time payment');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(630,'10/15/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','In reference to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] CREDIT CARD. On XX/XX/2018 I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Customer Service because I noticed that my payment in the amount of {$1600.00} was applied to my old account which was compromised ( fraudulent charges that I found and disputed and has since been settled ). This payment was intended to pay the credit charges I made on the new account. Upon speaking with customer service at both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I came to find that one of the fraudulent charges was posted to my new account and subsequently removed. The remaining balance on the account was {$890.00}. I directed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s customer service to use the {$1600.00} payment to pay the card in full and send me a check for the balance of {$700.00}, which they did. 
