INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(689,'10/03/2018','Checking or savings account','Other banking product or service','Managing an account','On XX/XX/2018 I went into the branch of Bank of America located at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NM [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was seeking to remove NSF feature from my bank account. If I do not have money in my account, I do not want the bank to pay anything. First of all my voice is loud and many people can mistake this to anger or raising of my temperment. The customer service rep for some reason sent my request to the Branch manager. In trying to explain my request, the Manager accused me of being angry. I raised my finger to make a point, & she yelled at me to stop pointing my finger at her. Banks are customer service bussinesses & this Manager proved that she lacks the skills to interact with upset customers, she was so unhelpful, that I left without my request being met. She was very happy to hand me a card with her Boss ''s name on it.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'branch of bank of America is located at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(690,'10/03/2018','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Written notification about debt','I have been paying on this account for over 10 years and I feel I have paid to much. The original amount owed was {$20000.00}, and the agreed amount is {$11000.00} I''ve paid this debt amount down to $ XXXXThe monthly payment is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The amount of the loan was {$5000.00}. They didn''t explain to me about the high interest amount. I thought I had paid the full amount, but they turned this into a collection agency. The collection agency is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The original account number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the current account number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ill you please investigate this company to see if this is legal Thank You.','D. SCOTT CARRUTHERS',2.0,2.0,'the original amount owed was $20000.00. the agreed amount is $11000.00. the amount of the loan was $5000.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(691,'10/02/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Westlake Financial Services has placed false & incorrect information on my credit report, which I filed a dispute for with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
They reported payments made from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - XX/XX/2017 and no payments were ever made. The papers for the original loan were not completed until XX/XX/2017, how could payments be made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when the loan didn''t exist yet? Once the loan was processed with the paperwork by my son, not me and we left the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dealership the truck broke down and went through repairs over the next 3 weeks. My son was told, by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Manager ), what to say to the bank when they called him or else he would not be able to keep the truck, so he did 3 days after the purchase speak with the bank rep and told them what he was told to say ( which was written on his envelope by Manager ; Down Payment {$8500.00} ( which was not given, there was a trade in ) / Drivers : my son and me only & the truck runs good ) while the truck was in the shop with a " promise '''' all would be fixed. Over the next 3 weeks it was back at the dealership 4 times, the last time it was to be repaired locally, when we spoke with the dealership. After this the dealership closed down and disappeared when we tried to return the truck. The bank told us they have no title for the truck and they don''t want it because they can not do anything with it without a title and we informed the bank no payments would be made on the auto loan due to us being given false information and no proper repairs to the truck. This was when they told us they could do nothing with it and had numerous other auto loans from this dealer that they also had no titles for and would be processing a complaint and lawsuit against the dealership if they could find them. The first dealings with the bank about no longer wanting the truck, nor needing the loan was around XX/XX/2017, which was within the first 30 days of the paperwork being processed. The bank was also notified that we tried to return the truck to the dealership which was when we discovered they were gone from the site and no longer answered any calls on any numbers that we had. 
We do not have possession of the vehicle, no payments were ever made on the loan, I never signed anything for paperwork on this loan, the dealership Manager, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me I was not needed on the loan, but somehow I was added on the loan when the papers were signed electronically. The only thing that I signed was an We Owe document stating what the dealership agreed to repair on the truck as part of the loan agreement and a few other docs that the dealership explained were for their use only due to me being his parent and his first loan, but it would solely be his responsibility, not mine. Then he specifically told me when I asked that I didn''t have to be the cosigner on the loan and my son could be on the loan by himself. I did not sign loan documents ( My son has copies of the loan docs that he was given which will be attached ), therefore the bank should not be able to legally file anything on my credit report. Copies of documents referenced are attached to this complaint. 
Also, aside from that I feel that the fact is this bank is crooked and files false information on peoples credit reports like mine and my sons. I want this removed from my credit reports, all 3 bureaus. If I can not get this resolved without having to take legal action, my next step will be to pursue a law suit against Westlake Financial and anyone else involved in the false reporting of information to our credit reports therefore causing distress and excessive upfront costs due to the drop in credit scores and unable to proceed with certain other endeavors to improve our lives, ie .... Purchasing a vehicle that does run, purchasing a home, refinancing our home.','Westlake Services, LLC',2.0,4.0,'westlake financial services has placed false & incorrect information on credit report. they reported payments made from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - XX/X');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(692,'10/02/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Communication tactics','I have received multiple mailings and phone call ( s ) from First National Collection Bureau about a debt and have informed them over the phone and in writing to contact my attorney numerous times. Most recently I sent them a certified letter which I have receipt of being delivered on XX/XX/2018. 

As you can see from my incoming [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] phone log a phone call was again received on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from First National Collection Bureau. I informed them I had receipt of my certified letter informing them that I had retained an attorney years ago and that he should be contacted and I would contact the FTC, BBB and my WA State Attorney Office.','First National Collection Bureau, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'first national collection bureau has received multiple mailings and phone call. I have received a certified letter from First National Collection Bureau. they have received a certified letter and a call');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(693,'10/02/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Written notification about debt','I check my report often to make sure my information is reporting accurately. A few years ago, I was a victim of identity theft and had several accounts removed because someone fraudulently used my personal information. I received a notification from my credit monitoring service that an account has been listed on my credit reports. It is reporting under the company [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as a collection for {$270.00}. I have never heard of this company and have no idea who they are. I was never sent any notice or dunning letters in the mail, therefore I have not had a chance to dispute this inaccurate information before being placed on my report. This a violation of my rights and I want this account removed from my credit reports immediately!','CL HOLDINGS LLC',2.0,4.0,'a few years ago, i was a victim of identity theft and had several accounts removed. a credit monitoring service has not yet removed an account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(694,'10/02/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I re-financed my home in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and the loan has apparently been sold or transferred at least twice since. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I prepaid my property taxes due in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for federal income tax purposes. Based on instructions received from the broker who arranged the refinance and representatives of the first company that issued the refinance loan, I did not make escrow payments with the mortgage payment for 3 months. The amount of the property taxes was {$2500.00}. The monthly escrow payment is {$470.00}, indicating that a total of {$1400.00} for the 3 month period and, as a result, the escrow still has a surplus. 
I have been receiving past due notices and phone calls regarding this amount. I called the company to resolve the issue in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The customer service representative was unable to assist me and I asked to speak to a supervisor. The supervisor indicated that an analysis of the escrow account would be done and they would get back to me within 2 to 3 weeks but that has not been the case. I did, however, continue to receive past due notices and phone calls. I called again in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] andf was again told an analysis would be done but that has not been the case. The phone calls and past due notices continue. 
I called the company today and, when the customer service representative was unable to help me, I asked to speak to a manager or supervisor. I was put on hold for over 15 minutes before I hung up. 
I am concerned that this will adversely affect my credit despite the fact that I am up to date on my mortgage and have a surplus in my escrow asccount.','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,2.0,'re-financed home in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the loan has apparently been sold or transferred at least twice since.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(695,'10/02/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Incorrect information on your report','There was a change on my credit report with a company " lobel financial '''' the account was showing as a closed account and started reporting current with a balance increase after years of no change. I contacted lobel and asked to please send me an itemized bill and advised them that I did not receive documents for the sale of vehicle at the end of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I called they forward me to legal department and I spoke legal rep names [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated that this was turned over to a collection agency and I needed to call [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I called the number on a separate line is disconnected. I advised [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that and also told her it does not show a collection agency on my credit report. She said she doesnt know what to tell me. When I asked her why it was thousands more from the original loan amount and even after sale of a car and she said legal fees. I asked her what legal fees and she claimed for the attorney. Advised that there is no judgement so what did the attorney do and she refused to answer. She tried to give me a break down of the charges and amounts but what she told me was over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] less then what was being reported. I told her to please send me the documentation and she refused to take my address. I tried to give her my new address multiple times and she said she would not send me anything and hung up on me. I did contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after and advised them that lobel has refused to take my address. They were able to take my address and said will contact lobel directly to have them send me the documents that I legally have a right to. I also mailed and sent my request to lobel on XX/XX/2018 advising if they are unable to provide me with the documentation verify the debt and amount owed to remove this from my credit report. I still have not received in proof that this debt is owed. After the sale of the vehicle the balance should only reflect [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. What lobel is doing and how they treat consumers is completely unjust. As of today lobel has not removed this from my credit DESPITE me requesting documentation and writing a letter of dispute with no response. In fact the balance continues increase every month on my credit.','LOBEL FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a company called " lobel financial ''''s" contacted them and asked to send me an itemized bill. they told me that they did not receive documents for the sale');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(696,'10/02/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','According to the company ( Chase Bank ) some type of credit checking report was done with it''s current customers and at that time they deemed some customers " eligible '''' for an increase in interest rate. They stated that I got the best interest rate a credit card company could offer. So, my interest rate went from 12.74 % to % 16.49 %, doesn''t sound like a very good deal to me. When I called to discuss a double interest rate charge, I was told that I " qualified for the rate increase '''' and only after three separate phone calls I was finally told that the purchases I already had on the account prior to the increase were protected at the original 12.74 % rate and the new purchases were now being charged the new rate of 16.49 % rate. As the new rate was not my issue, I wasn''t too happy to hear that i was being billed two different interest rates. However, my concern was that the account was paid off in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so there was no longer a balance prior to the rate increase ( and purchases made XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and after should only be at the new rate not both ) but I still got hit with TWO finance charges!!!!

This is UNFAIR!!!! Their explanation and reason for the charges is totally unacceptable. If there is no balance on the account, HOW DO YOU CALCULATE INTEREST?????','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',4.0,4.0,'the company ( Chase Bank) says some customers were eligible for an interest rate increase. the company says that they deemed some customers eligible for an increase. the company says that they were');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(697,'10/01/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I reached out to this company and credit bureaus to inform them all that this account was open fraudulently. I sent them certified letters on XX/XX/2018, XX/XX/2018, 2018, and XX/XX/2018. It is now XX/XX/2018. I sent the PMAB LLC and all 3 credit bureaus a copy of my police report, ID, and my social security card. The companies has not responded to any of my letter directly, which is a direct violation of the fair credit reporting act.','PMAB,LLC',2.0,4.0,'the company and credit bureaus have not responded to any of my letters. the company has not responded to any of my letters directly.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(698,'10/01/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Getting a loan or lease','To whom it may concern, I purchased a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Colorado on XX/XX/2018. The salesperson, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], was extremely helpful and professional. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], one of the finance managers helped with the transaction during the sale and was also helpful. Although I did not agree with the amount of trade in value on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I accepted the deal and went on to sign paperwork with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in finance. 

This is where the issues started. I have an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit score and he showed me a rate of 6.6 % on a new vehicle. In the past, I''ve been in the low 3 % range and I couldn''t believe this rate. I asked him multiple times if this is the best rate possible and he stated Yes, it is. He kept saying that because I was upside down on the trade in, this is the best he could do. I had a feeling this was not the case. 

We then went on to discuss the aftermarket warranty. I let him know my Father in law was a Finance manager in MInnesota and I would go through him on the warranty. He then went on to say if I didn''t purchase this warranty now, it is not possible to get a warranty later, meaning you have to buy it now, and that you must purchase the warranty from the seller ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Again, I thought this was incorrect. Keep in mind, I always consult with my Father in Law about these things but it was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at night in Colorado and too late in MN. 

That being said, I went through with the purchase. I woke up multiple times overnight, which I rarely do, with a bad feeling. This was a bad deal and I got swindled. I called my Father in law in the morning and discussed the details. He was unhappy with the way this dealership operated, to say the least. 

I then called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to say I would be returning the vehicle because I was blatantly lied to multiple times in the sales process. I liked the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but the unethical nature I had the issue with. I calmed down a bit, and went through the details with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], another finance employee at the dealership. She apologized up and down, went in a got the rate down in the mid 4 ''s, which I was okay with. 

If I would not have called that day and explained my disappointment and unhappiness with the process, it would have cost me thousands of dollars in the long run. 

A car buying experience is stressful enough as it is. This blatant disregard for the truth is appalling and unacceptable. If I was lied to that easily, how many others have been lied to? 

I still think the deal is just okay and feel like I''ve lost money and am unhappy with the experience. 

But again, this is terrible business practice and I''m not so sure it''s limited to one person. Why would they feel comfortable about lying? [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was a young man with a lot to lose, so is this coming from the top, down? My gut says yes. 

This should absolutely be investigated and am also curious what they can do to make my experience with this dealership make me want to come back to do business again. I buy multiple cars every couple of years and at this point, and will never go back to this dealership for a car. 

As a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] myself, I operate with integrity and believe all people should. If I owned or managed this dealership, I would want to know about this.','Larry H. Miller Group of Companies',2.0,2.0,'a salesperson helped with the transaction during the sale. he was very helpful and professional. he was also helpful and helped with the transaction.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(699,'10/01/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Other transaction problem','Our business received an e-mail from PayPal today, XX/XX/18, stating that after investigation our account has been limited permanently and all funds will be held for 180 days. We are not to do business with them and we are to remove paypal from all of our selling sources. The reason given in the email was that we violated the acceptable use policy. In reading the acceptable use policy again we found that we did not violate any policy as all of our sales come from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] does not authorize any illegal activity. We called PayPal and spoke with a representative that could not give us a reason as he stated it was above his pay grade as well as his managers pay grade and the people I need to speak with do not answer phone calls but I needed to email [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to which I did. I have yet to receive a response as to the reason or the violation we did. Our funds are now being held and we have no reason from PayPal as to why.','PAYPAL HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,2.0,'PayPal received an e-mail from PayPal today, XX/XX/18. it stated that after investigation our account has been limited permanently. PayPal has no reason to remove');
