INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(731,'09/24/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I called PHH Mortgage Services, my mortgage servicer, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requesting to cancel my PMI since I am at 79 % on my loan to original loan value. They stated that they would send me the packet for cancelling PMI and it would be received at my house within 7 to 10 business days. As of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( 14 business days after my call ), I have still not received my packet. This is the second time I have tried to cancel PMI and both times they have slow played the process and used sketchy business practices to keep their PMI proceeds coming in. The first time was in the summer of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We purchased our house with 10 % down and then completed approximately {$40000.00} worth of renovations to the kitchen and flooring of our home that we purchased for {$180000.00}. In addition, the approved appraisal of our property used to close our mortgage loan in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was for {$230000.00}. After 2 years of on-time payments, I followed the process to remove PMI based on the argument that the money we had put into the house plus the equity we started with according to the appraisal they approved at closing brought us below 80 % of the home ''s value. As part of the process, we were required to allow an appraiser that they selected value our house to ensure that our loan balance was less than 80 % of the home ''s value. Shockingly, the appraiser they selected determined that our house had gone down in value from {$230000.00} at closing in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to {$200000.00} in the summer of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] even after we put {$40000.00} into renovations. The number that their appraiser came up with was mysteriously about {$4000.00} less than the value we needed for the home to be able to cancel PMI. I sent in a detailed report stating why I believed that his value of our home was incorrect and I was denied any kind of serious follow up from the mortgage servicer. PHH mortgage is clearly trying to use every trick in the books in order to keep their precious high margin PMI in place.','PHH Mortgage Services Corporation',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage servicer called a mortgage servicer on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requesting to cancel my PMI.');
