INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(735,'09/23/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have reached out to Experian several times, but with no success in them correcting my full credit report. Due to the fact that I was a victim of identity theft, I decided to have all credit bureaus to show my legal first and last name, and my current residence address only. Experian was sent on XX/XX/2018 a notarized copy of my utility bill, drivers license, and my social security card which shows [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my address [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When receiving my updated credit report Experian did as they wished not as I requested of them- under my legal right. You will find a copy of my police report where I reported identity theft, you will also find 2 copies of certified letters. 

The first certified letter requested the above, the second certified letter included the removal Again of all unnecessary names, addresses, date of birth, phone numbers which majority are incorrect anyway. Now they show a spouse or co-applicant on my report which is my daughters current name [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my deceased mother which neither is a co-applicant to anything I own. I did inform Experian on my first request to update their records that if it was not done in a timely manner I would move forward to report them not only to your establishment, but also to the Attorney General as well as the Better Business Bureau. I am not able to download my documentation but I am more than willing to have this information mailed to your establishment. 

Your help in this matter would certainly be appreciated. 

Thank you in advance, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian sent me a notarized copy of my utility bill, drivers license, and social security card. you will find a copy of my police report where I reported identity');
