INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(749,'09/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Hello CFPB. I am writing in regards to follow up case # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would like for Equifax to remove the {$230.00} collections from my credit file/report, as my original complaint requested because it does not belong to me. Also, It has been well over 40 days and Equifax still has not provided me with a status update of my complaint. I had reported that I had a fraud alert on my accountt due to identity theft and that the collections of {$230.00} is not mine ; and it''s the only collections on my report. Also, CFPB reported to me, by email that Equifax could not verify the account because it is a third party ; which I had also stated in my original complaint and that I have never had any dealings or accounts with that third party. They should not have been able to collect my personal information on my credit file from Equifax because of a fraud alert that I have on my report and Equifax still allowed that third party to inquire my account. Therefore, in addition to the above statements, they also broke the guidelines of the fraud alert/security freeze. Again, I would like for Equifax to remove the collections of {$230.00} from my credit file/report.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'CFPB reported to me that Equifax could not verify the account because it is a third party. CFPB said that they should not have been able to collect personal information');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(750,'09/20/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I made correct and full mortgage payments to Freedom Mortgage for XX/XX/2018, and XX/XX/2018, a day apart. The XX/XX/2018 payment was 10 days in ADVANCE of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] due date. I made clear this was a payment in advance and NOT to pay to principal. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Freedom Mortgage contacts me about a missing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. I explained it was paid in advance, but the rep said it was returned for insufficient funds. My bank balance shows 1 ) the payment was NOT returned, 2 ) the funds were absolutely sufficient with tremendous excess, and 3 ) my bank did not charge me any fees for insufficient funds because no payments were returned. 

I took that opportunity to pay XX/XX/2018 and XX/XX/2018 payments again in ADVANCE because I didn''t want to bothered until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Both those payments were withdrawn from my bank and credited to my mortgage. 

A few days later, I get another call from Freedom Mortgage demanding my XX/XX/2018. I have paid 4 ( FOUR ) months of mortgage in full and correct amounts for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and we aren''t even past XX/XX/2018 yet. 

My bank provided me a letter from the branch manager on bank letterhead, dated XX/XX/2018, confirming all four payments were made and nothing was returned for insufficient funds. 

I provided several times the bank letter and a complete ledger of my bank history showing all the payments made and nothing returned. I made the XX/XX/2018 payment around XX/XX/2018, and Freedom Mortgage is demanding my XX/XX/2018 payment. The mortgage principal balance also shows no money accidentally went to principal. 

On XX/XX/2018, I gave Freedom Mortgage the ultimatum : they have all the information needed to determine that I made now 5 payments and the error is on their side for the missing payment, if this is error isn''t corrected immediately, I will lodge disputes with all three credit bureaus and retain an attorney to drive this matter to conclusion in court. Freedom Mortgage said they are still investigating and would have an outcome by XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that was in 2 more days. So I waited 2 days, and 2 days have passed. 

Today is XX/XX/2018, and I still don''t have a resolution. Freedom Mortgage now says the new date is XX/XX/2018. That was the wrong response. Therefore, I have filed disputes with all 3 credit bureaus and provided the same supporting information to the bureaus. I have retained an attorney, and we''ll see where that goes too.

I have been going back and forth with Freedom Mortgage for over four months about the XX/XX/2018 payment that they lost. They have billed me late charges. They have posted fraudulent lates against our credit at the credit bureaus. It''s clear they lost my payment. Freedom Mortgage knows it''s lost, and they can''t figure out where it went. I have recorded all the phone calls with Freedom Mortgage, so that information is available to the attorney as well. While Freedom Mortgage is still trying to figure it, I am continuing to accrue late fees and continuing to get hit with false lates on my credit.','FREEDOM MORTGAGE COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'XX/XX/2018 payment was 10 days in ADVANCE of the due date. XX/XX/2018 payment was paid in advance and NOT to pay to principal');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(751,'09/19/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I defaulted on three private student loans ( SallieMae through Navient ) in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was contacted by a debt collector ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and negotiated a settlement on one of those loans. I am currently negotiating with the same debt collector on the other two. I checked my account balance at Navient ''s website and the loan I negotiated a settlement for over six months ago still appears as due with a balance. Worried that I may have negotiated with the wrong party I contacted Navient and was informed that they do not update information for " delinquent '''' loans. The operator then identified a different debt collector than the one I negotiated with for the loan and question and could not answer my questions about the legitimacy of the company I was bargaining with. When I questioned how I, as a consumer, am supposed to make informed decisions about my finances when the company that services my loans will not give me accurate information the operator repeated that this was their policy. I have two lawsuits against me by a debt collector that Navient does not identify as the legitimate debt collector for my loan. What am I to do?','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a debt collector negotiated a settlement on one of those loans. he negotiated a settlement on one of those loans. he is currently negotiating with the same');
