INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(753,'09/19/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','In XX/XX/2018 under reference numberXXXX I applied for a credit card account with Chase. I was notified by chase that they needed verification of my identity so I sent them a copy of my Florida drivers license and social security card. I even called Chase to verify receipt of those items. I explained to Chase that I recently sold my home on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Florida and bought a new home on the beach in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Florida. I informed Chase that this information could be verified through the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Property Apprasierss Office for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] address and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Property Office for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( new ) address. Chase ignored all information provided to them and lowered my credit score with their inquiries. Chase then sent a letter to my old address even though they were given proof of my new address. This is NOT my first run in with Chase in applying for a credit account. Chase has a strong history of discrimination and violating the Consumer Credit Protection Act. I have several files on this. I applied with Chase about four years ago and they discriminated against me back then while they were accepting government bail outs and building new bank branches all over the USA with that bail out money. I applied for an interest free card with them recently. I can be reached at my home address of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Florida [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or you can contact me directly at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or you can write to me at my p.o. box at p.o. box [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Florida [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. All of this information is ON my credit report and available to Chase. Chase has a history of discriminatory practices related to me and will result in federal litigation being filed against them. But first decided to contact this agency first.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'in XX/XX/2018 under reference numberXXXXX I applied for a credit card account with Chase. I was notified by chase that they needed verification of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(754,'09/19/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act and the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, credit bureaus and credit reporting agencies have an obligation to investigate and remove erroneous information from a consumers credit report. In XX/XX/2018, I submitted an online dispute on Experian website through their Dispute Center to have specific accounts removed that I believe were placed in error. Among those were, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a notification via Experian ''s dispute center stating the accounts had been verified. They did not however, provide me with any supporting documentation or original contract bearing my signature proving I had a contractual obligation to pay the debts in question. Therefore, the accounts had not been verified. On XX/XX/2018, I sent a follow up letter via certified mail to Experian requesting the documentation for the accounts they previously claimed had been verified. Rather than providing documentation, I was sent a letter stating, " We have previously processed this dispute and the credit grantor has verified its accuracy '''' and that they " ... will not reinvestigate this information again. '''' By not providing documentation and refusing to " reinvestigate '''', Experian is in direct violate of my rights as a consumer.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'credit bureaus and credit reporting agencies have an obligation to investigate and remove erroneous information from a consumers credit report. a dispute on Experian website was filed ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(755,'09/19/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I have contacted the company on several times, requesting them to validate accounts that they are saying are mines. However, the company has sent me duplicates of billing statements in an event to validate the accounts. This is not proof that the debts are indeed mines. In order to resolve these accounts, I need the company to verify these accounts by providing a signed contract.','CAVALRY INVESTMENTS, LLC',2.0,2.0,'the company has sent me duplicates of billing statements to validate accounts. this is not proof that the debts are mines.');
