This was clearly an error on the part of HSBC, but HSBC will not take responsibility. I have been harmed by their negligence and fraud, whether intentional or random. HSBC should refund the {$72.00} fee to me and can do so by depositing that amount into my account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It is irresponsible that HSBC will not simply fix the problem that they have caused.

Following is a excerpt from my CHAT with HSBC where I attempting, however futile, to resolve this issue with the company ; Why did HSBC continue to take transfer after transfer after they already had the {$100000.00} transfer completed? 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : The initial transfers were not successful, so this would be why there were multiple transfers initiated. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : The initial transfer WAS SUCCESSFUL and {$100000.00} went to HSBC [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : HSBC had already received the {$100000.00} but continued to make withdraw attempts again and again [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : The initial transfer was not successful this is why there are multiple transactions.The transfer that was successful was the transfer on XX/XX/18. Which is the last transfer from the information of transactions you provided and the transfer that shows on the HSBC account transaction history. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : On my HSBC account Online information it shows the HSBC account was funded on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : Again my apologies for the inconvenience. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : XX/XX/2018 ACH WEBSINGLE [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] HSBC ONLINE TRANSFER {$100000.00} - {$77000.00} XX/XX/2018 ACH WEBSINGLE [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] HSBC BANK ACCT FUND {$100000.00} {$22000.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : Above shows HSBC taking 2 withdraws on the same date at the same time [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : The account was funded on XX/XX/18 and the only transaction in the transaction history is on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. If you are referring to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account I would not be able to validate that. Again my apologies for your experience. Is there anything else I can assist with today?','HSBC NORTH AMERICA HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,4.0,'HSBC made multiple transfer requests for $100000.00 instead of just one request. HSBC made multiple transfer requests for $100000.00 instead of');
