INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(770,'09/15/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have contacted Experiann several times via phone online, and via first class mailings on many occasions in regards to several accounts that were placed in my name that did not belong to me and that I did not authorize or was not familiar with. I get the same results and I have had it, It makes it look very bad on my credit report, and reporting negatively. I am trying to refinance something on my credit report and it makes it difficult when theyre checking credit, and I have negative accounts that does not belong to me reporting inaccurately. I have disputed and reach out to Experian several times and they say the same thing over and over, The companies either need to send proof or validation or it needs to be removed. This account does not belong to me. I''ve done the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Identity Report [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I''ve called and they''ve told me that their handling it and they received proper paperwork and I should see an update and I never do. The last rep I talked to stated she was in special handling, I haven''t had any luck with this. the following accounts that are reporting are : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] acct [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] acct [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] acct [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I file a complaint they instruct me to file dispute with them directly which I do just to keep getting the same results. I have even sent copies from Experian & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] showing that they deleted items that Experian keeps saying verified. How can they all be using the same information but some bureaus are correcting items