INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(775,'09/14/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','Over a year ago I embarked on a journey of cleaning up my credit in preparation of buying a house. I was one of those people ( in my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) that wasnt particularly savvy about checking my credit or how to increase it. So I started getting familiar with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and thats when I noticed two accounts that were in my name that werent mine. One was a credit card through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and another was with something called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a whopping {$1300.00}. Even though I wasnt credit savvy, I at least knew that I did not own any kind of credit cards during the time these accounts were opened. I disputed them through the online application with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the filed it for me. Within a month [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent me a full report about the details on the account that was opened- and I was able to discover it was an account opened up in my name online and delivered to an address I used to live with my ex-girlfriend- which she actually still lived at. It was then pretty obvious by the fact that all these transactions were cash advances until the card was maxed- that it must have been her doing this. We broke up on very bad terms and unfortunately she knew all of my personal information. So I filed a police report and sent the report to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I never received anything from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   though but it was marked as disputed on my credit file. For a year that has been the last of it and I moved on. Fast forward to now- Im in the process of buying a house and these two disputes are still on file. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they apologized and handled it without any troubles. The only number I had to contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was the credit agency they were working with- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I thought maybe they also needed a police report if it looks like the fraud started in the same place. So I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] yesterday- explained my situation and that I was a victim of identity theft that was discovered a year ago- and that I disputed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but needed more details in case I needed to also file a police report with my dispute. The man I spoke with was beyond rude- and spoke to me in a way I could not believe. He said he thought it was an account I opened up- ran up- and just forgot about- and that he doubted it was identity theft because whomever opened the account had made a few payments. All he would tell me is that it was with something [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and when it was opened. When I said that I dont just open accounts and forget about them- that I have a perfect payment history with three credit cards that I now have- his response continued to be rude. I explained that I didnt even know what [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  was- and that Identity theft can indeed include an ex girlfriend who opened up an account fraudulently in my name and was using it. His exact words were, What I think is going on is that youre trying to buy a house and you need this off your report so youre just trying to make up a police report to make your dispute seem legitimate. I couldnt believe what I was hearing. I reminded him that falsely making a police report was a crime- and I wouldnt be doing it unless it was legitimate. I told him I would be filing- and also filing a complaint against his company. His response? Go on ahead but this will stay on your credit report forever. I have since filed a police report in regards to the fraudulent account- and would like it known that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is horrible to work with.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',4.0,6.0,'a year ago, I began cleaning up my credit in preparation of buying a house. I disputed two accounts that were in my name that weren''t mine. one was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(776,'09/14/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Struggling to repay your loan','I have parent loans with Navient. I became [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They kept talking me into forbearance instead of income payment plan based on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and now my loan is so high I will never be able to pay it back.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'I became [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and now my loan is so high I will never be able to pay back it back.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(777,'09/13/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','In early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called the bank to request an increase on my existing {$300.00} limit U.S Bank credit card that I have managed well since 2012. I had very good credit in which I have been building for many years. 
I requested a {$1200.00} increase through a phone conversation with US Bank Customer Service Employee, which would make my available line of credit {$1500.00} total. About a week later, I received a denial letter from the bank for my credit line increase request. 
Each month when I would go into the bank, to pay the balance on my {$300.00} limit US Bank credit card, the bank teller would inform me I wasn''t earning any reward points on my existing card. So, a few weeks after I got the denial letter when I visited the local branch, like usual, the teller informed me that I wasn''t earning points. So I said, Okay how do I go ahead and get enrolled in points? ( Thinking I might as well get something out of my card if I am going to use it ) So that day, I believed I had been enrolled in getting points. A few weeks later, I went online to select my categories in order to earn a certain percentage back on each purchase. Only to discover that I had two available lines of credit open. One was my {$300.00} card and another was for {$6500.00}! Outside of my own knowledge, the US Bank employee had me sign on the electronic signature box for what I was explained to be credit card points, but turned out to be a credit card. When I set up a meeting with the branch manager, she was unable to do anything about the situation and could not explain to me how I was denied a {$1200.00} increase, but approved {$6500.00} on a new line only weeks later. I was told, by the US Bank branch manager, that US Bank employee received commission from me signing for the credit card that day. The manager informed me the teller signed me up for one of my pre-qualified offers. However, no offer was discussed with me that day, which also goes to show I did not know what I was signing up for. My best guess would be that with my good credit and standing with the bank that I had many offers and he picked the highest one without discussing them with me. The bank manager was unable to answer if I had other offers available and the only explanation was she felt that was the best one. However, it has a very high interest rate and I believe the line of credit is too high and put a huge ding on my credit score. It is just unfortunate that a commission driven employee is able to get away with a scam on a loyal US Bank customer.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a week later, a denial letter from the bank for my credit line increase request was sent. the bank employee had me sign on the electronic signature box for what I was explained');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(778,'09/13/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','For the last few months there has was not payment due there was all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] nor minimum payment all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I began making payments on my own in XX/XX/2018 for {$50.00} then another payment [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$41.00}. When I saw a payment due for {$17.00} for the end of this month on XX/XX/2018 I call and enquired. I was told I did not make a payment this month and that I had to pay. I was upset as each time I call I get a representative with a smart mouth. The representatives talk to me like I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as though I can not add or subtract and I by no means know what I am talking about. I have before tired of the insults. I have proof that I paid when I said I paid and I wish I would have captured a screen shot of the PenFed account page as further proof but it is long gone. ( see attached transfer to PenFed from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 

In addition I believe PenFed owes me transfer fees for the transfers made to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. There were several delays in transferring the money to pay off the high interest rate card and the INTEREST CONTINUED to ACCRUE for MONTHS, by the time the transfer was completed I had secured funds from another financial institution. I believe it is around {$430.00} PenFed owes me. I am positive there should be notation on this account regarding a three way conference call with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or XX/XX/2018. If not I am positive [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has this information. The delays in transfer cost me and it appearing this issue with this account is proof as to why there were disturbances within PenFed system. The last representative I spoke said you was behind. My thought is why should I be subjected to these frustrations because of PenFed system issues?','PENTAGON FEDERAL CREDIT UNION',2.0,2.0,'a payment due for $17.00 was due for the end of this month on XX/XX/2018. the payments were delayed and the transfer was completed ');
