INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(780,'09/13/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','This complaint is submitted by counsel as attorney for the complainant at his request. Complainant is a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-year old double leg amputee and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] veteran. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], complainant had his checking account with Synovus Bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] On that day, he visited a Synovus Bank branch and informed it of numerous unauthorized debit card transactions in his account. He was told the bank would fix it, asked not to close his account, and to make a police report. Complainant did so, making a full report to a police officer at the branch the next day. Complainant was not told of anything else he needed to do and believed the matter would be resolved by Synovus. Complainant visited the branch two more times to check on the matter. Each time he was told the bank would be telephoning him. It never did. 

Still having no word from Synovus, in early XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], complainant again visited the branch. He was told he had never disputed the unauthorized transactions, that he had to fill out the written form and that he could not recover anything for charges older than sixty days from that date. Synovus therefore denied complainant recovery for the month of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the month which had the highest amount of unauthorized charges. 

Synovus subsequently recredited {$2200.00} to complainant, but complainant has still lost over {$23000.00}, which Synovus refuses to recredit.

Additionally, complainant by letter to Synovus on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requested it to provide him with information and clarification pursuant to 12 CFR 205 et. seq. on : ( 1 ) All EFTs in issue from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to the present for which Synovus failed to recredit complainants account ; and ( 2 ) All EFTs in the same period the investigation of which Synovus closed for alleged lack of information. Synovus has made no response to these requests.

Synovus conduct above violates Regulation E.','Synovus Bank',2.0,4.0,'complaint is submitted by counsel as attorney for the complainant. complaint is submitted by counsel as attorney for the complainant. complaint is filed by counsel as attorney for the complainant.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(781,'09/13/2018','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Installment loan','Getting the loan','Around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I took out a {$2500.00} loan with a company online called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Their website left the impression that they were legally able to operate in the state of Hawaii and that they operated in accordance with the SCRA and MLA. All monthly payments were made. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I took out another loan with them for {$3000.00} at a 32.78 % interest. I combined my monthly payments for the two loans ( monthly payment : {$240.00} ) but the two accounts were still open. Fast forward to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when my last payment was made to them. I had some financial troubles as well as issues with my debit account. I do some research on lending laws and practices. I find out that the state I reside in- Hawaii- requires lenders to not only be licensed to do business in that state but also caps the interest rate at 24 %. I also find out that the MLA doesnt allow loan rollovers. I send an email to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] questioning the legality of the loan. I receive no response back but on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I receive a missed call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I return the call at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Im told by Mr. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my account representative, that I have a past due balance of around {$1600.00} and that my account will be charged off if I dont make a payment by the end of the month reflecting negatively on my credit. I set up a payment with him. I then begin to question him on the legality of the loan and he responds by listing the companys credentials and that any matter pertaining to the companys legality is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I then ask for the Lending Agreement. He responds by saying I can either email the company my authorization to email the documents or check online in the Documents section of My account. I head to my account and none of the Lending Documents are there only the updated Privacy Act. I also see that my original loan of {$2500.00} has been closed without my knowledge and appeared to have been refinanced without my knowledge. I call Mr [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] back to inquire about the lending documents. When I told him the only Documents that appeared was the Privacy Act, he responded with what more do you need then? He then proceeded to read of the loan details but made no attempt to send me the loan agreement. Only after calling him a fifth time did he give me the email contact so I could email the authorization but have no exact time frame of when Id receive a response. I am currently waiting for response as well as seeking legal advice.','MIDCOUNTRY FINANCIAL CORP',2.0,2.0,'a company online called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] took out a $2500.00 loan. they were legally able to operate in the state');
