INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(810,'09/06/2018','Mortgage','Home equity loan or line of credit (HELOC)','Struggling to pay mortgage','I modified my 1st loan in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through the Department Of Justice settlement due to loss of income. It took several years to obtain the modification. I was told that my 2nd lien ( home equity line ) had been charged off and forgiven " liquidated ''''. My first lien was lowered to the current market value. I have not received any correspondence from the 2nd lien holder for the past 5 years nor has the 2nd lien been reported on my credit report. Earlier this year I obtained a home equity line through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We assumed that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  was in 2nd position. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I learned that a NOD and Election to Sell had been recorded against my property. I was not properly served. The assignment from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is fraudulent. That assignment was allegedly notarized in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but not recorded until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  was not affiliated with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. SLS, the servicer for the 2nd, won''t release any documents to me. I have requested a copy of the letter that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent to me stating my loan had been charged off and liquidated. Furthermore, I was provided a document showing that I had modified the 2nd in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that my balance had increased from {$95000.00} to {$220000.00} in less than 2 years. This is not my signature on the document and how could an equity line increase that much in less than 2 years. The clock is ticking and I am not getting any explanation from the 2nd lien holder. See attached letter.','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,4.0,'a loan modification was made in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the 2nd lien holder has not received any correspondence from the 2nd lien holder ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(811,'09/06/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','USAA randomly chooses to hold credit card payments for up to ten days. The is the second time I have had my payment held. This time, my high utilization affected my credit score even though I made the payment.

I have called and asked three different representatives who have given me three different answers. One told me I have to sign up for a bank account to get rid of the issue. One told me that they as a company were not able to control the algorithms that withhold payments. And the last one told me that the federal reserve was the reason why they would not credit my account with my payment.

It is part of the terms of agreement that they can hold payments for up to ten days. But now they are implementing this more frequently. That, and they will not give me a reason as to why. I have had the credit account for more than 6 years and used the same bank account to make payments on this card. It is only recently that they have started implementing this hold.

I do find it necessary to file this complaint because it is an abusive policy written in the fine print. If I knew they would do this I never would have begun doing business with USAA. I have no idea whether USAA will withhold my assets from me and for how long when I use my card, it causes all sorts of problems with automatic bill pay. For those who are less financially stable, putting a ten day hold on a payment could be very difficult.

Thank you','UNITED SERVICES AUTOMOBILE ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a credit card payment held by USAA is the second time I have had my payment held. the federal reserve is the reason why they would not credit my account with my payment.');
