INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(824,'09/04/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','My husband used Wells Fargos [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] application on Friday XX/XX/2018 to transfer {$1300.00} to my checking account. It said that there was an error and funds could not be transferred, but {$1300.00} disappeared out of his account. He called immediately and was told that they would open a claim for him, but that the issue should be resolved within an hour. 

It took over 24 hours for the {$1300.00} to show up as a pending transfer in his account, but there was still no notice on my account and the money was still missing. He called again on Monday XX/XX/2018 and was told that they could open another claim and that they would expedite the money into my account the following day as the status of this transfer in his account now showed that the funds had been transferred. 

I called on Tuesday XX/XX/2018 as the {$1300.00} had yet to show up on my account. The first person told me it would take 14 business days for my husband to receive the money back to his account. The second person I spoke to was part of the online customer service team and told me it could take up to 10 business days for my claim to be resolved. I asked to speak to a Supervisor ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) who told me there was nothing they could do and I could file a complaint. She was extremely rude. I informed her that a check I wrote for rent would most likely bounce and that I was late in paying 3 bills because of this issue and she said there was nothing she could do about it because they didnt know when the issue would be resolved and if I was upset, I could file a complaint. 

Lastly, I was transferred to the complaint department. I was told that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was an executive and she had the authority to tell me that the money would arrive in my account by the next day. She also said she would request that Wells Fargo look into covering late fees and bounced check fees. I asked her why they were not able to put the money into my account because it is a documentation glitch and our money should still be physically available to us and she said she wished the same thing as she was also dealing with this personally. I told her I felt that Wells Fargo has essentially robbed us as they were withholding our money. 

And now, we wait again after another conversation with Wells Fargo and prior empty promises to see if we recover our {$1300.00} tomorrow. We will be closing our accounts and banking elsewhere as soon as this is resolved.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'$1300.00 disappeared from his account on friday. he called immediately and was told they would open a claim for him. the money was still missing and it');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(825,'09/03/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Exeter finance states that on XX/XX/2017 I applied for a loan which I never did. There are hard inquiries on my credit reports with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called Exeter finance and they stated there were no accounts under my name and they wouldn''t take this fraudulent hard inquirie information off my credit reports.','EXETER FINANCE CORP.',2.0,4.0,'Exeter finance states that on XX/XX/2017 I applied for a loan. there are hard inquiries on my credit reports with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(826,'09/03/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I received a correspondence from a company I do not recognize ever having done any business with nor have I enter into any contracts with KENNETH , EISEN & ASSOCIATES , LTD . I have never receive any notification 30 days prior to being reported to the credit bureau. I fail to receive any documentation showing any transfer title of ownership between from the original creditor to KENNETH, EISEN & ASSOCIATES , LTD. under Ohio Revised Code Title [ 13 ] XIII COMMERCIAL TRANSACTIONS - OHIO UNIFORM COMMERCIAL CODE Chapter 1319.12 Taking assignment of debts, I fail to see anything that would show they are in compliance with OHIO LAW.I declare Myself competent. I am not a Corporation or a Public Entity.As proof of claim, complete the attached CREDITOR DISCLOSURE STATEMENT and return within 15 days. Failure to respond with the completed CREDITOR DISCLOSURE STATEMENT, thereby providing your verified Proof of Claim, signed under the Penalties of Perjury and verified by your affidavit, you, KENNETH, EISEN & ASSOCIATES, LTD. are agreeing to your Commercial Dishonor, exhausting My Administrative Remedies. I will accept your Silence as an Acceptance, and your agreement that a Default be entered against you. You will also agree to a Full Tacit Contractual Agreement being a participant in Fraud and to forfeit all remedies under Administrative Law, Judicial Law, and / or MARITIME CLAIM RULES C ( 6 ). You should also be aware that sending unsubstantiated demands for payment through the United States Mail System might constitute mail fraud under federal and state law Your failure to satisfy this request within the requirements of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act will be construed as your absolute waiver of any and all claims against me, and your tacit agreement to compensate me for costs and attorney fees.','Kenneth, Eisen & Associates, Ltd.',2.0,4.0,'KENNETH, EISEN & ASSOCIATES, LTD. has never received any notification 30 days prior to being reported to the credit bureau. a company that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(827,'09/03/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','I apply for a credit card with capital one I have excellent credit and my credit score is almost 800 And I have sufficient income to apply for the credit card. for some unknown reason they declined my application I believe that my application was denied because of my race and national origin since there were no other reason given for my denial thank you.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'i have a credit score of almost 800 and my credit score is almost 800. my application was denied because of my race and national origin.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(828,'09/02/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','I was told I qualified for a {$50.00} credit on my purchase if I applied for a Lowe ''s credit card and was accepted, so I applied. I was denied and told, in public, in front of my daughter that I was denied. I asked if I would receive a letter. I was told " yes ''''. I paid for my purchase and immediately checked my credit score because I feared fraud. My credit score was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

One week later, I called Lowe ''s to find out why I had not received an explanation ; they told me I had not been denied and that all applications were routinely placed on hold. I asked for a supervisor and I was then transferred to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I asked for a supervisor again and was placed on hold again ; after waiting 5 minutes I was asked if I minded continuing to hold ; I replied " no '''' I did not mind. They then hung up. 

I called back and opened a Lowe ''s Incident # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; I was then transferred to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] again. 

I asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a reasonable explanation for why my application was " denied '''' originally and received none. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said my application was incomplete but did not require any additional information when he approved it, so that was a lie. He also said I will receive a {$50.00} credit on my 1st purchase. 

I found this entire process misleading and embarrassing in the extreme. I was on the phone over 40 minutes resolving it.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,4.0,'I was denied and asked if I would receive a letter. I was told " yes ''''. I paid for my purchase and immediately checked my credit score.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(829,'09/02/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I took out parent Plus loans for my children. A total of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] With the first disbursement of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the last disbursement of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have made repeated attempts over the last several years at getting an income driven payment plan but each and every time I speak to the loan servicing company they tell me one thing then the next thing I know they are capitalizing interest to the tune of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over the last three years. I did not agree to this, I did not ask for a forbearance or deferment. I am only willing to payback the principal I took out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I will not pay any more. I have a feeling these loan servicing agents are getting compensated by causing my loan balance to increase instead of helping me make an affordable payment plan to reduce my principal. I know the Department of Justice is aware of Navients unscrupulous practices and I refuse to be another one of their victims! I am more than willing to refinance the original loan principal amount with a respectable financial service company.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'parent Plus loans for my children were disbursed. a total of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with the first disbursement of [COMPTE');
