INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(843,'08/29/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','I made a one-time payment to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] online on Sat. XX/XX/2018 for {$140.00} and another one-time payment to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bank for {$37.00}. At the time there was more than enough to pay both bills. On Wednesday, XX/XX/2018 a check cleared for {$510.00} ; which I did not have enough to cover. I received a notice by Chase Bank that my account was overdrawn at XX/XX/2018 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However, instead of 1 overdraft fee, I received 2 overdraft fees and 1 returned payment fee on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Each fee was {$34.00} for a total of {$100.00} on overdraft fees. 
I contacted Chase Bank on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to ask why there was not 1, but 2 overdraft fees and 1 return payment fee, since I have opted out of overdraft protection and there was only 1 item paid that day. I was told by a supervisor named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Ohio office that all business transactions paid on the weekend are paid the next business day. This made no sense as the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment was returned on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], not XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and according to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment was made on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].  Moreover, the next business day was MondayXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], not the XX/XX/XXXXt. Not getting any satisfaction and being told he could not reverse the 1 overdraft fees and the 1 returned payment fee, I insisted on speaking to a manager named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from the same office. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] confirmed XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was not a bank holiday and gave me a completely different reason for the extra overdraft and returned payment fee. He explained that Chase Bank doesnt process payments necessarily as they come in and that they cash checks & purchases from the highest to the lowest, when they do decide to process payments. Even if this information was correct, which it was not, I asked the manager, "  then why were any payments made on the 2 lowest charges if I did not have overdraft protection and if there was no funds in the checking account? '''' I was told that since I make payments every month, they decided to charge the accounts as recurring, auto-pays although I made a 1 time payment. According to the manager any purchase made monthly irrelevant of the day and amount is considered a recurring payment. This is ridiculous. If I buy pizza every month from the local Pizzeria, go food shopping to the same local supermarket every month, or make monthly purchases on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], they, too would be considered a recurring payment. Actually, everything I was told was ridiculous and doesn''t correlate to the evidence at hand. Payments were made or returned on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the check which caused the overdraft didn''t bounce until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After spending 53 minutes, I was told there was no superior above [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that no one could remove these charges period. Since phone calls are monitored, this information can be easily retrieved. 
I have no issue with the {$34.00} overdraft fee charged for the {$510.00}. I was hospitalized and could not pickup & deposit the check necessary to cover the check. However, I should not have been charged an overdraft fee for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment and a returned payment fee for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank because of manipulation and fraud. 

I have enclosed a copy of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill with date of payment and also my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill which clearly shows I am not enrolled in auto pay. Plus a copy of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement and Chase email.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a check cleared for $510.00 on XX/XX/2018. a supervisor told me that all business transactions paid on the weekend are paid the next business');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(844,'08/29/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I was promised by several representatives from Ally Financial Auto Loan Department that they were able to remove late payments from Ally Financial. It never occurred and I''ve also sent goodwill letters hoping they would follow through. Again, nothing ever happened. My payments have been current for the past nine months. One of the representative that I spoke to name is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/2018, reference # : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','ALLY FINANCIAL INC.',2.0,2.0,'ally financial auto loan department representatives promised to remove late payments. it never occurred and I''ve sent goodwill letters hoping they would follow through.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(845,'08/29/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ran my credit without authorization me between XX/XX/2018 - XX/XX/2018 contact the company they dont know who ran my credit','EXPERT GLOBAL SOLUTIONS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ran my credit without authorization me between XX/XX/2018 - XX/XX/2018 contact the company they dont');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(846,'08/29/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Communication tactics','Getting repeated/frequent calls from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number. Finally answered today. A lady stating she was from RCS in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Ohio asked if I was " my name '''' and I told her yes. Then she wanted me to verify my address and wanted to verify my date of birth. All she would tell me is she was from RCS in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Kept pressuring me for the information. I told her I don''t give out personal info on phone to strangers. She kept insisting and wouldn''t tell me what it was concerning. I told her to try someone else and hung up. I searched RCS in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and found a Regional Collection Services in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Ohio. Since I am not past due on anything I owe I am not concerned and thought I should submit this. Thank you.','Regional Collection Services, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a lady stating she was from RCS in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Ohio asked if I was " my name '''' and she asked her yes');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(847,'08/29/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I protested [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charges appearing on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] First Bankcard [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Still unresolved are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of those initial [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] protests ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] being a charge by an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] store in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$1500.00} and the second was a charge from Hot Leathers of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$55.00}. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a letter by regular mail requesting additional information on the disputes and I replied immediately, sending all the requested documentation. I know they received this information in a timely fashion because they acted on all of the protests in my initial request except for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mentioned above. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I returned home from work at approximately [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and found a message on my answering machine telling me I had to immediately call dispute resolutions back at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to discuss dispute # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and the message went on to say today was the last day. I immediately called the number given only to get a recorded message saying they had " left for the day ''''. There was no alternative offered by the recording : no voice mail, no email, no way to advise that I returned the call. I tried calling again each day over the weekend but got the same recording. On Monday morning, I stayed home from work and called in first thing and spoke with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at Billing Resolutions. I explained that I sent all the required paperwork along with paperwork on ALL the protests made in my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter, and she acknowledged that they HAD received paperwork on the other protests but insisted they had not received the paperwork on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] protest. ALL of the paperwork went in a single envelope ( why on earth would I send multiple/separate mailings to the same place? ) I asked her how someone is supposed to respond to a previously unknown deadline given on voicemail at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on a Friday afternoon when they shut the phones off with no way to leave a message at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? She offered no explanation or resolution to that and she could not explain why they got the paperwork on all the protests but somehow didnt get the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] paperwork. Regardless, I IMMEDIATELY sent her another complete PDF copy of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] protest paperwork by email and then doubled back and confirmed that she received it. Despite the fact that it was clear that they somehow misplaced the original [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] paperwork, she was reluctant to do anything to help me, using the missed deadline and also saying it was a point of sale transaction, and left me saying she would look into it. When she used the " point of sale '''' excuse, I requested a copy of the credit card receipt ( backed up he request in writing ) with my signature which they did not produce. In a response to an earlier complaint made, they acknowledged that they tried, TWICE to contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding this purchase but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DID NOT RESPOND. The fact that there was no credit card receipt, no signature and NO REPLY OR COUNTER FROM [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to their request for supporting information on the charge should confirm the protest was legitimate yet they refuse to issue the credit to my account. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I sent a letter to the CEO of First National Bank of Omaha explaining in detail the problem and I included a check as payment in full for all legitimate charges outstanding and my cards ( cut in two ) demanding that the account be closed immediately. I know they got the correspondence because the cancelled check shows being processed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Yet on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], DESPITE THE FACT THAT THE ACCOUNT SHOULD HAVE BEEN CLOSED, they posted yet ANOTHER fraudulent charge to my account totaling {$1100.00}. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) Clearly First Bankcard/First National Bank of Omaha has serious issues with the ability to process mail received with any accuracy or in any timely fashion. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received another letter advising they were rejecting my protest on the second dispute listed above ( Hot Leathers of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ) for {$55.00}, despite the fact that the charge dates back to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the " resolution '''' comes over 90 days since protested in writing. Even more troubling, the reasons cited for the rejection of the protest include 1 ) ) at the time, I had informed VISA that I would be traveling through the " area '''' where the merchant is located in. During that time, we took a trip from upstate [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the copy of the credit card receipt included CLEARLY shows the vendor is in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which was nowhere near our travel route, not to mention the receipt has NO signature, has NO 3 digit card security code and NO expiration date. shows the vendor this explanation makes NO sense in that this charge is from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I was no where near [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  any time in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 2 ) at the time, I was in constant contact with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which is true because, despite the fact that we had notified them of our travel plans ( and all charges on the card were paid in full ), [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] still put repeated holds on the account, which hampered [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] LEGITIMATE charges and created significant delays, embarrassment and frustrations, with VISAs repeated excuse for shutting the card off being " suspected fraudulent activity ''''. Amusingly, they hampered [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] legitimate charges but missed the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge that was genuinely fraudulent. 3 ) VISA somehow determined the card was physically present during this charge and that other valid card transactions occurred after this charge, yet the only evidence they sent was a receipt showing a purchase made in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], ( when we were [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] miles away in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) with no signature, no security code and no expiration date - only the credit card number, which obviously is easy for thieves to use successfully if VISA security procedures are lacking. This charge is not valid and despite overwhelming evidence, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is insisting we pay it plus interest and fees. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter responding to my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter to the CEO cancelling the account, and after repeating the same old excuses for rejecting the protest, it advises that " as a courtesy '''' they will " review the matter again ''''. They are asking for copies of all the information I have already sent them TWICE and they are asking for a copy of the " contract '''' - as I told them before, there is no contract that pertains to the purported charge! So, I am betting this is the excuse they will use again when denying the protested amount. They can''t get the vendor to respond to verify the charges, they cant provide any sales or credit card receipts, with OR without my signature, and yet they want me to spend more time duplicating paperwork I have already sent. 

ENOUGH IS ENOUGH! 

Regulation Z is clear on consumer obligations for disputing charges - I have met every one of them - while the vendor has provided, literally, no concrete evidence of anything pointing towards a legitimate sales transaction, yet they refuse to credit the account the result of which has cost me considerable time, frustration and can possibly affect my credit history going forward. That''s not to mention they are allowing fraudulent charges to post to my account AFTER I REQUESTED IN WRITING THAT THE ACCOUNT BE CLOSED. 

I have also complained to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Attorney General and the Office of the Comptroller of Currency. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Attorney General ''s office advises that the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau initiated a suit against this same institution in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for illegal credit card practices. Clearly the information and proof I have submitted shows similar violations are still ongoing and I am at a loss as to why you are not doing something about it. If I cant get help from the very governmental agencies tasked with protecting consumers, then I''m left with the only option of writing my state and federal elected officials.','FIRST NATIONAL BANK OF OMAHA',2.0,4.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] protested charges appearing on my first bankcard. the charges were a charge by an [');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(848,'08/29/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Incorrect information on your report','I spoke with ten different representatives in the span of one month. The first initial call with this company was on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], ID Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This is how the call went : " He was very nice. He let me know that my payment were due on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month. The closing date for this account is on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month. He told me that for the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment, I had paid it too early. So I stated that they are reporting in 30 day late for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because I paid it too early. I explained how that does not even make sense. Then he proceeded to tell me that the late payment from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I actually missed the payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I told him that this account was always set up on auto pay and in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have fraudulent activity with my actual checking account, in which Bank of America did not properly change. I told him I tried avoiding this again in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so I paid it early. He asked what can he do for me and I told him to remove the late remarks. He agreed to remove both late payments and he said this will reflect on my Bank of America account in 48 hours. I asked him for a deletion letter so I could show my broker that this will be removed. He said he can not provide me a written statement of deletion, but it will be removed ''''. 
So, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I wanted to follow up with Bank of America as the late remarks were still reporting. When I called back, I spoke with two different representatives. This is how the call went : I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who was telling me I was late in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I told him the previous representative, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], gave me different information. Both of the information they were giving me was not the same. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] felt overwhelmed and transferred the call to his supervisor, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], ID Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] asked me what the problem was with my file. I explained conversation I had with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and how he agreed to remove these late remarks. He said [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] only gave me the late fees back and that they did not remove the late remarks, as this was not a bank error. I told him I was given the wrong information and that this would be removed from my credit report. I told him that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was so clear and confident that this would be removed and I told my broker that this is going to be updated. By doing so, I moved forward with my loan and now I was going to lose {$35000.00} because if the wrong information I was told. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said he was going to contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] supervisor and she will call me back in the next 48 hours. They will look over this call and if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] really did give me wrong information, that they will file this as a bank error and remove the late remarks. 

I called back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], as I never received a call back. I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Texas and the call went like this : " I told her exactly what was going on and how my file was not properly handled. I told her about all the wrongful information I was receiving and she put me on hold to look at my accounts. I told her I have repeatedly received wrongful information regarding this account. She agreed that this was a bank error and she has agreed to remove the late payments, since I was given wrong information. She sent out a request to the credit department that the late remarks are to be removed as this was from a bank error made by Bank of America.  She stated they will be faxing me a letter to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
I thought this nightmare was over and I finally had my issue resolved. I was wrong, however, as I called back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and received new information. I spoke with three different representatives and this is what they stated : The first two representatives stated they do not fax out any letters. I told them I had clear communication from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that they were able to fax me a letter. They transferred me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], their supervisor, as they could not handle the call. He said that they are able to send out faxes and they sent a fax on Friday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I told him I never received that document. He said he was going to send it again and I told him I wanted to wait on the phone for him to send it, so he knows if I received it or not. I was already on the phone for an hour. I asked him exactly what did the letter say. He then proceeded to say " the letter said .... '''' then the call dropped. I was already so frustrated so I decided to call back another day, as no one was able to help me ''''. 

I called back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke to a supervisor directly. Her name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and she was located in Arkansas. She proceeded to tell me the following information : " Instead of looking at the notes and all the people I spoke to, she wanted to start from the beginning in why I was late, etc. She could tell I was frustrated but I told her she would be too if she spoke to that many people and no one was helping or taking responsibility for this issue. I told her that I was told multiple times from Bank of America that the derogatory information would be removed from my credit report. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me there were no requests for anything and I told her that''s a lie, because I wrote down all the information from the conversations I''ve had with Bank of America. She then all of a sudden seen there was a letter was sent out on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I told her this is what I meant about getting wrong information, as I stated the last representative stated they sent out a letter on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She told me my initial request for this account was sent to the wrong department and still will put another request in. I also asked her to put a request in to pull ALL calls from everyone, as all the representatives gave me wrong information. She also specifically stated that I was not late at all in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which is the late remarks the credit bureaus were reporting ''''. 

I called back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to follow up on the last conversation I had with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from the customer service department and she stated : " Bank of America sent in a submission to the credit bureaus but she was unable to see what it said. She said this was mailed out on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She transferred me to the credit disputing department as she did not see any notes about the calls being pulled like I requested. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Arizona got on the line and he was a resolutions manager in the credit underwriting department. He was basically just stating general procedure that they do not remove unless it was a bank error. I told him this was bigger than that now as I received inaccurate information from multiple representatives that stated this was going to be removed. I told him this information has cause more financial issues in my life, as I was going to lose money from this loan. I also had to request for my calls to be pulled AGAIN, as my callas were never pulled. I told him this was very important, as they clearly told me on different occasions this will be updated. Then he said he was going to send that information to his supervisor. I was confused as to why I was speaking with him when he initially stated he was the manager. I told him to transfer the call and he said the supervisor was busy. I decided to give them a call back, as I could not handle these stressful calls anymore ''''. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Maine called my phone as he seen I put in a request to have Bank of America call me back after this was investigated. This is how the dreadful conversation went : " He was stern and told me they are not removing the late remarks based on the late payment history. I asked him if he even investigated this account like I asked and he stated he did not. He said he could just see I was late on two different occasions. I told him I requested to have my calls pulled and for them to really investigate and see that I should not have any late remarks. I asked him why was he even calling if he did not investigate this account? He said because he had a short time frame to call me back in. So basically he only called to make sure he called in the correct time frame, rather than resolving the issue. I told him I needed those calls pulled as this was the 3rd or 4th time I had requested it. He said he was going to. ''''','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'ten different representatives spoke in the span of one month. they were reporting late payments on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].');
