INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(874,'08/23/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','This is my 2nd complaint against Fifth Third Bank regarding my daughter, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   mortgage account with Fifth Third. I, her dad, have a durable power of attorney to handle her financial matters. As noted in my previous complaint, my daughter is recovering from a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that has caused her to be out of work for over 3 years ; over 3 years ago she had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & is still recovering. Also, her house caught fire on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; Meanwhile, she became delinquent on her mortgage and car loan payments ; her mortgage account is now current but she still needs mortgage payment assistance - so we filed the 1st hardship application in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and we were denied financial assistance because she did not have enough income and some other reasons that were not adequately explained. So on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we filed the 2nd hardship application. We checked the status of the 2nd hardship application on Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], by talking to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the phone ; we were told that one of the other reasons we did not get payment assistance on the 1st hardship application is because underwriting tried to qualify my daughter under a Loan Modification Program which is a permanent restructuring of the mortgage whereby terms and/or loan rate is modified to make the payments affordable ; I told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over the phone that it makes no sense to tell me underwriting modified the loan by increasing the terms and the monthly payments increased and that is the other reason why she was denied hardship payment assistance. I asked for a copy of the new payment amortization schedule and was told that it was not available because Fifth Third does keep those documents - I told him that makes no sense because you have to keep an audit trail for all loan modifications. So basically something is not right with what I was told. So I sent the following email On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and CC ''d several other Fifth Third customers service employees. BEGINNING OF EMAIL TO FIFTH THIRD... Hardship Application Please let us know ASAP what the status of the 2nd hardship application is. Underwriter 1. Please have you underwriter send me some type of verification showing that my daughter was denied a mortgage modification because her payments went up when the mortgage term increased and/or the rate was lowered or a combination of both. Like I said to you on the phone, this has to be some new math and I want to see it in writing. 2. Why don''t we qualify for the FHA forbearance program? - allows FHA homeowners to roll any missed or deferred payments into the mortgage balance 3. The fifth third website says something a little different than our discussion on Friday ( which made it sound like there are no options available )... note : there was an attachment from their website which is not shown here. In addition, please explain how your mortgage customers can get mortgage payment assistance when they lose their jobs and have no income but my daughter who also lost her job can not. And it appears Fifth Third has tried every possible mortgage payment assistance options available including freezing payments for 3 - 6 months. Short Sale We are not interested in a short sale - due to my daughter ''s [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; she wants to remain in her home Job Search My daughter is actively looking for a job. Fifth Thirds Reemployment Program Also, can you give us more information about Fifth Thirds Homeowner Reemployment program ( https : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to help mortgage borrowers find jobs. END OF EMAIL TO FIFTH THIRD The above email was sent on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and so far no one has replied to my email ( today ''s date is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). So today, I called to get a status update on the 2nd hardship application ( filed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and I was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that the 2nd file was never opened! So I said it sounds like Firth Third dropped the ball again - she did not like that answer. But here is the reason I was given... the 2nd hardship application ( filed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) looks like it came in on the same day the 1st hardship application was denied so it looks like the 2 applications got mixed up!!! I said [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that makes no sense because each application should have a time stamp when it came in and/or a separate case/tracking # for each occurrence ( so if there was a third hardship application, how would they not get that one mixed up and make the wrong decision to close the file and meanwhile the borrower is struggling ). She basically did not have a reasonable answer for this screw-up. So she told me to call back in 3 days to see if the file was opened. Unbelievable that a large company with a ton of people can operate this way. This is a similar experience that I pointed out in my first complaint stating that we never received any mail explaining that my daughter ''s house was going to foreclosure because Fifth Third sent all of the mail to the wrong address. But to their credit, they admitted it was their error. But my daughter would have lost her home to foreclosure over this small overlooked detail had I not taken a second look at the hardship application to see that I gave them the correct mailing address. This is why I am writing these complaints - our family could have been totally devastated financially because of poor customer service and I am even more upset about this latest Fifth Third oversight which adds another delay to processing the 2nd hardship application. I would not doubt if other Fifth Third customers lost their homes and are suffering because of poor customer service. Hopefully Fifth Third will improve their processes.','FIFTH THIRD FINANCIAL CORPORATION',10.0,10.0,'fifth third bank filed 2nd hardship application on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. she became delinquent on mortgage and car');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(875,'08/23/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I contacted Capital One ''s Spark Business Checking department at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I wanted to verify whether or not my old Spark Business Checking account was still valid and available for use. I was able to log into the account using my old credentials and saw there was a negative balance of {$280.00} I had since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].The representative I spoke with that day advised me the account was still open and available for use. She offered me an option to order a new debit card, but I thought I had my old one so I declined. I updated my phone number, email, and address from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] online as well. After confirming the account was in " good standing '''' I provided my employer with the account and routing number for my direct deposit. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I couldn''t find my old debit card and contacted Capital One ''s Spark Business Checking department at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to request another card be sent to me. The young lady politely confirmed my new address in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], sent me a new card, and advised me the new card would arrive in 3-5 business days. 

When I did not have the new card by XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called Capital One ''s Spark Business Checking department at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a third time to see if they were able to activate my old debit card. The young lady politely reactivated my old debit card and changed the PIN number for me. This was very important because I was scheduled to move into my new apartment onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after sleeping in my car for 2 months. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called Capital One ''s Spark Business Checking department at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to verify my old card was indeed active and was advised I would need to speak with another department to verify information before any incoming deposits. Upon speaking with the department, I was advised this was the collections department. I was advised my direct deposit would go into the account, but that after Capital One was paid their debt I would be sent a check in 2-5 business days with the balance. 

I completely understand the company wanting to collect their debt. I fully intended on paying it. However, I should not have spoken with 3 representatives before being briefed on the true status of the account. The account was by all appearances open, but per the collections department it was actually charged off. 

All I am saying is that I feel the company deceived me into believing I had an active account when in fact the account was not active at all. It was unfair of them to give me the idea that my account was available for use when in fact they were just attempting to collect a debt. The ordeal has caused a great deal of emotional distress. Yes, I will get the funds eventually, but I am hoping they still hold my apartment and I also hope my next direct deposit does not try to go into that account.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a representative told me the account was still open and available for use. the young lady politely confirmed my new address in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(876,'08/23/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','Nationwide Advantage Mortgage, is my lender for my mortgage. I have tried multiple times to do a modification with this company and I get the paperwork but then I get told different things by all the reps. My original modification started in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my loan was put on deferment but once that was over it started the foreclosure date starting XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I did modifications since then, they weren''t accepted because I didn''t make enough money, then they were saying I needed to send in documentation, like proof of insurance, things that I never filled out on the expense statement. Then my account was still being handled by Nationwide Advantage but was being handled by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated that modification was not sent over to then. My most recent issue is because I feel like this company is trying to force me into this sheriff ''s sale. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I spoke with a representative about my loan and that is when I was told that she was sending out paperwork and that and she told me that once I filled them out that I would have to call in to them because the reason they don''t call me is because I filed bankruptcy before so they can reach out to me ( 1st time ever hearing this ). She stated it would have to be in by XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I spoke to another representative on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I informed that rep that I overnighted my documents and she made sure that I had everything filled out and all my documentation that I need was with my modification packet I sent back. I spoke with a rep on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to ask if they received my paperwork, she stated that had not and it needed to be in within 30 days of the sheriff sale date ( 1st time hearing that ). I stated well why give a date of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the paperwork to be in by because that is a day after the 30 day sheriff sale date. Call on Tuesday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] spoke with another rep and asked was my paperwork there because the rep I spoke to the day before stated that it wasn''t but when I spoke to the post office they stated it was receive in by the company on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( tracking numb [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). She then stated that my paperwork is there but they will not open it because it had to be there 60 days before the sale date, I then stated well which one is it because you rep yesterday stated it would be 30 days. This rep then stated well 45 business days before the sale date. I asked then why would I be sent modification papers with a date of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on them and I have spoken with minimum of 5 different people and you are the 1st person to say this. She stated well you just have to let it go to the sale date. From the time I have had this loan with them I have gotten rude rep ''s, money being applied, wrong to my account, payments not being applied then hitting my credit like I was 30 days late and I wasn''t because the money was sitting there. I became unemployed in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I explained all of this to this company and if you look at my payment history I was not late until then. I lost my job because I was falsely accused a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I had to fight this case for 14 months and couldn''t get a job because it was an open case fighting [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I went 14 months with no income whatsoever. Once I started working for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I did another modification, I didn''t have enough income and they wanted copies of insurance etc, things I didn''t have. I have had steady employment and now they won''t accept my paperwork. I have been trying and wanted to start back paying my mortgage months and months ago and I haven''t been allowed to because my modification was not accepted. I called on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and asked to speak to a supervisor and was put on hold for 25 mins, transferred back into the queue and then hung up on. I just can''t believe that a company can treat someone like this and get away with it, when it''s concerning so serous as their home. Speaking to a representative now on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was informed that all the information is int the office, they will not accept my paperwork because I don''t have a bank statement. I was originally told that I just needed to send in a letter stating that I don''t a have a bank statement and why. I sent in that letter and now they are telling me that the letter isn''t good enough because I have to have proof of that even if it in deposited to a debit card because I have to show proof that I can pay my mortgage. I explained to the rep that a bank statement does not prove that you can pay your mortgage but check stubs do, I can not be forced to have a checking or savings account and even if I had one that still isn''t proof.','NATIONWIDE ADVANTAGE MORTGAGE COMPANY',10.0,10.0,'my original modification started in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my loan was put on deferment. once that was over it started the foreclosure date starting X');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(877,'08/23/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Since early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have attempted to get experian to correct their inaccurate reporting of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has given me assurances in writing and orally the account is and has been reported as closed to all 3 credit reporting agencies. However, EXPERIAN flatly refuses to correct their reporting and show this account as OPEN when it is closed. I have submitted numerous request to experian to show this account as closed and uploaded the letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating they too have told experian the account is closed several times but it is up to experian to update its own records. I sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s letter to experian and was given # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I completed the upload with yet another dispute of their incorrect reporting and experian promptly stated matter was closed and still show the account open with the dispute closed. I got another letter from experian XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] portions of report marked showing they have account open not closed as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting it. Their false reporting makes my credit score rather low because it shows I am using a over 50 % of my credit from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when in fact it is closed and I am using [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % just paying back the debt I incurred as we agreed I would. Please contact experian and instruct them to correct their records to show my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account has been closed since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] NOT OPEN and being used as a line of credit. Thank you.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian has been unable to correct their reporting of my account. the account is closed to all 3 credit reporting agencies. a letter