INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(890,'08/21/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','On XX/XX/2018 Experian reported my account as enrolled on a consumer credit counseling service. That action prevented my 19-year-old bank, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from extending a loan for a new vehicle. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had 3 of  my homes, my auto and has never being paid late, by denying my application without even considering my credit record, current income and impeccable history with them, they are discriminating against me under the FCRA act. 

There is no difference between a person like me that negotiated a re-payment plan with a few credit cards and never defaulted and a person that either has horrible credit or bankrupt. That is unfair to me and any other party that has kept their re-payment agreement as negotiated several years back. 
We are suffering the same faith as a bankrupt person. There is no incentive on us trying to protect our credit, we still get [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I did not cost any of the credit cards income or default on their books. I just negotiated a better rate that they do offer to other clients. This is not fair under the terms of the FCRA. 

