INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(895,'08/20/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is failing or refusing to complete action on my employer certification for Public Service Loan Forgiveness. When I transferred by loan to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] last autumn I had completed 109 qualifying monthly payments under the Public Service Loan Forgiveness ( PSLF ) program through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When my loan completed its transfer from my prior lender to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], after several months of administratively setting up and transferring the file, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s loan detail for my account showed only 62 qualifying months under PSLF. I had the same job with the same [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employer for the entire 109 months that were reported by my employer. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  by phone. They said that they have 120 days according to their own deadlines to count my qualifying payments. I was told that I was not being denied any credit for qualifying months but that they just hadn''t finished counting. Since that time I have called almost monthly to check on the status of the counting of my qualifying months. I have been told the same thing repeatedly, which is that they can see that I have a total of 109 months, that there is no problem with the 47 months that have not been added to the count, but that they just have not finished. I am now ready to file for forgiveness based on a total of 120 months in qualifying employment but I am stuck until they finish what should be the very simple task of counting my total payments.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] completed 109 qualifying monthly payments under the public service loan forgiveness program. when my loan completed its transfer from my prior lender to');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(896,'08/20/2018','Debt collection','Auto debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','Got a phone call on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] demanding my name address social number etc upfront without trying to tell me the reason for the call.finally got a name from them and reason and I did not refuse to pay said debt which is said to be lower than is whats on my credit which through a flag and then told me a different finance company than I signed with then proceed to threaten me me if I didnt set up a payment right then through bank draft that they were going to take legal action especially when I told them Ive never received anything in writing from them stating what I owed etc.funny that I just got a letter stating that said finance company just sold the loan to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ha but getting a call from California the very next day being threatened','Crown Asset Management, LLC',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] got a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] demanding my name address social');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(897,'08/20/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/2018 Bank of America without warning changed the balances on both my checking and savings accounts to - {$880000.00}. This was done with NO correspondence from Bank of America, no  phone call, no email, nothing. I later found out these represented holds on my accounts. I had no access to any money for the day. I noticed it the day it happened and contacted them about my accounts being frozen, and they wouldn''t give me any information, only that I had to go to the bank branch with 2 forms of ID. So I did the next morning, at which point the bank unlocked my accounts. I thought everything was back to normal and they just wanted to verify my identification, although it was a very outrageous way of doing so. 

It wasn''t until after that weekend on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I noticed a fraudulent {$1800.00} charge on my account. Again after calling and visiting the bank I was told there was nothing they could do until a picture of the check was uploaded. Finally on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] this picture of a bounced fraudulent check that was deposited on my account showed up. This was all officially reported to the fraud department by a bank employee on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at my nearest branch. They then closed my checking account and opened up a new checking account as the fraudster may have had access to my checking account number. I can only speculate ( as I still have been given no information by the bank ) that someone deposited this fraudulent check at a Bank of America claiming to be me, and that the teller believed this person was me and gave this person {$1800.00} in cash for this fraudulent check, which then bounced and was put as a chargeback on my account for {$1800.00} along with a fee for a bounced check. The bank did return the fee. 

It is now XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have still yet received NO correspondence from Bank of America about returning the funds to my account. I have filed a police report with the local police department, I have locked all my credit reports, I have filed a report with the FTC. I have called their check fraud department twice now for updates and am told after nearly 2 months they have no update and no information. This has been a nightmarish experience that has caused a great deal of hardship to my family with a total lack of communication and lack of empathy or urgency by Bank of America. And I feel that it is due to their failure to identify a fake check, and to properly identify their customers before handing out such a large sum of cash. My funds no longer feel safe at this bank.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'bank of America changed balances on both my checking and savings accounts to $880000.00. the bank unlocked my accounts and contacted them about my accounts being frozen ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(898,'08/19/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','I needed to get a credit report for a rental I was considering. I was aware consumers are eligible for a free credit report annually from each of the major credit agencies. On or about XX/XX/2018 or XX/XX/2018, I did an online search and was led to request a report through Experian. I followed the prompts online. It indicated a {$1.00} charge. I knew that wasn''t correct but time was a factor and I wasn''t worried about a {$1.00}. Before I completed the transaction there was a disclaimer of an approximately {$21.00} charge for an unknown service. I didn''t see an option to opt out of this unknown service. I had not seen anything preceding this message. I don''t recall if I skipped back to search although knowing me, I would think I did. I completed the transaction and immediately posted a message, on the same website, advising I did not want the service etc. It''s been approximately 2 months since the transaction and I don''t recall the " clicks '''' I made to find this contact method, but I usually search for the " contact '''' link. I always prefer to contact in person as you never know if there is resolution unless you speak to someone directly. It is unusual for me to message a company this way, even through their own website, so, now two months later, I wonder if there was no phone number provided ( challenges to find appropriate contact information to resolve this became an issue ). 

In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a credit card statement advising of a posting for {$21.00}, from Experian, on XX/XX/2018. Although I had not received my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement, I was concerned they had billed me again in early XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

On XX/XX/2018, I contacted the following phone numbers which I found through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] searches : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( 2 very brief calls ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( a 6 minute call ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2 calls, the second being 28 minutes. 

In the final call I reached a representative who offered to reimburse 1 charge. I stated I wanted both charges reversed, we could not reach an agreement. He then transferred me to supervisor/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in Arkansas. He too offered only a 1 month reimbursement. He stated I did not cancel properly as I need to cancel by phone or writing or whatever ( it was irrelevant at that point ). I advised I used their own method of contact provided on their website. I did not even know what the service was that I had signed up for. We argued back and forth ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not agree to a complete reimbursement. He only offered his Legal Dept ''s contact information ( ha, ha, funny [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). He  would not provide his last name or contact number, nor transfer me to anyone above him, nor provide me the Presidents name and contact information. 


I did not want the service, did not even know what it was about, had seen nothing to advise me of this service. This service was not the purpose of my inquiry that day. I have not utilized any service nor gained any benefits as I assumed the " membership '''' had been closed. Only in the process of requesting this reimbursement have I learned this is some sort of credit monitoring program which I already have my own subscription through my employer. I completed the transaction as I could not find another way to get the credit report I needed quickly. 

It is ironic that a credit reporting agency, that reports our " misdeeds '''' to vendors, hides a marketing program in their credit report request process, then makes it so difficult to cancel. If they check their records, they will find my message to cancel, through an option provided on their website. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s hedging and unwillingness to provide contact information just shows how difficult it is for consumers to resolve their complaints. I wonder, why do they ( apparently ) not accept notification via their own website message option. And if not, why was the message not forwarded on to someone to contact me. WHY DO THEY MAKE IT SO HARD???????????????? 

EXPERIAN CREDIT AGENCY = UNETHICAL','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',4.0,4.0,'a credit report for a rental was requested by a credit agency. it indicated a $1.00 charge. it was a disclaimer of an');
