INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(908,'08/17/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','Mortgage company has not provided requested information to verify debt, only providing a phantom account number which has been a widespread predatory lending practice of mortgage company. My letter sent XX/XX/2018 requested verification of debt pursuant to the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, 15 U.S.C. Section 1629g. On XX/XX/2018 in a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on behalf of mortgage company, the original debt owed was crossed out the show a different amount. Many pages of the accompanying loan history is illegible ( unable to read ).','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'mortgage company has not provided requested information to verify debt. phantom account number has been a widespread predatory lending practice.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(909,'08/16/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','When first contacted by this company, they called my work # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
This got routed to a group, i did not receive the call, my boss did, who then took the number down for me to call them back. When i called it back, the women who answered refused to tell me who was calling or what the call was about, she then transferred me to a man " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' who proceeded to tell me this was an attempt to collect debt, and that they were getting ready to take legal action. 

THIS IS THE FIRST I HEARD OF THIS. 

I told Mr.[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I could not be contacted on this number, and i could not have this discussion at work, that i would call him back after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

After [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], i called back the number that he originally called from, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
BAD NUMBER, could get through, didn''t know the company to which i was calling ( because they didn''t tell me ), so i couldn''t [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to find a different contact option. 


Two days later, at work again, I received another call from Mr. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], this time on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I answered I told him i had attempted to contact him on the last number, and got a bad number. He huffed under his breath and said " Um, NO. '''' I replied, Yes, 100 %. He then asked what number i called and then gave me another # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Main Line. ) I told him again not to contact me at work and I would give him a call on the new number after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Later that day i called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], got directed to Mr [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Mr.[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] indicated I owed a MUCH LARGER debt than the original loan ever was, and there were payments made - so the debt needed to verified and backed by proof, otherwise i assume this is a violation in his attempt to collect more money than is actually owed. 

Firstly, I asked Mr.[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for the following items before proceeding to setup an type of payment. I was willing to work with him. 

- Proof of Debt Verification Letter - Proof that debt is owned by Company he is working with - Copy of original loan agreement - Payment History - Explanation of how interest was collected on Debt. 
- Proof that State of Limitations was not expired - License Number Mr. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then told me he was not obligated to provide any of those documents, and stated that they had already sent a " Verification '''' letter to an address I have not lived in for 6+ Months. 

I asked him to send it again, I was told no, then I asked why I wasn''t contacted VIA Email, he stated that i was sent something by the original creditor. I informed him this was not true, I already went through my Inbox and there is absolutely nothing from the original creditor. 

He proceeded to tell me if i didn''t pay an amount today, this was going to closing and legal action would be pursued. 

I told him i was willing and trying to work with him on repayment, but wouldn''t do so until I got what I requested. 

This was only the second time we spoke, in a 3 day time span, how could they take legal action - don''t I have 30 days? 

Then, he " all the sudden '''' couldn''t hear me on the line, I checked to make sure i wasn''t on mute. I WAS NOT. I was speaking to him the entire time and asked if he could hear me? 

He then said " Ms.[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], If your not going to speak, i will assume this is a refusal '''' and hung up on me.','GMA Investments, LLC',2.0,2.0,'i called back the number from a group, i did not receive the call. the women who answered refused to tell me who was calling or what the call was about.');
