INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(950,'08/08/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/18, I initiated a transfer of {$2300.00} from my Chase checking account to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] checking. Unbeknownst to me, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had closed my account before the transfer went through. However, the money was not credited back to my Chase account and is currently lost. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] tells me my problem is with Chase and Chase tells me my problem is with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have spent the better part of 6 weeks shuttling between Chase and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spending countless hours on the phone. Neither bank is taking this half as seriously as I am so I needed to do all I can to get a resolution.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/18 transfer of $2300.00 from my Chase checking account. money was not credited back to my Chase account and is currently lost. neither');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(951,'08/08/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of this year I received a promotional credit card offer from Barclaycard Ring MasterCard. The offer stated that I would receive a 0 % APR Interest rate on balance transfers within the first 45 days. It also stated that there would be a 0 % APR for 15-months on the balance transfer balances and new purchases. I received the first statement and I had been charged interest on the balance transfer. I was so busy that I just paid it to avoid any dings on my credit and figured I would call to resolve the issue before the next bill. Well the next bill came and it was much larger and I was still being charged interest. Not the typical monthly compounding interest, but daily compounded interest raising my payments substantially. I called the company to resolve the issue and they claimed that I didn''t sign up for the offer for 15-month promotional period. I signed up to pay 10.74 % interest. This couldn''t be further from the truth. I then went to  download the cardholder agreement and come to find out it''s not online. You have to request a copy. Well if they''re denying my offer and telling me that it wasn''t the offer I signed up for then how should I trust them to send me a legitimate cardholder agreement. I never received the initial cardholder agreement in the mail either. The representatives we spoke with on the phone did nothing to assist in the situation other than deny what I was saying and telling me to send them the offer I received three months ago that has long since been thrown away. I tried to go to the old web page and it has been removed from the website with the exact same promotional offer the only difference being the promotional period of 12-months instead of 15-months. The  representatives were rude and wasted almost an hour of my time. They denied that any 15-month offer existed initially. Then they said well it did exist in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but definitely not [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I pointed him to the nerdwallet article I attached below and he claimed that it was outdated, but it''s the offer I was mailed. There are plenty of other credit cards with 0 % for XX month promotional periods I could have applied for with a 3 % or less balance transfer fee, which would be a lot cheaper than 10.74 % compounding daily.','BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE',2.0,2.0,'a promotional credit card offer from barclaycard Ring MasterCard was received. it stated that I would receive a 0 % APR on balance transfers within the first 45 days');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(952,'08/08/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Sent in a dispute letter to Experian that was received by them on,XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Got an update regarding my bankruptcy stating That the date was verified, and it remains on my report. I called Experian today on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and  spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Experian employee, explained to him that the dates were wrong. He said they were accurate from the third party that they use, could not give me the third party information, or who he spoke to. Said its a lot of companies they pull information from, asked him for all the numbers, said he does not know the numbers. Dont think its right that they verify information from anyone and not able to tell me who they got it from so I may call them and speak to them regarding the wrong date on my bankruptcy. Please advise this happens all the time.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian employee said the dates were wrong. he said they were accurate from the third party that they use. he said they could not give me the third party information ');
