INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(984,'08/01/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','My client ''s information was used without her consent to submit several fraudulent application for credit. While the accounts associated were not established the inquiries related to the applications were found on her credit reports. Among the creditors are American Express ( dispute submitted XX/XX/2018 ), [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( dispute submitted XX/XX/2018 ), and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( dispute submitted XX/XX/2018 ). Per FCRA 45 business days total is allowed for investigation of fraud issues and the consumer shall be notified of the results of the investigation. As of this date my client has not been notified of the investigation results from these fraudulent applications.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'credit reports found on client''s credit reports. a consumer will be notified of the results of the investigation.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(985,'08/01/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have reached out to Equifax to get some unauthorized accounts that do not belong to me off my credit report. They have failed to remove them.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'unauthorized accounts have failed to remove them.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(986,'08/01/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','To whom it make concern, In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I started my graduate student loans with FAFSA, then after graduation in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received an email from Great Lakes informing me that they are the going to manage my loans and the first payment going to be on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] At that time I applied to repayment driven by income, and since then I was sending the required documents to Great leaks every year to decide my ability to repay the loan. According to my income and family size, my monthly due payment was {$0.00} till the beginning of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] At the beginning of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Great lakes reviewed my renewal application with my supported documents, and decided to make my monthly payment {$23.00} I agreed and started paying this amount on time.

In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a phone call from Great Lakes, the associate said, you parent student loan will do in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the due payment is {$100.00} ( I had a parent student loan for my son who was studying at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but he stopped and didnt complete his studying ).

I explained to the customer service representative that I can not handle these two monthly payment, how am I going to pay this {$100.00} and Great Lakes just reviewed my income in the last two months and acknowledge that my ability according to my income and family size is {$23.00}, it is mean I have to pay ( {$23.00} + {$100.00} = {$120.00} ) this is too much for me! I want to pay and I dont want to default with my payments, but this is above my capacity.

She suggested to consolidate all the loans, and if I will do that, the total payment ( For my loan and the parent student loan ) going to be approximately {$70.00}, and this will decrease the payment significantly from {$120.00} to about {$70.00} The representative instructed me to log on online and proceed with a consolidation application. I told her to give me some time, and let me talk to my son and I will make a decision.

In May I contacted the Great Lakes and asked them about the consolidation which been recommended by Great Lake associate and the associate who talked to me over the phone agreed to the consolidation and how this can decrease/reduce my total payment to about {$70.00}, she added, keep in mind that you still need to pay the coming due payment {$100.00} in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], then after completing the process of consolidation, the total payment for ( your loan and parents student loan ) to about {$70.00} ( This is going to be the best repayment plan ) I called Great Lakes another time in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to ask about some details and started the consolidation process. I applied for consolidation and in my application I chose to start the consolidation process in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( It was optional to choose the time to start the process ) In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] surprisingly I received emails from Great Lakes informing me that they approved my application for the consolidation, while I requested and instructed in my application to start in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but I considered its done and at the end it is going to be good for me as the total payment going to be around {$70.00} Unexpectedly, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received an email from Great Lakes informing me that the due paying going to be on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the amount is {$320.00} I called Great lakes, explained all the details above, and told them that I did the consolidation according to the associate suggestion, and the entire goal was to reduce the payment from {$120.00} to {$70.00} The associate didnt help me to resolve the issue, she transferred me to a supervisor, and the supervisor informed me that she needs to hear the phone calls and then get back to me, it took a week till she called me back and said, I am not sure, I listened to the recorded phone calls but the voice is not clear and a little cut out especially when the conversation between you and the associate was about the {$70.00}, yes she recommended the consolidation but she just estimated the payment around {$70.00} I told her when someone estimating {$70.00} it may be {$60.00} or {$80.00} but not {$320.00} she suggested to me and I did the consolidation as a result for her advice. She said ; I cant help you with that, I will talk to my manager, and he will contacted you in 24 to 48 hours I told her yes, I want to escalate complain to a manager.

I left her 6 voicemails asking her to call me back, and informing her that her manager didnt call me back.

After a week of calling and leaving voicemail, I got a call from a manager who was not calling to listen to the situation, but to affirm that Great Lake will not be doing anything and will not be reversing the loan. I asked why didnt an underwriter see that my payments are going from {$120.00} to {$320.00} would be ok. And that no one checked my Debit to Income ratio to realize that I can not afford that payment. The manager didnt comment on that statement and kept saying that the company wont change anything, and he stated that this plan will take 20 % of my income.

I told him you are setting me to default, because two months ago, Great Lakes evaluated my ability and decided {$23.00} is my maximum, how do you approved me for a consolidation put me on {$320.00} as a monthly payment, how did you do the calculations, which equation you used to put me on this plan!

( I understood from the conversation, that he is the loan officer/underwriter who did the process ) All his concern was that the representative didnt suggest to me the consolidation, or after lot of back and forth he said yes she did recommended a consolidation but not this type, another type.

He told me that I can forbearance for 12 months, but there will be {$16.00} interest every day Here I am requesting a help to solve my issue with Great Lakes, as no way will I be able to make a payment that large. Please understand my situation. Im unable to make that payment nor am I able to afford a missed payment on my Credit history.

I had my loans for graduate program, as I did my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I completed the program with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out 4 and will not do this mistake, unless the two representative confirmed to me that this is the best solution and will help me reduce my monthly payment.

My request is to put me where I can pay my student loan and the parent student loan according to my income just like what I had before, something around {$25.00} for my loans and {$25.00} for parent student loan, in the same time I want to file a maximum complain about that manager who insist to defend himself and his team even when he knew that his team advised me for this plan and he completed the process with 100 % know I am not going to be able paying this amount, and with all my requests and explanations, he insisted to keep me on this plan.

Great Lakes ID : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Loan Account with U.S. DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATION ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Loan Account with U.S. DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATION ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Loan Account with U.S. DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATION ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Cell # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','GREAT LAKES',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I started my graduate student loans with FAFSA, then after graduation in XX/XX');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(987,'07/31/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','Chase is my bank and I have a credit card with them ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Last year someone used my card fraudulently to order clothing online from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was in the hospital at the time and when we received packages we didn''t order, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] allowed us to use labels in the packages to send them back for free, which we did. They acknowledged the return via email and said they issued a refund but then they never ever did. We have tried to work with Chase since they are our bank and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] won''t reply but Chase refuses to help. We have opened these disputes as disputes and as fraud and the close the case every time without even contacting us. I have asked them on multiple occasions not to call since I am very sick but they continue to do that. 
This is ruining my credit. I have stopped paying on the card. 
I have read over the fine print of my credit agreement and by law they have to support legitimate disputes and fraud cases .I have proved with documentation that these are legitimate cases and returned. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] refuses to reply with the tracking numbers, however, they did reply with confirmation of the returns which is enough to credit my account but Chase refuses and now the charges are getting older and older and nobody is doing anything. 

I feel some of this is discrimination against the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] since I am fully [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and can not call in most days or answer the phones and they take advantage of that. I have saved all correspondence with them and proof and all the times they have ignored my pleas. I need help. 

Please help me. 

charges are all for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].com XX/XX/17 {$190.00} {$140.00} {$82.00} {$660.00}','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a credit card with Chase ends in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of last year. a credit card with them ends in [COMPTE_ANON');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(988,'07/31/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Communication tactics','I am receiving repeated calls multiple times a day ranging in times from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE',2.0,2.0,'i receive calls multiple times a day ranging in times from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(989,'07/31/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Communication tactics','This is my 2nd loan with Republic Finance. The 1st was paid off early. I have paid on this loan about 18 months now. This payment was due XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but I didn''t pay it on time. However, it was paid before the next one was due. In XX/XX/2018, after several days of calls. I asked for a deferment to get back on track but was told they don''t do those but could renew the loan. I told them I don''t want to renew the loan. I was advised that is the only assistance available to me. After several days of calls. I told them to stop calling me. I didn''t get any more calls until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] timeframe. I told the same person as before I had told them not to call me. She then said they have to have it in writing. I told her that is not true. She said that is their policy. To have it in writing. I told her fine so when I went in to make the next payment on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I asked for a sticky note and put it in writing. I also put that none of my contacts or my job was to be contacted. She had to check with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to make sure it was acceptable. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told her to put it in my file. However, today I was checking my credit report and saw that they did a hard inquiry on XX/XX/2018. My loan was not 30 days late and to this date has never been 30 days late. There was no reason to pull my credit. I want to know how a company can just pull the consumer ''s credit report for no good reason and decrease their credit score. I can to some degree understand the need to renew the loan. That''s how they make their money but if someone is truly needing assistance to maintain or increase their credit score, it makes no sense to intentionally harm them.','RFNA, LP',2.0,2.0,'this payment was due XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but I didn''t pay it on time. I told them they don''');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(990,'07/31/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','I just got a notification that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reported a collection account on my credit report. I never received any letters from this agency giving me the right to dispute this debt. Under the FDCPA a debt collector has to provide a consumer with a G notice. The right to dispute the alleged debt within 5 days of the initial communication with the consumer. They have violated 15 USC 1692g. I also dispute this alleged debt','CL HOLDINGS LLC',2.0,2.0,'debt collector has to provide a consumer with a G notice. the right to dispute the alleged debt within 5 days of the initial communication with the consumer.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(991,'07/31/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','Case # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a response from the company stating that my payment was returned to my bank and the dispute was closed. They did not provide any documentation to show this and my bank has no record of the return. I had my bank on the phone to call them and received no answers other than they were going to reopen the dispute and would let me know. We are now over 2 1/2 months waiting for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to locate my large payment and it seems we are back to square one. This companys practices need to be examined because they seem very confused and disorganized. They dont appear to be a company who should be handling peoples money.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'a company has no record of the return of my payment. the dispute was closed and the company did not provide documentation.');
