back from someone running my name on the ground.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(993,'07/30/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','This complaint is associated with Wells Fargo Bank. I have had multiple accounts with Wells Fargo including a VISA credit card. Over time, I accumulated points by using that card. Recently I attempted to redeem rewards online without success. I went to a local Wells Fargo Bank to find out what was going on. I was told that Wells Fargo closed my VISA account. They maintained that I hadn''t used the account for some time and that they sent a letter to me notifying me that the account would be closed. I have no knowledge of any notice and, according to my card, it is not set to expire until XX/XX/2018. The person at the branch was also told that since my account was cancelled, all of my accumulated points were cancelled, as well, even though my online account still states that the points are valid. The person at the branch attempted to get a copy of the letter purported to have been sent to me but was told that a copy of that letter was not available.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a card was sent to me by Wells Fargo Bank to confirm that the points were valid. the card is not set to expire until XX/XX/2018 ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(994,'07/30/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','3 reporting credit beauru I haven''t been applying for credit cards I know I get rejected and with not so hot credit rating they think I''m made of money like Donald Trump I been fighting to get negative and inquiry removed and no luck and I''m tired of credit beauru treating me like either a little kid or criminal I even gone far to go with credit repair service and not getting anywhere fast and I refuse to get high interest loan and it''s not fair they all think I''m made of money like Donald Trump is which I''m not if I had Donald Trump money wouldn''t need credit but yet they give credit to illegal immigrants','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'credit beauru say they don''t want to get credit but give credit to illegal immigrants. they give credit to illegal immigrants.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(995,'07/30/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','Company sent out a letter which did not include the mini miranda or my right to dispute.','LINEBARGER GOGGAN BLAIR & SAMPSON LLP',2.0,2.0,'company sent out a letter which did not include the mini miranda or my right to dispute.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(996,'07/30/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','To Whom It May Concern : I have had correspondence with Wells Fargo over several letters and phone calls regarding account # # # # # # # # and the illegality of the foreclosure that occurred in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Again, this foreclosure was preventable, but Wells Fargo did everything in their power to make it unavoidable. The latest correspondence from Wells Fargo indicates that they offered a viable solution for us to stay in our home, but this is simply not true. The only modification we were offered on our home mortgage was for a temporary modification of $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/mo reduction of our mortgage. This was not a sustainable option and was only temporary. 

When we called Wells Fargo originally to discuss modification options, we were told we should not pay any amount of our mortgage in order to qualify for the HAMP modification. We were told to send many different sets of paperwork to Wells Fargo via fax. We sent all this paperwork in several times over and told almost every time that the paperwork was not received or was lost. Departments did not communicate with each other, so one person would not know what the last person had said or seen from us. We even sent things via mail because we were told so many times the faxes were not received or lost. We were told that Wells Fargo Home Mortgage could not communicate with Wells Fargo Home Equity so a combined decision on a loan modification was  impossible. 

Most recently, in the last letter received, Wells Fargo Home Mortgage indicated that the home equity loan was written off in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Unfortunately, we were not informed of this and continued to receive bills by mail for this loan. If we had known we could have only paid the home mortgage loan we could have afforded to stay in our home. 

Additionally, we qualified for a HAMP loan modification, but recently were told by Wells Fargo that they did not receive the required paperwork for this modification. We did send any and all paperwork we were asked to fill out and send because we were eager to stay in our home. We are so dismayed at the deceitful actions taken by Wells Fargo and have experienced a windfall of negative consequences due to this foreclosure that was preventable, but was forced upon us by Wells Fargos inability or their unwillingness to help our family stay in the home. 

Wells Fargo refuses to admit negligence in this matter and continues to ask us to provide evidence. Wells Fargo has evidence in their recorded calls and correspondence with us regarding the way they handled the matter. Faxes were lost, we were not informed in a timely manner, they did not want to help us stay in our home because we were paying Private Mortgage Insurance which  protected them from consequences of foreclosure, yet did not protect us as the homeowners.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',4.0,4.0,'the latest correspondence from Wells Fargo indicates that they offered a viable solution for us to stay in our home. the only modification we were offered on our home mortgage was for a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(997,'07/30/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I have made many attempts to remove debt collection company PORTFOLIO Recovery from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], this Debt collection company has been trying to collect a debt i do not owe in the amount of {$1800.00} for several months. 

I have messaged PORTFOLIO Recovery several times stating that this debt does not belong to me, i have requested copy of the original contract with my wet ink signature, i requested debt validation, i have requested voice recording or video surveillance of me signing up with the original creditor or agreeing to pay PORTFOLIO Recovery or the original creditor. I requested a photo copy of my id or a wet ink scanned signature. 

I have requested PORTFOLIO Recovery to provide a copy of certified letter and receipt that they claim that was sent to me. 

This company has not provided any of this after several request. 

This company keeps sending me in the mail a computer printed credit card statement with a name similar to mine with a balance that doesn''t show the purchase history, this statement doesn''t show what was purchased, where or when. This statement does not show itemized items of how this balance of {$1800.00} came to be. 

It appears to a be a fake credit card statement and a fraudulent debt generated by PORTFOLIO Recovery. 

I have never agreed to this debt, i never signed any contract or agreement to pay this debt with PORTFOLIO Recovery or any original creditor. 

What methods are being used by PORTFOLIO Recovery to validate this debt as accurate?','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,4.0,'debt collection company PORTFOLIO Recovery has been trying to collect a debt. he has requested a photo copy of his id or a wet ink');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(998,'07/29/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','I called CapitalOne concerning an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge that was on my card that i did not know about. I also told them that a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge was ok one time but it was not ok going forward because it is my X-Wife and she is no longer with me. The charge is for {$140.00} and is on my account twice without my permission. I can not stop the payments myself because i do not have the account information and this company never sends anything to this address in the mail. When i called they told me it''s all done via email and if I don''t have the account verification information then no account changes can be made. So i have these changes that will not stop. I told them to cancel the card and stop all payments to the account and they told me that all payments will be transferred to the new card per the agreement they have with Visa and Mastercard. So i can''t stop the charges unless i close the account. Closing the account will have a negative impact on my credit because i just opened the account less than a year ago. All that i asked them is to stop the charges they tell me they can''t. Please help me with this.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'i called capitalOne about an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge. the charge is for $140.00 and is on my account twice without my');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(999,'07/29/2018','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Applying for a mortgage','I was deceived into applying for a mortgage with Wells Fargo Bank on or about XX/XX/2018. I had previous experience with them as both a mortgage loan originator, and as a mortgage loan servicer, so I had no reasonable reason to believe that they would operate in any deceptive manor. 
