On XX/XX/2018 I was charged {$500.00} for what was supposed to be an independent appraisal that was supposed to be completed by a competent source, and was not to be controlled or influenced in any way by Wells Fargo Bank/Home Mortgage. 
That was absolutely not what occurred. Wells Fargo not only chose an unqualified and under compensated appraiser, they also put undo stress on the appraiser to control the outcome by limiting the appraiser ''s ability to properly comp the property.

The Appraiser [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( GA License # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) told the agent upon arrival that he hated doing appraisals for Wells Fargo, as they limited his scope, and they underpaid for the job. He was only paid {$280.00} for the appraisal, of the {$490.00} invoice. 
In turn, Mr [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] completed the appraisal at a value {$170000.00} below sales price. 
At that point, I brought this information to the attention of the licensed parties at Wells Fargo, and filed a formal complaint with their Compliance team, only to be left hanging with no result. As they simply denied the accusations, and confirmed the value with their Appraisal Escalation team.

There have been 2 formal appraisals completed following this by other appraisers, 1 opinion of value completed by a 3rd appraiser, and 2 BPO ''s completed by Agent/Brokers, all of which support the market value, and completely discount the appraisal completed by Mr [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Wells Faro has refused to refund my money.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'appraiser was charged $500.00 for what was supposed to be an independent appraisal. the appraiser was not controlled or influenced by Wells Fargo Bank/Home Mortgage');
