INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1013,'07/26/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','My oldest child [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was in a significant accident on XX/XX/2016. She was taken to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s hospital because of the severity of the injury and kept overnight with emergency [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the next morning. The accident occurred in a gymnastics center in the area. Not only did [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have medical insurance and coverage supplied through her father ''s employer she also had additional coverage for catastrophe by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have been constantly harrassed about a bill from this medical group because they did not file as requested by both my husband and my self for the additional coverage. I have documentation of all correspondence with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This company is fraudantly trying to ruin my credit by insisting that I pay them money they have already been paid and that I do not owe as insurance covered all expenses in full. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] turned this into collections and it in no way has anything to do with me! Again, simple solution they are covered in full, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has copies of the bills and correspondence was that if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] provided them with the specific itemized bill it would be paid. Companies like this collection agency should not be allowed to exist when they have complete control over getting paid. This is harrassment to attack my credit report, continue to call my phone etc.','Receivable Management Inc.',2.0,4.0,'a medical group has a bill covered in full, and the bill is covered in full. the company is fraudantly trying to ruin my credit by insisting that I pay them');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1014,'07/26/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Opening an account','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I visited the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] website and saw a publicly available page on the bank ''s website advertising a promotion for opening a checking account and meeting certain criteria. That website is, at the time of my signing up and at the time of writing this complaint, still accessible online and publicly available. 

The site says, " Earn up to {$400.00} with a new checking and savings account ... .must meet criteria - see below. '''' Upon looking below the headline, in the middle section of the site it says : " Choose which offer is right for you. Here ''s how : 1. Enter your email address on the form, and we''ll send you a promo code.

2. Bring the promo code to your nearest financial center.

3. Open your account ( s ) and complete qualifying activities. '''' While going through the sign up process, I had issues with the website and the signup process. On XX/XX/18, I called the support line to make sure everything was set up properly with the account. While on the phone, I decided to double check that the promo code was applied properly and asked the phone representative to check for me. The representative had to speak with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s back office employees, but shared two pieces of news to me.

1. I was not eligible to receive this promotion because according to the back office it was only for people who received a flyer in the mail and it was not for residents of Texas 2. It is illegal in Texas for a bank to give a bonus greater than {$150.00} Point # 2 appeared to be an outright lie from my perspective, because I have seen many advertisements in the branches of other banks in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advertising bonuses greater than {$150.00}. 

Point # 1 was news to me, because the site only says to enter your email address to receive a promo code for this bonus. Additionally, the site does not make any mention anywhere of specific states that are eligible, and does not specifically say that Texas residents are not eligible. 

When I disputed these points on the phone, I was instructed to go into a physical branch and I would be taken care of. 

I promptly drove to a branch 10 minutes from my location, and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about the issue. She repeated the same lines to me as the phone representatives did, except she added that the promotional code came from a third party. I flatly objected to that assertion, because the process to receive a promo code for this offer is by using a page that is publicly available on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] website at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] In my experience, when promotional offers are targeted to specific people, they receive a unique code in the mail. However, for this promotion a code can be received by anyone accessing this publicly available site. The site is quite clear that a promo code is required to receive the promotional offer, and that to receive a promo code one simply needs to request one by entering their email. The promo code form also asks you to enter your zipcode when requesting the promo code, so the bank was certainly aware that I was a Texas resident when I requested a promo code and before I signed up, yet the bank still sent me a promo code and allowed me to create a checking account. During the sign up process, there is even a box for you to enter the promo code and a button that says " verify promo code. '''' I used this button and did not receive any errors or messages saying I was not eligible.','WHITNEY BANK - NEW ORLEANS MAIN BRANCH',2.0,2.0,'a bank''s website advertises a promotion for opening a checking account. the site says, " Earn up to $400.00 with a new checking');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1015,'07/25/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Good Morning, I take pride in my credit and I value it very much. I have been trying to contact Experian and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  with regards to reporting a late payment from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on this account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the big issue is that they are lying about verifying the late payment when the company is out of business and has been for quite some time. These credit bureaus need to do their jobs and actually contact the company and verify what complaint/dispute is being made. This account has been closed out since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I have been trying to get this falsely 30 day late payment removed from this account and it still has a negative reporting on my credit profile. All I want is for them to do their job and get these 30 day late payments removed from my credit report as soon as possible. They are always saying that it was verified when they are not even contacting the company. 

Kind Regard, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',10.0,10.0,'credit bureaus have been lying about verifying the late payment. they are lying about verifying the late payment when the company is out of business. they are always saying that it was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1016,'07/25/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','This complaint is for the attention of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, the FTC, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the Equifax Credit Reporting Bureau. 

I am writing in reference to two accounts that I have sent numerous complaints about since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The issue is an account ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mortgage/Equity # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) that are past the statue of limitation and yet still displaying negative and destructive information on my report since over 7 years which should not be appearing on my file any longer. 

The very reason I ask that these two accounts to be deleted completely is because each and every time Equifax attempts to correct the inaccuracies it does not fix the issues on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Free Annual Credit Report, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The Remarks are the only information that keep changing along with the month to month status that are simply being deleted. Now, since Equifaxs last fix the remark on one account reads SETTLEMENT ACCEPTED ON THIS ACCOUNT, Bad Debt and Placed for collection and Skip since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. What on earth does that mean? What settlement? What bad debt and what collection? This is a government handled loan and was purchased many years ago by the FHA and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has nothing to do with this account and can not make such claims. By law produce to me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '' claims of this supposed " settlement '''' and produce court papers and send me information as to when and where this account was placed for collection and which company is handling the collection ; because this is all news to me. This is a government backed and purchased loan from a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] lawsuit for illegal loan appropriation. 

When I receive your dispute results and notice everything beside lates from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have been deleted I am very suspicious of your illegal practices and FCRA violation regarding reinvestigation laws. You should be very careful how you handle this going forward because I have thorough records of your illegal actions and I am ready to sue. 

The only correct way to fix this is to delete the 2 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts for mixed and inaccurate information. It is utterly illegal to allow this to continue. I have attempted to purchase two cars for my business in the last few months and have subsequently been declined a loan due to this inaccurate account. Please, I implore you to see my inquires to confirm this information as accurate. My business can not function without delivery vehicles and no company is entrusting me with a loan because of this old and mixed reporting. I can absolutely sue for damages, revenue loss and financial defamation, not to mention FCRA violations, but I am attempting to resolve this cordially and yet I am not being heard. I keep asking for a thorough and detailed dispute upon this matter but I am only met with insignificant changes to the remarks comments and dates sections of my credit report regarding the referenced account. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as well and they are terribly unhelpful and rude. 


Please reference my dispute sent via Certified Mail to Equifax in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( It should be in your records ) and also my first dispute on this website from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Please help me come to a proper resolution. Thank you all so much. 

PLEASE NOTE : My email address has changed.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a complaint is for the attention of the consumer financial protection bureau, the FTC, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the Equifax Credit Reporting Bureau.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1017,'07/25/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','Request for VALIDATION, NOT Verification [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Al [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2018 Wakefield and Associates RE : Accounts # To Whom It May Concern : This letter is being sent to you in response to notices sent to me from your company and more importantly, due to your erroneous reporting to the Credit Bureau { s }, the highly negative impact on my personal credit report. Please be advised that this is not a refusal to pay, but a notice sent pursuant to the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, 15 USC 1692g Sec. 809 { b } that your claim is disputed and validation is requested.

This is NOT a request for verification or proof of my mailing address, but a request for VALIDATION made pursuant to the above-named Title and Section. I respectfully request that your offices provide me with competent evidence that I have any legal obligation to pay you. 

Please provide me with the following : What the money you say I owe is for : Explain and show me how you calculated what you say I owe : Provide me with copies of any papers that show I agreed to pay what you say I owe : Provide a verification or copy of any judgment if applicable : Identify the original creditor : Prove the Statute of Limitations has not expired on this account : Show me the you are licensed to collect in my state : Provide me with your license numbers and Registered Agent or Agent of Service : At this time, I will also inform you that if your offices have reported invalidated information to any of the 3 major Credit Bureaus { [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] } this action might constitute fraud under both Federal and State Laws. Due to this fact, if any negative mark is found on any of my credit reports by your company or the company that you represent, I will not hesitate to bring legal action against you for the following : Violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act Violation of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act Defamation of Character If your offices can provide proper documentation as requested in the following Declaration, I will require at least 30 days to investigate this information and during such time all collection activity must cease and desist.

Also, during this validation period, if any action is taken which could be considered detrimental to any of my credit reports, I will consult with my legal counsel for suit. This includes listing any information with a credit reporting repository that could be inaccurate or invalidated or verifying an account as accurate, when in fact there is no provided proof that it is accurate.

If your company fails to respond to this validation request within 30 days from the date of your receipt, all references to this account must be deleted and completely removed from my credit report and a copy of such deletion { to any/all of the 3 major credit reporting bureaus : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] } request shall be sent to me immediately.

I would also like to request, in writing, that no telephone contact be made by your company to my home or my place of employment. If your offices attempt telephone communication with me, including but not limited to computer generated calls and calls or correspondence sent to or with any third parties, it will be considered harassment and I will have no choice but to file suit. All future communications with me MUST be done in writing and sent to the address noted in this letter by USPS.

It would be advisable that you assure your records are in order before I am forced to take legal action against your company and your client. This is an attempt to correct your records, any information obtained shall be used for that purpose. 


Best Regards, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','WAKEFIELD & ASSOCIATES, INC.',2.0,4.0,'request for VALIDATION, NOT verification is made pursuant to the above-named Title and Section. please provide me with the following: What the money you say I ow');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1018,'07/25/2018','Checking or savings account','Other banking product or service','Managing an account','I initiated a small transfer ( {$3700.00}. ) from an external bank ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ) to my Chase savings account on XX/XX/18. I was told by Chase the funds would be transferred in to my Chase account on XX/XX/18. On that day I logged into my Chase account, and there was a notice that my account had been suspended for suspicious activity, I had received no notice from Chase-no email, no text, none whatsoever, and I was scared that someone had accessed my account. I cancelled my appointment to meet someone, and called them. I literally had to speak to 4 people until I found out why they suspended my account-it was due to the transfer I had requested into my Chase savings account!. I was on the phone for close to an hour about this. They called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to ask if I had the funds to cover this, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] confirmed that I did have the funds. Then the Chase representative asked me, " What is the purpose of these funds you are transferring? '''' I told him it was none of his business, and he said he would not transfer my funds if I didn''t answer! I finally told him it was to buy something, but I felt violated and harassed by his coercing me to say this. I have filed a complaint with Chase, but I am contacting you because despite multiple calls to them, with multiple promises that the funds would be transferred, it has now been 5 business days, and they still have not transferred my money into my account. The money is listed under transfer activity on my Chase account ''s website page ( see attached ), but it is not even listed as pending. I have been a customer of Chase for many, many years, with not one single reason for them to do this. I have transferred funds with no problems in the past, NEVER EVER had any NSFs or any other problems. I have also complained to their Executive offices, and they promised me a return call, but they never called me.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a small transfer from an external bank to my Chase account was made. the money is listed under transfer activity on my account. the money is listed under transfer activity on my account ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1019,'07/25/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','The State of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Federal Court does not submit information of Public Records to ANY of the 3 credit bureaus, that was verified by me via mail with the State of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Federal Court - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], MO [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I had a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bankruptcy on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that is an outdated Public Record still being reported on my Credit Reports from Experian, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. All matters of Public Record that are not reported to the Credit Bureaus directly from the Federal Court, but by a third party data miner, are not to be considered valid or accurate. Please assist me in getting the Public Record from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] off of my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit Report. Thank you so much.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'State of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Federal Court does not submit information of Public Records to any of the 3 credit bureaus. I had a Chapter [COM');
