INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1040,'07/20/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Written notification about debt','I received a served notice stating that I was taken to court ( without notice in XX/XX/2018 ). Which I found to be false when I called the city court of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They stated they ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) just filed something but it wasn''t complete in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was going to try to work something out, although this is not my debt. My information was taken by someone that was a visitor in my home. I explained to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I have no money I am on a fixed income with the federal aid. I can not afford to pay this debt that I didn''t create. The letter I was served with is not correct and I think or feel I should not have to pay','Resurgent Capital Services L.P.',2.0,2.0,'a served notice was issued stating that I was taken to court. the city court of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said they just filed something but it wasn');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1041,'07/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I started running into some financial trouble. After the recession hit, I tried working with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to reduce the interest rate on my mortgage, which was currently 12+ %, to help reduce the payment. I had requested a reduction to half, even though at the time, the current interest rates were between 2 to 3 %. When that did not work, in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I tried to short sale the home, but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was unwilling to work with me regarding that also. Several different departments at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] suggested I dont pay and fall behind a couple of months then they would be more likely to work with me to help reduce my mortgage payment. That turned out to be a total lie and after a couple months I started receiving letters threatening foreclose and advising me to vacate the home I have lived in for 17 years. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the company that was trying to help with the short sale contacted me and informed me that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had filed a Notice of Default and had begun the foreclosure process. During that time, I had never even missed payment. Not realizing that these were lies, I moved from my home. I filed a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcy XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At the time of the filing, my house was surrendered to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I made every payment to the Trustee on time for 4 years and my bankruptcy was discharged in good standing on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After waiting the necessary time to pass after a bankruptcy I recently started looking for a new home. I was surprised to find out, that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not foreclose on my home until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 10 months after my bankruptcy was discharged. Please keep in mind that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] new quite well that they had ownership of the house because they provided yard care ( both summer and winter ) the entire 5 years it sat vacant. It was also brought to my attention that 4 months after the discharge of my bankruptcy they sold the servicing of the loan to another company. I quit receiving any type of notification from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] shortly after I filed.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage company was trying to short sell a home in XX/XX. it was a lie and a couple months ago, a company called me ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1042,'07/20/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Trouble using your card','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I checked my card account with American Express. I noticed that they had lowered my credit limit from {$11000.00} to {$3800.00}, and I was confused as to why. When I called in, I spoke to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who then transferred me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], he then read a script saying that they checked my credit report with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and reevaluated my relationship. Based upon what they found, they decided that it was best to lower my credit limit. I expressed to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I had several problems with this. First, my account with them has NEVER been late. I have been a member since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I have never missed a payment on any of my accounts. Second, my credit is excellent and my income is also great. I also find it very odd that they decided to do this after they denied me for another credit card ( I submitted an application four days ago for it ). I almost feel as if I am being punished for asking for an additional card, even though I have excellent history with them. This situation is humiliating and as a result of them lowering my available credit line, it looks as if I am maxing out my credit cards with them which will impact my credit score negatively. There has to be some type of protection for someone in my situation, and the representative was not helpful. I am trying to purchase another home next year, and I feel that this will impact my ability to qualify.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a member of the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has never missed a payment on any of my accounts. a member');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1043,'07/20/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Dear Sir/Madam, Our flood insurance policy was re-written by the insurance company due to late payment. As a result, the insurance premium has increased. Our mortgage company ( Chase ) is  responsible for paying our insurance premiums on time. However, the payment was received late causing the policy to lapse. 

Our insurance agent claimed that the insurance renewal notice was sent to Chase ( Our mortgage company ) with the due date of XX/XX/2018. The payment was not received until XX/XX/2018, which was 2 days past the grace period. 

Chase, the mortgage company, claimed that the insurance payment was issued on XX/XX/2018. However, it was returned on XX/XX/2018. They called the insurance company and was told the payment was sent back in error. Chase then issued another payment on XX/XX/2018. However, it''s two days past the grace period and the insurance company considered the policy had lapsed and re-wrote the policy. 

It seems that both Chase and the insurance company are not willing to take responsibility for the mistake and are pointing fingers at each other. 

As a consumer, we just know that it''s not our mistake that this happened. We are the victim of the bureaucracy between two companies. 

Please help!','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'insurance company re-written flood insurance policy due to late payment. insurance premiums have increased.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1044,'07/20/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I have been trying for the past two years to get these loans forgiven because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] scammed me. The loan I have has been very unhelpful with me to the point where Ive had to hire a lawyer to help me get some things done. The loan company has also pretend to help me by giving me fake phone numbers and having me call a number that has nothing to do with what I need. 

I also have no degree because of this and can not get a job in my field. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claims and told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  that I graduated but there is no proof. The company that took over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] transcripts has no degree for me.','GREAT LAKES',2.0,2.0,'loan company pretends to help me by giving me fake phone numbers. company that took over transcripts has no degree for me.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1045,'07/19/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have filed dispute before but I didnt receive any response. My credit score is being affected due to something which I am not reliable of. 

My credit score shouldnt be hurtled due to some other companies mistakes or until and unless they are entirely sure if I owe the amount and I am reliable to pay it. 

