I also currently work for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and am unfamiliar with the legal system so there was miscommunication regarding the paperwork for the garnishment with said company I work for. My checks were then garnished ( before the court made a final decision ) and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] began continuously receiving money from my checks despite my attempt to contact them to explain this. The head branch manager at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] location refused to return any funds to me and threatened to sue me again even if the judge does find me exempt for that moment. I''ve even mailed proof of why I''m exempt but found out in court ( late XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) they were not going to even present it because the attorney they sent was very unprepared and knew nothing about my case. They still ended up receiving up to {$600.00} and I requested a refund of this which the person ( head branch manager ) responded to with a " sure ''''. I''ve not heard back since but I do see that they have initiated yet another attempt to wage garnish me. They have not even updated the amount that was originally owed to reflect the funds they should have never received from the beginning. I''ve received nothing but rude and condescending treatment from the head branch manager but most importantly can''t believe they would follow through with illegal and immoral practices in attempts to collect a debt that would be considered " small '''' given that they are a bank.','MIDCOUNTRY FINANCIAL CORP',2.0,2.0,'a debt I fell behind years ago was a wage garnishment. the head branch manager refused to return any funds to me. the judge has now decided to sue me for');
