INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1147,'06/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to be guided on a personal loan I wanted to request and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] let me know the documents I had to provide. On Monday, XX/XX/2018 I sent the application online and then I sent the other documents by email as required by the instructions. The same day, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me to let me know that he was going to send me the application by email because the system had not registered it when I filled it out online. Immediately I proceeded to fill it out and sent it to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s email so he could process it. Today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me to inform me that he needed my husband ''s information so he could process the request. I informed him that the loan was going to be requested only by me since my husband has the credit very affected and I did not want that to affect the low interest rate that they could offer me if I did it by myself. I mentioned that I had previously obtained loans without including my husband, but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] replied that including the spouse was a rule of the bank. I told him that I didnt know that it was mandatory to request with the husband since it wasnt explained in the web page instructions, not in the application and not when I called to get the orientation. I told him that if I had seen that rule before I would not have applied for the loan because I wanted to do it by myself. I asked him if he had obtained my credit report and he said yes, that he had it with him and that the score had gone very well. I understand that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]