INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1154,'06/26/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','I have been a client with Citibank for over 30 years. My wife and i have a joint checking and savings account. In XX/XX/2018 we received notification of a Know Your Client program at Citibank, which honestly appeared as if it were a scam. I went into a branch and after checking with the branch manager, and being assured it was real, answered the questions over a telephone line clearly outside of the United States. I felt the questions were quite intrusive ( including employment information, salary information, etc. ). My wife had received the same correspondence. We assumed since it was a joint account with my name listed first, because I had answered the questions no further action was required. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we went to withdraw funds and discovered our account had been frozen. We immediately called, found that they needed the same questions answered by my wife, and we immediately provided the information. We were promised the account would be unfrozen. In the meantime, the bank bounced all of our checks and we had no access to our funds or to make transfers. During the ensuing four weeks, we have called daily and lodged complaints, and requests for the accounts to be unfrozen, all to no avail. We still have no access to our funds or our account.','CITIBANK, N.A.',4.0,4.0,'a client at Citibank has a joint checking and savings account. the bank bounced all of our checks and we had no access to our funds.');
