INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1163,'06/25/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of this year I applied for the IBR and had not revived a response on approval. I was offered forbearance and felt forced to take it as a result of not being able to get a hold of Navient. Despite harrassment almost every other day with them filling up my inbox they never called or sent a physical letter until last week threatening action with wage garnishment or tax penalty and so on. I did attempt to reply to the email and it was not responded to. This has effected my credit score drastically and it''s become damaging to the point where it is impossible for me to rebound back from. I have never had an issue before and I was always able to renew my IBR yearly. I was told I needed spousal signature but we never able to log in. Either times it was submitted. Evn after I have gotten a ton of emails saying I owe more and more.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of this year I applied for the IBR. I had not revived a response on approval. despite h');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1164,'06/25/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','We got flooded in XX/XX/2016 in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Louisiana and chase got our flood insurance check. We have a licensed contractor. They make excuses and excuses to release funds to us to pay the contractors. Our house is damaged still not done because chase will not release funds. We recently got a letter saying they are selling our mortgage. The only reason they are doing this is because our house is damaged and they want to hold on to our money as long as they can.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'chase got our flood insurance check in XX/XX/2016. we have a licensed contractor. they release funds to us to pay the contractors.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1165,'06/24/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Portfolio Recovery Associates is reporting on my credit report as a factoring company and is not a factoring company, they are a debt buyer. This is a violation of FCRA .Also on the account the terms are listed as one month. I never made agreement with PRA on terms for this account which is inaccurate and violation of FCRA.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,2.0,'this is a violation of FCRA.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1166,'06/24/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Lease','Incorrect information on your report','In XX/XX/2017 my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had GM Financial as an autopay account in the amount of {$400.00}. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] issued the check and removed the funds out of my account. This had been established and working for months prior and after. Apparently GM financial claims to not have received the check. GM Financial did not inform me they didn''t receive the check until 60 days later. I provided them with my bank statements and autopay history to show them the check was sent and the funds were removed from my account. When they could not find the check I stopped payment and reissued a check which was received. They are continuing to report that I was delinquent on my account for the months of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I did issue the check and have it mailed to them at the correct address. I never missed a payment or was late on any payments before and I am upset they did not inform me before the account was 60 days delinquent. I believe they lost the check and I am being reported negatively on my credit score for it when I have always paid my lease on time.','GENERAL MOTORS FINANCIAL COMPANY, INC.',2.0,2.0,'GM Financial did not inform me they didn''t receive the check until 60 days later. GM Financial did not inform me they didn''t receive the check until 60 days later ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1167,'06/23/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I''m requesting that the following accounts be blocked from my credit report. The credit reporting agencies will investigate and report back verified, but verified by whom, and supported by what physical documentation. As a consumer I have the right to request this so called vertification. However, I will file a law suit in my next attempt at this if for some reason this is again verified without providing me physical documentation. The following accounts in question are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] )','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the following accounts in question are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the credit reporting agencies will investigate and report');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1168,'06/23/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I mailed a debt validation letter to the three credit bureaus ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) requesting they validate my owing Midland Credit Management for a debt they purchased from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On Tuesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a phone call from a representative at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who stated he was an account manager, wanting to discuss the alleged debt. At which time I expressed to him, I would not be discussing anything pertaining to the alleged debt over the phone and I request that he mail me validation of the alleged debt. The rep then placed me on hold so he could speak with his superior. A few short moments later another person got on the phone and identified himself as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Supervisor. He too wanted to discuss the debt, but again I refused and reiterated, I needed in writing, validation of the debt. He asked me to be specific about what I was requesting of him and I went on to list : signature agreement of my taking ownership of the debt, the bill and all other documentation they have that proves my indebtedness to their company. He stated, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has already mailed me information about the debt. At which point, I respond by telling him I have no knowledge of the information or paperwork he was speaking of. He assured me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] could provide all of the validation I was requesting. However, he could not understand why we couldn''t discuss the debt at that moment over the phone? Again, I told him I would not be discussing anything with anyone at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] pertaining to any debt until I have received in writing complete validation of the alleged debt. He remained persistent and consistent in his approach. He stated, " He could not understand why I wanted to wait? And, he guessed we''d have to wait another 10 days to handle the matter. '''' I remained adamant about my request and the call ended. 

I have been checking the mail daily as I waited to see what would be sent to me as validation. Today XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a double enveloped bill. The date listed as the mailed date is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which means it has taken exactly one month for the bill to reach me by mail. I find this hard to believe! Also, the bill  quotes a settlement and tells me in order to benefit I would have to respond by XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is less than one week from today. I find this to be suspicious, erroneous and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] way of trying to cover ground they have failed already cover. 

According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act U.S.C. section 1681g, I have the right to demand [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] furnish me documents they have recorded and retained in there files concerning accounts they are reporting in my credit reports. At this point, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has received several request for validation of the debt and have demonstrated by way of failing to furnish the requested validation that they are not able to validate. Thus, by law, they must delete.','ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.',2.0,2.0,'on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I mailed a debt validation letter to the three credit bureaus. they asked me to');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1169,'06/22/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Good morning, We''re reaching out to you, in the hopes that you will assist us, with our negotiations, with Ocwen loan servicing. 

We are WELL aware of the fact that Ocwen has a very long history of deception and fraud, when it comes to dealing with distressed homeowners and we need your help in our situation. 

We began our negotiations with them on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At that time we got a snapshot of our account status and we told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that we would be submitting all paperwork required for review of our loan. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She informed us that all 52 pages that we faxed, were documented, imaged in and that the review process would begin within 3 to 5 business days. 

During the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we were required to resubmit the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] form, along with proof that my husband, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], was the Executor of the Estate on this account.. TWICE. We did so happily. 

During the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we''ve had contacts with them on a weekly basis and each of those conversations, we were told that our request for modification was being reviewed. 

We spoke with Ocwen on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and then to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At that point we were told that NO modification was being reviewed. 

We requested to be transferred to a supervisor and we spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He told us that the original request for modification was, in fact, closed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Meaning - Ocwen has been lying to us for the past 3 weeks. 

In order to review this loan for modification, a request ticket for an Assumption Modification must be made first. Documentation must be submitted for that and once approved, the formal modification can be completed. This was discussed during the very first conversation we had with Ocwen and they agreed that this would be done simultaneously, with our request. 

All of the notes from our conversations are attached to this complaint and we''re asking that you reach out to Ocwen immediately, so they take this matter seriously and we get to where we need to be as quickly as possible. 

Thank you for your help with this!','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,4.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] started negotiations with ocwen loan servicing. we told them that all 52 pages that we');
