INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1172,'06/22/2018','Mortgage','Home equity loan or line of credit (HELOC)','Trouble during payment process','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Complaint Re : Wells Fargo Bank In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I opened a NOW Line account at a local

branch with a limit of {$40000.00}. It was a Home equity product as it was sold to me. My home being used as security. Yesterday, while reviewing a subordination agreement I discovered Wells Fargo had placed a {$200000.00} lien on my property. NOT {$40000.00}! I NEVER authorized this. In fact, I have the original document the Now Line card came on clearly showing a credit limit of {$40000.00}. I also have a statement from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which also shows a credit limit of {$40000.00}. They have subsequently provided a deed/lien document with my signature on the second page. Yet, the first page which states a {$200000.00} credit limit is distinctly missing my initials. I firmly believe this page was replaced after signing. 
Further, I reviewed my modification documents dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and to my horror realized I had missed the statement of the original loan amount of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It never was {$200000.00}. However, the modification states Wells Fargo was to amend security documents to reflect the new agreement which would be a balance of {$36000.00}. Therefore the lien should have been amended. It was not. The subordination agreement is dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They now claim they do not have to change the lien despite the fact that the modification clearly states that. 
Additionally, as part of the modification Wells Fargo was to correct and bring current my credit history with all three bureaus. To date despite repeated calls and complaints, this has not occurred. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is still in error. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are somewhat corrected. 
Another issue is the proper application of payment to principal and interest. This is a fixed rate and term equity line with a fixed balance. 22.6 years, at 9.65 %. My most recent statement showed a finance charge of {$310.00} and principal of {$16.00}. The original loan amount was {$36000.00}. If you amortize it at 23 years, the principal would be {$37.00} by this payment! They now claim they can not provide an amortization schedule as it is a simple interest loan. This was NEVER disclosed to me.

To be quite honest, this is just the latest nightmare with this company. Over the years, Ive been lied to, overcharged, told we will not put that in writing when I requested a modification to terms years ago due to hardship and subjected to all manner of deception. 
I came back to the table with good intentions given their public relations campaign of the new Wells Fargo. I entered in to a modification with the intention of absolutely adhering to my obligation. Only to find that Wells Fargo is in fact, the same Wells Fargo of the days past. Since the modification I have endured nothing but continued stress which given my health ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] due to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) is incredibly detrimental. Its as if each day Im on the phone filing yet another complaint with them only to be told its being researched and theyll get back to me. Theres yet to be a resolution. My complaints have been escalated to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] however this is the third person who was supposed to resolve them prior to the lien issue which I just discovered. How long am I supposed to wait?! 
At this point I want everything corrected but I also want a punitive aspect. They need to be held accountable for their behavior. Fining them has proved pointless. They need to actually pay for their grievous behavior to the consumers theyve impacted such as myself. To place a {$200000.00} lien on someones home for a {$40000.00} equity line? Utilizing a fraudulent document? That rises to the level of a crime and that needs to be answered for.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'NOW Line has a lien on my property with a limit of $40000.00. the lien was placed on my property by Wells Fargo. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1173,'06/22/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I am writing a response to Helvey & Associates regarding a FTC avid avid and request for removal. A police report has been filed with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] military police. Documentation has been sent to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Indiana and will also be sent to you and will arrive soon. However, the item needs to be taken down immediately. I will also forward you letter to the FTC with police report as well. I have forwarded your response to the corresponding officer and my attorney. If the items is not removed immediately I will move forward with civil suite . Once again I ask that you remove this item from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  report. I would like to work this out with you but if a resolution if not met I will seek further legal action.','Helvey & Associates',2.0,2.0,'a police report has been filed with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] military police. the item needs to be taken down immediately.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1174,'06/22/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','My daughter missed her first payment to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I found out and called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to handle this ( I cosigned ). The rep told me he sees it all the time, and I should just take over payments. He offered me a reduced interest rate as incentive, and I agreed. 

I made the first payment that night ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and continued over the next months as per the agreement. However, in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that they rescinded the offer made in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I was now several months late ( even though they were still taking payments directly from my account ). 

Within 2 days I paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they said was now due. In any case it was too late and they reported me as delinquent to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I wrote [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a letter explaining this, and they refused to remove the mark. 

They did call me between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], telling me I was late ( even though they were auto debiting the full amount from my account ). I''d call and explain the agreement, and they would apologize for the confusion, assuring me it was a system error or some such. 

I have email history from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account, which I can provide if necessary ( just need to make sure I''m not crossing legal lines in doing so ). I also have detailed notes about all of this.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',4.0,4.0,'a rep told me he sees it all the time, and I should just take over payments. in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they said was now');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1175,'06/21/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I''ve been mailing letters to the credit bureau for the last 8 months about these student loans on my report. I have never attended a college with student loans. I have been incarcerated for some time. I am now trying to get my life back together by getting my credit up to standard, but I can''t because these fraudulent student loans is on my report. 
It has been taken off [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but some reason Equifax is staying. I need to know what to do from here.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'i have never attended a college with student loans. I have been incarcerated for some time.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1176,'06/21/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a notice that my loan from Loan Depot was being transferred to another division. On the letter it stated my old loan number and my new loan number. the new loan number was the same as the old except for one less digit. I made my payment on time with the new loan number and to the address on the letter. 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a call that I hadn''t paid my mortgage. I checked with my bank and they showed it was received by Loandepot via ACH. When I told Loan Depot this and told them the account number they said I put the wrong account number on there and and they gave me another number. I was transferred back and forth from their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] office which is where the payment went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The person at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  office saw that the problem was that someone at Loandepot had inadvertently put the wrong account number on the letter I received XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She said she would take care of it. 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received an email stating they had called an weren''t able to get in contact with me. I take my phone everywhere and there are no unanswered calls. I called the number on the email and they said they were see the payment but couldn''t put it on the right account, which just seems [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Loandepot has the payment, see where they made the error, but now they won''t correct their error.

Loan Depot is acting in bad faith and not trying to help find my payment and they keep passing the buck around.','loanDepot.com, LLC',2.0,2.0,'loan from loandepot was transferred to another division. on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a notice that my loan');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1177,'06/21/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','Please provide policy guidance regarding the Consumer Review Fairness Act ( https : //www.ftc.gov/tips-advice/business-center/guidance/consumer-review-fairness-act-what-businesses-need-know ). 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a phone call from the Executive Offices group of American Express, threatening me to delete a meme ( https : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) I had posted on Twitter, which''s my honest review regarding the execrable overseas Customer Care of American Express [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which has been, and is expressed by thousands of people on Twitter. 


I also have a recording of that phone call, in which the caller, identifying himself as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( didn''t get his last name ) from the American Express Executive Offices, claimed that the meme I had created, which is based on a popular [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a famous American comedian ) meme theme ( https : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), is related to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and American Express doesn''t want to be associated with violent images, so it won''t tolerate such memes. 
American Express '' desire to have that meme deleted seems to stem from the fact ( https : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) that people are more likely to share memes on social media, than they''re to share tweets without images, such as this one ( https : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 


In retaliation for posting screenshots of chats that portray one of its overseas [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] being highly unprofessional & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] team ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) of American Express has also been denying Customer Service to me since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Does the right to refuse service hold sway over the Consumer Review Fairness Act if a company ''s punitive sanctions against a customer are guided by posting honest reviews online? I hadn''t even been remotely rude to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] team since when it has been refusing to serve me. The caller had also lied to me that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] team would resume providing customer service to me after I''d delete those tweets. Since consumers ding their credit for getting credit cards, being denied customer service is a huge issue! I had raised CFPB complaint [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in this regard ( denial of customer service ). 


American Express '' punitive sanctions against me go a lot further than this. 
It has frozen my Membership Rewards points, although they''re listed as available. 
I''ve been told by multiple American Express supervisors in no uncertain terms that it''d take 6-10 weeks and no less, for the points to actually be available for redemption, but not a single reason has been provided as to what triggered this action. 
Such actions are usually taken if American Express suspects fraud, but all my transactions are legitimate, and despite my requests, American Express hasn''t even deigned to explain which transactions it suspects to be fraudulent. 
From what I gather from the CFPB complaint database, I''m far from the only one to  have faced such an issue with American Express. 
In fact, this practice by American Express satisfies the enforcement-action criteria for FTC Act ''s Section 5 ( Unfair or Deceptive Acts or Practices ), because there''s no way customers can avoid freezing of Membership Rewards points without being given as much as an explanation, so I''m not sure why the FTC/CFPB are reluctant to take any action against American Express. I had raised CFPB complaint [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & FTC complaint [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in this regard. I''ll send another email to relevant FTC & CFPB officials regarding how exactly American Express '' practices meet the stated criteria for enforcement-action, quoting other CFPB complaints on this issue, although I do understand that I''m not in any position to call the shots. 


Coming back to the issue raised in this complaint, if the FTC & CFPB determine that American Express is right to force me to delete that meme, I''ll delete it. But please also provide policy guidance regarding other issues in the email as well, as they seem to lack any precedent. This complaint will also be emailed to relevant FTC & CFPB officials.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a call from the executive offices group of American Express threatened me to delete a meme. the caller, identifying himself as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1178,'06/21/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','I have multiple inquiries on my report that i have no idea you authorized them to pull my report','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'i have multiple inquiries on my report that i have no idea you authorized them to pull my report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1179,'06/21/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my wife, who normally takes care of all household finances, was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was diagnosed with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which made her very ill for the duration of her [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. During this time, most of our bills were set up on automatic payments, but this Mortgage, in my name only, was unfortunately not. I take full responsibility here, I had the ability to pay, but with a sick wife and then a new [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at home, I fell behind on my payments. 

I have since caught up and will be making regular payments moving forward. I have been very happy with the service, but realize I was not the ideal customer and have made mistakes with the handling of the account. I became aware of the unpaid balance when I got a copy of my credit report in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I know that payment was my responsibility and I am not attempting to justify this breach of my user agreement. I was, however, hoping you might review the circumstances under which this non-payment occurred and consider removing the negative trade line associated with this account from my three credit reports. I have already contacted the Mortgage Company was told that they won''t do a good will adjustment, nor are they willing to help me fix the credit history. 

Wells Fargo has also continually lied about my account status. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a rep there told me I was able to make my next Payment in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but when I went to make the payment I was told my house had been put in foreclosure.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a new wife and a sick wife were diagnosed with a mortgage. they were told their house had been put in foreclosure. they have lied about their account status.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1180,'06/20/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Trouble using your card','I logged into my account today ( XX/XX/2018 ) and discovered I had no available credit despite utilizing less than {$600.00} of my {$2500.00} limit. I called customer service, and they told me that this was a computer issue impacting thousands of customers, and they were working on it but nothing could be done right now. I was NEVER notified of this issue. I only found out because I logged into my account and called. Later, I tried to submit a secure message on the credit card website, and that was not working either! None of my issues have been fixed.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'logged into my account today ( XX/XX/2018) and found no available credit. despite using less than $600.00 of my $250');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1181,'06/20/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','False statements or representation','Per credit report from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dated XX/XX/18. Grant Mercantile Agency has opened ( 3 ) Collection accounts on my credit, each in the amount of {$3300.00} ( all duplicate ) for a total of {$9900.00}. This is either an error or fraudulent activity by Grant Mercantile Agency. I will authorize 30 days to Grant Mercantile to correct the error. If not corrected by XX/XX/18 a lawsuit will be filed against Grant Mercantile Agency for all damages incurred for this error and/or fraudulent activity.','Grant Mercantile Agency',2.0,4.0,'Grant Mercantile Agency has opened 3 collections accounts on my credit. each account is in the amount of $3300.00 ( all duplicate ). this is either an error');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1182,'06/20/2018','Mortgage','VA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] customer service person at Pacific Union Financial said they over paid our annual homeowners insurance premium because they made a typographical error. As a result, this created a huge escrow shortage in our account. Due to their error, they raised our mortgage payment. Pacific Union paid our annual homeowners insurance premium in the amount of {$2200.00} instead of {$290.00} and as of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] our house note went from {$700.00} to {$1100.00} a month. They were previously taking out {$150.00} a month for taxes and insurance out of our escrow account up until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. As of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], they now take out {$550.00} a month out of our escrow account. 
In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we got a check from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$2000.00} for overpayment. There was no accompanying letter so we thought we over paid something. We have since made a {$2000.00} payment back to Pacific Union but our account still has not been corrected. We were told they would have to do an escrow analysis first before they could fix our account and lower our house note. Then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said they would have to wait for taxes to be paid before they could do an escrow analysis. We called so many times and talked to so many people and were always told to call back in a few days, a few weeks etc., but our account still has not been corrected even though taxes have been paid. We have asked to speak to a supervisor and get put on hold and no one ever picks up. We have asked for supervisor or management names and info as to where to complain about this but were told they didn''t have that information! This is horrible and a total nightmare. We have also been given conflicting information by some of the customer service people who said our house payment went up because Pacific Union mistakenly bought unnecessary flood insurance ( we already have flood insurance through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). We were even told we were going to get a refund however, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that was not true and our account was never charged for that. 

I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old and a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] veteran. My wife is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We live on Social Security and trying to come up with {$1100.00} a month is a huge struggle for us especially when they are the one who caused this problem. We have never missed a payment or made a late payment but we don''t know how long we can keep up having to pay {$1100.00} instead of {$700.00}. Our other bills have to be paid, too. We need our account corrected and our payment lowered and no one at Pacific Union has done anything to fix this. We need immediate assistance as our money is dwindling and we don''t want to lose our home because of a typographical error. PLEASE HELP US!','Pacific Union Financial, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a typographical error caused a huge escrow shortage in our account. they raised our mortgage payment due to their error. they have since made a $200');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1183,'06/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','The debt collector ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) has falsely " parked '''' old debt on to my credit report that was found to part of identity theft from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They have tried to " reage '''' this debt onto my credit report as being opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and owing {$1200.00}. They have also falsely and illegally reported twice on this same account for another {$1200.00}, and have falsely said this was opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Equifax continues to allow them to report twice on the same account despite several attempts to explain what has happened. It is clear on my credit report that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has reported falsely twice on the same account. I am calling into question Equifax investigation into my accounts. I have explained that this account was fraudulent and has been removed from my credit report several years ago. 
It has now " reappeared '''' on my account as an attempt to ruin my credit profile and collect a debt that is not mine. I have asked Equifax what information they have received that is proof that it is my account and they have told me over the phone that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] says its my accounts and that they have confirmed that I owe the amounts. So I asked them if they just take their word on it or actually receive proof. 
Their response was that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] responded that I owed the money. I have an issue with Equifax reporting on two of the same accounts because in their words " have different account numbers ''''. These new account numbers are made up and one account is named " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' as if this account is new. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] recovery services has illegally harmed my credit on a debt that is not mine. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] cleared this identity theft over 3 or 4 years ago. I have written [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no response. I have asked them to remove this from my debt as I do not owe on this debt. I have also asked Equifax to properly gain proof this is my account, which they have not done. Not only has [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] refused to give me information on this debt, they have now double reported on my credit report in an effort to collect more money from me. Equifax has allowed them to do so. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has cleared this up over 3 years ago. My next step is to sue them in court if this is not resolved. I have attempted to get this fixed for almost 2 years now with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Equifax. They have falsely reported wrong information on my credit report with Equifax, with the sole purpose of keeping this debt " alive '''', when it should have been removed from statue of limitations in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and when this was found to be used from identity theft years ago. Because this information was removed over 3 years ago from my credit report I did not keep that paperwork as I thought it was final and I have since moved several times. The original debtor was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and had been removed from my credit report only for them to sell this wrongful debt to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after it had been found to be part of several accounts used as part of identity theft. I have asked for any signatures of mine, driver license, proof that this was my account and have yet to receive anything back. Please help me get this matter resolved as I feel extorted to pay two debts on an otherwise clean credit profile while Im looking to purchase a home. After an inquiry on a mortgage is when the 2nd reporting of the {$1200.00} debt was added to my credit report. Equifax investigation practices should require proof that both of these are my accounts and shold have been able to see that the 2nd account was a duplicate account for the same exact amount and removed it immediately. Thank you for your assistance.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'debt collector falsely reported falsely on credit report. they have also falsely reported twice on same account. they have also falsely said this was opened XX/XX');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1184,'06/20/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Struggling to pay your loan','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2018 I called Chase Auto Finance to request a 60 day extension on my Auto Loan. Due to the the fact I was having a financial difficulty and I needed the extension not only to get caught up but to get some breathing room due to the past few months have been very hard on me financially. My spouse fell ill and has not been able to work leaving me the primary caretaker of our home and children. So prior to the call my reason was that and in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2018 I was a victim to damage to my current car that I requested the extension on. I was driving down the highway and someone transporting bulk waste didn''t tie down the contents and debris came and hit my hood windshield and undercarriage. I was not able to catch up to the car due to the accident it cause I had to pull over. So I have to pay for this out of pocket and the expenses are well over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This includes repairs and rental car and fuel. I just needed help. So I called Chase explained this to them today XX/XX/2018 I was told that I as eligible transferred to a specialist explained my position and was denied. Keep in mind my account has never been 30 days late ... I always pay between 7 - 17 days past due. I have never had a late fee until now and I have had this loan going on 36 months. I need help and I need my 60- day extension granted so that I can pay my loan','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2018 I called Chase Auto Finance to request a 60 day extension on my Auto Loan. my account has never been 30 days');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1185,'06/20/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Lease','Managing the loan or lease','In XX/XX/2018 we were referred to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] authorized person at the dealership worked out a lease deal for us that would give us payments of about {$390.00} per month. The lease was no money down, no first month ''s payment, and no security deposit which is a standard [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] deal. The lease term was 48 months with a residual value of {$18000.00} and a 10,000 mile per year. Well before we drove the two hours to get to the dealership I submitted the online application and BOTH [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Volkswagen Credit ran my credit report as a hard inquiry. We had provided a deposit to hold the car when they confirmed the lease and payment and they said that would either be applied to the lease to further reduce our {$390.00} payment or we could have it refunded. We arrived at the dealership to pick up the car which we had been assured several times was ready and all we would have to do was " sign and drive. '''' That turned out to be a lie. The dealership said they could not verify my income ( I am a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employee and I had already provided my past three Earnings and Leave Statements ) Then I was told that I was not allowed to use my rental income then they told me it was not necessary. Then they ran hard credit inquiries three more times which by the end trashed my credit score and then came to me and told me because they could not " verify my income '''' and because I had so many hard inquiries the only way they could make the " deal '''' was to add an extra {$120.00} the the payment ( going from {$400.00} per month to {$520.00} ) and they would now require that I pay {$1200.00} up front and have a higher payment than what was promised. They also claimed that they could not verify that I had any previous car loans -- although I had a lease with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   that was paid off early and still shows up in my Volkswagen online account. The other was an actual car loan through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was paid off in advance also. The series of lies were designed to increase the cost of the vehicle significantly -- {$6200.00} over the term of the lease. We were told our deposit would not be refunded if we did not complete the deal because they had taken the car out of stock and held it for us.','VW Credit',2.0,4.0,'the dealership said they could not verify my income. the dealership said they could not verify my income. the dealership said they could not verify my income.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1186,'06/19/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I have contacted this company 4 times, each time I get a different story. I would like to get this debt settled but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] says that they will not remove or delete this off of my credit file.I have offered to pay them 30 % of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which come to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I learned they bought this debt for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Everyone I spoke to was nice but was never able to assist me with this issue. I would like this item completed removed from my profile. I have asked them to please send me a letter to my address on their letter head stating that once I pay this amount they will remove and delete this from my credit report. Please help I would like to soon move into a home and this derogatory mark is preventing me from home ownership. Please CFPB I really need your assistance on this.','Convergent Resources, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a company has bought this debt for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. they will not remove or delete this from my credit file. I have contacted this');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1187,'06/19/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','Bank of America pick and chooses which check to hold. I have been banking with BOA and their policy has changed drastically. The check they hold do not apply to any of their hold policies. 

On XX/XX/2018 - 2 check out of 10 were held with no apparent reason. I have a history of depositing check from these same venders with no issues. I have a 20 year history of banking with BOA and now I''m unsure of which check they will hold. 
I called and spoke with a BOA Representative and I was told " they could not get verification from the bank '''' Is that just a way from BOA to hold my money and make interest on it. 

As Per BOA Web site : Situations that typically cause a check to be held include : There is reason to believe the funds may be uncollectable The source of the check The account has been open for 30 days or less The account has repeated overdrafts in the last 6 months The check is in an amount greater than {$5000.00} or larger than you normally deposit Fraud is suspected The check was previously deposited, then returned unpaid The check was not properly endorsed Emergency situations, including computer or communication failure Incorrect routing or account number information on a deposit slip','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'the check they hold do not apply to any of their hold policies. the check is in an amount greater than $5000.00 or larger than you normally deposit.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1188,'06/19/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received an alert from a credit monitoring service that my score had dropped due to an account change. I logged in and saw that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had reported my payments for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as 30 days late. I immediately contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to report that when I log into their payment system, it showed my account has having a balance due of {$0.00} ( screen shots attached ). The only time it would show a balance due was towards the end of the month. I made the payments at that time and then they were considered ''late ''. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] customer service stated on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : This is a site issue that we are aware of and our web designers are in the process of updating the system to get it corrected. 

There are also articles online where [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] admits having issues with their payment system when they updgraded in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].

I spoke with customer service both on the online chat and over the phone to explain my situation and have my account updated to show that the payments were not late due to an error on their end in their system. 

Even though they admitted they are having system issues, they said they will not do anything since they only have the date when my payment was received. 

I am being punished with late marks on my credit report even though their payment system has an acknowledged and admitted error.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'credit monitoring service alerted me that my score had dropped due to an account change. a credit report showed my account had a balance due of $0.00.');
