INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1195,'06/18/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was awarded a Garnishment Judgment in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Their Collector did not attempt to collect on this Garnishment until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Without warning or notice. According to the ARS 12-1551 ( B ) https : //www.azleg.gov/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] This creditor illegally garnished wages after the 5 year period. There is no record of them filing for an extension either. I have had this garnishment taken out of my check every pay period from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - Current. I would like this creditor to stop taking money from me and to refund all funds they have taken. Amounts varied as this was based off of my Net Earnings, not to exceed 25 % of my pay. The second Garnishment order was given to the below creditor in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Six Years after the original Garnishment Order. This makes this order Null and VOID [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is my Employer. The original Creditor was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; their Collector is : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], AZ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I would like a full refund of all of my funds that were illegally taken from me.','ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.',2.0,2.0,'a creditor illegally garnished wages after the 5 year period. the creditor was awarded a Garnishment Judgment in XX/XX');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1196,'06/18/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','In 2008 I had an account with US Bank, the following year I had an ex-girlfriend use that Card and Identity to steal and overdraft the account, I reported to the police and verified she was using drugs and did not have permission to use my bank card, after that US BANK never contacted me, I was understood the matter was resolved, Now a Company that refuses to verify their address only calling themselves [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Phone Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] continues to call not only I but my mother, my father and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] knows who else, when first speaking to them they stated the documents were from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] COUNTY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] COURTS, NOW it seems they only had two [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Address '' one in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and the OTHER in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], in which allegedly they sent documents to those address '' 45 days ago I never received, they have drove on my private road and created further civil complaints by pretending to be a company they are not, as well as Un Fair Business Practices, Badgering, Patronizing and All around being RUDE, I don''t owe the US BANK Anything..','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'in 2008, an ex-girlfriend used that card and Identity to steal and overdraft the account. after that she had not used her bank card, she was using drugs.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1197,'06/17/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Struggling to repay your loan','I graduated from high school in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Neither my family nor I hadthe financial means for me to pursue my education, so my aunt promised to help. I was accepted at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University which is a private college in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].Over the period of time that I matriculated at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University my financial needs were met by a series of loans. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University assisted with myobtained financial aid through Navient, ultimately with my aunt agreeing to be a co-signer on the loans. 

We were under the impression that Navient would work with us once I graduated with an amortization plan that I could afford and would ultimately help me to pay my loans off in a timely matter. Unfortunately when I graduated I found this not to be the case. My monthly payments were based on my income and my Aunts income and as I was paying the loans off alone, it was difficult for me to reach an agreement with Navient in which I could afford. In order for me to have the cheapest payment they would accept, which was still above my means at the time, it was a payment they would only put towards the interest and not the principle of my loans. 

I needed the money to obtain my education but little did I know at the time of signing that it would actually be anenslavement, as I have paid over {$56000.00} since my graduation in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the loan principal is now even higher than when I graduated. Navient has not been cooperative in helping me get my aunt off the indebtedness as a co-signer despite their promises and I can not get the indebtedness restructured so that I will eventually get the loan paid off. 

In an attempt to do so I reached out to Navient to have my aunt removed as the co-signer on the indebtedness. We were informed by Navient that if I made my monthly payments by auto draft, for one year, we could have her removed as co-signer. And in turn would be able to lower my monthly payments, to something I can afford based on my income alone, due to the fact that I am paying the loans off on my own. These payments would also then be able to go towards the principle of my loans instead of just interest. 

Unfortunately on month 12 of the year period I noticed my payment was not auto drafted. As soon as I noticed I called in and made the payment. At this time I was informed that the person I worked with previously had put me on reoccurring payments which only last 11 months. Even though I had called and still made my 12th month payment they said it did not count because it needed to be on auto draft for a year. I appealed this decision, seeing as I had made my payments with no problems for 12 months and it was Navients error that had the payments come out of my bank account incorrectly. Unfortunately Navient did not accept my appeal and I have been attempting to take my aunt off as my co-signer and lower my monthly payment ever since. 

Here are the specifics of my loans : On the following dates I obtained student loans from Navient in the amounts of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$39000.00} ( loan # 1 ), XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$28000.00} ( loan # 2 ), and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$25000.00} ( loan # 3 ). I graduated from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I have made payments on the loans for the total amounts of {$13000.00} ( loan # 1 ), {$17000.00} ( loan # 2 ), and {$25000.00} ( loan # 3 ). The outstanding balance for loan # 1 now is {$37000.00}, for loan # 2 now is {$32000.00}, and for loan # 3 now is $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].Which means that since graduation I have paid a total amount of {$56000.00} for the three loans and yet my three loans have gone from me owing {$93000.00} at graduation to me now owing {$100000.00}. Despite my total payments of {$56000.00} since graduation my student loans have actually gone up {$9100.00}. 


The above numbers prove that I continuously make my payments. In fact on loan # 3 I have paid more than enough to pay off my original balance and yet somehow owe more than what the original amount was for. I have made two requests of Navient for the loans to be placed in my name alone. My aunt has recently sought to incur additional financial obligations and her contingent obligation on these loans has been detrimental to her purposes. 

As I have fully complied with their requirements, butthe firm has not released my aunt from my obligations, I am asking for your assistance. 

I also have asked Navient for a new amortization statement under which I would eventually pay off the loans as all prior payments were mostly credited to " interest '''' alone and not much on principle. Apparently the customer service department of Navient isn''t bound by its promises and we are powerless to resolve the problem without damaging our credit, so we ask for your help. 

Please contact me if you need further information.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a series of loans helped me pay my loans off in a timely manner. my aunt agreed to be a co-signer on the loans. the loans were based');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1198,'06/17/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Last year I realized that the l was a victim of Identity Theft. After contacting Equifax they along with the other two requested an Identity Theft report from local police. I have sent Equifax the information more than 5 Times and they refuse to correct the 6 Inquires and Collection account reporting ( ALL Not Mine ). Since they refuse to delete the inaccurate information I am contacting you for your assistance. Maybe they have not learned their lessons from the past.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the l was a victim of Identity Theft. I have sent Equifax the information more than 5 times. they refuse to correct the 6 Inquires and Collection');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1199,'06/16/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Hi, First of all, I have to apologize as I may have chosen the wrong topic ( I could not find anything remotely related to my issue ). I am a paying consumer from the TransUnion company, and I have to report something they had been fined for : misleading the consumers. The only reason I registered myself with TransUnion was because I am in the process of purchasing a car, and I needed to know my credit scores. I worked toward paying off my credit cards, and all 3 of my credit scores were in the " Good '''' category ( over 680 ). While the other two bureaus had updated my score, TransUnion only updated mine yesterday at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Eastern time ). When I received the notification, I decided to make a 700 miles round trip from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to purchase the car I was interested in based on the credit scores I had received. Had I know there were two different models to determine people ''s credit scores, I would have never driven 700 miles ( and spent more than {$250.00} in tolls/gas ). It was a big shock to me when I decided to proceed with the purchase of the car to learn that my credit score ( from TransUnion using the FICO score when they are using the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on their website without letting the consumers know that there are two different ways to calculate a credit score, and they are using a model that very few lenders keep using, especially for a car auto loan! ). Nowhere on their website is it mentioned that the credit score provided is calculated from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] nor nowhere is it stipulated that the credit score shown is only one of the two models used to calculate a credit score. Why am I ( and many others ) for a service that is misleading? How can I make a decision regarding a financial transaction if the score provided for a service I am paying for is false? Needless to say that when I called customer service that I was disappointed with their communication skills : one agent told me that TransUnion never reveals the consumer to lenders that contact them ( which is utterly laughable ) and his supervisor not only could not answer my question ( Why are you providing a credit score based on a model that the majority of lenders do not use? ) but could not guide me through the website ''s page and told me to educate myself first with visiting their page before calling! I eventually spoke to an agent who finally provided with the information that credit scores are calculated through two different models. She also acknowledged that the TransUnion website should inform the general public ( and furthermore its consumers! ) that the score provided is only from one of the two models used to provide a credit score and that the score does not reflect the " true '''' credit score. She was apologetic for the behaviors of her colleagues but of course refused to make a gesture toward the fact that I had wasted money and time based on the " expertise '''' her company provided ( and charge people for!!! ). She did not even offer to refund my monthly payment as I feel I should not have to pay for a misleading service that will never help me in any financial decisions I have to make. Even if my complaint does not get anywhere, I would like to warn other people regarding TransUnion ''s service, so they are not getting mislead as I was.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a paying consumer from the TransUnion company was fined for misleading consumers. the only reason I registered myself was because I am in the process of buying a car. the credit');
