INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1203,'06/15/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','False statements or representation','I recently requested validation of a debt collection listed on my credit report under the company [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The company sent corresponds as to what they believe is proper validation of the account, however by doing this it was found that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to include their NC license permit number ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) on the stationery/correspondent form ( copy attached ) and is therefore in violation of North Carolina Department of Insurance General Statures ; 58 70 50. All collection agencies to identify themselves in correspondence.

All collection agencies licensed under this Part to do the business of a collection agency in this State, shall in all correspondence with debtors use stationery or forms which contain the permit number and the true name and address of such collection agency.

The permit to engage in the business of a collection agency shall at all times be prominently displayed in each office of the person, firm, corporation or association to whom or to which the permit is issued. ( 1931, c. 217, s. 9 ; 1969, c. 906, s. 5 ; 1979, c. 835. ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is in direct violation of federal & state laws, and therefore is illegally attempting to collect a debt in a state that they are violating the NC Department of Insurance State Laws & failing to abide by the Fair Credit Reporting Act.

Attached is the entire Article 70. Collection Agencies where the exact section mentioned above can be found, directly from the NC Department of Insurance website.

The account in debt collection assigned to this company must be deleted as the company collecting on the debt ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) violated not only federal laws, but also state laws mandated by the North Carolina Department of Insurance.','ERC',2.0,2.0,'the company sent corresponds as to what they believe is proper validation of the account. however it was found that the company failed to include their NC license permit number on the stationery/cor');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1204,'06/15/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Traveler''s check or cashier''s check','Fraud or scam','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I visited Bank of Americas financial center located at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to purchase a {$200000.00} cashier ''s check with cash. The source of these funds was my remaining home equity after my home was foreclosed and sold at a trustee sale in 2015. 


I had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] zipped BofA money bag containing two {$100000.00} cash bags from the Federal Reserve, sealed in clear tamper-evident [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  bags. Each {$100000.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bag was filled with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$10000.00} straps of {$100.00} bills. The total value of the cash inside my zipped money bag was {$200000.00}. 

The teller who assisted me ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) told me to a meet her at the banks private teller counter windows where the bank services and handles customers with high dollar amount transactions. I met her at that area where I handed her the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  zipped BofA money bag with my cash. She took the bag and told me that she had to go count the money and walked away from the counter window. At that point as the teller walked away from the counter window and I no longer had a direct visual on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   money bag, I sat at the chairs available across the counter windows in that area. 
A couple of minutes later the teller returned to the counter and told me that there was only {$190000.00} inside the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  zipped money bag. She had ripped open one of clear [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  bags and it was obvious that one of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$10000.00} money straps was missing and there were only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] straps left. She never run any of the cash through the large multi-pocket counting machine located directly across the private counter windows and in the customers direct viewing area. Yet she told me that there was only {$190000.00} in the bag without ever counting a single bill. 

The night prior to my branch visit, l had examined the contents of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] BofA zipper money bag. Both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bags were intact and sealed closed. There were [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$10000.00} straps in each [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bag, for a total count of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$10000.00} straps. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] x $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]= {$200000.00} ). There was no doubt in my mind that the teller had removed and stolen the missing {$10000.00} strap. I accused her directly of stealing the missing {$10000.00} strap and demanded to speak to the branch manager. 

The branch manager [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who should have been present from the moment I handed my money bag to the teller, to oversee his tellers count and to ensure that there are no discrepancies ( standard banking protocol for high dollar amount transactions ) finally arrived at the private counter windows. I told him that when I handed my money bag to his teller, it contained {$200000.00} in cash strapped, wrapped and sealed by the Federal Reserve. When his teller walked away to allegedly count the money, she tore one of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bags open, took out the missing {$10000.00} strap, and returned to the counter window claiming that there was only {$190000.00} cash inside the bag. I further asked him to playback the recorded video of the incident captured by the banks video surveillance cameras, as it would confirm that his teller was lying and was responsible for the missing {$10000.00}  strap. He told me that he could not review the video, because he did not have access to the video surveillance footage, as it handled by a third-party company. He told me that in order to verify what had actually transpired, he would have to submit a request for the recorded video surveillance footage to BofAs corporate security office. He further added that customers are never given access to the video surveillance footage unless they request it with a subpoena. He was being uncooperative, dismissive, reluctant to take any action to resolve the situation and was trying to rush me out of the bank. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and asked that an officer get dispatched to the branch to take down a crime report. 
Only when the Officers [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Police Department arrived at the scene did the branch manager report the incident to BofAs corporate security office and requested that an investigator review the video surveillance footage of the incident. He told me that this process could take several days, but he should have an update within 24 hours and that he would follow up with me with a phone call. The two Officers from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Police Department informed me that their body cameras had captured my conversation with the branch manager [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and a recorded video of everything that had transpired in their presence would be available under Incident No : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then asked me if I wanted a cashiers check for {$190000.00}. I agreed. The two officers then departed the scene and I returned to the private counter windows for the cashiers check. This time a different teller properly counted the money by running it through the multi-pocket counting machine in the presence of the branch manager [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and by making sure that I had a direct constant visual of all his actions and of the entire count. Once the count was verified and I received a cashiers check for {$190000.00} and left the branch. 

To this date, I have not received any phone call or any communication from Bank of America whatsoever. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was able to reach Bank of Americas investigator assigned to this case, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Even though she provided me with the case number assigned to her investigation [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she had no other information or update. She did not provide me with her contact information because she did not want to be inconvenienced by my constant phone calls. She told me that she would call me once she reviewed the case. I never heard back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I went back to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch to get an update from the branch [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He told that he could not provide me with any information regarding this incident and told me to call to the investigator for an update. When I asked him for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] contact number, he refused to provide me with her number and told me I will let her know that you are trying to reach her','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'a teller told me to meet her at the banks private teller counter windows. she told me that she had to go count the money and walked away from the counter window ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1205,'06/15/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','Last month I paid off my entire balance on my Capital One credit card. At the time, the balance reflected on the Capital One website was {$2400.00}. I paid the entire balance on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].

A full 10 days later I was still charged {$31.00} for interest. This was not reflected anywhere on the website statement at the time that I had paid my balance. I did call Capital One to let them know this and requested a credit of {$31.00}. They refused stating that this was interest already accrued. However, I stated to them that this should then be reflected on their website for pay off. The associate agreed that this was a flaw on their website and that he would mention this to senior management. The call was escalated. However, the second individual also refused to credit the {$31.00}.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'the balance reflected on the capital One website was $2400.00. a full 10 days later, I was still charged $31.00 for interest.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1206,'06/15/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','XX/XX/2018 called Wells Fargo Loan Modification [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they refused to do a loan modification even though I just had buried my mother and was getting to a point to save my home. They said I called in too late about 33 days before the sale and they needed 37 days. They would not postpone the sale or do anything about me working out something with them.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2018 called Wells Fargo Loan Modification. they refused to do a loan modification. they said I called in too late about 33 days before the');
