INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1208,'06/14/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Struggling to repay your loan','They raised my monthly payment from {$170.00} per month to {$560.00} at the beginning ofXX/XX/2018. I was told over the phone that I don''t qualify for a lower payment plan now. I am currently in forbearance for one year.

I tried to apply for loan forgiveness because I''ve consistently paid my loan and worked full-time as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for 12 years now. Federal Student Loan.gov turned me down, saying that I didn''t have the right kind of loan ( PSLF ). They told me to apply through Navient. I found the Navient [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  loan forgiveness form, but my financial officer at work says that it''s not the appropriate form. I can not find an equivalent form for Navient civil servants loan forgiveness.

I''ve read about the lawsuits against Navient. I had student loans through Sallie Mae before Navient took over. Likewise, I''ve read that it may not be wise to refinance through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would have to start all over to qualify for the loan forgiveness.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'federal student loan.gov turned me down, saying that I didn''t have the right kind of loan. I found the Navient [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1209,'06/14/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Problem with a lender or other company charging your account','I joined the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Total monthly fee was {$130.00} which I paid every month automatically. It was a month to month agreement, with an understanding that I could cancel at any time. Nothing was explained to me about canceling in writing. 
In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called the Club to cancel my month to month membership. The representative I spoke with said sure, and claimed membership would be stopped. 

About a month and a half ago, I noticed that the Club was still billing me. I called the club and they said again that they could cancel the membership. They did not, and refused to give me a refund. 
I called Chase to complain about this. They opened a claim, for the months from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and placed a temporary credit on my account. 
About 3 weeks later, Chase reversed the credit and denied the claim, stating the charges were valid and also that there is a 60 day lookback that they need to follow. 
Firstly, if there is a lookback period, why was I not informed of this and also why were all the months I was disputing credited back? 
Secondly, I did not authorize those charges. If the merchant isnt going to honor my request, and basically lie and steal from me, Id like to think that after 20+ years of banking tens of thousands of dollars with Chase with the same account open for those years, theyd at least honor my complaint.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a month to month agreement, I paid a monthly fee of $130.00. the club said that they could cancel membership, and refused to give me a refund ');
