INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1212,'06/14/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','False statements or representation','The amount claim owed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was incorrect. I talked with them on multiple occasions and they did not respond with evidence supporting the bill. Eventually they turned the dispute over to a collections agency " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' which sent me a letter. 
I immediately contacted them and emailed them filing a dispute with them and followed up a couple of times. I was told verbally and via email they were waiting for a response from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that " apparently [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sees this inconsistency as well ''''. Eventually they drop the issue after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was unable to substantiate there claim. Then I received a call & letter from another collection company " Diversified Consultants Inc ''''. I contacted them and explained the issue, emailed them a dispute, and sent the dispute letter, and supporting documentation within 30 days of notification. No response was recieved from them written or other. They did no investigation, and proceeded to immediately filed a collection with credit reporting agency ''s. " Diversified Consultants Inc '''' did not follow the law and provide or protect my rights under FTC rules and laws.','Diversified Consultants, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a collection company emailed them a dispute and sent the dispute letter. they did not respond with evidence supporting the bill. they turned the dispute over to a collections agency');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1213,'06/13/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I purchased an Official Check ( # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) for {$12.00}, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] against funds in my checking account to pay my property taxes. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called Citibank ''s customer service to place a stop on the check because it never reached its destination. I was told I had to do it personally at a branch. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I went to the branch ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) where I purchased the check. I was told I had to fill out forms and that it would take 90 DAYS before I got my money back. When I asked why it had to take so long I was told that was the policy ( with no explanation as to why ). The banker did mention it would be faster if I returned the actual check. The bank would then just re-deposit it into my account. I left with the forms and spent the next two weeks trying to recover the check via the US Postal Service, but I was unsuccessful. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I returned to the branch with the stop payment forms filled out. The banker took the forms and informed me that it would cost me {$30.00} to process the stop payment. Later that day the banker informed me that I would have to deposit {$5.00} to my account to process the stop payment. Later that evening I deposited {$12.00} via an ATM machine. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I emailed for an update and was told that the stop payment was being " re-processed ''''. Four days later on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received another email stating that my stop payment order had not been processed because I had not deposited any money as instructed. This is the worst customer experience I''ve ever had with a bank. There has been no effort to be helpful to me. First, Citibank insists on essentially holding MY MONEY hostage for 90 days and now Citibank is dragging its feet to place a stop payment on a check for over $ 10K of MY MONEY. Why is a bank permitted to do this to a customer? This has been an unbelievably frustrating experience.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I purchased an official check. I was told I had to do it personally at a branch');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1214,'06/13/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Fraud or scam','I was purchasing a house in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I was instructed by my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] agent to wire the {$25000.00}. I did at Bank of America on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] he called said run to bank cancel it, its fraud. So I did.i bank with Bank of America. The money was at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No one would give me information. 
