INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1216,'06/13/2018','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Communication tactics','I have written communication between myself and the company requesting that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and any other company working on there behalf not contact me by phone. The first request I sent to them to stop contacting me by phone was on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I sent an email as well as signed delivery letter by USPS. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent an email confirming receipt of my request. I have asked that all communications be in writing. They have honored my request up until yesterday. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] contacted my place of employment and left a recorded message for me. I contacted the company and asked once again that they stop calling me but was told that they will not stop calling. Stated they will contact my human resources department till the so say " DEBT '''' is paid in full. I''ve emailed the company again reminding them not to call me. This is really embarrassing. 

All I want is for them to stop calling me as I have requested in the past.','WLCC',2.0,2.0,'a company requesting that a company not contact me by phone. the company has honored my request up until yesterday.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1217,'06/13/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have a loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  &. I have always made my payments on time. For some reason I realized that there was a late payment on my credit report. As you can see, I have always had a stellar payment record with this company. I tried contacting both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & with no successful resolution. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] only reporting me late. There was definitely an error on their part. I was never 30 days late XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] andXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'a loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & a loan with a company that has a late payment record. I have always made my payments');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1218,'06/13/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','CFPB Complaint XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Subject : SunTrust Bank wrongful holding of Mortgagee insurance proceeds. 

Facts : 1. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] approved a Hurricane Irma damage claim in the amount of {$80000.00} +/- for a replacement of the total roof and issued an initial insurance check in the amount of {$52000.00} made payable to home owner and SunTrust. SunTrust has a copy of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] documents. 

2. Check was signed by homeowner and delivered to SunTrust on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 3. SunTrust advised Mortgagee to comply with SunTrust Claim-check procedure which mortgagee did in full on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

4. SunTrust advised that eventually Mortgagee would receive {$40000.00} of the {$52000.00} sometime and the balance in two equal installments. One when 50 % of work is complete and one when SunTrust determines the work to be complete. This is in addition to a {$12000.00} holdback held by the insurance company which petitioner accepts and believes is fair and reasonable. 

5. There is no need for SunTrust to hold any of the money or require Mortgagee to waste time and money completing the unnecessary Claim-check process. There is no risk to the bank as the balance of the mortgage is less than 35 % of the value of the house. This was documented in the attached XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter to SunTrust CEO [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Exhibit A ). This letter received by SunTrust via email on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Exhibit B ) and a few days later by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No response from SunTrust CEO. The letter detailed the wrongful nature of the money grab and demanded immediate release of the full amount of the insurance proceeds. 

6. A second letter ( Exhibit C ) was dated, sent and received by SunTrust on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] pointing out the harm to Mortgagee in having to use retirement assets to pay the {$25000.00} initial payment to the roofing contractor in connection with the roof contract executed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].This letter also pointed out that this wrongful holding of Mortgagee money may very well violate the SunTrust Code of Business Conduct and Ethics which may be of interest to other oversight agencies of the US Government . 

7. Mortgagee is advised that SunTrust will not pay interest on Mortgagee money it is wrongfully holding. 

8. A third letter ( Exhibit D ) critical of SunTrust CEO Non response and bank partial response was sent to SunTrust on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This  letter again demanded immediate full payment with interest. 

9. There is no rational or logical reason for SunTrust to wrongfully hold money due Mortgagee. There is absolutely no mortgagee risk to SunTrust. While there is language in the mortgage that seems to give SunTrust the power to hold Mortgagees money that is obviously a Contract of Adhesion and not enforceable in law. 
 10. In addition to processing this complaint I would like CFPB to investigate if this is a scam to force people without additional capital into high interest rate loans while holding their insurance and not paying interest..','SUNTRUST BANKS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'sunTrust issued a wrongful holding of mortgagee insurance proceeds. the wrongful holding of the money was documented in the attached letter. the letter detailed the wrongful nature of');
