INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1255,'06/05/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] weekend, I traveled to a real estate class in Utah. Upon my return, I attempted to pay a {$30.00} airport parking charge and my BBVA Compass card was declined. Since it had a {$12000.00} credit limit on it and only about {$2000.00} worth of charges on it, I did not understand why. On Tuesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I contacted BBVA Compass who informed me that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] provided them with a notification that I was overextended. I''m not. As a result of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  information, BBVA Compass lowered my credit limit to {$2500.00} leaving me {$11.00} in available credit, which obviously can not pay for a {$30.00} airport parking charge. I invested in real estate training to better my life and now I''m getting chastised for it. I have never been late or contacted any type of credit repair agency to fix anything as there was nothing to be fixed. There still isn''t. I am very angry over this unjustified action and I believe there has to be some type of law or something that can keep people like [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and/or BBVA Compass from destroying my life. The only equitable solution for me would to be reinstate the credit limit on this card. Anything else is an insult.','BBVA COMPASS FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'BBVA Compass lowered my credit limit to $2500.00. a $12000.00 credit limit on the card was lowered. ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1256,'06/05/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I timely submitted to SPS an appeal of the denial of my application to SPS ; SPS has not issued a response to that appeal. Despite the fact that loss mitigation is pending, SPS has scheduled a sale of my home for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. There mere fact that a sale has been scheduled while loss mitigation is ongoing is DUAL TRACKING which is prohibited.

I am also in receipt of SPSs mortgage statement dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], claiming {$1100.00} in charges/fees for FC ATTY FEES and FC COSTS. I am assuming that there are other 3rd fees and costs assessed to my account in prior months.

As Im sure SPS is aware, RESPA prohibits charging borrowers 3rd party fees if the work if not actually performed. Specifically, 12 C.F.R. 1024.35 ( b ) ( 5 ) requires that the servicer may only charge bona fide fees ; fees that the servicer determined it had a reasonable basis to impose. However, a servicer may not charge a for service that a service provider did not actually provide. Therefore, in order to prove these above noted fees are legitimate and all fees and costs assessed to my account, I demand a copy of all invoices evidencing all fees and the work completed for all fees charged. If I am expected to pay these fees then SPS must prove that are bona fide fees within RESPA.

These errors on SPS part must be addressed and reconciled immediately, specifically, pursuant to Regulation X, 12 C.F.R. 1024.35 ( d ) and ( e ), SPS has 5 days within which to acknowledge receipt of this request and must respond no later than 7 days.

Until these errors are properly addressed and corrected by SPS, there can be no sale scheduled on our property ; the currently scheduled sale for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], must be canceled if the errors are not corrected. See Reg. X, 12 C.F.R. 1024.35 ( e ) ( 3 ) ( i ) ( B ) and 1024.35 ( f ) ( 2 ) ; Official Bureau Interpretation, Supplement 1 to Part 1024, 35 ( e ) ( 3 ) ( i ) ( B ) -1. Therefore, we are requesting that you cancel the sale so that our appeal and previously issued Notice of Error have been addressed.

I also submitted the following QWR : As there exists violations and omissions in my account with SPS, this is a Qualified Written Request ( QWR ) under Section 6 of the Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act ( RESPA ) which is issued to obtain specific documents pertaining to my mortgage loan. SPS, be advised that under recently-amended Section 6 of RESPA, SPS must acknowledge in writing its receipt of this QWR request within five ( 5 ) business days of receiving it ; to issue a substantive response to the requested information within thirty ( 30 ) business days ; and to reconcile existing irregularities or inconsistencies within a maximum of forty-five ( 45 ) business days ( The Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act allows for a 15-day extension only if I am informed about it and given the reasons for the extension ). A failure to comply with this request may result in fines of up to {$2000.00} plus any attorneys fees and costs. In addition, RESPAs Section ( 12 U.S.C. ) 2605 ( e ) ( 3 ) directs SPS as the loan servicer to not report negative information regarding my account to a consumer reporting agency during the 60 days following receipt of the QWR concerning overdue payments related to that period or to the QWR.

Please ensure that all copies of the following documents that SPS provides are clear, legible, and copied in their entirety. I will check off the following items I receive from you as you provide them : An escrow analysis to reflect an itemization of the current amount clamed due ; Initial Loan Application and Final Loan Application ( 1003 ) ; Deed of Trust/All Addendums ; Copy of Wet-inked Note signed, with All Endorsements and/or attached Allonges ; Copy of any and all Assignments of Mortgage ; Copy of Complete Loan Payment History This must include all payments made, all fees incurred, any and all escrow account disbursements and how payments were applied, any and all payments listed as Corp Adv Statutory Exp Disb and/or Corp Adv Attorney Advance Disb, Other Fees & Adv, Unapplied Funds, fees and costs associated with any appraisal-related, loss-mitigation related ( short sale ) fees, legal fees, etc., on any payment coupon statements/detailed transaction history print-outs issued by SPS and all disclosures and rate sheets ; All escrow analyses conducted on the account from the inception of the loan to the date of this letter ; Truth-in Lending Statements and Disclosures ; All loan servicing agreementsincluding any modification decisions or declinations -- between the loan servicer ( s ) and the loan originator, the note holder/lender ( including nominees holding legal title such as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), and/or trustees from inception of the loan to the date of this letter ; All letters, statements, affidavits, and documents ( including Limited Power of Attorney if applicable ) sent among agents, attorneys, or representatives of your company ; Itemization of Amount Financed ; Good Faith Estimates ; Estimated and Final Closing Statements ( Final HUD 1 ) ; Appraisal, and Current Fair Market Value of property including the basis for this determination ; Title Report ; All insurance premiums along with an accounting of timely payments made to the insurance company throughout the servicing of the loan ; Grant Deed ( s ).

RESPA also requires : Copies of all executed loan modification agreements ; Documentation of all loss mitigation eligibility determinations, evaluations, and actions taken on this mortgage loan ; Copies of all correspondence to me from SPS, if any, regarding adjustments in fees and charges, and any involving loss mitigation for this mortgage loan, including modifications, forbearance arrangements, or short-sale arrangements and all notices of default ; A full accounting of all money paid and received on this mortgage loan account from any third party sources, including agreements, contracts, and understandings with vendors that have been paid for by any charges on the account from the inception of the loan to the date of this letter ; Additionally, please provide, in writing, the following : ( 1 ) Please identify the name, address, and telephone number of the current owner ( beneficiary ) of the Note ; ( 2 ) Please identify the name, address, and telephone number of the beneficiary named in the Deed of Trust if different from that of the lender, and the authorization allowing such ; ( 3 ) Please identify the name, address, and telephone number of the secured party ( the current owner of the mortgage ) ; ( 4 ) Please identify the name, address, and telephone number of, and any and all fees provided to, the mortgage broker ( s ) involved in this mortgage loan ; ( 5 ) Please identify the current location of the originals of the entire loan file, and describe the manner in which they are stored, maintained, and protected.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,4.0,'despite loss mitigation, a sale has been scheduled. a mortgage statement claiming $1100.00 in charges/fees for FC ATTY FEES');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1257,'06/05/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I request validation of the debt reporting negative on my credit reporting from an agency, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], {$970.00} acct # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who purchased the debt from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] original acct # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on numerous requests, last being XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I got a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of deletion they couldn''t validate the debt, nor send me any information pertaining to this line of credit that they are reporting negatively on my credit reporting. I instructed and showed proof to all 3 major credit bureaus, as of today [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] deleted it, however [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] still showing, they claim the creditor updated and all information is accurate and consumer still owes. I have no knowledge of this so called purchased fraud debt which [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting. I also Filed with Federal Trade Commission as a result of this matter not being properly handled and Fraud was placed upon all 3 of my Credit Reportings.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,4.0,'credit bureaus have not validated the debt reporting negative. they claim the creditor updated and all information is accurate. the creditor still owes.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1258,'06/05/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','When using the web site to make payment, loancare llc will put a added cost to your payment if not done in the first four days, This fee starts at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] $ AND GOES UP. My mortgage is not late until the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the month, and this company is charging late fees after four days. This goes against contract and to me is against the bound agreement of the contract.','LoanCare, LLC',2.0,2.0,'loancare llc will put a cost to your payment if not done in the first four days. this fee starts at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1259,'06/05/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','Within the last few days, issues have happened with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 1 issue is that my phone number is associated with an Ally account, and as POA in two people ''s sets of  accounts at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The sender from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] tried {$100.00} to me with my cell number and it didn''t even ask which account to send it to, it automatically chose a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account. It was supposed to go to Ally and it hasn''t yet. 

The 2nd issue is that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] took 3 days for my first [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] money sent. Yet it took the money out and held it back on day 2. They need to fix these communication issues with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','ALLY FINANCIAL INC.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] took 3 days for my first [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] money. but it took 3 days for my first');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1260,'06/04/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','On Thursday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a voicemail from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that stated the following : " Good afternoon this message is for ( insert my name ). My name is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I''m a private carrier and I''m calling you regarding your legal documents that we have here in the office scheduled for delivery today between the hours of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to the addess ... oh, okay sir, I''m looking here ... we don''t even have an address for you. So it''s very important that you call in and give us a good address because if we don''t get these documents to you and get you to sign for them, I''m going to have to send them back as undeliverable and mark it as a direct refusal of compliance and also as a missed appearance. if you have any questions regarding your appearance, your documentation or wish to reschedule the delivery times and give a good address, contact the office at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When you contact the office you will need to provide the documentation number, which is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Thank you, have a good day. Talk to you soon. '''' I called the number back and was told that I had by noon the next day ( Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to either pay the debt or I would be taken to court. I was told that their company was not a debt collection company, but instead a company that gets these accounts right before they will get taken to court ( however I could pay the full amount to the company to avoid being taken to court, which sounds like debt collection ). I was told their success rate in court is in the 99 % range and usually when these cases go to court they sue for 3 times the total debt owed. In my case this would have been around {$1500.00} because I was told I owed {$500.00} at one point, but then on a call later that day I was told I owed {$650.00}. The man on the phone said he could not even tell me which bank this debt supposedly originated from. He said it only came to them showing as a DDA ( direct deposit account ). 

He told me the account they were collecting on was opened on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and verified some information with me including the last four of my SSN and also my old street address. Note : On the voicemail that was left he had stated that they did not have an address for me. Also my mom and I moved to that address in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I was a sophomore in high school, I moved out in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but my mom still lives there. No communications had ever been mailed to that address. Also, the phone number that he reached me on I have had since about XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I asked how it was possible that for 10 years this debt had supposedly been owed, but yet I had not had one phone call or piece of mail from the bank or debt collectors, and then now this company instantly is able to reach me. The response was that their company has more resources to be able to track down people because they are not a debt collection agency. 

I told the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employee that I was going to call the only two banks I would have possibly had during that year, Wells Fargo and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to see if I could get any information from them. I called both banks promptly and both were unable to find any information regarding the account number I had been given my the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employee. The Wells Fargo employee even called her back office to have them check their records and they were not able to find any information. After talking to these employees I felt very confident that this was a scam. I researched online and came across the fact that under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act that I have a right to submit a debt validation letter to the company and require them to send complete documentation to verify that I owed the said debt and that I had legal obligation to pay to the company. 

The next day I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and got their email address ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and physical address ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) so that I could send my debt validation letter in both forms. When I called to request this information I spoke to someone named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he said he was new and didn''t understand what a debt validation letter was and asked me to repeat the name of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act that I had mentioned so that he could write it down. I recorded these conversations in case they could be beneficial later. 

I sent my debt validation letter via email the morning of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requesting the following : - Agreement with the creditor that authorizes you to collect on this alleged debt - The agreement bearing my signature stating that I have agreed to assume the debt - Valid copies of the debt agreement stating the amount of the debt and interest charges - Proof that the Statute of Limitations has not expired - Complete payment history on this account along with an accounting of all additional charges being assessed - Show me that you are licensed to collect in my state ; and - Your license numbers and Registered Agent On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received an email back with ONLY the following information : 1 ) My name 2 ) Last 4 of my SSN 3 ) Type of Debt : DDA 4 ) Acct number ( of supposed debt ) 5 ) Bank Name : Wells Fargo Bank 6 ) Original Repayment Amount : {$650.00} 7 ) Interest & Fees Amount Due : {$0.00} 8 ) Grand Total Due, Owing & Payable : {$500.00} 9 ) Original Loan " Charge Off Date '''' : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] So the response email included nowhere near the amount of information or proof necessary to verify that this is a debt I owe. Also the bottom of the email read as follows : " In addition to the above, and in most cases, we can also provide ; your date of birth, drivers license number, and email address that was submitted when you applied for the loan. To maintain your privacy, however, we do not disclose this information in writing. As you can see, we have truncated ( masked ) your social security number ( except for the last four digits ) to protect your privacy as well. 

The account/debt described above and currently owned by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is a debt ; due, owing and payable in the total amount of {$500.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has full power and authority to perform all acts necessary for the collection, settlement, adjustment, compromise and satisfaction of said debt ( s ). 

This communication is from a debt collector and is an attempt to collect a debt. Any information obtained will be used for that purpose. 

All of the information contained within this Validation of Debt is true and accurate to the best of my knowledge and has been confirmed and validated by me through research and verification. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' So on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I had been told that this was not a debt collection agency, but then the email states that it is. The debt validation letter that I sent states that if their company is unable to provide the requested documentation within 30 days that all future attempts to collect the debt should cease. I am positive that this is some type of scam trying to scare me into sending payments to this company. However with this supposedly being related to something 10 years ago this company is making me doubt myself, and therefore has created a very stressful time for me trying to sort through all this. 

I would appreciate help from the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau since this is the Bureau ''s expertise and may have a larger oversight or further information on this company and it''s legitimacy. Also guidance as to what can and should be done on my end of this would be greatly appreciated.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a voicemail from a private carrier stating that "good afternoon this message is for ( insert my name ). if we don''t get these documents to you,');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1261,'06/04/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] owned my mortgage load from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They then sold my mortgage to Homepoint Mortgage. My loan number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I got a notification from my credit monitoring company, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that Homepoint Mortgage has put a delinquency notification on my credit. I paid a mortgage payment on-line over and above my mortgage amount on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I''ve never received any paperwork showing any information on my mortgage from Homepoint, i.e. payment due, mortgage amount due, etc.','Home Point Financial Corporation',2.0,2.0,'mortgage load from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1262,'06/04/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','False statements or representation','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] EST I received a threatening phone call from someone who claimed they were with a " local courier '''' by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He left a voicemail stating that I better be available between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] tomorrow and that he would be going to my place of employment first and if I was not there would be speaking with my supervisor to find out when my next shift would be. He also indicated that he would then proceed to go to the homes of family and friends to locate me. He stated that I would need two forms of ID and a witness to sign for these documents. At the end of the voicemail he provided me with a phone number for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and a " case number ''''. Upon calling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with this information I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who informed me that they were a mediation firm working on behalf of Fifth Third Bank. He stated that Fifth Third had found me to have committed fraud for my own personal gain and that they were moving forward with court proceedings at which time I would owe {$810.00}. I explained to him that I currently have an account with Fifth Third Bank and was curious as to why they had not contacted me about this old bank account. He stated that they contracted with them for mediation on it and that it had been in default with them since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I asked him what the amount would be if I paid today. He placed me on hold for 10 minutes and then came back to the phone and stated I could make a payment arrangement for 3 payments of {$180.00} or I could settle for a one time payment of {$270.00}. I advised him that I would settle but that I needed confirmation that the date was settled and advised him that he needed to contact this " private courier '''' company to notify them because I did not want them showing up at my job, my house, or the home of my friends and/or family. He agreed to email me this notification which I have attached to this complaint. As soon as I got off the phone I contacted Fifth Third Bank to let them know about my experience. The representative that I spoke with stated that they wouldn''t have any information about the account since they sold it to a debt collector. I told her I was very upset and ready to cancel my current accounts with them because of this to which she replied " Well that doesn''t have anything to do with Fifth Third. '''' I told her of course it does, you sold the debt to this company and they contacted me with threats. I called the FTC to file a complaint about this private courier for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and gave them the phone number I received the call from, however when you call the number it states to email any inquiries to them at their website and conveniently does not give you a website. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] back at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and attempted several times to get the information for this " private courier '''' but he refused stating that they did not have this information. I explained that I intended to make a complaint with the FTC about this company and I needed their contact information. He continued to refuse and stated that they don''t work directly with them but that he could report it back to the attorney. I then asked for the attorney ''s contact information so that I could get the information myself, he refused to provide me with that as well. I informed him that since he was not willing to provide me with this information that I would be filing a complaint with consumerfinance.gov and his response was " Well if that''s what you feel you have to do. ''''','FIFTH THIRD FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a voicemail from a threatening phone call from a ''local courier'' he said he would be available to work with his supervisor. he said he');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1263,'06/04/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','On XX/XX/2018, I contacted Experian by phone to ask about an account that had aged off my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reports but not my Experian report. I spoke with a representative named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and then with a supervisor named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At issue was the date from which Experian counts for determining when a certain type of account will age off of a credit report. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was eager to persuade me to initiate a dispute. I stated at least twice that I did _not_ wish to initiate a dispute. However, today ( XX/XX/2018 ) I received a " dispute results '''' mailing from Experian. The " dispute results '''' mailing is dated XX/XX/2018 -- the same date as my phone call. Apparently [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or someone else at Experian initiated a dispute without my consent. The " dispute results '''' mailing is 14 pages long and after several minutes of flipping through it, it appears to just be a copy of my credit report with one sheet of dispute boilerplate attached to the front, and another sheet of dispute boilerplate added to the back. Despite the length of the mailing and amount of time I spent reading it, I have no clue what " results '''' this " dispute '''' purports to have produced. Having reviewed FCRA, I think this violates a few different provisions in addition to raising other legal red flags : -- 604 : Whatever purpose Experian gives for having furnished this copy of my report, it can not be among the " permissible purposes '''' listed in this section. -- 611 : Disputes require reinvestigation, but this report was issued the same day I called Experian. Moreover, the date was the Sunday before XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so the notion that Experian was able to verify any information with any information furnisher within hours on a holiday weekend is laughable. Presumably Experian will explain the fast turnaround by stating it made a determination that my concerns about the account that had not aged off yet are " frivolous or irrelevant. '''' However, such a determination requires the CRA to provide " the reasons for th [ at ] determination, '''' and no reasons were provided for any determination. -- Fraud : In response to a point I brought up about New York State law, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated that the CFPB had approved Experian ''s policies as to that point. I informed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  that his statement couldn''t possibly be true because the CFPB deals with federal rather than state law, but he replied by just revising his statement to an assertion that " the government '''' had approved Experian ''s policies. While not constituting fraud in my case because I did not rely on his statement, this would likely constitute fraud as applied to other consumers who call Experian. ( To be completely sure about the falsity of the revised statement, I contacted both the NY AG ''s office as well as the NY Dept. of State ''s Consumer Protection Division. Both told me they had not approved the stated policy either. ) FCRA allows the CRAs to treat a consumer ''s subsequent disputes less seriously than an initial dispute. Now that Experian has a false record of me " disputing '''' something -- probably the account that has aged off of my other reports -- it is more likely to deem any actual disputes I may initiate as " frivolous or irrelevant, '''' even if I provide supporting documentation. I called Experian at least three times today to ask what it claims I " disputed. '''' I was unable to get a human on the phone at any point. Given Experian prompts callers to enter their SSN and ZIP code before even following a series of number-picking menus, I suspect Experian has effectively blacklisted me from being able to reach a human on the phone. Notably, I had no trouble reaching a human when I called Experian on XX/XX/2018. And for what it''s worth, I also suspect this unauthorized dispute was the supervisor ''s revenge for catching him in a lie about the CFPB approving Experian policy as applied to NY state law. Thank you for your time and assistance.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'experian contacted me on XX/XX/2018 to ask about an account that had aged off my reports. at issue was the date from which Experian counts for');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1264,'06/04/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SOC SEC # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ADDRESS : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], TX [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Ive submitted enough information regarding the fraudulent account thats open in my name I have provided information for your company to have carried out a reasonable investigation of this dispute. If you had investigated properly rather then using your [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   system you would have noticed that this account is not mine which your companies have claimed to Verified.

This letter is being sent to you in response to notices sent to me from your company and more importantly, due to your erroneous reporting to the Credit Bureau { s }, the  highly negative impact on my personal credit report. Please be advised that this is not a refusal to pay, but a notice sent pursuant to the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act, 15 USC 1692g Sec. 809 { b } that your claim is disputed and validation is requested. 

This is NOT a request for verification or proof of my mailing address, but a request for VALIDATION made pursuant to the above named Title and Section. I respectfully request that your offices provide me with competent evidence that I have any legal obligation to pay you. 

Please provide me with the following : What the money you say I owe is for : Explain and show me how you calculated what you say I owe : Provide me with copies of any papers that show I agreed to pay what you say I owe : Provide a verification or copy of any judgment if applicable : Identify the original creditor : Prove the Statute of Limitations has not expired on this account : Show me the you are licensed to collect in my state : Provide me with your license numbers and Registered Agent or Agent of Service : At this time I will also inform that if offices have reported invalidated information to any of the 3 major Credit Bureaus { Experian, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] } this action might constitute fraud under both Federal and State Laws. Due to this fact, if any negative mark is found on any of my credit reports by theses companies, I will not hesitate to bring legal action against you for the following : Violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act Violation of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act Defamation of Character If your offices are able to provide proper documentation as requested in the following Declaration, I will require at least 30 days to investigate this information and during such time all collection activity must cease and desist. 

Since youve obviously neglected to investigate this account thoroughly I am demanding you remove this account off my profile. It is at this time that I will point out the in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Experian ), and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the courts ruled each and every time that the CRA couldnt merely Parrot information from the creditors and collection agencies that they have conduct an independent REASONABLE investigation to ensure the validity of the debt and honesty/integrity of the creditors/CA in question. Sending out a generic form through the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] system that doesnt even contain my reasons for the dispute is not reasonable. 


Which Im sure you are aware each violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act allows damages of {$1000.00} should this matter ends up in court. 
I look forward to an expedite resolution of this matter Thank you. 


Also, during this validation period, if any action is taken which could be considered detrimental to any of my credit reports, I will consult with my legal counsel for suit. This includes listing any information with a credit reporting repository that could be inaccurate or invalidated or verifying an account as accurate, when it fact there is no provided proof that it is accurate. 

If your company fails to respond to this validation request within 30 days from the date of your receipt, all references to this account must be deleted and completely removed from my credit report and a copy of such deletion { to any/all of the 3 major credit reporting bureaus : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Experian and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] } request shall be sent to me immediately. 

I would also like to request, in writing, that no telephone contact be made by your company to my home or my place of employment. If your offices attempt telephone communication with me, including but not limited to computer generated calls and calls or correspondence sent to or with any third parties, it will be considered harassment and I will have no choice but to file suit. All future communications with me MUST be done in writing and sent to the address noted in this letter by USPS. 

It would be advisable that you assure your records are in order before I am forced to take legal action against your company and your client. This is an attempt to correct your records, any information obtained shall be used for that purpose. 


Best Regards, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SOC SEC # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ADDRESS : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], TX [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'a letter sent to you is being sent to you in response to notices sent from your company. this is not a refusal to pay, but a notice sent pursuant to');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1265,'06/03/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','During the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my tenants left without notice, I called the bank and I asked for a repayment plant for the month of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was not late when I called. The suppose to give a repayment plan without affecting my credit but they lied not only that they charged me for a fee that I didnt agreed upon. I called several times [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I kept receiving these late fees letters and everytime I called I was told the repayment plan will take care of it that I wasnt being charged form them. I made my last payment in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My credit score went down 31 points thats when I found out they reported late payments. Im very disappointed, I complaint and they suppose to start an investigation but apparently that was never done. They are cheaters and liers they dont have a good customer service most of them dont know even simple math. They need to be investigated they dont even seem a serious bank. My loan was sold to them by my bank and at this point I cant even refinance with other bank because of the bad report. I havent been late with a mortgage payment in many years I believe they did this in porpoise because I threaten them with leaving the bank. Thank you','Seterus, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage payment was sold to my bank and at this point I cant even refinance with other bank because of the bad report. the bank lied to me that they charged');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1266,'06/03/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Problem caused by your funds being low','I have been wrongfully charged overdraft fees from PNC Bank, and this is not the first time. I enclosed my latest checking account statement ( dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and numbered each line to help explain my complaint. 
Line : 1 & 2 -Two overdraft fees already posted for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. ( Not Pending ). Balance before this debit {$520.00}. 
Line : 6 - Debit for {$22.00} dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Deducted last instead of the debits occuring on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Line : 3, 4, & 5 - These three XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] debits ( still pending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should have been deducted from my account after the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] debit allowing for only one NSF fee. 

Calling PNC Bank was a waste of time. I explained the situation, however, I did not receive a legit answer or refund of my NSF for their mistake. This bank seems to look for reasons to charge these fees.','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a bank has been wrongfully charged overdraft fees from PNC Bank. the bank has not received a legit answer or refund of my NSF.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1267,'06/03/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I submitted a complaint ( number assigned [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) in refgards to unauthorized credit inquiry. I received an email from Equifax on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating the dispute response was available and it could be read by entering an assigned number ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) along with other personal information. After following the email instructions a message came back stating no information was found! Is this a Equifax scam? I am concerned where my personal information went and is it safe?','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a dispute response was available on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. a message came back saying no information was found.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1268,'06/02/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Well first I had a fraud alert on my account which should of disallowed anyone to access my report without my explicit permission. Well that didn''t work and when I went to buy a car the dealership repeatedly applied to all these different companies without my permission. No one came to me and said, ok the first inquiry didn''t go through may we try the next? They ran it over and over again without my permission until they got a company that would fund me. I want all of these hard inquiries removed from my account, I tried removing them using my credit reporting agency but I was told that the company had to remove it and most of them dont have an address. Please remove the following hard inquiries from my report that all occurred on XX/XX/2018. Thank you Equifax => - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] | [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] => -  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] | [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] => - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a fraud alert on my account should of disallowed anyone to access my report without my explicit permission. the dealership repeatedly applied to all these different companies without my permission. I want');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1269,'06/02/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Written notification about debt','Capital One [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reporting on credit report however never did business with any of these companies','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'capital one reported on credit report but never did business with any of these companies. a credit report was not a credit report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1270,'06/02/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - servicer of credit card with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] decreased my credit limit by {$500.00} based on a credit score pull. this was done without my permission.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'servicer of credit card with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] decreased my credit limit by $500.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1271,'06/02/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I got a mortgage on my Mom and Dad ''s home to help pay debt. The loan paid of some debt and the rest covered the mortgage. The loan was with my parent ''s bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The mortgage was for : Principal and Interest {$740.00} Flood insurance [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mortgage Total : {$790.00} **Please note that hazard insurance, PML/FHA, Taxes and other were NOT apart of the loan as my parents are on fixed incomes and could NOT afford it. I pay their taxes and homeowners insurance seperately as I have proof of that. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold the mortgage to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who at one time tried to collect the escrow for taxes and homeowners, but I sent them the original loan documents and they corrected it immediately. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold the loan to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have been trying to get the to stop trying to take the escrow for Taxes and homeowners. They have received proof that I pay the taxes in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every year and this covers the payment due in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have also sent them records that I pay the homeowners quarterly. I was originally told to just pay my original amount until they get it straightened out, So that is what I did each month I pay the payment of {$790.00}, then in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they put payments in suspense, moved our payments to escrow and made it look like we were late on payments. Finally in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I talked with another supervisor who said once I paid the amount of {$3600.00} which would bring account current ( even though we were current but they were putting our payments elsewhere ) the problem would be fixed within a week and we would get the escrow money back ( WHICH WAS MONEY I WAS GOING TO PAY TOWARDS MY MOTHERS FUNERAL EXPENSES SHE [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). But again they lied and refuse to abide by the original mortgage loan. I have provided them with all 3 years of tax payments, documentation to show that I also pay homeowners. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] county also always returns their money to them and they have a note not to accept their payments. Now it is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they expect me to pay a payment of over {$1100.00}, which is way more then my Father has from is pension. WE DESPERATELY NEED HELP!!!','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,2.0,'mortgage was for principal and interest $740.00 Flood insurance. mortgage was sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who at one time tried to collect the');
