INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1280,'05/31/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','I opened checking and savings accounts with TD Bank. I have had nothing but problems with TD Bank since. When I opened the account, I accidently left my welcome packet behind, which contained all of my account information. I called TD bank and they put a freeze on that account and advised me to come into the branch and open a new account. Thats exactly what I did. TD initiated an investigation because there were transactions that I did not authorize. TD Bank then closed my new savings account without my knowledge or consent for some odd reason. Then placed restrictions on my current checking account. Even though there is no legitimate reason to do so. I spent over an hour on the phone with another TD Bank agent opening another savings account. The agent advised me that there are no notes stating why the savings account was closed or why restrictions are on my checking account. I checked my account balance today on my checking account and it was over drawn {$6.00} now I checked it again later in the day and now its overdrawn {$100.00}. That amount does not make any sense.TD Bank is willfully mistreating one of its customers. I have proof that TD Bank app and agents give false account balances. I deposited {$420.00} into my checking account. The charges TD bank has listed equals up to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] = - {$31.00} and if TD Bank charged me a {$35.00} transaction fee then my checking account would be [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but TD bank charged me an overdraft fee of {$100.00}. How does that make any sense?','TD BANK US HOLDING COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'TD bank opened checking and savings accounts with TD bank. a freeze on the account was put on the account. TD bank then closed my new savings account without my knowledge');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1281,'05/31/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have been trying to get this financial institution to remove this bankruptcy listing on my particular credit report since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they refuse to do so. My bankruptcy was discharged in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My bankruptcy began in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. All of my bankruptcy records have been dropped from all 3 of the reporting bureaus with the exception of this one record from this one bank and they are only reporting it to this one credit bureau. This is preventing me from refinancing my mortgage and getting rid of my current interest rate of over 7 %. Since this particular credit bureau has allowed all of the other previously listed bankruptcy creditors to be removed from my credit report, why is this bank being allowed to have this one negative record to stay continually listed in my credit report? This credit bureau is refusing to remove this record and I have written to them multiple times and have gotten the same response. They tell me that the record is accurate. I am not disputing the accuracy of the record. I am disputing the fairness and the logic of their actions. It is not logical that all of the other bankruptcy records from all 3 bureaus have been removed and that just this one remains. The bankruptcy was discharged through the courts, therefore the debt to this creditor has been satisfied and no further monies are due. Title to the vehicle was issued to me by this bank and I do not even own the vehicle any longer. In fact, the vehicle has been scrapped.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'bankruptcy was discharged in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they refuse to remove it. all of my bankruptcy records have been dropped');
