INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1291,'05/29/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Struggling to pay your loan','I contacted Santander Consumer USA about my car loan on XX/XX/2018 to discuss a payment plan. I was denied. I explained that I was experiencing a loss of income and wanted to modify the loan. The Agent met with a supervisor and flat out denied to offer any assistance stating " there is nothing we can do '''' I explained I could set up a payment for the next week but needed to look at the dates first. The agent went on to say the car was assigned and good luck. When we bought the car I was forced to purchase GAP insurance which I was told that the bank requires it. This extra monthly amount put the monthly loan higher than what I can afford. The Interest rate is excessive and I am paying [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] per month for a car that is worth [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Owe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) thus upside down. I have been paying this loan for 3 years '''' struggling '''' with the payment. Santander refuses to help me and/or modify as I know is possible upon hardship circumstances which I am in. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the dealer I bought the car from spoke to me about 3 months ago and offered the same model car but a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] per month which made me believe that something is wrong. I have tried to work with the bank and am willing to continue but I am not able to continue at this current rate or without assistance. Additionally, the bank is calling almost 10 times per day which is excessive and no correspondence has ever been sent. I believe that this loan is symptomatic of excessive interest, and the fact I was forced to buy GAP really is consumer preying. I am asking for help as this situation is causing credit issues and financially burdening and stressful but Santander seems that they will not help. I know notes can be modified for good cause yet they refuse. I am also upset that I was forced to add GAP by the bank because of the extra monthly expense. Can I please get some help with this matter?','SANTANDER CONSUMER USA HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,2.0,'a loan agent told me that the bank requires it. he said that the loan was symptomatic of excessive interest. he said that the loan was symptomatic of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1292,'05/29/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','This credit card account is not mine. I have contacted the original creditor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the collection agency handling the account. they said it was opened on line, they are unable to provide me with any signed contracts regarding this or validate the debt. I have never even heard of this company. They have now sent it to the credit bureau and said Im responsible for the debt. I dont understand how they can hold me liable for a debt that is not mine? It is fraudulent or they have made a mistake somewhere within their company either way this is not my debt. I want them to remove the debt from my credit report and seize any further collection attempts toward me and stop credit reporting regarding this account. Thank you.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,4.0,'credit card account is not mine. contacted the original creditor and the collection agency. they say it was opened on line.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1293,'05/28/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XXXX5 Re : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] partial account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] partial account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Dear [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] This letter is in response to the account being reported currently on my credit report concerning the collection of the above reference dating back to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].

I do not believe I owe what you say I owe therefore I dispute this debt. I am well aware of my rights under the Fair Debt Collection Practice Act ( FDCPA ) and my state laws so I hope to save both of us a great deal of time by letting you know that not only do I dispute the validity of this debt, I have also checked with my State Attorney General and verified that the Statue of Limitation for enforcing this type of debt through the courts in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has expired. I have attached a copy of my statue limitation that confirms the limitation in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   is three years. Based on the information reported to all three credit bureaus this account was open on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which will result in this account not only being unverified but also passed the timeframe of statute being open for a total of three years and five months. Therefore, should you decide to pursue this matter in court I intend to inform the court of my dispute of this debt and that the statute of limitations has expired. Documented status reported directly to the credit bureaus states that this account is scheduled to continue on my report until XX/XX/XXXXfurther more confirming the statute of limitation in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of three years. A copy of credit report is attached.

This letter is a formal notification that I consider this matter closed and demand that you or anyone affiliated with your company, as well as any collection agency attached to this un-validate account be removed from all credit bureaus. I look forward to you contacting me in writing to advise me that your debt collection efforts are being terminated or that you or the creditor are taking specific actions allowed by the FDCPA or my state laws.

Be advised that I consider any contact not in accordance with the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act a serious violation to my State Attorney General, to The Federal Trade Commission and, if necessary, take whatever legal action is necessary to protect myself.

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','CNG FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1294,'05/28/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I have been out of school and paying down my debt for a couple of years. I decided to switch how my payments were applied and paid off a vehicle that was very close to being paid off. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I looked at my student loans, and because of what my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  billing statement said at the time I decided to adjust what I was paying. My statement said that I was paid ahead by {$4300.00} and my next required payment was not due for 14 months. 

So I changed my payments, while continuing to pay {$100.00} per month to continue my paid ahead status. When I was completed paying off my vehicle, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my balance had not changed so I didn''t think anything of it. My statement said that I was still paid ahead by nearly {$600.00} and I didn''t have to make a payment until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

So I started back up making payment well above my required amount to further reduce this debt. But after a few months of making these payments, not a single dollar was reducing the debt. They were applying to accrued interest and nothing off the principle. But 4 month later on my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] billing statement ( while they were not applying any to principle ) I was paid ahead at {$1000.00} and didn''t owe a payment until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Not only did they not disclose the payment were being charged to accrued interest, they did not give me updated statement balances, and they held my money that I had paid and didn''t apply it correctly. 

This company is acting fraudulently and in bad faith to not only me but I would venture to guess Thousands of consumers who are using them for their student loans. If they are telling me I am paid ahead, that money should have been used to cover any accrued interest, and or been applied to straight principle. If they are saying I do not owe a payment, how is it that I can still be charged interest? 

I have reached out to Great Lakes and was treated very rudely by both the customer service agent as well as her supervisor. I submitted a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] complaint and got a canned response, not even answering my questions or concerns. 

I demand action be taken to fix this issue because the American consumers are being gutted by this company who is not handling payments in the correct way and not being truthful in the amounts of debt owed. They " hide '''' the true balance which gives consumers a false narrative of their account. This is extreme bad faith and needs to be corrected. 

I would like my account reviewed and any fees credited back to my debt. I have recently gotten so sick of dealing with this company I am refinancing with another company to get away from these unfair and deceptive practices.','GREAT LAKES',2.0,4.0,'my payment was applied to accrued interest and nothing off the principle. but 4 month later on my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1295,'05/28/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Struggling to pay your loan','I cosigned on a vehicle loan for my boyfriend to purchase a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], financed by the American Honda Finance Corporation ( AHFC ). At that time, I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old, a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and was working part-time as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Prior to that work, I worked as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  at an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where patrons could have pizza parties. 
My boyfriend at the time worked as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the Honda dealership where the vehicle was purchased. At the time, I was surprised to be able to co-sign for him since I could not even qualify to sign for my own car, because of my brief employment history, lack of credit and savings. In fact, my own car was in my Fathers name because I did not have any credit. The finance person at the Honda dealership assured me that since I was graduating in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that I was seen as an acceptable person to co-sign for him because I would be getting a full-time job in the near future. 
After breaking up with my boyfriend/childs father, He experienced several employment challenges including working as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. His payment of the car was sporadic and I received calls from the AHFC on numerous occasions. They informed me that I would be held responsible for the vehicle if he did not make the payments, since I was a co-signer on the loan. I informed them on numerous occasions that I was not going to make payments on the vehicle unless I was given the vehicle. 
When I applied for a loan to purchase a home, the mortgage loan office informed me that the vehicle had gone into collection. When I contacted AHFC, they informed me that they had repossessed the vehicle and sold it for {$7800.00}, almost half of what the vehicle is worth per [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] estimates for Private Party Value leaving a balance {$16000.00} that I would have to pay if my ex-boyfriend does not pay it. 
I have attached a copy of sheet entitled, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] indicating that the actual amount of the charge off is {$25000.00}. Although the balance is reported as {$17000.00} over an above the {$23000.00} identified as the balance. The High credit on the loan was {$29000.00} when the vehicle was purchased in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 
I believe that I was used by my boyfriend, the Honda Dealership and the AHFC. I believe that every trick in the book was used to finance my ex-boyfriends car because he was an employee of the Honda Dealership. AHFC never informed me that they were in possession of the vehicle. They just sold it and plan to bill me for the balance owed plus other charges. 

I am willing to pay for my mistake, but I should have been provided an opportunity to have the vehicle if I am being made to pay for it. AHFC never provided me that opportunity. 

I am going to hire an attorney and file reports with the State of Tennessee and the local District Attorneys office.','AMERICAN HONDA FINANCE CORP',2.0,2.0,'my boyfriend bought a car in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. he was a co-signer on the loan');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1296,'05/27/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','Franklin Collections has a collection on my credit file from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have disputed this collection twice of which [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claims that the debt has been verified. With that being said, I have yet to receive for what service was this for. Was it a cell phone? I have requested a detailed report from the collection agency with no answer in my last complaint. I refuse to pay a bill without a detailed description of dates and what it was for.','Franklin Collection Service, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'Franklin Collections has a collection on my credit file from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. a collection');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1297,'05/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I am writing this letter to you regarding the service that I received from the credit reporting bureau Experian. Beginning in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have been working with Experian Credit Bureau to dispute items that are posted on my credit report that are being reported in error. These items are drastically affecting my credit score in a negative manner and is causing me to be denied credit opportunities. I have sent four letters by certified mail within the past nine months to Experian Credit Bureau requesting that any, and all disputable items on my credit report be verified properly per the Fair Credit Reporting Act Section 609 ( a ) ( 1 ). 


Certified letters were delivered to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

According ; to the Fair Credit Reporting Act, Section 609 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), the credit reporting bureaus are required by federal law to verify - through the physical verification of the original signed consumer contract on all accounts that are disputed on a consumers credit report. Along with the verification process, I demanded to see Verifiable Proof of ( an original Consumer Contract with my Signature on it ) for the accounts that were being disputed on my file Under the FCRA, disputed accounts must be removed, if the credit bureau is unable to provide a copy of verifiable proof ie. ( Consumer Contract with Signature ), then the disputed account must be removed from the credit report. I have sent Experian several letters demanding that the accounts be verified per the FCRA. In their response to me ; Experian has stated that the accounts have been verified and updated. However ; Experian has yet to inform me on how they verified the disputed accounts and they have not provided me with a copy of the original contract with my signature on it as proof that the disputed account has been accurately verified. 



I have enclosed a list of the disputed accounts that remain on my credit report, as of the last credit report that I received from Experian dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Name of Account Account Verification Status per Credit Bureau [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Collection/Meets Requirement of FCRA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Paid Closed/meets requirement FCRA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Charge Off [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Purchased by lender [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Collection/Meets Requirement of FCRA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Collection/Meets Requirement of FCRA','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian credit bureau has been working with experian to dispute items posted on my credit report that are being reported in error. these items are drastically affecting my credit score in ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1298,'05/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I sent Equifax a 2nd written request dispute letter on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding the unverified [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] collection account on my credit report. 

