INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1337,'05/19/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has bought multiple minuscule debts of mine to get me to pay more money. One of the debts was originally owned by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was summoned to court over a month ago. I tried to work a payment plan out with the lawyer there but she couldnt get in touch with anyone at the office. I was told I would be notified by email or a phone call within the next 30 days and specifically told them to leave a voicemail if I did not answer. No call at all in over a month','MIDCOUNTRY FINANCIAL CORP',2.0,2.0,'one debt was originally owned by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. a month ago, a lawyer told');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1338,'05/18/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I AM FORMALLY DISPUTING AN ERRONEOUS REPORT MADE TO THE CREDIT BUREAUS BY LOANDEPOT ON MORTGAGE ACCT # : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I enter a 3 month forbearance program offered by LoanDepot to the Florida residents affected by hurricane Irma. As such, I did not have to make payment for the months of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I contacted LoanDepot to make payment arrangements to bring my account up to date. Along with the assurance of not reporting any negative information to the credit bureaus a loan modification was tentatively offered to me after a 3 month trial period in which I would have to pay the amount of {$1600.00} every month from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
After making all 3 payment ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), I contacted Loandepot on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to ask why my account was reported 90 days delinquent to the credit bureaus. LoanDepot representative told me that it had been a mistake on their part and that the account shouldnt have been reported late or delinquent. LoanDepot also stated they were going to report back to the credit bureaus to correct the erroneous report. On the same call a payment for the amount of {$4700.00} was made to bring the account to current ; therefore, the previously offered loan modification was not utilize. 
To this day two credit bureaus ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) are showing my LoanDepot account as 90 days delinquent ; consequently, significantly dropping my credit scores ( in the case of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] almost 200 points ) which in turn affects my ability to make significant purchases and investments previously planned. More importantly affecting my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] status. I am a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] subject to periodic background investigations in which credit history is given serious consideration and attention when determining the ability to maintain a trusted position such as mine.','loanDepot.com, LLC',2.0,2.0,'loan modification offered by loanDepot to the residents affected by hurricane Irma. loan modification was tentatively offered to me after a 3 month trial period. loan modification was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1339,'05/18/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Written notification about debt','I provided written notice to Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC initially on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], via certified letter disputing the validity of the debt owed. I further requested that Portfolio Recovery Associates, provide validation of competence evidence bearing my signature. The company signed for that notice on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Thereafter, I received a summarized statement from PRA alleging that I owed {$5900.00}, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I responded on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] again asking for evidence bearing my signature. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a letter from Portfolio Recovery Associates, again summarizing this alleged debt. The document provided was not from the Original debtor nor did PRA provide any tangible documentation bearing my signature. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dissolved EFFECTIVE XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. With this knowledge, I question the veracity of how PRA obtained validation, competent evidence that this debt is in fact legitimate, WITHOUT my signature. 

I verified via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit Bureau that Portfolio Recovery Associates, made a dispute statement under my name confirming that they completed an investigation of my dispute and further stated that I disputed this matter. 

I am therefore escalating my complaint requesting assistance to have this debt removed from all three of the credit reporting agencies. 

It is now my belief that Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC is willfully acting in bad faith given their refusal to provide the requested information. 

Please be advised, as per FTC opinion letter from Attorney [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a printout of a bill or itemized document does not constitute verification. I asked twice for a document bearing my signature to be provided, in addition to proof of how this information was verified without my signature. 

I am therefore requesting that the debt reported by Portfolio Recovery Associates, be removed from my Credit Reports immediately.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,2.0,'a letter from Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC, claiming that I owed $5900.00. the document provided was not from the original debtor nor did PRA provide');
