INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1346,'05/17/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','First, how and when the capitalized interest was applied was not fully explained. The impact of deferrals/forbearance was not explained. 
Second, I dont think that the capitalized interest is being calculated correctly. I have been paying regularly on my load for 10 years and the principle has not gone down. I feel like I am in a situation that I will die with. The interest is ridiculous. I contacted Navient to ask them the explain how and why I have received each charge of capitalized interest. They referred me to my account history. The account history does not show how it was calculated. I have paid $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in interest and $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the principle. I have pad a minimun of {$200.00} a month for 10 years.I will die before this is paid off. 
Attached is my payment, interest file','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'the interest is ridiculous, but I feel like I will die with the interest. the interest is ridiculous, but the account history does not show how it was calculated.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1347,'05/17/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Traveler''s check or cashier''s check','Problem with customer service','My new boss sends me a Cashiers check Monday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] telling me to deposit in my account. I deposited the check and she was very suspicious about it, asking me if imthe check cleared every 5 minutes. I called Chase bank customer service and spoke with a person in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to double check that everything was right with the check. My understanding is that if something is wrong with the check, the bank is the only entity that can tell me whats going on. I tell her the story and that I thought it was a fake check and she said youre fine cause the check cleared and it was a cashiers check. In order to have one of those you have to pay cash so youre fine that was at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Tuesday morning. At [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my boss tells me to withdraw [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and deposited in a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account to pay for some bills, since the bank told me that everything was fine I did it and I said to myself youre probably overreacting, the bank already told you that it was fine after that she asked the for a {$200.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I sent it as well. By [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my account was negative {$3400.00} ( the amount of the check was {$3900.00} ) I called my boss and she blocked me. When I called the bank they told me that it was my fault that I should be more careful next time. I filled a complaint at the police department and called the Chae complaint department yesterday and honestly, no one really helped.The last person told me I was a scam victim and that she was sorry for the misunderstanding with the customer service rep but I needed to pay that amount by XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] cause after that a debt collector was going to contact me. In conclusion, I called the bank before doing everything else, the rep told me that it was okay. When it comes to my Chase account I only trust Chase customer service. I dont work for them, they should know better!! I need them to find that conversation and deal with the situation. A miscommunication in that magnitude ruined my life basically. Now I owe almost {$4000.00} that obviously I dont have just because I trusted a Chase customer representative that didnt know what she was saying/ doing. Im really disappointed and a little scared of the situation. And at this point I believe theyre not going to help me get to the bottom of this.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a cashiers check was sent to me by boss. she asked me if imthe check cleared every 5 minutes. the bank told me that everything was fine.');
