INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1364,'05/14/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Communication tactics','I opened an account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] many years ago. I was trying to build my credit and my minimum was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  dollars. I made purchases for this amount and made payments on time except for one time and the payment was a few days late. After this I had them call me all hours of the day multiple times a day. They have called from multiple numbers and different states. I have tried to call [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  about this many times, I have somehow accrued over 2,000 dollars in debt for a maximum of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollar credit limit. I have made payments I should not be making and have tried to comply the best way that I could. I did some research and spoke with my bank when recently they took money from me that was unauthorized. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] first and asked them why the money was taken and they said they do not have a record of this money being taken out so I need to call my bank because it is their issue. I was hung up on towards the end of the call and then called my bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My bank was very helpful and put in a dispute to get my money back as well as put a stop payment for them. This is not the first time this has happened with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the lady at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  told me to let the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] know about what I have been dealing with. Just today I received a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] yet again a Colorado number this time claiming that I need to set up a payment to give them the money back that my bank disputed and took back from them. They hreatened that I need to have an attorney call them and I have one last chance before they take further measures. This happens so often and so many times and I am frustrated and worried. I try to do the best I can to pay off my debts and they are relentles. My husband and I both have asked them to stop calling or I have tried to set payment arrangements just to get rid of them but something always happens. I read their reviews and they have a D- by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and it has raised a concern to me with how they treat their customers rudely, by threatening them and calling them in a harassing manner and taking money that should not be taken. They take advantage of other people.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,4.0,'a number at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has called me from multiple states. a number claims that I need to set up a payment to give them');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1365,'05/14/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I paid a debt to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2017. 6 months later in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they reopened the previously close and paid in full debt and now it''s at {$100.00}. I do not owe this and it is affecting my credit rating. I am making this complaint and will hope they take it off my credit report. This still impacts my credit rating and my overall financial health. I was supposed to be building my credit rating to buy a house. Now I''ve been sabotaged!','Ray Klein, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'6 months later in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they reopened the previously close and paid in full debt. now it''s at $100.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1366,'05/14/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Managing the loan or lease','My payment is due on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month to Nissan Finance. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], their system told me that I owed not the {$450.00} monthly payment, but twice that - {$900.00}. They claim that because the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was a Sunday and because they do not process on the weekends and because I had not paid by the preceding Friday, their system told me that the current payment - due XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - was late and then included the payment for NEXT month and so it claimed I owed {$900.00}. Again, this was on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a {$450.00} payment due XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it was doubling what I owed to {$900.00}. So in the " Amount Due '''' they were including a payment not due until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. None of this is hard and I actually have a 10 day grace period on each payment, so they should not be acting like my next payment - due in 30 days - is part of the amount I currently owe. In fact, I believe it may be illegal.','NISSAN MOTOR ACCEPTANCE CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is due on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month. they');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1367,'05/14/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Problem caused by your funds being low','I contacted Citibank via phone to make a routine transfer between my accounts. At the time I was told my account was " blocked ''''. I later found out it was blocked due to a " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' review. An email sent to me in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I did not open requested information. Since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Citibank never contacted me to follow up on the email. They never : sent a follow up email, sent a letter via mail, called me or the additional signers on the business account, They did however hold on to our hard earned money which did not allow me to access funds I needed to make payroll for my 35+ staff. I believe if they blocked my account they should give me my money and close the account - not hold on to it until it''s cleared. 

Further, after I submitted requested paperwork and heard it will take 4 days to clear my account NO ONE from Citibank contacted me. Instead I had to contact them on the 2nd day to find out what is going on.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'Citibank never contacted me to follow up on the email. they did hold on to my hard earned money which did not allow me to make payroll for my 35+ staff.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1368,'05/13/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On all 3 of my credit reports Wells Fargo reported the credit card was charged off XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] however that is inaccurate information. The card was charged off fraudulently XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The late fees were refunded because Wells Fargo know they made a mistake and still forced me to pay for interest for a card that should have been closed XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However They have reported the card charge off date as XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is not true. It was charged off XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
