Submitted a dispute with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the past, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no resolution from agency','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1400,'05/07/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','can not qualify for loan because information on my credit report is not accurate. The delinquencies have all been cleared up but my reports do not reflect any of this information.','FIFTH THIRD FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'information on my credit report is not accurate. the delinquencies have all been cleared up.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1401,'05/07/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Getting a credit card','I originally caught the fraudulent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account in the amount of {$2000.00} on XX/XX/XXXXand immediately called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to report that this account was opened fraudulently under my name. They sent me a Fraudulent Charge Affidavit in the mail which I returned to them via fax on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I also included my Federal Trade Commission Identity Theft Report. When I hadn''t heard from them, I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  again onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They claimed to have not received my fax, but when I asked them to look again, they found the FTC Identity Theft Report but had lost the Affidavit. They asked me to send it again via email and I did on that same day. I followed back up today, XX/XX/XXXXand was originally told that they did not receive my documents. When I challenged this, the person I spoke with told me that " oh yes, they have the documents, but it would take 60-90 days for the investigation to complete ''''.','Atlanticus Services Corporation',2.0,4.0,'XX/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1402,'05/07/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Struggling to pay your loan','We purchased a used Harley Davidson motorcycle in XX/XX/2016. I have often signed into my online account with Harley Davidson Financial and scheduled my payment for a date later than the due date. I do this prior to the date the payment is due. Well, the due date is the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ... ..starting the VERY NEXT DAY, I begin getting multiple calls every day asking about my PAST DUE account. Every time, I tell them to check my account ; I have scheduled the payment for later. Every time, they ask why. Every time, I tell them it''s because of how my paychecks fall. My scheduled payment is normally 7-10 days after the due date, so it''s not like I am skipping a whole month ''s payment or anything. I just don''t understand why they have to REPEATEDLY call me when they can plainly see I have scheduled the payment. They have no leg to stand on anyway, as my personal banker explained to me that even if they say there is no " 10 day grace period '''', by law there is one. They are not supposed to call you until that 10 day grace period is up, but regardless, I have a scheduled payment. There should be no calls to my work or cell phone, much less multiple calls every single day until the scheduled payment has been made.','HARLEY DAVIDSON FINANCIAL SERVICES INC.',2.0,2.0,'a used Harley Davidson motorcycle was purchased in XX/XX/2016. a scheduled payment is usually 7-10 days after the due date. a scheduled payment is');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1403,'05/07/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','What happened? 
two of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], were compromised by a person i did business with that had all my personal information. They were issues cards on my account without my knowledge, they evidently changed my address to a fraudulent address in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] NY. ( A ) I have relentlessly tried to get [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to removed the fraudulent address from my credit report and they refused to. ( B ) I have also tried to resolve these fraudulent unauthorized charges off my profile and it continues to be a very impossible task. The facts are even verified by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  president office from letters they have sent to me. I have called them and left messages for the representative by the name [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ext [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and no call back. The fact is all the charges were made after XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], here reply letter stated the fraud unauthorize user taken off the account, why do they continue to give me a hard time to correct this problem? The account was carrying a - {$200.00} balance for 4 months and in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they even sent me the credit for the {$200.00}. Then in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 7 months after the issue was resolved [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] opened another account in my name with a different account number and sent me statement that i owed them [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], then by XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] it was a {$33000.00} balance, i have not did any transaction with them since the account was closed in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], they are still reporting these fraudulent numbers on my account, i need them to fix their errors and clear my account.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a person i did business with compromised two of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts. they changed my address to a fraudulent address in [COMP');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1404,'05/07/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I disputed an account on my Equifax report. It is from a collection company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Original creditor was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have no clue who this original creditor is. Equifax said the information was accurate but when I spoke with a representative I was told their investigation process was to ask [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if the information was correct. They replied that it was. The end. I have asked Equifax and the creditor to supply me any kind of proof that the account is mine. No one has. I have no idea how to prove that something does not exist. Please help. The amount of this collection is {$220.00}. Original date open was XX/XX/2013. I certainly do not believe that the FCRA held this type of investigation as appropriate protection for the consumer.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'disputed an account on my Equifax report. it is from a collection company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. original creditor was [COMP');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1405,'05/07/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Applying for a mortgage or refinancing an existing mortgage','We to local Wells Fargo Bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to refinance our home. We completed the paperwork and the mortgage manager looked at it and made us pay. {$500.00} to start process. He said it look great and they would call us back if we need to come back to do more paperwork! 5 days later a Denial Letter came in. They said they were sorry and they were keeping our {$500.00}. Dollars. No explanation. That day the had 10 others apply for a refince mortage and everyone was denied. I found out years later that the local Wells Fargo has been scamming Military Families for years. We look back and really felt that we were spam also as a military family!','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'the local Wells Fargo bank has been scamming Military Families for years. the bank has been scamming military families for years.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1406,'05/06/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Closing on a mortgage','The complaint is about Wrongful Reporting of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Resulted in More Taxes and Suffering. 
Mr Cooper had given wrong numbers on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Box 5, MIP ) for the years [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which resulted in more taxes to be paid. They ended up correcting the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for both years, but that was not proactive on their end and took me several attempts to convince them that they gave me wrong numbers. During the conversation over the phone, some employees referred me to some bogus, not-real IRS laws that don''t exist, and when I asked for a reference to those laws, they backed out and tried to change the subject, and ended up connecting me to a manager. I have been trying to amend my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] tax return, but the allowance I wanted to use for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] MIP deduction has expired and no longer available, which resulted in me overpaying taxes to the IRS that I can''t recoup due to their delay in correcting my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s. I asked to be reimbursed, but they declined my request. I had to send too much time researching and trying to amend my tax return, but it ended up time and money consuming, and worthless due to expiration of MIP deduction allowance. They denied responsibility and refused to help even though it was their mistake. I think that might have happened to many people most of which don''t know. They did tell me that they updated the IRS on my corrected [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s and that was all they had to to. 
The main issue is that I had my closing around XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], where Closing Costs included advanced payments of MIP and else that I agreed to pay at the time. I got my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they included only about {$120.00} of MIP paid which I thought was accurate, then I got my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which had about {$1300.00}. By reviewing Closing documents from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I noticed that what Mr. Cooper reported for my MIP in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was wrong. I had contacted them several time via email and even phone calls, but they denied my claims since they were sure their numbers were accurate. I had to ask to talk several people to over the numbers and insisted that the numbers were wrong, which they started to question but started referring me to IRS law that did not exist to justify their wrong reporting.I ended up asking for verification and references for those laws, and that''s when they panicked because they were in violations of some laws. They asked me to allow more time to investigate AGAIN and ended up sending me an updated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for year [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with MIP ( box 5 ) amount of {$3300.00}. I am not sure if they did that to others, but the way they received my claim and lack of seriousness caused me lots of frustration and over payments of taxes. They declined responsibility and want me to take the burden of their wrong doing, including my time, money and frustration. 

I can provide more documents upon request.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',4.0,4.0,'a complaint is about Wrongful Reporting of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the report resulted in more taxes to be paid. the');
