INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1430,'05/02/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','I have been on automatic payments with my Bank of America credit card and then all of a sudden, I get reported as 30 days late on my credit report and got a phone call from a customer service rep. There is no way. My payments were coming out on auto pay so how was I 30 days late. Then I made a payment and they lowered my credit limit to {$2300.00}. I just paid another {$1200.00} on my credit card too. I was doing everything I could to be responsible and make on time payments. Now I feel like I just keep getting punished. I was reported as late after I thought it was on auto pay and then my credit limit gets lowered.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'I was reported as 30 days late on my credit report. the bank of America customer service rep lowered my credit limit to $2300.00.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1431,'05/02/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','I sold my home on XX/XX/2018. My wife inadvertently provided her personal credit card for the wire transfer, and approximately {$330000.00} was transferred to that account. We immediately contacted Bank of America to begin transferring those funds to our personal checking account, and we were told the process would take 2-7 business days because of " the large amount '''' of the funds and because we needed a check for money laundering. 

We called back after 7 business days had passed and were told that it was actually going to be up to 12-17 business days. After asking whether Bank of America had performed all the checks they needed to perform already, we were told that yes, they had been. I explained that I was confused why in that case my money was being held hostage by the bank without interest, which seemed to be a violation of federal bank regulations. I was not given a reasonable response to why the funds were being held ; both the associate with whom I was speaking and her supervisor appeared sympathetic, similarly confused, but unable to help. 

At this point it appears to me that the bank is holding a significant amount of my cash hostage without reason other than profiting from the interest on it without any compensation to me. While this is a few hundred dollars of interest lost to me, across many this could add up to a substantial sum. I believe this is worth probing further.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a bank employee was able to help with the transfer of funds to a personal checking account. the bank is holding a significant amount of my cash hostage without reason.');
