INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1440,'04/30/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Threatened to contact someone or share information improperly','I am a victim of identity theft, company [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been reporting negative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account that is not mind this company is violating my rights this Account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was dispute on all 3 credit bureaus and remove,XX/XX/2017 this company is out of order.','ERC',2.0,2.0,'compTE_ANONYMISÉ is a victim of identity theft. company has reported negative account that is not mind this company is violating my rights this Account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1441,'04/30/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','I applied and got approved for a Wells Fargo Business Platinum credit card that comes with 1 % cashback on purchases. I have not received any of the cashback rewards despite having made over {$2500.00} in purchases on this credit card. I called to fix this issue and never got a call back.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'I applied and got approved for a Wells Fargo Business Platinum credit card. I have not received any cashback rewards despite making over $2500.00 purchases.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1442,'04/30/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','Citigroup ''s policy forcing vendors to refuse firearm sales to under 21 year-olds, regardless of the law. I don''t actually have a credit card account with them, but there is no option for filing a complaint regarding their discriminatory business policies. 

By instituting policies which require their banking customers to discriminate against prospective clients based on age, in an apparent effort to affect their own brand of restrictions on firearms ownership, CitiBank appears to be attempting to infringe upon the second amendment rights of millions of law-abiding American citizens. ( the ones that bailed them out ) Since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has not even remotely suggested that the financial activities they are targeting by this policy are illegal in any way, while they themselves enjoy government support and benefits, I believe they should limit the scope of their policies to deny only those transactions that might be illegal, or at the very least, those not GUARANTEED to the people by the US Constitution. 

While I do believe that businesses in the United States, for the most part, should be free to set policies as they see fit, this particular policy tends to force other businesses into breaking federal age discrimination statutes in order to continue doing business with them. Since it violates the rights of so many others, I hope that if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] does not voluntarily revise or abandon this policy, they might be legally compelled to do so.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citigroup''s policy forcing vendors to refuse firearm sales to under 21 year-olds, regardless of the law. a british law-abiding citizen has');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1443,'04/30/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','My wife and I had a consolidation loan, checking acct with TD Bank. Last XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we went into the local branch to conduct some business and the representative asked us if we were interested in a credit card. They said if we spent so much we would get {$150.00} back. This sounded interesting. When they ran my credit, I was awarded a credit card with a {$20000.00} limit and my wife was awarded one with {$7800.00}. I was shocked because I know I have a lot of things going on with finances. She said we could consolidate debt, take a cruise, etc. So based on all this information she sold us on, we accepted the terms. 
So I used my card to payoff 2 credit cards which was about {$7500.00} and put another {$5000.00} on the card for about {$12000.00} in use. 
Then around XX/XX/XXXXof this year they send me a letter saying they ran my credit and based on that, they would have to reduce my credit limit to {$13000.00}. They also said another reason was I was delinquent on my last payment. Delinquent, excuse me! Delinquent is when you are more than 30 days late not 4 days late. I happened to be sick during that time is the reason It was 4 days late. 
This Bank sold me a bill of goods to open up two new credit card accounts. I expected them to honor that obligation. 
If you look at the reason my credit score was what it was when they not only approved me for a credit card but for {$20000.00}, it pretty much matches the reasons they now say they have to reduce my credit limit. Yes my score is lower but it''s still good. 
It''s ironic, I had a consolidation loan with this bank and they give me a credit card. I actually paid off the consolidation loan prior to them reducing my credit limit. 
I''m sick and tired of financial institutions playing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with folks. They seem to do whatever they want without a penalty yet the honorable consumer gets screwed. 
Yes I put money on that card, we''re in the process of fixing up our house to sell it. Isn''t that why I have a card is to use it when I need to? 
I have done nothing to this bank to place any doubt on whether I can honor my obligations because I always pay my bills. But my bank has now turned against me and reduced my credit limit. I was at a 63 % debt ratio and by them reducing my credit limit that has changed to 93 %. This will certainly cause my score to drop even further. 
If we sell our house in the next 2-3 months, I will be shopping for a mortgage and now by TD bank actions, my score will be even lowered which may affect what kind of loans we can get. I feel betrayed by this bank. The ironic thing is despite our circumstances this bank still sends My wife and me mailers to do business. 
There is something seriously wrong here when Financial Institutions can play [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with peoples credit scores. They sold us a bill of goods for us to open up credit card accounts. I have honored my obligations and they have reneged on theres. 
Their actions are going to lower my credit score even lower which is what I don''t need now. I have done nothing to deserve this. I have fulfilled all my obligations with this bank. 
I currently have a checking account and this credit card account with them. I had a consolidation loan with them which I paid off ahead of time and this is how this bank chooses to treat this customer. They should be ashamed of themselves.','TD BANK US HOLDING COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a consolidation loan with TD Bank was approved by the bank. my wife and I had a credit card with a $20000.00 limit. a credit');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1444,'04/30/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','This all happened from the past 4 weeks and is still going on. I am having a major problem with my Citi simplicity credit card and I have been through absolute [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with their customer service for hours and hours and days and days and I just can''t take this anymore. I have made a lot of payments on my card to get rid of the cash advance fees but I have now had my card blocked because they said I have 2 returned check fees and a failed debit payment. When I looked on the statement I saw that they indeed received those payments from me with a confirmation number on the exact same days that they gave me those fees. The money has been taken from my bank account and they have put a hold on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] $ payments all while giving me those return check fees. After fighting with them for so long I finally started to make progress as they were going to remove those fees and put my money back on the card as well as I was promised by multiple people that since I went through all of this for no reason that they were going to give me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars worth of credits because of how badly I was treated. This was all promised to me from managers. It has now been a week and they put [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on my card which I went to go use and they declined it and took it right back. I was so upset that I was promised all of this for everything they put me through and received nothing. In fact I did get a woman that thought she put me on hold and actually mocked me to her co workers in whiny voice completely making fun of me and are just playing games with me now and I have bad [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] problems as it is and this whole mess is making me sick. The funny thing is that yes I have to have consent from them to record the phone call but I do not have to have the consent when I am placed on hold for long periods of time. Well it just so happens that I didn''t fact get the woman who placed me on hold mocking me when she thought she put me on hold and that is a serious problem and I am going to discuss this with my lawyer. Citi has really screwed me over and now I get mocked for wanting what is owed to me so please let me know if there is anymore of a blatant disrespect and disregard for a customer and a complete showing of defamation of character and I will be talking to my lawyer about the way I have been treated.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a woman who placed me on hold mocked me to her co workers in whiny voice. she said she put me on hold and mocked me to her co workers');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1445,'04/29/2018','Checking or savings account','Savings account','Opening an account','I have been a Chase checking account owner for over 15 years. I recently tried opening a Savings account online ; I went through the process of logging into my checking account and transferring funds from my checking account into the new savings accounts. Once the process was done, I was asked to create a PIN for an ATM card. After this, I was informed that the Savings account was successfully created and the card would be mailed to me within 7 - 10 business days, while the Savings account was supposedly opened immediately.

I went to my accounts on the Chase.com website and I saw my Chase credit card, Chase Checking account information but not the Savings account. 

After two weeks of waiting, I called Chase customer service on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the lady I spoke with confirmed that my account had no savings information on there. She advised me to go through the process again. 

On the same day, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I went through the same process described as above. After which, I looked at my online Chase accounts and still, no Savings account. I immediately called Customer Service and they once again confirmed that there was no incidence of a Savings account creation.

My concern is that the system might be slow and since I have transferred money twice to the phantom Savings account ( s ), in the future, these accounts may be created, thereby prompting the funds draw from my account twice and then I will be hit with overdraft fees.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'I recently tried opening a Savings account online. I was asked to create a PIN for an ATM card. the account was supposedly opened immediately.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1446,'04/29/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I am having a hard time with Ocwen removing a foreclosure from my credit report because they were able to resell the property at more then was owed on the loan. They would not work with us at the time to even modify the loan at rates we could afford. We had owned the house for over 7 years at this point and asked for the principle to be lowered due to what the property was worth so we could stay in the home. I talked to at least 50 people in the company because they were always assigning us a new case manager so nothing would ever get would ever get taken care of because the next person would have to start the process over and over each time. Then this led to an increased payment. I paid 2 loan modification payments which were never included in our loan and then the payments were always higher then what we agreed on. I are not the type of people to not pay my bills as you can see for the first home that I bought and now rent due to the foreclosure. I am at the point that I would like to buy another home and feel Im very capable of taking care of the bill each month as long as the lending company is sticking to their side of the agreements which I know that Ocwen did not. How can I get some type of help stating that Ocwen loan company did not try to really help me only really wanting to foreclose on my house??','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',4.0,4.0,'a foreclosure was re-sellable and the mortgage was owed on the loan. the company would not work with us to modify the loan at rates we could afford. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1447,'04/29/2018','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Payday loan','Charged fees or interest you didn''t expect','Before I applied for this loan, it was advertised that if I log into the mobile app everyday that I will not be charged a membership fee. It says thats the fee is usually {$29.00} a month but for logging in everyday the fee will me {$0.00} a month. After contacting customer service, I was told another story that was never explained before accepting this me loan. Once I reached out, I was told that I would be charged my loan payment every pay date and then a {$36.00} membership fee that will apply {$50.00} a month to my investment account, leaving the remaining {$29.00} to go towards my membership fee but logging into the app each day actually just makes it so that a dollar a day goes towards that same investment account instead of me paying {$0.00} for a membership fee as it advertised. I would have never known this information if I never reached out to the company about this so I feel as though this was very deceptive. I was told that there was nothing they could do because since I have the loan Im obligated to pay these fees until the loan is paid in full but I would have never agreed to this loan if I had the correct details in the first place. I have the screenshots that show how the loan is actually advertised but nowhere does it break down the actual process of the loan and the fees the way the agent I spoke with broke it down to me. It literally just says the membership fee is {$0.00} a month if you log in to the account every day, which I did. Ive never felt so deceived by a loan company in my life and even when speaking with the agent that explained it to me, he also agreed with me that the website does not accurately explain the way the loan really works so to me it seems like a very shady way to get people to get stuck into the the loan and have these fees come out of their checking accounts every single paycheck, thinking that the process would be different.','MoneyLion Inc.',2.0,2.0,'logging into the app every day makes it so that a dollar a day goes towards that same investment account instead of me paying $0.00 for a membership fee.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1448,'04/28/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Other service problem','I find it reprehensible that Bank of America and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are using social engineering to punish legal businesses that deal in firearms. 

For companies that were saved by government ( taxpayer ) bailouts and have substantial government business, they have no right to deny financial services to any businesses that are conducting legal and constitutionally protected commerce.

I will review any future personal dealings I might have with these two banks if they continue their plans to punish these types of businesses and proceed with their unjust intentions.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'banks and COMPTE are using social engineering to punish legal businesses. they have no right to deny financial services to any businesses that are conducting legal and constitutionally protected commerce.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1449,'04/28/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','Two banks [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Bank of America are now saying they will stop doing business and extending credit with business and maybe in the future people who are involved in the gun industry and rights.

These activities are legal under law and the banks are using their power to dictate what happens in the US shutting out business and people who they disagree with then controlling the public. 

This tactic in the future could be used against anything they disagree with or want to control or sway in the country. 

This situation sounds highly worrisome.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'two banks are now saying they will stop doing business and extending credit with business. they are using their power to dictate what happens in the US shutting out business. this tactic');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1450,'04/28/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Other service problem','This is a complaint on Bank of America ''s new policy discriminating against customers because they don''t believe in the customers 2nd Amendment rights of law abiding United States citizens.

The company took billions of dollars in bail out money without questioning whether the tax payers that paid for it were 2nd amendment advocates or not. This new discriminatory policy is hypocritical at best. If they chose to have the basis be religion, race, gender, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] orientation or if you used your freedom of speech to express an opposing viewpoint, the outcry would cause them to be fined or put out of business. The constitutional protection for the 2nd amendment is no different. 

Bank of America must stop discriminating against law abiding citizens. It is unethical for them to try to use their influence to dictate to customers what their constitutional rights are.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'bank of America took billions of dollars in bail out money without questioning whether the tax payers that paid for it were 2nd amendment advocates or not. this new policy is hypocritical');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1451,'04/28/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','My federal student loans through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] were being serviced through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I went from being an employed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with children to unemployed/not enrolled in school due to an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] diagnosis in Spring of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I made my institution of higher education aware of my situation, as I was on a scholarship. I was immediately placed in deferment until I was able to return to class. I was never contacted by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that they owned my loans or how to begin payments. I received a letter that they were going to garnish my income tax refund for tax year [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I filed an extension for my tax return until I was able to sort out the discrepancy. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and informed them of my circumstances, as well as explained that I had not received any communication from them about my account at all. I was told I would be immediately placed on deferment by their representative and she requested proof of my income/welfare eligibility. I faxed in everything that was requested. I later discovered that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] placed me in a temporary forbearance instead of deferment and my loan amount ( {$4500.00} and {$2200.00} ) gained interest ( {$810.00} ) and was sold to a new creditor. The new creditor contacted me upon gaining ownership of my loans and consolidated my loans into one loan and I owe {$7500.00}. I have 28 late payments reporting on my credit reports in the 24 months they serviced my loans. While my 2 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts show as being closed, my student loan is reporting on 3 different accounts- 2 negative accounts being [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has unfairly and incorrectly reported my history to all 3 credit bureaus for years. Reporting any invalidated information to major credit bureaus may constitute defamation of character, as negative listing on credit report does not allow me to enjoy the benefits of good credit and jeopardizes my credit worthiness. I have the right to fair credit reporting and want them to report accurately.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'my loans were being serviced through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1452,'04/27/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Dear Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, Please accept this letter as a request to file complaint against PHH Mortgage Services regarding charges assessed to an escrow account, and request for restitution of charges. Please also accept this letter as a request to file complaint against [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for request of property charge reimbursements, and for dismissal of reimbursement request with prejudice. 
Accounting We hold a conventional home mortgage loan with PHH Mortgage. It was established XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and matures on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The property ( also later referenced as parcel ) under mortgage is the primary residence. Property taxes are assessed via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County. PHH Mortgage Services, since the loans inception in year XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], has collected the parcels taxes and held them in escrow, as part of the propertys monthly mortgage payment. PHH Mortgage services biannually issues [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County payments to cover the propertys taxes out of the escrow account. 
The mortgage holders received an escrow overage check in year XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasurers office to confirm the property taxes had been paid, which they had. The mortgage holders then called PHH Mortgage Services to confirm the overage check was not a mistake. PHH Mortgage  confirmed the taxes had been paid, the escrow account was not negative or in an Advance position with PHH Mortgage Services, and  that the overage reimbursement was indeed valid. 
The mortgage holders continued to received escrow overage checks until year XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The same process was followed by the mortgage holders with every check received : the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasurers Office was called to ensure taxes were paid, and PHH Mortgage Services was called to ensure it was not a mistake. Every inquiry had the same results : the taxes had been paid and PHH Mortgage Services confirmed the overage reimbursement was valid. 
In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the mortgage holders received a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] division. The letter stated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had mistakenly paid property taxes for the parcel from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requested reimbursement in the amount of {$13000.00}. 
The mortgage holders were astounded. The mortgage holders did not know the parcels taxes were being paid by any source other than PHH Mortgage Services. There was certainly no expectations [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would ever pay the parcels taxes. Neither mortgage holder had ever held accounts with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; not loans, bank accounts or any other form ( s ) of credit. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had never been requested to pay the property taxes, nor were they obligated to do so. 
The mortgage holders directly contacted the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasures office and inquired to how this might have occurred. A clerck, in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Tax Department, noted it could be a result of a misapplied parcel payment. The clerk further explained that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] likely had a typo in a parcel number, and it could have resulted in payments being made on the property taxes accidentally. At the mortgage holders request the clerk put a flag on the property to ensure that only the mortgage holders or their lender ( PHH Mortgage Services ) could pay the property taxes for the parcel going forward. 
The mortgage holders immediately following the phone call with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasures Office, called PHH Mortgage Services. The mortgage holders alerted PHH Mortgage Services of the likely reason for the escrow refunds that had been occurring. They may be a result of misapplied parcel payments by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. PHH Mortgage Services was unaware this was occurring. PHH Mortgage Services was able to confirm their system showed they had sent funds to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County for the parcels property taxes biannually. PHH Mortgage Services documented that they had later received refunds from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasury, for overapplied parcel tax payments. The overapplied funds returned by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County were then sent out to the mortgage holders as escrow overage reimbursements. PHH Mortgage Services put a note on the account to ensure the parcels taxes were paid to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County and that should overapplied escrow funds be identified going forward a review would take place. PHH Mortgage Services also immediately started an escrow review on the mortgage holders mortgage account. 
The mortgage holders sought legal counsel regarding the funds [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was requesting reimbursement of. The attorney counseled the mortgage holders to deny the reimbursement request from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as there was no legal obligation for reimbursement. A letter was sent to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], via attorney, on the mortgage holders behalf denying the reimbursement. This was at a personal cost to the mortgage holders of {$990.00}. Inherent in the denial for reimbursement was the denial of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] request to speak to the mortgage service company ( PHH Mortgage Services ), who was responsible for paying the parcel taxes. 
The mortgage holders followed up with PHH Mortgage Services once the letter had been sent by attorney to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] denying the reimbursement. The purpose was to confirm that recent property taxes due on the parcel had been paid by PHH Mortgage Services, confirm an overapplied funds situation had not again occurred, check in to see if anything was found in the audit PHH Mortgage Services was performing on the account, and to notify PHH Mortgage Services [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] request was being denied. 
A few days after the mortgage holders called PHH Mortgage Services, PHH Mortgage Services called the mortgage holders. PHH Mortgage Services notified the mortgage holder the escrow account now had a negative balance. The mortgage holder was asked if they wanted to pay the balance due in full or have it divided up into monthly installments, which would be added to the mortgage payment. When the mortgage holder inquired as to why there was now a negative balance, PHH Mortgage Services confirmed that PHH Mortgage Services had contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and issued a reimbursement to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$13000.00}. 
Again, the mortgage holders were astounded. PHH Mortgage Services had given no indication in any form ( call, email, text, portal message, letter ) they may/would contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding the reimbursement request. The mortgage holders had never asked/authorized PHH Mortgage Services to contact and/or make a reimbursement to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding the reimbursement request. As noted above, according to counsel, there was no legal obligation for the mortgage holders to reimburse [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Yet PHH Mortgage Services issued reimbursement to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$13000.00}, had already added this amount to the mortgage balance as an escrow advance, and had done so without notice and without the consent of the mortgage holders. 
The mortgage holders arranged a call to speak with a PHH Mortgage Services supervisor. The purpose was to voice concern with the process, its legality, and to negate the {$13000.00} PHH Mortgage Services had charged to the escrow account without authorization from either mortgage holder. The supervisor noted it was done and that PHH Mortgage Services acted in its own best interest to protect the asset from a possible lien ( against the parcel ) originating from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for reimbursement of the mistakenly paid property taxes. 
No documentation was ever provided by PHH Mortgage Services on the {$13000.00} charge. Further, no documentation was ever provided by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] noting PHH Mortgage Services had reimburse [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The only documentation evident of the {$13000.00} transaction is reflected in the PHH Mortgage Service portal, in viewing the Mortgage Accounts Annual Escrow Statement. 
Conclusion Reasons stand that the mortgage holders did no harm, and also conducted due diligence in : paying into escrow to cover their parcels property taxes ; vetted parcel taxes were paid with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasurers Office ; vetted the mortgage holder, PHH Mortgage Services, was paying the taxes and processes were being followed in paying the parcel taxes ; never requested payments be made on their behalf on parcel taxes by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; immediately notified [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Treasurers office of the unintentional payments by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to prevent future occurrences ; immediately notified PHH Mortgage Services of the unintentional payments by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to prevent future occurrences ; sought out and paid for legal counsel to determine if there was legal obligation to repay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for unintentional property tax payments ; never requested PHH Mortgage Services reimburse [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for unauthorized payment of property taxes. 
Complaint & Restitution The mortgage holders request the following complaints and restitutions be made : The complaint against PHH Mortgage Services : PHH Mortgage Services made a non-obligatory payment to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and then assessed the amount to the mortgage holders mortgage, in the form of an escrow advance. Prior to PHH Mortgage Services taking any action with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the mortgage holders denied [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] request for reimbursement and informed PHH Mortgage Services of this denial in a phone call ; the denial notifying [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was sent by mail via attorney. Despite the notice given to PHH Mortgage Services regarding the denial, PHH Mortgage Services contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and made a non-obligatory payment to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], without the knowledge or consent of the mortgage holders. The amount PHH Mortgage Services paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was the amount [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had requested reimbursement for, because of unintentional tax payments [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] made on the mortgage holders parcel, {$13000.00}. 

The remuneration request against PHH Mortgage Services : the mortgage holders request the {$13000.00} charged to their mortgage as an escrow advance be stricken from their account permanently, and any payments the mortgage holders made toward the advance be refunded them, without harm. It is further requested that PHH Mortgage Services actions may not result in any harm to the mortgage holders, should attempts be made by PHH Mortgage Services to reclaim the {$13000.00} from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

The complaint being made against [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requested reimbursement in the amount of {$13000.00} for unintentional payment of property taxes on a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County parcel. The mortgage holders did not request [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to pay their taxes and were not aware of the taxes being paid by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] until so notified. The mortgage holders should not, under any circumstances, be held responsible for the actions ( mistake ) of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

The remuneration request against [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : the mortgage holders are denying the request for reimbursement to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The mortgage holders seek written confirmation the reimbursement request made by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is dismissed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] without reimbursement and that no further request/attempt for reimbursement may ever be pursued. Should PHH Mortgage seek to reclaim the {$13000.00} reimbursement payment it made to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], no actions may be taken to  seek reimbursement by any party the reimbursement request denial stands under any condition ( s ), without financial remuneration to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and with prejudice. 
Enclosures/Documentation In the form of attachments : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Reimbursement Request XXXXReimbursementRequest $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Attorney Letter Mailed to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Denying Reimbursement DenialOfRequestSentToXXXX Attorney bill for counsel and letter to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] IMSB Billing.pdf PHH Mortgage Services Escrow Statement showing additional charge of {$7400.00}, {$1800.00}, {$1500.00}, {$1500.00}, and {$1400.00} totaling {$13000.00} PHHEscrowCharges $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Respectfully, Mortgage Holders','PHH Mortgage Services Corporation',2.0,4.0,'PHH Mortgage Services has collected the parcels taxes and held them in escrow. the mortgage holders received an escrow overage check in year XX/XX/');
