I missed a few payments due to the previous payments made towards this loan, and that caused me to be late paying other bills rent, utilities etc. I received a letter in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that I would be taken to court if I did not follow the new payment schedule for a balance of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Granted, this is a loan that I know has to be repaid but the interest rate is ridiculous. The new contact that Ive spoken with is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ext. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It is as if nothing I paid was applied to the loan. As of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have paid this lender the following. 
XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Amt [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Amt [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Amt [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Amt [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Amt [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Amt [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Total {$1700.00} Even with a missed payment what is the actual amount owed?','MoneyLion Inc.',2.0,2.0,'money Lion phone borrowed a loan in the amount of $1700.00. the payments were $410.00 a month and I thought a portion of that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1454,'04/27/2018','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I paid {$10000.00} to reinstate my mortgage on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was told the amount included XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. I spoke to several consumer service representatives that confirmed that my mortgage was paid untilXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I filed a complaint on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after receiving automated calls that I owed for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I received no response until XX/XX/XXXXwhere Mr.Cooper/Nationstar admitted they had miss informed on me XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( 10 days after the payment was accepted ) and incorrectly applied my mortgage payment to legal fees. The explanation is unacceptable the restatement amount should have included legal fees. The representative on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( which was recorded ) told me no legal fees were on the account. I had him check three times if the reinstatement amount was correct. He confirmed it was then I paid the amount requested that day. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in response to a letter I was sent by Nationstar/Mr. Cooper saying I would have to request that the mistakenly applied mortgage to the legal fees be reversed to be applied to my mortgage. I ask her to reverse the payment to its original intent. I dont understand this, if Mr. Cooper/Nationstar admitted they made a mistake why would I have to call them in order for them to fix their mistake. Also, it isnt legal to quote a reinstatement amount and accept the payment then say it was an accounting error. Especially, when 3 different representives confirmed I paid the correct amount through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Now they have a demand letter saying Im 3 months behind when Im 2 months behind.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid $10000.00 to reinstate my mortgage. XX/XX/');
