INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1478,'04/24/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','False statements or representation','I received a letter from Mitchell Bluhm Law regarding a bill for my adult son stating it was an older bill from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with a balance of {$170.00}. I contacted MBA Law and set up payments with my debit card. After they have my card information, the next letter I get states the date of service was in fact not form XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The letter was dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. NO account is going to go to collections in 4 weeks time. They had already taken payments out of my bank account with the impression that this was an old bill, not a bill from 4 weeks ago.. and my son was not in the hospital on that date. So I called MBA on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice and left 2 messages questioning this, and asking for a call back. I emailed 2 people asking them to stop the payments ( they told me on initial contact that I could request to hold payments ). I got ZERO response from either contact. So I called again on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. So on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I contacted my bank and told them what had happened. My bank reversed the charges and put a request in to MBA for contact. The next thing I get is a notice that they have reported me to the credit bureaus. Without even acknowledging my requests for clarification of a debt that say I owe for my adult, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] son who is also on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Yesterday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called MBA again and left 2 messages. I got no returned call. Today I have emailed them twice, no return messages. But yet they want my money and can not validate a debt.','The Law Offices of Mitchell D. Bluhm & Associates',2.0,2.0,'a letter from Mitchell Bluhm Law stating a bill for my adult son was dated. it states the date of service was not form XX/XX/');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1479,'04/24/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have an investigaton with CFPB involing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on my equifax I have paid aall payments ontime except when I was hit by two natural Disasters Equifax says they need more time to investigate this I feel Equifax should change [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to Current never Late on my Equifax credit report','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'CFPB has an investigaton with CFPB involing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COM');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1480,'04/23/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','For a year we did over {$55000.00} worth of purchasing, and prompt full-balance payment, through our American Express gold card. Throughout that time, AmEx repeatedly and consistently raised and lowered our allotted credit limit. The assurance was made that once we proved ourselves throughout that year, the limit would be stabilized in accordance with our spending habits and credit score. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we were offered an AmEx Platinum card. Our maximum allotted limit was {$50000.00}, with a {$25000.00} ''layaway '' for certain qualified purchases ( air fare, travel, etc. ). 

While still completing the credit application, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the main cardholder on the account asked several questions. 

MA : Am I able to take out a cash advance on the card? 

AmEx employee : No, you can''t. 

MA : Ok, well can I make a payment to my own business? 

AmEx employee : No, that''s not permissible either. 

MA : What about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? 

AmEx employee ( excitedly ) : Yes! Yes you can! 

We went ahead and did that transaction, which we''ve since found out was not permissible after all. We were flagged for a financial review, and submitted all paperwork they asked for with the reassurance that it was simply a formality because of the error regarding the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] transaction. We even offered to return the money to the card. 

The culmination of the investigation was that our limit would be reduced to {$12000.00}, when we had already spent {$17000.00} on the card. We are in the middle of closing on a home. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has suffered, and he has suffered multiple [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as a result of the stress being caused. Where we were previously at less than 20 % usage on that card, we are now at 150 % usage, and it has artificially tanked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s previously pristine credit rating. 

We have dealt with AmEx loyally and in good faith over the past almost three years. We''ve had several different cards with the company. They have never been consistent. We have requested the recording of our conversation when the aforementioned employee incorrectly told us we were allowed to commit an act that we''ve since learned was not permissible. The company has responded that they will only release the recording with a subpoena. 

At this point, we are hesitant to pay AmEx anything, as we are concerned they will immediately terminate our account, or lower our credit limit to something worse. With the upcoming home purchase, we can not properly plan our available finances due to the instability with this company. Additionally, we have tried to reach out on multiple occasions and have been forwarded on to employees overseas ( who have lied and said they are based in Florida ; we have caught them mid-lie ). We have been a willing party in the resolution of this matter, in a way that is fair and respectful to all parties, particularly us, considering the amount of business we have done with the company. We are stunned and appalled, and are unsure of where to turn at this point.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a year ago, we had over $55000.00 worth of purchasing through our American Express gold card. the limit was lowered to $12000.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1481,'04/23/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Other service problem','OnXX/XX/2018 Our company received a email from Pay Pal stating they have limited our account Dear [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], We are hereby notifying you that, after a recent review of your account activity, it has been determined that you are in violation of PayPal ''s Acceptable Use Policy regarding your sales / offers of Unauthorized item ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

As a result, your account has been permanently limited. Please remove all references to PayPal from your website/s and/or auction/s. This includes not only removing PayPal as a payment option, but also the PayPal logo and PayPal shopping cart.

Per the User Agreement, when PayPal permanently limits an account due to an Acceptable Use Policy violation, any funds on your account are held for 180 days. In addition, you may be liable for any amount of damages PayPal incurs for each violation of the Acceptable Use Policy.

Note that should any chargebacks result in your account balance falling below zero, then you will also need to settle the amount owed to PayPal to avoid further action.

The PayPal User Agreement states that PayPal reserves the right to limit an account for any violation of the PayPal User Agreement, including the Acceptable Use Policy.

Under the PayPal Acceptable Use Policy, PayPal may not be used to send or receive payments for items that infringe or violate any copyright, trademark, right of publicity or privacy, or any other proprietary right under the laws of any jurisdiction. This includes transactions for counterfeit items or unauthorized replicas or copies of items.

You can find the complete PayPal Acceptable Use Policy by clicking Legal at the bottom of any PayPal page. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PayPal, Brand Risk Management PayPal Hello PayPal In regards to this email I am asking that our funds be accessible to transfer our funds to our bank account. 
Be advised we can legally sell a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] disc and hard drive, there is no law that says we can not do the following. 
Please be advised of the LAW. The first sale doctrine, codified at 17 U.S.C. 109, ALLOWS US TO DO SO We understand that you have the right to have or make up any rule in your policy, however you have no right to hold our funds as your institution isn''t a Federal Bank or Federal institution but merely a processor only. 
Please be advised in the case filed against your establishment for the same illegal act [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : C [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SBA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PayPal institution settled out of court to avoid heavy penalties. 

You may contact our Trademark and patent attorney for further question regarding your alleged claim ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Patent Attorney [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] We are asking that the funds be released ASAP If we do not receive action within 10 calender days we will have to process this with our attorney ( s ) Certified mail sent to address below ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] http : //www.paypal.com Paypal Executive Escalations dept : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Contact Information [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - Supervisor,  Exec Escalations [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Owner ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ceo ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Director ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Sole Proprietor )','PAYPAL HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,4.0,'PayPal has a right to limit an account for any violation of the Acceptable Use Policy. PayPal may not be used to send or receive payments for items that infringe or violate');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1482,'04/23/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Struggling to repay your loan','For the past ten years, I''ve made the biggest mistake of ever attending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   due to a suggestion of going there to finish my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and get an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] degree. I attended one semester, and realized that the school wasn''t true to it''s mission when I was forced to take out student loan after student loan, while taking classes that had nothing to do with what I wanted to major.

I left [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  one semester after, and transferred to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  college. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had other plans to damage me unfortunately. I couldn''t get any credits transferred to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] college I went to, so I started from the beginning. No sweat, only one semester of work but still was some good core classes. The loan providers of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] wanted to start taking money out of me, threatening me with all sorts of actions. This forced me to take a break from school to work and make some money to repay that.

The final coffin was transferring to a four year, because after I submit my application, I was left in limbo with no words or anything. Was told to re-apply a year later, a ton of fake excuses, and all this while still [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s many loans wanted to linger and damage me even more.

HESC ( where my loan currently is ) has tried plenty of times to garnish my wages, to have me pay MUCH more than what I can even currently budget for. Refuses to ever work with me, and pretty much has destroyed every aspect of my life credit/money wise.

All this while I just heard that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] closed it''s doors, yet I''m stuck paying so much money cause the school claims I was there for a full year which is a huge lie.

I really don''t know what to expect from this, I''ve pretty much given up. But it still leaves a huge bad taste in my mouth knowing I never had a traditionally college experience due to my mis-education while trying to receive an education.','NEW YORK STATE HIGHER EDUCATION SERVICES CORPORATION (HESC)—',4.0,4.0,'a student loan provider threatened to take money out of me, threatening me with all sorts of actions. the loan provider of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] wanted');
