On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] another payment was taken out by Mr.Cooper for {$600.00}. I then contacted Mr. Cooper again at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I spoke with a woman by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in there Georgia location. She was in the insurance division apparently. She stated to me that she could see in the system where [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent over insurance proof and that she would change the system to reflect this. She then went on to say that I need to call back in 5 business days, speak to someone in the escrow department to be sure that this is in fact fixed. I said, that does not make any sense, you told me you were fixing it right now. She stated, well I can only do some much just contact them in 5 days. Then I proceeded to ask, when will I receive my refund for the 2 over payments that total {$300.00}? She said, oh, well why would you think you would get this money back? I said, because I have my own insurance and you are charging me for your insurance. She said, oh you pay for your own insurance? I said, isn''t that the reason we are having this discussion. She then said, well if in fact they do owe you money you will need to wait to call them in 5 days, then they will process it from there and that will take another 5 days. This is just unacceptable ....','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] received a letter stating that our mortgage loan had been sold to a company by the name of');
