INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1516,'04/17/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','This is a continued ongoing complaint. Again [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has responded with allegations that they were in their right to pull my credit and perform a hard inquiry, but again and again have failed to provide documentation that supports their right under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). I never gave my consent for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to pull my credit history, I never submitted a loan application, I never showed or implied interest in any of their loan products and I never suggested that I was in the market for a loan of any sorts, yet TransUnion continues to side with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] without requesting that they produce material that would support their right under the FCRA claim.. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] just to talk to a loan " specialist '''' for information regarding how much time from the date of a foreclosure would it take before being once again eligible for a mortgage loan? I was told that they would need some basic information and after giving said info I was then told that I was not eligible for a loan mortgage at this time ... Huh ... I already knew that? Then was told it would take 5 to 7 years before being eligible for any of the loan products that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] offers, with that I said Okay thanks for your time and hung up. Many months later I came to find out that without my permission or knowledge my credit was pulled for asking a mortgage question only ... This is violation to my rights as a consumer and rights under the FCRA. Furthermore [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   response that I had interest in a loan product because I asked a question and therefore they were in their right to pull my credit is total [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and preys on unsuspecting consumers.. So I ask again for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to provide proof of my interest in being approved for one of their loan products other than a letter that states I called and had a conversation with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] rep and was denied a loan ... Please be advised that I will continue to use ant ans every platform available in resolving this matter ...','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a complaint has been filed against TransUnion. they have failed to provide documentation that supports their right under the Fair Credit Reporting Act. they have denied that they were in their right');
