INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1599,'04/02/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','National Business Factors through previous complaints with CFPB has agreed to delete this item from my credit file. This dispute has been going on since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and more recently through a letter sent to National Business Factors ( which have gone unanswered ) via certified mail received on or about XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as of late XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] state National Business Factors have verified the information is reporting correctly on my credit report instead of deleting the item as National Business Factors have promised.

I did receive notice from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  that the item was deleted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].

I am willing to try this one more time ( 30 more days ) to allow National Business Factors to DELETE this item from ALL my credit reports. However, at the end of the 30 days if the item remains on my credit reports I will be forced to file in Colorado Federal and civil court to enforce my rights under the FCRA and FDCPA. I was declined for a Mortgage partially due to this item on my credit report. I pay higher insurance premiums and have high interest rates on my credit cards because of this item. I have been financially harmed now in the hundreds of thousands of dollars and will seek damages in at least that amount as well as punitive damages.','National Business Factors',2.0,2.0,'dispute has been going on since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and more recently through a letter sent to National Business Factors via');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1600,'04/02/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I am the cosigner on a loan with Nelnet. On XX/XX/17 the primary borrower made a payment to the account for the amount of {$560.00} and received confirmation from Nelnet that the payment was processed. Approximately 3 days later Nelnet informed the borrower that the payment did not go through and that he would need to re-submit, which he did. He again received a confirmation that the payment went through ( and this time showed me the confirmation, which included a confirmation number ). At the time he received the confirmation ( with the confirmation number ), the payment was still within the 90 day window before they would report a delinquency to credit agencies. 

Nelnet replied back to the borrow approximately 4-5 business days after the borrower submitted the payment letting him know that the payment was unable to be processed and that he would need to resubmit payment. What they did not communicate is that they also reported the payment as delinquent to reporting agencies, causing my credit score to plummet. What I feel is wrong about this is that the borrower was actively working with Nelnet to make the payment and received a confirmation number twice indicating the payment went through and yet they have now permanently damaged my credit score as a result. The issue is that they gave us an incomplete picture of the state of the payment ( nowhere in the confirmation image does it mention the payment is still pending and in fact it contains a button that says " print for your records '''' which causes the user to think that the payment has completely gone through )','NELNET, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the primary borrower made a payment to the account for the amount of $560.00. he received confirmation from Nelnet that the payment was processed. ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1601,'04/02/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Ive noticed a few changes to my credit report where some inaccurate erroneous information was removed and I totally appreciate it but I listed these accounts along with the last dispute and I dont know why they werent removed. The information that I am providing to use is factual information and it isnt an account Ive ever opened or had to my knowledge. This is an internal dispute and I have record on the dispute, phone calls, certified letters and more for court when the time arrives. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I have to continue going through a dispute process because your company is placing errors and inaccurate information on my credit for no apparent reasons and it isnt fair to me at all. Please look in the attachment area to see the letter I attached. Please read carefully and this is my final warning letter to remove the erroneous information off my credit report within 48 hours and no longer.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'I have listed accounts along with the last dispute. the information that I am providing to use is factual information. this is an internal dispute and I have record on the dispute, phone');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1602,'04/02/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Problem caused by your funds being low','When I had my checkbook stolen in 2016, I opened a new account with Bank of America and was pushed into opening a Business Checking Account that was inappropriate for my needs. I informed the representative who opened that account that I would be transitioning back into " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-status '''' and still the representative advised that I open a Business Checking Account with the bank. I had the account for approximately two years, and late fees began to accumulate on the account. When student loans were deposited in my Savings account, BofA transferred at least {$1200.00} from my Savings to cover the ridiculous late fees. The bank literally stole money without my permission from my Savings to cover {$1200.00} in late fees. They also refused to refund any of the fees when I complained to a branch representative about the issue. I would like help in addressing this and receiving a refund.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'a bank representative had my checkbook stolen in 2016. he told me that he would be transitioning back into a Business Checking Account. the bank literally stole money');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1603,'04/01/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','AARGON AGENCY INC [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NV [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Dear Sir or Madam, This letter is in reference to SOME BILL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NO ACOUNT NUMBER NO INFO JUST A COLLECTION AGENCY for services provided to NO NAMED PERSON on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] In regard to the bill on this account in the amount of ( {$760.00} ) Please be advised this is not a refusal to pay, but a notice your claims are being disputed. 

Under the Fair Debt Collections Act ( FDCPA ), I have the right to request validation of the debt you say I owe you. I am requesting proof that I am indeed the party you are asking to pay this debt, the date of the alleged medical service, the name of the patient and proof that there is some contractual obligation which is binding on me to pay this debt. 

Please attach copies of : Any agreement with your client that grants you the authority to collect on this alleged debt, or proof of acquisition by purchase or assignment, and or authorization under subtitle D of the ARRA, SEC 13401. APPLICATION OF SECURITY PROVISIONS AND PENALITIES TO BUSINESS ASSOCIATES OF COVERED ENTITIES ; and SEC. 13407 ( 1 ) BREACH OF SECURITY. 

The term " breach of security means, with respect to unsecured PHR identifiable health information without the authorization of the individual. 

Please note that enforcement of penalties against you is covered under the penalty rules of the omnibus final rule effective XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] interpreting and implementing various provisions of the Health Information. Technology for Economic and Clinical Health Act of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( HITECH ACT ) as issued XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the penalty rules of the FCRA and FACTA including FACT Act changes final rules effective XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Please also attach copies of any agreement that bears the signature of the alleged debtor wherein he or she agreed to pay the creditor and as this is a medical account and a copy of any HIPPA authorization. 

Please also be advised that this letter is not only a formal dispute, but a request that you cease and desist any and all collections activities, including reporting of or verifying of this account on my credit reports. 

In the event of non -compliance, I reserve the right to file charges with the OCR on your HIPPA violations and appropriate County, State and Federal Authorities. I require compliance, I reserve the right to file charges and/or complaints with the OCR on your HIPPA violations and appropriate associations for violations and appropriate County, State & Federal authorities for violations of the FDCPA, FCRA and Federal and State statutes on illegal collection activities on any account that may be time-barred as well as in violation of California medical privacy rules. 

I also hereby reserve my right to take private civil action against you to recover damages. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Aargon Agency, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'AARGON AGENCY INC. is a 501(c)(3) organization that provides health information to a person. a 501(c)(3) organization that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1604,'04/01/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','This company placed a fraudulent inquiry on my credit report I have not authorized and have failed to respond to my numerous calls and I think they hire these foreign employees to purposely ask you the same question multiple times and place me on hold only to hang up on me and I have to repeat the same process and I am sick of it its not right and its not fair when Im following the procedures as described in the Federal Fair Credit Reporting Act. I deserve an investigation immediately without having to argue or be put off only because they dont care because it aint happening to them. As described in 623 ( a ) ( E ) of the Fair Credit Reporting Act I want the office listed to place this fraudulent inquiry under investigation  and remove it off my credit report now because it wasnt me and I have no knowledge of applying for this mess.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a fraudulent inquiry was placed on my credit report. the company has not authorized the inquiry. it has failed to respond to my numerous calls.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1605,'04/01/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Unable to get your credit report or credit score','I have been trying for more than 6 month that my mortgage company which is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] report my payments to the 3 agency credit bureau but they have been refusing to do it. I file for bankruptcy over 7 years ago and I have sent them a confirmation letter written for me and talked to my attorney and he said the confirmation was include when I filed. so in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they asked me for a bankruptcy discharge, I sent it to them, then a confirmation letter in XX/XX/XXXXand another documents and calling and ask them many times to report my payments so I can improve my credit score and get better interest when I apply for any kind of loan ... I don''t know what else to do ... please help with this Thank you','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'mortgage company is ''COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ'' and ''COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ''. they have been refusing to report my payments');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1606,'03/31/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Problems at the end of the loan or lease','My initial complaint through CFPB about Credit Acceptance was submitted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). My complaint is related to Credit Acceptance failure to notify the co-signer as well as myself of intent to sell a repossessed vehicle. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a phone call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  was unprofessional during the phone call, as it seemed as if he was trying to coerce me into saying that I received notification of intent to sell. Credit Acceptance responded to my initial complaint by providing documents that were supposedly sent to the co-signer as well as myself. The problem that I have with the alleged proof a notification sent before selling the vehicle is that the co-signer denies receiving notification as implied in the response by Credit Acceptance. The co-signer has resided at her residence for over 10 years. Therefore, its not possible that she didnt receive notification due to relocation. Hypothetically speaking, if its a possibility that I didnt receive my notification because of an issue related to the postal service, how can it be possible that two individuals with separate addresses not receive mail coming from the same company. I strongly feel that the documents provided by Credit Acceptance are falsified.','CREDIT ACCEPTANCE CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a complaint was submitted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the co-signer denies receiving notification as implied in the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1607,'03/31/2018','Checking or savings account','Other banking product or service','Managing an account','OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I logged into my WELLS FARGO Online portal to utalize the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] money transfer feature. I was trying to send {$580.00} from my WF savings account to myself via my telephone number as the recipient. This was the first time I had tried using this option to send money to myself. After completing the transfer I realized there was an issue because I did not receipt an alert on my phone number indicating that I have money received. I called WF immedietly to figure out what was going on. The money had left my instantly yet it had not come to my phone as an alert. I panicked as WF told me theyd have to open a case claim that could take 10 days. I kept calling them every few days and I was concerned and unsatidfied by their response. They claimed that the funds went to someone that had my phone number formerly registered to them yet the name on the transfer did not match. Then WF told me that Im basically [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and that theres no way to retract the funds back and that Im left without any resolution of getting my money back. Im very irate at Wells Fargo and at their lack of due dilligence in trying to protect their customers funds. There should have been a third step in verifying the transfer. The manager whom I spoke to told me that this happens all the time with customers. That is extremely alarming and concerning given that telephone numbers are recycled all the time. I have had my number for approx. 5 years so I am completely still confused as to how this happened and the fact that I have been without this money for over a month now.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a customer was able to send $580.00 from my savings account. the money had left my instantly but it had not come to my phone. the money was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1608,'03/31/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','I signed up for Experian credit monitoring in XX/XX/2015 I have no complaints over the information I have received. However, I now want to cancel my credit monitoring subscription which costs {$25.00} a month. 

There is no way to cancel a subscription online, and when I have called the phone number they give to cancel ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) the wait times are extremely long. I have called 5 times now in the past month. The first time I was told the wait time was 45 mins. The next 4 times I called, I was told the wait time was more than 2 hours!! I have called at several different times throughout the day to try to find a shorter wait time, but with no success. 

It seems very clear to me that Experian are intentionally understaffing their cancelation call center to reduce the number of people that are able to cancel membership.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'credit monitoring subscription costs $25.00 a month. there is no way to cancel a subscription online.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1609,'03/30/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I am writing you because I have attempted to contact Customer Service and they are unwilling to address this issue. 

In reviewing my student loan account I can see from Navient ''s records that including payment to the school and interest I borrowed a total of {$29000.00} Since paying on my loan I have paid a total of ( {$18000.00} ) Meaning I should only owe the remaining balance of {$11000.00} However Navient is reporting in my account and to credit bureaus that I owe {$26000.00}','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'I have paid a total of ( $18000.00) since paying on my student loan. I have paid a total of ( $18000.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1610,'03/30/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','We purchased the timeshare in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Our children were young, and we used the exchange to  vacation with them. After the children grew up, my husband and I continued to use the timeshare. When the maintenance fees began, we paid as expected. We are seniors now ; both of us were laid off and we have only Social Security as income. The invoice for maintenance fees was sent in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and, in good faith, we paid them because we could. However, we noted that we could not continue to pay them because our income was insufficient. We had met with a bankruptcy attorney, and decided that it was our only relief. Our bankruptcy was filed, and all creditors, including our timeshare, were notified and given the hearing date for creditors. The timeshare creditors did not respond. All debts were [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Later that year, we received the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] invoice from the timeshare. I sent a letter explaining that we had to file bankruptcy, and were no longer owners. They did not respond. When it was clear that we were not going to pay any more, we began receiving threatening letters even though we no longer held any claim to the unit. The timeshare inventory agent told me that they had been made exempt in the bankruptcy law. I reviewed that law, and found that it spoke of " ... intentional wrongdoing '''' by consumers, and " ... society ''s interest in excepting those debts from discharge outweighs the debtor ''s need for a fresh economic start. '''' We take exception to that because we knew nothing of the law, and the timeshare did not respond when notified by the bankruptcy attorney. The fact that we surrendered the timeshare unit, and had it included in the bankruptcy, without dispute from the timeshare agents, should relieve us of any further attempts from them to collect from us. This is not a " postpetition assessment '''' issue. If we had been advised that by paying the XX/XX/XXXXmaintenance fee it would exempt the timeshare from bankruptcy, we would not have paid it - again, we were acting in good faith. In turn, they have not.','STEWART INFORMATION SERVICES',4.0,4.0,'timeshare was sold in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and paid as expected. the timeshare was sold in XX/');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1611,'03/30/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my husband and I filed for Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bankruptcy. In regards to this particular account, Wells Fargo Home Mortgage, we filed a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Individual Debtor ''s Statement of Intention onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We stated that the property would be retained in the bankruptcy and the debt was to be reaffirmed. We claimed the property as exempt. We had never been late or delinquent on this account. Neither us nor our lawyer received any documents from Wells Fargo after this submission. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we visited out mortgage broker to start the process of qualifying for another home loan, as we are ready to purchase another home and sell this current home we are in. It was discovered on our credit reports that Wells Fargo reported to the major credit bureaus that our mortgage account had been " Included in or Discharged through bankruptcy ''''. Wells Fargo quit reporting on this account inXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In each phone call to Wells Fargo we have been told different information. In one call the customer service representative told us that they do not send out reaffirmation letters. In another one told us they sent us one, that the letter would have gone to our attorney ''s office. When I asked for proof that this had been sent they told me they only send them regular mail via the US Post Office and could not provide that information. Which I found odd since any letter that they ever sent us was also available online to view. I then contacted my attorney ''s office who filed bankruptcy for us. Their office told me that EVERY reaffirmation letter they receive from ANY creditor is sent either [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or USPS with delivery confirmation/signature required so proof of delivery is available. I have filed multiple disputes with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no changes made. I have sent them all the supporting documents including proof of all payments made, Statement of Intent, a letter from our attorney ''s office, and proof that we are current on our payment to Wells Fargo. How can this account be being reported as closed when we are clearly making payments to them? Today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   that the documentation I provided was not enough for them to make any changes. When I asked what was needed the agent told me they don''t have a specific list of what documentation would change the status because Wells Fargo is their client and they have to go off of what they are reporting. I feel the last 2 months of trying to dispute this have been a waste. What good are these credit reporting bureaus if they work for the companies that are reporting to them? Where is the consumer protection in this when there are disputes. This error on Wells Fargo part is severely impacting our ability to get another mortgage. OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I submitted all the same documentation to Wells Fargo and was suppose to have an answer from them by now about how to resolve this incorrect reporting/not reporting to the credit bureaus. I am including all documentation sent to Wells Fargo and the credit bureaus as well as documentation of all payments made to Wells Fargo.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my husband and I filed for Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bankrupt');
