INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1614,'03/29/2018','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Payday loan','Charged fees or interest you didn''t expect','i took out a {$400.00} loan in XX/XX/2017 and have made {$120.00} payments on time biweekly since that time. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] weeks ago I contacted the company inquiring how to pay down the loan and was informed that any additional payments made at the same time as the original payment would be applied to the principal. I have been paying {$120.00} plus an additional {$200.00} for the last to payments and to date only {$37.00} has been applied to the principal. The company states that they have no way to apply the additional payments to the principal therefore they apply the entire payment of {$120.00} to interest and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to principal from the additional {$200.00}. To date I still owe {$810.00} from a {$400.00} loan the principal has been reduced less than {$40.00}. The interest is 699 %. It would seem that if the entire original payment is applied to interest then there is nothing but principal remaining for the additional payment to be applied to. It is also contrary to what I was informed the process would be. I would not voluntarily pay additional money for additional interest payments. As of now I am paying {$120.00} plus an additional {$200.00} per payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in total to be applied to the original loan amount of {$400.00}. I have been informed that I will pay the loan off earlier than anticipated in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if I keep this rate up. Wow!','GVA Holdings, LLC',2.0,4.0,'i took out a $400.00 loan in XX/XX/2017 and have made $120.00 payments on time biweekly since that time');
