Please see attached dispute and supporting docs. My dispute requested that Chase Bank provide the substantive information used to verify and authenticate the purported account. The failure to report the items " disputed '''' with in 30 days constitutes an immediate removal of this item from my credit report ( time stamped credit reports 31 days after Chase Bank signed for the certified letters ). Per federal regulation these items must be immediately and permanently removed from my credit reports for Violation of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( including but not limited to Section 807-8 ) and Violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( including but not limited to Section 623-b ).','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a dispute of 2 questionable reportings from Chase Bank was signed. the account is being reported as charged off for $5400.00 and $3700.00 ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1623,'03/28/2018','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I fell behind on my mortgage for two months and attempted to make up a payment arrangements with the company ; however was unsuccessful. When I made a payment, it was returned to me. I received a letter from their lawyer stating that I was in default and property will go into foreclosure if full arrears wasn''t paid. I did not have the monies to pay the amount in full. When I called the lawyer office, they did not have a resolution for me other than pay the amount. I called the mortgage company and they suggested that I attempt to apply for a loan modification. I completed the application with the help of Neighborhood Housing Services of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I received a court date. Filed my answer and appeared in court. Court appointments lasted from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I completed the full application about five times and additionally, continued to send them additional pay stubs, bank statements, hardship letter repeatedly every month. I kept in constant communication with the lawyer who all documents were sent directly to ; however, every month I would receive a letter stating that my modification package was incomplete. Every court appearance was dealing with documents that they did not receive hat I had fax confirmation to sending to the lawyer office. The judge lost his patience and dismissed it for myself and the bank to complete. I felt that filing Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was best to save my home but I would like for a fair chance at modifying the loan and dismissing the bankruptcy. I feel that I was not treated fairly. The communication between the mortgage company and myself was very poor and I feel as if I was given the run around from the beginning. My plan is to remain in my home. I now have sufficient income to sustain ; however, I can not afford to pay the bankruptcy and mortgage and maintain my home. I do not want to lose my home.','loanDepot.com, LLC',2.0,2.0,'mortgage company suggested that I attempt to apply for a loan modification. a letter from the lawyer said that I was in default and property will go into foreclosure if full arrear');
