INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1629,'03/27/2018','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] deposited around {$400.00} into my account as a payday loan. They took out 2 payments or so from my bank which exceeded the amount that was borrowed. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] continued to try and take money from my bank account even after the loan was paid off because they were trying to charge extreme interest fees. I informed them that it was illegal in California and that I paid the loan in full. Now over 5 years later, I checked my credit report and see a collection account from Midwest Recovery Systems for {$780.00}. I called them to ask what is was regarding and they informed me that it was for a payday loan and they reminded me that I made 2 payments. I informed them what [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was trying to do is illegal in California and by their own admission I had made 2 payments on a {$400.00} loan and that is was paid off. They are still dinging my credit report over and over.','Midwest Recovery Systems',2.0,2.0,'COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ deposited around $400.00 into my account as a payday loan. they took out 2 payments or so from my bank');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1630,'03/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I pulled my credit report, and discovered that late payments were reported for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for my account. 

During that time, I was on an around the worldwide [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I wouldnt dare purposely be irresponsible with this account. For some reason, I setup automatic payments, but did not have sufficient funds in the account when it processed. 

The men and women in the armed forces deserve the absolute best financial products on the market. These products should be simple, transparent and offer excellent customer service and an understanding about our difficulties that ensue during [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I sent Chase a goodwill letter explaining my situational and they responded in a very unreasonable manner. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] members face unforeseen circumstances daily. We can not plan for everything that happens. 

I believe Chase failed to research my situation and complaint. Everything is not black and white. Although they have a program that allows reduced interest rates during [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], they fail to advertise that to servicemembers. When they found out I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], they could have made consideration for the late payments retroactively. 

My circumstances should be considered and their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] policy and advertisement needs to be revamped. They should be here to support not hurt the military.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a credit report found late payments were reported for my account. a spokesman for the armed forces said the account was not a "black and white" he said');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1631,'03/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','Over a year ago I disputed a fraudulent Wells Fargo Credit Card on my credit profile a long with sending in police report. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claimed after investigating that the account was mine. I sent the same police report and filed a CFPB complaint against Well Fargo ( CFPB # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Wells Fargo sent me a letter dated XX/XX/2017 stating the account was fraudulent and they will stop reporting to credit bureaus. I again disputed the account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They have not deleted that account from my credit profile.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a year ago I disputed a fraudulent Wells Fargo Credit Card. they have not deleted the account from my credit profile.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1632,'03/27/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I suffered some financial, personal and physical hardships due to Hurricane Irma in Florida. 
As a result of my circumstances, I contacted my creditors of which one was BMW financial services. I had heard that they had a disaster relief program that afforded their customers the opportunity to enroll in their loan deferment based on such disaster circumstances and needs. 
The terms that were discussed and extended to me was that I would be able to receive up to 3 months skip payments without any penalties. The reason being was that these payments would be placed at the end of the loan and in addition they will not be reported as delinquent to any of the credit Bureaus. 
Needless to say, the exact thing they told me would not happened, actually did. From [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/XXXXmy credit score was between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no skipped, late or missed payments. I have had a vehicle financed with BMW Financial Services from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], up to present and have never been 30 days late or missed a payment throughout the entire period. 
At the end of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my score went from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where it is currently based on the report that was sent to the credit bureau by BMW. In essence, the three months they agreed to not report any late payments, it is now showing 30, 60 and 90 days delinquency on my report via BMW Financial Services. 
I have spoken to BMW and they have disregarded everything that was agreed with me and instead seemed more concerned with placing blame and stating what their police is. The fact is that I had other options and would have taken those one of those option rather than have my credit score drop to the such drastic level based on untruths and lies. 
In closing, let me say that this situation has already affected my ability to do financial stuff in my life. I have turned [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old recently and had been making plans to buy a small cheaper condo. However, the sudden reality for me now is that my current Credit status has already began to affect my ability to buy something reasonable in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Florida even though opportunities exist.','BMW Financial Services NA, LLC',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/XXXXmy credit score was between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1633,'03/27/2018','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Managing the loan or lease','I purchased a car from a dealership and financed it through Capital One Auto Finance Account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The Dealership never sent the title to Capital One and then the Dealer Ship went out of business. I continued to make payments to Capital one ( ON TIME ) for 6 months. I finally discussed turning the car back to capital one since I was unable to get plates or a title on it with the dealership being gone. 

Capital One is showing this as a repossession on my credit file with a balance owing that is just less than the original amount of the loan. 

1 ) I can not be held liable for a vehicle that I was unable to drive from day one until 6 months later when I turned it in. If anything, Capital One owes me just over {$3000.00} for a vehicle that I paid for and ONCE AGAIN ... could never drive for even one day. 

2 ) I certainly should not have a repossession and owe a balance of {$23000.00} for NO VALUE RECEIVED.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a car from a dealership went out of business and the Dealer Ship went out of business. I continued to make payments to Capital one for 6 months. the dealership is showing this');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1634,'03/26/2018','Checking or savings account','Savings account','Closing an account','Last week, I received a message when I tried to login to my Chase account online that told me my checking and savings accounts were being closed. I immediately called them and they confirmed they were closing my accounts, but they couldn''t provide a reason why. I then went into the closest Chase branch ( where I had opened my accounts ), and tried to get my money out. The banker there told me she could not give me money. I had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in my accounts, so this is not a small amount of money. She gave me the same number I had called before and told me to call them. They told me they are holding my funds while they investigate my accounts. I''m not sure why they even closed my accounts in the first place, but it is ridiculous that they can hold my money after they close them. I want a check mailed ASAP for the balance of my accounts so I can pay my bills. Thank you.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a message from a banker who opened my accounts told me my accounts were being closed. she told me she could not give me money, but she gave me the same number ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1635,'03/26/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','I was proactive about my credit card debt and proactviely working to come up with a solution prior to my debtors reaching out to me or becoming concerned. 

I had two American Express cards, a gold card and a plum card. The total balances are {$8600.00} I called and spoke to a representative who explained that they have a " Hardship Program '''' and I can setup a 36 month payment plan. I was told that you must pay the initial 3 months up front, and the monthly payment amount will be drafted automatically every month thereafter for 33 months. I accepted and signed up for this program and paid the initial 3 month payment ( over {$900.00} ). I was given a confirmation number and read all disclosures and was told everything was successfully setup. I explained that I was thankful that they had a program like this and that I had 100 % intention on getting the debt paid off in full within the 33 months and that I accept 100 % responsibility for the debt. 

Roughly a month later I receive a letter in the mail from AMEX regarding my accounts and that they are suspended and past due. I called to figure out why I was receiving letters about delinquency when I had already made a payment agreement? they told me they would have to research the account and call me back. 

I never received a call back, so I contacted them the following week. I was told by a " customer care representative '''' that something went wrong, and the account was mistakenly not setup in to the program. I explained that I was given confirmation and a confirmation number and they explained it did not matter, and that my accounts were not enrolled into the hardship program. I was told the only way to fix it was to re-apply for the program and to pay the first 3 months payment again. They waived all late fees and interest as the account should have been enrolled in the program. 

I explained it would be extremely difficult for me to afford and how would I know that this would not happen again. They told me that under no circumstances would it happen again and the rep I was speaking to said that they would personally monitor the account to ensure the program is setup correctly. I was extremely nervous, but went ahead and setup the account into the hardship program for the second time, against my nerves. Again I paid the initial 3 months payments ( over {$900.00} ) and have now paid 6 months of agreed upon payments in less than 45 days, and was in a financial crisis. Again, they promised that it would not happen again, I was given confirmation that my account was signed up into the program, and given confirmation numbers for both accounts. 

after another 10-15 days, I noticed the accounts were still open and late fees were accruing, as well as receiving a debt collection phone call from AMEX. I explained the account was setup into a hardship program, gave them the confirmation numbers, and the representative told me that the account was no enrolled, and that they are preparing to report the delinquencies to my personal credit. I explained the overall situation and the multiple issues I faced, he said there is nothing they can do and re-iterated the amount I owed and that my credit would be effected. He then tried to send me to the " Hardship program '''' to sign up again. I explained for a third time I am already signed up, was given confirmation numbers, and do not want to sign up again. He said he could not help, but would research the account and call me back in one hour on my cell phone with a supervisor on the line ( Friday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 

I never received a call back. 

At this point I realized that AMEX had no intention of assisting me as a customer, and that the " Hardship Program '''' was simply a scam to get debtors/clients to make a " 3 month '''' payment. They claim the account will be enrolled and automatically drafted each month and that all debt collection attempts will cease. In reality they simply are misrepresenting their debt relief program/products and forcing client who are in a tough financial situation to make payments without actually putting them into a program. 

I decided at this to find a balance transfer credit card to transfer the debt to. I was approved by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and told the AMEX accounts would be paid in 14-21 days from Friday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I contacted AMEX to let them know that the accounts were going to be paid in full within 14 days. 

Monday morning XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the AMEX debt collection rep called again to explain my accounts are past due and now delinquent and that they are reporting to my personal credit. 

They are taking advantage of people on a massive scale, and misrepresenting their debt relief products while taking advantage of people who are clearly in a financial hardship. 

*Can send confirmation numbers upon request *Can send proof of waived fees/interest after rep said the account should have been signed up','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a rep told me that the account was mistakenly not setup in to the program. he said that the account was not enrolled in the program. he said that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1636,'03/26/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a hard inquiry showed up on my Experian and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  credit reports for a line of credit I did not open at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I then ran my credit reports for all three agencies, only to discover 2 of the 3 showed what looked like someone''s profile on my report. I discovered incorrect variations of my name, incorrect home addresses and places of employment, and about 16 accounts that did not belong to me. Naturally I freaked out. The odd thing was a lot of the incorrect accounts were from 2-8 years ago and these had never ever shown up on my credit reports before XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I check my reports often so I would have seen these. 

So the first thing I addresses was the recent inquiry. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PST I called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that made the hard inquiry on my credit report and they were unable to pull up an account with my name and social security number. None of the info I gave them pulled up an account ... which further made me believe there was a problem with the credit bureaus and not a case of identity thief. 

So, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PST, I called Experian and they looked into my credit report and the customer service rep noticed that my profile was actually merged with another person with a very similar spelled name ( mine is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the incorrect one was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and social security as mine. They started the process of un-merging my account with this other person. Somehow bc another person has a similar spelled name and social, our records were being merged in their system. Thankfully the customer service rep took the time to go line item by line item to separate the records. Sadly I now have to do this same thing with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because these same errors were on that credit report too. I didn''t see anything incorrect on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  yet but I''ll keep monitoring it.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a hard inquiry showed up on my credit report for a line of credit. a lot of the incorrect accounts were from 2-8 years ago. the inquiry was made on ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1637,'03/26/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have disputed an account reporting on my credit report with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit Bureau as well as the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] this has been ongoing for months. 
I havent received any results.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'i have disputed an account reporting on my credit report with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit bureau. I havent received any results.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1638,'03/26/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','NOTATION : This is a CHALLENGE and NOT A DISPUTE I am always CHECKING for TOTAL COMPLIANT & CERTIFIED COMPLIANT REPORTING that gives testimonial and irrefutable PROOF of the undeniable TRUTH, correctness, completion, timeliness, ownership of, responsibility of, and compliance and or else wise for any and all items accused, even any and all aspects of allegations. 
Per Federal reporting regulations and the MANDATED COMPLIANT [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] format reporting standards of practice any and all items of adversary or derogatory nature must be certified as entirely true, accurate, complete, timely, of documented ownership, of undoubted responsibility, and documented testimonial certificate of compliance marking undeniable lawful standing of claim ( s ). Per law, any deficient of substantial and evident matters of fact ( s ) would be unethically reported and even illegally reported. My state and the federal laws alike agree that neither willful nor ignorant disregard is acceptable, so I demand here today, even RIGHT NOW, that the allegation in challenge be eradicated in full or else wise demonstrated in it''s entirety to be compliant in every aspect of it''s reporting. To retain much less report otherwise would be a vile misrepresentation and done so in unlawful and injurious infraction of mandated compliance laws. The currently unfounded and even not certified true or correct misinformation of hich is misreporting is as follows and must be deleted immediately, so please do so without delay : Alleged Reporting Data Provider -- > [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Not Proven Compliant Account -- > [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Alleged Reporting Data Provider -- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Not Proven Compliant Account -- > [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',10.0,10.0,'a DISPUTE is a CHALLENGE and NOT a DISPUTE. a testimonial is a testimony of the undeniable TRUTH');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1639,'03/25/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Closing on a mortgage','Guaranteed Rate has made fraudulent, reckless, and negligent misrepresentations during an application for a mortgage, and its unfair methods and deceptive practices in handling the application for a mortgage has caused financial damages and inability to secure a mortgage on a property. 

On XX/XX/2018, we reached out to Guaranteed Rate regarding obtaining a mortgage for the transfer of title on the Property. The next day, we texted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate inquiring about obtaining a mortgage and the process by which we apply for a mortgage. We informed Guaranteed Rate that we wanted to do a cash-out refinance and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] texted Back that we should do this form of refinance. 

On XX/XX/2018, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate again us informing us that the best way to proceed with the transaction would be " as a second home cash-out refinance '''' and that it would be " [ v ]  ery uncomplicated that way. '''' After we asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to include another person on the texts, he stated he will and to text the person " you want to apply as a second home refinance ; cash-out. '''' On XX/XX/2018, we texted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate inquiring about the " options for locking in a rate '''' and where he " can see [ the ] current rates. '''' [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not respond. He delayed for several days and did not provide any rates or information. He eventually responded, in an indirect manner, texting to us that " we can price [ out ] all of the loan options... and go over credits from me against costs. '''' [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], however, never once did this, after we continually asked him for rates. 

Guaranteed Rate by this point had laid its bait for the its bait and switch tactic. 

On XX/XX/2018, we submitted the necessary loan application materials per Guaranteed Rate ''s instruction for " non-binding and no cost. '''' [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] received an email notification of the completion of the submission on this day. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate copied the other person to the texts on XX/XX/2018. 

On the following day, XX/XX/2018, we informed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate via text that the necessary application was completed online per your instruction. We texted Guaranteed Rate for rates to lock in and asked Guaranteed Rate to send the Good Faith Estimate, as required by CFPB regulations, namely 12 CFR 1024.7. Guaranteed Rate refused to provide rates or any information. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated in response " [ w ] e will be checking over the on-line applications and financial back-up documents tomorrow! '''' Guaranteed Rate never responded regarding the application, rates, or with the loan options or the credits. 

We then texted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate three days later, XX/XX/2018, inquiring " do you have everything you need '''' and what are the next steps. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate then said she was working on the file that day and would let the us know if Guaranteed Rate needs anything. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent a confusing email that day asking about documents from a completely different party, and then apologized due to working on multiple At this time, on XX/XX/2018, it was many days past the three days after we submitted the application on XX/XX/2018, and Guaranteed Rate had provided no information on its rates, credits, closing costs, or " Guaranteed '''' and " locked '''' rates, let alone a Good Faith Estimate, in violation of at least CFPB regulations. This is true despite us expressly requesting Guaranteed Rate to provide a rates and information including a Good Faith Estimate. Guaranteed Rate did not price out the loan options or go over credits, as it expressly represented. 

On XX/XX/2018, after not hearing anything for several days, we again followed up with Guaranteed Rate. We inquired whether [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate needed anything else, as it had been nearly two weeks and no information on the application had been provided. Guaranteed Rate again delayed and responded that it was working on the file today and that it had everything. 

We then again inquired about how we see and lock-in rates and the process for locking in rates, costs, etc. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed rate refused to respond and did not provide rates or costs. Guaranteed Rate didn''t answer the question, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate responded on XX/XX/2018 that " [ w ] e are working on putting your file together and working  out the debt to income rations for adding [ the wrong party ] to the property and both of you  signing for the new cash-out mortgage loan. '''' We then informed Guaranteed Rate that it was working on the wrong file for the wrong person. 

We followed up asking, again " at what point are [ you ] able to lock in rates if we wish. '''' Guaranteed Rate and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not respond. 

We then followed up stating we " need to see a GFE per CFPB regs '''' and need to have idea of rates and everything before signing or moving forward. 

After several misrepresentations and deceptive acts and failures to respond, Guaranteed Rate then provided, for the first time, a rate and estimate of costs. The rate and estimate of costs do not comply with Consumer Financial Protection Bureau regulations. The delayed rates Guaranteed quoted were " 30 year fixed rate 4.375 % - 0 points ; {$840.00} ; monthly for principal and interest. No credit from me against costs '''' or 4.500 % - 0 points ; $ XXXXmonthly for principal and interest. {$960.00} credit from me to you against the refinance costs. '''' Guaranteed Rate stated that the offer for the 4.500 % " is subject to market volatility until your lock in your new mortgage loan interest rate. '''' Guaranteed rate did not place any contingencies on the 4.375 % rate offer. We immediately accepted the 4.375 % offer and lock in rate with the costs Guaranteed Rate quoted, providing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate with credit card for the application based on this locked in rate. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Guaranteed Rate confirmed she received, and was only authorized to charge for a 4.375 % rate loan. We then signed documents, including the Uniform Residential Loan Application signed and prepared by Guaranteed Rate, showing a 4.375 % rate for refinance. 

After [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate laid the bait, stalled, delayed, dodged questions, and worked on the wrong file, the market unsurprisingly dropped 35 basis  points. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate had perfected its fraudulent switch in its bait and switch tactic. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate then attempted to renege on the 4.375 % rate offer. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate offer a new higher 4.500 % rate and ambiguously stated he and Guaranteed Rate would " reduce the credit accordingly. '''' We then inquired what [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] meant by " reduce the credit accordingly '''' and inquired about how Guaranteed Rate would compensate us for its conduct. We also informed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate of its violations in not providing a good faith estimate, costs, rates, or anything. 

Being caught, Guaranteed Rate and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then attempted another fraudulent and deceptive tactic to renege and tried to place blame on us. Guaranteed Rate first stated that the loan application that we submitted back on XX/XX/2018 was  marked as a no cash-out. This was a false and fraudulent statement in an attempt to get us to move forward with the 4.5 % offer. Guaranteed Rate made this fraudulent and deceptive accusation after it and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had discussed at length via text and phone the nature of the transaction as a cash-out refinance. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate made this accusation after they stated they had received and reviewed the application several times over the course of weeks. Moreover, Guaranteed Rate ''s application process does not have any questions on whether the mortgage is cash-out versus no-cash out, and the Residential Loan Application signed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and us likewise does not distinguish between a cash-out and no-cash out. 

To add insult to injury, after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate represented that they would provide the loan application submitted online by us, and we requested it, they made the remark that " I would think that the client would have printed out a copy of what they completed themselves, online. '''' Again, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Guaranteed Rate misrepresented information to us in an attempt to place blame on us. My credit card was then charged {$550.00} for the application process and have not received a mortgage from another lender. 

We then requested to speak with someone in the legal department. When having discussions with the Guaranteed Rate ''s legal department and compliance officers, they informed us that no one follow the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ''s regulations and that the regulations and agency have absolutely no teeth. They tried to place blame on us, stating they had no duty to provide rates or disclose information to us during the loan application. We told them we would investigate taking legal action and file a complaint with the CFPB.','GUARANTEED RATE INC.',2.0,4.0,'Guaranteed Rate has made fraudulent, reckless, and negligent misrepresentations during an application for a mortgage. the next day, we texted Guaranteed Rate about obtaining a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1640,'03/25/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I discovered a fraudulent account had been opened in my name which resulted in a collection account being posted on my credit report by a company name [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the outrageous amount of {$450000.00} dollars. Just recently the balance skyrocketed from {$450000.00} to {>= $1,000,000}. I contacted several contacts within the collection agency, the original creditor posted on the account as well as the three major credit reporting agencies. I followed the steps laid out by the fax, sent debt validation letters certified mail, sent in the police report showing the identity theft etc. Long story short [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  deleted the item, Equifax and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   have not, as well as they won''t send me any documentation showing me how they linked this account to my report. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Equifax deleted the account, but re-inserted it on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no documentation showcasing the reason for reinsertion.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a collection account was posted on my credit report by a company name. the balance skyrocketed from $450000.00 to >= $1,000,000');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1641,'03/25/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','Card opened without my permission or knowledge in my name. Thousands charged on card and even fraudulently paid by my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] business account.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'Thousands charged on card and even fraudulently paid by my account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1642,'03/24/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Several attempts have been made since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] by contacting Navient by phone and in writing to resolve the inaccuracies with the payment history of my credit reports. I have followed up with them every 90 days and have found no resolution to this issue. Navient has made several 30/60/90/120 late payments reflecting that my payment has been late but I had my account continuously in forbearance due to financial hardship since they had ownership of my account. For the period of time they have me reported as late, my student loans was still with Dept of Education/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. For some reason, when they merged accounts, it caused my accounts to be duplicated and incorrect. It seems as though the customer service representatives have no way of correcting this issue with finding pertinent information concerning the financial hardship request in there system. The inaccuracies starts as early as XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but my account did not transfer to Navient until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and at that time I contacted them directly to notify them that I was not in position to pay my student loan debt because I was contemplating on filing for bankruptcy and I suffered with financial hardship dealing with medical problems, decrease in finances due to divorce and trying to maintain household expenses as a single parent. I''m asking for Navient to work along with Dept of Education ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to resolve this reporting issues. I found that some of my accounts has been updated but not all of them.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'a number of attempts have been made since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the inaccuracies start as early as');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1643,'03/24/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I have written at least 15 CFPB complaints about the Servicing Mortgage Company, and no action has been taken. I received a Certified Letter dated, XX/XX/2018, from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Assistant Vice President informing me that a copy of my complaint has been forwarded to SPS Inc., and that SPS will provide me with a separate response. 

This issue was elevated by me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], after numerous written attempts directly to Select Portfolio Servicing., Inc. , ( SPS ), for them to provide me with written proof of Real Estate documents, reflecting the Sale/Transfer of the property from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , as the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Georgia Superior Court records only show [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as the owner. 

According to 15 U.S. Code 1692g - Validation of Debts, this is the Federal Law, and SPS is not complying with the law by not providing me with that inmformation.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a copy of my complaint has been forwarded to SPS Inc.. the complaint was elevated to a copy of my complaint.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1644,'03/24/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I want Sallie Mae to stop calling me ; their amount of telephone calls are illegal and harassing. I blocked the phone number, but calls still relays onto my voicemail. 

Im also a victim of cyber extortion, blackmail, and randsomware online, who stolen my identification online. Perhaps, the debt collection agency or Sallie Mae has stolen my most personal and private information to use tactics of randomware to exploit me online.','SLM CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'i want Sallie Mae to stop calling me. they have stolen my personal and private information.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1645,'03/23/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','We have been requesting the removal of PMI since our mortgage reached 80 % of the original value of our Mortgage. When we began requesting the removal of PMI Weichert sent us a package explaining the options for which PMI was to be removed. We followed the instructions and ordered an appraisal of our home, through Weichert. The appraisal came back and they still denied the removal of PMI. At 78 % of the original mortgage Weichert did not automatically remove our pmi pursuant to the package they originally sent to us. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is the date our original amortization table shows we would be at 78 % for automatic removal and they did not remove it and we requested removal again. This time we received a letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requesting we pay additional principal payment of {$540.00} to bring the principle to 70 % of the original loan and pay for an appraisal through Weichert to have PMI considered for cancellation. This is a direct contradiction to the previously received packet that states : " First Mortgages secured by 1 family principal residences / 2nd homes Earlier of [ 1 ]  the date that the mortgage balance is first scheduled to reach 78 % of the orginal value of the property ( lower of purchase price or appraised value ) or ( 2 ) the first day of the month after the date that is the mid-point of the mortgage amortization period. '''' I tried to contact Weichert direct by phone on the provided letters on  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke a customer service representative named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I informed her the letter I received contradicted what we received previously and would like to speak with someone in PMI department. She said a letter date XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that our PMI was being terminated, I confirmed with her that was the case. I inquired about a refund for PMI payments made after automatic termination was supposed to take place and she said everything will be explained in the letter. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received my mortgage statement for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I was surprised to see a charge for PMI. I did not call Weichert yet as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated a PMI termination letter was sent on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Today XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating to qualify for PMI cancellation at this time I may either pay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to bring down my principal to 70 % of my original value and order an appraisal through Weichert. Weichert has violated the Homeowner ''s Protection Act and I have done as much due diligence to have them comply. I have never missed a payment and there are no payments in arrears.','WEICHERT FINANCIAL SERVICES',2.0,2.0,'we have been requesting the removal of PMI since our mortgage reached 80 % of the original value of our Mortgage. we sent us a package explaining the options for which PMI');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1646,'03/23/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','To Whom It May Concern ; I write this to formally dispute what I consider a gross error on my credit report. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who the holder of my auto loan, has reported that I have been in arrears on my auto loan. I repeatedly attempted to pay through their telephone system, even with their personnel. My bank has verified that the information I submitted was correct and there were always available funds ( document A ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not request the funds from my account until my third submittal, after I had paid the amount due in cash at a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch ( document B ). 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has concluded there was no bank error, therefore they will not request amending my credit report even though I repeatedly attempted to pay through their system, with their representatives, answering their questions as asked, was in immediate response to every communication, have double paid, and have been to various branches repeatedly to resolve this issue. 

This is a chronology of events : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I made my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment of {$180.00} through their telephone system. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating the payment was not received. I called twice on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I spoke with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] representative each time. I asked that the late fee be waived. I volunteered to pay my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment ( 10 days before the due date ) ( {$[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]} + {[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]} ) to show I was not trying to shirk paying. I gave the information as requested from the representative. When I got off the phone I remember thinking, I guess he already has the routing number? He never asked me to give him all the numbers. But I assumed that since he was the representative, he was taking care of the payment. He knew what he was doing. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received another letter stating now my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments had not been received which I opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the evening. I had just received two separate letters from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding the updating of my information prior to this time. It is unfortunate this letter showed up a week or more later after the previous. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] California time and spoke with someone in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I gave him all the information as requested, which he repeated back to me, three times to verify its accuracy. He said it would take up to five days to post. I told him I was going to call every day and check my bank account to make sure it had posted. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received an email alert from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that my credit score had dropped 120 points. 
I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The representative recommended that I pull money from my ATM and walk it into a branch office. I did this, walking into [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I paid {$380.00}. I spoke with an associate, whose name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who recommended I speak with a manager, who was not in at that time. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I went back to to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], twice, to speak with the manager. The second time, the manager was still not available and I spoke with another employee. She was very nice and could only verify everything I already knew. At this time, the third payment I had submitted had not been posted. She wanted me to have an auto-payment instituted, but I declined. Once there is a problem with the system, it is a nightmare to correct the error. My current situation being a case in point. She recommend that I go to my banking institution, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], get a letter verifying what my routing and account numbers were and that there funds available for the draw every time I attempted to make the payment. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The payments I made with the representative, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] posted. I was now paid in advance through the end of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter from my credit union verifying the availability of funds for all dates requested. 
I walked the letter into a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We faxed the request for inquiry. I believe she asked them to expedite the request. I believe I was told to check back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I walked into the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to find out whether there had been resolution. The man I spoke with called and spoke to someone. He said he was only able to ascertain, they were not finished with their inquiry and would need until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I came home to find a letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], stating [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : ... confirmed your account reported correctly and does not need corrections Besides being vague whether this was that my account balance had been made current and was no longer in default or if this was about the inquiry, since I had spoken with their representative on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was told the inquiry had not been completed and to wait until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it seemed as if this was about the balance, not the inquiry. I will attach it separately. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number on the letter and spoke to a manager, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She told me the letter was about the inquiry. The bank had found no bank error so the negative report on my credit report would stay. The initial representative told me, the bank would not, as a COURTESY, remove the notice. I could not speak to someone in the review division regarding this. 

I drove to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke with a man at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch about what I could do. He recommended that I come in the next day and speak with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because I had initially spoke with her. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I came in and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Because I repeatedly had come back to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to pay, they never had to come looking for me, she thought I should be able to appeal on the executive level. She would reach out to them and someone would get back to me in 24-48 business hours. This was a Friday. It would be Monday or Tuesday before I heard from someone. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] A representative of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me. I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who facilitated a conference call between us and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a representative of the reviewing agency. I told them I thought the problem was in the second call I had made to attempt to pay. The representative had asked me for my account number and then whether there were zeros before the number. He never asked for the full account number. I thought this was where the problem lay. I was told they would listen to the tape and that someone would get back to me within 24-48 hours. I asked that I receive a copy of the recordings that had been made. It was not possible but, I was told I could have the transcript of the events as they had them as they occurred. I have never received them. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The 48 hour mark passed. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and left a voicemail because no one had called me. She returned my call and said she would look into it and have someone call me back. No one called. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], twice and left voicemail messages. She never returned my calls. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and left a voicemail. She never returned my call. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and left a voicemail. She never returned my call. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I came into [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No one was responding to my phone calls. I had been told I would have a response in 24-48 hours. She called someone, ascertained a manager would be there the next day XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that the recording in question would be reviewed and she would have an answer on Monday. 

XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me. The tape had been listened to. She had heard it. That which was in question was the exchange between their representative and myself. He had asked me for my account number When anyone asks me for my account number at my credit union I tell then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This is what I told him. He asked where there any zeros before it. I said yes, there were 5 zeros. He never asked me to give him the entire account number. The representative in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] asked me to repeat the routing number and the full account number from the colon, three times. This representative never asked me for this : Because he never asked me to verify all the numbers at the bottom of my check, Because I didnt ask him, dont you want me to give you all the numbers at the bottom with the routing number? 
Because he did not verify the accuracy of the information I gave him, Because I only answered his questions as he asked them of me, the information was entered incorrectly and without notification until after the due date, my account became over 30 days late. 

For 29 months this account was paid on time. This is the only time I have ever been considered late, even though I was repeatedly attempting to pay through Chases system. I have never had a late payment on my credit score, and I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old. 

I have been assiduously nurturing my credit score. 

My son and I lost our home in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Fire in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No one was home to evacuate. We lost everything. 

I have been working on rebuilding our home for the past five years. It has been an extremely difficult process. The insurance was difficult. The mortgage holder was difficult. The general contractor I had been required to hire before the plans were finished, was more than {$200000.00} over bid after all the financial numbers had been secured. I fired him and am now my own general contractor. I have been working very hard to bring the construction costs down and had gotten them to an almost manageable amount. Because no one would give me a construction loan or a HELOC on an unfinished home, I have had a rough time finding a lender to finance the amount I need to finish construction. 

I finally found a lender. I was getting ready to hand in all of our paperwork the beginning of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Now because of this miscommunication, this penalty is not just my credit score number but my ability to be able to get the money I need to finish rebuilding our home. Also, since this process began, the interest rate I was originally offered will not be valid because interest rates have risen. 

It never was or has ever been my intention for these payments become late and show up on my XXXXdit score. The only reason I tried to use the phone system was that because of other exigencies, I did not mail the payment in time. It is advertised that one can make a payment over the phone. I was afraid I would be a day or two late. I had no idea it would become what it has become and jeopardize what I have been working toward for the past five years. 

By the time I run out of funds, I will have invested {$530000.00} into the rebuilding of my home. Why would I do anything to jeopardize our lives like this? 

I have attached supporting documents from my credit union, the cash payment receipt, the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and phone records from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through mid-day of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; calls to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are highlighted. I do not have records from this month ''s statement. 

Thank you for your help, and I pray you can help me. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a bank has verified that the information I submitted was correct. a bank has concluded there was no bank error. a bank has concluded there was no bank error.');
