INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1657,'03/22/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Struggling to repay your loan','My student loan went into default due to me not paying it because I was not getting any information on my student loan mailed to me or through email. Once I found where my student loan was I began repaying it through a rehabilitation program, which I completed successfully. I have been out of default for a year paying on {$45.00} a month. All of the sudden my loan servicer Navient raised my monthly payments to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a month which I can not afford. I attempted to apply for multiple income driven repayment plans and the only plan lowered my payments only {$40.00}. They told me if I could not take care of my monthly payment my only option was to go into forbearance. They also told me I had to make one time payment to begin forbearance. I was never offered any other repayment plans and was forced to go into forbearance. I was trying to get a public service loan forgiveness and now that has come to a stop because I can no afford my student loan payments with all my other bills.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my student loan went into default due to me not paying it because I was not getting any information on my student loan mailed to me or through email. my loan servicer Navient raised');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1658,'03/22/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','IN XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I bought an ATV, was offered Zero % Interest due to my nearly perfect Credit Score. I accepted that offer from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and the payments were billed by an internet service, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], directly to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which is paid in full every month thru direct debit to my checking account. Never an issue. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a collection call on a Saturday from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] asking when I intended to make the past due payments on my account? I was floored, because I had never made a payment, they were drafted automatically monthly ... at least from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I questioned the caller quite a bit, as I was completely unaware of the past due status ... after some time the Customer Service Specialist II, said " You know I remember something like this with another caller a few months ago, can you please hold '''' She returned with the name [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the internet service that was actually taking my payment and processing it to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I searched my email for anything from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to find contact information, and I did find an email dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] thanking me for the payment..nothing further ... .after I inquired why they stopped making the payments I was informed of a huge data breech they experienced and that they had suspended all operations. That an email was sent to all users in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] notifying users that the service was terminating..well that''s great if you get the email ... after several back and forth conversations, sending all the documents I was able to gather, hoping BBT ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) would retract the past due report to Credit Bureaus, due the obvious and previous experienced issue with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ... [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] staed that they offer no ''Good Will '''' Adjustments to items reported to the 3 major Credit Bureaus ... .This couldn''t be clearer, it was NOT my mistake, yet my credit report has taken a significant hit because of the 60 days past due report. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has offered via email to join in a call with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to help support my request for a retraction, admitting that the email they " Sent '''' to me was NEVER OPENED, no record that it was ever delivered ... ..spam filter, whatever ... ..and that they were sorry for the problems this has caused. 

This was a failure of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] system, and for the error to cause negative rating to my credit, again nearly perfect for 25 years..is very disturbing ... and doesn''t in any way reflect my personal credit responsibility and awareness. Only when I saw the FICO score drop in a monthly statement, did I become alarmed ... ..now 2 weeks into this I''m no better off than when I started this dispute. 

Please help!','BB&T CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a customer service specialist says the service was terminated. the customer service specialist II says the service was canceled. the customer service specialist II says the service was canceled.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1659,'03/21/2018','Debt collection','Auto debt','Communication tactics','I took out a personnel loan using my car as collateral. Well for I while I was making payments pretty much on time with once in a while being late. Which is technically my fault. Then I started making payments again on time. Well then in last few months a had some finical problems come up, car breaking down, getting sick and being out of work. I informed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of this and told her ( Manager ) that I was doing a mortgage on my home and was gon na pay them as soon as all that was taken care of. The manager of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] keep calling and kept calling sometimes five or six times a day. It got so bad that I refused to take any more calls. That I understand, but when you tell them that you waiting on your closing date and that when that happens they will get their payoff, the phone calls should not be coming in at five to six times a day. The last payoff I got one of the clerks in the office said that if payment was not received by the end of this month legal actions will be taken. This happened on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of XX/XX/2018. Well this past Monday there was a legal document brought to me by a neighbor who said it was dropped off at their house by mistake. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] whom works there that they will receive the check for pay off Monday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/2018. I asked who delivers the court papers and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that they have a third party that delivers it. My concern is that my personal information was on this form and what right do they have to give papers to someone and they aren''t even checking too make sure that person is the right person. I don''t care about the phone calls but to leave court papers with someone other than me is beyond me. I know that all this could have been avoided had I paid my payments.','REGIONAL MANAGEMENT CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'gon na paid me a personal loan on my home and was gon na pay them. a clerk said that if payment was not received by the end');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1660,'03/21/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','National credit systems Inc placed an collection account on my credit file XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the amount of {$500.00} disputed with company in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they have refused to remove information from my credit file','National Credit Systems,Inc.',2.0,2.0,'national credit systems Inc placed an account on my credit file XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the amount of $500.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1661,'03/21/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','On XX/XX/2018 I put a deposit on a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/2018 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], The deal did not go thought, I left the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], with no car but the next day, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Charged my credit card for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I''ve talked to Citi and they have put the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] back on my card. I NEVER bought a car from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have never purchased anything from any [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I bought a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Has done nothing to help resolve this issue','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2018 I put a deposit on a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COM');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1662,'03/21/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','We live in Florida and had to evacuate for Hurricane Irma. Our area was declared a disaster zone and we were told that mortgage companies were required by the federal government to give us a 90 day grace period on our mortgage payments because of that. We contacted our lender, Mr. Cooper, and they confirmed that this program was available to us. They immediately put us in some kind of forbearance/deferment which they confirmed in writing. At the end of the 90 days, they declared us in default and demanded immediate payment of three months '' worth of mortgage payments. We contacted them and they''re saying that we have to apply for refinancing. In other words, they''re not moving the three payments we were given grace for to the end of the loan. It doesn''t make sense that they would expect us to have all three payments available since the whole purpose behind this program was to compensate for the fact that we weren''t able to work while our area recovered.

We''ve talked to Mr. Cooper several times and they''re refusing to work with us outside of forcing us to refinance. They''ve accepted several payments from us, but they''re still forcing the issue. We don''t think this is just or in the spirit of the law. It sounds like a scheme to try to take our house.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'mortgage companies were required to give us a 90 day grace period on our mortgage payments. they immediately put us in some kind of forbearance/deferment which they confirmed in');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1663,'03/21/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a Notice of Acceleration of Maturity that was delivered by certified mail from Ocwen Loan Servicing ; LLC stating that under the Deed of Trust my home is scheduled for foreclosure on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Ocwen was not the loan originator. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was the first lender, then sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], GMAC, Ocwen. I believe the loan was sold at least four times and the amount owed kept increasing. After calling the loan servicing agency ( Ocwen Loan Servicing, LLC ) I still could not get a clear understanding to why the amount owed increased shy of {$70000.00} on a less than a {$47000.00} loan that originated in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I never received a copy of the loan documents ; communication with Ocwen Loan Servicing was difficult. 1. Never receive copys of paperwork 2. Everything was verbal up until now 3. Mortgage increasing without explanation 4. Refused copies of the loan told I would have to pay a fee 5. I stop paying in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because I needed correct information. Never had a problem until Ocwen took over the loan 6.I am current [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I asked about Servicemembers Civil Relief Act ( SCRA ) to no avail 7. Language barriers and misinformation given 8. I am alleging redlining even when I tried to address my default','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a notice of Acceleration of Maturity was delivered by certified mail from Ocwen Loan Servicing. the notice was delivered by certified mail stating that my home');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1664,'03/21/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','On the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] this year ( XX/XX/2018) I noticed that the credit card I took out in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of last year had been accruing interest. 

I immediately thought this must be a mistake and called the bank to clarify why I was being charged interest and made clear to them, as it was made clear to me ( initially through an online advertisement and confirmed by a US Bank agent over the phone ) before I applied for the card that I would be under a 0 % interest plan for the first year. 

I was advised to reach out by fax to their compliant department at which point I sent the following fax : -- -- -- -- -- -- - Fax number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Name account number Detailed description Sign and date Name : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Card number : xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx To whom it may concern. 



In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of last year I applied for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card under the impression from both online advertising and a conversation with a representative of US Bank that I would be under 0 % interests rate for the first twelve months. 



I neither recorded the conversation nor did I bookmark the website where the twelve month promotion was advertised. 



Nevertheless I have since found an article online that reflected the same exact deal. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) also contacted the author through email and she has again verified, as I am confident, that her article reflects truthful valid and unambiguous information when stating the 12 month 0 % interest. 



I have now three points of confirmation regarding you promotion of twelve months 0 % interest rates. Twice before I opened the card and this author again confirming after the fact. 



I would frequently check my online app to look at my charges and had not once seen an interest charge. So you can imagine it came as a shock to me when I saw an actual statement yesterday with both interest charges and fee charges. 



Please help me correct this issue as Im confident that the interest and fees being charged to my account are a mistake on your end. 



I believe that this issue can be resolved quickly, easily, and retroactively by yourselves and without me having to seek outside counsel.

Regards, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- -- -- -- -- -- -- -- - Today it has been two months and I have yet to receive back a correspondence from them regarding this issue. 

What''s most concerning is that this type of promotion is very common and every time I''ve had a chance to speak to US Bank ''s customer service reps and supervisors they''ve been adamant in their opposition to help me remedy the interest accumulations ( which are now as high as {$600.00} ). Their arguments point to the fact that I have no defense since my complaint came 90 days after the opening of the account ( I''m about 30 days past when I originally noticed the mistake, and the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statements ahd no interest so I just didn''t worry about it ) and that their promotion does not apply to me since they did not reach out to me directly, ( although this was not made clear to me in their online promotion and it explicitly explained to me over the phone by their rep that I would not be charged interest for the first 12 months ). 

I would like to reiterate they have a tape of the conversation wherein a rep assured me of the 0 % interest for 12 months but I do not. 

Here is the link not to a similar advertisement as the one I saw when I was first interested in the card. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] This whole situation feels very unscrupulous on the part of the bank, very much like a bait and switch situation. 

Please help me as this situation, it would be reassuring to know that when companies act unethically my government will serve to help as best they can. This is my last recourse. Thank you.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a credit card I took out in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of last year had been accruing interest. the card was made clear to me before applying for');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1665,'03/21/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','CRA VIOLATION / NO KNOWLEDGE OF FRAUDULENT ACCOUNT DUE TO ID THEFT APPEARED ON MY TRANSUNION CREDIT REPORT. FTC ID THEFT REPORT # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'CRA VIOLATION / NO KNOWLEDGE OF FRAUDULENT ACCOUNT DUE TO ID THEFT APPEARED ON MY TRANSUNION CR');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1666,'03/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','This is my third attempt with Transunion for an item [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The item was deleted on XX/XX/2017 and recently was reinserted in my report. I have reached out to them asking them to investigate this issue and they have failed. 

In accordance with FCRA Section 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( B ) ( ii ), you are required by law to notify me of reinsertion in writing within 5 days. 
( B ) Requirements relating to reinsertion of previously deleted material ( ii ) Notice to consumer If any information has been deleted from a consumers file pursuant to subparagraph ( A ) is reinserted in the file, the consumer reporting agency shall notify the consumer of the reinsertion or, if authorized by the consumer for that purpose, by any other means available to the agency None of the above steps were taken according to law. Transunion has violated FCRA laws and has continued to violate by not properly addressing and investigating this issue. I am asking a third time to please remove this item from my report due to the blatant disregard for consumer laws.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the item was deleted on XX/XX/2017 and recently was reinserted in my report. I have reached out to them asking them to investigate this issue.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1667,'03/20/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Closing your account','Had about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  personal credit cards, 4 were Chase personal credit cards. Applied for the Chase Hyatt credit card on XX/XX/18. Without any warning, all my chase credit cards were shut down a few days after. This is immediately right after I paid the {$450.00} annual fee on my Chase Sapphire Reserve card ; Chase reps stated my refund would be eventually refunded. All of the spend on Chase CCs was organic spend. Called Chase, but got moved around from rep to rep. Finally, was able to submit an appeal for my shutdown ... will hear back in 7-10 business days.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'4 of my Chase personal credit cards were shut down a few days after. the $450.00 annual fee on my Chase Sapphire Reserve card was organic spend.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1668,'03/20/2018','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I''ve sent multiple letters to this agency about this not being my account. After being advised by identitytheft.gov, I''ve completed and sent a fraud affidavit via certified mail. I can see they received it, but nothing has changed. See supporting documents. Even the USPS tracking.My official complaint is against AD ASTRA. My information was used to obtain an apartment, cell phone, and an auto loan with my ex-partner. I am a victim of identity theft and have put this off for too long. I''ve completed the proper steps, 1. notify creditors 2. police report 3. informed the state of Texas.','Ad Astra Recovery Services Inc',2.0,4.0,'identitytheft.gov sent fraud affidavit to the agency. affidavit was sent via certified mail.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1669,'03/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Hello, On XX/XX/2017 I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to look and buy a new car, and I was in the process of getting one. The salesman at that time told me that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   has a bank of their own and that they would use that bank to check out my credit and give me a price. The salesman was taking so long and I decided to not take the car instead and look somewhere else. Around a couple of weeks later, I check my credit report on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and see that there is six different hard inquiries on that specific day. The names are Capital one, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2017 I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to look and buy a new');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1670,'03/20/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On XX/XX/2018, I ordered a copy of my credit report. Upon review, I noticed well over 30 unauthorized inquiries on my credit report. I immediately called each credit bureau and filed a formal complaint as well as the Federal Trade Commission so as to provide them the necessary information so as to have these unauthorized inquiries removed from my credit report. Well after 45 days of waiting I received letters stating that these inquiries have been verified and when I inquired as to how the bureaus stated they sent out emails or some sort of electronic communication asking were these inquiries made by me. They stated each company had responded as " YES '''' but when I asked whom did they speak and what kind of physical evidence could be found they all said they didn''t speak to anyone or review any documentation. I am completely baffled by this so they just sent basically a TEXT requesting the company in question do they KNOW me and those companies said YES. This is completely disturbing to know they did not truly validate these applications yet are reporting I made them. I supplied them with a copy of my utility bill, driver license, and social security card so they could validate said requests which I found in most cases were inaccurate or simply erroneous as the companies who made the inquiries did not have my personal information correct in ALL CASES yet the laziness of each credit bureau is of such they do not care or truly try to investigate such matters as serious as this. Please assist me in this most serious of matters.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'XX/XX/2018, I ordered a copy of my credit report. Upon review, I noticed well over 30 unauthorized inquiries on my credit report. the ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1671,'03/20/2018','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Trouble during payment process','This complaint is in regards to a {$150000.00} ( excluding fees and interest charges, attorney fees, etc. ) loan modification that I NEVER signed for. Wells Fargo Bank tacked on this modification to the back of the original mortgage note of {$350000.00} on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was on the original mortgage with my then husband but divorced in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Leaving my ex-husband solely responsible for any additional debt obligations he accrued after the divorce including the modification. I was interested in purchasing a home I was renting in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when the broker called to inform me that he pulled a credit report which stated I modified my home. I immediately called Wells Fargo bank modification specialist at ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] extension [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The customer service representative stated to me that my authorization ( signature nor verbal ) was not needed for a mortgage modification even if I was divorced. When my ex-husband passed away in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I had a chance to go through all his paperwork which confirmed that I did not sign. I contacted a friend ''s lawyer who contacted Well Fargo while I was in the office and Wells Fargo bank verified that my signature was not on the paperwork. In essence, I take full responsibility for the original mortgage but not the additional ( {$150000.00} loan modification ) attached. Wells Fargo attached the modification to the back of the original loan.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a loan modification was tacked on the back of the original mortgage note. the modification was a $150000.00 loan modification. the modification was a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1672,'03/20/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hospital in Iowa sent a medical bill to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Illinois, for an unpaid medical debt for our son. The hospital sent the debt in my ex husbands name only since he is the insurance carrier, legally responsible for all medical debt for our children after XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in divorce decree and the grantor on the medical bill account. In prior years when we were married, we had accounts together through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hospital sent the account through to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the automatically attached my name to the account in collections. I never received a bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in this account and never received a bill through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on this account. I found that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had done this when I checked my credit. When I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they said they couldnt bill me because they didnt have my address or number but had tried communicating with the ex husband whom was sent to collections in the first place with no response. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] representative threatened to take me to court, said they did not want a copy of the divorce decree, talked over me in a hollaring voice, belittled me. The original creditor, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hospital did not send me to collections, never billed me for the services on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but sent it to collections on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] due to a nonpayment on a bill my ex husband is legally responsible for paying. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] took it upon themselves to add my name to this collection account and put a derogatory mark on my credit when this account was not in my name in the first place when [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hospital sent the account to them. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has put a derogatory mark on my credit for an account that is not mine, threatened me, would not allow me to send evidence that the account was not mine, has not submitted proof that I owe the bill because the do not have my address and should not have my address since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hospital submitted the account on my ex husband and all of his information. We have been divorced since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Hospital is also working to remover my name from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] since they did not send my name on this account.','Avadyne Health Holdings, Inc',2.0,2.0,'hospital sent debt to ex husbands name for unpaid medical debt. hospital sent debt in ex husbands name to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONY');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1673,'03/19/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], USAA Savings Bank deactivated/suspended two of my checking accounts and referred both accounts to their Financial Crime Unit ( Fraud Department ), and when I contacted USAA on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the bank representative told me that my accounts are under investigation for fraudulent activities by the financial crime unit. I have been a customer at USAA bank for six years and have a direct deposit account. Because my accounts are freezed, I''m having hard time using my funds.','UNITED SERVICES AUTOMOBILE ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'USAA Savings Bank deactivated/suspended two checking accounts. the bank representative told me that my accounts are under investigation.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1674,'03/19/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I went to the hospital and provided them with two forms of insurance. The hospital has both insurances on file yet their collections team posted two negative accounts on my credit reports. I called an asked why they said the hospital did not give them the second insurance information. I gave them the insurance information. They turned around and posted the same negative on my cresit report at another bureau. The numbers they have listed now go straight to voicemail and when I did speak to someone she advised they would removed the information after i gave the insurance information but that has not been done. I had this conversation in early XX/XX/2018. This is happening with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$100.00} and {$62.00}. My secondary insurance was through the state medicaid department and the hospital is aware they can not accept a payment from the insurance company then bill a patient additional charges. I spoke to the representative at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at Online collections  and informed her the accounts were updated. She told me they would not remove the negative information from my account until I paid it. I refuse to pay them for a bill I do not owe.','ONLINE Information Services, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'the hospital has both insurances on file yet their collections team posted two negative accounts on my credit reports. they turned around and posted the same negative on my cresit report. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1675,'03/19/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','My debit card was fraudulent use on XX/XX/2018. {$700.00} and {$800.00} was stolen from my atm card. I called BOA the next day I check my account, bank of America cancelled my card and issued another one and I was told they will investigate it and they will refund me in 10days if they didn''t finish their inveatigation.

Apparently the thief/thieves also tried using the same card at well fargo but the transaction was declined, according to the customer agent I spoke with.

Next day I saw {$2.00} debited from my account, I called BOA and the agent told me the same card was used to check account balance at other bank, immediately {$2.00} was refunded back yo my account.

On the 10 day I was suppose to get refunded, an agent from BOA called asking me just 3 questions that " do you have the card with you on the day of the fraudulent charge, do you give you atm card to anyone and lastly did you give your pin to anyone ...

The next email I got after 20mins from BOA is the claim has been resolved and claim was not paid. 
I was shocked because this so called bank did not investigate the claim. 
My hard earned money was just gone like that? If bank is no more safe to keep my money I''d rather save my money at home. 
I already filed a small claim suite and hoping to get back my money.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'a debit card was fraudulent use on XX/XX/2018. a customer agent from BOA called me and asked me 3 questions. the thief/');
