INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1713,'03/12/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','The original account was with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over 7 years ago. When the account was closed, the remaining balance was credited and was left with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance. This account was removed from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but is still being reported by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This account is more than 7 years old and I am no longer liable for this account as it was paid prior to going to collections with Trident. Each time that there is a new acquisition of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  accounts, this account keeps getting transferred instead of being formerly closed out. I have never had an account with Trident Asset Management and this should be removed from my credit report as it is infringing on my rights to Fair Debt Collection practices. This account appeared on my credit report in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( never reported prior to this time ) and when I noticed this old debt I contacted the agency to remove. It was agreed that they would remove it, but the debt keeps appearing on my credit report. I contacted the better business bureau and they have sent on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I also spoke with their representation onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I escalated the call to the manager of the rep as she was unable to produce information as to how my credits were applied ; she advised that this debt was merely validated. I asked for an explanation of charges and this was never produced. This debt is too old to report and should be removed from my credit report instead of keep getting sold to additional credit collection agencies. Please have the company update the records and remove from my credit report.','Trident Asset Management, L.L.C.',2.0,2.0,'account was removed from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over 7 years ago. the remaining balance was credited and was left with a [COMPTE_AN');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1714,'03/12/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','OnXX/XX/XXXXI wrote a complaint letter to US Bank Home Mortgage Customer Advocacy Center stating that I wanted to be reimbursed for all the PMI payments USBank had been fraudulently collecting from me since the FIRST time I asked for PMI removal in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I also asked them to waive my appraisal fee since if I hadn''t done my own detective work, the advice USBank gave when asking to remove my PMI several times ( including the first inquiry back in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) was incorrect which would have had me paying on PMI for years to come.

The reason they stated they could not refund me back toXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and why they incorrectly stated the guidelines was that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PMI guidelines had just recently changed and that they were NOT AWARE of the change in guidelines. This is again not true and I again had to do my own detective work to find out what the truth was. The truth is that the guidelines were last updated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. And according to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : " an approved insurer must conduct and complete a self-assessment of its COMPLIANCE with all requirements of the PMIERS as of the effective date and certify to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that it satisfies all the PMIERs ''''. So stating they were not aware of the changes from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is also a lie to protect themselves. I am appalled at how USBank continues to falsify information at the consumer ''s expense. I request PMI removal from original stated request ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) as well as appraisal fee waived for the gross misrepresentation of the truth which would not have been identified if it hadn''t been for my due diligence. This company is certainly committing FRAUD by every sense of the word " WRONGFUL DECEPTION INTENDED TO RESULT IN FINANCIAL GAIN ''''','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,4.0,'onXX/XX/XXXXI wrote complaint letter to US Bank Home Mortgage Customer Advocacy Center. he asked them to waive my appraisal fee for the gross');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1715,'03/12/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','At the beginning of the year I was a victim of identity theft ( FTC affidavit attached as well as proof of fraud alerts on all three major CRAs ). This caused me to look deeper into my credit. After doing so I discovered several inquires I did not recognize. One being from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/18 I sent a certified letter to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requesting proof of " written authorization '''' by me with my signature to pull my credit. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] only responded stating my file was accessed by " a vetted subscriber ''''. Thus I am assuming they have to such documentation and do not have written authorization from me to either themselves or their " vetted subscriber '''' According to section 604 permissible purposes are : Firm offer of credit, insurance, employment and court order. Section 604 also states the consumer MUST give " written instructions ''''. I have attached an FTC advisory opinion ( below ) which interprets Section 604 of the FCRA on what is both permissible and considered " written instruction ''''. According to this FTC advisory opinion [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is in direct violation of Section 604 of the FCRA. I again request that the UNAUTHORIZED inquires be removed from my credit report or be provided proof I have given " written instructions '' to pull my credit.

https : //www.ftc.gov/policy/advisory-opinions/advisory-opinion-landever-10-12-99','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a certified letter to a vetted subscriber requesting proof of " written authorization '''' by me. a consumer MUST give " written instructions '''', according');
