INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1812,'02/23/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Dear Sir/Madame : I''m writing to request that you look into the operations at US Bank. US Bank is the mortgage servicer on a home I own. Please review the following : 1. I believe, based on several personal experiences, that the bank ''s processing center is intentionally holding over-payments ( payments with additional principal ) to artificially inflate the interest earnings of the company. 

This month, I sent a check on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], including a {$1000.00} check from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  account as well as an endorsed check for {$2300.00}. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called to begin an inquiry into my lost checks, as the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] check had not been cashed. I called again on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to follow up on my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] call, since I hadn''t received information from the bank on the whereabouts of this mortgage payment. Still, the bank had no answer. I requested that a supervisor return my call with more information, but the bank stated they couldn''t call guarantee a call in less than 48hours. During my conversation with the supervisor, I was restrained and extremely angry at the Bank ''s inability to a ) find my money, b ) follow up with my request to find this money c ) inability to escalate this issue to sufficiently address my issues. 

As of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I noticed that my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] check had cleared. I called the Bank to find out why they hadn''t let me know about the receipt of said money ( which had been allegedly ( per the date stamp on the cleared check of XX/XX/ ) on the day of the call. 

I am concerned that the bank is intentionally withholding overpayments. I also believe that the bank ''s communication system is woefully inadequate. 

Finally, since this is not the first time that the bank has held checks for extraordinary periods of time, I am concerned about the application of principal. I have requested the math from the bank to ensure that the bank is not acting inappropriately, but I believe thay they are ... the last time that the bank had problems depositing my money, the bank claimed that the receipt date of mortgage payments does not have a material impact on principal and interest. This doesn''t accord with how principal and interest works in my own financial analysis, and I am suspect.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a check from my account and a endorsed check for $2300.00 was sent this month. the bank has no answer to my questions.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1813,'02/23/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I have been trying to get a payoff letter to pay off a mortgage loan ( sale closing scheduled XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) from this company ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) which has taken on the servicing of my mortgage from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Here is my correspondence to the CEO of the company including relevant dates and communication : Hello. 

