I advised [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that the buyer ''s attorney is considering putting the proceeds of the sale in an escrow account until written payoff is available, and that if that happens on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that''s fine, but that one of the people we spoke with today said it would be 30-60 days, which is not acceptable. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- -- -Original Message -- -- - From : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] To : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Cc : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Sent : Wed, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] am Subject : Urgent : payoff letter needed immediately I and my attorney have been attempting to get a payoff notification for my mortgage from your company since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Effective XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], your company took over the servicing of my mortgage with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I had a home sale scheduled for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the closing was brought forward to today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I and my attorney ''s office have spent hours on the phone with your customer support people attempting to get a payoff. 

