INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1824,'02/21/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I recently submitted a complaint about how Equifax stated they verified a Bankruptcy on my credit report. I am aware that under the Fair Credit Reporting Act of 1971, are to only report one hundred percent accurate information. I submitted my complaint through the CFPB and their response was not made through the CFPB which is also a violation of my right to due process. Equifax did this to hide the fact that they know that they are reporting inaccurate information. The response has been the same, verified through a third party [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The information purchased by Equifax from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has redactions that are required under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] laws. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is not provided a full and complete social security number nor are they provided a full and complete date of birth when they purchase public record information from any Court. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then sells that incomplete information to the major credit bureaus as verified and validated information. In doing so, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Equifax have violated the Fair Credit Reporting Act of 1971 by reporting and providing inaccurate and unverified information about consumers. I demand that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Equifax be investigated for fraudulent business practices as well as violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a complaint was submitted about how Equifax verified a Bankruptcy on my credit report. the response was verified through a third party [COMPTE_ANONY');
