INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1829,'02/21/2018','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On three recent occasions, JP MORGAN CHASE BANK has been manipulating/ reordering transactions on my checking account.

The first two purchases ( same merchant ) were made on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( for {$10.00} ) and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( for {$8.00} ) and posted quickly. However, the transaction disappeared a month later, and now reappeared as posted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - almost a MONTH later. The third transaction ( second/ different merchant ) occurred when I made a purchase on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( for {$7.00} ) and posted within two days. However, transaction disappeared as well, and now re-posted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - WEEKS later. 

I called both merchants to verify when they collect and their funds from the bank and assured me that they do so within days. When I called the bank, they deflected stating that it is unlikely merchants collected so quickly and that they usually/can take up to a month to collect funds from the bank. What?? I informed the agent that by logic, no merchant - especially a small vendor would want to wait that long to collect monies, and I reminded her that I had originally seen these amounts posted to my account and now re-posted under a new transaction date as of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

