INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1845,'02/18/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Unable to get your credit report or credit score','There is an issue with the reporting agencies using their own methods of scoring a FICO score. I read on the FICO website that the agencies are allowed to use their own method to score a FICO score, WHY? IF businesses are using a FICO score in which the standard of that score keeps changing, then how is that Fair Credit Reporting? I recently needed a FICO score for a home mortgage application and the FICO from all three agencies were vastly different with the bottom score being 80 points lower from the top score. Needless to say I didn''t get the loan. These agencies need to be held to a single standard if businesses are going to use them in their credit reports and analysis of peoples credit applications.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',4.0,4.0,'the agencies are allowed to use their own methods to score a FICO score. the agency is allowed to use their own method to score a FICO score.');
