2. Without being provided this concrete evidence, I feel discriminated when after I exercised my rights to file a fraud claim, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] American Express closed my account, denied me credit and forwarded my account to collection department.

3. I have filed a previous fraud claim but in the letter ( see attached ) denying my fraud claim it is indicated that the decision was based on account history and notes and not on concrete proofs establishing the responsibility for the fraudulent purchases.

4. I feel it will be unfair for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] American Express to collect the above mentioned amount and any related finance charges because of failure to present the requirements of a thorough investigation.

5. I have been a loyal [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] American Express credit card holder for a very long time and I am proud to claim that I am in good standing, always paying on time.

I will very much appreciate your help for a reconsideration to reverse the decision made and restore my account status.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'a fraud claim is equivalent to $11000.00 which is a great amount of loss to me financially. my credit rating is affected when my [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1867,'02/14/2018','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Closing on a mortgage','The seller, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], represented by its servicing agent, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and its listing agent, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] utilized [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as an auction platform to sell to the public their bank owned property known as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
