INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1898,'02/08/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/ XX/XX/ Fee TRANSACTION FEE {$370.00} Show details TRANSACTION FEE XX/XX/ XX/XX/ Fee TRANSACTION FEE {$26.00} XX/XX/ XX/XX/ Fee TRANSACTION FEE {$50.00} Chase has charged me Cash Advance fees when all other times [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was a regular tranasaction. There was no warning communication or anything to let the consumer know. I will stop using [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] purchases for Chase credit cards. 

The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] fees comes as a shock as they readily accept it as a regular purchase before.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] fees come as a shock as they readily accept it as a regular purchase before.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1899,'02/08/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose prepaid card','Problem with a purchase or transfer','Unfortunately, I purchased a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift card for my granddaughter from a company called netSpend without reading the fine print on the card wrapper that states she was required her to give them her Social Security Number when she called to activate the card. Rightfully so, she was very reluctant to give someone her SS number over the telephone. Their legal paperwork states they need her SS number because of the Patriot Act. Like other [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift cards that require no personal information for their use, the intent of this card was to use it for a one or two-time purchase for the total amount on the card, not for continuous use. Therefore, I requested a refund for the card via their website. 

I tried to call their Customer Service number to inquire about a refund as it says on the card wrapper, but the only options on the recording was to 1 ) activate the card ; or 2 )  enter the card number. Since the card cant be activated without revealing her Social Security Number, I was unable to speak to a human representative, so I emailed them. 

I was told to call their customer service number or email them. Since I again could not reach a human at Customer Service to discuss this matter, I emailed them. They responded again by saying they would call me. They did, however, I was disconnected before I could answer. I again emailed them to contact me but received no response. 

All I want is a refund. I want nothing to do with this company in the future.','NETSPEND CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'netSpend purchased a gift card for my granddaughter. she was reluctant to give someone her SS number because of the Patriot Act. the card can only be activated without');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1900,'02/08/2018','Debt collection','Other debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] fraudulently placed a negative collection account on my private consumer credit profile. This company is trying erroneously claim civil dispute between them and I for an alleged debt that is not owed to them nor the company they represent. The plaintiff did not provide any services nor provide any goods to me and has no rights to any debts owed. The Fair Debt Collection Practices Act clearly states that a debt collector can not collect any amount of money that is not authorized by the agreement creating the debt or permitted by law. Being that there is no agreement between the plaintiff and the defendant, that would mean the Plaintiffs collection attempts can not be sustained and are in fact fraudulent. The plaintiff is trying to collect on debt that has passed the statute of limitation in California and has illegally re-aged the account in an attempt to collect a debt not owed to them. They are an unqualified third party and a liability which offers no assistance to this alleged civil dispute. If they are the Fiduciary in this matter, I need a copy of the contract between us to continue further communication. I do not give permission or consent by assent for them to enter as a third party to this alleged civil dispute, nor to issue letters of threat to my private property or person, including their fraudulent reporting to various credit reporting agencies. They are attempting to enter into an alleged civil dispute without the contract and/or my permission and are in trespass. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] v [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) ). They must Produce a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or cease and desist. Unless you are a Secured Party, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Creditor, Debtor or Signer of the Original Contract, you are a third party. You are a liability and no assistance. Take Notice : You are lawfully and legally dismissed. I will not discuss my Private Affairs with an Unqualified Third Party. The laws in this country do not provide a remedy for a collection company that knowingly and voluntarily takes on a bad debt and then goes after the supposed debtor in an attempt to collect that alleged debt ; therefore, the Plaintiffs actions fall under the precedence set forth in scienti et volenti non fit injuria. They are ordered to remove the negative and fraudulent reporting of a collection on my consumer credit report and vacate any judgments they have put forth on the public record. They are not allowed to resell this alleged debt to any other company and will report it as a loss in their books. 

They should be advised that issuing letters of threat and trying to collect on a debt for which no contract exists is a crime of mail fraud and punishable in united states. I am a litigious consumer and I plan on seeking remedy in venue closest to me if they do not perform in the way that I have set forth in this presentment. This is an attempt to peacefully settle this matter. Please be sure that your documents are in order if there is need to pursue litigation.','Kimball, Tirey & St. John LLP',2.0,4.0,'plaintiff is trying to collect on debt that has passed the statute of limitation in California. the plaintiff is trying to collect on debt that has illegally re-aged the account. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1901,'02/08/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have sent several letters to the three reporting agencies and to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about this account. I have asked for original paperwork to support the loan. All I have received is a promissory note. I asked for all paperwork with my ID attached. Never received what I asked for. As I periodically checked my credit report, I noticed the account was closed and transferred. I filed my taxes and found out the day that I was to receive my refund that it went to the Department of Education. How can they collect when they closed out the accounts and transferred to what I found out is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they told me they closed out the loan and transferred to the collection agency. Again, how can they collect on a debt when they no longer own? The lady I spoke with on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me that a letter was sent to me dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that I had 65 days to take action. I told her that I never received it. She stated she could send me another letter. The lady also stated that she will contact my employer to garnish my wages. I spoke with an attorney and that is not legal in Pennsylvania or Texas. What good will that do? They already took my money and as far as I am concern, the letter comes after my tax refund was taken. The problem is collecting on a debt that they no longer own. If I had received the letter, I would have taken action. I never mess with the IRS or let anyone take my tax refund. And if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] owns this loan now, what happened to them contacting me, why does it not show on my credit report? [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should not be able to collect on debts they stated that they no longer own. On my credit report, these items show as closed/transferred. They should not be an exception to the rule when it comes to collecting a debt. They should be held to the same standards as all creditors.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a letter from a woman who has received a tax refund is sent to me. the letter comes after my tax refund was taken. the issue is collecting on a debt');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1902,'02/08/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','I obtained my credit report from Equifax, report confirmation # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and noticed a hard inquiry was recorded on my report from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] submitted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have never applied for credit or a loan through this company. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I contacted Equifax to inform them of the incorrect information on my credit report and that I did not apply for credit through this company. The employee, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], informed me that she could not do anything to assist me to have the hard inquiry removed and that it was my responsibility to contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to obtain a letter from them verifying I did not apply for credit. She also asked if I contacted the police department to report it. Also, she confirmed it would stay on my credit report for two years until Equifax receives a letter. I asked to have a fraudulent inquiry put on my file to ensure this does not occur again.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a hard inquiry was recorded on my credit report from Equifax. the employee, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], informed me that she could not do anything to assist');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1903,'02/08/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','My loan servicer ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) mistakenly applied a retroactive forebearance to my loan payments for the months of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after I had already made the payments in full and on time. They are now refusing to count those payments as part of my public service loan forgiveness ( PSLF ) qualifying payments. In addition there are various other months where they miscalculated my payments and as a result they are 16 months short of what my records indicate the right number should be. Since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have been requesting a review/recount and have been strung along by them repeatedly. The latest excuse is that they are waiting on approval for an expedited review since it has been so long, but even that approval has taken them over a month.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'my public service loan forgiveness ( PSLF) payments are now refusing to count them. they are now refusing to count those payments as part of my public service loan forgiveness.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1904,'02/07/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','False statements or representation','I received a phone call to collect a debt of {$730.00} for a medical bill. I asked the representative that contacted me in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] what the debt was for and I was told that ''''it was for a visit to see my primary care doctor for a routine exam in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''''. This is health information that the debt collector should not be in possession of I asked the name of the ''''primary care doctor '''' and I was not provided with that information. It is my right to know the original creditor. I also asked the agent if she was in possession of anything that would give her the legal right to attempt to collect a debt from me she never answered that question.She never verified my information so I asked her my address to make sure she sent the validation to the correct address and she verified an incorrect address with me. 
I asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to validate the debt and I received a letter ( that went to the incorrect address that was later forwarded to me ) stating that this debt is from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the sum of {$510.00}. 
The debt is reported on my credit as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PA XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$730.00} {$730.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I then requested that I do not want the company to contact me anymore until they call legally show me proof that I woe this debt to them.','HCFS Health Care Financial Services, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'debt collector should not be in possession of ''''primary care doctor''''. she never answered the question and asked her if she was in possession of anything that would give her');
