INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1913,'02/06/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','My name is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
I am requesting Capital One to correct the mistake that it made, and remove the hard inquiries on my credit file that were performed in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/2018. The timeline of the events is as follows : I have received in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a " You already pre-qualified letter for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], reservation # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and access code : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Signed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Senior Vice President, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] P.S. Don''t miss this exclusive offer. Get the NEW [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Card and watch your points add up! Reply today. 

Since I already have 2 credit cards with Capital, I wanted to make sure a third application will be favorable, and therefore I called Customer Service and I was rest assured the application is pre-approved and it would be no problem to apply. I have also stated to the Customer Representative that I have changed my address from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and again the representative stated it should be no problem with the application. 

After the conversation with Capital one representative, I have temporarily removed the security lock on my credit file, and completed the application on-line for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I have received the message that I am conditionally pre-approved and I must call for more details. In the call, the Capital One Customer Rep stated I need to send additional information about my identity to prove that I am the person making the application. 

I have noted that Capital One have accessed my credit file, and made 3 hard inquiries with all 3 credit bureaus. After the inquiry has been made successfully, the credit file security lock was activated again. 

As a response to the request, I have sent few faxes with all documents requested, but with no success received. I have called again multiple times to confirm if my documents were received, but Ive been told the Fax images are not clear and I must send the documents again and again. In total, Ive send 3 different faxes ( in color and black-white ) and also Ive mailed an envelope with copies of my documents. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Capital One has made unauthorized attempts to access my locked credit file, only succeeding with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
The result was my application for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was declined.I am very disappointed with the Capital One and the overall application process for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

I made multiple calls, sent faxes and mail, and lost a lot of time trying to clarify what I was told to be a sure thing. Above all, I am perplexedly disappointed that Capital One made another ( unauthorized ) enquiries on my credit file, without asking my permission. 

I had applied for this credit card in good faith, however it was done under the false pretense that I was " pre-approved '''' - in the end all I have got was 4 hard inquiries and a lot of frustration and time lost. 
Respectfully, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a third application will be favorable, so I called Customer Service. the application is pre-approved and it would be no problem to apply. the representative said it should be no problem');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1914,'02/06/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','I have a bank account with BB & T that I had forgotten about. The account went dormant because it was inactive for one year. I ended moving to a part of the country that does not have any BB & T branches. When I discussed the issue with a customer service representative I was told to write a letter authorizing a friend or relative to go to the branch where the account was created to collect a new debit card and that the dormant status would be removed. I followed their instructions. After my relative took the letter to the branch the staff claimed that the information I had been given was wrong and that I would need to write another letter, have it notarized and send it to the same branch I mentioned before. I write the letter, have it notarized, and send it to the branch. I check the status of the letter on the USPS website and it says it has arrived. A few days pass and I have not heard anything from the BB & T Branch. I call them and a staff member claims that they haven''t received the letter. At this moment it becomes obvious that no one at this branch has checked the mail. When I call him out on this he checks the mail and confirms that the letter has arrived and claims that it is being passed along to someone who can verify it. A different staff member calls me asking me for a picture of my drivers license and I immediately email her a picture of it. A week passes and the status of my dormant account has not changed. I call the branch and they claim that the letter and photo of my ID are still being verified. Another week passes. I call them again and they give me the same story. Several weeks later, account still hasn''t been reactivated. I have spent around {$50.00} to have two letters notarized and shipped across the country and have not gotten any results. BB & T is by far the worst bank I have ever dealt with. This experience has shown me that the company is full of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employees who don''t care about customer service. It seems like they think they can get away with not doing anything and that customers will just give up and stop contacting them. At some point in the near future, I will have to travel cross country to get this matter resolved. This is beyond ridiculous considering it is 2018 and this problem couldn''t be resolved online or over the phone.','BB&T CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a bank account with BB & T went dormant because it was inactive for one year. a relative took the letter to the branch and said the dor');
