INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1929,'02/03/2018','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','On Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I tendered payment on my student loan. I was informed that processing the payment would not occur until Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It was explained to me that Nelnet was unable to accept payment on non-business days. This is a reasonable policy that most business, courts, and other industries follow. Unlike, these other industries Nelnet has decided to continue to toll time against me during the weekend. My due date is Sunday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. As a result, I was informed that even though I tendered payment two days before my " due date '''' I would still be considered late as the payment will not be processed until Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This policy is counterintuitive and unjust. If a loan processor can''t accept payment on the weekend then why do I have a due date on a weekend? The due date should be changed to the next " business '''' day. This seems like a policy that is designed to collect late fees and potential harmful to other individuals. I would like the CFPB to investigate the business practices of student loan processors.','NELNET, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a student loan processor can''t accept payment on the weekend. this policy is counterintuitive and unjust. a student loan processor can''t accept payment on the weekend');
