INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1956,'01/30/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I initiated a domestic wire transfer from my personal checking account at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to the bank of Coinbase, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Coinbase ''s publicly published policy for wired funds is to have it credited within 1-2 business days. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], after checking my Coinbase account and the money was not credited to my account I opened a support case with them through their online support platform. I did not hear back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] until I called their support number on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], waited on hold for almost 2 hours, only to be told my case was escalated to a " wiring specialist ''''. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] there was an update posted to my case by the support rep I spoke to on the phone, but since then there has been absolutely no response from their support team nor has the {$5700.00} USD been credited to my account. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called their bank, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], spoke to someone in their wiring department, and this individual confirmed to me over the phone the funds were received and had been credited to Coinbase ''s " general '''' account and it was now up to Coinbase to credit my account. 

On an almost daily basis since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have requested an update in my support case but no one has responded. 

On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I visited Coinbase ''s bank branch in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. During this visit a representative confirmed to me again that they, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], had received the wired funds and had credited the funds to Coinbase ''s general account but again that it was up to Coinbase to credit my account. 

As of today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 41 days after having sent my wire transfer the funds are still not available to me and there is absolutely no communication from Coinbase on the matter.','Coinbase, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a domestic wire transfer was initiated from my checking account at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the money was not credited to my account and was not credited');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1957,'01/30/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Struggling to repay your loan','Hello, I am back again to discuss Navient. I have been having problems for a while. My federal loans are on a more affordable monthly payment. However I am having problems with the private. I received a letter yesterday from my federal loans demanding the payment of my entire loan in full. I was confused because i had just started the new lower payment program. I called them and they stated that it was past due but later said i was up to date. He then told me it was my private loans. I spoke to the private loan department last month to discuss some options for repayment. The first person i talked to said that they could not lower the interest rate under 7. Her manger then told me he could get it to 1 but for only a short time then it would go back up. Then he presented me with a payment plan that would have been automatic and had other information about the plan he could not email me in writing. They wanted me to listen to a voice automation that was talking so fast that i did not feel comfortable agreeing with the terms. he told me to just keep replaying until you understand!!! I was taught to read before you sign. He made it seem like it was an offer I had to take or would lose it. He kept telling me that he could not email me the document. I cant get anywhere with the private loan side. I would like from them to send me copies of all of my history. I would like to see the original document i signed at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I also would like to receive the document with that payment plan that they could not provide. I strongly felt bullied in that situation. I would like for them to send me the correct info. Are they going to help with my private or are they demanding the money i dont have, and cant borrow. They stopped taking credit card payments but even still at this current time i cant give them the full. My salary is just as much as my loan. I cant switch careers because its hard finding a Job as is. I have been paying on my loan for since 2009 and i just started having issues. 8 years of payments and my loan has gone up.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my federal loans are on a more affordable monthly payment. but I am having problems with the private. i have been paying on my loan for since 2009.');
