INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1967,'01/28/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I filed a complaint about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] aka [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This complaint was forwarded to Equifax ( Case # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Equifax finally responded to this complaint and claims that all of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts have a balance of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on my credit file, they also stated that they were sending a copy of my credit report that reflects all of the accounts are reporting a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance. I have since received this credit report dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the one account question that I am disputing is still showing a balance of {$2500.00} which is opposed to what Equifax claimed in their response to my complaint. I will be attaching the page from my credit report that shows the account in question with a balance of {$2500.00}. 

