INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1989,'01/24/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','The account with simons agency isnt correct. I was in insured at the time and now the hospital says i owe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I gave birth and was completely insured so this is invalid.','Simon’s Agency, Inc',2.0,2.0,'the account with simons agency isnt correct. I gave birth and was insured so this is invalid.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1990,'01/24/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','In my credit report it shows 2 late payment to my mortgage company ( Ditech ) with dates of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. During those times I was on military duty and submitted copies of my orders for that time period. However, it still shows in my credit report and I have requested the company to correct this issue. I submitted the documentation again and I have not heard from them on this issue. Under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] law, I am protected of such things due to not being available at the time of these issues. I have since paid them with the late fees.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'in my credit report it shows 2 late payment to my mortgage company. it shows dates of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] &');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1991,'01/24/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','The credit bureau is refusing to delete a collection account from my credit report that can not be validated. The debt is with a company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$8700.00} and the account number is # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. For the past couple of months, I have been trying to get this company to explain and validate the amount of money they say I owe them. The last time I sent them a written request, it took them over 45 days to respond back to me and even then, they were not able to verify the amount of money they are reporting to my credit. I am filing this complaint because this account is inaccurately being reported to my credit and the credit bureau is not processing my dispute properly.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'debt is with a company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for $8700.00. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1992,'01/24/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Mobile or digital wallet','Problem adding money','I wired [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to coinbase on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/18 so I could purchase coins and trade, but it ''s been 3 weeks as of tomorrow with nothing. The website said the money would be credited same day or next day, but I ''m going on around 20 days now with nothing. I ''ve submitted multiple tickets in hopes that I could get a response, but nothing.','Coinbase, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'the money would be credited same day or next day, but it''s been 3 weeks with nothing. the website said the money would be credited same day or next day ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1993,'01/23/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] present the wrong verification of claim in my chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I over paid in the chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent me a letter out expressed I was just assume to pay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On the last letter Chase expressed I did n''t pay anything besides [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have enclosed my Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] print out to demonstrate what I paid.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent me a letter out expressed I was just assume to pay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the last letter');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1994,'01/23/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','BBVA has erroneously posted an auto loan under my social security number and has caused significant damage to my credit report. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I notified BBVA customer service that an erroneous entry on my credit report showed an auto loan that I did not have. After several phone calls to BBVA they promised a call back but never did. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called BBVA offshore customer service ( in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) which they advised they had confirmed with the auto dealership where the loan was opened, and that the social security number was correct. I knew this was not true, so I asked the rep for the name of the dealership where the auto loan was opened. The BBVA rep gave me the information and I called the dealership and spoke to the finance manager. He confirmed the Social Security was miskeyed by BBVA. I then called back BBVA and advised them of my investigative findings. BBVA promised a call back and I never received one.  Last night the rep stated that I should just get a lawyer, which is a horrible response to solving this problem. I would like to file 1 ) complaint regarding the issue with incorrect SSN displaying on my credit report 2 ) I would like to file a complaint to your executive managers regarding the false investigation that was conducted on your part. 3 ) I would like to file a complaint to your executive managers regarding every representative who promised to call me back but did not. Per FCRA law the item must be removed from my credit report immediately. The customer service that I received from this bank is horrible. All calls are contracted out to a call center in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and their customer service skills are horrible. I am not even a customer and I am glad I am not.','BBVA COMPASS FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'BBVA offshore customer service notified BBVA customer service that an erroneous entry on my credit report showed an auto loan that I did not have. after several phone');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1995,'01/23/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','False statements or representation','This dispute involves [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and their collection subsidiary GC Services Limited Partnership. I entered into a payment plan with GC Services Limited Partnership to reduce my interest rate, waive late fees, and pay off my debt. I was told it was a 27 month program where I paid {$200.00} per month which would cover my balance. At the time of this arrangement I had a past due amount owed. I was told that the past due amount was rolled into the balance and that the payments would cover the past due amount as well as the remaining balance. I checked my credit report however to find that since the arrangement in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have still been receiving late payment reports on my credit report each and every month even though payments have been made each month. I was also told that the program of reduced interest and waived fees only in fact lasts 12 months, not the 27 months I was promised when I agreed to the payment arrangement. None of my {$200.00} payments had gone toward the past due amount. ( i ''ve paid {$1200.00} so far ) the past due amount was {$700.00} approximately so it should be paid at this point. Now I just get passed back and forth between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and this collection service and no one can help me.','GC Services Limited Partnership',2.0,4.0,'dispute involves GC Services Limited Partnership and collection subsidiary. i was told it was a 27 month program where I paid $200.00 per month. the past due');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1996,'01/23/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','TODAYS DATE : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SOC SEC # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ADDRESS [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ATTENTION DISPUTE DEPARTMENT : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$1600.00} Your company have violated FCRA 615 ( f ) ( 15 U.S.C. 1681m ( f ) ) ( f ) Prohibition on sale or transfer of debt caused by identity theft You have not responded to my request to provide me with an investigation report. 
I need this resolve, under the Fair Credit Reporting Act, these disputed items may not appear on my credit report if they can not be supported by any evidence ( 1 ) In general No person ( company ) shall sell, transfer for consideration, or place for collection a debt that such person has been notified under section 1681c-2 of this title has resulted from identity theft. 
( 2 ) Applicability The prohibitions of this subsection shall apply to all persons collecting a debt described in paragraph ( 1 ) after the date of a notification under paragraph ( 1 ). 
( 3 ) Rule of construction Nothing in this subsection shall be construed to prohibit -- ( A ) The repurchase of a debt in any case in which the assignee of the debt requires such repurchase because the debt has resulted from identity theft ; ( B ) the securitization of a debt or the pledging of a portfolio of debt as collateral in connection with a borrowing ; or ( C ) the transfer of debt as a result of a merger, acquisition, purchase and assumption transaction, or transfer of substantially all of the assets of an entity. 
A person that furnishes information to any consumer reporting agency shall have in place reasonable procedures to respond to any notification that it receives from a consumer reporting agency under section 1681c-2 of this title relating to information resulting from identity  theft, to prevent that person from refurnishing such blocked information. 
The reference items are listed below please take this matter very serious [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$1600.00} I have report your company to consumerfinance.gov As a form of record and I am prepare to sue your company Example In re [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Telephone Consumer Protection Act Litigation, Case No. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], in the U.S. District Court for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] District of California Stop collection proceedings against me Signatures on applications and accounts Investigators report [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SOC SEC # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ADDRESS [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Commonwealth Financial Systems, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a company has violated the fCRA 615 ( f) and is prohibited from selling, transfer or transfer of debt caused by identity theft. the prohibitions of this subsection');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1997,'01/23/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','False statements or representation','I want to begin by saying thank you for providing a wonderful service to consumers where their voice can be heard against unscrupulous creditors and their horrendous tactics against consumers. I also want to state that I am an honest person and will admit that I did fall on hard times and failed to pay Bank of America money that I charged on one of their credit cards a few years back. This complaint I am filing is not about whether Bank of America was owed money but rather their misleading representations, bait and switch tactics, and their continual to simply waste everyone ''s time and not deliver on promises they made simply in an attempt to extort money out of me. 

To give you more clarity on the situation, I began contacting Bank of America in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In the ensuing conversation I informed B of A that I was aware I had defaulted on them and was now in a position to attempt to make amends. Unfortunately, I was not able to pay them in full and was hoping to come to an arrangement with them. After some discussion, B of A and I agreed to a lump sum settlement of {$750.00} on a {$1200.00} balance due by the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was content and so were they. However, as an informed consumer, I asked if they could forward me the agreement in writing so the agreement was documented. B of A agreed and I gave them my address so they could forward me the letter. And although they technically did send the letter, they sent it to a wrong address. Instead of using the address I gave them, they simply used a previous address that was in their system a few years back. When the letter was forwarded to me a month later, the deal had already expired weeks back ... 

I then called Bank of America on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I received the letter but I was n''t able to get through to a representative for 2 days so I waited until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to try again. Remember, the agreement had expired on the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which was 13 days prior to me receiving any documentation. I finally reached a representative by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I had informed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of what had transpired and that I still wanted the settlement offer to go trough and was simply asking for the offer in writing with a non-expired date to protect myself. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] seemed very annoyed and took down my correct address but I was no longer confident in her by the way she used her tone with me and her responses towards me. It was as if I was inconveniencing her even though I was literally telling her all I needed was something in writing and I would happily pay them on the spot. I then asked if it was possible for them to either e-mail me or fax me a settlement letter so I could simply pay them right then and there instead of waiting for another letter. After much griping she finally agreed to send it to me by fax. I gave her the fax number and she said I would have it within 24 hours. I did n''t receive it within 24 hours. I did n''t receive it at all. 

I called a few days later and would never reach the same representative and was even hung up on twice. I explained the same situation to the representatives who did answer and asked for a fax with a settlement offer as was promised. I would always get the same answer that it was coming. Both by mail and by fax. I would never receive it. Finally I decided to stop worrying about it until after the Hollidays. If bank of America was not desperate to obtain money owed to them I was not going to spend my Hollidays worrying about giving it to them. Keep in mind that all calls about this debt and this settlement were initiated by me. NEVER did I receive one phone call from B of A about this just to show who is interested in resolving this debt. 

After the new year I decided to call Bank of America and see if I could get this resolved once and for all. I called them on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I first reached a representative by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Texas and this is when " all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] broke loose. '''' [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was very cordial and very soft spoken and seemed like he was going to simply resolve the situation once and for all but then tried to pull a fast one on me. He said I ''ll go ahead and send you a fax right now but I need your cell phone number so we can send you a confirmation text. I sensed some skulduggery happening so I simply refused and asked for the fax so I could pay them but he said " just a minute, who is your employer? At this point I knew he was not trying to help me and was pulling a bait and switch tactic. I told him that I was upset and that I was not a fool and was not going to give him the name of my employer. The only reason they would ask for that was so they could sue me. I wanted to speak to a supervisor instead and he then transferred me to a representative in the collections department so they could give me " the letter right away ''''. 

I then spoke to a representative in the collections department. Unfortunately, I then had to get transferred to the recoveries department ... I then reach a representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I have to do the same dance that I ''ve been doing with everybody since my agreement in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I simply wanted a settlement offer in writing and I gave her the same deal I gave everybody else over these past 5 months. I will pay you on the spot if you could simply provide me with the letter. I was getting very sick and tired of being given the run around and everything I was being put trough was the exact reason why I wanted a letter in the first place because they obviously were not trustworthy and I could n''t take anybody at their word since every representative I ''ve spoken to up to this point had lied to me. She said faxing letters was possible and that it would take 24-48 business hours for it to arrive. I said great, no problem. She then back pedaled and began trying to question why I wanted a settlement in the first place. Wait WHAT! 

I asked her that I had already negotiated a settlement months back and that they knew my circumstances and hence why the agreement was reached. I told her I had been on this phone call for a ridiculous amount of time just to simply obtain a letter that was promised to me for months. ( The phone call ended after 58 minutes and 1 second ) She then started trying to place blame on me asking why I waited so long to call back to fulfill the settlement agreement. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then went and said that they ca n''t submit a settlement letter since the original agreement had not been fulfilled and that they would have to see if they could even offer me a settlement ... I had enough at this point. I asked for a supervisor immediately. 

I was then transferred to a supervisor by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Again I gave her the entire ordeal and explained to her everything that has happened since the beginning. She also feigned surprise as had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] earlier when I told them I did not appreciate them asking for my employer information instead of providing a settlement letter as promised for 5 months now. She apologized profusely and again feigned sincerity but in the end she gave me the same excuses as to why she will not provide a settlement letter. She too tried to blame me for not fulfilling the settlement even though she was aware B of A sent the letter to an address I had not lived at for years and I was fortunate to even receive the notice nearly 2 weeks after the agreement had expired ... The fact that I attempted to reach out to them on numerous occasions and provided my address, e-mail address, and fax to receive another letter did n''t seem to matter. They were more interested in shutting me down and place blame on me then actually trying to collect their money and fulfill their promise to me. She even went as far as saying they ca n''t fax settlement letters even though every representative before her said they could.. 

In the conversation I caught her in many lies and obviously she was not even trying to help me but just appease me. In fact, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me she ca n''t offer a 50 % settlement offer again. I told her that was not the terms of the agreement. She then said I ''m sorry 56 %. I was even more upset as that was n''t the term either. She did n''t even know what was being offered to me or what the terms of the settlement were! I told her {$750.00} on {$1200.00} was not 50 % or even 56 %. She said I ''m sorry I was told it was {$700.00}. She then said " your right that it was 60 %. '''' She even said " I ''m sorry in a condescending tone and said " there are no notes for me on this account '''' SERIOUSLY! NO NOTES AFTER 5 MONTHS OF CONVERSING WITH MULTIPLE REPRESENTATIVES INCLUDING THREE PRIOR IN THIS PHONE CALL! Again, this entire ordeal was a farce and Bank of America was trying to extort me for money by pulling bait and switch tactics. There were many more things that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said which were lies but for the sake of not wasting any more time I will simply say that she lied on many occasions, said " i ''m sorry '''' in a condescending tone at least 4 times when I presented her with facts that caught her in a lie and her company ''s blatant disregard for me. 

This has been the single most horrifying experience I ''ve had with a creditor and I ''ve had it. Unfortunately, bank of America is also holding me hostage. Because this debt is unpaid, my credit report shows that I owe Bank of America and this will hinder any future creditors I deal with until 7 years pass and the debt falls off my credit report. This will cause me to be denied for credit and have less favorable terms with creditors who do extend credit to me. Furthermore, the report only shows what Bank of America chooses to show. It does n''t reflect that I have been single-handedly trying to pay them their money according to the terms they agreed upon. It also does n''t reflect that they have been lying to me and attempting to extort me for money on false and empty promises. It does n''t reflect the grueling amount of time and the mistreatment I have been put trough by Bank of America when I am simply trying to pay them. It is unfair and is completely not reflective of what is being reported on my credit report. At this point I would contend that their reporting of this account on my credit report is a violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act as well as the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act. This account is not being reported accurately as I have done everything in my power to get them to fulfill their end of the agreement so I can pay them their money based on the terms they agreed to. Please help me and publish this so that people know even to this day Bank of America is still trying to bully their customers and acting in shameful ways. In the meantime I am going to contemplate on whether I should retain council as this is actually causing me harm and preventing me from moving on with my life.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a complaint is about whether Bank of America was owed money. it is not about their misleading representations, bait and switch tactics. they are continuing to simply waste everyone''s');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1998,'01/23/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','I keep getting theses Low APR Balance Transfer promotions at 0 % ( especially with my own Bank of America ). The fine print reads they will charge a 4 % transaction fee for balance transfers. To me the 4 % should be included in the APR. Here ''s a copy of what I saw : Low APR Balance Transfer 0.00 % promotional APR until XX/XX/XXXXon balance transfers completed byXX/XX/XXXXAfter that, 10.49 % a variable APR based on the U.S. Prime Rate The transaction fee for balance transfers is 4 % ( Min. {$10.00} )','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a 4 % transaction fee should be included in the APR. the transaction fee for balance transfers is $4 %.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(1999,'01/23/2018','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] billed me for services I did n''t authorize Since day one I asked for proof of authorization and I will gladly pay this off. All they have is an itemized bill that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] made up and sent to them. No signatures or anything on mybehalf. 

I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] today. She is a manager in the billing department and the one who has been handling my case. 
She let me know that as of today they only have an itemized bill. This has been the case since day one. 
She always states that they requested proof of authorization from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] office and they are still waiting for it. I asked if theres a timeline or deadline given to their office and she said no. 
So I am just supposed to allow this to remain on my credit for as long as they want to i guess. 

I called back and asked to speak to another manager. They connected me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] @ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] He provided me with a record of dates of when I called. ( listed Below ) He then said that I needed to write a written letter within 30 days of them receiving my file which was on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to let them know I ''m contesting it. But if you look at the dates, I called 2 days after it was submitted to their office and no one let me know about this written protocol. 

I ''ve always been told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that once the Dr office can not prove authorization then all negative marks on my credit will be removed. 


XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Date claim received at Capital Accounts Calls by me to Capital accounts for updates and information XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Capital Accounts [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Letters can be sent to : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] TN [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Initial billed amount : {$2500.00} Current amount due : {$2700.00} Collection sent from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Capital Accounts, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a manager in the billing department has been handling my case. she always states that they requested proof of authorization from their office. she said that they are still waiting for it.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2000,'01/22/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I was told that What they had was accurate when i never made thise inquiries and the false address wad never removed. I have never been to Arizona so I know I should n''t have an address there. The numerous inquiries made by multiple agencies wo n''t be removed. Also late fees for things that are inaccurate.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the false address wad never removed. the numerous inquiries made by multiple agencies were inaccurate.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2001,'01/22/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Fees or interest','I had made a purchase and signed up for a store credit card at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I was travelling to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NV ; however, I never received the credit card and statement after that. Few months later, I got a call on my cell phone from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], saying that I had a past due. I told the lady that I never received neither the credit card nor the statement. She told me that I need to wait for the next credit card statement and she could not email me the statement. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Store and paid cash for the transaction. By the time I received the credit card statement, I had three months '' late fee accumulated. 
I have the feeling that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is proposely not sending the first statement to initiate the late fee from the credit card holder. When the time I found out I had a past due, I told them to email me the credit card statement, so I can make the online payment ; they said they did not email out credit card statement. I told them I got it all the time from other banks. I have called the bank this morning ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), they said they had record of sending out monthly statement with postal office proof, so they ca n''t waive any later fee.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'a credit card statement was sent out to the store. the statement was sent out by the bank. the statement was sent out with postal office proof.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2002,'01/22/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','When I first applied for this credit they offered a promise to charge no interest for the first year. As soon as I received my first months billing statement they denied me their promise of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] interest for the first year, and so on in every months statement from then on. 
In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I made a full payment on the balance of about {$10000.00}, and after I finished paying the full balance i was sent on the following months bill a balance of {$100.00}, without me having made any purchases. I ended up paying that, and continued to use the card. 
