XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - I received an alert that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] delivered the check to the landlord, 17 days after it was due. At this point, my brother had been evicted and I ''d already been forced to make payments in another method to the landlord for the first 10 days that my brother lived in the house. I called Capital One and asked why the manager had not asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to return to sender ( the manager had called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke with them but did not request the check be intercepted or returned. According to the notes this manager took in Capital One ''s system, he mentioned nothing about my request to get [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to return the check to sender ). I asked the Capital One customer service rep to file a complaint with Capital One ''s customer service department that this manager had not honored a simple customer request and this failure has cost me {$650.00} and requested that they review the recorded call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which proves my request. 
Capital One failed to act on multiple accounts to try to help me as a customer avoid this loss of {$650.00} and did not act at all to get [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to return the check. They basically ignored my pleas to help me so that I would not lose this money. This is in addition to the fact that the delay in the check delivery was not my fault and caused by their vendor and partner, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and therefore they should be responsible for the damage it caused me and should have acted quickly to help me.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'cashier''s check from his account was cancelled. he was told the cashier''s check had been cancelled. he was told the original cashier ''');
