[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Account Number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Transunion : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- Account Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Account Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'someone has been applying for credit using my personal information without my authorization and consent. someone has also opened a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit account. no');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2024,'01/18/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','I contacted Wells Fargo Bank today [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017, to provide additional evidence to support my case in a large purchase I made, for which the merchant did not provide. I was told there is nothing more I can do and that after arbitration, there is no more appeal process. What frustrates me is that on multiple occasions, when this bank has decided a dispute in my favor, they have come back and changed their minds. However, in a large transaction, where the merchant did not perform the service they promised, my bank is refusing to help me. They are refusing to accept new evidence and are saying there is nothing further I can do. The bank ''s dispute process and arbitration is biased toward businesses and they are not advocating for their customers, as they promise. Furthermore, in the initial consultation, I was never told this dispute was going to arbitration. Instead, I was told by the dispute analyst, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that all I needed to get was an invoice or an estimate from another merchant to show the service was not as expected ; yet the dispute was still decided against me. I was not given full disclosure to the magnitude of this process and now, after reaching out a second merchant for definitive proof that I did not get the service I was charged for, the bank is still refusing to help me with this. I filed a complaint earlier about this matter in the previous evidence. This new complaint is about the fact that my bank is refusing to accept the new evidence I am presenting and they are retaliating against me for filing the original CFPB complaint. I have been a Wells Fargo customer for years and it is shameful that they are treating me like this. This transaction is worth 1 full month of my paycheck and my bank is helping this other business rob me of my money.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a dispute analyst told me that the merchant did not provide the service. he says the bank is refusing to help me with the dispute process. he says the bank is');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2025,'01/18/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I enrolled both of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to begin getting myself out of debt in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Both accounts were current and I was advised by my counselor to stop making payments, as they would be made on my behalf through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. {$150.00} and {$66.00} respectively were paid to the accounts in both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( proof attached ). The amount paid to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not cover the full [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment, and this resulted in a late status being posted to my credit reports for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was informed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that the accounts would " re-age '''' in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that the late status for those three months would be removed from my report. This has not occurred. I would like for the late payment status to be removed for the months of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for both accounts.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'both accounts were current and I was advised by my counselor to stop making payments. the amount paid to both accounts did not cover the full payment. this resulted in a late');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2026,'01/18/2018','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','This is a follow-up to previous complaint # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] against Specialized Loan Servicing, LLC. 

After over a month of trying to get the amount due to reinstate our mortgage, we finally thought we were making progress. However, more obstacles were put up by SLS. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Saturday afternoon ), we received a letter in the mail from SLS giving us the payoff amount to reinstate our mortgage. The date on the letter was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the postmark on the envelope was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( meaning the letter was held for a full week before mailing ). The expiration date on the payoff was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( a national holiday ). This made it impossible for us to wire the payment on time, as the banks were closed during this entire amount of time. ( payoff statement attached ) Then, on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we received an email from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( representing SLS ). This email had a completely different reinstatement payoff amount ( and to them, instead of SLS ), but the payoff expiration was for the VERY SAME DAY ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). We immediately called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to get the correct payment amount, so that we could immediately get to the bank and make payment ... [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told us not to make the payment until he got back to us with the correct amount ... He never got back to us. ( emailed payoff statement attached ) On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but they did not have any new information. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to again attempt to get payoff amount. Talked with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who told us that the expiration date had passed, payment would not be accepted. She said she would contact SLS to get approval despite date. She emailed SLS multiple times, but did not get a response. She said she ''d get back to us. 

Same day ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) we called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who transferred the call to Customer Resolution. They transferred us to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who told us he would figure it out ... Put on hold ... He came back and confirmed our information, then put on hold again for nearly an hour. Transferred multiple times before speaking with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He said he had no idea what to do. Transferred call to Executive Service Team and put on hold for another [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mins. Finally spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who agreed that the expiration date on the payoff was too short. She transferred us to another department for another reinstatement quote. Spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], again put on hold for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mins. while he reviewed loan. Were told that a new reinstatement quote would have to be submitted. We were told that the new quote would be available on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and that they would mail it. We were also told that if we called on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we could get amount over the phone. We will call back on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

PLEASE HELP US! This endless cycle is now beginning again. When we call back on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we assume, like last month, we will not be able to get a correct amount, and by the time we do, it will be too late. We can only assume at this point that SLS is purposely delaying and planning on assigning a foreclosure date. We have never seen such a level of deceit and/or ineptitude. We have spent countless hours on the phone. We are staying diligent, trying to save our home, but can only assume that others going through what we are, could be giving up all hope. 

I have attached the quotes from both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SLS..','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',8.0,8.0,'a letter from SLS gave us the payoff amount to reinstate our mortgage. the date on the letter was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMP');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2027,'01/18/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I purchased a pair of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] audio headphones. After using them, I was n''t satisfied with some of the features such as sound quality and noise cancellation. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], well within the 30-day return period, I proceeded to the store to return the item. I was then told I was not allowed to return the headphones. When I inquired as to why, I was told that I had made " too many returns '''' and could not return merchandise for 1 year. I was given a slip with the name of the third-party vendor that BestBuy utilizes to monitor return activity. Nowhere is such information listed on their receipt, or in the store. The merchandise was functional and completely returned in the original packaging. When working with the BestBuy Executive Resolution Specialist, follow up was by coincidence slow to intentionally ensure if I were able to return the item, I would miss the 30-day window. After demanding an update, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] informed me that she was unable to lift the blackout of returns and offered me a {$100.00}. At that time, I advised how disgusted I was with the treatment and felt that since this was the best customer service I could get, I ''d take the gift card. HOWEVER, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], denied my acceptance of the offer, and instead informed that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   that I declined. Per the documentation, that is an outright fabrication. This return policy is deceptive. We as consumers do n''t have any idea that our purchases and returns are even being monitored. Let alone, that we only have limited capability to truly determine if we ''re satisfied with the purchase. This policy is well hidden and extremely convoluted leaving a consumer to feel as if they do n''t have rights. This is an unfair and deceptive business practice employed by BestBuy. First, as an Elite member,  we are given 60 days to make returns based on the volume of purchases. Secondly, as a BestBuy credit cardholder or Elite Member, they NEVER disclose that they track purchases based on your e-mail or account information to limit the amount of returns you can make. So while BestBuy has their " general '''' return policy posted in stores, what they do n''t advertise is that they have two separate return policies in place that greatly limits the consumer ability to fairly choose whether a product is right for them. Therefore, I demand that Best Buy honor their offer of providing a gift card, as well as lift the " blackout '''' of no returns from my account immediately.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'a pair of headphones were returned within 30-day return period. the product was functional and completely returned in the original packaging. the return policy is deceptive, leaving a consumer');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2028,'01/17/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Experian, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not fix an error on my credit report. The contract was canceled by the company.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'the contract was canceled by the company. the contract was canceled by the company.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2029,'01/17/2018','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','For ten days I have been trying to get modification doucemnts from Union Home Mortgage. The first time they said would take about 48 hours to be email. Nothing happened within this time frame. I called back and it was stated the request was never put in. This has been going back forth for 10 days. It has to be requested and then I was told it could not be email. I gave them a fax number to fax it to and still they are saying it will take 48 hours for the request to go through. Today X/XX/2017 I called again trying to get the documents and was informed of the soame 48 hours request to be sent. I spoke with a supervisor and got the samething and never got to the right person. It was never the modification department. I was informed that the modification department does not take phone calls. They only do modification.','Union Home Mortgage Corp',2.0,2.0,'the request was never put in and it has been going back forth for 10 days. it has to be requested and then I was told it could not be email. the modification department does');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2030,'01/17/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I initially began disputing this account with each of the credit bureaus in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The responses from the bureaus reflected that this account entry was verified. I sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s a letter ( see attached ) in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], requesting that they investigate this account. My formal request included informing them that each of the 3 bureau reflected a different charge off date. This was the first inaccuracy. Additionally, I requested that they submit a payment history of the account as well as the accounting ledger they maintained that reflects all payments made. Too, this would verify that the amount alleged as owed is indeed accurate and more importantly, it would reflect when this account was charged off as well as if [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s wrote the account off as a profit and loss. 

I received documentation from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( see attached ) which was over a year old from when I actually submitted a dispute. How then was this company able to send me a letter dated for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when my initial dispute to them was in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? As reflected on the letter, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( as signed ) stated this response she provided was based on my inquiry, yet as I have mentioned, I only requested this information in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It appears this letter is backdated in order for them to cover up the fact that they are violating my consumer rights. Included within this letter was a check dated for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. If this was the only payment made, then why did they not provide me a clear registry that reflects this. Also, they again did NOT honor my request to prove that the balance they are alleging I owe is accurate, timely and verifiable. 

What is the actual charge off date? Where are the summaries of payment history for this account? What does the general ledger account reflect for this account? All of this requested information should be housed with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s and provided to me upon request. It ''s obvious this company can not substantiate their reporting as the FDCPA outlines as well as the FCRA ; therefore, this entry must be DELETED!','Colony Brands, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a letter from the credit bureaus reflected that this account entry was verified. the letter was dated for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONY');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2031,'01/17/2018','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I was a victim of serious Identity Theft, I was out of the country for several years, as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in a 3rd world country. I have a Issue with KOHLS department store, they open the 1st account in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I was able to get an alert and I had them to close it because I was out of the country. Kohls refuse to remove that account even with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance. I want it removed it does not belong to me. Kohls department store then open a 2nd credit card in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] someone racked up {$910.00} dollars of Identity theft credit card fraud. I sent police reports once I made it back to the united states, I even got the attorney generals office involved. they refuse to take it off I been fighting to close it from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I saw the 2nd Kohls account. The Company has been very sketchy, I do n''t want my credit profile to say it meets federal code or what ever they are putting on my report. this account was not open by me. I had fraud alert and no accounts should have been open without calling the phone number on file. this is against the ; law. I want this account to be removed from all credit burials and my reputation be restored. I have been treated worse than human when I call and it looks like Kohls is the place  to open fraud accounts, might be a inside job.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a u.s. attorney general has been involved in the case. a u.s. attorney general has been involved in the case. a u.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2032,'01/17/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Student loans sold many of my private loans to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. While looking at my credit report I see several " payments '''' made to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I never made, therein extending the reporting period on my credit report. These payments appear to be a direct result of the transfer between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and therefore should not be represented on my credit report. 

I have NEVER made a payment to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so I tried contacting the company through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have made several complaints with the Better Business Bureau. To date [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has not given me any  information on the alleged " payment '''' that were made by me through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] besides some graphs that could ''ve been made in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. None of the items furnished even have an account number so it is impossible to link them to my account. I argued that if these payments were made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should be able to furnish proof of these payments via EFT confirmations, voided checks, etc however they refuse to give me any information.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] student loans sold many of my private loans to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I never made. these payments');
