When I got my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement in early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I saw that Chase billed me for the two unsuccessful payment attempts to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] confirmed via email ( dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) that they only received one payment for this transaction, the one on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for which they previously sent me a receipt as stated above. I immediately submitted a dispute for the two transactions ( attachments were not allowed ). Soon after ( date unknown ), I received a phone call from Chase and was verbally told that they would issue a credit for one of the transactions because it was clearly a duplicate charge. That credit appeared on my XX/XX/XXXXstatement issued in early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and is the only credit of any sort that has been issued to date. I was also told that I would need to provide a copy of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill via their online email interface to validate the payment via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] before the second [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge could be credited to my account. I provided a copy of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill ( Email dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Chase contacted me again by phone in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( exact date unknown ) and claimed they never received the copy of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill, so I resubmitted it ( Email dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Both emails are still available in my Chase mailbox for them to review and Chase has sent confirmation of the receipt of both emails. 

As stated above, Chase has only refunded one of the two erroneous charges. They have refused to refund the second charge ( letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), claiming that they talked to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] confirmed that they were paid for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] membership. This is true ; however they were paid by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], not Chase. Furthermore, their rejection letter indicates that they intend to reverse the credit they previously issued so that I will still be charged for BOTH erroneous items even though [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never received either payment. 

This is all deliberate theft by Chase.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a card issued in early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] confirmed that the payment was made using the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card.');
