INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2063,'01/11/2018','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','My father and aunt had a joint account with Santander Bank that funded a safety deposit box. Both of the people have since passed and I returned the safety deposit box keys.i have also written Santander multiple letters stating the box was closed, the keys were returned and both of the people on the account are dead. not only are they still trying to collect, but they are no billing me for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]!!! They will NOT STOP trying to bill me for something I rectified and communicated to them YEARS AGO! they are trying to assess a late fee on me too. if they stopped ignoring my letters this would have been done away with two ( 2 ) years ago when I closed the account! I feel harrassed since they ignore my letters and are now trying to charge me with late fees and now billing me for another year when they [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] well know BOTH ACCOUNT HOLDERS ARE [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]! [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 7 years and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 3 years! Come on!!!','SANTANDER BANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'both of the people on the account have passed and I returned the keys. they are still trying to collect, but they are no billing me until XX/XX/[COM');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2064,'01/11/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','An account was opened and closed the same day with Barclays Bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. But an order for an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] computer went through the next day. The company sent the bill to the wrong address, the unlisted/unregistered house address instead of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] given. They started calling my work so much that the secretary said stop calling. She later notified me and I checked my credit report. It was on there as a negative late. I called and they argued asking if I purchased the computer. When I demanded they remove the late for or I would not pay, they said no problem. I asked for a letter payment date because of my job, the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they said okay. The next month the late fee was still there. I called. They said they changed it but I had to file a complaint with the credit reporting agencys and they would remove it. It was just a ploy to get me to admit to having purchased the product. I filed but then my mortgage broker said remove the dispute. So I did to find another late on the credit report. I called them and again they said they had removed it and the fees. They did remove the fees to my account but Only one late mark on my credit report! One late mark remains even though they credited my account and said they would fix it all. I have spoke with several representatives, the last was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who all but one stated they had been and would remove the late marks, it just takes time for the credit bearues to update the information. Yet, they still have not been removed. I recently resubmitted as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stayed to do so that it would be sure to come off and be updated. 
Yet, the results were verified and updated, which is not removed. They also lowered my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account with them due to the credit score changed by them. It is the only late mark on my 25+ years in the system! Honestly, the worst company I have ever dealt with in my life. They are crooks that will weasel every dollar!','BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE',2.0,2.0,'the company sent the bill to the wrong address instead of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] given. the secretary said stop calling and she checked my credit report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2065,'01/11/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Closing your account','This is in reference to my original complaint regarding our Capital One credit card that was closed in error by Capital One. Please refer to our original complaint cfpb [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

We first contacted Capital One about their error on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we received a letter requesting a street address for my wife. We contacted Capital One on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and provided the street address. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Captial One provided two new credit cards as promised with a XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] expiration date. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we were notified that our credit card account had been closed because we did n''t provide the information that was requested ( we did by phone on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 

After dealing with an estimated 19 to 25 representatives from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], nothing has been accomplished with one exception. We got a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( employee #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) at Capital One ''s corporate office on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and he acknowledged to us on the phone that Capital One had made an error which was responsible for the cancelling of our account. I asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a letter from Capital One to confirm that their error was responsible for the cancellation of our credit card account ( open since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said he would see if a letter could be sent to us acknowledging their mistake. He also said we could reapply for an account. We said we did n''t want to reapply for an account, just have the old account reopened. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that they do n''t send out letters regarding mistakes until the account has been reopened. It we reapply for the account, and for whatever reason the account is not reopened, they do n''t send out a letter acknowledging their mistake. It ''s now been 3 weeks since we last heard from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the Capital One Executive Offices. 

In a nutshell, we ''re done. We will not conduct business with an organization that has sloppy record keeping, poorly trained customer service reps, dishonest customer service reps, offer unprofessional treatment to long term customers and have absolutely no sense of urgency. Fortunately, we have other long term credit card accounts and we will remain faithful to those companies. As for Capital One, we ''re done playing this endless, fruitless game of nonsense. We are no longer interested in doing business with this unprofessional banking organization. 

I would suggest that people who are thinking about doing business with Capital One, think twice. We ''ll never go back!','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a letter from capital One requesting a street address was sent. on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we received a');
