INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2092,'01/06/2018','Mortgage','Home equity loan or line of credit (HELOC)','Struggling to pay mortgage','To Whom It May Concern : I am writing this letter to inform you of the deplorable customer service and the unfair and deceptive acts and/or practices of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] concerning my Loan Modification application. I believe that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] managers are not treating my Loan Modification application fairly as well as committing due process violations because I have a bankruptcy that has been discharged. 

On Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I applied for a Loan Modification of my second mortgage thru [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Housing Counselor Supervisor, ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). This option was chosen because my loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was maturing on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The balloon amount that was due at that time would be {$31000.00} of which I could not pay so I applied for a Loan Modification. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] completed the necessary paperwork and faxed it to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Loss Mitigation Department on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] received the paperwork indicating my intent to keep my home and apply for the modification on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to get a status update on my loan application and spoke with Account Representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). He stated that I did not qualify for a loan modification and that a promissory note would be a better option for me, since my payments would be applied to the principal. I said ok. So he then told me what documents were needed to complete the process and that he could email or mail me a cash flow template that was needed to be completed. However, I was still expecting a letter of explanation for the denial of my loan modification application, along with other options that were available to me to be mailed. 

On Thursday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called to speak with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to see if he could email me the cash flow template. He said that he would email it but I did not receive it. 

On Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called and spoke with Account Representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about my account because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was not available. Since I did not receive the cash flow template, I asked if he could email it to me and he did. Later that evening, I faxed all the necessary paperwork back to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for review. 

From this point on, it has now become a cat and mouse game. I would call [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to get an update on my application and would not be able to get through to their line, getting a recording stating that my call could not be completed as dialed and that I would have to try my call back later, or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was not available, or when I did reach him, he would state that he did not get a chance to review my application. So I kept calling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to get a status update on my promissory note application on several occasions. All while still waiting for my letter of explanation for the denial of my loan modification application, along with other options that were available to me in the mail. It never came. Please note that I made these calls from my cellphone that keeps record of the date and how many times I called a number. 

On Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and the line was busy.

On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the line was busy.

On Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice.

On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice.

On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 14  times. I believe that I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] concerning the cash flow template for the Promissory Note. He stated that it was inaccurate and needed to be corrected. I corrected it and faxed it back to him later that evening. 

On Thursday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the line was busy. 

On Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] four  times. 

On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] four  times. 

On Tuesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice. 

On Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice. 

On Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me at home @ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He told me that he finally had a chance to go over my paperwork and stated that because of my income I would have to pay a down payment of {$15000.00}. I simply explained to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I could not afford that. I am finally getting back on my feet from battling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and getting back into the workforce. He then asked me what down payment could I make? I told him none. At this point, I am perturbed to say the least because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never told me that I had to make a down payment when I spoke with him concerning my loan modification application on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. So then I asked him why was I denied a loan modification and he stated that it was because of my account. He also stated that I was behind in payments. I then asked him if they were trying to foreclose on my home. His answer was not encouraging. So I asked him why didnt I receive a letter explaining this denial because I know for a fact the paperwork was sent to his bank in XX/XX/XXXXand that I can surely confirm this fact. He then stated they did receive my paperwork on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; but that I needed to use their loan application in order of applying for a loan modification. I stated that that was ridiculous because they could have mailed me the application especially since my paperwork clearly stated my intent to keep my home and apply for a loan modification. 

At this point, I asked him for the name and number of his superior. He said his name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He stated that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was fully aware of the situation. So I told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that if that is the case, then I would be making a formal complaint to the CFPB. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then stated that he knows that our call is being recorded and that he didnt want to say the wrong thing. He then stated that he would send his superior an email about seeing what he could do about lowering the amount of the down payment for the promissory note. He assured me that they were not foreclosing on my home and that he would work out something for my account. I told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I could not afford to pay a down payment. He stated that he was going on vacation and would be back early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and would get in touch with me then. 

On Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the line was busy.

