On Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me and left a message to return her call. I called her back and explained the situation with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to her. She stated that I did not qualify for a loan modification and that my home is not in foreclosure. I also told her that I could not pay a down payment. She then stated that she would reassign my case to someone else to handle. I asked her when I should expect a call from my new representative, and she said next week. I never received a call. 

On Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the line was busy. 

On Thursday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] while sitting in the office of my Housing Counselor, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as we were trying to find out the status of my application for my second mortgage. So I called to speak with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to find out why my new rep never called me back. But she wasnt available. So I told the rep that I would like a loan modification packet sent to me. He asked for my account number and stated that he had to transfer me the right department. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] came on the line and I again requested that a loan modification packet be sent to me. She refused. She stated that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is working on a Promissory Note with a lower down payment for me. She asked if I could make a {$500.00} upfront payment, and told her maybe. However, I told her that I would prefer a loan modification, and that I felt like they are cornering me into a promissory note agreement. She then stated that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would be back on Monday, but Account Representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would call me tomorrow to go over my account with me. I said fine ; but, at this point, I would be alerting the CFPB. She said fine. Account Representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never called me. 

