INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2116,'01/02/2018','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Incorrect information on your report','Chase Account number beginning [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] appears on all 3 credit reports as purportedly " late '''' with a payment in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That is inaccurate. At the time, I requested a new closing date on the Chase account to coincide with other closing dates such that I can make payments to all my credit cards at one time instead of scattered through a month. I was informed by phone that the closing date was changed, and payment was made by the new due date in a timely manner. However, it was n''t until one month later that I was informed the payment made in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was considered " late '''' because the new closing date would not go into effect until the following month, i.e., exactly the opposite of what I was told by phone. The problem with the credit report is that there is no way I can " prove a negative '''' in the sense that it was a recorded conversation but, I do not believe any of the the 3 credit reporting companies were provided the correct information by Chase with no evidence of the recording ( which Chase tells you at the beginning of any customer service conversation is recorded ), thereby leaving me to no fair opportunity to properly dispute the so-called late payment or prove it is incorrect. The account has since been closed and paid in full.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'Chase Account number beginning appears on all 3 credit reports as " late ''''. the payment was made in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2117,'01/02/2018','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I called NAVIENT regarding the two account ( s ) on which I am co-signer in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On two occasions I was given different information regarding accrued interest fees and late fees. I made a payment and was advised that all accounts were " up to date '''', only to learn that there were still outstanding late fees. This impacts my ability to keep the loans " in good standing '''' for other re-payment programs. 
Also, I was deceived into thinking that my daughter would receive a lower interest rate on her loans if I called and updated my personal and financial information. It became clear to me that NAVIENT simply wanted my updated information so that garnishing wages could take place for both me and my daughter, if necessary Customer service made no attempt to reduce her interest rate. 
Our interest rates are " variable '''', but there have never been any adjustments in lowering them when the federal interest rates were lowered over the past 7 years. 
Finally, my daughter is now in " interest only '''' payments which still allows the high interest rates on the loans to grow exponentially. Her loans have doubled since she took them out.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'a co-signer in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called NAVIENT regarding the two accounts. I made a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2118,'01/02/2018','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Payday loan','Struggling to pay your loan','I was approved for and received a small loan from CashNetUSA. This is not my first time to receive a loan from this company. The problem is I work for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where unexpectedly I ended up filing a Discrimination and Equal Pay Rights complaint agaist the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that made it as far as the Hearing level. This has been a very intense case that took over 2 years to come to a settlement agreement. This was done just recently. Unfortunately I was placed on extended leave due to stress and once I no longer had leave on the books I no longer was receiving an income! I contacted CashNetUSA multiple times explaining my situation and that I take full responsibility of my debt to the company but have no way whats so ever to continue making payments until my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] case was over. I ensured CashNet that even if I lost the case I would be retiring receiving a full annuity after 38 years with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Im finally going to receive a settlement amount and will start receiving my retirement so I will be able to take care of all financial obligations. 
My problem is with the interest this loan company is charging me for a small loan where something came up preventing pay day payments from being paid. During the time this hearing process has take until I signed an agreed Settlement amount I lost my home of 20 years, my car and just about everything I owen trying to survive as a single parent with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] boys and no income on top of surviving the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] thats thrown at you every time you ask for help! There is only one process available to an employee that is set up to support management. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has its own way of handling employees who are a threat to upper management. 
Because I was very informative keeping CashNet up to date with my lawsuit by writing letters, email and discussions on the phone, in an effort to avoid the high interest rates Im being charged. My total balance now is almost 3 times more then the amount borrowed. I have a feeling because this falls under their contract that Im going to be stuck paying the full amount including all interest during the 2 year waiting period. All said and done, Is there any kind of protection to individuals getting this type of loan that fall under the circumstances I have explained preventing me from making Pay day payments? I have another loan with a different company that is also a small pay day loan that has already sued me. I dont even know what the out come of that law suit even is. 
The hearing process for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] employee is absolutely ridiculous the way it is set up forcing the employee to settle out, transfer out or take an early retirement due to what is known as forcing the employee and their family into starvation to get them to accept other options that dont serve justice! As you are aware Im sure the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] will avoid going to court in every way possible. 
I am one of the fortunate ones that was able to out starve them and I won my case! 
Do, Can you please guide me in any positive direction or give me advice on what I can do if there is a way, to avoid paying such high interest rates on a small loan? Please advise Sincerely [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','ENOVA INTERNATIONAL, INC.',2.0,2.0,'cashNet has a small loan company that is charging me for a small loan. the company is charging me for a small loan where something came up preventing pay day payments from');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2119,'01/02/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Check cashing service','Problem with customer service','The customer sevice said that she was going to help me with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and did not assist me. I am still waiting. I have a goverment licence for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and told her that I have to register the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] funds for my compensation for my program. She said ok. I explained to her that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] agent said that the computer device to register the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] funds was at payomatic and that the computer has been there for a long time. The agent told me this in 2015.  Please note that as a licensed contracter, please notify the payomatic director [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of my rights to register my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] shareholder funds. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that she would speak to anyone who can call her to let her know that I am ready for the funds to be released from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  agent said that the computer device to register these funds is at payomatic and she told me that in 2015. I  already confirmed with the Federal Trades Commission with proof of funds and I already confirmed with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] agent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and she said that my funds are ready to be released as a grant [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] licensed with the federal government. Please let the payomatic director [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] know that I am ready to retrieve my funds.','PAY-O-MATIC',2.0,2.0,'the customer said that she was going to help me with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and did not assist me. she said that the computer device to register these funds');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2120,'01/02/2018','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I need the assistance of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau with the issue that I am facing. For the past couple of months, dozens of inquiries have been added to my credit report that I have NOT authorized. A scam company called " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' has been using my personal information and sending it out to several outside sources to pull my credit. I have not signed any documents or applications to cause more than 100 inquiries to be made on my Experian report. They initially sold me on the promise of helping me start a business but nothing ever became of that. I requested a Cease and Desist months ago and contacted them again this past XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but that has not stopped them from sending my information out and causing more unauthorized inquiries to be made on my credit. The person who was in charge of my account at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I am including a copy of the email I sent to his company requesting a Cease and Desist. I  have discovered that they are still causing more inquiries to be made with other companies I have not requested to work with. I am considering taking them to court and suing them but I also need Experian to delete ALL unauthorized inquiries. I also will need a fraud alert to be added to my credit as my information has been compromised by this scam company.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'dozens of inquiries have been added to my credit report. a scam company has been sending my personal information to several sources. a fraud alert is needed to be added to my');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2121,'01/01/2018','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Virtual currency','Money was not available when promised','I sold Bitcoin through Coinbase and their system claimed to have completed the wire deposit to my bank account on the same day, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The amount total is {$2900.00} after fees. As of submitting this complaint, it is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have reached out to them several times trying to get an estimated date of the arrival of my withdrawal. At first I received an automated response telling me that wires would be delayed up to 10 days, which is clearly not true. After the 10 days passed, I reached out to them again and did not even get a reply. They have provided no transparency as to why I can not get my funds from that transaction.','Coinbase, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'the amount total is $2900.00 after fees. I have reached out to them several times trying to get an estimated date of the arrival of my withdrawal.');
