I became aware of the situation when I checked my credit report showing that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting me charged off. I immediately called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who referred me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], with whom I paid the account in full. I have sent letters to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and filed a complaint against them with the BBB ( complaint ID [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] responded saying " Unfortunately, we are unable to purchase [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit Card account from Portfolio Recovery Associates ( PRA ) because the balance has already been paid in full. We have forwarded his concerns to PRA and have requested PRA delete the trade line from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit bureau files. '''' last XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Portfolio Recovery is saying that they did not receive any instructions from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with regards to deleting the account from my credit report. Last XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], from the Office of the President of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], emailed me saying, " I will be reaching back out to Portfolio Recovery Associates ( PRA ), with regard to the matter. Once I receive a response from PRA, I will mail a formal written response to you. ". Portfolio Recovery Associates still is reporting the account even though the original creditor admits that they ''ve made a mistake. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] even Deleted the account from their end as stated in their BBB response. Please see attachments.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',4.0,4.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paying for my $24.00 store purchase. the card was actually incurred on');
