INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2213,'12/12/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], via Citibanks website, I applied for a Secured Mastercard Application ID  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I submitted all the requested information and authorized a {$1000.00} withdrawal from my checking account to cover the security deposit. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], about a week later, I receive a letter from Citibank, requesting additional information the bank needed to allow my application could proceed : a copy of a recent bank statement and a NEW deposit. I promptly mailed both via USPS on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bank statement and a [ paper ] check for {$1000.00}. Citibank received my mailing a few days later as evidenced by the fact that my check cleared my checking account on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Per the information on the back of the check, it was deposited on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and processed on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] seeing that my check had cleared - I called Citibank to inquire about the status of my application. I was told that my application was in good standing and that I should expect to hear confirmation by the end of the week. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - not having heard anything from Citibank the previous week, I called again to ask what seemed to be the hold up. I explained that, as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was approaching, I needed access to the money Citibank was now holding for almost 2 weeks i.e. I really needed the credit card I had applied for. Once again, I was told that I would hear something within that week. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] once again not having heard anything from Citibank the previous week, I called AGAIN, this time requesting to speak with a Supervisor so I could get some more informed and detailed answers. After being kept on hold for some 15 minutes, I was finally connected to a Supervisor named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ID : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was apologetic but not helpful. I explained to him in some detail what had transpired to date, including that the check I sent as a security deposit had cleared my account 3 weeks ago. Oddly, he still could not ( or did not want to ) grasp the fact that Citibank ALREADY HAD MY SECURITY DEPOSIT and kept telling me that the bank needed to verify that I had the money in my account. He assured me that I would have an answer by the end of the week. When I said that, given the outrageously awful Citibank service thus far, I may just want to cancel the entire application and get my money back, he said this was not possible. I could not believe my ears! Not only was Citibank holding my money hostage for 3 weeks now, I could not get it back even if I wanted to! 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Friday ) I routinely checked my bank account and, much to my bewilderment, overnight Citibank had removed ANOTHER {$1000.00} from my account!! This was done without my authorization and, at this point, Citibank was holding {$2000.00} of my money with NO indication about when ( or if! ) I would be receiving my card! I immediately called Citibank and after another 10 or 15 minute wait was connected to a Supervisor named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Once again, I described everything that transpired to date and added that Citibank had now removed ANOTHER {$1000.00} from my checking account, this time without authorization. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me that he would immediately rectify the situation and call me back within the hour to confirm. 

I never got the promised call back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] so that evening I called Citibank AGAIN and this time was connected to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. AGAIN I described the situation and AGAIN expressed my outrage that Citibank was now holding {$2000.00} of my money hostage,  {$1000.00} of which was removed from my account without authorization! [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me that the department dealing with my application was closed for the weekend and that she will make sure to communicate my issues to the appropriate people so they get them Monday morning. She suggested that I try putting a stop payment with my bank on the 2nd {$1000.00} Citibank withdrew which I tried to do but was unsuccessful. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was informed by my bank that I was charged a {$38.00} overdraft fee to cover Citibanks 2nd, unauthorized, withdrawal! 

