INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2251,'12/05/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Written notification about debt','Thank you for your recent communication wherein you claim to have validate the alleged debt. The information you have provided is woefully deficient and fails to establish that this is a valid item. 

First, you have not, by any credible means, demonstrated that I owe this alleged debt to YOUR organization. You have failed to provide any document bearing my signature that would establish that I have any indebtedness to your company. You have also failed to provide me with a complete statement of accounting as required by law to be considered full and complete validation. 

Second, you have merely supplied me with copies of alleged bills on the account in question ( OR contract ). These documents, which you could easily have fabricated, fail to prove that there is any legal or contractual obligation between myself, your agency or the creditor. 

Third, as you have failed to establish any relationship between me and the purported debt, I demand that you discontinue reporting this item to the credit bureaus and, in fact, that you delete the item. Additionally, note that if you continue to collect on this purported debt, such action will be in violation of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act. 

Fourth, I do not appreciate the insulting tone that my validation request was answered in. I have a right to request ANY and ALL proof that I owe this alleged to your organization AND to the original creditor. Your answers were condescending and I WILL be sure to report this negative response to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, Federal Trade Commission and the Better Business Bureau. Your hostility was completely uncalled for as I am acting within MY rights under the law.','Credit Bureau of Lancaster County, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'aaron miller: you have not demonstrated that I owe this alleged debt to your organization. he says you have failed to provide any document bearing my signature ');
