INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2279,'11/29/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I applied for a mortgage loan modification with Bank of Hawaii, they sent me an offer letter for a forbearance agreement. I had a friend in the mortgage business review the letter, and he said I may be worse off after the 1 year of lower payments offered due to I will still owe all of the outstanding difference between the contractual payment and the reduced forbearance payments. I am unemployed and on private [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] insurance. Since the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is 1 year or longer I ''m not sure why they were not able to do a permanent modification? I asked what would happen at the end of the 1 year forbearance period, and if I could re-apply for a modification at that time, and they said no I need to sell the property before the 1-year forbearance period ends. I wondered if someone at CFPB could help me review my options and the offer letter? I need to send 1st forbearance payment by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017.','BANK OF HAWAII CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a friend in the mortgage business review the letter. he said he may be worse off after the 1 year of lower payments offered. he said he will still ');
