INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2307,'11/22/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','My Equifax credit report was recently downgraded by 152 points ( it was above the 800 ) with no apparent reason. Trying to communicate with Equifax to find out the reason has been a cross between a nightmare and a joke. I can not get anyone who speaks clear English and all they do is argue that they are speaking English ( at least I think that is what they said ). I want to make contact with a clear speaking person I can understand and find out why they have my credit rating so low. Their customer service stinks ... .they just argue and argue with me about what a good job they are doing.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'my Equifax credit report was recently downgraded by 152 points. it was above the 800. a joke has been made.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2308,'11/21/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I applied for PSLF and selected my preferred plan ( and only plan that I wanted to be placed in ) as PAYE. This was in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2017. I submitted all of the required documentation. I had not heard anything for over a month. Then I submitted a consolidation application. After that, I had a payment that became due ( after my grace period ) for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the standard repayment plan ( for over {$2000.00} ). I chatted with a rep at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who said that my consolidation application is what put me in the standard repayment plan, and that I should delete my consolidation application to be put in PAYE in time for my  payment due date. So I did that. 

Then I still remained in the same standard repyament plan, owing over {$2000.00}. I then received an email that I was not in a good repayment plan for PSLF as I would have nothing forgiven ( if I continued to pay in the standard repayment plan ). So I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to discuss in person, and this time they told me that when I deleted my consolidation application ( as I was instructed to do, because I was told it placed me in the standard repayment plan ), that my PAYE request was deleted ( even though I had applied for PAYE separately and months prior to my consolidation application ). 

So they told me that they now have to re-process my application for PAYE. I still have a payment posted for over {$2000.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( in one week ). But they told me to just ignore that and not pay it, as once my application is complete it will un-do the previous payment that was required, and that they do n''t report people for deliquency until 90 days, and that my app will be complete by then so I will not have to worry.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'I applied for PSLF and selected my preferred plan as PAYE. after that, I had a payment that became due for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2309,'11/21/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Payday loan','Charged fees or interest you didn''t expect','I applied and was approved for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] line of credit. This is my second time financing with company. Agreed to biweekly payment of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]?? Was taken out of my account fine. They then submitted a second payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which they claim is part of their monthly service fee of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This was not properly explained to me I did not have this on my first loan with them. They have hidden in their fine print they charge a XXXXmonthly fee in addition to their biweekly payments. This is fraud and should have been out into loan docs properlybstating what payments will be','MoneyLion Inc.',2.0,4.0,'a XXXmonthly fee is charged in addition to biweekly payments. this is fraud and should have been out into loan docs properly.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2310,'11/21/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I defaulted on a mortgage in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( the date of my last payment was in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). The property went into foreclosure in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my creditor ultimately sold the property in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It is now XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the mortgage is still on my Transunion and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit reports. The Transunion and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] report clearly shows that my last payment was in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reported that I went from 120 days delq to current in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and then back to 120 days delq in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. As a consequence, this derogatory item is still on my credit report and I have been unable to secure a mortgage refinance for my primary residence because lenders wo n''t make loans when a foreclosure is still on the credit report. this foreclosure should have dropped off my report 2 years ago. I have written [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they have yet to respond. when I call [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I am ask to hold while I am transfered and then they hang up ( this happened twice ). I have filed two complaints with transunion via phone and between the language barriers and lack of customer service, nothing has happened ( in fact my transunion credit score, which I monitor, inexplicably dropped 30 pts ). The written responses from transunion and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claim that a change had been made, but the derogatory is still on my credit reports. Pls help!','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the mortgage was sold in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the mortgage is still on my Transunion and [COMPTE_');
