[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my son was at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. he was loaned to Navient Bank ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2314,'11/20/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] there was a hail storm in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CO that damaged my home extensively. Due to the dollar amount of the damages, my home owners insurance company, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had to make the checks out to myself, my wife and the lender for the home. The lender ''s process to release the payments is to release 50 %, then send an inspector, then release 25 % more then inspect it again and then release the final 25 % when the restoration/repairs are complete. 

The lender for my home, Rushmore Loan Management has had the majority of the funds for over 3 months, totaling {$16000.00}. I have filled out all the necessary paperwork, beginning four months ago. I have called a total of 14 times to find out when they would be releasing the funds so I can proceed with repairing my homes. They have given me every different excuse in the book on why the funds have not been sent. 

Here ''s a small breakdown on my communication with them ( most recent ). On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they told me that the hand writing was too light. This is not accurate as the email came from me and it ''s crystal clear. Last week on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a " manager '''' there named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me that she was going to call me that day with a tracking number for the check being sent. 

On Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called and the call center person told me that they were waiting for the payee information to be approved. 

Today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was given two different reasons for it not shipping. The original person who answered the phone said they were doing a system update today. Then a manager named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) gave me a different excuse about the IRS approving the payee on the check to be issued. She told me it would be shipped on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the latest and said that she would call me when it does ship. They have told me this before and have never, ever called me. 

For context, I have three windows that are boarded up in my home from the storm and nothing has been repaired except for the roof, downspouts and gutters because I need the funds from Rushmore to complete the repairs.','RUSHMORE LOAN MANAGEMENT SERVICES LLC',2.0,2.0,'a hail storm damaged my home in a hail storm. the lender for my home, Rushmore Loan Management, has had the majority of the funds for over 3 months. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2315,'11/20/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','The holder of my FHA mortgage loan Loancare is refusing to review or look at my current financial information to consider me for loan modification or other homeowner assistance programs. Every time I call I speak to a different person, and they give me the runaround and have set a foreclosure sale date instead of letting me be considered for any homeowner assistance programs. They have set a sale date of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and over the past several months have never once looked at the paperwork I submitted or given me any feedback or communication. Additionally they have failed to provide Occupied Conveyance paperwork prior to the scheduling of the sale date as required by HUD guidelines. 

I bought this home a little over a year ago. At the time I was making a solid living in sales, and my wife worked at a doctor ''s office. We applied for and were qualified for this FHA government purchase loan based on our income at that time. Not long after buying the home my wife was involved in a bad car accident. She was unable to work and I had to take a couple of months off to care for her, so for a period of time there was NO income coming in. When I went back to work the business had dramatically slowed down and it was the holiday season so it was a bad time to try and switch and find a new sales job. Once my wife was ready to go back to work she found that her hours were drastically cut because the doctor she worked for was cutting back on his hours and went on a long vacation as well. The combination of these factors over a few months affected our income and we ended up defaulting on our loan. 

I immediately contacted Loancare to try and resolve this matter and offered to make partial payments while I got back on my feet. I was told no, that I should wait and make the full payment when I could. When I called back to try and make the full payment I was told that they would not accept it because now they needed two months of mortgage payments AND late fees in order to accept my payment. I could not do this and the situation began to snowball. I contacted their agents repeatedly to request the chance to be considered for a loan modification. Every time I called in I would talk to someone different. No one gave me the option to apply for help or be reviewed for any programs, instead I was told the only thing I could do was reinstate the loan. 

I have since found a new job and make a solid living again. I have filled out the home retention package and sent it in to Loancare on several occasions but have never actually been reviewed, never had an assessment completed of my financial circumstances and have never had a point of contact assigned. Instead Loancare marches to foreclosure and denies me access to these programs they are required to review me for. I can afford a reasonable payment and deserve the chance to fix this problem and get back into regular payments on my mortgage loan with Loancare.','LoanCare, LLC',2.0,4.0,'holder of my mortgage loan Loancare refuses to review or look at financial information. they have set a foreclosure sale date of XX/XX/[COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2316,'11/20/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I am have trouble with American Education Services ( AES ). On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received an email stating that my most recent payment is past due. However, the payment was due on Friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I processed the payment around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the full minimum balance on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which was the due date of the payment. I reviewed the website both on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my payment is listed on their website as scheduled on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but not processed. I contacted their customer service office on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was told that I was three days past due and the rep requested a second payment. When I stated that I made a payment was made on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was told that is correct we do have a payment, and we usually clear payments between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] however, we did not clear yours because 1 % of our customers make payment without having funds in their account. Although you may have never done this we will not show your account as paid until we receive payment from you bank. I said if that is your internal process then you should not send me nor my co-signer late notices. ( Which they did on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). The rep stated well that ''s what we are going to do because some of y''all do n''t properly pay your bills. I told him that I would seek legal action. I believe it is improper for AES to list my account as past due when I made a payment on the due date and prior to the close of business time listed on their website. I made the payment directly on their website to ensure something like this would not happen. I believe they are providing misinformation not only to me but to my co-signer by sending her a notice that I am behind on a payment when I am not. Even if they are not sending this information to the credit bureau they are sending incorrect and misleading information to their loan holders and co-signers. Please tell me what I can do.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a rep on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] asked for a second payment. the rep said that is correct we do have');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2317,'11/20/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Struggling to repay your loan','I dont understand why my loan went from {$5000.00} to {$7000.00}???????? That is unbelievale I can not afford to pay that off, I am currently not enrolled in school and currently not working, I dont know where to get that kind of money?????','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'loan went from $5000.00 to $7000.00???????? I can''t afford to pay that off, I am currently not enrolled in school and currently');
