INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2332,'11/16/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is my case number with institution. 

I simply accessed my online account in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to switch auto-draft accounts from one bank to another. When doing so, the website explained that it would take 30 days to reflect the changes. What actually happened, is they removed the current banking information immediately and waited 30 days to update the new account. In turn, I was balancing my checkbook for the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and realized my mortgage payment had not been deducted. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] immediately. They stated that I was 32 days delinquent on my account. I asked why they did not attempt to contact me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after verifying all of my account information was correct, something they ask every time you log in ). They had no answers. Why would they have not called or emailed if I was late? I resolved the payment issue immediately and asked them if they had reported it to the credit bureaus. They stated that they report 30 days delinquency ( essentially I was 2 days late ). I asked for a reversal they said I would have to dispute via an online application, which I did, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] separate times. It is now 4 months later and I have not received correspondence to correct this issue. My credit score has dropped over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points for the one discrepancy. My score went from a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] overnight. I am now getting declined for premier credit cards [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which I had no problems previously [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and my student loans payment has increased by 1 full point as there is an adjustable rate which is dependent on your credit score as a factor. This is costing me a substantial amount of financial distress. I feel that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should remove the delinquent report immediately. Their website verbiage was misleading, and they made ZERO attempt to contact me and allow me the chance to make the payment before reporting my delinquency to the credit bureaus. This is not fair