INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2343,'11/14/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','Credit card companies continues to allow charges after filing a lost or stolen card. Credit card company say they have the right to continue to allow charges to go through well after the cancellation card has been placed. I believe I was misled by a particular credit card company as well as by others that when submitting a lost or stolen card they can allow charges on new card number. I contacted my credit card company and they state that this is a common practice. I believe that once you submit a lost and stolen card and get a new number no one else should be able to charge until you give them specific permission. I feel that the credit card companies are protecting the vendors/merchants, not protecting the consumer or card holders. I believe this is fraud on the part of the credit card companies to allow continued charges after card has been canceled due to lost or stolen circumstances. Credit card companies continue to collect interest and allow fees to continue in direct favor of the merchant/ vendor and credit card company. Regardless of their policy this is fraud. What protects me and my number from these activities?','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'credit card companies continue to allow charges after card cancellation. they say they have the right to continue to allow charges to go through well after the cancellation card has been placed.');
