INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2357,'11/12/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I opened a mortgage with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$100000.00}. My monthly payment including taxes ( $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/yr ) and insurance ( $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/yr ) was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] per month. That payment remained the same from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In early XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the mortgage was sold to Mr. Cooper mortgage. When I received my payment information from Mr. Cooper, it had gone up by $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month to $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month! I called Mr. Cooper to discuss this and was told that my account was behind in escrow because my property taxes had gone significantly. However, I went to the county to talk to the tax assessor and was told that the property taxes only went up $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/yr. At this point, Mr. Cooper is saying that my monthly principle + interest is about $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/mth and my escrow is $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month. There  is no possible way that I should be paying {$6000.00} per year in escrow. If my escrow account was behind, then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would have told me that at the end of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], or at the end of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That never happened. Instead, Mr. Cooper must be trying to skim money off the top of my mortgage.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'in early XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my monthly payment was $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/yr');
