INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2370,'11/09/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I received my Annual Escrow Account Disclosure Statement on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Included with it was a check for {$640.00} for overpayment on my escrow account. Initially, I was very happy to get that, considering it " found money ''''. After more careful examination of the statement, I realized that Nationstar Mortgage [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was estimating my Real Estate tax to be {$1700.00}, which is HALF of the yearly amount. Because of this, they grossly underestimated their anticipated annual disbursement for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and not only refunded money to me, but calculated my monthly mortgage payment to be {$140.00} lower every month going forward. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to find out how they arrived at this deflated tax amount, and the agent could n''t tell me. He stated that the last disbursement they made to my town was {$870.00}, I pressed him and said " that was a quarterly payment, right '''', to which he agreed. And then I asked " Well, would n''t it stand to reason that my YEARLY taxes would be FOUR times that amount?? Taxes do n''t go down, they go up ''''. I asked him what my previous year taxes were, and he confirmed they were over {$3400.00}. He then suggested that the escrow department would revisit the issue when the next tax bill came out. I said, " well, in the meantime, you want me to send you {$150.00} less each month, on top of you reimbursing me {$650.00}?? Do you know how much of a shortfall that is going to end up being??? '''' He then suggested that when I make my payment each month, which I told HIM was going to be the same amount I had been already sending, that I call in and tell them to direct the extra amount to my escrow account until my escrow account was recalculated. 

So, I will be sending that nice check for {$650.00} back, continue to make my same old monthly payment and have to call them every month until they recalculate my account, taking time out of my life to address their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] up. 

Luckily for me, I took the time to thoroughly examine my escrow statement. I am making this complaint because I do n''t want some other mortgage customer to possibly NOT pay attention, and then end up with a HUGE shortfall that they ''ll have to scramble to come up with. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is coming, and had I not looked closely at that statement, and questioned their amount, that money could ''ve been spent quickly on gifts, and put our family into a pretty negative financial situation when it came time to correct that shortage. 

This [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] infuriates me, and I would HATE for someone else to be mislead in this way. If I had not caught this, I would ''ve ended up with an almost {$1800.00} shortfall over the course of a year!! That ''s a huge amount for a family to have to come up with. 

NOTE REGARDING UPLOADS : I am attaching XXXXwo town real estate tax statements and the escrow statement from Nationstar Mortgage [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The town of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] does have a strange way of formatting and sending out tax bills, sending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] quarters of billing out at a time, but it does note on the invoices that the payments are for QUARTERS. We bought our house in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so one statement is for 3rd and 4th quarter of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the previous owner ''s name, and the other statement for 1st and 2nd quarter of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], in my and my fianc ''s name. I am also attaching a copy of the escrow statement that I received from Nationstar Mortgage [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which has the projected tax amount that is only {$.00} different that the amount on the most current town FY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] real estate tax statement. I am assuming this is where they got that figure from, but again, if they had actually read the statement, they ''d know it was not for one year.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'a check for $640.00 for overpayment on my escrow account was included. the statement was a check for $640.00 for overpayment');
