INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2372,'11/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a mail letter from US Bank, notifying me that I had a late payment on my credit card account. I immediately made full payment which was owed on the same day. Then I applied for a home loan equity during [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and was informed by my loan specialist that a late payment was posted on my credit report for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I immediately tried to dispute with US Bank, considering that the late payment happened in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I was not notified until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the same time with when they reported to the Credit Bureau. I also had auto payment set up on that account and it did not work. Even now, I had to manually make payment every month because the auto pay function is still not working. I tried to contact US Bank Card member service twice and they only sent me a general response and kept asking me to give them more information, which I already did. I already made request twice to them that the false report has to be removed from my credit report. They did not want to acknowledge the fact that the had failed to give me proper notice within 30 days when the incident happened. I was not allowed the proper time to act on it. 
This false late payment report has hindered me from closing on my equity loan, which resulting in thousands of interest I had to incur during this time.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a letter from US Bank stating that I had a late payment on my credit card account. the letter was sent to me by my loan specialist. the false late payment report');
