INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2406,'11/02/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Managing the loan or lease','Kia Motor Finance took two payments this month from my bank account. I called customer service because of the error by Kia. At first they were fine in reversing the payment ; however they said they would mail me a check in 10 days. I asked if their was some way to expedite it and if they could include the cost for the NSF fee my bank may charge. The initial person basically ignored my request and just restated i would get a check in 10 days. So i asked to speak to a supervisor. This is where the problem began. The supervisor. I believe her name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said she would not do anything because they were not responsible for bank fees and seemed to insinuate she would not refund the payment to me. She then tried to blame me saying the reason it came out twice was because I made a payment then set up auto pay which came out on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However their own website said my auto pay was set to begin on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I asked her why she just continued to blame me. Not only do I know I did not set up auto pay to start on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Kia Fiances own website confirmed it was not set up that way. Not only did she threaten to not refund the payment but when I asked her for her full name she refused. I asked for the name of the previous person and her answer was imply " no '''', and when I asked to speak to her supervisor her answer was again " no ''''. Then I asked to be transferred to the complaint department and she transferred me to a totally unrelated department that when they answered told me they were the wrong department. This is a major Reg E violation. Not only did they not help but the manipulated the facts to shift responsibility the customer service supervisor should be reprimanded.','HYUNDAI CAPITAL AMERICA',2.0,2.0,'customer service supervisor reprimanded for reversing payment. he asked to speak to a supervisor. she said she would not refund the payment.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2407,'11/01/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','When we heard that Equifax was hacked into we were told to go online and request protection. I did that. Now Equifax has gone into my account and it ''s a hard inquiry. If I had known this would be a hard inquiry, because hard inquiry brings your score down, I would have never allowed them to enter my credit report. I think it ''s unfair and consumers should have been told that what this means is that there will be a hard inquiry into to your accounts. I would have not allowed this to happen. By not stating communicating what this would do is misinforming consumers.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'if we heard that Equifax was hacked into we were told to go online and request protection. if I had known this would be a hard inquiry, it would have');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2408,'11/01/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','I have a citi card with a 0 apr promotion that expires on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I made a payment of {$800.00} to pay off the balance so that I would not be charged all the back interest. My payment did not go to that promotion. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Florida informed me that my payment does not apply to the 0 apr. It will be applied to the purchases that incurred after the balance transfer. So on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] all the interest that would have incurred during the promotional period will be applied to my balance. Its not right. I really need advice on what to do. Thank you.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a 0 apr promotion expires on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. my payment');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2409,'11/01/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','I had paid my credit card off using my checking account. The checking did not have enough funds, and I did n''t bother with transfering the money from savings to cover it because I was going to rely on " overdraft protection. '''' I was then charged a fee of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for that which I have never been charged for before. I called and complained about that, and all they said was " this was in the paperwork. ''''','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a credit card was paid off using my checking account. the checking did not have enough funds. I was then charged a fee of [COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2410,'11/01/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I own a home in Florida. It was damaged during the recent storm on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I rent it out to tenants. My insurance company is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I reported the damage. Fortunately, the house was habitable at all times. The main damage was to the roof. To mitigage damage to the house, my property manager, at my request, had the roof repaired as quickly as possible. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] later sent an adjuster, " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' to the property. Its report is attached. It begins on the sixth page of the set of documents that are attached. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent me a check based on the adjuster ''s estimate. However, to cash the check, I needed the endorsement of my mortgage company, Wells Fargo. I went to a Wells Fargo branch to obtain this endorsement on Saturday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However, Wells Fargo required me to sign the attached document entitled " Insurance claim check endorsement & Property Inspection Agreement ''''. I regret that my wife and I did not think this through before signing. There are provisions that I think are unconscionable. First, in clause 3, it is stated that if repairs are not completed in 120 days, I admit that I have breached the terms of my mortgage and Wells Fargo may call our loan due. In addition, on the prior page, it is indicated, in the second paragraph, that those repairs need to be 100 % complete. This provides, in my opinion, far too much discretionary power to Wells Fargo. I consider it unconscionable that a person trying to repair their home but perhaps not meeting Wells Fargo ''s definition of timely completion or an inspector ''s definition of 100 % completion ( rather than some more sensible level of substantial completion ) could lose their mortgage. This requirement was not written in my insurance policy with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No consideration was provided by me for this additional right conferred upon Wells Fargo. Is n''t making this provision mandatory inconsistent with consumer protection laws? Also, clause 2 provides me 10 days from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to indicate any disagreement that I might have. I suspect that this means that I can keep the proceeds, apply them to the repairs, and not agree to these extreme provisions. I plan to indicate in additional ways in writing my disagreement to Wells Fargo, but I want to know what my rights are. In order to keep the proceeds, am I required to sign something with such draconian provisions which place my entire mortgage at risk? I suspect many others in Florida are facing the same situation. This may be a good story for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]!','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',4.0,4.0,'a home in Florida was damaged during the storm on january 1. the house was habitable at all times. the main damage was to the roof.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2411,'10/31/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','This account is about my child support payment to the Texas OAG office. The account balance and the reported payments are always reported wrong to all the credit reporting agencies. 

Since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I had been awarded and receiving a monthly social security survivor benefits in the amount of {$1300.00}, to which the Texas OAG attached a lien and had since been collecting one third of my benefits every month in the amount of {$450.00}. The OAG office collects this amount from my survivor benefits promptly without fail. Also in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I settled an auto insurance claim for about {$13000.00}, and between the lawyers, the hospital bills and the rest of the other medical bills, the OAG got {$5900.00} of the settlement, and the rest went to the attorneys and the rest to the medical providers to settle the medical bills. Not a penny for went me. I do n''t have a problem with the OAG taking the money for my child ''s support, what I have a problem with is the reporting errors. 

For instance, my total monthly child support payment is {$340.00}, of which {$220.00} is for the chaild ''s support, {$75.00} for the child ''s medical, and {$100.00} to go towards reducing the arrears, which as of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] before the social security survivor benefits I started receiving my benefits my arrears was then at a little over {$10000.00}. But as I already indicated, the OAG office is actually {$450.00} from my benefits. Yet for the past 10 months, my credit consumer report is showing zero payment into the account, it shows that no payment has been made on the account for almost a year, that has always been past due for 30, 60, 90 days, and that is just not true. I have all the documents to prove it if requested. As of today when l checked the account balance, it shows that the account is past due 8 months, and the remaining balance does not accurately reflect the arrears balance.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a credit consumer report shows zero payment into the account. the account balance and the reported payments are always reported wrong. the account balance and the reported payments are always reported wrong.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2412,'10/31/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter in the mail from McCarthy, Burgess & Wolff ( MB & W ) stating that they are a debt collector attempting to collect a debt from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I immediately called them at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I disputed the debt and asked for additional information. Between the dates of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I repeatedly called MB & W at the same number requesting updates and continuing to dispute this charge. I also spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] numerous times and was advised over the phone and in writing that I do not owe them any money. I provided all this information to MB & W verbally and via email. Repeated calls to MB & W resulted in the same answers where they confirmed that they had received my information and were waiting to hear back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a letter ( .pdf attached to an email ) from MB & W subject of a debt verification notice. I called and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] again and she transferred me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( who I have spoke to before during this process ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] identified himself as a supervisor. He acknowledged receipt of the information I provided from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and stated that " for some reason that is not enough for them to close this debt. He further went on to state that people call all the time and say they are n''t responsible for debt and until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] provided them further information this was going to sit in collection with MB & W ''''. I believe that I have sufficiently proven that this is not my debt, therefore, I am opening this complaint against MB & W.','McCarthy, Burgess & Wolff, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'MB & W disputed the debt and asked for additional information. MB & W responded to the same calls and asked for updates. MB & W confirmed that');
