INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2438,'10/25/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I ''ve never been late on my mortgage payment. My XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment I paid {$2600.00} which was an extra {$50.00}, which they applied to principal. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] there was an escrow adjustment and my payment of {$2600.00} was {$25.00} short, so they did not apply any of my payment, reporting me 30 days late. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I paid {$3000.00}, covering the {$25.00} short, plus their {$89.00} late fee. On my credit report it shows I was 30 days late. However my due date is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they reported me at the end of the month, which is not 30 days. In addition I asked them to considered I ''ve always paid on time, usually more than the payment, that it was {$25.00} short. I also asked if they could reapply the extra {$50.00} from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to cover escrow and then reapply my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. They claim by law they can not do that, will not escalate my calls and frankly this is not a black and white issue. I ''ve talked to a number of financial institutions and DITECH has options to help me, I gave them an easy method to reapply payments, but they just choose not to do anything to help out a long time customer. They have a very rude customer service. My credit score which was well over 700 dropped by 50 points. I ''ve worked hard on my credit and I find this very unfair and any reasonable person would agree.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment was $2600.00. they applied to principal and paid $2600.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2439,'10/25/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I called LendUp and explained that my account is still open but being reported as closed on my credit report. I was asked to take a pic of the account showing its closed. I took one picture because its been reported to all credit reporting agency. They told me it would be a couple days and should be resolved and it still remains on my credit report dropping my scores because its listed as closed. They reported it closed because there was a .89 transaction made on the account last month that was not by me. So instead of calling, emailing, texting or evening faxing they decided to report my account as closed. The first time I called about the problem their attitude was terrible and they transferred me to the fraud department. They put me on hold and then hung up the phone and never called back. The fraud department operator was very rude and nasty to me. Terrible customer service and the company communication is the worst I have ever experience or seen in my life. LendUp could care less what it did to my credit report they just keep claiming it will be fixed. After 4 phone calls to the company its still on my credit report.','LendUp Loans LLC',2.0,4.0,'lendUp reported the account closed because it was not by me. they reported it closed because there was a.89 transaction made on the account last month. they transferred me');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2440,'10/25/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Communication tactics','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] am I was contacted by a person saying they were calling from Comenity bank from a blocked number. I believe she said her name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I had to ask 3 times what company was calling. She just kept calling me by name. She never verified that I was who she thought I was. She then discussed my personal information about the debt not even bothering to identify me. She also did not disclose that the call was either monitored or recorded if it was. I ended the call. I was called 4+ times that day after I had made contact with her that morning. These people call me sometimes in excess of 16 times a day. I have also received messages that I felt threatened by. Since these people are saying that they are the original creditor is there anything I can do to stop this harrassment?','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'a person called me from a blocked number was called from a blocked number. she never verified that I was who she thought I was. she then discussed my personal information about');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2441,'10/25/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Title loan','Vehicle was damaged or destroyed the vehicle','My car was stolen and upon the theft that took place it was totaled, I had just lost my job so I than called Navy Federal Credit Union ( my loaner ) and informed them of the incident that took place, I than asked what my options where and was told about the payment protection plan, I was also informed that navy federal was no longer contracting with this company, I than asked about my Guaranteed Asset Protection insurance ( GAP ) and was told that navy federal has a phone recording of me calling in and cancelling the GAP insurance on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which I disagreed with, at this point I left the situation alone because I had misplaced my contract which showed that I agreed to GAP insurance. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I had been shreeding some old papers and came across my contract with navy federal I then called on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke with a representative to inform them of the differences in the dates of my susposidly cancellation and the signed contract, I told the representative that I was informed a few months ago that I cancelled my gap insurance which I did n''t and that the date of the final signing of the contract was after the cancellation date in question and it would show that I agreed to have the gap insurance in place, so she then looked in to my account and agreed with the findings that the contract was signed after the susposidly cancellation of the gap insurance and said that navy federal would autimately go by the most recent signed contract, she than said that she needed to speak with a supervisor and put me on hold, upon her return to the conversation she infomed me that she had made a mistake and that I signed a letter stating that I cancelled the gap insurance which I did n''t I than asked if she could email me this letter and she started to beat around the bush with me I got frustrated and hung up, upon calming myself down I then called navy federal back and spoke with another representative which I informed her what I was told in and earlier conversation, I also informed her that I had recieved [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] seperate promissary notes and that the second one was sent because I did n''t sign and initial the first one which at that point would have made the contract void without my signature so to asume that I agreed or disagreed to anything would be specilation at this point, she than said that the cancellation took place on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I than notified her that I did n''t initialy sign the contract until after the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reason being I did n''t recieve notice of this incomplete document until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which I have the original notice that was sent out, upon telling her the date in which I initially signed the contract and trying to get her to understand the dates of cancellation does n''t add up she than asked me if I would not raise my voice which I was n''t anyway, at that point I fell as thought she was unwilling to see the truth as it was and asked to speak with a supervisor, upon speaking with the supervisor I then told him what my disagreement was about and he then went on to try and explian to me that navy federal was going by the cancellation letter I than tried to explain in detail that I recieved the initial promissary note but because I did not sign my signature and initial it I recieved a letter in the mail along with a replacement promissary note from navy federal on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that I needed to sign and initial to indicate my voluntary selection of the payment protection Plan ( PPP ) and the Guaranteed Asset Protection ( GAP ) and because of this and me continuously stating that I did not cancell the gap insurance navy federal made a mistake, I was then told by the supervisor through out our continued conversation that navy federal does not go by the promissary note and that it ment nothing, I then informed the supervisor that I had no other choice at this point but to seek legal representation. 

P.S Upon the initial approval of the loan from navy federal I agreed to have Guaranteed Asset Protection ( GAP ) on the 1sXXXX promissary note I recieved I agreed to have GAP and on the initial signing of the replacement promissary note I agreed to have GAP, I never cancelled the Guaranteed Asset Protection ( GAP ) not by phone, mail, email, or in-person','NAVY FEDERAL CREDIT UNION',2.0,4.0,'navy federal has a phone recording of me calling in and cancelling the insurance. a representative said that the contract was signed after the susposidly cancellation of the gap insurance ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2442,'10/25/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Other features, terms, or problems','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], when I purchased an new oven from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I opened a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card, which was issued by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the bank informed me that they were closing my account because " a number of dishonored payments ''''. However, this was not true and the only payment that had been " dishonored '''' was an online payment that was not accepted because of a problem with the bank ''s website. After I contacted the bank and told them I believed the real reason they had closed my account was age discrimination ( I am currently [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old ), the bank re-opened my account. 

In the winter of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was having numerous billing problems with my Lowes credit card account. For example, the Lowes bills I received did not include an itemized list of charges, but simply listed the categories of items purchased, e.g. the bill would say " HOUSEPLANT SOILS AND ACCESSORIES ; GENERAL PURPOSE ; COMMODITY SOILS AND SOIL AMENDMENTS '''' with a total dollar amount of {$33.00}, instead of listing the particular items, such as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Potting Soil, 4 lb bag, with the price of each item. 

I was also recieving email messages from the bank saying that my payment had not been received and my account was past due. However, the due date listed on the emails were not the due date on my bills, and the emails were sent 7 to 14 days before my payment was due. The bank also had charged me several late fees totaling over {$100.00}. The bank was also charging me an interest rate of 24.99 %! And on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the bank sent me a letter saying they had closed my account again. 

In earlyXX/XX/XXXXI filed a complaint with the Better Business Bureau about the bank. OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Senior Specialist, Corporate Consumer Relations at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent a letter in reply to my complaint and agreed to reverse the late fees totalling over {$100.00} that had been charged to my account, and denied that my " age was not a factor considered in this matter ''''. There was no mention of the fact that my account had been closed, but I discovered that my account had not been closed despite the erroneous information contained in the banks letter of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], when I went to Lowes to make a purchase, the cashier told me that the charge on my Lowes credit card was not approved. When I checked my account online, it appeared my account had been closed again, despite the fact that I had made every payment in a timely manner and my account balance did not exceed my credit limit. The following week, the bank sent me a letter saying they had closed my account, once again, with a list of bogus reasons for doing so. 

I believe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has discriminated against me because of my age. And they have engaged in business practices that are fraudulent, or at the very least, willfully negligent. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,4.0,'in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the bank re-opened my account. the bank told me that they were closing my account');
