INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2450,'10/24/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','Our firm handled a closing for on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On the day of closing, we had a payoff statement from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] showing an amount due good through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Interest was calculated and added through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and our check was sent to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$160000.00}. After two weeks passed and the check had not cleared our bank, I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was told the check was received, but the loan was transferred to Shellpoint, along with our check. Our [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] tracking notice shows the payoff check was received by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] then forwarded to Shellpoint on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Shellpoint received the check on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I contacted Shellpoint and was told they would have to research the missing check and it would take [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] business days. When I called back, I was told the payoff was short, and that a payoff statement from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] firm had been sent to our firm on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was able to find the payoff statement from RAS in our file, which was entered after closing on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; so we were unaware [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was involved until after closing. When I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about this second payoff that was sent to us, she confirmed it was sent on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and that because it was sent to us after our closing date, the initial payoff statement from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would be honor