INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2461,'10/21/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Personal line of credit','Problem with the payoff process at the end of the loan','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a Mail Correspondence to consolidate my credit card debt into one loan- From Bank Of America- I called and agreed to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Line of Credit for a term of 96 months. I called in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to discuss with Bank of America as to why I was continuing to be billed after my Pay Off date- I was told that I did not understand how interest accumulates and that I still owed over 10,000. I said how is that possibly- If I purchased a car over 60 months at the end of the 60 months I would own the car- after 3-4 calls being on hold being transferred to numerous departments, I asked for all of payments to be sent to my address with my original agreement. I was told that my account has been closed and Bank of America can only retrieve records back 7 years- so let me get this straight you have no record of a commitment to our agreement- you have closed my account. Very Good- yet they continued to bill me and additional [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been paid to them- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan - Bank Of America HAS RECEIVED OVER 84,000 FROM ME [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] OVER MY 96 MONTH AGREEMENT. After I told them I was filing a complaint I received a phone call and they stated that we resolved this issue last year [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- I said this issue was never resolved I just kept paying you- The agnet said Sir the rates changed in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we sent that information to you in your bill - I said WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT- How can the rates change - and why was the term extended- no response.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was billed for a term of 96 months. I called in XX/X');
