However, my direct debit agreement from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was no longer valid as I had already paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans off and I had provided additional payment processing instructions in writing on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for how to properly allocate my payments. Not only did Fedloan servicing fail to execute on my request to allocate my payment properly, I had call them to have them correctly allocate funds.The payment to pay off a portion of my loan per the payment instructions provided was made on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and appropriately applied on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my automatic payment was {$630.00} as expected. It was not until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I noticed my automatic payment was surprisingly changed. Based on my payment instructions, I expected my payment to remain at {$630.00} however, it was modified and apparently the source of truth as to what my payment would be was rather obscure considering the website was telling me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] different things. 

