INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2473,'10/19/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I short sold my property on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. During or prior to receiving the sale information, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], acting as Attorney-in-Fact for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], submitted a motion for summary judgement ( with a fraudulent affidavit ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] approved this judgement with judicial sale date of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].  This date has been changed a few times and is now scheduled for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After I submitted a previous complaint to the CFPB on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), my attorneys received the short sale approval letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After complying with their requirements for closing, they included an affidavit which required buyers and sellers signatures. I have attached the affidavit here, The 2nd paragraph has a line saying '''' the servicer ... .agrees to accept less than the amount owed to resolve its Loan ( pursuant to a separate agreement between the servicer and the seller ). I do not have any separate agreement. Also, in # 10 on this affidavit, '''' each signatory to the affidavit agrees to indemnify [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the investor ( supposedly [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) for any or all losses resulting from any negligent or intentional misrepresentation including, but not limited to repayment of the difference between the amount owed on the loan and the discounted amount payment. '''' I questioned why I do n''t have the agreement they referred to in the second paragraph and why # 10, they were referring themselves to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They now have told my attorneys they will change the wording so it will say [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as attorney-in-fact for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I still do n''t have the agreement that was referred to, which I believe would be the release from liability. Now the buyers have been waiting since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to close, we were ready last week-I had the home checked by the water department as required, paid the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] will not provide the release from liability. The scheduled judicial sale is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. If they ca n''t provide a release from liability, we ca n''t close on the house. I believe they are stalling again or plan to come after me for the claimed deficiency once the short sale is closed.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a court judge approved the judgment with a judicial sale date of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the court ordered the');
