INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2475,'10/18/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','This problem has to do with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We have had this card for many many years and never had a problem receiving the statements and being able to make our payments on time to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] website. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2017 we went to the website that we have used for many years to log in and make the payment and was directed to a website for Capital One. We called the phone number on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement we had received for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke with a representative and was told that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had been transferred to Capital One and that we would have to register for online services. We went back to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] website and when Capital One came up we tried to reregister. We were unable to reregister as we did not have a 3 digit code from a current credit card they were requesting. We then called back to Capital One and was told by a customer representative that we would not be able to reregister for on-line services and be able to pay our bill on line like we have done for many many years as we did not have the 3 digit code they were requiring. We were then transferred to another customer service representative and was told the same thing. We have never had a returned payment or a late payment to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We were told we could make the payment due for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] by a customer service representative. We asked to be transferred to a customer service representative that could take a payment. We were then transferred to another representative and the representative took the payment. When we mentioned that we had spoken to 2 other  representatives we were told that either one of them could have taken the payment. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment was paid on time. 
We did not receive a XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement. We called Capital One to see about the statement and the representative could not see where a statement was sent to us. I asked how are we to know the amount due and the due date and was told we would have to call in. When I asked for a mailing address I was told it would take 12 days to process a payment as we do not have the statement remittance that would be returned to them along with the payment. 
We feel this needs to be looked into with Capital One. If they are taking over the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the existing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] customers should be able to receive statements and make their payment on-line if they choose to. It seems that Capital One is not sending out statements so [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] customer will not make their payments and the account will become delinquent and be reported on the credit bureaus as a bad debt and hurt the customer. 
Your assistance is greatly appreciated.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a customer representative told us that we would not be able to reregister for on-line services. we were told we could make the payment due for XX/X');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2476,'10/18/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received my statement with an amount due of {$200.00} due by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I made the payment as I usually do on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] believing that my loan payment was accurate and on time as usual. However dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] two days prior to my planned and scheduled payment I was sent a change in payment schedule notice that was unclear. It did not clearly indicate the reason for the change, the difference in the increase amount, or that the change was being applied mid billing cycle. I simply assumed the change would apply next cycle and that it was a small increment increase or a change in the number of payments. 

I was shocked when I logged into Navient on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to schedule my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment and saw that I had been assessed late fees on three loans and that the total monthly payment amount on my loans was now almost triple what it had been. After an immediate reaction of panic I attempted to find an answer through the website, but it was not helpful and I got error messages more than once forcing me to log back in or refresh the screen. I did send two emails through the email link and was sent an automated message that my email would be reviewed. I also looked at my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement and realized that it did list that I was past due and my payment due had jumped from a barely manageable {$200.00} to an impossible {$640.00} and that was just on some of my loans, not all of them. I do not usually look at the statement in depth, especially e-statements, because I log in to the website around the same time each month to make my payment as planned. I just like to have them saved for my records. 

Now I am really concerned because I was under the impression that I was on a long-term repayment plan with the potential for forgiveness if I made all my payments. With this sudden mid-cycle change by Navient I am concerned that not only is my credit bureau being impacted, but my eligibility for this much needed forgiveness program is in jeopardy or lost all together. It is completely impossible for me to make the drastically higher payment to become current again.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'dated 2 days before my planned and scheduled payment I was sent a change in payment schedule notice that was unclear. it did not clearly indicate the reason for the change, the difference in');
