INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2482,'10/17/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','A fraudulent purchase was made on my Macy ''s card  on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. As this is a rarely used card and I had paperless billing set up, I did not notice the charge until I started receiving phone calls for my account being past due. The fraudulent purchase was reported to Macy ''s immediately upon discovery on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They sent me a form to fill out that was dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which was filled out and returned to them with all requested information on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have called them nearly every month to check on the extremely slow progress since then. The majority of the charges were finally removed in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], however, late fees accrued that are directly related to the fraudulent purchase still remain on my account as of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In addition, this has reflected extremely negatively on my credit score, as all of this has been reported to the credit bureaus as if I am not paying my bill.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'a fraudulent purchase was made on my Macy''s card on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2483,'10/17/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','Capital One opened a credit card fraudulently in my name. After unsuccessful attempts to work with Capital One I filed a CFPB complaint. That resulted in Capital One admitting the action was fraudulent and removed card from my CR. I then asked for all documentation used to open the card and was told there was none because it was opened by telephone but regardless they required a subpoena to provide the information. I knew that was not true so I filed a second complaint. That complaint resulted in a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I was correct but had to supply them with a signed letter request and two forms of ID. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I faxed the requested information to the number provided in their response letter. To date I have had no response so I called on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] using the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number and the specified 6-digit pin to inquire on the Capital One Case #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was never offered an opportunity to enter the 7-digit extension specified in their letter. When I reached the CSR I was told there was no such Case # in their system. At that point I called the CFPB to determine why the CFPB case was closed and after discussing the status it was suggested I either mail all the documents I originally faxed or open a new complaint. I decided on the latter because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would likely claim no such case existed and I would be nowhere in resolving this issue.I am uploading the fax cover sheet, the signed request letter, the response letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the two forms of ID, and the fax tx verification report that I faxed to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]..','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'capital One opened a credit card fraudulently in my name. the CFPB contacted me and asked for all documentation used to open the card. a second complaint resulte');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2484,'10/17/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','The complaint is regarding how the company accepts payments. Ever since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bought out my loan earlier this year, I have been dealing with the servicing company American Education Services ( AES ). Each month I call to make payment, AES employs strong-arm tactics to try to force me into giving them my banking account and routing number. 

I continue to be told, every month, that they will accept my banking account and routing numbers as the only form of payment. Each time they conclude our transaction by reminding me that they will allow the " courtesy '''' of a debit, only after being transferred to a number of gatekeepers who all try to dissuade me or deveieve me that debit is not an option. I deal with this every month that I call. 

I was told today, by AES, that " this is how we ''ve always done it '''' when it comes to accepting payments strictly through banking routing numbers. This is a dubious explanation as debit is clearly possible. I have also been told by a supervisor that they actively discourage debit because it costs them money to process payments this way. I ''m not sympathetic as this is the year [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I would like to conduct my business- as I do with countless other merchants and vendors- and use my debit card. 

I have told AES that I can not and will not provide them my banking details, yet they will not accept this explanation each month I call.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'complaint is about how the company accepts payments. a supervisor told me that they discourage debit because it costs them money to process payments this way. a supervisor told me that they');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2485,'10/17/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I opened an account with Citibank for the sole purpose of holding security deposits for a rental property. I told Citibank that this was the purpose, that is, I did n''t need any extra services for this account other than to hold the money and to write a check to outgoing tenants, which would happen at most twice a year. I requested, and was confirmed, that there would be no service fees on this account, in part because of the purpose/needs of the account and in part because I have been a long-time customer of Citibank that usually maintains a somewhat large balance in my main checking account ( currently $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but over the years has been more or less than that ). 

The bank clerk signed me up for a Citigold account, which unbeknownst to me carries with it a $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month service fee. I admit I should have been more vigilant about checking up on this, but I ''ve always had a good experience with Citibank, and had no reason to suspect they would do anything other than what they said they would do. In addition, because of the purpose of the account, I had no reason to check on the activity of that account. 

It was n''t until about two and a half years later ( approx XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), when I was getting ready to write a check to some outgoing tenants when I checked the balance and noticed that it was much lower than expected. 

I have contacted Citibank in person twice, on the phone two or three times, and written them mail about a dozen times. I will sometimes be offered relief on the fees going back four months, but they claim to be unable to do more than this. They will often tell me to contact the customer service center ( by snail mail ) but this has been the least fulfilling ; the responses usually indicate superficial comprehension.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I opened an account with Citibank for the sole purpose of holding security deposits for a rental property');
