INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2518,'10/10/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I thought that lenders - for any loans, not just student loans - were required to provide timely and accurate billing statements. I am attempting to re-finance my student loans currently serviced by Navient, and much to my surprise there is not a way to access your billing statements via their web portal. I have been on autopay for years, and not had a reason to look for a statement, but I am appalled at how difficult it is. It is hard not to wonder whether they are hiding something. My guess is that they want to make it difficult to re-finance with another lender, and they know that is more than likely the only reason you would be accessing billing statements, so they make them difficult to obtain.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'student loans are not a way to access your billing statements via their web portal. it is difficult not to wonder if they are hiding something.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2519,'10/10/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','I recently viewed my credit report for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I notice U.S Collection West was being reporting twice for 2 different accounts. I disputed and asked them to send me variable proof that this debt is accurate, instead I received two letters just giving me a break down of the debt, nothing with my signature, nothing stating that they purchased this debt. And on top of that I never received notice after they purchased these items to allow me time to dispute it before impacting my credit. 




FDCPA Section 809. Validation of debts [ 15 USC 1692g ] ( b ) If the consumer notifies the debt collector in writing within the thirty-day period described in subsection ( a ) that the debt, or any portion thereof, is disputed, or that the consumer requests the name and address of the original creditor, the debt collector shall cease collection of the debt, or any disputed portion thereof, until the debt collector obtains verification of the debt or any copy of a judgment, or the name and address of the original creditor, and a copy of such verification or judgment, or name and address of the original creditor, is mailed to the consumer by the debt collector ...

( b ) If the consumer notifies the debt collector in writing within the thirty-day period described in subsection ( a ) that the debt, or any portion thereof, is disputed, or that the consumer requests the name and address of the original creditor, the debt collector shall cease collection of the debt, or any disputed portion thereof, until the debt collector obtains verification of the debt or any copy of a judgment, or the name and address of the original creditor, and a copy of such verification or judgment, or name and address of the original creditor, is mailed to the consumer by the debt collector ...','U.S. Collections West, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a credit report for a credit report for a credit report for a credit report for a credit report for a credit report for a credit report for a credit report');
