INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2546,'10/04/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I took a withdrawal of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account using a Citibank ATM outside of the branch at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I am also a Citibank customer and attempted to deposit {$900.00} cash into my citi checking account ( {$800.00} from the previous withdrawal and {$100.00} cash ). After attempting to deposit the cash 3 times, the machine gave me credit for {$330.00} and then spit out a error ticket claiming an error occured and to call customer service taking my whole amount of {$900.00}. I immediately went in to the branch and was told there was nothing they can do, and to call Monday. After 7 attempts of reaching someone Monday with no luck, I called Tuesday afternoon and spoke to customer service. I was told they have no information and to contact the branch. I called and spoke to a woman by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she explained they would " escalate '''' my issue.I was called at EOB on Tuesday evening and told the amount would be in my account in the morning and I would be called in the morning. No one called. I called back and was told, I now have to wait 7-10 business days as they are investigating something. They said there is nothing they can do and I need to wait. How is this legal? they have {$600.00} of my money, I have bills, they told me they found the discrepancy and yet I have to wait? I have bills, and a life to live. HOw is this fair that I am being punished due to an ATM Malfunction?','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a customer took a withdrawal of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from my account. he spit out a ticket claiming an error occurred and');
