INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2561,'10/02/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not communicate with all three credit bureaus within 30 days of receiving any of the two letters sent to you that the item in question was in dispute as per the Fair Credit Reporting Act. As proven by my most recent credit report from all three credit bureaus. 
I have disputed a debt and you have failed to report it as disputed with the credit bureaus. 
Protection under the Fair Credit Reporting Act. ( FCRA 623 ) If a consumer notifies a furnisher, at an address specified for the furnisher for such notices, that specific information is inaccurate, and the information is, in fact, inaccurate, the furnisher must thereafter report the correct information to CRAs. Section 623 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( B ).
If a consumer notifies a furnisher that the consumer disputes the completeness or accuracy of any information reported by the furnisher, the furnisher may not subsequently report that information to a CRA without providing notice of the dispute. This identified by an informational line about the dispute added in the comment section of the item on the credit report. Section 623 ( a ) ( 3 ).','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'credit bureaus did not communicate with all three credit bureaus within 30 days. the item in question was in dispute as per the Fair Credit Reporting Act. if a consumer');
