INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2565,'10/01/2017','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] t is a collection agency in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], PA, and has reported three medical collections to the credit bureaus that I do not owe : 1 ) Reported opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$10.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Reported Delinquent XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2 ) Reported opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$20.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Reported Delinquent XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 3 ) Reported opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$340.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Reported Delinquent XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] This is the exact information reported on my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit report ( no full account numbers or name of original creditor ), and I have confirmed with all my doctors that I owe no money. I pay every single medical expense at time of service and have never left an appointment owing any money, period. I have never received anything in the mail from " '''' [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' or any medical provider, nor have I ever received a phone call. It is preposterous that completely false information can be reported to credit bureaus, especially without any details as to where the alleged debt originated. I am contacting my representatives and the Delaware Attorney General ''s Office, where I am currently employed, to find out why this is legal and this company can get away with this. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','BYL Collection Services',2.0,2.0,'a collection agency in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has reported three medical collections to the credit bureaus that I do not owe. a medical collection');
