Thanks, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have requested in writing via fax for them to prove this is a legitimate debt. They have not provided any such proof.','WAKEFIELD & ASSOCIATES, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a letter from Wakefield & Assoc stating that they were representing my dermatologist in collecting an unpaid debt. the amount was for $97.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2573,'09/29/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','Synchrony bank has charged me for a Card Security fee without my authorization and told me they would cease this service and give me a refund within 1 week. I have yet to hear back from the company and yet to hear about anything regarding a refund to my account. The past year I have been receiving a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollar Card Security Fee without my authorization.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'the company has charged me for a card Security fee without my authorization. the company has yet to hear back and yet to hear about any regarding a refund to my account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2574,'09/29/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Regarding complaint # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Ditech ''s answer is quite misleading. The payments were submitted as their customer service rep advised. Later, the story changed and electronic payments are now the problem. Which is correct? [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never addressed the question of whether my information was sent to another customer, just as another customer ''s information was sent to me. I would hope in this day and age, they would be more careful with private information but they sent me another customers papers twice. I would like a written statement from them that my information was never revealed to another customer. Thank you for finally getting to the truth and getting them to admit they changed their platform. I was told several times there were no changes made.','Ditech Financial LLC',4.0,4.0,'ditech''s answer is quite misleading'' regarding complaint #. the payments were submitted as their customer service rep advised. the story changed and electronic payments are now the problem.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2575,'09/28/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','I applied online as a member of Navy Federal Credit Union for a credit card onXX/XX/XXXX2017. Within a few hours in was an online message declining. I called the next day and onXX/XX/XXXX2017 to inquire why but was told the letter was mailed out last week explaining the reasons for being declined. However I never recieved anything so I called again todayXX/XX/XXXX2017 to ask could the letter be resent cause I never recieved it the representative told me no they wont do it. I explained as a consumer there are fair creit laws that state I have a right to be notified. The representative stated they will not email it through their secure online banking website nor resend it. This is pure nonsense things get lost in the mail so it should be no big deal to reprint and mail my credit decision letter. 

This is horrible customer service.','NAVY FEDERAL CREDIT UNION',2.0,2.0,'a credit card application was sent out to the navy. the representative said they will not email it through their secure online banking website.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2576,'09/28/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Equifax has not deleted these unauthorized inquires from my credit report. They sent me a response saying " inquiries are a matter of fact ... .. '''' but they still DID NOT show me where I signed any consent at all. I DID NOT AUTHORIZE these inquiries and there was no investigation done at all. On behalf of the Equifax breach, I STRONGLY wish to have these inquiries deleted because THEY ARE NOT MINE. They did not even delete an inquiry in which the creditor themselves sadi they submitted to them that it should be deleted. I have tried calling Equifax ''s phone number and it hangs up on me every single time. They are purposely not answering their phones to correct their own negligence involving this data breach. I want these inquiries removed promptly.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a credit report sent me a response saying " inquiries are a matter of fact..... '''' but they still DID NOT show me where I signed any consent');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2577,'09/28/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was contacted through mail by Fidelity Information Corporation dba of Fidelity Capital Holdings , INC, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], about a debt they accused me of owing to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The alleged debt was in the amount of {$740.00} to an account referenced as No. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I do not believe this debt to be mine. 

In response I sent a letter via Certified Mail asking for validation of this debt on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The letter was signed for and received by what appears to be a " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

