INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2605,'09/23/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have been trying to get [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to remove late payment history from my account for about 3 years. They accused me of missing a payment, which I had n''t. It started in approximately [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was accused of missing a payment, which I had n''t. After they said I missed the payment, I started accruing late payment fees, etc. I was on a fixed income so it was impossible for me to give them [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments, so I disputed with documentation, and then they would n''t accept the money unless I gave them additional fees, which continued to keep me in arrears. 
They never resolved the issue with me personally, however, there was a class action settlement in which I received a payout of a about {$1000.00} due to payment history errors. While I received the monetary payment, they have not yet corrected the information on my credit report. 
When I ''d have a phone meeting to talk to a account manager they would cancel, reschedule or something last minute. 
They finally approved a modification for me but never reconciled the past due payments that wrongly reported. They show [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] lates because the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment continued to appear in arrears every month. That is incorrect. I would like to have that history removed.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a class action settlement in which I received a payout of $1000.00 was made. the payment history errors have not been corrected.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2606,'09/22/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','This debt of roughly {$680.00} should not have gone to collections, but was created and sent over to a different company originally several months ago due to a mistake made by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This debt is supposedly for a past due balance and non-returned equipment. At the time i was told that if all equipment was returned, the amount due for the equipment AND the past due balance would be closed out, this however was not done. I have told Diversified consultants of this and informed them i have proof that all equipment was returned yet they still contact me daily about this debt. Even after speaking to a " floor manager '''' and setting up a plan to pay off my debt, they are still calling me multiple times. As well, I have never received ANY mail regarding this debt.','Diversified Consultants, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'debt of roughly $680.00 was created and sent over to a different company. this debt is supposedly for a past due balance and non-returned equipment.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2607,'09/22/2017','Checking or savings account','Other banking product or service','Managing an account','I have been a customer of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for about 10 years, and they were purchased by Ally fairly recently. I trade stocks and options regularly, maybe once a month or more on average over that 10 years. I had positive experiences with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and usually fund my account with wire transfers from my credit union. My issue is that Ally is allowing me to use the money WITHIN their system like they are required to, but they are extending holds on my funds of 10 business days. My account is not new, I am not new, I am not risky, I am approved for margin trading, etc. So what is with the extended hold that they refuse to even look at changing? The wires have come from my same checking account for the entire period, so the risk to them that somehow the funds will be attempted to be pulled back is zero. I think under the guise of risk management they are ignoring proper risk management and placing an unnecessary hold time to keep a low cost of funds or encourage more trading with the associated fees to Ally. It ''s ridiculous in my opinion. When I attempted to resolve via chat with an agent, that was also disappointing.','ALLY FINANCIAL INC.',4.0,4.0,'ally has extending hold on my funds of 10 business days. the wires have come from my same checking account for the entire period. the risk to them that somehow the funds');
