INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2613,'09/21/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I received a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that my loans were being transferred to FedLoan Servicing because I qualified for PSLF. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a letter from FedLoan stating that my previous employment had been approved and that I was in a qualifying repayment plan. I was told they would track how many remaining payments I had to satisfy the 120 payments needed for forgiveness. After my account continuously said 0 qualifying payments, I contacted FedLoans to inquire. The customer service representative stated that I had made several late payments outside of the 15 day grace period. I told her this was inaccurate because I had always been on automatic deductions since I started repayment of my federal loans. I was told in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that it would take 90 days for the information from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to be in their system. After speaking with them on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was told that they would have to re review it and it would be another 60 days. The customer service rep said that she was not qualified to review my file. This contradicts what I was told in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I was told that everything was approved.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a customer service representative said that I had made several late payments outside of the 15 day grace period. the customer service representative said that it would take 90 days for the information to be in');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2614,'09/21/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','Citibank is engaging in deceptive business practices, allowing vendor ''s, merchants to place reoccurring charges on the consumer credit card without the consumer knowledge or consent. 

Each time I had to reach out to Citibank for reoccurring charges the only remedies provided is the consumer having to closed out existing card and open a new card.
I had to change cards ( 4 ) times in the last year due to Citibank allowing vendors merchants to access and charge my account at will and without my consent.
Citibank is claiming that if the merchant claims membership or some sort of dues they have the right to submit authorization for reoccurring charges without any documentation or consumer signature authorizing said reoccurring transactions.
The consumer is under the impression that only authorization provided is for a one time charge neither the vendors, merchants or Citibank is disclosing reoccurring charges were set-up allowing unauthorized charges to be placed on the consumers account and Citibank making monies off the additional interest charged.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citibank is engaging in deceptive business practices allowing vendor''s, merchants to place reoccurring charges on the consumer credit card without the consumer knowledge or consent ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2615,'09/21/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I recently transferred my loans from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in hopes of eventually pursuing public service loan forgiveness. After taking nearly 3 months to complete the transfer, Fed loans have incorrectly counted the amount of qualifying payments towards PSLF that I have made ( they count only 12, while my records show 28 qualifying payments ). I call them to discussed this and spoke with employee ID [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who stated that she agreed that it appears that an error has been made on their part, but states that it would take a minimum of 3 MORE months to correct.
I can not understand what about counting payments takes 3 months to do. I understand that these payments must be deemed " qualified '''', but this company has already had my records 3 months. Now they want another 3 months. It can not possible take HALF A YEAR to correctly count payments, can it? 

I need to make life-altering decisions over the next few months that might be affected by my faith in this program ''s ability to do what they have promised.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a loan company has already had my records 3 months to correct. it can not take HALF A YEAR to correctly count payments. it can not take HALF A YEAR');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2616,'09/21/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I disputed an account on my credit report that I had no knowledge of. Was supposed to be finished on X/XX/17 and its still not resolved. Ive called all companies and theres no resolution and its been longer than 30 days','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'disputed an account on my credit report that I had no knowledge of. was supposed to be finished on X/XX/17 and its still not resolved.');
