INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2621,'09/20/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','I pay bills the day I receive them, and I always pay my credit card bills in full. And because I am uncomfortable with electronic means, I insist on receiving a MAILED paper monthly statement. 

So when I am charged {$25.00} for a late fee, it either means that the letter carrier somehow " lost '''' the statement, or the bank did n''t send me one.
In the past few years I have been charged over and over for paying late. I suspect that the credit card company ( in this case Bank of America ), declines to mail a paper statement every few months to customers who pay in full their balances.
I have paid " late fees '''' over and over in the past few years, and I am tired of it. One or two of those I may have misplaced and was thus legitimately charged, but the majority of them I did not receive.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a paper monthly statement is a monthly statement. the company declines to mail a statement every few months to customers. the company declines to mail a statement every few');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2622,'09/20/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I attended school online via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University as well as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] College from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At the time I was unaware that my high school diploma was from an unaccredited school. I contacted my loan servicer to make arrangements to pay back my loans which are totaled at {$48000.00}. I received a letter from a debt collection agency stating they ''d purchased my loans from the Department of Education. I contacted the Department of Education once again on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to make arrangements to pay back my loans but was redirected to the debt collection agency and no one answered so I left a voicemail. These student loans are updating monthly showing a negative status and impacting my ability to purchase a home and I am unable to contact anyone to make payments or arrangements to bring the loans current. These loans have also affected my ability to gain employment which is kind of contradictory. If I ca n''t get another job due to these loans, how am I supposed to pay them back? I ''ve tried for months to contact someone with no response.','NELNET, INC.',2.0,2.0,'student loans are updating monthly showing a negative status. if I can''t get another job due to these loans, how am I supposed to pay back them?');
