INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2659,'09/14/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with fraud alerts or security freezes','I am one of the 143M Americans whose credit information was compromised by the recent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] data breach. I have worked many hours to try to understand and respond to the situation, and I am still not out of the woods. It appears the most complete level of protection for my information is a security freeze, which will cost {$10.00} in my state, Texas. Though I may get it free from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who has announced no-charge freezes and thaws for a few weeks, for those whose information has been accessed. ( I do n''t know yet if this applies to me, whose information " may have been '''' exposed in this breach, as expressed in their web tool in which I entered the last 6 digits of my SSN- how come they ca n''t just say yes or no?? ). I would strongly suggest that ALL credit reporting agencies offer free freezes and thaws upon request from any customer ( with appropriate ID verification ). Forever. And that they notify us any time that anyone has requested our information. These agencies are making money on OUR information, and I do n''t recall giving them the OK to share that. If that ''s what they do, they should be totally accountable for the safety and privacy of that information. 
At this time I do not think anyone has committed any fraud against me, but the danger is clear. I believe any credit reporting agency, business operation or bank which uses people ''s SSN ''s and financial information must be held totally responsibly for any losses the person sustains.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',4.0,6.0,'143 million americans whose credit information was compromised by recent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] data breach. a security freeze, which will cost $');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2660,'09/13/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with fraud alerts or security freezes','I was part of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit information hack. It is unacceptable that I have to PAY to freeze my credit when I did n''t consent to my information being stored by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the first place. 

