INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2665,'09/13/2017','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Virtual currency','Confusing or missing disclosures','I transferred [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PAY tokens ( TenX Cryptocurrency ) from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account ( another exchange ) 47 days and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hours ago ( on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PST ) into my Ethereum wallet at Coinbase. 
Since the PAY tokens are an ERC 20 token ( ethereum platform ) I thought they ''d be no issues. The transfer was successful and delivered to my Ethereum wallet at Coinbase. I ''m still new to crypto currency trading, so I viewed this transaction as any other financial transactions ... if wrong address or not supported, the transfer would be rejected or worst case scenario reversed back.
However this is not the case, although the tokens are currently sitting in my Ethereum wallet, I can not access them because Coinbase does not support this specific crypto currency. They ''ll accept the transfer in, but will not allow you to access them.
Only Coinbase has the private key to my wallet to access the tokens, but they refuse to send back the tokens, saying it would be too much work for them. The ability to fix the problem is available but they are not willing to do it. I am not the only one who made this mistake in the past, I ''ve read in various forums of similar cases where the transactions were reversed, so it is definitely possible. The problem now is that Coinbase has grown so much and so fast that they have not scaled their support staff to match the number of users.
The value of my tokens at the peak, a week or so after the transaction went up to over {$410000.00} - now the value has dropped to below {$110000.00} I ''m fine with the fluctuation in price, I just want my tokens returned. I ''m afraid someone there might steal the tokens or a hacker might take them, since the amount is quite large I would prefer to store them in my hard wallet ( offline ).
This is such a new field, I understand my explanation might be a bit hard to follow so below is a quick summary.
Sent crypto currency from one exchange ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to another ( Coinbase ), Coinbase accepted the transfer but because they do n''t support the tokens, they will not allow me to access them to transfer or sell.
Coinbase can access them by retrieving the private key to my wallet but refuses to do so because they said it would be a lot of work for them. They felt this was my mistake and I ''m essentially out of luck.
I disagree because Coinbase is a financial institution, if they do n''t support this token they should of rejected the transfer or at least reverse it, instead they are keeping the tokens and refusing to retrieve the private key to my wallet, which only them can have access to it. 
Thank you for your help. Please let me know if there ''s anything else you need from me. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Coinbase, Inc.',10.0,10.0,'the transfer was successful and delivered to my Ethereum wallet at Coinbase. the tokens are currently sitting in my Ethereum wallet. only Coinbase has the private key to access the tokens');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2666,'09/13/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with fraud alerts or security freezes','I am one of the 140 million American whose data was exposed by the Equifax breach. In order to protect my credit and my financial future, I now have to freeze my credit with all three credit bureaus, including Equifax. As Equifax charges a fee for this freezing, they are essentially charging me for their own negligence and profiting off of this situation. I should not have to pay for this company ''s negligence.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'i am one of the 140 million americans exposed by the breach. I have to freeze my credit with all three credit bureaus, including Equifax.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2667,'09/13/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a due date change was conducted with Toyota Financial Services for my monthly car payments for my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It was changed from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month. My monthly payments are {$450.00}. I have never been late on any of these payments and my contract gives me a 15 day grace period where no late fees or interest charges will be held against me. I sometimes pay the full amount on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day, or I ''ll split the payment in half and pay half on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and half on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or whatever date lands on 15 days. Ever since my due date change I started getting calls from Toyota Financial Services about being late or my payments not being received. Each time I would stay on the phone for an hour ( being bounced around ) explaining what my contract says and how my due date was changed. Each time this information was always confirmed and the call was always ended with an apology. I get these same phone calls at least twice a month. I then checked my credit report and saw that Toyota Financial Services reported a 30 day late marker to my credit report for the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This greatly affected my credit score. When I called and asked them about it they admitted that they never updated my due date change in their system, which caused every payment to show up late. They once again apologized and said they would send a letter to all 3 credit bureaus on their behalf. The late marker for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was removed, but then I received ANOTHER 30 day late marker on my report for XXXXI called them on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to get this resolved and was once again bounced around on the phone for over a hour, just to hear a manager tell me " I honestly ca n''t give you an answer as to why this is happening. '''' This whole experience has been dreadful. Credit is everything and a company should n''t have the right to keep reporting false negative marks. Especially when they ca n''t even give you a reason why.','TOYOTA MOTOR CREDIT CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a due date change was conducted with Toyota Financial Services for my monthly payments for my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2668,'09/13/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with fraud alerts or security freezes','I have had immense difficulty in trying to freeze my credit with all reporting agencies. After the hack that stole data from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], freezing my credit should be free across the board at minimum. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] yet, they should automatically freeze all credit until you unfreeze it.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a hack stole data from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the hack should be free across the board at minimum.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2669,'09/13/2017','Mortgage','VA mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I received a letter from Wells Fargo in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that they have charged me late fees for the months of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They further stated that the late fees were for payments received on the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the month. This is contrary to the monthly statement, ( a legal document ) which is sent out by Wells Fargo which clearly states that late payments are those that are received after the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the month. I have attached and circled a monthly statement showing where Wells Fargo is saying that late payment is after the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the month. This lines up with the terms of the VA loan at close. 
It is not true that I was late either of those months, and both payments were received on or before the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In fact in nearly 10 years of payments, I have only one payment that showed up a few days late. In the month of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Wells received electronic payment on the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Wells received electronic payment on the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], both on time according to the monthly statement furnished by Wells saying late after the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ],  which again is in-line with the terms of the VA closing contract That contract has been made available before here at CFPB during the 3 years of complaints lodge here against Wells Fargo.. 
Over the past 3 years [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been many things in its relationship with me, but professional is not a term I would choose. Every month they send late statements before the payment deadline. They use that to pilfer the very solvent escrow account by taking money that would otherwise be place in escrow and put it in an undeclared funds account. They manufacture and enable this misapplication by pretending that the account is late, when in fact is its not late until after the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] according to both the Veterans administration and Wells own statement, ( see attachment ). 
They have back tracked numerous occasions, including having to restore miss appropriated funds, falsely billed for shortages then a few months later and send me checks for overages. These backtracks only happen after Wells burdens me to complain and escalate those complaints before they act. They have been inconsistent and certainly not meeting the bar expected for accounting professionalism and ethics. I am, like many others, without trust in Wells Fargo, due to the lack of honesty and their abuse of laws. I really dont understand why the Federal Government continues to do business with them.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'Wells Fargo has sent a letter to the CFPB stating late fees are for payments received on the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONY');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2670,'09/13/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with fraud alerts or security freezes','I attempted to instate a credit freeze with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Experian, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. All attempts failed beginning at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PST. It looks like I will have to either call in the middle of the night, or do this by mail. 

