INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2689,'09/11/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax mishandled my information which has led to a breach that puts myself and millions of others at potential risk. I am extremely disappointed with how equifax has handled reporting this breach. Very little was done to notify the public for nearly a month after the breach was detected. I received no email, letter, or phone call and instead had to discover it via social media.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'equifax has handled reporting this breach. equifax has not been notified for nearly a month.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2690,'09/11/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','First let me start with I have been on file noted with the Federal trade as a victim of ID theft and it is clearly noted on my credit bureau files that I am the victim of identity theft, yet I still have all these credit inquiries which are negatively impacting my credit ... I did find out that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about 2 months ago removed everyones credit inquiries and then put them back on, without sending a 5 day reinsertion letter which is a violation of 6.11 of the Fair Credit Reporting Act. I did call in this morning and was on hold with operator, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding both issues. She is stating she is not able to do anything for me. I did notify her that I would be filing a complaint with both the CFPB and the Attorney Generals Office. 
All inquiries made against my social should be removed. I have not attempted to purchase or open any accounts. I am just finding out about all of this since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have been desperately trying to fix this disaster.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a credit bureau file noted that I am the victim of identity theft. but all these credit inquiries are negatively impacting my credit. a 5 day reinsertion letter is ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2691,'09/11/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Payday loan','Problem with the payoff process at the end of the loan','I applied for a loan with Big picture loans for only a small amount of {$600.00}. I was approved and had the information sent to me via email. The interest rate was 694.669 % APR. I knew I only had a small amount of time to cancel and so I tried calling there [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number and was either on hold for an hour and had to hang up, or was disconnected multiple times. After the deadline had passed I realized that my only other option was to just pay it off as soon as I possibly could. 

The loan started the day I received the funds [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
The loan states that I will pay {$160.00} on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the last day of the month in accordance to my paydays for a year. I knew I would n''t have the full amount by the first payment on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] plus the interest so I submitted a payment online for {$250.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

My daily interest rate is 1.91507 % as stated in the loan documents. So on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my {$250.00} payment should have left me with a principal balance of : {$430.00} and then when my normal installment of {$160.00} came out on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I should have had a balance of : {$300.00}. However when I checked on my account online on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to see what my priniciple balance was so I could put in for another {$250.00} payment it was above {$530.00}. The website still showed a " pending '''' payment of {$250.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I took a screen shot of this and called them. When I spoke with someone she repeatedly put me on hold, gave me ridiculous reasons for the online payment not being submitted ( like you placed your payment online before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] pm and that why it is still " pending '''' ), and finally after being on hold over and over again for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes they said they could submit the payment now but it would not be able to go through until Monday or Tuesday the next week because they need to processes this. Which made no sense because it was Thursday at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] pm. It should be processed immediately. However they lady I spoke with said that I would still be charged for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] more days of interest while it was " processing ''''. After a long phone call with someone who I struggled communicating with and needing to get back to work I said fine just process the payment. 

They did process the next {$160.00} payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but nothing for the {$250.00} and on the website it states I have a " pending '''' payment of {$500.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so to stop them from collecting anymore money [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or more money then they should be [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I closed that bank account and sent a certified, signature required piece of mail to them with a check for {$250.00}. Which once they received that I got an email stating that I had a returned payment of {$250.00}. I cancelled the check I sent to them 5 days after receiving that email, not seeing it clear my bank account/ or post to my big picture loans account, and after not receiving my check in the mail for fear someone else might use that check. ( I have had numerous credit cards be stolen from my mail box along with other mail, and did n''t want to take the chance of the check being stolen as well. ) I strongly feel that they have been bullying me into paying more money in interest then I should by not processing my extra payments. I have printed screen shots of my account with them and I have emails they sent to me. I have paid them a total of {$320.00} and my account is currently at {$560.00}. If they had processed all the payments I have tried to send them it would be paid off by now.','Big Picture Loans, LLC',2.0,4.0,'the loan states that I will pay $160.00 on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the last day of the month in accordance to my payday');
