INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2697,'09/10/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','My information was compromise in the Equifax security breach on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Also, why did the public just learn of this breach in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when Equifax knew in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? Equifax should pay to have my credit frozen.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a breach on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was compromised by the breach. the public should have my credit frozen.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2698,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','Equifax lacked basic security to protect my consumer information from cyber attack.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax lacked basic security to protect my consumer information from cyber attack.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2699,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax mishandled my information which has led to a breach that puts myself and millions of others at potential risk. I am extremely disappointed with how Equifax has handled reporting this breach. Very little was done to notify the public for nearly a month after the breach was detected. I received no email, letter, or phone call and instead had to discover it via social media.
Equifax has mishandled my information, did n''t notify me, and now has cost me several hours, some money ( to freeze my credit with three bureaus ) and will continue soaking my time and money to deal with paying for and unfreezing reports as necessary in the future.
Going forward Equifax should be required to monitor every account and notify victims if any fraud occurs. Credit fraud protection should be mandatory for every account, not an option for us to have deal with.
This should be rectified firstly by making credit freezing free and refunding everyone who paid for it following this data breach. Requiring a police report is absurd when they clearly know if you were affected.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'Equifax mishandled my information andn''t notify me. a month after the breach was detected, I received no email, letter, or phone call. a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2700,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','The massive hack/breach at Experian exposed my personal information. I have put a fraud alert onto my account, and will need to be extra vigilant to make sure my identity is not stolen.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'the massive hack/breach at Experian exposed my personal information. I have put a fraud alert onto my account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2701,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mishandled my information which has led to a breach that puts myself and millions of others at risk. I am extremely disappointed with how [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has handled reporting this breach. Very little was done to notify the public for nearly a month after the breach was detected. I received no email, letter, or phone call and instead had to discover it via social media.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mishandled my information which has led to a breach. a breach puts me and millions of others at risk.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2702,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Equifax announced a cybersecurity incident impacting approximately 143 million U.S. consumers. The information accessed primarily includes names, Social Security numbers, birth dates, addresses and, in some instances, driver ''s license numbers. In addition, credit card numbers for approximately 209,000 U.S. consumers, and certain dispute documents with personal identifying information for approximately 182,000 U.S. consumers, were accessed. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I used the https : //www.equifaxsecurity2017.comXXXX website to check my impact. I received the following information : " Based on the information provided, we believe that your personal information may have been impacted by this incident. '''' As of today [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have not been able to get any further information from Equifax about the status of my credit, whether my information is secure, how it was released, why I was not informed earlier, or why I am not able to get credit monitoring immediately ( see below ). 

Although Equifax is offering credit monitoring, they have not yet allowed me access. Creating a further problem for me and my credit, Equifax is covering the credit monitoring for only one year. Malicious parties who stole my information can sell this information on black markets and simply wait one year to begin exploiting my data to steal my identity and illegally get credit in my name. 

Equifax did not secure my information with appropriate best-standard practices. My credit and financial life are now at risk and very vulnerable to fraud. Equifax did not properly disclose this breach to me. I learned about it on the news rather than directly - they have my contact information therefore should have notified me directly as their customer. Additionally Equifax has failed to provide sufficient information or protection for me and my credit/financial data. 

Equifax did not properly secure my protected personal information from intrusion, such as through appropriate patching, 2-factor authentication at the point of service, segmentation of data, etc. As such, it appears my full name, Social Security numbers, birth date, addresses, and possibly driver license number is cross-matched to each other and in the hands of criminals who can use this data to breach any number of accounts in perpetuity such as my banking and financial data, medical data, legal complaints, political data, and any other number of sensitive accounts.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'143 million americans are affected by a cybersecurity incident. the information accessed includes names, social security numbers, birth dates, addresses and driver''s license numbers. credit');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2703,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','The Equifax credit reporting organization has allowed unknown persons access to my personal information that could be used to effectively destroy my life. They ''ve allowed access to my Social Security Number and much of my personally identifiable information that could be used to open fraudulent credit cards and bank loans that could destroy my credit ( also managed by Equifax ) which would make it impossible in the future to apply for loans that I would need such as for a newer vehicle. This is not even a service I want from Equifax but they have been given my information and have effectively distributed it. They ''ve potentially stolen and sold my identity ; a crime. Now I have to look over my shoulder every day to hopefully protect myself from invisible pickpockets and thieves.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'the credit reporting organization has allowed unknown persons access to my personal information that could be used to effectively destroy my life. they have allowed access to my Social Security Number and much of my personally identifiable');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2704,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','It ''s been recently reported that equifax was hacked and personal information leaked. Through their provided site it shows that I am impacted by this','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'equifax was hacked and personal information leaked.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2705,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax mishandled my personal information including Name, Social Security #, Address, Birthdate, etc. resulting in a data breach in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2017 that they confirmed I was affected by per their " Potential Impact '''' site www.equifaxsecurity2017.com. 

They have put me and millions of others at risk of identity theft/fraud due to negligent security protocols in handling consumer information. They ''re attempting to capitalize on the situation by signing injured parties up for " trial periods '''' of their ID protection services. 

They are simultaneously defrauding these injured parties with hidden terms of service that waive their right to sue the company in what is clearly a situation of criminal negligence/fraudulent behavior as indicated by the three Equifax executives that dumped stock immediately prior to the data breach announcement.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'Equifax has put me and millions of others at risk of identity theft/fraud due to negligent security protocols in handling consumer information. they are simultaneously defrauding injured parties with hidden');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2706,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Upon investigating the potential of my personal information, my identity itself, of being exposed to the recent Equifax breach it was indicated that my information was indeed placed at risk by the breach. I did not feel comfortable signing up for a repair service offered by the very company that allowed the breach to take place and am leery about the terms of agreement regarding this service potential to smuggle agreement of non-action against Equifax. I feel this concern is warranted considering the potential unethical dumping of company stock shortly before the announcement of the breach a full month after the breach actually occurred.','EQUIFAX, INC.',4.0,4.0,'a repair service offered by the very company allowed the breach to take place. a full month after the breach, I was able to investigate the potential of my personal information.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2707,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I contacted USAA to inquire as to why my credit card reporting status showed under adverse accounts on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  report.I was never late with the account. I was advised that the company closed the account and that is why it is reporting as adverse. I specified the company closed the account because I had to go through a credit counseling agency to get an interest reduction and the stipulation for the reduction was that the account be closed. USAA would not negotiate a lower interest with me even though I was not late. I was instructed to dispute the account with the reporting agency [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 
I filed a dispute with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because USAA stated they would not change the status. Initially, it appeared as closed. However, the completion of the investigation with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  now shows the account is being managed by a financial counseling program. This addition to my report caused a decline in which my score went from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. If USAA did n''t have that notation on my credit report before hand why did they feel compelled to place it on my credit report now.','UNITED SERVICES AUTOMOBILE ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a credit card reporting agency has closed the account. the report was based on my credit report. the report was based on the company''s decision to close the account ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2708,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','My information was leaked by the Equifax hack which is information that will affect me forever, however, they have no solution to protect my credit reports. The only thing they offer is to protect it for a year after which I have to pay them for the service -- essentially, they are charging me to protect my data that they leaked.','EQUIFAX, INC.',4.0,4.0,'the only thing they offer is to protect my credit reports. they charge me to protect my data that they leaked.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2709,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Unable to get your credit report or credit score','First off, due to the data breach with Equifax, I do n''t feel that I should have to pay them {$10.00} to initiate a credit freeze. I would n''t have done so if they had n''t had the security breach. Now, they are profiting due to their own ineptness. 1 year of credit monitoring is n''t sufficient as a response either. They need to offer a free credit freeze to anyone who is affected by the breach and their own website said that I was. 

Despite the above concern, I initiated a credit freeze with Equifax ( and the other two ) and then went to pull my credit report at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The Equifax site said " The System is Currently Down for Maintenance ''''. Unacceptable. I went back in again and it let me get all the way to verifying my identify before the system went down again with the same message. Still unacceptable. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has a similar issue where the report would not generate.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'despite the above concern, I initiated a credit freeze with Equifax. they need to offer a free credit freeze to anyone affected by the breach. the report would not generate');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2710,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax recently announced a massive data breach. I have used the website they set up to confirm my information was compromised. They have not provided me written notification that my information was compromised, and have not provided details on exactly what information of mine was compromised. 

By failing to personally notify my of which data of mine they compromised they are placing the investigative burden on me. They are making me responsible for finding out if they compromised my information. 

Once I determined that some of my information had been compromised ( but not details of which information ), the only recourse they offer is one year of " free '''' credit monitoring by their service. They are leveraging the problem they created to benefit their business. While they may not have created the situation, it has the appearance of a shakedown scheme. 

The risks Equifax has exposed me to are serious. Their response has been anything but. They have failed to provide adequate notification to those they placed at risk and failed to assume responsibility for placing them at risk. I consider this especially egregious since I do not have a consumer relationship of any sort with Equifax ; they store my information for the benefit of themselves and their customers, yet it is me currently facing the risks of their negligence.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax has announced a massive data breach. they have not personally informed me of which data of mine they compromised. they are making me responsible for finding out if they compromised my');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2711,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017 On this day I found out that my information, ALL of my personal identifying information, had been compromised in the breach of Equifax. I was not contacted. I had to learn about it from first social media, then the news. I had to do the legwork to see if my information was compromised. 

This information, trusted within this company, is everything required to steal my identity, disable fraud alerts, unfreeze freeze ''s that I place on my credit, fraudulently file taxes, etc. Now this information is in who knows who ''s hands, and unless more secure safeguards are put into place to protect it in the future, I will ALWAYS have to worry about identity theft because of Equifax ''s lax cybersecurity. 

I do not believe that the social security number is enough protection anymore. Technology continues to advance, however the social security number does not. I believe modern safeguards need to be used to authenticate and identify the person, and as soon as such is put into place, the reliance on social security numbers needs to be ended, and that they should be public knowledge, just like a license plate number or drivers license number. 

I believe Equifax needs to make this situation right. I am disgusted that for the foreseeable future, nothing I can do will make my identity safe, nothing I do will make my credit safe. I should not have to be doing all this legwork when I have done nothing wrong. I certainly should not have to pay to make my compromised credit slightly more secure. Equifax needs to act to protect us moving forwards.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'if more safeguards are put into place to protect identity theft, we will have to worry about identity theft because of the lax cybersecurity. if more safeguards are put into place');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2712,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax was hacked and based on their own website check, my personal information may have been impacted by the hack. They did not agree to have my personal information released to hackers, so the information in my credit report was used improperly.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax hacked my personal information based on their own website check. they did not agree to have my personal information released to hackers.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2713,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax mishandled my information which has led to a breach that puts myself and millions of others at potential risk. Equifax has been negligent in handling this breach. Very little was done to notify the public for nearly a month after the breach was detected. I received no email, letter, or phone call and instead had to discover it via social media. 

A company that can not properly handle sensitive information should not be trusted and consumers should not be responsible for rectifying the issue.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax has been negligent in handling this breach. a company that can not properly handle sensitive information should not be trusted.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2714,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','Thursday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I logged on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] website to see If my personal data had been involved in the hacker security breach. Clicking the " Check Potential Impact '''' button automatically enrolled me in TrustedID [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was not given any option to decline this service and I did not agree to this. I do not want this service.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'logged on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] website to see if my personal data had been involved in the hacker security breach. clicking the " Check Potential');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2715,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Today, X/X/17, Equifax mishandled my information, putting myself and so many millions of other people at risk of identity theft, for the rest of our lives. I was informed by Equifax that I am affected by this data breach. They have shared all of my data, some that can never be changed, with who knows who - with everyone, essentially. My private data is now public, and there is no going back, for the rest of my life. 

Free freezing of my credit should be offered ; that they can now profit, indefinitely, from their negligence by charging me to freeze my credit, or to monitor it after a short period, is unacceptable. They failed completely in their most basic duty : protecting personal information from identity theft. They ''ve compiled massive amounts of data on millions of people, and failed to safeguard it, essentially handing over this data to scam artists on a silver platter.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'X/X/17, X/X, mishandled my information, putting me and millions of others at risk of identity theft. they have shared all of my data');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2716,'09/09/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','My entire life is tied to my social security number which was handled with improper care by Equifax. I consider thier negligence which lead to this breech to be pretty serious. Equifax has no business handling confidential information and I had no choice in giving them my most crucial personal information in order to be part of society to begin with.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'thier negligence led to this breech. thier negligence was handled by Equifax.');
