I am deeply disturbed not only be the fact that they allowed this breach to take place but that they waited three months to notify impacted individuals about the breach.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a part of the breach was not notified for three months. I have not been informed about exactly WHAT information was compromised.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2721,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Today, Equifax released a press release that there was a breach in there system from mid XX/XX/XXXXuntil XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Around 143 million US had their information stolen due to unsatisfactory security techniques utilized by Equifax.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'around 143 million americans had their information stolen due to unsatisfactory security techniques.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2722,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','Equifax has told me that my identity has likely been compromised because of their service ''s improper handling of my credit information. I am not willing to give up my legal rights in exchange for their freeze/monitoring offer. I should not have to give up my right to sue for damages in exchange for these services.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax has told me that my identity has likely been compromised. I should not give up my legal rights in exchange for their freeze/monitoring offer.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2723,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','The Equifax security breach media release provided a website where you could check if your information was breached and have enrollment to a credit protection plan to monitor your record for 1 year.
I went to the website where it confirmed my information was part of the breach and I was eligible to enroll. I selected the enroll button, entered some information, and was presented a message that I needed to follow the line and click ''continue '' to complete the enrollment process. I followed the instructions, but when I did the ''continue '', it returned to the check if data was breached - - it just kept circling in the verify your eligibility screens, One message said because I chose to enroll, that I would not receive further notices from Equifax on any credit breaches. 

I then called the phone number on their website to contact them ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). It answered with a greeting, but then disconnected. 

In short : They offer free credit monitoring enrollment, but the website will not allow you to enroll, and by making the enrollment attempt, you relieve them from their obligation to keep you informed. They offer a phone contact for questions/support, but the phone number does not work.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the website was a breach and it confirmed my information was breached. it was sent to the website where it confirmed my information was part of the breach. it returned to the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2724,'09/08/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','The amount of {$8500.00} is being reported by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as in " Collection ''''. This account has truly stumped me because it was originally owned by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which I believe from the bit of research that I ''ve done, was owned by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].
The confusing thing about this debt is that it was recently opened a year ago but was never reported in collections before that by the original creditor or any other party. There was no letter to verify that I own the debt. It also states that I am a co-signer for the account ; I believe this to be untrue.
I have contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to verify the debt and have also disputed it several times. I have also disputed it with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they have also refused to verify the debt, simply stating in the " remarks '''' section as, " Dispute resolved : reported by grantor ''''.
