Thank you.','Dream Center Education Holdings',2.0,2.0,'the amount of $8500.00 is being reported by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as in " Collection');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2725,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Other personal consumer report','Incorrect information on your report','mI have contacted Early Warning by phone and by mail and made them aware that they are continuing to report fraudulent information against me, and I have informed them that the accounts that they are reporting were as a result of identity theft. Early Warning has told me that they do not care that they will not stop reporting this information unless the banks themselves tell them to not report this fraudulent information. I tried to explain to Early Warning in Writing and by phone that this was fraudulent information and that these accounts were opened when my identity was compromised in 2010, but again they have told me they are not concerned. I have sent them requests to delete this fraudulent information by phone and by certified mail and they have ignored my requests. I have made them aware that they were defaming my character and they were ruining me financially by continuing to report these fraudulent accounts and they have again told me that they refused to stop reporting this fraudulent information.
The fraudulent accounts they are reporting are the following : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Routing Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Account Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Routing Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Account Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Routing Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Account Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The above accounts were opened in my name using my correct personal information fraudulently and Early Warning refuses to do anything about it but to continue defaming my character by disseminating information they have been told was fraudulent.','EARLY WARNING SERVICES, LLC',2.0,4.0,'mI have contacted Early Warning by phone and by mail and made them aware that they are continuing to report fraudulent information against me. they have told me that they do not care that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2726,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','I am filing a complaint in regards to the recent Equifax security breach -- according to the Equifax impact inquiry site ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), checking my information indicates a strong likelihood that I was impacted and that my information was compromised. 

Equifax did NOT contact me about their security breach, and took no measures to alert me about my information being compromised, despite having it on their record and having access to my contact information. Issuing a national press release is not an acceptable substitution.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a complaint is filed in regards to the recent security breach. checking my information indicates a strong likelihood that I was impacted.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2727,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Unable to get your credit report or credit score','There was a major security breach at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I found out about this on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] today ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Not from the company, not from any other bureau, but on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( thank you [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I checked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it told me my information was likely compromised, but that I should contact them on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to take further action. At that point I decided to freeze my credit through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and TransUnion. Not only is this inconvenient for me, but I had to pay a total of {$20.00} to do this. So, in essence, I am having to fund the company that lost my information in order for them to agree not to further release my information. That is unacceptable. 

I also find the entire credit reporting racket to be unacceptable. We can not track our own credit scores without paying for a service. We can only get credit reports for free once a year. There are no posted guidelines on how to improve your score because each place has their own proprietary way of handling things. 

Identity theft is just going to get worse if we insist on having everything tied to a social security number. Giving these credit bureaus full control over all the buying power of Americans, without them having to say how to improve your standing is also terrible. This should be a wakeup call that this needs to change. It is only going to get worse if it does n''t.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a major security breach at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was reported. the company that lost my information was unable to track its own credit scores. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2728,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2017, Equifax announced that a hacker obtained information about 143 million consumers. This data included Social Security numbers, birth dates, addresses and, in some cases, driver license numbers.
Users can check if their information has been compromised by going to equifaxsecurity2017.com. It was determined my information may have been compromised as part of the attack.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a hacker obtained information about 143 million consumers. this included social security numbers, birth dates, addresses and driver license numbers.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2729,'09/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','A child support agency in North Carolina sent information to Credit Bureau ( Experian ) for child support arrears in ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and only after i applied for a modification of my orfer. Before this i was never reported to thus or any other credit bureau ... and these arrears are from the year [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
