INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2746,'09/08/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Written notification about debt','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2017 I received a letter from Northstar Location Services , LLC, about a debt they were trying to collect in the amount of {$32000.00}. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I sent them a letter requesting them to, among other things, establish their ownership of the debt, verification of the debt, and information about their authority to collect the debt. This letter was sent via USPS certified mail, and received in their office XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a series of account statements, which appeared to be in my name, for a debt I do not recognize. There was no information about their ownership of the debt, their authority to collect the debt, the status of their debt collection license ( if any ), etc. All of this information, and more, had been requested in my original letter, as well as my assertion the debt was disputed. To date, this company has failed to provide any of this information.
They have, however, began to call my elderly mother, and presumably other people, despite the fact they are clearly able to communicate with me via mail, and despite my written request that they do in fact communicate with me by mail. There is no reason for them to be contacting others in an attempt to " locate '''' me.
As a result I believe this firm to be in clear violation of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act. They have failed to verify the debt, their authority to collect this debt, and their ownership thereof. And finally, they are needlessly contacting third-parties to " obtain location information '''' when we are already in written correspondence, a tactic which seems closer to harassment of my family than a good-faith effort to find me.
I have attached my written response to their original letter.
Thank you for your attention to this matter.','Northstar Location Services, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a letter from Northstar Location Services, LLC, was sent to them. they asked them to establish their ownership of the debt, verify the debt. they have failed to provide');
