INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2750,'09/07/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Payday loan','Was approved for a loan, but didn''t receive the money','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I applied for a payday loan for {$1500.00} through a website I found through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received an e-mail from usfastcash with a loan approval letter that was attached to the e-mail that I was approved for a loan. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called to confirmed and and spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I register my bank account at bofl federal account to have the loan sent to. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me that they do n''t do business with that bank so he asked if I can have the loan processed through my credit card and I gave him my credit card information. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  told me that in order to get the money that I must buy [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift card for {$100.00} and pressured me that I must do it within 1 hour. I went to the rite-aid store and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me while I was in the store before I even had the chance to call him and asked me am I at the store. He told me to buy 4 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift cards worth up to {$400.00} and I must buy it through a credit card. The cashier told me that they only accept cash payments. so I left the store and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the phone and he started arguing with me asking me why did I have him on the phone at the cashier and did n''t tell the cashier that I was buying the gift cards for my own personal use. I told him that instead of processing my money through my credit card I rather collect the loan through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he told me that its going to charge me {$100.00} at the check cashing place. So I called him 2 more times and he was always appearing to be very aggressive with me on the phone so he calmed down and told me that if I want to collect the laon through moneygram I must go buy 1 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift card for {$100.00}. I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s and bought 1 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift card of {$100.00} purchased through a credit card. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] again and gave him the code on the back of the card and find myself repeating the process several times because he was getting the numbers wrong. Within 5 minutes after being placed on hold I was then told by his manager that I must purchase 4 more gift cards of {$100.00} so I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s again and was told that I can not make credit card transactions over {$100.00} of the gift cards so [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me again and asked did I buy the gift cards and I told him I could n''t buy the gift cards with the credit card and it lead to an argument and I told him that I will report you then he threatened to tell him he is sending the police to my house to arrest me for threatening him and he is suing me so he hung up the phone on me, he calls again 5 minutes later and tell me to go to another store and buy those 4 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift cards {$100.00} each and I told him okay. He calls me 20 minutes later and ask me am I at the store yet and I told him I am on my way then he lied and told me that I was lying to him and I am at my residence which is a lie so he immediately called the police on me through 3 way then he hung up. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] calls again 5 minutes later with a police officer in my jurisdiction in a 3-way call and lied to the police that I was defrauding him, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  also lied to me and the police officer that he called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] store where I bought the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift card from because I e-mailed him the receipt of the purchased and said that someone at that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ''s location said I never made a purchase of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gift cards. I explained to the ploice officer over the phone that I was trying to get a loan and was not frauding [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in any way so [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hanged up, 15 minutes later [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] calls me again and