INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2751,'09/07/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','False statements or representation','I would like to speak to someone as soon as possible please about filing a complaint and getting a fraudulent " legal order '''' lifted off my bank account. The current representative for the debt collector has in NO way communicated with me that there was a supposed issue. She stated that the supposed judgement was made against me in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  2007 and that their office purchased my debt. When I asked for documentation of the original debt and who the original creditor was -- she was unable to give me that info because she said " it has passed theu lots of hands but our company is representing it now ''''. The attorneys office seems to be unclear on what the actual " amount '''' is that they want me to pay. They told the bank one amount, told me a different amount, and when I offered to pay in full the total balance nearly doubled to just over {$15000.00}. The representative says the original debt is believed to be a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit Card balance that originated almost 15 years ago -- plus " applicable fees over the years ''''. My 3 accounts at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have been all wiped clean of any funds because of this issue -- my family checking, my minor sons checking, and a small savings account. When I called the debt collector office they are very unhelpful and wo n''t give me much information. When I questioned the important details of who original creditor was and could they prove that I had any knowledge of the supposed debt -- the representative told me they " are n''t obligated to communicate that to me ''''.
Now the attorneys office is telling me that they will give me a % 20 discount off my balance if they keep all the $ the bank is holding plus I set up monthly payments with them and they want me to use my home - that is mortgaged through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - as collateral. Obviously that is in their best interest. I have spoken to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] representative and would appreciate any input I can receive from your office on this collectors suspicious and what I believe to be fraudulent actions. I have all my accounts being held at this time and am having house, auto, and insurance payments returned because of this.
I believe they have absolutely acted against the Texas Debt Collection Act by failing to identify who held the supposed original debt, failing to contact me in any manner regarding this issue, give varying amounts to myself and my banking establishment, and MOST importantly holding accounts in this manner for repayment of a Consumer debt. In Texas I believe debt collectors Can Not garnish wages for this purpose yet all 3 of my accounts ( totaling {$1200.00} ) are being held hostage currently. As well as I myself have my United States Postal Paycheck being direct deposited tonight and my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year old sons pay day is tomorrow.
Please advise at your earliest convenience about the Texas Deceptive Trade Practices -- which I believe definately covers what this collector is attempting to do. I most definately feel this is a violation of the Consumer Protection Act and would like to file a formal complaint.
This whole incident is all very suspicious. As a matter of fact when I input the supposed " attorneys '''' office phone number into google it comes back as a known Scam # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] response and action is needed before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is forced to actually release these funds to the criminals that are attempting this.','Oak Harbor Capital, LLC',2.0,4.0,'debt collector''s representative says the original debt is believed to be a credit card balance. the debt collector''s office has in no way communicated with me. the attorney office');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2752,'09/07/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','After twice writing to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Equifax asking for them to adhere to federal law sending me physical proof of these alleged debts they ''re reporting, both times they have NOT and keep reporting these two fraudulent accounts as this infringes upon my consumer rights and also are violating my civil rights.The alleged debts they are reporting are from some company named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$4800.00} and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with a paid charge off of $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].I have also reached out to the both of them to no avail.I thought [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Equifax were suppose to physically verify alleged debts before reporting.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'alleged debts are from a company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Equifax. they have NOT and keep reporting them as this infringe');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2753,'09/07/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I was informed by another credit monitoring company that a former creditor is still purposely reporting inaccurate account status information to TransUnion Credit Bureau. This is my third time reporting this company. The company is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The company repossessed their vehicle back in 2014. The company is intentionally report inaccurate account status information as " failure to pay '''', 30 days late, 60 days late '''' when I no longer have the vehicle and the vehicle has been re-sold. I do not owe this company anything. The account status should be Repossessed-Closed. Would you please help me? This company is purposely decreasing my credit score. This is fraud and abuse.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'credit monitoring company is intentionally reporting inaccurate account status information. the company repossessed their vehicle back in 2014.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2754,'09/07/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','A while ago I disputed a collection account that appeared from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) for a debt that was originally from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I disputed on the bases on NO Contract, No Validation and it was removed from my report with TransUnion, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit bureaus. Over the last week XX/XX/17-XX/XX/17 it reappeared on all 3 bureaus again, with no notice or warning. Basically, this alleged debt was removed over a year ago after it was disputed, and then re-added within the last week. No notice from either credit bureau ( TransUnion, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ). I called all bureaus and asked that it be removed based on the the fact that it was removed after a previous dispute yielded No Contract or No Validation. I was told that it would not be removed but re disputed and would take up to 30 ( MORE ) days. Meanwhile this Inaccurate, Unverified, Non-Validated, No Contract alleged debt has done significant damage to my personal credit report and credit scores.
Either removed from all 3 credit reporting bureaus ( not able to re-add ) or Legal action filed against all parties involved','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'alleged debt was removed over a year ago after it was disputed. it reappeared on all 3 credit bureaus again, with no notice or warning. alleged');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2755,'09/06/2017','Debt collection','Medical debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','There were two glitches in the system of TransUnion. These glitches were in fault a problem of TransUnion and not mine and resulted in the deletion of All inquiries on my report. Later TransUnion added them back onto my credit report without giving me the legally required written notice 5 days prior to them re-adding them. I contacted TransUnion twice ( first rep name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and second rep name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) in good faith to ask them to delete the inquiries that they had illegally re-added. These inquiries add hardship to me financially and my rights have been violated by TransUnion. I ask that you please help me make TransUnion stop victimizing me.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'two glitches in the system of TransUnion resulted in the deletion of all inquiries on my report. transUnion added them back onto my credit report without giving me the legally required');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2756,'09/06/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','I chatted online with a Capital One supervisor, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], today X/X/2017 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2 screen shots of this chat is attached To ask why I was charged interest on my last 2 statements ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]& XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) where I had paid more than the last statement balance due. 

His response is because I did not pay in full the last statement balance for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which was due by closing of my billing cycle XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This is correct due to the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] holiday, I was late & payment was made on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

