INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2784,'08/30/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','False statements or representation','My care credit account was charged for the wrong amount by my dentist. I disputed this amount and was advised by Care credit this will be credited. I called and spoke with several agents however I kept getting told this will be credited and the issue resolved. Care credit also enrolled me into one of their insurance plans where by they would make my payments if I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or became unemployed. It so happened I did become [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and later unemployed and provided all documents requested by care credit .I was getting charged a monthly fee for having this insurance to pay for my care credit account while I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and unemployed. Care credit did not pay a single penny towards my bill and the dispute was never resolved. Everytime I would call I would be told the account will be reviewed and no one would take ownership. Finally they sent my account to collections and I disputed the collections account too. The different companies my account went to never sent me any correspondence. I was able to obtain all this infor from Care credit after calling several times. Finally this account was sent over to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I requested a validation of debt letter. Till today this company has not provided that and has threatened me several tme that they will sue me and will make sure I lose my JOB. They served a letter to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] person where I get mail and this letter was open. employees at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  store knew what the content of the letter was as well as it was handed over to them. I have called Care credit again and again and now keep getting told care credit has changed names and I am not able to obtain any information from then. I have to call the attorneys office who the debt was sold to. Care Credit sold this debt to a 3rd party and now I am been told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] since they purchased this debt they are not obligated to provide a debt validation neither can I dispute this debt at all. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advised me they will sue me unless I paid {$500.00} upfront and pay the balance in a lump sum. I am been charged for a debt that I do not owe nor can this debt be validated by Care credit or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'care credit enrolled me into one of their insurance plans. they would make my payments if I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or became unemployed.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2785,'08/30/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I ''ve disputed this account before, and still have not seen proof that this account is mine per FCRA section 609. It ''s just being verified verbally without supporting evidence that it ''s mine. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is the old complaint, I know for a fact that account is not mine, show me my signature that it is. Still waiting for a fair shake from these people. Maybe my next step after this should be the FTC, or the attorney General.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'''i have disputed this account before, and have not seen proof that it is mine''. it is being verified verbally without supporting evidence that it is mine.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2786,'08/30/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','TRANSUNION states erroneously that Chaper [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcy that was dismissed/withdrawn is the same as a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was Discharged, and the Two concepts are completely different : as follows One shows the abdication of debts= discharge The other shows the LACK of follow through and should not be counted against you in a credit file. 


I should not bear the negative consequences of changing my mind ( due to bad legal advice in a divorce ) since it affects no creditors and the item should be removed and my credit score increased','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the two concepts are completely different. the following shows the abdication of debts= discharge. the other shows the LACK of follow through and should not be counted against you');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2787,'08/29/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On X/XX/2017 I was made aware of multiple unauthorized charges on my account by a merchant that has made unauthorized charges to my account before. I immediately disputed the charges with my bank, PNC Bank and contacted the merchant responsible for making the unauthorized charges. PNC disputed the charges and immediately replaced the amount of the disputed charges back into my account. Unbeknownst to me PNC shut down my card for further use. I was made aware of the card issue when I went to go grocery shopping at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In the parking lot of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called PNC customer care and I was told that the representative should have told me that the card was going to be shut down and since the change was made less than an hour ago the current representative was able to re-activate my card and I was able to make a purchase at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The representative put in an order to send me a new card in the mail within 3-7 days and in the meantime the representative assured me that I would still be able to use my card until the new card arrives. The information I was given was that as soon as the new card arrives I was to cut up the old card and call PNC customer care to activate the new card, and once again the representative assured me that I would be able to use my card until then. On X/XX/2017, which is today, I was assigned a property inspection report to complete which is located in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Florida. Once I completed the inspection I was on my way home when I decided to stop to make sure I had enough gas just to make it home. I proceeded to try to use my card to purchase a gallon of gas for {$3.00} and my card was declined. I immediately called customer care that notified me that the card was shut down yesterday. I requested to speak to a supervisor and the supervisor explained to me that the card was shut down and since the card is owned by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the only way the card could be re-activated was if the card was shut down and then re-activated within 24 hours of the shut down. I notified the supervisor that was exactly what had occurred, the card was shut down and then re-activated less than an hour later, which is why I was able to make a purchase at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The supervisor notified me that someone shut the card down again after I used it at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and since it has been 24 hours ( Although it had not been a full 24 hours yet at that moment ) they were unable to re-activate my card, even temporarily, and even if it was only for {$3.00}. So I asked why I was blatantly lied to about me being able to continue to use my card until the new card arrives. The supervisor said she apologize for the misinformation I was given. I was not misinformed, I was lied to. They closed the card without my knowledge, re-activated the card with my knowledge, and then closed the card again without my knowledge again. I was stuck and stranded two counties away and over an hour away from my home and I asked what possible solution could there be. The supervisor notified me she could give me the location of a Branch near me. Unfortunately there was not a branch within 20 miles of my location and I was stuck at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] gas station believing that I had access to at least {$3.00} from my account balance that has over {$410.00} available for purchases. So not only did PNC lie to me about me having access to use my card until my new card arrives, the lie left me stuck and stranded over an hour away from my home with no possible solutions from the bank other than to make other arrangements or call someone I know that lives nearby. Not only that, but the entire reason I had to dispute the charges is because PNC allowed the same exact merchant that made unauthorized charges to my account before, too continuously make more unauthorized charges although I have already had a conversation with PNC in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to not let this particular merchant make any more additional charges on my account because they are all unauthorized, and PNC still allows the merchant to continuously make multiple unauthorized charges. Luckily for me there was a good Samaritan that gave me the {$3.00} for the gallon of gas I needed to make it home. Please note, if there was not a good Samaritan at the gas station today, I would still be stranded at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as PNC offered no logical solutions to a problem caused by the bank ''s own " misinformation '''' it chooses to give to customers.','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,4.0,'a merchant made unauthorized charges to my account on X/XX/2017. he immediately disputed the charges with my bank, PNC Bank. he immediately replaced');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2788,'08/29/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was demanding, to : TransUnion LEGAL DEPARTMENT, TransUnion Consumer Solutions [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] PA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The removal of this public record notation ( bankruptcy ) from my credit report. 

