I also do credit monitoring with Discover and I was surprise to see that Discover negatively reported me for going over my credit limit. I immediately called them and was told there was nothing that could be done about it. How can they allow you to go over and then report for doing so. Are they so hungry for you to use their card that they would allow you to go over by a substantial amount and not inform you or deny the transaction.','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'DISCOVER CARD authorized 2 charges which put me over my credit limit by $1200.00. they also authorized a charge for $110000.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2816,'08/23/2017','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I had pay day loans with a place called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I lost my job I could no longer pay what was due and I explained this to them. They at the time said they would make it a charge off. Which it did appear as a charge off. A few months later they sold the debt to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( a bottom feeding collection agency ) and they have harassed us for going on 2 years about this by calling several times a day despite us asking for communication in writing only and they continue to report this to the credit monitoring companies so it appears every month or so on our reports to knock them even lower. 

We debt was paid and we do not owe it. We took [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to court several times and had this dismissed. At one point we even had a lawyer sue them for making false threats of imprisonment, arrest and warrants against us and we were awarded {$1000.00} for the harassment. 

We just want this place to stop bothering us and let us clear our credit up without having them constantly hounding us and putting things on our credit report.','JH Portfolio Debt Equities, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a place called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold the debt to a bottom feeding collection agency. they have harassed us for going on 2 years about');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2817,'08/23/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Struggling to pay your loan','I had received a call from the credit company that I have my car loan from, which is through the car dealer directly. I had been 14 days late on my payment, which I had completely been aware of. I had missed the call due to being at work where it is nearly impossible to answer my personal phone. A voicemail had been left that the car had been [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] due to the late payment and that the were sending a " repo '''' man. Now mind you, I had not heard that voicemail until later in the day. With that said, I was in the middle of conducting an interview at work and receive an urgent call from office staff. They informed me that a " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' was here for me and I informed the staff that I was in the middle of an interview. I finished the interview and the front staff informed me that a " repo '''' man, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], was here and booted my car. How is this acceptable to send a repossession company to enter the place of employment to render a vehicle, and relinquish my personal information with employees in the office who are NOT aware of my financial situation. This not only reflects poorly on that dealership but more importantly defames my character in front of others. This is not only embarrassing but has caused me emotional and physical distress due to my private information being discussed with unauthorized persons. This is a clear violation of the Federal Trade Commission.','Merchants Automotive Group, Inc.',2.0,4.0,'a voicemail had been left that the car had been [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] due to the late payment. the call was sent to the credit company that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2818,'08/23/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Title loan','Can''t contact lender or servicer','My Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcy was discharged on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017. {$2900.00} was issued by Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Trustee to Wells Fargo to clear my auto title. This amount was sent to the wrong address and returned to the Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Trustee. Now Wells Fargo will not release my vehicle title. Wells Fargo claim that they have not been paid. 

