INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2847,'08/17/2017','Checking or savings account','Other banking product or service','Managing an account','I am filing a complaint against JP Morgan Chase in reference to my online [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] transaction # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] processed through Chase.com in the amount of {$520.00} on SundayXX/XX/2017. The amount was debited from my chase checking account but was n''t credited to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account for which was to be sent by mobile number ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The funds were never received by the orher party. After I completed all the required information needed to send the funds, the receiving party received a text message from her banking institution, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], confirming that the fund were being sent to her account with the confirmation # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], however the money was n''t credited to any of her accounts. Both the other party and myself has reached out to both Chase and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to attempt to recover the funds and have had no success and have only been given a run around. I have already filed a claim with Chase to trace the the funds ( claim # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). That claim has been denied because Chase has determined that the funds have been credited to A [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ACCOUNT eventhough I ''ve made it clear that it was n''t any of the accounts of the correct receiving party. After a visit to a branch and multiple calls to the claims department pleading my case finally, Chase made a courtesy recovery attempt to recover these funds. I was advised that although Chase was able to determine the account holder that incorrectly received the funds they are not able to recover those funds from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No reason was provided t