INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2850,'08/17/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I had a short sale due to financial difficulties back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was the first trust lender. IT was agreed upon that for the short sale to be approved, that settlement was to happen no later than XX/XX/15. ( actual settlement was XX/XX/15 ). The proceeds to be received by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from the sale must be greater than or equal to {$340000.00} ( which they received ) and a cash contribution on my behalf for {$6000.00} in certified funds ( which they received ). I have a signed letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  loss prevention supervisor to reflect this and also a HUD 1 settlement sheet. I had my credit pulled this month and to my surprise a collection from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] showed up on my report in the amount of {$54000.00}! I have called numerous times and have been transferred to other departments. I had left messages with no avail. I need your help to have this updated and removed. Is n''t a short sale taking less than what is owed? No they want me to pay them back over and above to what was agreed. This is predatory in it ''s best nature.
Thank you,','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'short sale due to financial difficulties back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015. the proceeds to be received must be greater than or equal to $34000');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2851,'08/16/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I p
ay with Auto Payment. When I make an addit ional payment to Loan A, I state to " Not pay ahead the account '''', either with a separate piece of paper or using the company ''s online option. This is what Navient has told me to do several times. Almost EVERY TIME, Navient " pays ahead '''' Loan A s uch that : -I get an email saying my payment will be lower this month -The Auto Pay amount ends up being the same ( it is not, in fact, lower ). - The amount of the payment that is allocated to Loan A is reduced from {$100.00} to {$25.00} ( this is regardless of how much the extra payment was - typically around {$500.00} ) This is documented in the attached file as happening on X/XX/17, X/XX/17, XX/XX/17. Each time there is a misallocation, I contact Navient and typically receive a correction with 1-2 calls. Additionally, the amount allocated to each loan occasionally varies, for no reason that I know of, and with no explanation, as on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/XXXX17 and X/XX/17. ( I have been making extra payments on Loan A starting this year - I made extra payments on Loan B ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Direct Plus [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) for the last 2 years with the same problems )','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a payment to Loan A is made on loan A. Navient has told me to pay ahead the account ''''. the amount of the payment that is allocated to Loan A');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2852,'08/16/2017','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','Hi, I initiated a wire transfer from my bank, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to Coinbase two days ago. Wire transfers usually take a day, so I gave them a day before I called their bank, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Their bank said they have received the funds so I need to contact coinbase. I sent coinbase an e-mail but they just keep giving me automated responses. I searched online for people similar to my problem and it seems many people are having this problem for I do n''t know what reason. They charge money to wire but they do n''t give us funds in the same day. I am afraid they are stealing money. Here are the details of the transaction. Wire amount [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] U.S. Dollars ( USD ) Wire date XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ETXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ET Message to recipient [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Message/instructions to recipient bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Transaction number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Fed reference number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Status Completed','Coinbase, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'wire transfer from my bank to Coinbase took two days. wire transfer takes a day, so gave them a day before I called their bank. they charge money to wire but');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2853,'08/16/2017','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Closing on a mortgage','I few weeks ago I was in discussion with a couple of my friends and related that I thought that I had been treated a little unfairly by my HAMP mortgage holder, Specialized Loan Servicing. They told me about Consumer Financial Protection Bureau and that you help and protect consumers who may have a disagreement with their financial institutions. So I have decided to contact you. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I applied to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a HAMP loan which was completed and sent to the bank. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I faxed an appeal to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] relating that I had misunderstood the directions on the Hamp application. I had checked off both owner-occupied and second home which I should not have. I ''m the sole owner of the HAMP property ( located at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], MD ) and co-owner of another condo and my mindset was in order to be as thorough and honest as possible with information, I somehow had to show both properties. My mistake in not fully understanding the HAMP form requirements. I explained that I spend 4 to 5 days a week or more at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] property. I have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the salt air at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is beneficial and therapeutic for my medical well being and my occupation allows me the benefit of being able to work during my time there. Therefore under HAMP rules this should be considered a primary residence. I have attached that appeal and the related Hamp application. Reason number one is the item in question and reason for this correspondence to CFPB, reason number 2 has been resolved with the bank. I then called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to inquiry about my appeal, they said that the loan had been sold to Specialized Loan Servicing ( SLS ) and I would have to take up the situation and appeal with them when the loan is fully transferred. When I received official notification of the transfer, I then faxed the same appeal documents to SLS. I then later asked SLS about the status of my appeal and was send a letter of denial on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The letter indicated that my original appeal with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had been denied and SLS was holding to that decision. But that was not truthful and very discerning because of my knowledge of my prior conversation with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the fact that I never received a letter of denial from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Please keep in mind that my loan was still in process and not completed or approved as yet, letter is attached. The consequence of all this is that the {$82000.00} principal was deferred rather than forgiven based on my application error which I attempted to correct very early in the approval process. My husband and I are both on social security and I believe that I am rightly deserving of a reversal of SLSs decision. I understand SLSs desire to keep the money in deferred status for financial reasons but my understanding is that HAMP was created to assist the borrower not the banks. I give my permission for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my husband, to ask and answer any questions in this matter. Thank you, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SLS Loan # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage holder told me about the consumer financial protection bureau. he said that he had misunderstood the directions on the HAMP application. he');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2854,'08/16/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','This complaint is in reply to a previous complaint # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Much of the reply from Citi was not true. I have the emails and letters I received from Citi. Citi said I did not send all documents requested. I have always returned all documents they requested. I have never taken a month to return documents. They are usually returned within a couple of days and not more than a week .I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I received an email from her on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. If the underwriter reviewed my file on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and found documents were missing why were n''t these documents mentioned in the email I received from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when she told me the file was still on the underwriter ''s desk and had not been reviewed yet? ( see attachment ). Also in my phone call on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was told by someone named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that my modification was turned down on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that a demand payment notice was sent. I never received either of these notices. Our account online was never updated as documents were sent in like it was for our previous modification so we did not know what was needed. Also [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not advise me of the documents I needed, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did in an email dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. ( see attachment ) And speaking of a delay, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never answered any of my emails and why did it take so long for him to contact me with the necessary documents I needed to send them when I asked to reapply on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? I did not receive his email with the necessary documents needed until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]