INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2860,'08/15/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','Because I had had to close my accounts, Peoples wo n''t help further : My husband and I had opened a joint checking account where he banks, People ''s United Bank, when we got married. I opened a personal checking account and a savings account at People ''s United Bank at the same time. ( My husband ''s personal financial accounts remain active and are not part of this problem. ) I was out of work from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of XX/XX/XXXXthrough [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and used up the " buffer, '''' our wedding money, to make the mortgage where unemployment left off. I was hired in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and out of work again in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My unemployment compensation, what little it was, was directly deposited to my own account. The balance was very low because I not had time to rebuild the buffer ; but I had the direct deposit. I managed to keep a decent balance in the joint account to pay the mortgage. Last winter, I could n''t balance my checkbook. I went nuts. I ''d bounced checks and could n''t afford the fees.I use [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the same spreadsheet layout I ''ve used for over ten years, and could not find my error. This has never happened to me. I was mortified. With assistance, I managed to pay the fees and keep checks from bouncing until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], when my unemployment ran out. I ''d never been able to catch up from the winter error ; and bills that were falling behind fell further since I ''d lost money paying the fees ... I deposited what I could get, but did n''t realize that there was an added charge : $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  monthly fees since I did n''t have direct deposit. I bounced more checks. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : I ''m not sure which account was overdrawn at the end. I closed one, and closed the other to pay the fees on the first ( with {$50.00} or so that I borrowed ). A little more than a week later, I got a call : the bank had made an error, and had a check for me to pick up. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I picked up two checks totaling {$1100.00} or so. The missing money from last winter. I got to the bank a day or two later. The same morning, I ''d had to ask my husband for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the charity box at religious services. I cried when the bank manager handed me the check that evening. He walked over with me to  cash it. I closed out my savings account at that time. When I ''d calmed down, it occurred to me to ask about the bounced check fees. I have no idea how many there were. The manager said that they could not be refunded because I do n''t have an account with them. WHAT? Their error was the reason I ''d had to close the accounts. I do n''t know if it ''s bank policy. I also do n''t know if it ''s legal ; I had an account when the problem occurred, after all. I was unable to move further with the manager. I remain ashamed that I needed to cash my husband ''s and my joint account, ashamed to the point that I ''ve waited since mid-[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to write because I simply could not. Anything you can advise will be appreciated. Cordially, / s /','PEOPLE''S UNITED BANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'my husband and I had opened a joint checking account at People''s United Bank. he used up the " buffer, '''' our wedding money, to make the mortgage');
