INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2864,'08/14/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Fees or interest','As of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I owed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], dba Comenity Bank {$450.00}. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I paid them {$300.00} although my payment was n''t due until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The mortgage company that I am working with to buy a home required that I pay this account in full so on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I paid the remaining {$140.00}, still days before the due date. Since they did n''t show the now {$0.00} balance on my online statement we had a three way call with someone from Comenity Bank along with myself and someone from my mortgage company to confirm that I had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance. A few days later I go to check and see if the online statement now reflects a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance and instead I see a balance of {$6.00} which was added to my account a week AFTER I paid this account in full. When I questioned it this is the response I received from Comenity Bank : " Your question in regards to the interest charge is understandable. On your previous statement, we informed you of an update to your Credit Card Agreement ( CCA ). This notification was to inform you that beginning on your next statement, purchases made outside a Grace Period would be assessed trailing interest resulting in a finance charge after the balance is paid in full. Interest is charged from the transaction date until the balance is paid in full. Since interest is calculating until the date the payment is received, you will receive a statement for the interest charged in the previous billing cycle. If you pay the trailing interest finance charge statement by the due date, you will not be assessed finance charges during that bill cycle the following month. '''' Keep in mind that I had not made any purchases at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in months and also I, like many people these days, pay my bill online. While I do receive a " paper bill '''', I do n''t even look at it as I know when my payment is due and I pay it days before it is due so they slipped in this " trailing interest '''' without me knowing about it. I feel it is completely unethical for any company to do this especially when they have already charged the consumer over 20 % interest. While this {$6.00} does n''t affect me financially, I feel it is an underhanded practice and should be investigated. Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'dba Comenity Bank owed me a balance of $450.00. the mortgage company required me to pay this account in full. the balance was ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2865,'08/14/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Other features, terms, or problems','Since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have been receiving monthly statements at my home address for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that is not mine. I do not, nor have I ever, had any business with Towne Bank. Here is a history of the attempts I have made to get this corrected : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : Called Cardmember Service at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and explained what I received. She verified that this was sent to the wrong address and would correct it. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : Called and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and told her I was still receiving statements, and was very concerned with how this account got associated with my address, and concerned that they hadnt corrected it yet. She consulted with her supervisor and said they would try to contact the customer and get the correct address. She assured me this is not associated with me. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : Called and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and explained what was ( still ) going on. She transferred me to supervisor and I was cut off. I called back and spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who transferred me to her supervisor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ID # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I explained ( again ) everything that has gone on, and she said she would change the address to the business address. I have received 3 more statements since then ( the latest on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), and am over calling them to get this resolved. In this day and age of Identity Theft, this really worries me that they can not verify a correct address for a customer, can not get my address removed from the account, nor can they provide me with a positive email or letter to say they have corrected it. They have asked in several of the conversations that I simply disregard and discard the statements. When I requested they send me some sort of confirmation that they had corrected the problem, they said they could not do that. After multiple attempts to get this corrected, and assurances that it would be taken care of, it is clear they are unable or unwilling to follow up and correct this. Whether this is incompetence, laziness, or just complete lack of concern I do not know, but my biggest concern is that if this is their response to my problem, how would they prevent someone from completely stealing my Identity? They already have their statements coming to me.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been receiving statements since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
