INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2868,'08/14/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I paid off my mortgage loan in full on Wednesday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have not received my {$920.00} escrow refund within 20 business days as required by RESPA regulations. It has now been 28 business days and after repeated calls I am constantly told that the " check is in the mail ''''. My online account activity states that the escrow funds were disbursed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] however when I just spoke to the Mortgage company ''s escrow representative they state that the funds were mailed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( conveniently the 20th business day ). I stated that I just received mail today that was sent on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] by my current mortgage servicer and again told " I will receive in mail '''' with no remedy on receiving these funds. I believe that this constitutes violation of RESPA regulations since the company has not offered to take any actions to expedite the delivery of funds that I should have already received. It has been very frustrating to deal with this mortgage company and I believe that they are not properly equipped/staffed to satisfy customer complaints. I stated very clearly that I felt this was a violation of RESPA and that I would place a CFPB complaint and they did not attempt to take any further actions to remedy the situation.','RoundPoint Mortgage Servicing Corporation',2.0,2.0,'mortgage company escrow representative says escrow funds were disbursed on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] escrow funds were');
