My mother had accounts at other financial institutions and I was able to withdraw my percentage without have other beneficiary present. ( i.e. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. )','KEYCORP',2.0,2.0,'key bank I am a 50 % beneficiary on my mothers bank account. they stated that both parties must be present in order to distribute and close my deceased mothers account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2891,'08/09/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Opening an account','I am being accused of, by the bank, of perpetrating the fraudulent activity. I deposited a fraudulent check unbeknownst to me at the time of deposit. When I realized that something was " not right '''' I went to the bank and tried to explain what happened and the bank representative informed me that I could not do anything at the time and that I should wait to hear from them to pay what I owed on the account. I never heard from the bank. A couple years later I tried to open a new account and was denied. I was informed that I had to admit to being responsible for the fraud committed and pay the bank fees and then they would consider my request to open a new account. After I refused to admit any wrong doing the bank representative informed me that he could not help me nor advise as how to resolve this situation. I have submitted all the documentation necessary to evaluate and support my side of the story. Including the initial email contacting me in this fraud.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a bank representative told me that I could not do anything at the time. he told me that he could not help me or advise as how to resolve this situation.');
