INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2893,'08/09/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','On Tuesday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 I lost my debit card shortly after leaving the bank. It took a couple days for me to realize my debit card was missing and when I called the bank the following Thursday or Friday to report my card missing I was informed that over {$1800.00} had been fraudulently charged to my account. At first the funds were credited to my account but then about 2 weeks later I recieve notification that the charges were not made in error and that I was responsible. Then the bank reversed the funds out of my account and left my account balance in the negative. I filed an appeal to their decision and did everything they instructed me to do and they still refused to cover my fraud claim even though their policy is 100 % Fraud Protection. When I refused to pay the negative balance now owed to my account as a result of this injustice, the bank went ahead and filed a negative report on my credit with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I found this out today when I was applying for a business account at another bank and was DENIED due to this erronious reporting. First they promise total fraud protection, then they break promise and take my money, and now they attempt to ruin my otherwise perfect credit. I ''ve accepted my fate and ignored the fact they STOLE over {$1800.00} from me but now reporting negatively on my good credit is where I draw the line.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'a bank report on my debit card was made to my account. it took a couple days for me to realize my card was missing. the bank reversed the funds out of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2894,'08/09/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','I have been working with Wells Fargo for possible home retention options in order to avoid foreclosure and remain in my home. After several attempts and even hiring an attorney, I feel defeated. My first submission was denied due to Wells Fargo stating they could not reduce my monthly payment, I think re-applied using my girlfriends income, which double my income at the time, they still would not provide me with options. Finally a 3rd attempt was made which reflected my most recent income, my rental income and proof of ability to pay and yet once again I was denied as they stated they " can not review the file due to the changes of circumstances being the same '''' although that is not true, my income is different. I am not asking for a lowered payment, I am simply asking to start making my payments again. I explained my hardship, in 2010 my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] son was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], additionally I then went through a divorce. These too major events impacted my life and was unexpected. I did not intentionally default on my mortgage but things happen and I am grateful to even have the opportunity to be considered for options but feel I have been treated misfairly and not being properly considered for all options to save my home.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',8.0,8.0,'a 3rd attempt was made to reflect my most recent income, my rental income and proof of ability to pay. I was denied a submission due to their stating they could');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2895,'08/08/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','On Tuesday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017 I tried to use my Bank of America credit card to make a payment of {$750.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to purchase a flight to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This transaction was declined WITHOUT a representative from the financial institution calling me to confirm that I was, in fact, trying to make this payment. I had n''t even reached 20 % of my credit limit for the month, and even with the purchase, I would still have 80 % of my credit limit remaining. I have never encountered an issue like this before. My credit score is higher than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I have never missed a payment! This is absolutely unacceptable and I feel that their practices are predatory.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a bank of America representative called me to confirm that I was trying to make this payment. a credit card representative called me to confirm that I was trying to make this payment.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2896,'08/08/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Communication tactics','Company continue to call my phone, my parents landline phone which they have NEVER been given permission to, and other numbers related to me. They will constantly call throughout the day and they do not say who they are or what they want which is why I refuse to answer their calls.','VIRTUOSO SOURCING GROUP, LLC.',10.0,10.0,'company continue to call my phone, my parents landline phone. they will constantly call throughout the day.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2897,'08/08/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Fees or interest','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Sleepys open-ended credit account - Payment due date was XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which was a Sunday, so payment was made on Monday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The Truth in Lending Act : SEC. 106. RULES REGARDING PERIODIC STATEMENTS. ( a ) IN GENERAL.Section 127 of the Truth in Lending Act ( 15 U.S.C. 1637 ) is amended by adding at the end the following : ( o ) DUE DATES FOR CREDIT CARD ACCOUNTS. ( 1 ) IN GENERAL.The payment due date for a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan shall be the same day each month. ( 2 ) WEEKEND OR HOLIDAY DUE DATES.If the payment due date for a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan is a day on which the creditor does not receive or accept payments by mail ( including weekends and holidays ), the creditor may not treat a payment received on the next business day as late for any purpose. Was charged a late fee, but called and agent said as a courtesy they would credit it since they understood the due date was a Sunday. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] continues to charge late fees ( and then interest on the late fees since this account is deferred interest ) because they claim I should have still made the minimum payment to include the late fee, but this was not explained and no disclosure was read at the time. My XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] statement that 2 more fees had been charged and again, they credited them, apologized for the error and promised this issue would be corrected so that this would stop happening. He promised to note the account so if it happened again, I could call and get it corrected yet again. Again another fee was charged on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Called again on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and promised it would be corrected and was advised to only pay the minimum payment and it would all cancel each other out and reset to normal for the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. Apparently, unless you STILL pay the minimum payment showing on your statement, they consider you late, but no one has ever told me that until now. Called again on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and asked to speak to two different managers NOW IN COLLECTIONS because no one will fix this issue by resetting the minimum payment to what it should be after the credits. I have been told that collections does not have the ability to do that or remove any fees and I need to call Customer Service. Customer Service says they can not help because it is in collections. The collections manager I spoke to last was very apologetic and said that if we were promised this would be resolved, it should have been and he was going to escalate this to the " Concerns '''' department and that they could pull the call if needed to confirm what I was told. He said he would try to reach out to CS to see if he could get them to reset the account to reflect the correct minimum payment due so this will stop happening and told me to call back on Tuesday ( today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to see if anything had been done and he would note the account with details. Called Customer Service today-still unwilling to remove any more fees and refused to help with anything. Said minimum payment is inclusive of a " past due fee, not a late fee ''''. What is the difference??? Said if not paid in full another fee will be added again. They keep giving me the run around. This company is deceptive and has fraudulent practices. I can see why they had to pay {$220.00} million in 2014 for deceptive practices. Working on getting a bank loan to transfer this balance out of this company.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,4.0,'payment due date for a credit card account under an open end consumer credit plan shall be the same day each month. was charged a late fee, but called and agent said as ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2898,'08/08/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Starting in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and thru XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Homepoint erroneously ACH a greater amount ( {$420.00} more ) than the agreed mortgage payment. They said it was to purchase Lender ''s insurance due to our failure to provide evidence of coverage. It has come to light that they made an error. Their insurance department had confirmed that all the paperwork was in order, and there was no lapse in coverage and it was the mortgage ''s company ''s error. Over a period of 6 months, they withdrew {$2300.00} from my checking account, and after admission of their mistakes, they finally refunded me {$1300.00}. They still owe me {$1000.00}, which I once again contacted them. Homepoint acknowledged that this {$1000.00} was due to a lender ''s policy for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they bought under the wrong account in error. Every time I call, I had to recap the issues over and over again and kept getting the run around. I finally spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who is a supervisor at ext [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he said that the company that they no longer work with the company whom they purchased this policy from and that it may take a while to get the money back on my behalf. This is clearly an error they made and should return my money while they try to recoup. Why should I be the one out of pocket for their error? I demand a refund of the {$1000.00} that I am owed.','Home Point Financial Corporation',2.0,2.0,'homepoint erroneously ACH a greater amount ( $420.00 more) than the agreed mortgage payment. it has come to light that they made an error');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2899,'08/08/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Credit monitoring or identity theft protection services','In 2014 I attempted to get a deferment on my student loan as I was not making enough moment each month for regular repayments. I had gotten several deferments for forbearance for the same reason over the years. Eventually I did get the payments deferred, but I have a " late '''' payment in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014 on my credit report. It dragged my credit score down [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points and now I have trouble getting apartments and believe it will cause me problems if I attempt to purchase a car or home.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'in 2014, I tried to get a deferment on my student loan. I had gotten several deferments for forbearance for the same reason. now I');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2900,'08/08/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Struggling to repay your loan','I recently graduated college in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have just about 90,000 in private student loans from Sallie Mae. I have my federal loans under control with an income drive plan and I am hoping for something similar from Sallie Mae. They want me to pay about {$1000.00} a month for the loans, which I have called numerous times to say that it is too much with the amount I make and other expenses I pay a month. Right now they are 2 weeks overdue and I have been trying to get a more realistic payment plan for about a month and a half with them. I have spoken to someone from the collections team many times and they have taken in account all of my expenses and say the lowest they can go is {$370.00} a month. This obviously is much better, but still way over what I can pay at first a month first right out of college. Between all my loans I have 3 co-signers. My nana, who recently deceased is on about 65 % of them. My aunt who is in no way financially stable is on 20 % of them and my girlfriend who makes the same amount as me and we split our bills is on the other 15 %. Sallie Mae keeps trying to reach out to her even though I said there is no way to reach her and I never planned on using any of my cosigners to pay back my loans and let them know that multiple times. I call Sallie Mae and say I want to be in good standing with you and my credit and make these payments on time so I am trying to work out a plan that I can pay you every month, just not that much. They just refuse to go below {$370.00} a month, which I can not do and want to get a payment I can afford out of college and not default on every month.','SLM CORPORATION',4.0,4.0,'i have just about 90,000 in private student loans from Sallie Mae. they want me to pay about $1000.00 a month for the loans.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2901,'08/07/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','To whom this may concern, I have asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to verify there means of the account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has on me, all the keep telling me that the information is accurate. I need to see proof of my signature and also there means of verfication thanks in advance.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'i have asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to verify there means of the account [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2902,'08/07/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Struggling to repay your loan','i have had a student loan for years. I was kicked out of the school because they changed the program hours and I could n''t do day hours. I have tried to get the money back but have not been successful. Now the school is closed and I am at a loss. My husband is in the military and Im trying to claim SCRA. Im so tired of this loan. Please help me!!!!
