INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2903,'08/07/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I paid for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit repair service to provide ways of removing old or incorrect data from my credit reports. Some items were removed except [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who first reported that I was on default for 90 days during the timeframe of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I had submitted application for forebearance because I had returned to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] school. As you would assume, these items, incorrect or not should have been removed from my credit reports because these items are over 10 years old. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] law supposedly contacted them requesting a response but not only did they not respond to me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has yet to remove these items of late payments.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'some items were removed except [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who first reported that I was on default for 90 days. this was because these items are over 10 years old');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2904,'08/07/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','Borrower is currently facing a foreclosure sale of his home scheduled to be held on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017. Please see notice of sale attached hereto. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017 borrower, through his attorneys, submitted a complete application for loss mitigation to his loan servicer PHH Mortgage. Please see application for loss mitigation and confirmation of fax delivery attached hereto. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017 PHH Mortgage issued a letter stating that borrower ''s application for loss mitigation was been denied as incomplete. This letter cited no documents as missing from borrower ''s application. Please see letter from PHH Mortgage dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017 attached hereto. We assert that borrower ''s complete application was submitted more than 37 days prior to a sale date andso PHH is required by 12 CFR 1024.41 ( c ) ( 1 ) to evaluate borrower for all loss mitigation within 30 days of receipt of the complete application. Additionally, PHH Mortgage failed to cite any documents as missing  from borrower ''s application in their notice of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017. This being the case, pursuant to 12 CFR 1024.41 ( c ) ( 2 ) ( iv ) borrower ''s application for assistance is facially complete. As borrower ''s application is facially complete, borrower is forbidden from conducting the foreclosure sale by 12 CFR 1024.41 ( g ).','PHH Mortgage Services Corporation',2.0,2.0,'borrower submitted a complete application for loss mitigation to his loan servicer. he is currently facing a foreclosure sale of his home scheduled to be held on [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2905,'08/07/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','Company sent me a collection letter mid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017 and when I tried to call because I have no idea what this is from the customer service agents was unable to speak with me unless I verified my information. I gave her my social and the account number furnished on the letter. She was unable to speak with me as the information didnt match. When I asked her to send me a letter stating they had the wrong information she hung up in my face. I called back and asked another agent and he said its against their policy to discuss the account because the information doesnt match, when I asked him to send me verification of the debt and to cease collections he stated they wouldnt collect anymore but he couldnt stop it from going on my credit if I didnt pay. I AM NOT PAYING FOR AN ACCOUNT THAT IS NOT MINE and they couldnt even verify in their system. I have never attended [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University and I have no knowledge of this account.','Account Control Technology, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'company sent me a collection letter mid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017. when she tried to call because');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2906,'08/07/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Managing the loan or lease','( 1 ) I, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was accepted for an auto loan from Automotive Credit Corporation through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] CA on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I spoke with a loan rep named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from ACC that finalized the loan. During this conversation [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advised me that I will be receiving loan and payment information via mail with-in a week from our phone conversation. Since our conversation I havent received the loan or payment information which was supposed to be sent to me. But what I have received is several calls from your employees that tell me my loan is in default, but no one to date have sent me loan information to make a payment. I am requesting my loan and payment information sent to me via US mail. ( 2 ) I, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have received your correspondence, dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that states YOUR ACCOUNT REMAINS PAST DUE. YOU MUST IMMEDIAETLY REMIT {$320.00} IN ORDER TO BRING YOUR ACOUNT CURRENT. As I previously advised this company, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a loan representative told me I would receive car loan information via US mail. But I wasnt provided any information in regards to my car loan via US mail. And still to date the only response to my request to get car loan information dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is a letter demanding a payment more than quoted to me by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a representative from your company. According [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who only provided me with payment information via phone quoted my loan payments to be {$300.00}. Those are two of the letters I sent ( 1 ) XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and ( 2 ) XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to acquire information regarding my auto loan # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to ACC. Since then the only response from them have been threatening letters. Also I have made a complaint against [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with multiple reporting agencies for forgery. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] responded to the Better Business Bureau on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was that I was on repossession status and I should rescind the loan. However, the checked for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was received by ACC and deposited on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','AUTOMOTIVE CREDIT CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a loan representative from ACC has received a letter demanding a payment. a loan representative from your company has received a letter demanding a payment. a loan');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2907,'08/06/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','I called these companies to have all my inquiries removed because some one tried to apply for credit cards in my name and was not authorized to do so. Now these are listed as hard inquiries on my credit report with the 3 bureaus. None of the inquiries have been removed yet. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XXXXt- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] AMEX- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- Hard Inquiry- [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'all my inquiries have been removed from my credit report. none of the inquiries have been removed yet.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2908,'08/06/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','An account that was deleted off my transunion and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit report was re-inserted and put back on my credit reports. This account ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) was removed now upon checking my reports it is showing as accounts that are closed and as a charge off. Transunion has it listed under accounts that are closed and marked as needs attention ( which is wrong ). This account was completely removed off my report as it was suppose to be ( according to corporate office over at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has it listed just as a closed account but upon reviewing the closed account it shows charged off. This account was completely deleted off my reports and now re-inserted into a different spot. Once deleted they are not suppose to re-insert.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'account was deleted off transunion and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit report. account was removed and put back on my credit reports. it is showing as accounts');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2909,'08/05/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Fees or interest','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Comenity credit cards I ''ve had all of these store cards for years ( except JJILL ) with no problems. No interest charges, no underserved late fees before they became Comenity.
Apparently some time in   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   they switched from whatever servicer they were to Comenity and I have had nothing but problems every since.
The following information is specific to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  because it is the latest of my problems with this credit card servicer but it applies to all Comenity credit cards listed above.
When I originally opened a   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    Credit card we paid our paper bill every month and had no problems. I do n''t know when we went paperless but my recollection is that we were on automatic payment prior to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  when the Comenity servicer took over service. We moved in   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   of last year. Since then I have n''t received any bills on my seldom used Comenity credit cards and so received late charges and finance charges on all of them.
I went on line to see what happened and realized that we are on paperless billing with no ability to automatically pay these credit cards. Email is not a reliable nor secure way to make sure my credit cards are paid on time with all the junk mail we receive from these same stores. Also, I called on all of the above cards, within the last month and made them go back to paper bills and still was never told about the new finance charge fees until today! At least   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   ''s had the decency to explain to me about the new way finance charges are being calculated monthly on all charges even if your bill does n''t show a recent charge.
I object to credit card companies having the ability to switch this way and still have no way to automatically pay ALL CURRENT charges in order to never be late and never receive finance charges with no errors.
I feel this is deliberate and so different from previous ways of paying credit cards as to constitute fraud.
I called  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  this prior month when I received a late fee notice and finance charges and they explained why I was getting a late fee and finance charge bill. They told me what my current balance was, took off the late fee and gave me my current balance including my finance charges and let me pay it in full that day on the phone. I put it back on paper billing now that we have a permanent address so I would n''t ever be late again. Even though they did n''t take off all the finance charges I felt this was fair enough not to cancel my credit card.
Now I receive a bill for {$1.00} in finance charges in my bill for closing date  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /2017. I called to find out why when I paid in full over the phone last month and they explained the new way of doing finance charges. I spoke with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  over the phone and she confirmed for me that there is no way to automatically pay my balance in full every month on their websites and how the new financing calculations work so I closed all my Comenity accounts. Again, if there is no way to INSURE that you are never late, I feel is purposeful and misleading.
I just want others to be aware and my complaint on file as to the the unfairness of not being able to be assured that my bill is never paid late nor incur finance charges.
It should be REQUIRED that any credit company have the ability to have automatic payment online if they have paperless billing.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,4.0,'a credit card servicer switched from whatever servicer they were to Comenity. a credit card servicer switched from whatever servicer they were to. a new way');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2910,'08/05/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I submitted a payment for my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$13000.00}. US Bank only credited me with a payment of {$3700.00}. I contacted US Bank by phone on 2 occasions, and by e-mail on at least 3 occasions. They consistently deny that they received a check for {$13000.00}. I contacted my bank ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to confirm that US Bank presented the check for payment, and that the payment has cleared. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated that US Bank presented the check 3 times for payment - the 2nd time due to stating the amount incorrectly the 1st time apparently. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was unsure why they presented the check a 3rd time, but does confirm that US Bank received the payment of {$13000.00}. US Bank has had my payment for over 2 weeks, and  so far has refused to acknowledge this, and has provided no assistance during my multiple contact attempts as far as I can tell.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] submitted a payment for my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2911,'08/05/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','I was 1 month behind for several months in a row, I continued to pay my mortgage to try to get caught up, I started to receive notices about being past due right away, which I understand as I was late. Letters got more aggressive in nature so I called them, the agent set me up on a pay arrangement, the arrangement was taking the 1 month past due and spreading it out over the next 4 months. I thought now that I called them that they would stop sending letters and making phone calls, but it did n''t stop. I made my agreed upon payments and each month would receive a late fee and several letters weekly advising to call to avoid foreclosure. I answered the phone a couple weeks ago and they advised me that their automatic dialer should not have called me because I was on an arrangement. They sent someone to my house to hang a notice a couple weeks ago because I still had my final {$300.00} due in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , I called them and they advised me that yes I do have an arrangement but because of the way they do their accounting it looks like I still owe from 2 months ago but not to worry about it. Now today I received a certified mail letter asking me to call to setup a face to face meeting to discuss options to bring my account current, I called and asked if I had an arrangement, they advised me I do but I will still get calls and letters because I am still past due even though my arrangement is n''t due for another 10 days. Also when I call or look online in it says my balance due is over {$2000.00} but when I talked to the representative I only owe {$1300.00} because of unapplied funds. Because of this I am not able to make my payments online for free because I can not pay a lower amount than the total they say is due, so I pay over the phone for {$19.00} for each payment, or I can pay by mail but then I would be late because you can not guaranty when the payment would be received. I get 2 statements, several emails, and phone calls monthly, and several letters weekly, not to mention my credit report.','Ditech Financial LLC',4.0,4.0,'I was 1 month behind for several months in a row. letters got more aggressive so I called them, they set me up on a pay arrangement. each month would receive ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2912,'08/04/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Struggling to repay your loan','I do not have the dates off hand because it happened over 2 years ago, but after reading the following forbes article, I can definitely state that I was a victim of at least 4 of the 6 common complaints that were being made about Navient. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 1. created obstacles to repayment by providing bad information ; - Almost every 2-3 months for over at least 2 years, I was provided applications to submit for income-driven repayment plans that I would fill out and re-submit and A ) was told they never received and B ) was told was the wrong form. Each call ended up in a forbearance with interest accrued. The total cost of my loan has gone up dramatically since. Needless, to say it was an endless cycle of torment.
2. processed payments incorrectly ; - Upon finally agreeing to begin making the monthly payments, I was given on three different occasions 3 different addresses to send the payments to, which subsequently caused a return of payment to my bank, and delay in paying off actual student loan. This took over 3 months to get resolved.
- failed to act when borrowers complained ; - I asked on dozens of occasions to receive my payment or any correspondence via post-office mail and not e-mail as it was not reliable for ensuring that I was receiving my applications for refinancing / monthly payment adjustments / statements, and until today, have not received a single letter via standard post office mail.
- illegally cheated many struggling borrowers out of their rights to lower payments, which caused them to overpay for their student loans ; - My original federal student loan amounted to only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I had under 3 % interest and it was highly recommended that I consolidate everything and go to a private vendor to simplify everything ... .I now have an interest rate of 6.5 % on my student loan with a monthly payment of over {$1300.00} now and a total loan of over 100k. I feel that I was GROSSLY cheated.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a forbes article reveals that Navient was a victim of at least 4 complaints. a total of 6.5 % of student loans have been processed incorrectly ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2913,'08/04/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Incorrect information on your report','This is regarding COASTAL CREDIT , LLC at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - This account is still being reported to the Credit Bureau ... [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This account is closed long ago and still showing on my report. Account opened in 2005 ... .Bureau notified but will not delete this account. All the bureau does is verify the data and keep it on the report. Nothing to verify ... ..Account closed for over 10 years. Please have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] remove the account - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did comply and removed the account from my report due to the AGE of the account - No more valid or serving a purpose to keep having this on my credit report. This is a violation to continue to report this very old account. Thank you ... ..','Coastal Credit, LLC',2.0,2.0,'account closed in 2005.Bureau notified but will not delete account. account closed for over 10 years.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2914,'08/04/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Struggling to repay your loan','The problem is n''t really listed. I attended the aforementioned school which made many promise to those who attended during enrollment. This lead to a class action lawsuit filed against the school representing thousands of students spanning 14 states in which the verdict came down against the school. I continued to make student loan payment for a while of over {$350.00} a month even though I didnt receive any of the things that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had promised. I became ever more frustrated as the company know as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] back then ignored my plea to fulfill what the school had promised themselves or find someone else to do so, especially since they still planned to charge me almost triple the price through the terms of repayment for services that I did not receive from the school itself. So I look for help and was contacted by a company called Consumer Protection Council, who present me with their program that was supposed to deal with this issue but also provide legal defense ... which as of earlier this year stopped because of some legal issue against the owner of that company. So that is where it stands right now. The school mislead me and those who attended it which has been established by the class action suit, but am unwilling to fulfill what was agreed upon between the school and I ... but charge a highly inflated price for services that I had not received. So I will virtually be paying for nothing.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'the school mislead me and those who attended it which has been established by the class action suit. the school has charged me almost triple the price through the terms of repayment for services');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2915,'08/04/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] REFUSES TO VALIDATE THE ERRONEOUS DEBT BEING REPORTED BY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], IN. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] REFUSES TO VALIDATE THE ERRONEOUS DEBT BEING REPORTED BY [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2916,'08/04/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','I have a collection account listed on my credit report twice by the name of " Jefferson Capital System ''''  original creditor " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''''. " Jefferson Capital System '''' is n''t licensed in the State of Texas and therefore I ''m disputing this collection account.','CL HOLDINGS LLC',2.0,2.0,'" Jefferson Capital System '''' isn''t licensed in the state of Texas.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2917,'08/04/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I have disputed, notified, notarized documents, and sent numerous letters to the following agencies, lenders, loan servicers, default depts, etc. Telling them all THAT THESE LOANS ARE NOT MINE, AND I WANT MY NAME OFF, MY MONEY REFUNDED, AND CREDIT REPORT CORRECTED, AND COLLECYIONS STOPPED. No one LISTENS. I have told : 1. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 3. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 4. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 5. AES/PHEAA 6.AES/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 7. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 8. AES/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 9. AES/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 10. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 11. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I paid my PUC student loans off years ago before XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and that my first student loan at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I paid off over 25 years ago, so how they could say it went into default in XX/XX/XXXXis absurd. It says paid off on the promissary note they sent me. As well as there ''s no way in he -- the Federal government would give me a 2nd student loan if I had a loan that went into default 6 months earlier. They claim # 1 Lon at BBI, Which I got in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], paid off inXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], went into default, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and 6 months later federal government gave me a # 2nd student loan XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for PUC. No flipping way would governmention ever do that. Also, and Bank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] confirms they never gave me a student loan, which all these loans were made by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They even showed at one point BBI loan came from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] too, which it did n''t it Came from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Common sense tells you this info is not correct.
No [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was sold, and is no longer open, but was split and bought by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].
I have my original loan documents from PUC showing amount of my loans, amd they do n''t match the amounts these 11 federal agenvies are claiming that are mine. What do I do to resolve this. They continue to steal my money, I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and on a fixed income, and they continue nonetheless. Not to mention their pathetic response to my disputes, is to simply give/sell the loans to someone else.
At one point these loans were in 3 states, 3 different account numbers, at the same time/years, same amounts, and all 3 charging their own additional fees. A [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan is now over 18k, after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  worth of payments they stoled from me. And they are not even mine. Please help.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,4.0,'disputed, notarized documents, sent letters to lenders, default depts, etc. no one LISTENS. he says paid off on promissary note,');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2918,'08/03/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','My husband received two credit cards offer from AARP ( through Chase ) on Wednesday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017. Both offers were the same, but neither contained the required clearly listed APR, cash advance fee, balance transfer fee, late payment fee, etc. This information is provided on the credit card offer, but in very small print as a footnote to the offer. Most credit card offers, including those I ''ve received directly from Chase, include a separate Terms and Conditions page which clearly lists this legally required information. I ''m not sure if it ''s a violation or just an unfair practice, but I take exception to the way this card offer is hard to understand considering it ''s marketed specifically to an older demographic. My understanding of the law regarding fair credit practices is that the separate, clearly readable terms and conditions are required to be included in an offer so that consumers can easily compare and evaluate credit card offers. The law was not followed in this case in a marketing effort toward an older population. That is not acceptable.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a credit card offer from AARP ( through Chase) was received on a credit card offer. both offers were the same, but neither contained the required. the law was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2919,'08/03/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','This is regarding [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - This account is still being reported to the Credit Bureau ... EQUIFAX & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This account is closed long ago and still showing on my report. Account opened in 2005 ... .Bureau notified but will not delete this account. All the bureau does is verify the data and keep it on the report. Nothing to verify ... ..Account closed for over 10 years. Please have Equifax & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] remove the account - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did comply and removed the account from my report due to the AGE of the account - No more valid or serving a purpose to keep having this on my credit report. This is a violation to continue to report this very old account. Thank you ... ..','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'account closed long ago and still showing on my report. account opened in 2005.Bureau notified but will not delete account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2920,'08/03/2017','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','I did an online money transfer with Western Union on Wednesday X/X/17 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The amount was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the fee of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Total for transaction was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The transaction processed smoothly and a tracking number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was issued. On Thursday morning the receiver went to a western union counter in Florida and she was told no such transaction existed in their system. I called Western Union and someone in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me they are authorized agents for Western Union and my bank was holding the money and I should ask the bank to release the funds. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was very clear that the funds were sent from my account to Western Union. I called back Western Union and the man told me it is normal for all money transfers to be kept for several days. I was told there is nothing I can do or anyone else I can complain to. The funds would be available on X/X/2017. At no time during the online process did any indication of the money getting delayed appear as any type of notice. I asked to cancel the transaction so I can use another money transfer service and I was told I would get a refund of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a minimum of seven days after XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This entire experience smells like "bait and switch".','WESTERN UNION COMPANY, THE',2.0,2.0,'the money was sent to Western Union on X/X/17. the money was sent to the bank and sent to the bank. the money was sent to the bank.');
