INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2984,'07/23/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reported that I am 30 days late to credit reporting bureaus even though I had made arrangements to pay late with a promise they would not penalize me. I paid as promised and they reported me 30 days late anyway. Their agreement with me was extremely misleading and this was the first time I was in this type of situation with my payment and I have been a good customer. Please have them remove the late payment on my credit reports.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'credit reporting bureaus reported me 30 days late. they reported me 30 days late anyway.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2985,'07/22/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have contacted both Experian and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] numerous times to resolve this complaint and account with inaccuracies. Both reporting agencies have responded with saying the information I was disputing ( never late ) has been verified by the creditor. However, the creditor told me that they actually never responded to the disputes that were filed but the reporting agencies said they had. I took the following steps according to the law and asked for the method of verification from the reporting agencies and they told me they did not have to give me that information. I stated the law and what it says about a consumer requesting that information and they had 15 days to send it to me. They told me I was wrong, and that the creditors were responsible for sending that documentation. I was transferred to a supervisor with both agencies ( Experian and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and they would not confirm nor deny my rights but they both said they did not have to have verified proof, or any physical information from the creditors to display it. All they needed was an electronic message. I again read the law stating they had 15 days to respond to me after I requested verified proof and again I didnt get anywhere. Both agencies told me the exact same thing, they did not have to have anything from the creditors to report the information. However, they are required to have this information in their hand, and send it to me in writing with the business name, phone number, and names of the people they talked with for the investigation. They both stated they did not have any of this information and stated it multiple times. I sent certified mail asking for the verification in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have yet to receive anything from them on how it was investigated. They are damaging my ability to gain credit and get the best rates possible on our home loan. The account in question is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a credit card with an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit line and closed in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 2016. I have attached the certified mail and receipt for the request of verification. Its been almost 3 months.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'both reporting agencies have responded with saying the information I was disputing has been verified by the creditor. the creditor told me that they actually never responded to the disputes that were filed but');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(2986,'07/22/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Opening an account','I opened a checking/debit account on friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I deposited my paycheck of {$270.00}. I was told the funds would be available [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the next business day. The mobile app gave the same info. On the morning of the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my balance still showed {$0.00}. I went to the branch. The first represantitives answer was basically, ''if you do n''t like it close the account. '' VERY helpful. The second rep I spoke with was the woman who I opened the account with. She now informs me there ''s a 1 week hold on all my funds. She tells me this is normal procedure. That ''s not what she told me the day before. Now according to their app, my check was cleared and the funds made available and instantly froze my account for 7 days. Now I have no money, have no paycheck, and am left with the burden of traveling to work for a week with no money, food or gas. Their underhanded tactics and lies are going to cost me my job.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a checking/debit account was opened on friday, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the money was deposited on');
