INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3098,'06/30/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Struggling to repay your loan','OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I faxed a re-application to Navient to maintain an Income Contingent Repayment plan for my two Department of Education Consolidated Parent Plus Loans. These loans are approximately {$250000.00} at an 8.5 % interest rate. I had been notified by Navient by U.S. mail that the deadline to re-apply for ICR wasXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My communications with Navient are by U.S mail only, by my request, not by email messages. Today, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I contacted Navient by telephone because I noticed on Navient ''s website, where I pay my loan payments each month, that my ICR payment had risen from {$780.00} to {$820.00} although my income verified by my XX/XX/XXXXfederal income tax return had decreased by {$2000.00}. Navient informed me in that telephone call that my re-application was defective and Navient had notified me by email onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that my application had been denied. When I informed Navient that I had signed up for paper communications only, I was told I had signed up for email notifications and that the new amount was in place because my application was defective. Navient then offered to place my account in forebearance while I straightened out my application. I declined a forebearance because I did not want interest to accrue while I put an ICR in place. My complaint is that Navient did not inform me by U.S mail that my ICR re-application was defective, increased my payment amount without notice, and lied to me by stating I had agreed to accept email messages as notices of my repayment plan status. While this increase may be small, my income is extremely tight -- I struggle each month to pay for both health care and for student loan payments. I am a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year old single woman who lives on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I can get