INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3113,'06/27/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','On the dates [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I sent disputes to Equifax to investigate the incorrect reporting of a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) on my credit. I am a victim of identity theft. Someone opened an account with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] using my information in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and left an unpaid debt of {$11000.00} on the account. This debt was eventually charged off and placed back on my report as a bad account. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I contacted and filed an FTC Identity Theft Affidavit to open an investigation and get this matter resolved and removed from my credit report. I have recently re-filed a police report to get Equifax to understand the situation I ''m in and finally remove this bad account from my credit. I have contacted Equifax on multiple occasions with the attached police report but they are refusing to remove this account from my credit. This account was reporting on all three of my credit reports but once [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] initiated an investigation, this account was promptly deleted from my report when it could not be verified as accurate or complete on my credit. I am including an attachment with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] exact response showing the results of their investigation. I am also including a page of a recent report showing how this account is only on Equifax. Equifax is automatically disregarding my dispute as frivolous despite having information that states and supports otherwise. The issue is that the account is not even supposed to be reporting on my credit at all. I do n''t understand how this can be possible? How can Equifax ''s investigations yield a different response from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]?','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a debt of $11000.00 was charged off and placed back on my report. a police report has been filed to get the issue resolved. a bad');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3114,'06/27/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','My complaint is with all three credit bureaus. I will make this short and concise : I have not missed a payment in greater than 10 years. I have {$100000.00} worth of available credit. I have had 55 auto loans, mortgages, student loans and credit cards in the past 15+ years. I currently sit at a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( Experian ) credit score and I can not improve this score by more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or so points. <P/>Now I understand all about credit utilization. I have had as little as 28 % utilization and I have had as much as 67 % utilization ( I am carrying about 61 % right now ) over the past 2-3 years. With perfect payment history and zero derogatory issues, even with a credit utilization of 61 % my score should not drop from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points ). <P/>Here is part of the problem : every time I pay an account down or off, one of my accounts that is at zero gets closed by the creditor. Think about that ... say I owe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I pay {$10000.00} off to bring it down to 40 % and then one of my old cards at {$0.00} balance is suddenly closed by a creditor for " lack of use ''''. My 40 % ratio suddenly returns to 50 %. In order to increase my available credit to {$100000.00} I am forced to open a new account which drops my score and I have to build it back up. Its a vicious cycle. This is just one of the tactics I have been forced to endure. This forces me to have to carry balances on every account now in order to avoid them being closed. So now the new tactic is to reduce my available balance ( for no reason ) in order to show a higher debt utilization per account. Its ridiculous. <P/>I have used simulators at sites like [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], etc and it even supports what I am claiming. I pay all my debt to zero today and next month my score will only rise [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points. I seek suggestions as to how to improve my score and I am offered 6 new credit cards to open, all with " excellent '''' chances of being approved! <P/>I have paid my balance down to less than 10 percent and my score only increases a max of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Think about that : > 10 % balance on {$100000.00} of available credit. No defaults, no  missed payments in over 10 years ... nothing and I can only bring my score up to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( my highest in over 3 years ). <P/>I have scoured my credit reports ... I do n''t even have as much as a negative comment. <P/>This is what ''s interesting : I get APPROVED for every and any credit application I apply for. Every one! But because my score is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s they always come with the highest rates. <P/>So my complaint is this : I am being kept at a low rate in order to have to accept the highest interest rates i ''m offered. I ''m willing to bet I am not the only one this happens to. I make excellent income so I believe the creditors know that I make excellent money, I ALWAYS pay my bills so it is in their interest to keep my score low and force me to pay more than other people. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and a veteran. There can not be any other explanation. I am sure you will investigate. One look at my credit report and you will see exactly what I am explaining and if you can honestly state that this is entire normal and acceptable then I will rescind my complaint and move on.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a credit score of 61 % is a problem. a credit score of 61 % is a problem. a new account is closed for lack of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3115,'06/26/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I had an overdraft protection feature on a checking account opened in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the time. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] it was reported as late and due to me being young and not financially sound I did n''t pay some overdraft fees that totaled [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars. Several years went by and as a worked toward my professional career I wanted to get my credit in order. So in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I checked all my reports and saw this [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge I knew nothing about not remembering what it was from. I paid it immediately. However, my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and FICO report is showing that I failed to pay for years which equals 65 months of failure to pay status on my report. This is literally tanking my credit over 250 dollars. The worst part is that due to the timeline it would have been better for me to never pay it off and just let it fall off my report after the 7-year limit but I thought I should pay what I owe. I do n''t think it is fair to have 65 failure to pay statuses on my report when the bank writes off as a paid profit loss and then I proceed to pay it when I learn how to manage credit as a young adult. I do n''t think it ''s fair for the life cycle of this account to restart since I choose to pay off what was owed instead of letting it fall off the report. It ''s doing a ton of damage to my report over 250 dollars from a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. And again I PAID IT BACK in full to the original creditor.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',4.0,4.0,'a checking account opened in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. it was reported as late and due to');
