INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3125,'06/23/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Written notification about debt','On or around XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I sent a request for validation of a supposed debt to Portfolio Recovery Associates, LLC ( " Portfolio '''' ) regarding a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account with a supposed balance of {$3800.00}. I received three responses, datedXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], all of which stated that I " had the right to request substantiation of this debt '''' but containing no substantiation of the debt in response to my validation request. On or around XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I sent a second request for validation and received two responses. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Portfolio sent a letter advising me that they had " already responded to a previous dispute substantially the same as you present dispute '''' and would not be providing the requested validation. OnXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the sent me a nearly identical letter to the first three, stating that I " have the right to request substantiation of the debt '''' but without substantiation/validation as required by the Fair Credit Reporting Act. They continue to report this debt on my credit report despite not responding to my validation request as required by law.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,2.0,'a debt was supposed to be $3800.00. on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I sent a second');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3126,'06/23/2017','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','We entered into a Loan modification with our Mortgage lender Select Portfolio Services On our home 2 years ago. We were told to not make a few payments before they could start the loan modification. For 2 years they denied us but then let us appeal. Every time we would appeal we would have to resend all of the paper work in again because they misplaced everything. We did this around 12 times over the coarse of 2 years. Our house has been in a constant foreclosed state. We have not made any payments because we were afraid we would loose the house. We were just notified that they denied our Loan modification because the process has taken too long, which was not our fault, but would reinstate our old loan We only had 2 weeks to agree to the new terms or we will be foreclosed upon. The new terms are ; They doubled our payments so instead of {$3000.00} a month now it ''s {$6000.00}. The whole reason we did the Loan Mod was because we could n''t afford the old payment. Also they want a baloon payment of {$85000.00} in one year. Is this even legal?? These terms are rediculous and we can not afford this and are going to loose our beloved home of 26 years we have raised [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] children there. They have forced us into foreclosure and we can not get a new loan because of back payments. Please help as the deadline is today. Sincerely [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,2.0,'we entered into a Loan modification with our mortgage lender Select Portfolio Services on our home 2 years ago. they denied us but then let us appeal. every time we would appeal we would');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3127,'06/23/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I obtained a settlement with payment of {$2300.00} and Discover takes 30-45 days to report it to credit bureaus. We are trying to buy a home and we need this reported efficiently. The company is quick to send negative information to credit bureaus but slow in reporting settlement.','DISCOVER BANK',4.0,4.0,'settlement with payment of $2300.00 takes 3045 days to report it to credit bureaus.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3128,'06/23/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] purchased this debt from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and decided to temper with the original dates. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to inquire about the date of delinquency in this account which was the first day after I missed a payment [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2009 and should have been reported within 90 days .this account should be in default After I did n''t make a scheduled payment for a period of 270 Days from last payment according to federal Regulation. I included documentation for payments schedule and proof that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] got no payment past the date stated above and admitting to the last payment date ... [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] provided fraudulent information to the credit agencies to default the loan at a later date so the status of limitations can be changed giving them a longer time to try to collect. Negative account information should not be reported after 7 years from the delinquency date which was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2009. Yet till this day [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is posting negative information and their customer service is unaware of federal regulations and ignore my submitted documents that I provided. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should remove all negative information from all credit bureaus since the delinquency date was more than 7 years and no payment have been made since. Legal action will follow for this fraud.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] purchased this debt from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. he purchased this debt and decided to temper with the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3129,'06/23/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I checked my statement on 6/23/2017 because I knew I had a payment due on 7/3/2017. My payment was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] higher than it had been previously. I have 2 loans with this servicer, both of them have been in an interest only repayment plan. The most recent statement, published on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2017,  noted that the repayment plan on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of my loans would end on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2017 and noted the amount it would increase to. When I called my loan servicer about this amount, I was told that it was actually the OTHER loan that would increase after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2017.  This other loan was NOT noted on my statement as the loan that would increase. They claimed they sent a letter to me notifying me of this change. I never received this letter. They cited an old address that they sent it to. I corrected the address and asked them why they did not send me this notification via email, like they normally do. They normally do not send me these notifications in the mail. I usually receive notifications of loan status/amount changes in my email inbox. They did not have an explanation for this. The man I spoke with on the phone proceeded to lecture me about my responsibility to pay back my loans. I told him that I would pay what I could but that I was not comfortable with the lack of accurate communication about my payments increasing. He then asked about my co-signer and if my co-signer ( who is my mother ) would be able to help me make payments. I told him I did not think so. I wanted to see if we could come to an agreement about a payment that works better for me at this time. My loan has increased at least twice in the past year. Once because of an interest rate change, the second time my loan increased around {$10.00} and I did not receive proper notification, but overlooked it because it was only a small increase. I probably should not have ignored that, but I ca n''t go back and fix that now. This time it ''s increased again and it ''s almost {$100.00} more than what I ''ve been paying monthly since the last {$10.00} increase, and I can not afford a payment that is almost {$100.00} more than the payment I have been making. I ''m at my wits end with this loan servicer. They have terrible communication, terrible customer service, when I call in no [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] seems organized enough to know anything about what anyone else already knows about my account, and they continue to raise my payments when they know I can not afford to make more of a payment than I already make. I have other loans and other obligations outside of this loan. THey are unreasonable and a pain to work with. The man I spoke with on the phone today spoke to me in such a way that it made me cry ... ..I have NEVER had such poor customer service. I have never had anyone from customer service speak to me in such a way that made me cry. I do n''t know what else to do. I can not afford to have my payments jump higher and higher without proper advanced notification of the rate change so I can plan my finances accordingly and the bullying I get from customer service when I call about the changes and question the changes is over the top. Please help.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my payment was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] higher than it had been previously. my loan was in an interest only repayment plan. the other loan was NOT noted');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3130,'06/23/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting the same loan twice on my credit report. I have reported this to the credit bureau however [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] keeps verifying both accounts as valid. I have only had one [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  loan but reporting the same loan twice with slightly different account numbers is not helping my credit. Transunion has listed one account # as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the other as account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] needs to remove these duplicate records from my credit report but they are failing to do so even after I have asked Transunion to reinvestigate.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting the same loan twice on my credit report. I have only had one [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3131,'06/22/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Closing your account','Today, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017, I called Citibank to close my AAdvantage Platinum Select credit card. I was referred to a " senior account specialist '''' whose job was clearly to talk me out of closing my account. I calmly and politely explained my reasons for closing the account figuring they would make sense : I do n''t use the card anymore, have n''t used it in a year and a half, and do n''t want to keep paying the annual fee for something I ''m not using. <P/>This person kept pressing me not to close the account, and despite my continued explanations it sounded like he was following a script instead of actually listening to me. For instance, he was amazed that I had no balance on the card and always paid it off on time ; is that so surprising when I have n''t used it in over a year? He offered to refund the full annual fee instead of a pro-rated amount if I first spend {$1000.00} in the next 3 months on the card ; I responded that I was not interested and would rather just close today. STILL he kept pushing, and at this point I got angry. Despite his continued emphasis on being able to get my full annual fee back, I told him I saw through his game : this is a ploy to get me to keep the card, try to follow a bunch more little rules, and be too lazy to call back in 3 months. He ''s probably right that I would n''t do all of that successfully ; that ''s why these banks have so much money! Yet I had to yell at this guy repeatedly to get him to finally give up and close my account, which he eventually did. <P/>I wanted to be proud of myself for finally getting around to crossing this off my todo list. Instead I had to get angry and exasperated ; a calculated move, since he clearly was n''t listening to me when I was being polite, but that does n''t make it easer or less stressful. That awful memory will be my parting experience with Citibank. <P/>You can tell Citibank that they just lost a customer permanently ... unless they decide to pull a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and reopen the account without my permission, of course. After that phone call, they sound like exactly the type of company to do such a thing.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a senior account specialist ''''s job was clearly to talk me out of closing my account. he kept pressing me not to close the account, and despite his continued explanation');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3132,'06/22/2017','Payday loan, title loan, or personal loan','Installment loan','Problem when making payments','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold me a business credit builder and landing page design and they financed it for me through Universal Account Services. The amount borrowed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Universal Account Services. The credit builder turned out to be about 3 web pages worth of reading. There was no landing page design. When I asked about the landing page design, I was told someone would contact me. When they did contact me they wanted another [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars. So I hung up on them. Even though I try to make the payment to Universal Account Services, they keep drawing the money out of my account. I gave them permission to do this one time. But they are doing it every month. I really want them out of my bank account. The fact that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold me almost nothing for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars I guess is the fault of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They completely misrepresented to me what I would receive for the payment. So I guess I am not sure if I should complain about Universal Account Services or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would very much like to get Universal Account Services to no longer have the right each month to withdraw funds from my bank account.','Universal Account Servicing, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a credit builder and landing page design sold me almost nothing for me. they financed it through Universal Account Services. the credit builder turned out to be about 3 web pages');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3133,'06/22/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Communication tactics','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in an attempt to set up payment arrangements. The representative said she was unable to work a paymnt plan out with me that I could afford.said if they garnished my wages they would get more. I ask to speak to a supervisor. I told them several times i could only commit to {$25.00} a month without losing my house. The supervisor was extremely rude and kept over talking me. I actually had to tell her she did n''t have to be so rude. At that point I agreed to {$75.00} a month that i am going to struggle to pay starting [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She stated she would have the paperwork sent to me and I needed to fill it out and send it back so they could file it with the courts. As of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I had not received the paperwork. I call them back and the representative apologized stated she sees where I spoke to the supervisor, but the notes are very viege. Stated no paperwork was ever mailed out and the agreement was not noted. This representative was very polite and said she would get that out to me and I should have it by next week. If I would not have called my wages would have been garnished due to the supervisor not submitting the payment arrangement she agreed to with me.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'if they garnished my wages they would get more. the supervisor said she would have to send the paperwork back.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3134,'06/22/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','A past account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was deleted from my credit file [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The original creditor was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The amount is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The account has reappeared under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Experian refused to provide documentation of the deleted account. but verbally acknowledged the account was previously deleted but allowed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to enter this account on my credit file again. This is not a new account as I have communicated this to Experian customer service and supervisor ( s ) several times via phone call. I have also explained the debt is currently being paid under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is a consolidation of all student loans which include [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Documentation has been sent Experian via U. S. postal mail service. Experian has informed me the company does not have a fax number. Experian downloading website for sending documents for disputes does not function. I have tried for eights months to load documents on the website and all instructions and criteria were followed and documents do not load. Documentation has been sent certified mail but returned. This has been ongoing for couple months. A complaint was sent to the Better Business Bureau as the account remains on my credit report','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'account deleted from credit file by experian. account has reappeared under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3135,'06/22/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I recently reviewed my credit report ( because I became suspicious after receiving various calls from countless collection agencies calling my house ) on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and therefore, I became aware of odd credit card accounts lodged on my credit report which does not belong to me. I am classifying this incident as a breach of my personal identity and thus reporting this as fraudulent activity against me. I was a prior victim of identity theft back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], while [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] during my eleven and a half years in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( this situation seems to be never ending ). Now, I am finding out I have fallen victim to the same circumstance like [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] incident, in which my mother filed the police report on my behalf during my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and placed various fraud alerts and a credit freeze on all three credit files, plus reports with other government agencies. I have filed an online identity theft report with www.identitytheft.gov, ref # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; filed a credit bureau fraud alert at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  confirmation number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; and filed a fraud alert with the Federal Trade Commission at www.consumer.ftc.gov, ref # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I did not authorize, collude, conspire, or give authorization, or grant permission for anyone to open up any credit card account in my name, nor did I have prior knowledge of any accounts opened in my name.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'a prior victim of identity theft in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was a prior victim of identity theft. my mother filed the police report on my behalf during');
