INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3140,'06/21/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Incorrect information on your report','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called card servicing for my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Cards continental finance. I made a payment on both cards prior to their due dates. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a credit alert that I had a delinquent account. After reviewing the alert I contact continental finance to advise that I made my payment. Instead of the customer service representative applying the payments as requested one to each account. They applied both payments to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Card. This happen to me in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Card they claim that I missed a payment and have been reporting such. I suspect in this case they applied the payment to my mother ''s account as I also call in payments for her account. I suspect that the same thing happened in this case. This behavior is unacceptable and could cause people to have damaged credit due to this types of mistakes.','Continental Finance Company, LLC',2.0,2.0,'on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a credit alert that I had a delinquent account. they applied');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3141,'06/21/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I have an issue, I had a car loan through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have always been current and been paying on this, I pay it off in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and now a bunch of late payment remarks were added back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is inaccurate. I have attached the page of my credit report in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reflecting paid as agreed and never once late and the report that was pulled in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] showing a bunch of inaccurate late payments. How can I be penalized for paying off an auto loan. This is not correct.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a bunch of late payment remarks were added back from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is inaccurate.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3142,'06/21/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Made purchase at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Oregon {$87.00} I requested to use my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card for purchase I told the associate that I wanted to make a payment for this purchase while I was at the store. Associate [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] rang up purchase, accepted personal check in the amount of {$87.00} for payment of purchase and entered the payment information into the register. The associate attempted to complete the transaction a different register and told me that my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card had been declined. She checked and found that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] cc which was issued through Capital One was no longer valid as Capitol One was not the company now used to cover the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] cc. At that point I opted to use my VISA card to complete the purchase. As the associate had already accepted the payment check and rang it up on the register she said that I could contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] customer service to have a refund issued to me in the amount of {$87.00}. She provided me with the customer service phone number of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. A couple days later I called the customer service number provided to me to initiate the process to have my payment refunded. I was transferred to the credit card unit where I explained the situation. I provided all of the account information to the call taker who checked in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] purchase history and showed both the purchase on my Visa card, and the payment made by personal check. I was told that a refund check would be issued to me in 10 30 days. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called again and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who said that a paper check had been issued on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and mailed out. I advised that I had not received a check and was assured, once again, that a check would be re-issued within 30 days. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called again and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who said that he was able to access the history of the my phone calls, verified that there had been an payment made by me and should be refunded to me and assured me that a check was being processed to be sent to me in the amount of {$87.00}. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called to verify that a refund check had been requested and would be sent to me. There was no record of a check having been issued but I was assured ( once again ) that a request for a check would be submitted and would be delivered to me in 10 30 business days. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was told ( for the 5th time ) that the records did in fact show that Capitol One did owe me {$87.00} for a payment on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was told Yes - a refund check would be issued to me. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called the Capitol One General Customer Service number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which was provided on their website. I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and explained the situation and the number of times I had called to get this matter satisfied with a refund check. She too was able to read the log of my calls and what information had been given to me in each call. She then transferred me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who was going to help me get this resolved. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] too accessed the call history and said that a check had been mailed in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but had been returned as undeliverable. I explained that I had lived at this address for over 12 years and had not had a problem with having mail delivered. He read to me the address that they had in their records and I confirmed that was the correct address. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that he was requesting a check be issued to me to end this transaction. He assured me that a check would be coming in between 7 14 days. He gave me a phone number to call back if I had any questions. That number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called this number the next day to verify the address that they had in their records, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] assumed me that they did in fact have the correct address and the check was going to be issued and sent to me. NO CHECK ARRIVED. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He said that on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a check was issued in the amount of {$87.00}. He said that he would check on this and get a tracking number to provide to me and call me in 24 hours with information on what action is being taken and when this will be resolved. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] no call has been received from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at Capitol One. I know that Capitol One has a record of my address somewhere in their files as I get multiple offers in the mail to apply for a Capitol One Credit Card. If they have the information to send me offers surely they have that same information to send me a refund check. I feel that I have been more than patient in this situation. Were the " shoe '''' on the other foot, Capitol One would be requiring that I not only honor my commitment to them to pay my debt - but would  charge me interest if my payment was late.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] made purchase at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_AN');
