INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3180,'06/13/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Problems at the end of the loan or lease','Chase Auto Loan Account Number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had a listed balance of {$930.00} as of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on a loan that matured onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which should have been the last payment. The payoff quotes stated projected payoffs of {$1200.00} if payoff was done on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ],  and a separate payoff of {$1200.00} if paid off on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] <P/>The loan was created at the dealership with a {$320.00} monthly payment but a calculated amortization shows payment of {$320.00} a month. A request was done to Chase Auto Finance on 6 different occasions to get a copy of an official Amortization Schedule to confirm the calculations of the payment and interest allocation over the life of the loan. Each copy received had {$0.00} in each row and column for Principal, Interest and Balance.
<P/>
I have contacted Chase to settle to correct balance contingent on a Amortization Schedule. They have since sent the account balance to a collection agency who attempted to settle the balance but unwilling to correct the 3 lates on my credit report. <P/>I believe it is Chase ''s responsibility to validate the debt they say I owe. I made all 60 payments on my loan and should not have an outstanding balance of over {$900.00}. Payment history will show that even on later payments I paid more than the minimum as well as payments that were on time.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a loan that matured on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should have been the last payment. the loan was created at the');
