INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3202,'06/08/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem when making payments','A payment was made for {$3300.00} to Chase Bank on X/XX/17 to be credited for X/XX/17 in error on an account that is closed. This payment was made thru bill pay. On X/XX/17 I was made aware the payment was never received. My wife made an inquiry thru bill pay and discovered her error in making payment to closed account. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent proof of payment and request for refund to merchant on X/XX/17.  Chase Bank requested proof of payment thru a transmittal report and provided a fax number. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] an outside party that handles [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill pay submitted information requested from Chase on X/X/2017. They were requesting incorrect account number that money was sent to and the correct account number the payment should have been applied to.This information has been supplied from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] more than one time to Chase Bank. There have been numerous requests from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in between these two dates to resolve this issue. There has been no help from Chase Bank to help me resolve this issue. I have had the account with Chase for a long time and I use the card on a weekly basis and always pay my bill in full each month. The due date on this card was X/XX/17. I have been sadly disappointed in the customer service and lack of concern that Chase Bank has shown me. The dollar amount is quite substantial to me and my credit score is of great concern also is getting this matter resolved. I realize the first mistake was ours but feel they have had ample time in reapplying payment to the correct account number which has been provided to them.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a payment was made to Chase Bank on X/XX/17 in error on an account that is closed. the payment was made through bill pay. my wife made an');
