INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3210,'06/06/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Transunion is reporting chapter  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  bk on my credit report on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  2015 . I have send information from bankruptcy court stating courts do not verify a bk and transunion continues to report a bk on my report. This is the only bureau that reports this. They refuse to remove with the proper documation submitted','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'transunion is reporting chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bk on my credit report. court records show courts do not verify a bk and ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3211,'06/06/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Struggling to pay mortgage','To whom this may concern. I have asked for your help in the past and you absolutely did but I continue to have a big problem with our mortgage servicer, Nationstar.  <P/> In  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  we had a sale date of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ; because of your intervention the sale date was postponed and ultimately cancelled. After continuous paperwork and submitting a financial package a modification was approved and my 1st payment was supposed to begin in  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I made my  1st pa yment and 2 days before my  2nd w as due I received a letter stating that my modification paperwork had not been signed and dated on  one  of the pages. They were going to send me the page that they said was incorrect and told me to not make my  2nd p ayment until they had the documentation they needed to proceed. When I received the page, I signed and dated it and sent in back to them.  <P/> The next time I heard from them, they informed me that the modification was no longer valid because the payments had not been paid and there was a glitch in the paperwork. They said I needed to begin the process again so I sent them a complete financial package again ( RMA Package ) and waited for them to process the paperwork through their Underwriting Dept.  <P/><P/> Soon after I received a Notice of  Sale  for the date of  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . When I called them up to inquire about the sale date I was told that there must be some mistake because my modification package was still in review. They were going to check into it and get back to me and assured me that it would get straightened out.  1024.41 ( b ) Receipt o f Loss Mitigation application - A servicer shall exercise reasonable diligence in obtaining documents and information to complete a loss mitigation application.  <P/> About 10 days after that conversation I received another letter stating that the sale date had been moved to  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  instead of  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I immediately called them to find out what was going on and told them that I was in review for a modification. They told me that the Underwriting Dept. needed a minimum of 37 days to review a homeowner for a modification so there wasnt enough time to modify the loan. Are you kidding me??? There was plenty of time to review until they moved the sale date up 30 days!!! Violation of The Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act ( Regulation X )  1024.41  Loss mitigation procedures. The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau established rules to protect mortgage borrowers from costly surprises and runarounds by their servicers.  <P/> They now tell me there is nothing they can do to postpone the sale date or modify the loan. Nationstar continues to violate the  Dodd-Frank Consumer Protection Act . They have dual-tracked my mortgage while avoiding an opportunity to work out something rather than foreclosure for us.    1024.41 ( g  ) Dual Tracking is prohibited. Servicers can not start a foreclosure proceeding if a borrower has already submitted a complete application for a loan modification or other alternative to foreclosure. CFPBs mortgage servicing rules ensure that borrowers in trouble get a fair process to avoid foreclosure, borrowers shouldnt be surprised by the start of a foreclosure proceeding until they have had time to explore all available options.  <P/> Please help us again with this egregious, unlawful attempt by  Nationstar  to take our home that we love. The sale date is  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , PLEASE HELP!!!  <P/>  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  &  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'a sale date was postponed and the sale date was postponed. the modification was approved and my 1st payment was supposed to begin in XX/');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3212,'06/06/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I am on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and my truck is financed with Chase. This payment is being paid by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  insurance that was sold to me when I bought my truck. Recently the insurance company held up my payments on the truck when I was switching doctors. When Chase received the payments to catch it up, they applied one paym ent (  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ) to the loan and the credit bureau is still showing that the  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  paym ent are past due. We have no idea what Chase did with our payment and they wo n''t fix or tell the credit bureau that we are current.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a paym ent is being paid by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] insurance that was sold to me when I bought my truck. the insurance company held up');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3213,'06/06/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','I have attempted multiple times to communicate with Navient and receive some help in discussing my repayment options since  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]     2015  when I graduated. They forced me into a 10 year repayment without consulting or helping me through it. I have felt really confused and sort of pushed since I graduated with them and now that I saw they were in a lawsuit I realized maybe they could have actually been helpful had they approached my situation the correct way. I would have liked to have my repayment plan discussed with me and I am now a little worried that I am going to be end up paying more than I need on my loans.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'I have attempted to communicate with Navient and receive some help in discussing my repayment options since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015 when I graduated. they forced me into');
