INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3262,'05/25/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','Nationstar recently completed the PMI removal process from my loan but is refusing to refund my PMI over payments in the amount of {$540.00} for the months of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 is the day of record for my PMI request for removal. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is the day I was transferred to Nationstar. Nationstar claims they ''re only responsible for refunding the PMI I made to them. This is a clear violation of the Homeowners Protection Act. I have spent hours and hours trying to resolve the issue of PMI removal with the company. This particular incidence is different than recent complaint # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which Nationstar claimed the issue had been resolved.
Nationstar claims they refunded my appraisal fee of {$450.00}. In my opinion, this is an attempt to further break the law. All I ''m asking for is my rights to be honored. Please cancel any {$450.00} appraisal fee " reimbursement '''' ( wherever that money is floating ) and refund the over-payments in the amount of {$540.00}. That is the law and legal accounting is what I ''m asking for. Attached is the letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where they ''re attempting to address a different CFPB claim that they have no responsibility in refunding any PMI payments. This is a business issue between Nationstar and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], as Nationstar initiated the purchase of my loan and it ''s not my responsibility to deal with business related problems between these [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] companies.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'Nationstar refuses to refund my PMI over payments in the amount of $540.00. the company claims they refunded my appraisal fee of $450.00');
