INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3284,'05/21/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','Store credit card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','On X/X/2017 I overpaid my account by {$270.00}. I intended to pay another account I held with Synchrony Financial. I recognized my mistake and called them on X/XX/17. I call them to inform them of this mistake. They assured me they would correct the mistake and credit the correct account. They mistakenly transferred twice that amount. They then sent a statement showing I owed {$270.00} because of their mistake. I called and spoke to 2 representatives in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who told me I owed the money. I asked to be transferred to a representative in the United States. I then spoke with a young lady who could n''t assure me they would fix my issue. I then asked to speak to her boss by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] could n''t have been any more rude or disrespectful. He finally admitted the mistake but gave no assurance they would make it right. This company seems to be deceiving their customers in order to gain financially! They need to be audited federally to show this unethical practice.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'on X/X/2017 I overpaid my account by $270.00. they assured me they would correct the mistake and credit the correct account. they then sent ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3285,'05/21/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','To w hom it may conc ern, I mailed a  Multiple Inquiry Rem oval  Letter  on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,    2017  by certified mail in order to dispute information, in regards to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  hard inquiries, that was being reported on my credit report. They received the letter on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,    2017  and they completed the request on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  2017 . The request that I submitted included  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Hard Inquiries that were not factual and I received the same response for ALL inquiries, which was " Inquiries are a factual record of file access. If you belie ve this was unauthorized, please contact the creditor. '''' According to the FCRA Rules, FCRA 623 ( b ) ( 2 ) and 611 ( a ) ( 1 ), it states that any information can be disputed and MUST be investigated and if you do not investigate AND respond, the CRA must delete the disputed information from its files. The fact that I received a response 8 days after the receipt of my certified letter, one can assume that there was no investigation into the matter. I plan to purchase a home this year and having this many hard inquiries on my credit report  display as a sign of financial trouble, when this is not the case. I am submitting this complaint due to the lack of investigation into my original dispute for hard inquiries that does not belong to me. I did not sign for anything. This is unfair practices by a credit reporting agency with no concern for the credit worthiness of a consumer.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a letter to a credit report requesting information was sent to me. the letter included hard inquiries that were not factual. the letter was sent to the creditor.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3286,'05/21/2017','Debt collection','Payday loan debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','On Thursday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  2017  @  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I spoke to a representative o f Majestic Financial  and I was told that my payment scheduled for  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  2017  would pay off my balance on my account. I requested all communication be in wrting and to cease & desist all phone calls in an email that the supervisor had given me if I wanted to dispute the debt. I sent the email as instructed on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and I stated I was disputing this debt and i stated that if they feel as though I owe anything, to send me a letter in writing with my pay off balance. I received a phone call from their call center the following day,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  @  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and I can provode cipies of my phone redords if needed. I also received a letter with no balance and threatening to take action against me if I do n''t pay my balance. Under the Fdcpa, if a consumer disputes the debt, my understanding is the creditor has to send validation of debt and the balance owed. I requested this in writing within 14 days as instructed and have yet to receive anything outside of this letter','Tribal Lending Enterprise, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a representative o f Majestic Financial told me my payment would pay off my balance. he asked to cease & desist all phone calls in an email that the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3287,'05/20/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','I believe the company failed to properly notify me of the terms and conditions of the debt such as the amount owed and payment due dates. The company stated because they have not received a payment in over over 30 days that they forwarded the account to the state of California tax franchise board for collection. I have not received any communication from AllianceOne prior to    XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  .  The terms of the payment agreement was NEVER outlined nor was there a payment agreement. Therefore, to send my account to another company is unjust and unfair legal practices. Secondly, the company charges a {$10.00} fee to make payments by credit card online and {$0.00} to mail a payment. I believe to charge such a ridiculous amount is also unfair to an consumer who is trying to settle their debt and are forced to pay {$10.00} as a " convenience fee '''' when payment by mail are easily lost. AllianceOne is a terrible company that needs better business practices. There was never a payment schedule identified so it is unfair to suddenly send a threatening to suspend my driver ''s license and forward it to the Calfornia Franchise Tax Board. AllianceOne mailed a lette r dated  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and on   XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   t  hey forwarded the account to another collection agency without giving me an opportunity to respond the letter.','AllianceOne Recievables Management',2.0,2.0,'the company has not received a payment in over 30 days. the company charges a $10.00 fee to make payments by credit card online. the company charges ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3288,'05/20/2017','Debt collection','Medical debt','Threatened to contact someone or share information improperly','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    called me three t imes at my workplace on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  2017 afte r being told during the first phone call that I ''m unallowed to take calls at work. The second phone call, they spoke to a co-worker and left a message. The coworker told them not to call the job. And then he called a final time, requesting to speak to me and spoke to the coworker that repeated not to call. He said he was an account manager and needed to speak to me regarding my debt, and he kept harassing my coworker. She simply hung up. This was all within less than an hour and a half.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'afte r told me that he''m unallowed to take calls at work'' he called me three t imes at my workplace on ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3289,'05/20/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Closing on a mortgage','I am writing to complain that PNC Mortgage extracted loan fees from us under false pretense. We submitted a loan application to PNC Mortgage on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017, requesting a conventional 15-Year Fixed mortgage for a total loan amount of {$94000.00}. After submitting all requested paperwork, we were told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Loan Processor ( Phone : ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Email : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) that our loan was " conditionally approved, '''' and that we needed to pay an up-front appraisal fee of {$650.00}. I asked what the conditions were, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card. after a couple days she said there was a {$2000.00} judgement on our title report that we needed to clear before the loan would be approved. I asked for information about the judgement, as I was unaware. The next day, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] responded that the judgement was not going t be a problem, and that there were no barriers to our loan. She then asked us again for the appraisal fee, which we paid via credit card. A month passes before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] contacts us again on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to say that the underwriter would not approve the loan unless the judgement is cleared. I asked again for information about the judgement. She responded with : " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], My apologies, you are correct! This judgment was cleared on your title. It was just not removed from the list of things we are paying off with your loan. Therefore, I mistook it as something still needing to be paid off. After further investigation, I noticed that the amount was the same as the judgment we cleared on your title a while back. The judgment will be removed from the list by the underwriter before closing. Again, my sincerest apologies for my misunderstanding. Regards, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Loan Processing Associate PNC Mortgage, a division of PNC Bank, NA '''' The following day, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Senior Mortgage Loan Officer, e-mailed : " Good afternoon, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] informed me what has transpired on your loan and Im sorry for the confusion. It appears that that judgment does have to be paid off prior to closing. Is this something you want to do? If not, we will not be able to close the loan per the underwriter. Thks [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Senior Mortgage Loan Officer Home Lending Center NMLS # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] " I replied : " As I explained to her, and now for the third time, we have no information about this supposed judgement, or why we are expected to pay it. This came up a month and a half ago. At that time I asked her to forward to me what information you had. After a day she said the matter had been cleared and was not a problem. This issue was apparently put aside in order to get me to pay for the appraisal, and then it could be brought up again at the last minute. Send me whatever information you have about the judgement. If I do not receive documentation within 48 hours, we will withdraw our loan application, and I will expect a refund of our appraisal fee, which I now believe was extracted under false pretenses. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] responded with a New Jersey state courts case number, which the state court could not find when contacted by phone. Later a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] contacted me and promised to find our how we can clear the judgement from our records. Three weeks have passed with no response to my phone calls. This leaves us in a catch 22 : we can not complete the loan without clearing this phantom judgement from our credit report, and no one can tell us who we need to pay or why. PNC has now closed the loan application, and we feel we have been duped into paying loan fees based on deceptive statements when the bank had no intention of processing the loan.','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a loan application was submitted to PNC Mortgage on a total loan amount of $94000.00. the judgment was cleared on your title, but the judgment was not');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3290,'05/19/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','On about  X/XX/17   , I saw that there was a fraudulent charge on m y TJ Maxxx Cr edit Card, so I called the company and they automatically cancelled my card and got me a new card soon after. I was charged for {$800.00} ( card insurance company ), random {$1.00} charges, and {$20.00} for   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   in Massachusetts on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( I do n''t live there ). I was satisfied at first, because my fraudulent charges were refunded on  X/X/2017   . I got my new  TJ Maxx cre dit card on around  X/XX/2017    ( because that ''s when I made my first purchase on it ) and between  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  -  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , I made purchases at local stores only. On  X/XX/2017   , I was charged again for {$33.00} for a fraudulent charge through a company called   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  . I have never used   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   before and was surprised that my card information was taken again. I called the company and they " fixed '''' it for me, by running a fraud report and taking away the fraudulent charg e (  by  X/XX/2017   , I had everything taken off of my account ). On  the day I calle d them about the fraudulent charged I asked for my credit card to be canceled completely, because I was unsure how anyone gained access to my new credit card information. Around  X/XX/2017   , I was going to get a check for {$.00} for over charges, and it was sent to me on  XX/XX/2017   . It is now  X/XX/2017   , and I got an email about my balance on m y TJ Maxx c redit card, which confused me, because my card was cancelled. I went and checked it and saw tha t TJ Maxx h ad recharged me for the fraudulent charge on my account of {$33.00} and that I had a credit of {$48.00} for extra interest charge (  X/XX/2017    ). I was angry, becau se TJ Maxx never sent me a check for the {$48.00} ( the {$.00} one the y sent me within 3 days of it being on my account ), yet it is today  X/XX/2017    and I never received it. I was also angry, because again I was being charged for a fraudulent purchase. I calle d TJ Maxx a t around  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  on    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]     . Speaking to customer service, I was told that   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   had sent them information that " proving '''' that I made a purchase through their company ( which I never di d ). TJ Maxx charged m e for this fraudulent charge again on   X/X/2017    . When I spoke to the customer service lady, she told me  TJ Maxx sent me information regarding this in the mail, yet I have not yet received any information regarding this purchase that " I made ''''. The customer service  lady said she would reissue a fraud claim on my account and sent me to the fraud expert, who sent me back to customer service for no reason! I do n''t believe this company is truthful in any way with how they handle their business. I believe it ''s very weird that I get fraudulent charges on a brand new credit card with in two weeks of having it. It seems that someone got my credit card information somehow, when the only people that know it are me and the credit card company. I also thing it ''s weird that they never sent me my {$48.00} refund check, yet they sent me the   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   refu nd check. This credit card company has been nothing but a headache to me that has hurt  my credit score (   because I cancelled my account over the continuous fraudulent charges ) and I wish upon no one else the pain and frustration I ''ve gone through with them.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,4.0,'m y TJ Maxx Cr edit card was cancelled after a fraudulent charge. a company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] automatically cancelled my card');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3291,'05/19/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Problems at the end of the loan or lease','Complaint number :  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  This has not been resolved, we have made numerous calls to  Hyundai Financial an d we still do not have our title, even the   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   called them on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and we still ca n''t get it.     First they said they sent the title on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , then the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  on the next call.     Then they said they had sent us a title release letter on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  we finally did get one dated  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and it ''s absolutely worthless it has to be electronically transmitted to the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .     The last call a couple of days ago they claimed they sent it electronically to the   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  we live in Nebraska and have done for 25 years.     We have repeatedly asked for call backs from managers and they tell us they do n''t do call backs. These people are incompetent!     Summary of your complaint Complaint number :  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Date submitted to CFPB :  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Date sent to company :  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Product : Consumer Loan Issue : Managing the loan or lease','HYUNDAI CAPITAL AMERICA',2.0,2.0,'the last call a couple of days ago they claimed they sent it electronically to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3292,'05/19/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','This charge was not authorized at any time and the company that made the unauthorized charge,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , has not responded to our attempts to contact them to reverse the charges. An initial charge first made on the card was authorized, but the company did not complete work we had hired them to do as agreed upon, and this second charge was made without our permission or consent and absent any proper notification. The reason being that the work the company was hired to do was not completed as agreed upon. We agree we owe a final payment, but we do not owe {$2800.00} and should not have been charged without a renegotiation.     As is clearly indicated in highlighted portions of printed emails,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  agrees that all the work agreed upon in the contract with them was not done and that they would agree to an adjusted ( lowe r ) final price. Instead, they charged our card for the full   amount without our permission and have avoided our calls and emails asking for this charge to be reversed.     We phoned Bank of America at the very first notice that this was charged and we informed the representative that this was an unauthorized charge. It was posted to our account anyway. In my conversations with  AAA Financial Services/Bank of America representatives on several occasions since, I was informed that we  would not be charged any late fees or penalties and that I would not have to pay until this investigation was completed.  One representative I spoke with said there would be documentation sent for us to complete, but I have not received this. I have only received bills. Please adjust your    records to reflect that this is an unauthorized charge that should not result in any late fees or penalties.
We never received any notice of any required documentation involving an alternate contractor  , nor were we informed by letter of any rejection of our case or contradictory finding of our claim. We were told by phone that the case was not resolved in our favor without any proper explanation. My last conversation with a dispute supervisor  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  on Sunday,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  , he gave me this mailing address and that perhaps someone here can help.     We sent a payment for {$2400.00}. This is the proper amount owed, and we hoped this will resolve this matter.     Specifically,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  did not dispose of the old appliances as they were supposed to, did not clean the work site in accordance with the agreement, and installed less labor-intensive floor tiles which was both incomplete and done improperly. The overcharge transaction was not authorized at all and if we wind up in court, we are confident that any fair judge will find in our favor.     The disreputable vendor in question,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , has been notified numerous times and his still refused to rectify this situation.     We recently sent payment for {$610.00} with the stipulation that we are making this payment under duress and only in an attempt to clear our credit rating. We fully intend to pursue this case in the courts and retrieve this money from  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .     Bank  of America/AAA Financial Services was   notified immediately that this charge was unauthorized and took no action to protect consumers from a fraudulent charge. Additionally, it agreed by cashing the check we sent earlier this year to resolve the matter with that payment and then violated that stipulation.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'unauthorized charge was not authorized at any time. the company that made the charge has not responded to our attempts to contact them. the company that made the charge, [COMPTE');
