they did, they did it purposely to say they lost money. Not to mention the depreciation of the vehicle that always works in their favor, never the consumer.     In reviewing the original lease agreement, the following amounts were also paid : {$1500.00} - lease signing {$350.00} - Turn in fee Why was no one notified until 7 months after the vehicle was returned to the dealership that they now claim a balance is owed? They were advised there would be no estate and they agreed to the terms because of his death.     Thank you  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  deceased  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   )','AMERICAN HONDA FINANCE CORP',2.0,2.0,'CFPB contacted the CFPB in regards to my complaint. a leased car was charged $1500.00 even though he was yet again leasing another car');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3296,'05/18/2017','Mortgage','Other type of mortgage','Applying for a mortgage','I have been trying to modify my mortgage for  six mont  hs with Shellpoint Mortgage Servicing, everytime they tell me I ha ve all the documents submitted and it will go to underwriting it never happens, I would call back and they would say they need new or updated documents. It would take me to call them to get that answer. On  X/XX/2017   I  called and spoke to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and she told me the documents I needed and I faxed them over. On  X/XX/2017   I d id call again to see the status on the loan and they said they were procesing it. They did send out  one lette r back on    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  , 2017  stating the package was incomplete. On  X/XX/2017    I did fax over the information that they had requested with a cover page stating to please call me immediately if any further documentation was needed. No call back, when I called in early  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  they said I needed additional documentation, so on   X/X/2017  I   f axed over the items requested. No call back.  Early   XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I called to see the status and they said they needed additional documentation. On  X/XX/2017   I fax ed over items requested. No call back.    X/XX/2017   I s poke to   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    and he told me i needed to send additional documents I did so on    X/XX/2017  . N o call back. In early  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I finally was able to speak to the person in charge of my loan  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and he told me the information his representatives was telling me was not true, and began to tell me the documents he needed for it to go to underwriting. ( I have left numerous messages for  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and he never returned the call. ) O n   X/X/2017   I s ent over all the information that  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  requested with a cover letter stating to please call me if he needed any additional information, and left my cell number. No call back. On    X/X/2017   I spo ke to a representative named and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and she said I needed to send additional documentation which I did with a cover letter to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and no call back. Every time I sent over the documentation that was requested I felt the package was complete and going to underwriting and when I would call to see the status, it always resulted in wanting additional documents.I have called and sent documents over other times in the past 5 months but did not document them. I have called and asked for  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  supervisor and left messages but no return calls and never any letters from  Shellpoint e xcept for the  one i n  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  , 2017','Shellpoint Partners, LLC',2.0,2.0,'shellpoint mortgage service has been trying to modify my mortgage for six mont hs. everytime they tell me I ha ve all the documents submitted and it will go to underwriting');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3297,'05/18/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','False statements or representation','I received my first call from this company AFTER they contacted my former in-laws and gave them information about my supposed debt. My forme r MIL ...   former by 7 years ... .called me with the number to contact  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   at Brennan and Clark . She told me that   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   claimed she was an attorney and that   I needed to get this squared away so I did n''t get taken to court. This was the FIRST TIME I HEARD OF THIS COMPANY. How incredibly embarrassing. This debt is a recent debt from a car insurance company that cancelled my insurance. I called  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  back. She apologized right away for giving away my personal information to " secondary contact ''''  ( former inlaws ).  She knew right away that what she did was not acceptable, and illegal. I have NO idea where she got their information ... from a   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   search of my name? This is when she got my phone n umber ( a number that has been the same for nearly 4 years ). This was under four weeks    ago. When she spoke with me, once again, she claimed she was from an attorney ''s office. The debt is obviously mine and instantly I said I would pay half the debt within the hour and that she could call me to pay the rest in  one  month. She has been relentlessly calling while I ''m at work, for several days. She has le ft two add itional voicemails to " fix my debt '''' but today left a threatening voicemail that their lawyer will contact me if not " fixed by   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  . '''' I immediately called back and asked her if she worked for an attorney. She said no. I asked if she were part of an attorney ''s office. She said no. I asked if any attorney ''s worked in that office. She said no. She said she believes that a department works with some type of legal services. At that point she would no longer answer any of my questions and tried to send me to her supervisor. He did not pick up but his phone but his extension is  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I called her back to get more information but she will no longer pick up. Her phone number is  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Brennan & Clark, Ltd., LLC',2.0,2.0,'a former in-law called me with the number to contact her. she told me that she claimed she was an attorney and that I needed to get this squared away so I did');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3298,'05/18/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','This is an ongoing issue with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and Experian.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  has resolved the issue. On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,    2017, I  sent a letter to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  requesting a Chain of Title proving that THEY OWN A DEBT of which they are entitled to collect and therefore allowed to report on my credit report. They sent back a letter, but were unable to furnish any documents that verified that are in fact, the actual debt owner. Since that time I have been fighting to get this account taken off of my credit report. If  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  can not prove that they have the proper documents showing that I owe them a debt, they ca n''t possibly be able to add that to my credit report. Regardless of the information that they have on me - my name, my date of birth, my social security number, account numbers, etc. - they do not have proof that I owe them anything. Does this mean that as long as I have someone ''s personal information, I am allowed to report on their credit claiming that they are not paying me a debt??? No, that would not be legal. It is not legal for  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to report on my credit report if they ca n''t prove that they own a debt of which I owe. I asked  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to prove that what they are reporting on my credit report is truly a debt as to which they own a title that I owe, and they were unable to provide that. This tells me that they have nothing showing that they own this debt and therefore I do n''t owe them anything and it ca n''t be legally reported on my credit report. I have the name and information and social security number of several of my family members and employees. This does not mean that I can submit information through my company to   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    or  Experian and st ate that they owe me money and ruin their credit and when they file a dispute as long as I can provide   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   and Experian with their personal information it will stand on their credit report? That  is EXACTLY  what is being done to me.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ca n''t prove that they own a debt that I owe and therefore, they ca n''t report it on my credit report. I have been told by   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   and Experian that  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  has provided them with my name, social security number, address - all of my personal information ... HOWEVER THEY HAVE NOT PROVIDED PROOF THAT THEY OWN A DEBT OF WHICH I OWE THEM. There has not been any paperwork that proves that  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  owes  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  a dime. How can this be reported on my credit report??? If a debt ca n''t be proved you ca n''t just add it to my credit report. Am I able to say that  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  owes me {$50000.00} and report that on his credit??? I have his name and his soc and all of his personal information, so if you asked to me verify that I could, but I just pulled that number out of the air. There is nothing anywhere that I have that proves he owes that. I have no documents signed that I can show you, but because I have his personal information, I can report that on his credit file? Is that what you are telling me??? No way!  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  needs to be removed from my credit report immediately. They have failed to show that I owe them any money and therefore ca n''t be saying that I do on my credit report.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a letter to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has resolved the issue. it is not legal for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to report');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3299,'05/18/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Myself and wife had  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Federal  Liens on our credit report. The IRS withdrew them on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / 17  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /   17  and filed notices of withdrawal of filed  Federal Tax Liens in th e  correct county.  We disputed with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  the tax liens and sent copies to have them deleted since they were withdrawn. The first time they " verified '''' them both and then on reinvestigation corrected only  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and still reported the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /   17  tax lien as " verified '''' again. We have done this process twice once for myself and once for my wife with the same results.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  used a third party vendor for their information, LexisNexis.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  is ignoring  our Lien Withdrawal.    Since our state is included in the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  settlement and  Federal Tax Liens are t o be deleted we find this conduct very irregular.','LEXISNEXIS',2.0,2.0,'the IRS withdrew them on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / 17 and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / 17.');
