INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3301,'05/17/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','I currently carry a large balance, over {$13000.00}, on  a US Bank consumer credit card which I h ave had in good standing since  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Most of the balance owed is on cash advances, which I took in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to help fund a business startup. Since  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , m y FICO credit score , which I track meticulously, has increased by more than  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  points and is currently near  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Despite this, and despite my other credit card companies having lowered my Variable APR significa ntly, US Bank  is charging me 22.74 % on purchases and 24.74 % on cash advances. When I contacted cardmember services to ask if the bank could lower my rate, given the positive change in my credit and length of time I have had the card ( and never once had a 30 day late payment in over 13 years ), I was told by a supervisor,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , that my APR has been frozen at 22.74 %. What was especially troubling, is that another customer service rep  at US Bank me ntioned earlier in the same phone call that there was an offer to lower my rate on my existing credit card to 19.99 %, told me that I was eligible for it, then retracted and said my APR was frozen at 22.74 %, so the offer would not apply. When I asked for the reason for my APR being frozen at such a high rate, the supervisor said I was sent a letter as to the reason  one ye ar ago ( which I did not recall receiving ). When I asked if he could retrieve a copy of it, he said he could not. He also offered no explanation as to why my APR has been frozen at such a high interest rate, and why it can not be adjusted downward to a lower rate based on my good credit. Meanwhile, as you can see i n the US Bank  Credit Card statements I have attached, the total interest I am being charged is going up each month, even as I pay the balance down.','U.S. BANCORP',4.0,4.0,'m y FICO credit score has increased by more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points. despite this, my other credit card companies have lowered');
