INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3308,'05/16/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','I dispute this Item  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  : Account  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Amount {$250.00}. please deleted this item TransUnion. TransUnion did not compile with the State Attorney General  Settlement Agreement and 609. Disclosures to consumers [ 15 U.S.C. 1681g ] ( a ) Information on file ; sources ; report recipients. Every consumer reporting agency shall, upon request, and subject to 610 ( a ) ( 1 ) [ 1681h ], clearly and accurately  disclose to the consumer : I have the right to demand that you disclose to me all of the documents that you have recorded and retained in your file at the time of this request concerning the accounts that you are reporting in my credit report. Please dont respond to my request by saying that these accounts have been verified. Send me copies of the documents that you have in your files that were used to verify them. If you do not have any documentation in your files to verify the accuracy of these disputed accounts then please delete them immediately as required under  Section 611 ( a ) ( 5 ) ( A ) ( i ). By publishing these inaccurate and unverified items on my credit report and distributing them to 3rd parties you are damaging my reputation and credit worthiness. According Section 15 U.S. Code 1681d - Disclosure of investigative consumer reports ( b ) Disclosure on request of nature and scope of investigation Any person who procures or causes to be prepared an investigative consumer report on any consumer shall, upon written request made by the consumer within a reasonable period of time after the receiptby him of the disclosure required by subsection ( a ) ( 1 ), make a complete and accurate disclosure of the nature and scope of the investigation requested. This disclosure shall be made in a writing mailed, or otherwise delivered, to the consumer not later than five days after the date on which the request for such disclosure was received from the consumer or such report was first requested, whichever is the later. The description of the procedure used to determine the accuracy and completeness of the information is   hereby requested as well, to be provide within 5 days of the completion of your reinvestigation.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'I dispute this item [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. please delete this item TransUnion.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3309,'05/16/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','Discover fail ed to pay me {$300.00} for my credit card account  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .     I spent {$3000.00} in purchases at  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  using   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   in    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]     ( s hown i n SCREENSHOT 1 ). Under  the terms of promotion,  Discover was   supposed to give me 10 %, which would be doubled at the end of the year to 20 %. The " double cashback '''' promotion was  one I was  enrolled in from   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   to   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    ( the fin al amount deposited is shown in SCREENSH OT 2, provi ng I was enrolled ).     On   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ,  Discover finally awarded th e cashback ( shown in SCREENSHOT  3 ). However, the amount was only {$300.00} ( shown in SCREENSHOT 4 ), which is 10 % rather than 20 %. I am the refore owed an additonal {$300.00}.     I contacted  Discover customer  service, where a supervisor named  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in their  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  office opened an investigation for me. However, at the end of their internal review, they refused to award me the additional cashback owed with no further explanation, and refused to provide an email detailing how the cashback was calculated.     I am owed an additional {$300.00} from  Discover from  their   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   and  Discover Match pro motions, and ask for immediate cash relief.','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'Discover failed to pay me $300.00 for my credit card account. Discover was supposed to give me 10 %, which would be doubled at the end of the year');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3310,'05/16/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','My name is  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  from the great state if new jersey and I have been the victim of fraudulent credit reporting. inaccurate medical debt information has been shown as a credit liability in terms of suits and typical double-dipping of insurance which is an admonishable obimination of that greed. So much so it is illegal as clearly described in the free credit reporting act. Nothing is being done and this has SERIOUSLY compromised my ability to do business as a   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   Please see that someone actually does something about this and not in the ridiculously short time the major agencies allow. I do not need   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  . I need the parties responsible for this to remove the petty and destructive occlusions NOW and I furthermore feel I deserve compensatory damages.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'if new jersey has been the victim of fraudulent credit reporting. inaccurate medical debt information has been shown as a credit liability. it is illegal as clearly described in the free credit reporting');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3311,'05/16/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I consigned for a loan, had a missed payment, and was never notified about it before it was reported late on my credit report. The payment was not made late. I got no phone call about it or any opportunity to make the payment. The account owner is also going to file a complaint today.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the payment was reported late on my credit report. the account owner is also going to file a complaint today.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3312,'05/16/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Today   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I spoke with a Transunion Manager by the name of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  about removing a couple of unauthorized inquiries on my credit file. Before I even spoke to him Transunion had a automatic message stating there was a glitch regarding inquiries and if we were affected by the glitch to have the inquiries name and date. Furthermore  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  was the manager that answered my call and he said to have inquiries removed I would have to contact the creditor and have them write a letter on my behalf to get the inquiries removed. I stated to him that the inquiries I wanted removed had already been removed and they were readded because of their glitch which is not my fault. He further stated there was no glitch but Transunion has a automatic message stated so. I then went on to ask him how do they investigate inquiries since I have recently disputing these inquiries once again and that same day they came back factual. He stated that they do n''t investigate, that once something hit my credit report it ''s factual and will remain. I told him that ''s not an investigation and that by law if a credit reporting agency such as themselves want to add and remove things that they have to do so in writing within 5 days and they have yet to do so.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'Transunion manager said there was a glitch regarding inquiries. he said to have inquiries removed I would have to contact the creditor. he said they don''t');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3313,'05/15/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Advertising and marketing, including promotional offers','Applied and rece ived First Progress Card. Init ial  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  paid by Bank card on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  . Paid remaining Bank balance of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  .    Contacted First Progress  at  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to ask for refund of my  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and to cancel the new card, I was instructed that I would only receive  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  due to they ca n''t find the initial payment on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .   Both transactions are clearly on my bank statement which I have sent to them.','Synovus Bank',2.0,2.0,'Applied and rece ived First Progress Card. paid by Bank card on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3314,'05/15/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Fees or interest','What a nightmare to get someone who I can hear. It has only gotten worst instead of better.  Citi card does not care. 3 hours of no help again t oday. I am so exhausted by the timr help arrives.     The voice system is not clear either.  Overseas  is a nightmare too.     I was told my annual fee would be waived or a promotion.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'Citi card does not care. 3 hours of no help again t oday. the voice system is not clear either.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3315,'05/15/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','This company,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , sent me a letter and claimed I have unpaid amount {$380.00} to Sun  Trust Bank . Except I do n''t do business wit h Suntrust Bank. I visited Suntrust an d ask them if they have an account under my name, gave them my driver license and the letter from  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Suntrust search and came back negative, they do n''t have me as a customer, they also checked back dated to year   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  , nothing.     I also checked my credit report and verify a possible identify theft, again, nothing. Contacted  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , gave them the reference #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Informed them they have the wrong person which they denied ... I asked how they get my record. They could n''t give me an answer.       [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','SUNTRUST BANKS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a letter from a company, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent me a letter. they claimed they have unpaid amount $380.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3316,'05/15/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Getting a credit card','I have inherited a  Discover credit card. As I look at my Credit Report, the report says  that I opened this account in    1993 ( which  is not true ). First of all, Discover Bank does not give credit cards to someone th at their credit score  is around  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Secondly, if I would have opened this account i n 1993, I have  had  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  bankruptcies and the card would have been wiped out. Here is the most important part, this card belongs to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  who passed away several years ago. My wife inherited her estate and I was not a part of that. The estate has be all settle and then I started getting calls about this card a couple of years after  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  passed away.','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'a credit card belongs to a person who passed away several years ago. the card belongs to a person who passed away in 1993.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3317,'05/15/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','There have been so many servicing errors and terrible customer service experiences regarding my private student loans with  Wells Fargo th at I will just touch on the main ones here.    Wells Fargo preyed on  my father and myself in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , pushing me to take out a private student loan even though neithe r one  of us showed adequate credit or evidence to be able to pay it back. These loans have caused hardship on my cosigner as well as myself.  Wells Fargo  failed to provide any resources for borrowers to assist them during economic hardships after loans were taken out. I took out the student loans to pay for a college education, but I would be better off financially if I had never been pushed to take out a private student loan with  Wells Fargo. {$14000.00} wa s financed in   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   and I will have paid more than {$33000.00} by the end of the payment period. I have received nothing but harassment, misinformation, and damage to my personal as well as financial reputations.   In   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    (   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   )  during a repayment period, I had automatic payments scheduled. I found out from my cosigner that he was receiving letters that the loans had late payments. I was confused and found out the day the payments had been scheduled was technically after the due date  Wells Fargo  had set. This meant I was accruing extra fees and late fees even though I was making full payments on the loans every single month. This reflected on my cosigners credit report as well as my own. They told my cosigner, We are charging you {$30.00} each month for being late. My scheduled payments were coming out the first of each month, and the due date was the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  of each month.    Wells Fargo fa iled to provide me with information regarding releasing my cosigner from the loans. I had over 24 months of consecutive payments, so I inquired about cosigner release. On   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   my account was not able to be located even though  Wells Fargo Representatives via  phone were able to identify my account given the exact same information. ( Please see enclosed copies of letters. ) Due to the delays and inadequate treatment of my account, my cosigner was not released.      [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    my household went from  two incomes to one.  I called  Wells Fargo  immediately, attempting to plan for the incoming months. I was met with disdain. The representative said there was absolutely nothing they could do for me until I had already missed payments. I am a responsible borrower and consumer ; thus, I did not want to wait. I also did not want that kind of negative activity filed on my cosigner or my own credit ratings. I wanted options and resources, and I was given none. I reached out for deferment in the next couple of months because my financial situation had not changed. When I sought this, I again was met with disdai n. Wells Fargo repres entatives told me things like, You should just ask a relative. I do not have a wealthy relative, and I find it insulting, demeaning, and condescending to assume I have not explored all of my options, including being privileged with a bloodline possessing an abundance of money. Why would I have taken out a student loan in the first place if I had financial support from family? I have a better chance of winning the lottery than finding a wealthy relative, so that was the answer I gave the representative on the phone. They told me,  Maam,  I can not put that down as an official response. If I do your deferment will be denied. I was forced to say, I will find another job that pays more money. In order for the deferment to go through.   As of   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   I became unemployed. The non-profit in which I had full time employment forced all of its employees to take  two full weeks of furlough prior to that as well. I have actively searched for employment si nce then. In the meantime both of my loans have been charged off.   As soon as I became unemployed, I again, notifie d Wells Fargo  of my status. I assumed, incorrectly, that I would be helped. I asked the question, Surely I am not the very first person to become unemployed who has student loans to pay? The representatives response was silence and then he said, I  imagine not, but  we dont have anything for you.   On   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   at   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   a third party was contacted regarding the student loans. The  Wells Fargo rep resentatives excuse was that a skip trace was put out on the cosigner. The cosigner had been in contact with  Wells Fargo almost continuously for several months. Wells Fargo absolutely had all of his information. Their call logs reflect this fact. They had been in phone contact with him less than seven days prior. Wells Fargo called the third party on the third partys personal and unpublished cell phone number. He was in a work meeting and thus could not and did not answer the call. It went to his voicemail, where the Wells Fargo representative did leave a message. I immediately contacted Wells Fargo to investigate this. They admitted it was a mistake, and moved my account to an executive repr esentative named  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , titled Research and Remediation Analyst,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  xecutive Office, Customer Experience Team. She blocked the third partys number from being contacted in the future. I n the follow up letter  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  says, If we call but are not able to speak with you, we  may c all several additional times a day to reach you. I consider that harassment, and she openly admits to harassment as well as future potential harassment. Even though  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  had informed me that she would be the onl y one contact ing me about the account, on Saturday   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   in the morning, my cosigner received another phone call from a particularly rude  Wells Fargo r epresentative who was NOT  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Her name is  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , ID number  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . She did not have the cosigners full name. When he corrected her, she spoke in an inconsiderate tone. It had nothing to do with pronunciation. She had the name wrong. She admitted to the cosigner that, I know this account has gone to  executive, bu t Im still calling. The cosigner asked her what her ID number was.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  raised her voice telling him she can not give out her last name. The cosigner never asked for her last name. He simply asked for the ID number to follow up with the call. The following Monday, I reached out to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  via phone, but she has yet to return that call.  ( Today is     [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   )  There have been so many mistakes made with my account that I fear other relatives or friends will be contacted and my personal reputation as well as my cosigners will be damaged even further.   Both my cosigner and I have been repeatedly called by  Wells Fargo numerous times a day. Wells Fargo has failed to do their due diligence in mai ntaining accurate data. They inaccurately called my cosigners home phone number asking for me. My name has never been listed under that number.   As recent as   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  , a  Wells Fargo representative asked me, How are you paying your other bills?. I appreciate that someon e is concerned about my welfare. I do not appreciate personal questions that have nothing to do with the private student loans.   They threatened both my cosigner and I that if we did not pay a certain amount towards the loans that they would report this on our credit. We, of course, knew this fact already. There is a better way to inform people of policies besides sounding threatening and ask people to repay a debt. Threats do not need to be made.    Wells Fargo re presentatives harassed my cosigner so many times in regard to these student loans that he requested they stop all phone contact with him. The cosigner asked multiple times not to call him or contact him regarding the loans. The cosigner advised  Wells Fargo Representatives tha t they were calling at inconvenient times, including at meal time s ( dinner hours ) and too  late in the evening. They continued to call during those times up until   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  .    Wells Fargo Education Financial Services, a division of Wells Fargo Bank, N.A. harassed me. They compromised my personal reputation by contacting  third parties. My financial reputation has been destroyed because of the negative credit reporting. They need to be held accountable for their actions. These were student loans for education. It does not matter that  Wells Fargo is  worth {$1.00}  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , and I am not. I would love to simply pay these off with  one big chec k, but I can not at this time.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'neithe r one of us showed adequate credit or evidence to pay back loans. neithe r one of us showed adequate credit or evidence to be ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3318,'05/14/2017','Debt collection','Medical debt','Threatened to contact someone or share information improperly','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]     - negotiated total out of pocket expense with medical provider.    XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  - billed {$280.00}, in addition to insurance payment, for previously negotiated  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .    XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  - disputed collection attem pt b y H & R Accounts c iting the Fair Cre dit Reporting Act US C 1681s-2.      XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   -  H & R Ac  counts re ported non-payment of disputed debt to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .  H & R Accounts   did not indicate in their report, in violation   of the Fair Credit Reporting Act, that the debt was disputed. Following is the relevant excerpt from the act :  605.  Requirements relating to information contained in consumer reports  [ 15 U.S.C.   1681c ] ( f ) Indication of dispute by consumer. If a consumer reporting agency is notified pursuant to section 623 ( a ) ( 3 ) [ 1681s-2 ]     that information regarding a consumer who was furnished to the agency is disputed by the consumer, the agency shall indicate that fact in each consumer report that includes the disputed information.     I ''ve info rme  d H & R Accounts th at they are in violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act and asked them to remove the reports.','Avadyne Health Holdings, Inc',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - billed $280.00, in addition to insurance payment, for previously negotiated');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3319,'05/14/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','CitiMortgage has committed egregious violation in servicing our former account. CitiMortgage ref uses to take responsibility for  3 f ailed attempts at modification. It is THEIR failure, we cooperated and met our obligations under agreements fully.      CitiMortgage  refuses to report this modification period as required in regulation to all major credit bureaus/ reporting agen cies. CitiMortgage offe rs a lawyered and morally deficient explanation for not responding.  CitiMortgage re fuses to respond any further than attached documents reflect . CitiMortgage  has done great harm to former clients. Clients have continually corresponded t o CitiMortgage f or redress. These practices must cease.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'CitiMortgage ref uses to take responsibility for 3 f ailed attempts at modification. it is THEIR failure, we cooperate and met our obligations under agreements fully.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3320,'05/13/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with your lender or servicer','Over the course of the loan which has been o ver ten years  customer service only give information about deferment and forbearance. I found out about income base repayment plans from a coworker. I have been a   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   for over  tw  enty years and no one ever told me about the student loan forgiveness program until I learned about it two years ago from a  coworker.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'customer service only give information about deferment and forbearance. no one ever told me about the student loan forgiveness program until I learned about it two years ago.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3321,'05/13/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','On Tuesday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   I spoke to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  about a payment postpone ment ( piggyback ) a nd they agreed to do it. I asked several times about the effect it would have on my credit score. The consultant assured me that my credit score would not be harmed in any way. Today  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   I checked my credit score and the company has indeed gone back on their word and reported the payment as a 30 day late. I am now going to file bankruptcy because of the incorrect information I was given on a recorded call. This has effected my credit in such a manner that makes it impossible to fix the situation at hand. The spiral effect that is about to incur is the fault entirely of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a payment postponed on a nd they agreed to do it. the consultant assured me that my credit score would not be harmed. today [COMP');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3322,'05/12/2017','Money transfer, virtual currency, or money service','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','I feel th at western union should be held accountable for the large fees they charge for money transfers in minutes, when in fact it can take 2 hours for it to complete. Money in Minutes is misleading. I h ave had  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  transactions in the pa st 2 weeks that have had a 2 hour review process. My banking info and card I am using match my western union profile. The person I am sending money to is my h usband.   I contact ed Western Union about both m y transfers.      [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  transaction was on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / 17  in the amount of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in which I was charged  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for money in minutes. I contacted them to find out why my money transfer was in review, I was told he just needed to go to a person with his ID and not one of their Kiosks. However the email did not state that. At this time it was to late for me to go to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  since the funds had already been removed from my account.      [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  time was today  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in which I was sending my husband  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in which I was charged  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for transfer in minutes. After initiating I got an alert to call them to expedite the process or I could wait. I called and spoke to a woman at about  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  est. She asked me questions like, why I was sending it, where, and my relation to the receiver. At the end she said I will get an email with in 5 min and  that the transfer will be ready for pickup in which this time he could go to a person or Kiosk It is  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   est time and the transfer is still in progress under review. I called and spoke to a gentleman and he told me the review t akes 2 hours an d I would have to wait.     This was a domestic transfer as well.','WESTERN UNION COMPANY, THE',2.0,2.0,'money in minutes is misleading, but it can take 2 hours for it to complete. ed west union has a 2 hour review process for money transfers. a woman asked');
