INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3327,'05/11/2017','Credit card or prepaid card','General-purpose credit card or charge card','Problem with a purchase shown on your statement','We were using the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  MasterCard for fuel for our company vehicles. We just established this account in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . All employees  that drive  company vehicles were assigned a card with a unique PIN to avoid unauthorized transactions.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  contacted me via email on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   about suspicious activity on one of our employee ''s cards. After looking into it, we discovered that this person ''s card was used to run up over {$2700.00} in charges, while the employee was in a different city on a jobsite with the card in his possession. Only explanation is the card number was stolen by a skimmer on a gas pump. I was told to fill out a form to file the claim. I have conflicting emails from this company telling me how to file the complaint - some told me to fill a form out and email it, others told me to file online. I did both. Afte r 4-5 attem pts - I was finally able to get somebody to look into the claim. This was in late  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I have many emails showing my repeated attempts to get someone to help me with this issue. All that they do is open a claim for you, email you the claim #, then close the claim without doing anything. I received an apology via email for their poor service. I was promised resolution by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  . I did not receive any further communication until  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   at which time they denied the claim, stating that the disputed charges were not covered under our Terms & Conditions due to a "  10 card rule ''''. They said this is one of the many reasons they provide us with " tools necessary to monitor your account on a real-time basis to identify unauthorized use proactively ''''. However, I can not get anyone at the company to tell me how this card was used without the employee ''s unique PIN number. The PIN numbers are supposed to be one of the " tools '''' to prevent these incidents, and clearly this did not work. Also since I short paid our invoices by the fraudulent amount, they cut off all of our fleet cards without warning, leaving our drivers in bad positions because they could not purchase fuel when needed. This company has the worst customer service department and response time of any credit card company that I have ever worked with in my 25 years of experience.','REGIONS FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'employees were using the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card for fuel. they were assigned a unique PIN to avoid unauthorized transactions. the card number was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3328,'05/11/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','My mortgage company  Ditech  changed the monthly escrow amount during my  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   statement and due to business travel, I missed their letter informing of the increase of {$29.00}. I have auto pay being set up with my bank which did payment on time but short of {$29.00 } ( escrow increase ).  This resulted in a late fee of {$33.00}. I called on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to asked if the fee could be voided which they refused. I explained that considering my escrow balance is positive of {$450.00} and that they received my payment for the principal, the interest and most of the escrow monthly fee, they should not consider this a missed payment and therefore should not trigger a fee for this type/scale of error. I think this is unethical practice from a loan servicer and would like to file a formal complain.   My loan number is  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'mortgage company Ditech changed the monthly escrow amount. my mortgage company has changed the amount during my statement. this resulted in a late fee of $33');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3329,'05/11/2017','Vehicle loan or lease','Loan','Struggling to pay your loan','I had this SUV for maybe about a year, prior to it being totaled in an accident.  O  n  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   , my SUV  , tha t was financed through  Westlake Financial,  a   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , was in a rear-end collision that caused minor to moderate visible damages, but caused major computer and electrical damages-from the car that hit us, going under my  SUV, whi ch eventually caused it to no longer run. When taken to shops, I was told several different stories- from it needs a programmer, to it needs a new engine. When I to ld Westlake this, they  said they did n''t want to repo the vehicle, since it does n''t run, and that they did n''t loan me the truck, they loaned me the money, so that ''s what they wanted. As I said- we are still in the process of a settlement for this accident, meanwhile, I had to purchase another vehicle, so I could work everyday, get my  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  kids to school, to practices, to games, to the grocery store, and what if there was an emergency? I live    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   miles from the nearest hospital. I explained to the very rude rep at  Westlake, t hat I could not affor d to continue to pay {$500.00} a month, for this  SUV that is  no longer operable. They offered no solution or assistance and put the full remaining balance on my credit report and left the vehicle in my possession but never sent the title. Then, they sent just out a repo person out today- 2 years later?? I ''m confused and very frustrated- this charge-off on my credit report has prevented me from getting anything- a home, a person loan, or any kind of debt relief. I do n''t feel this is fair because, even if I paid the full amount to them, they still have the truck repossessed, and sell it at auction? and then I still have the bad report on my credit for the next 7 years? I explained to several of  the reps that ca lled from Westlake, th at I planned to pay them off, using the settlement money, if enough, and try to buy another SUV like that one that runs, or another engine, and try to fix it- I re ally liked it and it was great sized for my family, taking kids to school, carpooling with other moms for school pick up, games, etc. They offered no reduction in the amount, no assistance of any kind, and now I ca n''t get a straight answer out of anyone there- they know nothing about anything going on, or why they recently re-opened the repossession ticket, in the end of  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , this year, 2 years after they wrote the debt off and put it on my credit report. I would like to keep my  SUV and c ome to a much lesser settlement amount- since the vehicle is totaled- and have them remove the negative report from my credit reports. I thought that is what normally happens, after an accident that totals the vehicle, the insurance is supposed to pay off the vehicle- I had full coverage insurance and so did the guy that hit me- but the guy was from Florida,  where we were on vacation, and Florida is a no -fault state, so his insurance-  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]     [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  -refused to pay for the damages that were not visible. They only repaired the rear bumper. The tow package was messed up, the frame is bent, the suspension no longer airs up in the front, and it wont stay running, it spits and sputters, and shuts off. It was that way when I went to pick it up from the repair shop and the guy said  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  was aware but denied payment. The other driver was clearly  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and allowed to leave the scene. My insurance paid for everything else- my medical bills, my husbands medical bills, both of our physical therapy, and my rental vehicle. There were many problems with the accident, and then the way we were treated-by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] plus   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  and even the repair shop. That ''s why we are still in the lawsuit, to try and correct the problems, but I do n''t understand why I should have to pay the full price for the totaled vehicle, plus the repo it to sell at auction, plus my credit is ruined for 7 years? All because some   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   driver rear ended me, at a red light, and I get all of the negative effects, while the at fault driver, gets to walk free and have nothing done to him- and he got a new car from his insurance after the accident! This has definitely not been fair and needs to be addressed by someone of more authority than myself. Thank you for your time and assistance with this matter.','Westlake Services, LLC',2.0,2.0,'tha t was financed by westlake financial, a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3330,'05/11/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Improper use of your report','I HAVE SENT CERTIFIED LETTERS ON  3 DIF FERENT OCCASIONS TO ALL CREDIT BUREAUS ( EQUIFAX,   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    AND  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   ) I N  REGERDS TO A LL INQUIRES THAT I HAVE SEEN ON MY REPORTS THAT I WAS UNAWARE AND HAVE NO RECOLLECTION ON DOING OR APPROVING MYSELF, UPON LOOKING AT MY REPORTS ALSO NOTICED ALIASES AND MY  NAM EIN  DIFFERENT FORMAT WITH ADDRESSES BELONGIN G TO CALIFORNIA AND TEXAS WH ICH I HAVE NEVER LIVED NOR VIVISTED IN MY LIFE! THERE WERE PHONE NUMBERS INCLUDED FROM THOSE AREAS TOO! I SENT A PERSONAL UPDATE AND THEY WERE ABLE TO HANDLE THOSE BUT DIDNT UPDATE MY BIRTHDATE THEY HAVE ME AS  XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   THOS E ARENT MY BIRTHDATE, MY BIRHDATE IS   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   I FEEL THERE WAS FRAUDUALANT ACTIVITIES GOING ON AND LAST YEAR I REPORTED TO THEM ABOUT IT THEY WERE ABLE TO REMOVE  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ACCOUNT FROM   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   BUT  LEFT A NOTHER  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  IT ISNT MINES OR UNAWARE OF  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  FROM  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  THIS ACCOUNT ODESNT BELONG TIME AND I DISPUTED WITH ALL  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  COMPANIES AND NOTHING YET! I AM CONCERNED, FRUSTRATED AND FEELING HELPLESS! To whom it  may concer n, I mailed a Multiple Inquiry Removal Letter on   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   by certified mail in order to dispute information, in regards to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  hard inquiries, that was being reported on my credit report. They received the letter on   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   and they completed the request on   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  . The request that I submitted included  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Hard Inquiries that were not factual and I received the same response for ALL inquiries, which was " Inquiries are a factual record of file access. If you believe this was unauthorized, please contact the creditor. '''' According to the FCRA Rules, FCR A 623 ( b ) ( 2 ) and 611 ( a ) ( 1 ), it sta tes that any information can be disputed and MUST be investigated and if you do not investigate AND respond, the CRA must delete the disputed information from its files. The fact that I received a response 4 days after the receipt of my certified letter, one can assume that there was no investigation into the matter. I plan to purchase a home this year and having this many hard inquiries on my credit report display as a sign of financial trouble, when this is not the case. I am submitting this complaint due to the lack of investigation into my original dispute for hard inquiries that does not belong to me. I did not sign for anything. This is unfair practices by a credit reporting agency with no concern for the credit worthiness of a consumer.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'I FEEL THERE WAS FRAUDUALANT ACTIVITIES GOING ON AND LAST YEAR I REPORTED TO THEMABOUT IT THEY WE');
