does not have any documentation other than the PDF JH Portfolio provided to the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   ( i.  e.  signature contract agreeing to pay  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  they need to retract this from my credit file immediately.','JH Portfolio Debt Equities, LLC',2.0,2.0,'credit control LLC representing JH Portfolio violated the FCRA. he sent a letter to a previous address through credit control LLC. the credit collection agency attached a PDF');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3334,'05/10/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Problem with a credit reporting company''s investigation into an existing problem','Experian committed fraud and damaged  my credit score. I comp lained to a Experian associate on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / 2017  about  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  collections on my report that were wrong and low and behold on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / 2017  Experian made the criminal action of dropping my score  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  points for no other reason than spite! There is not one single solitary change on my report that would cause my score to drop in 3 days! There needs to be a government agency to watchdog over these corrupt credit reporting agencies. On their website they offer no reason as to why they dropped my score  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  points and I checked the other agencies my scores actually went up so I only can figure Experian has broken the law and damaged my credit for no legitimate reason. I ''m getting tired of having to complain all the time with the corruption that goes on with these agencies. I know this complaint will probably do nothing and I ''ll probably have to contact my attorney but I ''m trying to find a solution before it has to get to that point.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'experian committed fraud and damaged my credit score. there is no one single solitary change on my report that would cause my score to drop in 3 days. there is not');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3335,'05/10/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','The following are many letters- over 6 months, attempting to eliminate the PMI on our rental home loan. The last letter refers to a page out of our original mortgage with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( at the time ) being sent from the B of A to us stating under ''Automatic Termination of MI '' that when the loan balance reaches 78 % of the original value of the property, the MI will automatically be dropped. We have received NO response from The B of A.   In our research we have also discovered many complaints about the B of A doing the same thing to others. We also currently have a call into  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ''s office.   We look forward to your assistance in resolving this ongoing problem.   Thank you.      [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  (  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  )  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  IMPORTANT- LEGAL ACTION PENDING  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Bank of America MI Department RE : Request to Cancel PMI Loan #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  To whom it may concern ; We recently paid down our mortgage to 80 % of value. This payment will be received by B of A on   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   in the amount of {$5500.00}. Based on applied principal our debt should be below {$150000.00} at that time. The recent appraisal that you had requested dated   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   shows the property value at {$190000.00}. 80 % of this is {$150000.00}. Please cancel our PMI. If for any reason The B of A does not cancel the PMI we will move to refinance this loan with another lender. Thank you for your help.    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , CA.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Follow Up Notes :  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I have now received several documents from the B of A supposedly detailing the MI requirements on my loan to. NONE of these documents say anything about a 70 %  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  requirement. Unless you can show me documents that I executed when I borrowed this money from  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , I will expect that the MI be dropped, as I have met the only written requirements that I have- 80 %  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and after I spent the time and money to obtain an appraisal.   I will expect your response within  one  week or by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .   Thank you.      [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  (  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  )  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  We recently received another package dated  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  from The Bank of America, including another copy of our appraisal and a third letter stating that The B of A refuses to cancel our PMI due to a requirement for a 70 %  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in order to do so. None of the materials sent from the B of A have included the simple document that we have asked for : We need to see any document or disclosure that we signed at the time we took out the loan stating that we need to have a 70 %  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to remove the PMI.   If we do not see some confirmation of evidence within 10 days we will take legal action against The Bank of America. This action will include a charge for reimbursement of our appraisal cost, lost work time and all PMI charges- due to The Bank of Americas  continual  failure to provide any proof or documentation to support their claim, while we are forced to keep paying the PMI.   Please provide the documentation requested on or before  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  or we will take further legal action.   Sincerely,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , CA.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  (  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  )  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  NOTICE : Spoke to  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  who said that The B of A was sending a copy of my original  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  loan documents which should clear up this ongoing PMI issue. I found that these documents said nothing about whe n my PMI could be canceled. This was yet another disappointment from The Bank of America. SoI am going to contact HUD to complain that not only did I not receive the information requested within the required 60 days, I did not receive any confirming evidence of the PMI rules at all ( its been almost 120 days as of today ). I also plan to take legal action for past due PMI payment s for the last 6 months.   Sincerely,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  PS : I am currently at 78 % of the Loan value on my mortgage. The recent appraisal came to {$190000.00}. 78 % of this is {$150000.00}. I show a current debt of {$150000.00}.   Please cancel this PMI on or before  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  when my loan will be under the 78 % requirement.   Sincerely,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I received the ( enclosed document ) from  The Bank of America a week ago covering the Automatic Termination of MI. This document states that when I reach 78 % of the original value of the property which was {$200000.00} or, if you care use the latest appraisal : {$190000.00}, the MI will automatically terminate. My latest statement shows a balance on th e account of {$150000.00} which is 77.9 % of the latest appraised value. Now that it has taken some 5 months since I paid down our mortgage to allow for the removal of the MI, I would ask for the last time Please remove the MI of {$150.00} from my loan costs or it will surely be determined to be  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  by the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Please confirm the receipt of this letter and your removal of the MI by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to avoid legal action.    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'the last letter refers to a page out of our original mortgage. the 78 % of the original value of the property will automatically be dropped. the B of A has');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3336,'05/10/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Attempts to collect debt not owed','I have written  Portfolio Recovery Associates  several letters asking them to verify and to remove a debt that is not mine. In addition, I asked them to provide me with the original contract between myself and the original creditor. In return, PRA asked me to send them additional information to help them verify the debt. It is not my responsibility to help them verify a debt that is n''t mines. PRA does n''t have any of the necessary paper work to prove this is my debt, yet they will not remove it from my credit reports and they are still trying to collect this debt. In fact, they have even threatened to sue me. The debt is less than a {$1000.00} and the PRA is located in different state than me. Thus, the cost to hire an out of state lawyer would be much more than the {$800.00} that they claim I owe. This is clearly a scare tactic and this company is violating the FDCPA in several ways.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,2.0,'portfolio recovery Associates has written several letters asking them to verify and remove a debt that is not mines. in return, PRA asked me to send them additional information to help them verify');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3337,'05/10/2017','Debt collection','Credit card debt','Took or threatened to take negative or legal action','I enrolled with a debt settlement company  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . One of the accounts was a Bank of Ame rica ( BofA ) credit card debt.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  of the other credit cards and debts have been successfully paid off or are still in a repayment program. Payments to BofA w ere initiated  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and followed on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I received a piece of mail from a law firm in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , AR, offering their services for representation regarding a lawsuit filed against me by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  law firm on behalf of BofA. I was unaware of this at the time. My name was also in the Sunday,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , newspaper noting said lawsuit. I contacted my debt settlement company,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , Thursday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  inquiring why I was being sued. They had informed me at that time that  BofA  had already received payments for the debt and would check into this matter. After further communication with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , they informed me they were in process of negotiating a new settlement with  BofA and c ould not explain why I was being sued. I informed  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I would contact  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and attempt to settle this debt without their assistance. I was formally served the lawsuit papers the evening of Tuesday,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  at my home. I contacted  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Wednesday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and spoke with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ( spelling? ) and negotiated a settlement with her that same day. Subsequent papers were sent out which I received the following Tuesday,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I spoke with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  the following day and she informed me the papers I received were null and void and would n''t be honored. She asked me to mail them back to her and then later in the conversation advised me to shred them. I still have these papers in my possession. I then attempted to negotiated a second settlement with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and was advised to call her back if I did not hear from her. I attempted contact again Monday,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , left message and again Friday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  left me a message Monday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and I attempted return call approximatel y 30 min  after and have not had return call from her through end of business day today,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I feel I have been diligent in trying to reconcile this debt and I was unjustly sued by BofA, through  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . L I have spoke with, although have not retained an attorney at this time and have concerns there may be Fair Debt Collection Practices Act violations with this manner. Thank you for your time regarding this manner.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'payments to BofA w ere initiated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. they followed on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3338,'05/10/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','I never do this but my disappointment in USAA is extreme. I have been a member for 20 years. I was an employee for 6 years, and for the life of me I ca n''t understand the way this bank has changed. Today I made a mobile deposit using a money order. Without prior warning before the deposit, my funds were put on hold for a week. I make this same transaction every month to pay my rent but for whatever reason this time my funds have been placed on hold. I was transferred to the executive resolution team and was told they will review for an exception. I was denied this because, I do n''t deposit enough money to get the exception. What kind of treatment is this? I have a direct deposit every  2  weeks, and the solution I was given is to apply for a USAA credit card or borrow the money. Unbelievable USAA. What is the difference between you and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  or  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  or any other big bank that only cares about their profits. Do you even remember what it means to serve? What does  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  stand for USAA. Lesson learned. Sure my rent check will be returned and you will charge a NSF fee as well as whatever fees my landlord is going to charge. Thanks  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','UNITED SERVICES AUTOMOBILE ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a mobile deposit was made using a money order. the bank has changed its operations and has a direct deposit every 2 weeks. the solution is to apply for a USA');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3339,'05/09/2017','Student loan','Private student loan','Dealing with your lender or servicer','Student loan through  Navient was originated ( under   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   ) on   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in the aggregate amount of {$43000.00} with a fixed 6.5 % interest rate. I had financial issues early on and went through periods of forbearance, etc. which I understand would capitalize interest and increase the balance of the loan.     In roughly late  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I was past due, and contact ed (   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   )  the provider at the time. Spoke with a Rep, brought my account to date and was placed on a graduated payment plan which I was pleased with.     I have been paying {$300.00} per mon th (  {$290.00} due ) on time each month since that time. I have recently discovered that my balance is now over {$54000.00}. When I researched my account online I found that no monies were applied to my principal, all to interest, and late fees have been charged each month even though payments were not late. The last time I had payment applied to my principal was  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .     I contacted Navient today and was told that my monthly interest is {$280.00} based on my principal, which has been increasing based on the lack of payment going toward it. The gentleman could not explain the late fees or why my entire $   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    monthly payments were all going to interest rather than the {$280.00} only.     I have attached my entire account history and proof of monthly payment and due date as supporting documentation. I was never informed that my " payment plan '''' would only cover interest. Today I was told that I would need to pay {$470.00} monthly to cover payment on the principal as well.     I would appreciate investigation into this matter. Thank you for your assistance.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'student loan through Navient was originated on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. in roughly late late [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was past');
