INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3360,'05/05/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] it was implied to a District Court Judge, that Bayview Loans Servicing LLC ( Bayview ) had filed suit against me for foreclosure on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Judicial District in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NM. The originator of my loan was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had failed to apply my payments, and returned multiple payments, claiming that I owed unauthorized and illegal fees. In fact, in one instance [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] wrote me and told me that it had charged me fees for both properties when in fact I only owed one ( 1 )  property. To make matters worse, even with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] returning my payments in contravention of the loan contract, I had made thousands of dollars in advance payments to my loan. In other words, after paying thousands of dollars in early payments there is no possible way that my loan could have been in default at the time Bayview now claims it was in default even after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to apply my subsequent payments. This means that either Bayview did not review competent loan information or Bayview ignored the circumstances of my loan prior to filing the unlawful suit against me. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was sued by the Federal Trade Commission for the very conduct it had engaged in regarding my loan. That lawsuit resulted in a Federal Court Order issued by the United States District Court Central District of California onXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] The Federal Court Order in effect until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Restrained and Enjoined [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and its successors and assigns ( allegedly Bayview ) from filing suit against me under the circumstances of my loan. See Exhibit A at Section VI.
Bayview is not a bank as defined by the Federal Court Order. See, Exhibit A at Definitions 3. Bayview has violated a Federal Court Order by filing a lawsuit against me after the Court had restrained and enjoined it from doing so.
Here, Bayview either failed to review competent and reliable evidence regarding the circumstances of my loan or ignored that evidence which clearly demonstrates that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to apply my payments and ignored my written dispute regarding its failure. In further violation of the Court Order, Bayview failed to resolve or even address the dispute with my loan which included numerous written notices beginning on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and concluded with a written notice of Breach and Termination dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Bayview continues to ignore this dispute in order to unlawfully pursue the foreclosure case against me in violation of the Federal Court Order which explicitly prohibits in from filing suit under the circumstances of my loan.
Bayview has falsely represented to the district Court in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that there was no dispute. To the contrary, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was provided a Notice of Breach and Termination of the loan contracts dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], as a result of the dispute that Bayview now falsely claims did not exist. See Exhibit B. A brief investigation into this matter will quickly reveal that there has been an ongoing dispute regarding the failure to apply my loan payments sinceXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was also charging me illegal and unauthorized fees ( charging me fees for both properties when I only owned one property ). It was that very conduct that resulted in the lawsuit by the FTC and subsequent Federal Court Order which Bayview has violated. Exhibit A. For example, after sending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] three ( 3 ) checks on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( see Exhibit C ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] first said the checks were missing. See Exhibit D. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] later returned those payments falsely claiming that certified funds were required. In a letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] however, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] admitted that the payments did not require certified funds stating, This will confirm that although your account was past due for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] andXX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] installments at the time ; your loan had not been referred to our Foreclosure Department and ; as such did not require certified funds. See, Exhibit E at p.2, bullet point 4. When asked to explain why the checks were returned, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to respond. See, Exhibit D. Here [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to accept and apply my payments claiming the payments required certified funds, then later admitted in writing that the payments did not require certified funds. Exhibit E at p.2, bullet point 4. As a result of failing to resolve this and other issues, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was issued the Notice of Breach and Termination of the loan contracts on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Under these and other circumstances, Bayview is in violation of the FTC / Federal Court Order ( Exhibit A ) by filing and maintaining a foreclosure suit against me particularly as it has misrepresented to the District Court that I failed to make these payments when such a statement is clearly false. The misrepresentations are also a violation of Federal consumer financial protection laws. Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','BAYVIEW LOAN SERVICING, LLC',2.0,4.0,'a district court judge implied that Bayview Loans Servicing LLC had filed suit against me for foreclosure on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3361,'05/05/2017','Debt collection','Other debt','Written notification about debt','CAINE & WEINER COMPANY INC,  i was contacted by this company about a debt i was presumed to owe   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   (  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  $  ).  I asked kindly for them to forward something in writing. they stated they already had and would not do so again. I tried to explain i had no record and that possibly i had misplaced what had been claimed to be sent. still no luck, then i tried to further explain that with all the robots and scam collection efforts in this country that i really needed this confirmation, I received no less than  4  calls from the same collections person presumably in California, same thing each time, they did insist i contact progressive, I asked if they were the ones servicing the debt? answer yes, again asked them to confirm by mail and assured them we could do something about the debt than all would be happy, still no luck they were unwilling and somewhat inconsiderate and unhelpful in the collections attempt, also disputed was the amount, they would have no part of this, ultimately  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  did contact me about an error in the amount (  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  $  )! !! but by this time the debt had been reported to the credits agencies b y Caine & Weiner.  it would seem unfair if not illegal for a company or person be able to report a debt for collections if they are unwilling or unable to service a debt','CAINE & WEINER COMPANY, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a debt i was presumed to owe was reported to the credit agencies b y Caine & Weiner. a company or person could report a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3362,'05/05/2017','Checking or savings account','Checking account','Managing an account','What a nightmare situation. On the last week of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I accepted a subscription for {$120000.00}. Paperwork prepared by our company attorney. I received a series of personal checks from the investor from different accounts equaling the {$120000.00}. On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I made the deposit at a branch TCF bank. Prior to the deposit I had a positive balance, money that cleared a year ago, in the thousands. On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  my account had been put in the negative the {$120000.00} plus my available balance. I called and spoke to a rep who was very helpful in explaining this was not normal and that my original balance would be made available again the morning of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and the deposit of {$120000.00} should be available the morning of Friday the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  the deposit of {$120000.00} was not made available so I called to see what the status was. I was told by a rep that I would need to ask my investor to get verification of the checks from his banks in order to release the funds. Meanwhile TCF had already contacted the issuer themselves to verify he had issued the checks. My investor stated he did issue the checks and those funds had already been taken out of his account on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I received a letter from TCF stating it had the deposit of {$120000.00}, they released {$5000.00} of it and the rest would be made available on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . On Saturday the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I noticed the deposit and my original balance had been released. Keep in mind I own an upstart and these funds were what we needed to green light our project. Ive been working on my company for over 750 days to get to this point. In the morning of Monday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I gave my vendors the go ahead to move forward. At around  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  pm Monday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I check my balance to find out TCF put a hold on my entire balance again, the {$120000.00} deposit along with my already cleared funds. I called TCF only to get a run around and the only information anyone would give me was it was In Review On Wednesday  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I went to a branch location to see if I could get some help figuring out whats going on. I met with the  Assistant Manager  of that branch and she was trying to be very helpful. I explained the situation and she confirmed something wasnt right. She made a phone call and was told the account was In  Review  and that it would all clear by  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . She had no clue why the bank would hold funds already cleared so she recommended she talk to he r manager and see if they could release some of those funds. I stated I didnt need the funds as much as I needed to get the situation resolved. She went and spoke to her manager and her manager came to speak to me. The manager  of that branch was cold, calculated and lacked the empathy one would expect given the situation. Kept giving me the standard  theres nothing we can do and I understand your frustration She then contradicted the information given to the assistant manager and s aid they didnt know when the account would clear and that is was In Review On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  I visited the same location to drop of bank statements given to me by my investor showing all of the funds had been released to TCF on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . I spoke to the same assistant  manager and she faxed and called to check the status. She said all she can tell me was the account is In Review Since then I cant get any answers and my attorney has sent a letter via email and mail. We still cant get any answers and today is 22 days since the deposit. I get TCF has The Right but does having the Right make this right? How is it I get no answers, no correspondence and no path to resolution? Now, Ive green lighted my projects, vendors are getting antsy and my credibility is on the line all because TCF doesnt extend a professional courtesy. Also, I started this account over a year ago with a deposit of several personal checks equally {$64000.00} and that was cleared within two bu siness days. To date,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   no one from  TCF has attempted to contact me given this situation and our company attorney has attempted to make contact with TCF ''s  Lead counsel with no avail.  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  has made no attempt to help resolve this issue or has offered any explanation.','TCF NATIONAL BANK',2.0,2.0,'on the last week of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I accepted a subscription for $120000.00. on [COMPTE_ANON');
