INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3382,'05/02/2017','Credit reporting, credit repair services, or other personal consumer reports','Credit reporting','Incorrect information on your report','I have  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  accounts reporting on my Experian,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  reports. One ends in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and the other ends in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . Over the past year, I have disputed the validity of these accounts multiple times. These disputes should be available in your database. Each time I ''d submit the dispute, I received some silly letter from  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  saying, " We received your dispute, but most of the time when we receive disputes, they ''re either the result of an error or other mistake, so we are n''t taking your dispute seriously. '''' Finally in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , I was able to get  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to investigate the accounts.     FCRA states that when an account is in dispute, the lender  MAY  NOT report the account as delinquent or demand that the amount owed be paid until the lender completes its investigation into the matter. If the lender determines the balance owed to be legitimately owed, the lender must give the customer sufficient time -- usually 30 days -- to make payment on the amount owed. Even though I disputed these accounts countless times,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  continued to report them as delinquent. When  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  received my dispute and actually paid attention to it, they still continued to report my accounts as delinquent despite the fact that the entire amount owed was in dispute. On account  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  reported a 30 day delinquency in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , and 60 days delinquent in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , 90 days delinquent in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and then 30 days delinquent in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . On account  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  reported a 30 day delinquency in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  -- again, the time of the dispute. These were the times I was disputing this account with  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] . As soon as  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  informed me of the legitimacy of the account/charges, I promptly paid the account.     I have contacted  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  about this, explained that they were not to have reported my accounts as delinquent while they were in dispute, but they refuse to make the correction to my credit report. By refusing to correct this,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  is violating the provisions of the FCRA. My final recourse is to ask  Experian ,   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   and  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to make these corrections.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'accounts reported on my experian, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts. the dispute is a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3383,'05/02/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Attempts to collect debt not owed','ERC collections (  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ) has been calling me multiple times a day for months. If I answer it goes to an automated system that tells me to press numbers for making a payment, removing my number from the list, or speaking to a representative. Not once does it state what the debt is or who they are trying to contact.     For a while, I would select the option to remove my number from the list, but they would continue to call. I few times I decided to speak to a representative. Each time they would tell me that they do n''t see my name or phone number   in their system. They would tell me they do n''t know why I ''m getting called and would say they ca n''t remove me from the list because I ''m not on one.
The calls continued. I got so frustrated by them that I changed my phone number yesterday. Today, less than 24 hours later, ERC managed to call me on my brand new number.
This has to be illegal. I ''m at my   wits end and I need these calls to stop.','ERC',2.0,2.0,'a number of calls a day has been called by ERC collections. the system tells me to press numbers for making a payment, removing my number from the list ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3384,'05/01/2017','Mortgage','Conventional home mortgage','Trouble during payment process','On  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ceased servicing our loan and sold those rights t o Select Portfolio  Servicing. We disputed  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  ''s handling of the servicing and the late fees they had alleged were due and this dispute was ignored.     Then, during the transfer from  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  to  Select, Select did  not pay our Real estate taxes on time in  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   School District verifie d the receipt of the late payment penalty check #  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in the amount of {$290.00} prepared on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  from  Select Portfolio ( see attached ). (  This tax payment should have been made by the discount date as wel l ). Th is failure to pay our real estate taxes timely and had we not caught Select ''s error, our home was placed in jeopardy of being sold at sheriff sale by them. Upon learning of the error we filed verbal and written complaints with Select that were initially ignored, acknowledged on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  &  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  and eventually dismissed. They forwarded to the real estate taxing authorities amounts that were greater than the discounted amount and the face value. They have not refunded those penalties and interest to us. They had us absorb and pay amounts that we were not legally required to pay. This higher payment disbursement amount and their failure to fix what had been done was the direct cause of financial hardship for us.  Select Portfolio  then increased our escrow account monthly payment to approximately {$660.00} an increase that was calculated incorrectly and caused an even greater financial hardship.     These errors and increases resulted in threats to foreclose on our principal residence.     After getting no reasonable response to the above issues, we prepared and submitted a request for mortgage assistance and that was not handled properly. We provided Select with all of the information they requested timely. We have been paying 5.125 % interest on our loan when we should have been approved for a reduction to below 4 %. This would have resulted in a savings of at least $ 200 /mos.      Their use of foreign call centers has contributed to this company ''s failures as well.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Select Portfolio ceased servicing our loan and sold those rights. Select disputed the handling of the servicing and late fees they had alleged were due. the school district verified');
