INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3455,'04/17/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Delinquent account','My creditor is using abusive collection tactics. I told them I am in the process of filing a bankruptcy as recommended by a consumer credit counseling agency. The company then tried to demand payments and told me they would potentially refer me to their attorney for further collections. The lady I spoke to was very rude and very much not understanding of the situation. She made several threatening and intimidating statements during the call including that calls would possibly even continue while I am in bankruptcy and that they may conduct a review of my income and assets for dealing with further collection of this {$800.00} debt. I informed this person I barely had enough money to pay for my food and prescriptions and that my income had been greatly reduced. She kept pressuring me to make a payment. I told her my bankruptcy would be filed in the next two days and I did not have money and she just kept pressuring me to pay her. She really frightened me to the point where I was afraid she was going to keep calling during a time when she should n''t.','Alliance Data Card Services',2.0,2.0,'creditor is using abusive collection tactics. she told me that she is in the process of filing a bankruptcy. she made several threatening and intimidating statements during the call.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3456,'04/17/2017','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Making/receiving payments, sending money','JP Morgan Chase Bank   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  for their Clients Good afternoon to all that are receiving this email.  Below is a horr ifying story I shared with family &amp; friends last night on  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  &amp; other sources of media. Just a side note, I ''ve already gone to my local news about how  JP Morgan  Chase Bank does not protect their clients like they claim to. An  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  call me a couple of days ago saying she ''ll look into it &amp; do all she can to help me out &amp; recover my funds,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  days later she calls saying Chase will not help out &amp; I can file a complaint on the ftc.gov website. I ''m at a loss of a decent amount of money due to Chase Bank. The representative put me on the back burner for  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  days, show  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  empathy of my situation &amp; then calls me  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  days later, beats around the bush &amp; then finally says  Chase  is n''t helping out. My decision to proceed with this transaction was based upon the assurance from a Chase  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  rep repeating numerous times " everything is good, they check out, they ''re a LEGIT dealership '''' his exact words stated a few times.    [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] /  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   my local news company is running a report of my interview about how poorly I ''ve been treated &amp; how  JP Morgan Chase Bank is just sitting in their multi-million/billion dollar office telling me tha t I ''m  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] .   I keep getting the run around from your institution, no one is comprehending a word I ''ve been saying, I the associates keep talking about things that are n''t even relevant to my nightmare I ''m going with. I ''m besides myself right now on what to do, I keep hitting a dead end after another. I need for someone to read my story below &amp; take me serious &amp; who actually cares about customer service &amp; will go the extra mile for their client . JP Morgan Chase Bank Co. i s a huge financial institution &amp; I ''ve been a client of theirs for well over  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  years, so it would be nice to be given professional business respect &amp; due your part into looking into things &amp; having my best interest.   I ''d greatly appreciate some sort of contact/response back via email &amp; or call back. Please restore my faith with this institution by showing me that someone with any kind of say so &amp; can make things happen without continuing to keep passing me off &amp; making me someone else ''s problem.   ATTENTION FB FAMILY, PLEASE READ ...  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]    What I ''m about to share with you all really really pains me &amp; want everyone to be careful &amp; do your research before making purchases online.   I ''ve recently fallen victim to an online scam with a auto dealership in Alliance, OH which I had found through the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  website. The beautiful truck I had posted last week sharing with everyone what my new truck/baby looks like ended up being a huge scam &amp; was completely unaware of such a thing until I had wired them a $  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  deposit.   My auto loan was/is with Chase Bank or  JP Morgan Chase Bank whatever they go by. After I was approved for my auto loan, a few a ssociates with the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  supposedly checked to verify the legitimacy of  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  Auto Sales which entailed of them checking their website, business license, &amp; dealers resale license. They all said everything was good,  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  associate went as far as saying numerous times to me that everything looks good, they check out, &amp; they ''re legit. After sending them my  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  &amp; then not getting the rest of the documents that my bank was needing to cut them a check for the remaining balance, they were n''t retuning my calls or emails, I contacted the  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  in Ohio &amp; the woman I spoke with conducted a background check on them while I was on the phone &amp; found out that they ''re in fact not a legit dealership, they ''ve operated under many different business names, she then contacted a friend friend of hers from the Attorney  [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]   [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]  we found out that this group up scammers have been doing this for quite sometime &amp; are currently under investigation with the FBI along with my case now.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a rep says he''s ''at a loss of a decent amount of money'' he says he''s ''not helping out'' a rep says');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3457,'04/17/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','This pertains to Case number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Today, I have called Ocwen to find out why the modification process was not updated yet. I was instructed that they were still missing one last document. I explained to the lady that we sent all the paperwork but would be happy to send it again. We got into this mess because back in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we paid the {$5200.00} that was due to reinstate the loan back on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] via wire from our bank. I called for days and monitored the account but no funds from the wire ever showed posted. It was explained to me today that their records show they did not receive payment until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that is why they did not honor the reinstatement of the {$5200.00} and put us into foreclosure, not returning our funds until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Ocwen ''s bank is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( we all know about them ) who clearly told me they can take up to 3 days to post a wire! How criminal is that? I also talk to another agent at Ocwen who said it was sent back because there were foreclosure fees from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that were never paid and they are due and have to be paid. Even thought I told him what their own letter said, he stated that form is n''t really for our loan. We have an FHA loan. So neither person could really tell me the truth. So now we are in foreclosure with new fees being added to the account. We applied for a modification to stop the foreclosure process and today I was checking on the status. The young lady did tell me we could pay the {$9900.00} that is now due to reinstate the loan ( you ca n''t pay your monthly payments while in foreclosure and late fees keep adding up plus new fees ). She stated there are new foreclosure fees that are being added but those will be added to the end of the loan and not necessary to reinstate. I explained to her that is why we are in the mess we are because Ocwen said we have to pay the original foreclosure fees and the {$5200.00} did not satisfy the total amount due despite what their letter said. She said, no, it was denied because it did not have XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment in it because we did n''t get it until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. So why did [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who is the bank for Ocwen keep the money for 3 days? And now I am in foreclosure but she assured me I can send the {$9900.00} to reinstate and they wo n''t need the foreclosure fees of {$2000.00} up front, just at the end of the loan. Looks like [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ca n''t open bogus accounts with lines of credit so maybe they are taking the wires and using those as cash for federal reserve money for points? Interesting .... And Ocwen ca n''t tell me the truth about the letters they send to their customers ....','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a new fee is being added to the account. the new fees are being added to the account. the new fees are not necessary to reinstate the loan.');
