INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3542,'03/28/2017','Debt collection','Credit card','Communication tactics','I scheduled a payment for {$100.00} on my CC ending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with Key Bank Collections Dept on XX/XX/2017 to bring up the account to current status. soon after that, I got two letters from Key Bank with dates XX/XX/2017 and XX/XX/2017 as a reminder confirming the transaction to be processed XX/XX/2017 with a confirm # given. 

Today, XX/XX/2017, I find that the transaction was correctly processed yesterday and posted today in my checking account from where I agreed the payment be withdrawn. 
Key Bank Collections Dept clearly states " PROCESSING MAY TAKE UP TO TWO BUSINESS DAYS ''''. 

MY COMPLAIN IS that I have been harrassed and abussed by Key Bank Collections dept as they have called me AGAIN today XX/XX/2017 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) in order to collect the very same amount of {$100.00} that I previously scheduled and FULLY payed yesterday. that is wrong!! and it is totally unfair business. 
It DID NOT matter that I fully met my commitment, but KEYBANK still call me again???, why? I want an explanation for that WRONG AND ABUSIVE COMMUNICATION APPROACH. 
I spoke with call center supervisor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ID # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] were call was originated, but she blames the system as they schedule payments but dont care to wait 48 hrs to call again in case the payment was not made. 
I am convinced that the Bank ''s collection Dept has this dark and fraudulent strategy to attempt DOUBLING the payment and cash extra from those oblivious clients that may have forgotten at the time of the call that such payment has already been collected. Key Bank Collections Dept. shall have their automated calling system set up to wait 2 business day to call again in the event the scheduled payment did not go through. 

Besides I am feeeling harrased and abused by the Bank, I am feeling completely vulnerable, since I could have forgotten the payment I scheduled 2 weeks in advance and I could have fell in their fraudulent trap to collect a double payment the very same day, That puts me at the risk as a consumer that I may accept to pay in order to avoid more late fees, but I fall in to being short on funds in my acount and being double punished for insufficient funds by my Checking Account bank and by the Key Bank Credit card collections dept. 

I greatly appreciate your valuable help in processing and following on my complain as I am sure that I am not the only victim of such wrong strategy this and other the banks and Credit card companies are creating as a trap to consumers. 

I will be looking forward on your response and for the next step as I have proof documentation of my claim. I will be happy to provided it, along with my personal info. 

Thank you.','KEYCORP',2.0,4.0,'a CC ending with a payment for $100.00 was scheduled for XX/XX/2017. today, XX/XX/2017, I');
