INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3654,'03/01/2017','Mortgage','VA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I submitted a complaint ( Case number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) on the CFPB website, regarding illegal business practices at The Money Source ( TMS ) and their theft of monies from my escrow account. At that time, I was led by both the CFPB and TMS to believe this problem was resolved. It has been 14 months and this problem HAS NOT BEEN RESOLVED. 

As [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], State of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Judicial Branch ), of TMS, admitted at that time, the DUPLICATE monies TMS stole from my spouse and me were eventually returned to the proper account only for TMS to steal the same monies a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] time ( 14 months later ). My spouse and I realized this when we recently attempted to file our annual income taxes with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Internal Revenue Service ( IRS ). According to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] office ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), I paid {$2800.00} in property taxes for the entire year of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However, TMS claims I only paid {$100.00}. 

When I brought to TMS ''s attention the gross error they made in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( paying property taxes to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] twice in one calendar year ), the County immediately refunded TMS the overdue amount. Unfortunately, upon receiving this refund TMS wrongfully placed this money into our account as a " credit '''' instead of giving it to the rightful party ( THEMSELVES ). Because of TMS ''s gross oversight, TMS now claims we paid {$100.00} in property taxes for the calendar year of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], even though the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Tax Assessor ''s Office clearly received our payment of {$2800.00}. How can TMS use monies from our escrow account to pay county property taxes only for TMS to state we paid no property taxes? This is a clear and obvious violation of RESPA, and the Rules of Professional Conduct. 

I called TMS to inquire about this discrepancy on Friday ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), and was told there was a " credit '''' ( of {$2800.00} ) to my escrow account, which precipitated the discrepancy. However, upon further examination, the " credit '''' is actually the DUPLICATE ( stolen ) money that was returned to TMS in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

THERE WAS NO " credit! '''' The returned DUPLICATE ( stolen ) money, which [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] acknowledged in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], SHOULD NOT and DOES NOT change the amount of property taxes we paid to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( {$2800.00} ) for XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However, TMS returned the stolen DUPLICATE money from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( {$2800.00} ), and illegally applied this to our escrow account, wrongfully reducing our IRS paperwork for taxes paid in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to {$100.00}. 

Any imbecile at TMS should realize the repeated error in their ways, as well as the shockingly illegal behavior they continue to impose on paying customers. Again, when I called TMS on Friday ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), I was given the same poor customer service excuse as I received in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was told to " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] it up & deal with it. '''' Presently, my spouse and I CAN NOT file our State/Federal annual income taxes until this discrepancy, from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is FINALLY RESOLVED. Please help us communicate with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to, once again, return our stolen money and cease and desist with obvious violation of RESPA, and the Rules of Professional Conduct. We continue to be illegally denied our right to file State and Federal income taxes due to TMS ''s violations. Thank you in advance.','MONEY SOURCE, THE',2.0,4.0,'a complaint was filed on the CFPB website. the CFPB and TMS have been led to believe this problem was resolved. the monies tMS stole from');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3655,'02/28/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Unable to get credit report/credit score','I became aware someone stole my identity and was opening credit cards I did n''t apply for in my name. I called Transunion and placed a fraud alert on my credit file. I then tried to obtain a copy of my credit report from Transunion ( through the " www.annualcreditreport.com '''' website ). Transunion has blocked or " masked, '''' as they say, my social security number, and will not allow me to access my credit report. After numerous hours on the phone with Transunion phone reps, they acknowledge the problem but Transunion refuses to correct it despite my numerous requests. As I have explained to them, I need to check the credit report to make sure there is no other unauthorized activity. All the Transunion reps have done is transfer me back and forth among three numbers ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) but none of them have helped me access my credit report or provided a solution to Transunion ''s acknowledge problem. I am out of options with Transunion. Maybe the FTC can get them to do something before my credit is ruined? Maybe they ''ll listen to the federal government, they sure do n''t give a darn about consumers. Thanks for any help you can provide.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'a fraud alert was placed on my credit file. a fraud alert was placed on my credit file. the reps have blocked or "masked, '''' as they');
