INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3663,'02/27/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I have a student loan with Navient. I had some [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans in XX/XX/2010 which Navient took over. I consolidated the loans to help with lower payments. Navient said that one loan was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but it was a private loan. and I could not consolidate it. It is in the amount of {$19000.00}. plus. I offered a down payment of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if they could make the payment at {$100.00} a month. 
They want [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] down payment. I am supporting my Grandmother who has been ill and out of work. The house went into foreclosure and I had to help save our home. I am just starting a full time job but I need some time to get caught up. I ca n''t take out another loan as I ca n''t afford another payment. Navient is threatening garnishment of my wages which I ca n''t afford. They have hard to deal with always. They did n''t tell me the other loans had been paid off when they were and they have n''t explained what this private loan ( which is a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan ) is and they have locked me out of any internet interaction with them..','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a student loan with Navient was taken over by the XX/XX/2010. I offered a down payment of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3664,'02/27/2017','Debt collection','Credit card','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','On or about the last week in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to pay my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank collections in full. They referred me to the Law Offices of Mary Jane Elliott. I called the law offices to obtain the payoff balance which was {$600.00} and made arrangements to pay it in full by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On Friday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called the law offices of Mary Jane Elliott and made a phone payment in full via my checking account in the amount of {$600.00}. The deb collector on the phone told me that a lawsuit had been filed, however, I had not been notified or served and she stated that the lawsuit would be dismissed and I would receiving a paid in full letter and also documentation that the lawsuit would be dismissed and removed from public record. 

Throughout the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have been receiving daily robo calls from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] attempting to collect on this paid in full debt. 

Yesterday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I pulled my credit report. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is still reporting this debt as outstanding with a {$55.00} balance, even though it was paid in full on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Today [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I called the Law Offices of Mary Jane Elliott, and was told that my account was paid in full. However, they have not dismissed the lawsuit and the rep on the phone refused to give me a time frame in which they would dismiss it. She said they would not vacate the judgement. She also said her office would not be sending a paid in full letter. 

I am reaching out for help because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been in trouble with government and CFPB before for unfair debt collections practices. This is a debt that was paid in full that they are still attempting to collect on, which is negatively impacting my credit. 

Both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Law Offices of Mary Jane Elliott ( which is just a shell company for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), need to be held fully accountable.','Mary Jane M. Elliott, P.C. Attorneys At Law',2.0,2.0,'a deb collector said a lawsuit had been filed. she said the lawsuit would be dismissed and removed from public record. the deb collector said the lawsuit would be dismissed ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3665,'02/26/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Late fee','Current customer of American Express for over 7 years. Continuously spend over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] $ monthly, and pay my bills on time. The last few months, something has been happening with my bank, that my payments are a day or two late. I called customer service, asked to speak to supervisor to see if the fees could be credited as a courtesy for being a long-time customer. The first supervisor hung up on me, and when i called back and asked for supervisor, the second supervisor did not even review my account, but told me that he will not credit anything, as people who spend more money than me dont even get credited. He was rude, and not customer oriented, and did n''t give my account the time and review I requested.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'customer service customer hung up on me, and asked for supervisor. he did not even review my account, but said he will not credit anything.');
