INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3667,'02/25/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','Bank or America made an error. On XX/XX/2017 I was to receive a deposit from the VA. It showed as a deposit alright however, it had a negative sign attached to it. Which left my account negative and over drawn. I called and was told that the deposit shows as negative because it had n''t posted yet. Well, the next day it still had n''t changed and this time it read " error. '''' I called and was told that they would have it corrected within 15 days. On XX/XX/2017 my other deposit from the BA hit as a positive leaving my account with less than five dollars. I kept in touch with the bank and talked to a handful of people including a bank manager. I am still waiting for them to fix the issue. In the meantime I have gone back to paper checks which take longer and I am going to have to cash them a different way because I do n''t trust Bank of America. I went to the bank yesterday and they said that the VA has to basically release the funds all over again and that is what they are waiting on. Once that is fixed they have to submit a ticket for the next check and the overdraft fees. I was not given another time line for that. I lost my home and have had to move into a friend ''s house because the Bank owes me over 3,000 dollars.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2017 deposit from the bank hit as a positive leaving my account with less than five dollars. the next day it hadn''t changed and this time');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3668,'02/25/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','I contacted Equifax after receiving documentation from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that they have removed their listing from my credit file after their investigation. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] listing has been removed from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Equifax is the only credit bureau reporting the old [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] listing. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is the owner of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Account. I contacted Equifax and advised them of this and provided documentation and requested that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account be removed from my credit file. When [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold the account, they sold their rights to the account. Previously, they updated the date reported on the account after a previous dispute. The date reported is not what is disputed and when the company sold the account they sold their rights to update it. I then spoke with the Fraud department and spoke to supervisors who requested me to fax in the documentation and that they would remove the account upon receipt. They did remove [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but they have not removed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was advised that I needed to get a letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advising that they sold the account to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they sent me one via fax. I have also sent the affidavit that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] used to remove their listing. This account is too old.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'Equifax is the only credit bureau reporting the old [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] listing. when [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sold the account');
