INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3693,'02/19/2017','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Deposits and withdrawals','I have an Equity line of credit with US Bank. The total of the loan was {$55000.00}. I unfortunately was scammed by a guy I met on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He told me his name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He suckered me into giving him my Equity Line of credit information. He paid it off and then all of a sudden it was back up to the max. I received a letter from the bank asking me if I wanted to raise my limit and never sent the letter back. Yes it was my fault that I gave this scammer my info but I never gave the bank the authorization to raise my line of credit. I was a victim of a scam. I did n''t find out about this until I got a call from someone at the bank telling me I owed over {$84000.00}. If they can call me and tell me that I owed that much then why did n''t they call me to ask me if I wanted my equity line of credit raised? This is very scary for me because I can not afford to pay back {$84000.00}. I will pay the {$55000.00} because that is what my husband and I agreed to when we first took the loan out. My husband passed away on XX/XX/2008. I am living on social security and working a part time job just to make ends meet. Please if you can help me I would appreciate it so much. I have spoken to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the Fraud dept at US bank phone # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and email is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he told me because I gave this scammer my info I am responsible for the total amount. I do n''t feel like I should have to pay the extra money. The bank has my phone number and could have called me to see if I wanted to raise my equity line. They sure called me when the equity line got up to {$84000.00} but did not call me to verify that I wanted it to go over!!! I need help PLEASE!!','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,4.0,'a guy who met me on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me his name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and paid it off ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3694,'02/18/2017','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','My mortgage was sold in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to Specialized Loan Servicing LLC ( SLS ). I contacted SLS regarding an application for a loan modification due to some unforeseen circumstances that had happened regarding my home. They mailed me out an application and I also printed one from their online website. I contacted them regarding how I should return the application. The lady said I could mail it to the address on the application, email it to the address on the application, or fax it to the number on the application. Since I had pictures to attach to the application I decided it would be best just to send it via email. The email address they gave was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Every time I sent an email I got a confirmation email back saying my documents were received and waiting to be processed. Starting on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I started receiving calls from SLS ''s main number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the caller identified herself on my voice mail as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with the underwriting department at Specialized Loan Servicing. After a few days of phone tag, we were finally able to touch base. I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and she was wanting to discuss my modification approval for a HAMP modification. She also said the paperwork had been mailed out but since I had n''t gotten it she would email it to me and that I would n''t be able to open the email without a code and the code would be my social security number. She said this was for my protection. I received the paperwork and looked it over. The loan number on the paperwork was mine, the amounts added up, the phone numbers were to SLS so everything seemed legit especially since the only people who have my loan number were me and SLS. Remember loan numbers are NOT public information. I signed the document and sent it back to SLS ''s email at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and got a confirmation email back saying it was received and being processed. I also made 2 payments towards my trial period payments totaling {$1200.00}. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a call from SLS touching base to see how things were going and to let me know they were missing some documents to finish up a loan modification. I told him I always spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], he said that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] worked out of their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] office and it was only by chance that I always got her. I explained I had already signed a modification agreement with them that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had sent me and made 2 of my three trial period payments. He looked at the agreement ( 6 days after they received it ) and told me it was n''t something they had sent me. Then tells me the numbers on the agreement were n''t to SLS he said that the number for where my loan was at was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Obviously, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did n''t have very good [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because that is the exact number that was on my papers. I have made a report with my local sheriff ''s office, the white collar crimes division of the FBI, and the fraud department with HAMP.','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,4.0,'my mortgage was sold in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to specialized loan');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3695,'02/18/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle lease','Managing the loan or lease','I had a car loan with Santander Consumer for almost 3 years. When I decided to switch for a lease, the loan balance was paid off but there is not an option in their website to stop the automatic monthly payments drawing from my checking account. I should ''ve called them earlier but did n''t do it and they drafted one more monthly amount of {$320.00} and when I called them they told me a prepaid visa card will be mailed with that amount and that I have to wait a month. I spend several minutes arguing with the guy in customer service asking for a check because I just need the cash and finally they told me that they will do it. The guy told me that he started a process to substitute the prepaid visa for a check. 
A week after another person called me telling me that is impossible to send a check but I will be able to get cash from that prepaid card. So he asked me if I agree with that and I say yes. When I received the prepaid card the instructions said very clear that THIS CARD DOES NOT HAVE ATM CASH ACCESS So beside the incredible high interest I was paying with that loan ( I decided to lease a car so I get rid of that loan ) they want to keep my money for longer time and keep earning fees every time I use this prepaid card in every business I will buy from. I do not need this prepaid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card. I just need my money back in cash.','SANTANDER CONSUMER USA HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,2.0,'a car loan was drafted by the company and the loan balance was paid off. the loan balance was paid off but there is not an option in their website to stop the automatic monthly');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3696,'02/18/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Managing the loan or lease','I have a car loan with West Financial and I have been asking that money paid over the loan amount be paid on the principle. For months they have been telling me ok, but I noticed the next month ''s payment was lower. I did not take the bait but the online service would say I owed the full [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment but the statement says I owe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( i.e. ). However I was told a couple of days ago that they do not apply extra payment amounts to the principle. Is this legal. I live in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the finance company is in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- WestlakeFinancial. 
The interest rate is almost 25 %.','Westlake Services, LLC',2.0,2.0,'west financial has been asking that money paid over loan amount be paid on the principle. the online service would say I owed the full [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3697,'02/17/2017','Mortgage','Other mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','This is the second complaint lodged against Ditech from us. The first is Case number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], was named administrator of my father ''s estate. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I reached out to Ditech again. I spoke with a rep named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at Ditech. I told him that we would like to come to an arrangement on the loan since my father has passed. My mother would like to resolve the loan issue, since she has been staying at the home for almost 30 years. I also told him that because I am unfamiliar with mortgages, that I will have someone else speak on behalf of the mortgage since my father left quite a jigsaw puzzle of an estate that I am still trying to figure out. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advised to me to send a written notification that has the name and number of our representative to him and then that will authorize my representative to discuss the mortgage with Ditech. Our family representative is named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he is my uncle and my mothers brother. I sent the letter, as requested, and Ditech has been speaking with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the phone. However, Ditech, suddenly has no recollection of this and had the nerve to accuse me of Fraud on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ... 
At some point in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], our new representative at Ditech was a man named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He helped us figure out our options and we decided to pursue a Loan modification. We sent in the documentation in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we tried to call to inquire about a settlement to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and turns out he was fired. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we got repeated notifications in the mail saying our representative was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and now another person. We feel like we are being strung along and not being given someone who can consistently work with us making it hard to find a resolution. 
So, we now have a THIRD representative we have to deal with, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] seems to have no idea of what was discussed with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], effectively making it as if we are starting from zero in regards to the Loan, when in essence, we have been VERY consistent and earnest in our communication with Ditech, sending many faxes, and calling dozens of times to all the aforementioned people. All faxes and dates can be provided at your request. 
So we tell [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that although we are pursuing loan modification, we would like to reach a settlement arrangement. At Ditechs request, I wrote a settlement offer and sent it in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We believe the settlement offer was a VERY reasonable and showed that we were earnest in our desire to end the matter. My father received the loan in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$350000.00}, and he has already paid {$370000.00} ( est ), at the time of his death. We offered {$140000.00} to settle the remaining {$180000.00} left on the mortgage. We feel this is VERY reasonable. 
Once we turned in the settlement offer in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we have heard nothing formal from Ditech. Instead, we hear from some law firm office issuing us a Notice of Intent to Foreclose, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Our home is now being fast-tracked for foreclosure. Our loan modification request is currently being ignored. Again, we are alarmed as to why this sudden notice was given. Considering how much we are working towards finding a solution. 
We received a note on the door from Ditech, asking us to call to schedule a meeting in the week of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( I was not home, So I do not know what day it came exactly ). I make the call on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to schedule a meeting. I speak with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she says she does not know of any request for a meeting. So we believe that there is something fraudulent happening because the things being said, and being written are not the same. We are at a loss on what to do and whom to speak with because we do not feel that they can be trusted at this rate. Nor does she have info regarding the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who is also authorized to speak on the loan. Accusing me of fraud of on the phone. Needless to say I am at a loss on how to best proce','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,4.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was named administrator of my father''s estate. in [COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3698,'02/17/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','I have account with US Bank and the issue or concerns I have are fees for over draft, extended fees ( check account ) and charges to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of my credit cards that I have not authorized to be an over draft for my checking account. Over the past 24 months, I have paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars in Overdraft fees. They refused to pay my regular bills and reorder my account transaction to hide what there doing. I have request a in chronological accounting of my bank transaction and they will not provide it. For at least two year my bank deposits of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars in that account and they missed managed every transaction. They hey items for pay for excess of 3 days or more and re-ordered when transaction to cover up and released money held pending for payment back in to the account. also, have countless over draft fees place on my credit card ending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I did not have agreement. I spoke to a bank rep a few days about it and still not attempt was make to follow up or correct the matter either. I need so help getting the matter corrected. Its just criminal what they are doing and it cost me a significant amount of money.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'over draft fees and extended fees are charges to my credit card. the issue or concerns I have are fees for over draft fees. they refused to pay my regular bills and reorder');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3699,'02/17/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Taking out the loan or lease','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I went to a so called friend who has a dealership cause i was in need of a car. They used a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as the car to see if i would be able to get financed.The car was not even on the lot and i never seen it. They told me they were just using it to see if it would go through that i could change cars once approved. I was approved and next day they said to come back. They had car there and I didnt want it, they said finance co.wont change to pay for 6 months and i can come back and exchange.I did and then they wanted more.I couldnt do that, i just gave they [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].I was mad and upset they lied and was stuck with this car but i paid on it 2 yrs.It was way overpriced!!! [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] car? I still owed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and i just could do it anymore so I did a volunteer repo. I notified co several times to get car.My landlord had car towed off property.I notified finance co letting them know where car was, the tow company notified them by phone and certified letters and noone came to get car. Now Im being still charged full amount plus interest and late fees. The process was suppose to be they sell car at auction and any money left is what I could be responsible for but that is not what happened. The tow company salvaged the car because finance company never came to get the car. Now I am trying to buy a home and this one thing is stopping me from my dream of home ownership for my family. Please I need help to resolve this.','American Credit Acceptance, LLC',2.0,4.0,'i was in need of a car when i went to a dealership because i was in need of it. the car was not even on the lot and i never');
