INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3709,'02/15/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I spoke with TransUnion and my report updates from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never took place or uploaded to TransUnion system. There is massive fraud in regards to my personal and professional information being reported by TransUnion. Name Alias, Business attached to addresses, other mortgages that are not mine and with an ex girlfriend listed as a spouse, wrong phone numbers, wrong points of contacts and above all it looks like countless ends of financial fraud with banks and financial institutions. Today [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I spent close to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes reviewing the fraud and TransUnion was helpful to have me know that I will have a report shipped to my address. It looks like all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit agencies are not correlating information timely or have been able to do so due to this fraud. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was supposed to clarify these matters with TransUnion, and the matter got far worse within in the process. It ''s helpful to work with all the credit agencies to double and triple check the progress of inaccurate information.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'transUnion has a massive fraud in regards to my personal and professional information. it looks like countless ends of financial fraud with banks and financial institutions.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3710,'02/15/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I have had many problems with Wells Fargo disbursing the correct amount of tuition I asked for in my loan. They are expecting me to apply for a second loan when I only asked for one loan from the beginning. I have had to call many times due to incorrect dispurment of school funds and I even got a late fee for tuition in the 1st semester. It does not make sense to apply for two different loans in the same school year and that ''s what they are trying to make me do. Wells Fargo never got it correct from the start and it has been extremely frustrating dealing with them over the phone. I am not capable of going to school for my second semester because they are not disbursing the correct amount. They are not being of help and I have talked to more than 3 representatives and an executive about the problem. I finally spoke to a respresenative on XX/XX/2017 who understood my situation and he explained that he would speak to my lender and have an answer for me by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I never receive anything from him and I was forced to call Wells Fargo to check in on the loan process once again. The women I spoke with told me the male agent was not in the office today, when I was expecting a call from him because he told me he would inform me.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',4.0,4.0,'I have had many problems with Wells Fargo disbursing the correct amount of tuition. they are expecting me to apply for a second loan when I only asked for one loan');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3711,'02/15/2017','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Issues in this complaint : Improper handling of escrows Failure to pay property taxes timely Repeated provision of false information concerning the status of property tax payment Duplicate payment of property taxes with full knowledge that they had already been paid Failure to reimburse duplicate property tax payment timely Loss of earnings on retirement savings withdrawn to cover unpaid property taxes Details : Freedom Mortgage withdrew {$4900.00} from our escrow account for property taxes on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We were scheduled to refinance on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and a few days before closing our banker informed us that the taxes had not been paid. 
I called Freedom 3-4 times between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to follow up on the missing tax payment. I was repeatedly given false information that an individual check for our taxes had been sent to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Our banker and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] revenue department informed me that mortgage companies typically do not send individual checks for property taxes but rather bulk payments through a tax servicing company. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I requested an escalation from the Freedom call center and finally got confirmation that no check had been sent directly to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was told that the tax processing servicer was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but that they could not contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on my behalf but only open some kind of ticket with another Freedom department. The ultimate result of the " ticket '''' was an email that repeated the false information that our taxes had been paid ( see attached ). 

I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] directly on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They were able to find our taxes in the bulk transmission from Freedom, and informed me that they did not intend to pay them before the end of the year. As a result, we were forced to withdraw money from retirement savings on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in order to pay this unexpected expense and fund our new loan. 

