INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3749,'02/06/2017','Debt collection','Mortgage','False statements or representation','first citizen bank gave me short term [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 7 year loans on my home for 18 years [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. was the end of my loan, after I made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment I went to see [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bk. manager he put me off saying it was too early to start proses I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they wrote me a loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan I was still working with first citizen they said I could get {$300.00}. to {$1000.00}. closeing cost. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had my loan ready with a {$4200.00}. closing I stay in contact with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] there was always some delay I finly told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to close. then first citizen charge me a {$5600.00}. late fee it change my debt to income {$29.00}. to low I had to take a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my credit score was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] first citizen cause the delay I never had a late payment for 18 years, I contacted customer service for someone else to handle my loan no change, first citizen cause all the delays and no reasen to charge me alate fee I wont my money back','FIRST CITIZENS BANCSHARES, INC.',2.0,2.0,'first citizen bank gave me short term loans on my home for 18 years. manager put me off saying it was too early to start proses. manager put me off saying it was too');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3750,'02/06/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Can''t repay my loan','I received the loan repayment information in the mail stating that I needed to begin repaying the Parent Plus Loans my daughter used to go to college on. I told them that I could not make those payment at this time due to my financial hardship I was going through. The told me that they could offer me a foreberance on the loan until I can make the payments. I ask what was that, and they explained to me that I would not have to pay right now and I would be allowed to take a break from making payments I said OK but I was not told that the interest was going to continue to pile up against my loan. The loan was for {$40000.00} and now I believe it had grown to over {$100000.00} with the tacked on interest that is now due. I do n''t think that was fair to me for them to pile that interest on me without offering me something else.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'the loan was for $40000.00 and now I believe it had grown to over $100000.00 with the tacked on interest that is now due ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3751,'02/06/2017','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Settlement process and costs','Our ISSUES : 1.Processing time : We were initially told that it will be a 30-day process. Then it became 45 days.It ended up being 88 days despite submitting all our requirements ASAP. 
2.Communication : Initially, the communication was prompt. When we submitted all paperwork & signed on the dotted lines, the communication went downhill esp. when we pointed out errors in their documents.Based on the email from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the expected completion was 30-45 days without clarification when the 30-45 days will start.On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I started emailing Americash about the status of our application. I was never given a clear answer.All I got was excuses for the delay giving me an impression that our file was " too complicated '''' to process. Americash had all our documents and they should have told us earlier that our file will be too complicated for them so I could have moved to another lender.From Day [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Americash agreed to communicate via email only. We were assigned to a loan officer who works from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was never made aware to us. It seemed like her schedule to reply to her emails is a few minutes before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], leaving us with almost no chance to continue the exchange of emails ( on the same day ) because she has gone home. We had no choice but to wait for the following day to get a reply back.It was a challenge to communicate effectively. If there is any deadline or urgent matter or update, we would have appreciated being emailed ASAP instead of us chasing Americash or being told the last minute about a deadline. 
3.Accuracy of paperwork : Paperwork was amended more than once due to their errors. The answers given to us were : " they were not aware of said requirements '''' or " they do not know why their computer made such calculation '''', etc. Loan processing is their main business so do they expect clients like us to pick up their errors because of their lack of knowledge or un-reliable computer system? 
4.Debt consolidation : We understand the Debt to Income ratio. The details of the debt consolidation were never discussed with us. We only found out when we received the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Initial CD. We appealed to Americash ( more than once ) NOT to pay out the credit cards that we have pre-paid the interests until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].We asked them to pay out the purchase option of our leased car so we can own the car outright and reduce our monthly debts.Our request simply fell on deaf ears. Americash went ahead and paid those credit card balances making us lose {$310.00} on prepaid interests. 
We were never told about the actual closing date and we were never given a proper update.I continued to pay off our debts so we will not risk ruining our credit. We told Americash about this & they said that they will pull out the latest credit report so they will have the correct balance for pay out and/or they will tell us when to email the latest statement so they can capture the correct outstanding balance. Americash did not do both so they ended up overpaying our credit cards by {$2300.00}, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mortgage was over paid by {$4900.00} and Property tax by {$140.00}. It was left to us to chase their overpayments. We had no access to the funds that should have been in our hands on settlement and had to wait for the refunds. The last refund check was received in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]! 
5.Customer service.I emailed Americash on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to request copies of all signed documents for our file. To date, we are still waiting for our copies. 
I went with Americash because they advertised and claimed to be the # 1 lending company. 
I lost {$310.00} on prepaid interests on various credit cards plus the interest on all the refunds. I want to be refunded for all the lost interest and copies of all signed documents.I look forward to your help on this matter. Thank you.','AMERICASH',2.0,2.0,'88 days despite submitting all our requirements ASAP. a loan officer who works from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was never made aware. a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3752,'02/06/2017','Debt collection','Credit card','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','My wife and i are trying to buy a house and when my credit report got pulled a judgement of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was on my report. When i dug deeper into it i realozed that this debit belongs to my father and not me. a couple years ago he showed me a letter stating that he needed to appear in court because midland funding was suing him for an unpaid balance.Also said it was for a credit card my parents decided not to pay anymore and just let it go. Now fast forwarding its on my credit and not my fathers. We have the exact same name cause we dont use our middle name. Midland funding did not investigate this matter to make sure they had they right person and now its affecting me and my family. I need this taking off my report immediately.My parents had the card for a very long time about 15 or 20 years. so that alone says i would be to young to have a credit card.','ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.',2.0,2.0,'midland funding was suing midland funding for an unpaid balance. he said it was for a credit card my parents decided not to pay anymore. now fast');
