INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3758,'02/04/2017','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Our mortgage started out with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mortgage Company in 2007, then was sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We have had some difficulties with our mortgage due to insurance that was added even though we had homeowners, which went to litigation. We did eventually receive funds back, but then our loan was turned over to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Home Loans, now Fay Servicing. When we were with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received notice that the city was putting a lien on our property due to non payment of our property taxes. We paid escrow payments every month, faithfully to cover our homeowners insurance and property taxes. This was not being done until I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and asked them about the issue. After our taxes were caught up, our loan was turned over to Fay Servicing. Fay informed us that our monthly house payment is going up over {$100.00} a month due to an escrow shortage. This puts our mortgage payment up significantly and will be hard to pay every month. Please, can you help us to understand what has been happening to our escrow payments that we paid every month? This is our complaint and plea for help! Thank you for your time.','Fay Servicing, LLC',2.0,2.0,'mortgage started out with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mortgage Company in 2007. it was sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] home loans,');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3759,'02/03/2017','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','Nationstar [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Yet another complaint against Nationstar for the fraudulent fake auctions, made up values, and belief that they are not required to adhere to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and FDCPA guidelines. Honestly, when will the CFPB actually do something about this organization? 

Nationstar has run this property through their fake auction system ( in order to gain a 5 % buyer ''s premium for their own personal benefit at the expense of their investor ) and surprise surprise .... No bidders. The counter offer then made to the original buyer was once again ridiculously over market value. When asked if they could explain the value -- - we were told that they do not release value information in direct violation of ECOA guidelines. When asked the last time that they had had someone inside the property to value it ... ... NO RESPONSE AT ALL. This is likely because they have not had anyone in the property and the limited pictures that they do have were given to them by us. Which raises the question .... Where did the value that they countered us at come from? They made it up and it has no basis in fact. While I know that Nationstar ''s business model ( as outlined last [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) is to defraud their investors, borrowers, and the federal government ( yes, we just caught Nationstar again defrauding the Treasury Department on a HAFA short sale and have an ongoing complaint on that file ) at some point the CFPB needs to stand up and say enough is enough. 

I would appreciate if Nationstar would actually complete an interior value on this property and counter the buyer appropriately ... .. I know that their goal is to attempt to get this buyer to leave so that they can attempt to run this through their fake auction again in hopes of getting a 5 % buyer ''s premium ( once again at the expense of their investor ), but enough is enough.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,4.0,'Nationstar has run the property through their fake auction system. they made up values and belief that they are not required to adhere to ECOA guidelines. the CFPB has ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3760,'02/03/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','Chase bank breached my account, and gave my information to someone else and me access to someones account. The resolution is for me to change my account info and update my automatic payment and direct deposits, for my safety? Though the bank had an obligation to keep your information safe? If they do n''t what happens? Where can we get help fighting the banks?','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'the bank breached my account and gave my information to someone else and me. the resolution is for me to change my account info and update my automatic payment and direct deposits, for my');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3761,'02/03/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','ACS violated the following : ( 1 ) unfair and deceptive practices related to payment allocation. 12 U.S.C. 5531, 5536 ; unlawful practices related to payment aggregation in violation of Section 623 of the Fair Credit Reporting Act 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( a ) ( 2 ) I took out [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] individual loans. ACS aggregated the balances and rates into [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] " packets '''' exactly like a loan consolidation, without consent. 
XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$5100.00} 9.97 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$5100.00} 9.25 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$5100.00} 10.02 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$5100.00} 10.03 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$5100.00} 9.43 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$6300.00} 12.06 % Variable THE NEW LOANS THEY CONSOLIDATED Before payments began, ACS shows the loans set up as follows XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$5100.00} 9.97 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$15000.00} 9.25 % Variable XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : {$11000.00} 9.43 % Mixed The following are my allegations. 

1. ACS created a packet where only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans were shown to the consumer. The bill shows [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans, online shows [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans, and customer representatives only see [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans. The same for balances and interest rates. It is a consolidation. 
2. Rather than combining for billing, the rates and balances were mixed and a new repayment method was introduced. Rather than paying {$50.00} each month towards the loans, around {$40.00} per loan per packet was applied. This drastically increased the amount of interest the company would receive on the loan. Again, without consent. Around {$8000.00} was stolen using this scheme. Another {$3000.00} for 10 years of interest is due. 

3. ACS denied me the opportunity to make payments individually towards the loans. They denied the opportunity to see balances for the loans individually. They denied requests to allow payments to go through individually and applied them how they wished. They applied extra payments to the next month, applied payments late, and held payments up to 20 days before processing making my loan late. 

4. ACS sent partial promissory notes with page numbers redacted in black to hide the number of pages in the document. They also sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] promissory notes to hide the fact that I had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans. They lied and told me " you have been given all of the promissory notes '''' referring to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they sent. Then when I found out I really had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans and could prove it they sent me all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it was time stamped from when I originally asked for them. They just withheld this and lied about it. 

5. ACS misrepresented my loans, rates, balance histories, and gave factually incorrect financial information in order to keep me from knowing the truth of my loan. They additionally sent fraudulent payment histories that show balances accumulated before the loan had even been taken out. 

6. ACS billing only included information on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] packets. I can not see the individual loans, nor are they online. I had no knowledge of my interest rates for my individual loans either. There was no way for me to know any details for loans [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

7. I requested ACS correct my credit reporting information that only shows [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans when I had proof of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans. They refused. I sent the request to the credit agencies. ACS still refused to change or show that I had disputed the false information. 

8. I had decided to change companies by refinancing my loan in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and requested payoff information and lender information as the information online was incorrect. They refused and did not respond. Certified letters were received. I then tried again in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the company needed the payoff, statements, credit information, balance history, etc. They all needed to show the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans I had. They delayed information, sent incorrect statements, made my loan go into late status, and refused to show my credit report correctly. Interest rate then jumped greatly. I still can not refinance. 

The rest of my complaint is in updated complain','ACS Education Services',2.0,4.0,'ACS aggregated the balances and rates into [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] " packets '''' exactly like a loan consolidation, without consent. ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3762,'02/03/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','ECSI Heartland ( which just acquired [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) charges a " convenience fee '''' of {$.00} for each autodraft payment -- effectively forcing the individual to pay in order to pay their loan. They claim this is for " website maintenance '''' for a website which they have said they will no longer update ( this is for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] site ) and that the convenience fee will continued to be used once [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] borrowers are rolled over to the ECSI Heartland website ( which they wo n''t give a timeline for ). This is just another example of student loan servicers profiting off of student loan borrowers after winning lucrative contracts with the federal government. There are plenty of other servicers that do not charge for this. When I asked if I could lodge a complaint, I was told they do not take complaints. Additionally, their website is currently stuck in the XX/XX/1990 and borrowers are n''t able to update much on the website without calling or mailing in information to the servicer. When setting up Auotdraft for example, it took a month and half to set up and I never received the correspondence that my autodraft would not be in effect for my next payment ( although I filed it well before their deadlines ). Supposedly this information was mailed to me, but I ''m signed up for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- also a " service '''' that ECSI / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] does n''t seem to keep updated as none of the correspondence I get is ever electronic.','HEARTLAND PAYMENT SYSTEMS INC',2.0,2.0,'a convenience fee is charged for each autodraft payment. the fee will continue to be used once borrowers are rolled over to the website. the servicers claim this');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3763,'02/03/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','I recently opened an account with BMO Harris bank through the online platform. The process itself took about an hour and they asked for multiple different documents and information which I have never been asked for previously. Once I completed the online portion I received an email stating that all parties and the account must call in and speak to a representative or the account would be closed. Upon calling into the bank I was asked the same questions that I just finished filling out online. When my wife called and spoke with the representative they advised that the account was already opened and she did not need to speak with them which contradicts the email we received. In order to open the account a deposit of {$100.00} was needed. We opted to transfer money from an existing external account. In order to verify the account the funds were coming from we were to receive [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] small deposits from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and then verify these deposits on the website. Once these deposits were received we were unable to find the link we were directed to use. Upon calling into the bank we spoke with a gentleman that did not understand the issue at all. We were advised that the transfer needed to be made from our external account and that he would call our bank. We had spent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes telling him that we processed the transfer through BMO at the time of the account opening and that BMO already knows my external account number because they deposited the probe charges, and all we needed was to find out where to verify the deposit amounts to complete our transfer. Seeing as this was getting us nowhere we requested a supervisor. After being on hold over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes we were informed that his supervisor was not in. So again we requested any available supervisor. When the supervisor came onto the line she began to read off information that was not what we said to the previous person. Now being even more upset we went into the story again and were hung up on. Soon we received a call back from the original gentleman stating that he is going to transfer us to another department since we were " disconnected ''''. After the transfer the new [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not have he correct information again regarding our complaint and we went into the story again at which point we were advised that no one would be able to help and we would have to call back another time. After waiting on hold for almost [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes. At this point we requested to not do any further business with BMO and to close the checking account because this was more irritating and annoying than it is worth. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] advised us that we would have to call back to close the account and we would be charged a fee of {$50.00} for closing the account soon after opening. Something that should have been a single task ended up taking over a week to complete. During the whole conversation with BMO we felt like our concerns were not being heard. After correcting multiple people the wrong information was still being forwarded to the next representative. BMO Harris is using deceptive and unfair business practices and misleading their customers. I would highly recommend that others send their relationship with BMO as well and I would not be referring this bank to anyone else.','BMO HARRIS BANK NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a gentleman who did not understand the issue was asked to call the bank. he was told that the transfer needed to be made from our external account. he called the bank');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3764,'02/03/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] CFPB : XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I paid the Full Balance of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$230.00}, so I should NOT have been charged Interest on that Payment. But JPMChase did charge me {$5.00} Interest on that Payment, having erroneously recorded the date that I paid as XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I want JPMChase to refund me {$2500.00} and remove all detrimental information that it has placed against me in its reporting to Credit Bureaus. 

Sincerely, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], IL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'JPMChase charged me $5.00 Interest on that Payment. erroneously recorded the date that I paid as XX/XX/[');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3765,'02/02/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','The complaint that I have is with fstprogress. Over the last 6 months I have requested validation on multiple occasions for a debt that is listed on my credit report. I have been asking for evidence that bears my signature that shows that I have contractual obligation to pay fstprogress. I have not received anything that I requested and it is still on my credit report from all three of the credit reporting agencies. All my letters where sent certified with signed receipt verifying they received the letters. 

can you Please help me','Synovus Bank',2.0,2.0,'fstprogress has received a debt listed on my credit report. the debt is listed on my credit report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3766,'02/02/2017','Debt collection','Federal student loan','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I have been notified that Great Lakes Borrower has been abusing my payment loan plan, by charging me more than they should.','GREAT LAKES',2.0,2.0,'Great Lakes Borrower has been notified that he has been abusing my payment loan plan. he has been charged me more than they should.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3767,'02/02/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Managing the loan or lease','Auto being financed was repossessed without proper notification. When account settled, I was informed the repossession fee would be put at end of loan, instead it was charged the next month. Contacted them about it, they said it was just their policy and not to worry about it. I did that, but now they added a late fee due to not making full payment.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'auto being financed was repossessed without proper notification. when account settled, I was informed the repossession fee would be put at end of loan. they added a late fee');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3768,'02/02/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Last [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 I took on a mortgage through American Homestead in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], MT. The whole process seemed seamless and very effective until after I signed all of the closing documents. Before I went to the Title company to sign a rep from American Homestead called to tell me that I would have to put down less money than was disclosed on the original closing disclosure documents. She said great news the owners gave you a buyers credit and you only have to put down x amount of dollars. I was a little surprised and confused at the same time. I asked her twice so I do n''t have to put down the full 3.5 % down that the FHA loan requires and my payments will stay the same as what the closing disclosure documents stated. She said yes! I was elated thinking that I would have to put down approximately [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] less than what was disclosed and my payments would stay at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Long story short, 2 months after I signed the contract, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the mortgage company sent me a letter saying that my escrow account was short and that I needed to come up with {$1200.00} ish or that my payments would go up {$100.00} a month for a year. I called American Homestead and spoke [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the head loan officer and explained to him the situation and he spoke semi aggressively and said that I was trying to take advantage of their mistake?! I was appalled with the nature of the call and decided I would just [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] it up and make the adjusted higher payments. I have 4-5 payments left at the higher amount and it has been [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] readjusting my calculated budget to make sure no payments are missed. On a side note my credit bureaus show perfect payment history and I intend to keep it that way even with the higher payment that was a surprise to me. Bottom line if I had been told that by making the smaller down payment than was originally agreed to and that my payments would go up {$100.00} in just a couple of months I would have stuck with the original down payment that I had ready to go from borrowing against my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The way the rep worded the sellers credit and the readjusted down payment was deceptive. The way I was talked down to by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was uncalled for and I will never reconsider American Homestead or recommend them to anyone! Everything up until the down payment glitch was a great process. I was very happy with American Homestead until they made this mistake and told me that I was trying to take advantage of their mistake?! I was n''t asking for extra money back, I just wanted my payment to stay the same just like the rep had told me, even after I asked twice that with the reduced down payment that my payments would stay the same! I am in sales myself and if I make a mistake I ca n''t go back to the customer and tell them tough luck and by no means would I ever tell any of my customers that they are trying to take advantage of my mistake if I made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. No one is perfect, I get that, but I was treated rudely and mislead. This is an example of how not to treat a consumer.','American Homestead Mortgage, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a rep from American Homestead called me to tell me that I would have to put down less than was disclosed on the original closing disclosure documents. she said great news the owners gave you');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3769,'02/02/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','Capital One mislead me and then lied to me about bank account opening bonus and is now refusing to honor the offer after I have met all the requirements for it Capital One advertised this offer [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I applied for a new account recently and set up my direct deposit etc and met all the requirements for the bonus. 
I called today to check on the bonus and they are now telling me that I am not eligible for the bonus. They put out these advertisements out there and then refuse to honor them. When I opened the account, I read all the fine print of the offer and it had no language regarding there saying that it is for specific people only. They ca n''t put out these offers and then deny people the bonus when they have gone through the effort of opening the account and setting up the direct deposit, etc Now they have added this to the fine print but it was not there earlier " If you did not receive an email or mail piece directly from capital one 360 with the above code, you are ineligible for this bonus offer. ''''','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'capital one advertised this offer and set up my direct deposit. they put out the fine print of the offer and then refuse to honor them. they are now telling me that I am not');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3770,'02/01/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Communication tactics','Summit receivables keep calling threading to take legal action against me for a debt i have know clue about. I have asked them for them to send me the letter of the debt, and never received anything. Now they are continuously calling from different numbers, threatening to take league action, very rude, and asking for my information birthday, last [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of social i told them I do n''t give out my personal information to anyone i do not know. So now they have become more threatening and will not stop calling me.','GMA Investments, LLC',2.0,2.0,'summit receivables are calling from different numbers to take legal action. they are constantly calling from different numbers, threatening to take league action.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3771,'02/01/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I currently have a private student loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] serviced via AES. I have made several attempts to have my monthly loan payment lowered. I have been given conflicting information from several different agents. First I was told that I had to apply with my cosigner ''s financial information which I later found was untrue. Then I was told that negative remarks on my credit would be back dated after I applied for loan modification. I was also told that information was missing from my application which was also untrue. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] AES supervisor did n''t know I was on the phone and expressed how she was happy that I hung up. ) After months of attempting to lower my payments, I finally got my application in. I was denied because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] felt that based on my income and expenses, I would not be able to afford the lower monthly payment they were willing to offer me. If I ca n''t afford the lower [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] how do you think I can afford the higher payment? AES sets you up for failure and bad credit and it ''s absolutely unfair.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a student loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] serviced via AES. I have made several attempts to have my monthly loan payment lowered. I');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3772,'02/01/2017','Mortgage','Other mortgage','Application, originator, mortgage broker','Royal United Mortgage contacted me ( by phone ) and we discussed a Re-fi with cash out on a home that is in my name, but my son lives there and make the pymts. I explained I wanted his name along with mine on the new mortgage, so I was told ''no problem '' .After taking my personal info. and asked to forward my income tax for 2 yrs., I can no longer make contact with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , assit.AVP of Lending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] w/Royal United Mortg . Does not return calls, plus I have found that it is not even possible for that type of loan to be done in Texas. So I am not sure what damage I have endured as yet, I know she has a lot of my personal info.','ROYAL UNITED MORTGAGE LLC',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage lender contacted me and asked me to forward my income tax for 2 yrs. he has a lot of personal info and is not even possible for that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3773,'02/01/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I have no knowledge of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] debt and I would like it removed as it ''s reporting to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit bureaus and negatively affecting me','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'debt is reporting negatively to the credit bureaus and negatively affects me. I have no knowledge of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] debt.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3774,'02/01/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Balance transfer','I received a 0 % interest for balance transfer from CITI. After filling up the application and being approved, I proceed to do the balance transfer. Once the balance transfer was completed I received a letter stating the terms of the transfer including a 22.49 % interest fee. I requested a revision of the account, requested evidence of my acceptance of the offer with an interest rate, and CITI is not willing to provide the information.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a 0 % interest fee was received for balance transfer from CITI. a letter was sent stating the terms of the transfer.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3775,'01/31/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Making/receiving payments, sending money','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a charge for {$430.00} appeared on my checking account from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I contacted Citibank that day to initiate fraud charges. As of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Citibank has not resolved this issue. I have made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] separate phone calls to them, and faxed them twice. ( Although I first lodged the complaint [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was not told to fax a written statement until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. ) Citibank representatives constantly reference their attempts to call me, though my phone shows no missed calls, and no messages were ever left.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citibank has not resolved this issue. a charge for $430.00 appeared on my checking account. Citibank has not resolved this issue.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3776,'01/31/2017','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Disclosure verification of debt','BYL COLLECTION SERVICES [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Has sent me a letter stating that they want me to pay a 50 % settlement for the amount of {$130.00} and it looks like the original creditor was referenced as total [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Client account number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Unfortunately This BYL Collection Services is a third party collection company that up until this time has NEVER communicated with me. I did send them a letter via mail asking for validation of this debt by supplying to me the original signed contract between myself and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At this juncture I have not received anything stating their position that I owe them anything. I have never entered into a legal binding agreement with this company and do not owe them anything. The FCRA states that in section [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I have the right to ask for and be supplied with the original documentation stating that i owe any such balance. Simply sending me an itemized bill or a letter offering me a settlement opportunity does not meet the requirements of the law. In my last letter to BYL I requested that all collection activities cease since no proof of validation was supplied to me and yet they continue trying to solicit me to pay them something that I do not owe them.','BYL Collection Services',2.0,2.0,'a letter to BYL stating that they want me to pay a 50 % settlement for the amount of $130.00 has sent me a letter asking for');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3777,'01/31/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','To Whom It May Concern : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SOC SEC # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I am in receipt of your letter stating that my dispute of items in my credit report was " irrelevant and frivolous. '''' I am upset that your credit reporting agency would try such a blatant stall tactic. I am demanding that you reinvestigate my credit file under the Fair Credit Reporting Act Section 611 [ 15 USC 1681I ]. You have no way to ascertain the legitimacy of my action without investigating the items in question. 
