If you have any questions, please contact me at the address listed below. 
Thank you. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] SOC SEC # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DOB XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'''''I am upset that your credit reporting agency would try such a blatant stall tactic'''' you have no way to ascertain the legitimacy of my action without investigating');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3778,'01/31/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle lease','Taking out the loan or lease','Dear Examiners, I will preface this complaint with the following statement. I am a compliance manager in the financial industry and have been in compliance related roles since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This complaint is coming an informed consumer, not a baseless accusation. This complaint is against Fleet Financial , Inc - DBA - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CO. I retained the services of a broker to skip the hassle of going into a dealership, never was I informed or disclosed any such document to indicate there was a fee for broker services, nor an exact amount. The broker worked for the company, the company negotiated the car price, I assumed they made money on the back end with the dealership. After all, the dealership did n''t have to acquire the business, it was brought to them. The transaction occurred in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; I am submitting this now because of my most recent conversations with Fleet Financial. I never received a copy of my signed loan documents ( Lease ). When I requested them, they directed me to contact the dealership and advised that I did not complete my transaction with Fleet, but directly with the dealership. I never stepped foot in a dealership for this transaction, I signed loan documents in the parking lot of Fleet ''s office in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with my broker and with a manager, both are no longer employed with fleet. I am now learning that Fleet placed erroneous fees that have nothing to do with the transaction aka fee padding which is what the CFPB cracked down on title companies for in the past. My assumption is that Fleet does this on every transaction and has made millions from it. My broker can testify to that as we ''re still in contact. Furthermore, I learned that fleet added thousands of dollars to the price of my vehicle without my knowledge or consent, thus making the price and overall monthly payment more expensive. In the mortgage industry, a lender can not charge or assess a fee unless it is properly disclosed and acknowledged, I assume, the same should apply for auto financing since it is a financial disclosure. 

In the same transaction I traded in a vehicle, which Fleet paid much lower than market value for because they informed me that they do n''t have a used car lot or even a process to selling cars and that they would have to mark-up the price to either sell wholesale or retail, either way, their intention was to re-sell and refused to pay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I later learned that they used my car as a tax write-off by giving it away for FREE to a family who experienced tragedy. Not only did they rip me off for the value of my car, they used it to their advantage by writing it off on their taxes as a charitable donation. If I did not complete my transaction with Fleet as they suggested, then who did I trade my car into? How did they give it away for free? How did they pad fees and increase the cost of my loan? How did they make money? Who paid off my vehicle? And why was I asked by a fleet employee, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to sign paperwork that they lost and to have it backdated to the date I traded in my car? Yes, they lost the bill of sale or title document relinquishing ownership of my vehicle, to Fleet, and required that I re-sign and backdate it. If I did not comply, they would have rescinded my transaction. 

I am asking the CFPB to step-in, review my case, and three others who experienced the same/similar issues that I did. I am also asking for a refund of all monies charged by fleet for this transaction, including, but not limited to the amount added to the loan to increase their profit, due to failing to provide a reasonable fee disclosure.','Fleet Financial, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a compliance manager in the financial industry has been in compliance related roles since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. a complaint is against Fleet Financial, Inc ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3779,'01/31/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I have been mailing my mortgage payment to Ditech for three months and each time the payment is mailed back to me with no explanation. Upon calling Ditech, I am being told I did not include the late fee and per FHA if all fees not included the payment can not be processed and must be returned to the homeowner. I then include the indicated late fee with the original mailed payment and mail back to Ditech only for the payment to be mailed back to me with a new late payment fee that was n''t mentioned before. This has occurred three times resulting in my mortgage now being late for several months. I feel Ditech is purposely causing my mortgage to fall behind in an effort to foreclose on my home. My loan was recently sold to Ditech from Greentree Mortgage and since being with them I have had nothing but problems. My loan was modified with Greentree about two years ago. I can not believe I am having this much trouble mailing in my money for my mortgage payment. I have never heard of this so-called FHA new rule Ditech is speaking of and nor have I ever had my payments returned for late fees. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment in the amount {$600.00} was returned to me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/17 and per the representative, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Ditech wanted two months payments and that was the reason for the return. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I mailed {$1200.00}, which was returned to me. I phoned Ditech and spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she indicated the late fee was not included and that was the reason the payment was returned. I included the late fee and mailed back to Ditech in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the payment was returned again to me. I contacted Ditech, spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2017, she indicated the payment was returned because I mailed {$1200.00} and the payment is now {$1300.00} I am not sure what or where the fees are coming from. With the returned check there is no correspondence explaining the reason the check is returned. I have to call and find out each time what is going on with my mortgage. This is ridiculous. Ditech is holding the payment for a month and then returning the payment for non-payment, when in fact I am mailing the payment and they are sending it back to me. I do not want to lose my house because of a corrupt mortgage company or system.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'my mortgage payment was sent to Ditech for three months. I included the late fee with the original mailed payment. the payment was returned to me.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3780,'01/31/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','In the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] school year, I was currently enrolled more than half-time in an educational program, during this same time frame Navient reported all of my current loans as in default despite my student status ( and having mailed documentation to the loan servicer to provide documentation ). Navient incorrectly reported more than 27 late payments demonstrating an extraordinary intent to induce harm on my consumer file. This has caused a tremendous amount of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It is my intent to file suit against Navient for these violations.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'in the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] school year, I was currently enrolled more than half-time in an educational program.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3781,'01/30/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','CHEXSYSTEMS IN REPORTING FRAUDULENT ACCONTS IN VIOLATION OF DODD-FRANK ACT','Fidelity National Information Services, Inc. (FNIS)',2.0,4.0,'CHEXSYSTEMS REPORTING FRAUDULENT ACCONTS IN VIOLATION OF DODD-FRANK ACT.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3782,'01/30/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Customer service / Customer relations','I ordered a radar detector from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/2017, received it XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Used it 2 days decided it was junk. Tried to get a RMA, they said they would. They did n''t. They wo n''t respond to my calls or e-mails ( I ''ve left over a dozen ) I believe these guys are scam artist and are hoping I will just give up','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a radar detector from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was sent on XX/XX/2017. a 2 days later, they decided it was junk');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3783,'01/30/2017','Debt collection','Payday loan','Communication tactics','Coastal Financial Solutions continues to call my place of employment after I have told them that I ''m not allowed to receive phone calls at work. They have also not sent any formal written communication regarding this debt. This company will also leave voicemails on my work phone stating my debt.','Coastal Financial Solutions, LLC',2.0,2.0,'Coastal Financial Solutions continues to call my place of employment. they have not sent any formal written communication regarding my debt.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3784,'01/30/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Improper use of my credit report','I was a victim of identity theft and now I have pay day loan inquiries on my report under my old name [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the person even tried to carry me on income taxes. I ''ve tried to dispute them but the credit reporting company is telling me to contact the company. The companies wo n''t remove them saying that it ''s my information, even though I have documentation from the IRS, say I have identity theft on record','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'credit reporting company says it is telling me to contact the company. the company says that it''s my information''');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3785,'01/29/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Credit line increase/decrease','I have been an American Express customer for nearly 7 years now and have gotten caught up in a loophole where I ''m not receiving any resolution to my concern. I have had my American Express charge card and have faithfully made my payments every month ( there was 1 month where my account was late but I quickly brought it current ). Somewhere along the line, American Express applied a pre-set spending limit on my account of {$1500.00}. Yes, this is a charge card, so immediately I asked why they would apply a pre-set spending limit? Well I received a completely [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] political answer but I let it fly. 
Flash forward to today when I called and spoke to 9 different representatives and various departments. I finally got to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Employee # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who informed me that he can only see up to 12 months or pre-set spending limit history ( this situation is much older than that ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] put me on hold to speak to several departments and came back to advise that ; 1. He can not determine the original reason why the pre-set spending limit was placed. 
2. He does not know how long the pre-set has been on my account ( only that it ''s been over 12 months ). 
3. There is no way for him to remove it. 
4. That I have to wait for periodic account reviews to get the limit removed. 
Although he was polite as he could be about it, I find these answers to be extremely appalling. How can American Express apply such a predatory lending practice to a loyal customer like this and not even know why they ''re doing it? I am asking that American Express immediately remove this restriction off my account or clearly outline why it is there to begin with. I will raise this matter to each and every regulatory body I have to until answers are provided or American Express reverses the decision. And at the very least, arm your employees with answers so that we do n''t have to resort to these matters.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a customer has been an American Express customer for nearly 7 years. he has had his charge card and has faithfully made payments every month. he has a pre-');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3786,'01/29/2017','Mortgage','Other mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','This is in connection to Complaint Conf # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It is not [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I apologize for this error. 

This [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mortgage was not included in the bankruptcy. Please see attachments ( pages 5 & 6. ) There are two [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts : one is home equity loan and the other one is mortgage. It was transferred to Ocwen Loan Servicing later on. Before we filed for bankruptcy, we applied for loan modification. which process took more than 2 years. The house was sold on a short sale in XX/XX/2016. I contacted Ocwen regarding the inaccuracy of my credit report about what ''s included in the bankruptcy. Ocwen have immediately suppressed the two accounts from credit reporting. I am requesting [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to do the same. 
Thank you so much!','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'this [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mortgage was not included in the bankruptcy. the mortgage was transferred to Ocwen Loan Servicing later on. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3787,'01/28/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I was approved as an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/2016 which was cleared and I subsequently passed the background investigation. However in XX/XX/2016, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] informed me that it would be conducting another background check which I did not pass. I failed the background check because of a previous [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I sustained. I immediately submitted certified proof issued by the court the the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has been reclassified under a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Additionally, state law does not permit for this type of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to be re-portable beyond seven years from the time of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Checkr also conducts background checks for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I failed the background check with this company as well due to the information that is being reported erroneously.','Checkr, Inc',2.0,2.0,'a background check was cleared in XX/XX/2016. the company also conducts background checks for the company.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3788,'01/28/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','I want to submit this complaint in reference to a service or lack of service from JP Morgan Chase Bank. Chase has closed my checking account and refuses to provide a reason as to why. They did this one day before my direct deposit from my bank would be processed. I fully understand that Chase is the owner of the account and can close my account for any reason at any time. It is frustrating though that the only income I have is in that account and I do not have access to it, or that they can not give me the reason as to why my account was closed. They also indicated that my direct deposit was going to be forced deposited into that account, therefore restricting my employer from giving me a check for my paycheck. They indicated to me that they would not mail me my funds in a cashiers check until the account is fully closed which can take 10 business days. These funds were to be used to cover my rent which is due on the first. My account was not overdrawn and there was no fraud activity occurring on my account, so I can not understand the reasoning for this. I believe it is unfair for them to close this account when I have been a loyal customer for over 4 years. I believe they are deceiving me by not providing me with an explanation as to why they are doing this. I would just like my funds back from the bank.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a complaint was filed against the bank after a service or lack of service. the bank has closed my checking account and refuses to provide a reason. the bank has closed');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3789,'01/28/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I recently entered into a repayment plan with Navient. I was never informed by them that the payment was well below the required monthly interest assessed on my outstanding debt. This was very surprising to me, as I have been paying over {$200.00} per month on approximately {$25000.00} for over 20 years. Consequently, the repayment plan was adding to my overall principal because the unpaid monthly interest was being capitalized and thus, I was being charged interest on that unpaid interest. When I requested an amortization schedule, which I believe every borrower has a right to obtain, I was informed that the only documents available to me were linked on my account. None of those documents were a detailed accounting of how my payments have been distributed between principal and interest over the life of my loan repayment. They were merely summaries of my account which did not satisfy my request nor did it put my mind at ease that my loan repayment was, indeed, being administrated properly. Unknown to me, was the fact that Navient compounds interest daily. At an 8.25 % interest rate, I will never get this loan paid off. The company never ever provided information to me in order to gain some relief over this never-ending debt. If the government wants to bring down the debt, do n''t penalize those of us that have paid our payments on time. Bring down the interest rates and do n''t allow the loan providers to compound interest on a daily basis. That aside, I want an amortization schedule to review the accuracy of my payment distribution. Where can I legally obtain one? If the servicing entity can not provide it, who can? I think it should be unlawful to deny a borrower such information on money that he/ she has been repaying.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'a loan company has never provided information to me to gain relief. a borrower should not be penalized for the debt he/she has been repaying.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3790,'01/27/2017','Debt collection','Credit card','Disclosure verification of debt','Disputed the account being in collections due to it being fraudulent. Contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they had no record of charges in order to prove we did not open or have control of the card. It has been more than a year ( exceeding the 30 days required to respond to a dispute ) and nothing has been provided to us. We are demanding that the report be removed from our credit history. The account is listed twice, both showing " disputed '''', and we want both to be removed.','ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.',2.0,4.0,'Disputed the account being in collections due to it being fraudulent. contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they had no record of charges.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3791,'01/27/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','Navient is the lender for several of my loans. My original loans were never properly credited. I was always told about deferment or forebearance when I was employed in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] working for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would have been beyond eligible programs for repayments of {$0.00} because my salary was {$[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]} hr for family of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I finally got introduced tip repayment program and how it would work for me I got a {$0.00} payment but reapply every yr was a process. Either my forms werent received so ended up with missed payments. Offered deferment until I sent them in again. Once I was denied for missing spouse information, when Ive never been married. Once denied for only sending 4 weeks income verification. Never understanding those deferments changed my status with company but no correction to credit agencies. This still hinders a person from employment opportunies. I wanted a lot from obtaining my degrees, sadly the market still only affords me a salary under $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a year. Once I was laid off and used 401k money so it made my payments go up but because I received numerous communications it can be confusing to a genius. The combination of compounding interest, complex communications and settling for deferments is a recipe for never ending debt. Customer service reps seem to ask u about deferment as those its not a solicitation but of course every one will accept it because they cant jeopardize a bad repayment history. I failed to mention I worked on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 3 years. When I was laid off for 5 months in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I refused to call the lender for fear by credit for my {$0.00} repayment would result to me being put back on forbearance which doesnt help me with payment credit to satisfy the loan just make it were I dont have a payment.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'Navient is the lender for several of my loans. I was always told about deferment or forebearance when I was laid off. when I was laid off for');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3792,'01/27/2017','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','This company is trying to collect on a debt for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that is not mine. I have never had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account. I asked for validation of debt and all I received was a bill. Where is the proof I signed for this account. I have never lived at the address they had listed. I would like proof of this debt like paper work with my signature showing this is a valid debt. It is negatively affecting my credit and I would like this removed.','Trident Asset Management, L.L.C.',2.0,2.0,'a debt for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is not mine. the debt is negatively affecting my credit and I would like this removed.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3793,'01/27/2017','Debt collection','Credit card','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I settled my LL Bean Visa Acct [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] debt with Barclay ''s Bank by two electronic payments with a total of {$1900.00} pursuant to an agreement dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a lawsuit was filed against me by Barclay ''s Bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( MA ) District Court seeking full payment of {$4100.00} and failing to account for the settlement or even for the payments of {$1900.00} made in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called the bank and spoke to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who told me they have no record of the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] settlement.','BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE',2.0,2.0,'LL Bean Visa Acct settled my debt with barclay''s Bank by two electronic payments with a total of $1900.00. a lawsuit was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3794,'01/27/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Can''t repay my loan','I took out [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Parent Plus loans for my daughter back in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Over the years payments have been made regularly and I am currently up to date. I sought to renegotiate the terms of these loans because I am now older and can not afford to handle the repayment costs that are about to escalate on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I am currently paying [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 18 months on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan, which will drastically jump to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan is at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 17 months, then it will jump to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This was the only option that Navient Loans would give me. I recently read about a lawsuit about this organization making it hard for people to repay such loans and as a parent who helped his child to have a college education, I will not be able to handle this increase next year. From [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] per month to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] per month for 6 years. I was given no other option but to call back in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to try to get it lowered. I am trying to be proactive and receive help and guidance. Thank you.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'I took out [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Parent Plus loans for my daughter back in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3795,'01/27/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','On XX/XX/2016, I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and had a security freeze on my information with them. On that same date, I opted out from reports in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] system. On approximately XX/XX/2016, I sent correspondence to Equifax inquiring about a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankrupty listed on my credit file. I stated that " Due to Civil Case No. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , Et Al., v. Equifax Information Service , LLC, I do not know the source of your information on the bankruptcy you have listed on my account, and due to this, Equifax has violated the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). '''' I asked Equifax to send confirmation within 15 days that the bankruptcy had been removed from my credit file. Instead, Equifax claimed to have " confirmed '''' the bankruptcy using information [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] data on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], even though I had placed a security freeze on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] data almost a month prior to that. I am asked that the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau investigates this matter and mandates that Equifax removes their bankruptcy from my report, as they are not reporting truthful information.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2016, I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and had a security freeze on my information. on that same date, I');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3796,'01/26/2017','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Disclosure verification of debt','Initially was not given a written notice to dispute debt. After I received it via email, I responded in writing to dispute the debt. I did not receive any response, and was then contacted months later stating they had reported the debt to the credit bureau. I had requested documents to forward to my lawyer, but they stated they could only provide verification and documentation to the lawyer and would not provide any verification of the debt. After speaking with my lawyer, he advised that it would not be financially beneficial to retain him for the amount of the debt and advised me to file a complaint for the company ''s lack of compliance of debt collection policies and procedures.','Midwest Recovery Systems',2.0,2.0,'Initially, was not given a written notice to dispute debt. contacted by the credit bureau stating they had reported the debt. lawyer advised it would not be financially beneficial to');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3797,'01/26/2017','Debt collection','Medical','Disclosure verification of debt','Valley Credit services, has reported, on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit report, a collection account for an alleged debt. I contacted the agency today at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , whom failed to disclose communication was attempt to collect a debt ever during the phone call. I obtained a recording of the call as proof of the violation to my consumer rights. The agent also informed me the account has been sold to another collection agency, since I live in that state of Texas. Under Section 392.101 of the Texas Finance Code laws a third-party debt collector or credit bureau is prohibited from engaging in debt collection in Texas unless the third-party debt collector or credit bureau has obtained a surety bond and filed a copy of the bond with the Office of the Secretary of State. According to the Texas Secretary of State, Valley Credit Service does not have a bond filed in the state of Texas therefore are not bonded to collect in the state of Texas. The account is reporting as open on my credit file, as well as showing an updated date for the balance they are currently trying to collect on. So this account is now being collected by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] separate collection agencies, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] showing as open, and current on my credit report, which again is a violation to my consumer rights. I sent Valley Credit a certified letter with a tracking number, requesting validation of the alleged debt, which they received XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I never received validation, or a response of any kind from the agency. I then disputed the account with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit bureau, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the account came back as verified and accurate, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Again, Verifying not only false information to my credit file but the account in general, with the Credit bureau, before sending me, the consumer validation of the account is violating my rights. Valley Credit not only failed to conduct a reasonable investigation, but clearly has a blatant disregard for my legal rights.','Valley Credit Service, Inc. (OR)',2.0,2.0,'a third-party debt collector or credit bureau is prohibited from engaging in debt collection in Texas unless the third-party debt collector or credit bureau has obtained a surety bond ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3798,'01/26/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I received a notice on or about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that they had sold my mortgage to Carrington Mortgage Services and they were no longer servicing my loan. By the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I still had not received anything from Carrington Mortgage so I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] concerned about making my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mortgage payment that was due by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reassured me that I should receive information soon and that Carrington was not assessing late fees. I finally received some information from Carrington regarding the purchase of my mortgage but never received a billing statement to make my payment with them. I used an address in the information they provided to send my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. By [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I still had not received any billing statements from Carrington Mortgage, so I called them. The representative ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) requested a payment for both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I advised that I had sent my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments several weeks prior and it had cleared my checking account. She did some research and advised me, they did receive my payment, just did n''t post it to my account. I requested an explanation on why it was n''t posted when it was received and she apologized and said she did not know why it was n''t posted and had it applied to my account that day. I also made a phone payment that day for my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mortgage payment. During this call, I also questioned by they did not have the most current information on my account from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], they had a phone number that was over 10 years old and my last name has n''t been updated since I was married in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I advised that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had all the most current information and documention from my name change. They did not know why they had ''old '' information and requested new documentation to update my records. I sent the documentation necessary including automatic withdrawal information for my payments since their website only allows me to log in and view my information but I can not make an online payment, even though is a service advertised on their website. It states it can not process my request each time I try to do an online payment, the representative could not answer why to this question either. Yesterday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a certified letter from Carrington Mortgage Services that my mortgage was 60 days past due since my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments were not received and that my mortgage may go into foreclosure. I immediately called them and stated both the payments had cleared my checking account already, I explained the issues I had from the call on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment not applied, and making my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment by phone and the representative said " you ''re account is current now, have a good day '''' and attempted to hang up. I requested a manager to speak to, the manager introduced herself and said " is there a reason you requested to speak to me, you ''re account is current '', I explained the certified letter I had received about not receiving my payments, and she just kept saying well your account is current now. I asked why I do not receive my billings statements and she replied because my mortgage was discharged in a Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bankruptcy and they do not have to send me billing statements. I advised that my loan was not discharged in bankruptcy and that they are required to provide billing statements for me to send my payments in with, she argued about this then finally put me on hold and said she submitted a request to have billing statements sent to me. Neither of these representatives could answer any of my questions, why they said my loan was in bankruptcy, why I do n''t receive billing statements, why I received a past due/foreclosure notice, or why my payments are not posted to my account when they are received. In my opinion, this company is breaking many laws!!','CARRINGTON MORTGAGE SERVICES, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a representative asked me to send my payment to Carrington Mortgage Services. she said they did not post my payment and did not post it to my account. she apologized and said');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3799,'01/26/2017','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','hi my wlfe hads been out of work for a bout 2 years .I [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is the only one working at the time.i been paying my morage late but it get paid .bank of America been threating me that they are going to put me and my wlfe out and grand son.i hand ask theme for help and they turn me down.and they have all kind people callin me and sen me letter a bou my late pay ment.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'my wlfe had been out of work for a bout 2 years. i hand ask theme for help and they turn me down.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3800,'01/26/2017','Bank account or service','Checking account','Making/receiving payments, sending money','I wanted to pay my credit card with my checking account on Chase bill pay. I signed onto my account, clicked on pay my credit card, and entered the amount to be paid. Ten days later, I received a letter saying that the payment had been refused by my back and returned. I realized that the default account that the site offered was my equity account, not my checking account. It seems that you can not make a payment on a checking account with an equity account. I was trying to pay with my checking account. Why then does the page default to that equity account? It is not possible to remove that account from the list, and it must default to that account ; an account that can not pay. If you add all the people who might make this error, and if they were therefore late on their payment, how much money would Chase bank make on late fees? I complained to a bank employee ; he said they get lots of complaints, and he passes them on, but nothing has changed.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a bank employee complained to me about the payment. he said they get lots of complaints, and he passes them on. the account defaults to an equity account.');
