INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3820,'01/23/2017','Credit card',NULL,'Closing/Cancelling account','Bank of America abruptly closed both of my credit cards with the bank ( in a letter dated XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but which I only received yesterday ). The only reason provided was " your risk profile no longer aligns with the bank ''s risk tolerance. '''' I have a credit score of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( FICO ), have always paid my credit card bills on time, and received no warning that these cards might be closed. The only previous actions Bank of America had taken with these cards were to increase my credit limits on both. I called Bank of America and they said they have no say over it and I had to talk to FIA Services, who apparently administers Bank of America branded credit cards ( I was never told this ). FIA Services told me on the phone that they could n''t provide any further explanation, and that there ''s no way to appeal the decision internally. In the process, Bank of America / FIA Services eliminated all reward points I ''d gained on the card. I ''m especially concerned that this may hurt my credit rating, which has otherwise had no negative events. What can I do?','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'FIA Services apparently administers branded credit cards. FIA Services said they couldn''t provide any further explanation. FIA Services eliminated all reward points I');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3821,'01/23/2017','Debt collection','Payday loan','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I am a victim of Identity Theft I sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] an I D Theft report and they have not responded to me in in over 60 days this is beyond the FCRA allotted time frame. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is also reporting the same account ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) twice under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] different account numbers','CURO Intermediate Holdings',2.0,2.0,'Identity Theft sent COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ an I D Theft report. they have not responded to me in over 60 days this is beyond the time');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3822,'01/23/2017','Prepaid card','General purpose card','Fraud or scam','I was given a {$50.00} Citi Prepaid gift card that did not work. I reordered it and never got a replacement. I then reordered it again, someone fraudulently obtained it and spent all the funds. Citi sent me a fraud form, told me to fill it out and send it back. I called today as I never heard anything and they stated that the can not process a fraud claim on a prepaid card and apologized for the misinformation. They never notified me of their intention to not process the claim.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citi Prepaid gift card was given a $50.00 gift card that did not work. reordered it and never got a replacement. Citi sent');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3823,'01/22/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I have both private loans and federal loans that are serviced through Navient. Every time I have tried to have them work with me in regards to making my payments affordable their only solution is forbearance. They have no other options and state there is nothing else they can do for me.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'both private and federal loans are serviced through Navient. Navient has no other options and state there is nothing else they can do for me.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3824,'01/22/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Can''t repay my loan','After graduating from law school, my stepfather was helping me make my loan payments. I never missed a payment or requested my monthly payments be reduced. My stepfather unfortunately passed away unexpectedly XX/XX/2015, and all of our family ''s assets were tied up in his estate. I was no longer able to pay my loan, which at the time was over $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month. I applied for a forbearance based on financial hardship, and maintained my forbearance for six months. When I came out of forbearance, I requested an income-based repayment plan, which was granted, but brought my payment down to $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month, which was also an extreme hardship for me. I was told this was the lowest possible rate. However, after only a couple of months later, Navient increased my payments by over {$400.00} per month. When I called to try and reduce these payments, I was heavily encouraged to apply for another forbearance. I was instructed that the payment rates had been bumped up by the Department of Education. I tried once again to apply for income-based repayment, and then Navient told me that they had to calculate my payments based on my combined GROSS income with my husband. Mind you, my husband also pays {$1000.00} a month to Navient for his own loans. That means they were calculating my payments based on combined, pre-tax, pre-Navient payment income. When I tried to point out how wrong this is, I was just told that was policy. Then, they told me that the {$400.00} bump ( now a $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month payment ) was actually LOWER than the rate would be if I had elected IBR. This was the ABSOLUTE LOWEST they would go. Any time I requested a reduction, I was encouraged once again to apply for forbearance. Again, I have never defaulted. I have never missed a payment unless on official forbearance. I am an attorney with a good job, and I have not been able to save to buy a house with my husband or put anything away for retirement. Half of my income goes toward my loan payments, causing extreme financial hardship for my family.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my stepfather passed away unexpectedly XX/XX/2015. he was unable to pay my loan, which at the time was over $ [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3825,'01/22/2017','Debt collection','I do not know','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','There is an open account from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I have no knowledge of. I had an account about a year ago that I canceled, but that was through a different carrier as well. Even then, my monthly bill was under {$50.00} dollars at the time. Not only did I not open this fraudulent account, it would have taken me years to accumulate this size of a bill. The amount is preposterous! Additionally, there is an On-line forum discussing fraudulent accounts and collection attempts on those accounts for this company. I want this off of my account and confidence that this company will never do this again! This company needs investigated for illegal business practices!','Diversified Consultants, Inc.',2.0,4.0,'account from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is open. it is an open account that I have no knowledge of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3826,'01/21/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I received my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in 2014 which I paid for with private loans, since Federal loans are not available for graduate students. I moved to Florida after completing my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I ''ve struggled with repayments. My loan was in deferral for a year and since then I have made 3 months of payments. I recently called Naviant to explain my situation. You see, I take home {$2400.00} a month. My monthly expenses including rent, cell phone, car, travel to and from work, and utilities leaves me with {$300.00} to spend on food and have for emergencies. Naviant told me I could afford to pay them {$270.00} a month and they will not accept anything lower. This payment is just impossible for me and they wo n''t do anything to help. I ''ve tried to find help and I ca n''t. If i had known that trying to further my education would wind up hurting me and my credit this much, I would have never gone back.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'i received my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in 2014 which I paid for with private loans. my loan was in deferral for a year and since');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3827,'01/21/2017','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','As part of our divorce settlement, my ex wife agreed to take full responsibility of a vehicle loan. The car was always in her possession. My ex wife decided to make partial payments and non payments after our separation. I tried to explain the situation with the reporting agencies.','EQUIFAX, INC.',8.0,8.0,'my ex wife agreed to take full responsibility of a vehicle loan. the car was always in her possession.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3828,'01/21/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Can''t repay my loan','I was told that they could not lower my payments, however I was continually advised to request forebearance subsequently accruing unaffordable interest.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'i was told that they could not lower my payments, however I was continually advised to request forebearance. subsequently accruing unaffordable interest.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3829,'01/21/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Can''t repay my loan','I was paying through Sallimae before it was moved to Navient, I recall that I was n''t making any wages during that time and my loan interest suddenly increased the actual balance significantly without notice. The account was suppose to be on hold until I was able to find a job. Currently, I ''m paying {$660.00} every month without any consolidation for my income or any help from Navient to be able to make these payments easily. I almost have no savings due to this issue and with a very high interest rate. In addition, they would try to contact you regardless of your status and really want you make these ridiculous payments ( sound like collection agencies ).','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'i''m paying $660.00 every month without any consolidation for my income. I almost have no savings due to this issue and with a very high interest rate ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3830,'01/20/2017','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Disclosure verification of debt','Caine & Weber has been contacting me concerning a debt transferred from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to communicate and validate I owed this. I canceled [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] before this balance was due and acquired more affordable insurance through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Caine & Weber are now threatening to report this on my credit. If this is reported on my credit, it will affect my ability to get a job and many other products. I have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit & this is unfair.','CAINE & WEINER COMPANY, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Caine & Weber has been contacting me regarding a debt transfer. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to communicate and validate I owed this ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3831,'01/20/2017','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Improper contact or sharing of info','I spoke with the EOS CCA representative ( male ) on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on Tuesday XX/XX/2017 ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) about my supposed debt to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Property Tax Department . I advised the rep. that I did n''t own one of the vehicles that were listed and that there is an error that I have to discuss with the Tax Department themselves. He said he was notating file to wait before contacting me again, for either me or the City of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to provide resolution if possible. However the next day I receive a frantic call from my mom ( who is battling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) who asks me why did someone call her asking for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( I do n''t live with my mom-she lives in NY )? She stated that the person ( male ) called from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] @ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on XX/XX/2017 and she asked why are they calling her private line regarding [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ? She continued to state that he does not live here & since they called her line she demanded to know what that the call was about & where he was calling from. The man just plainly said it was a private matter & hung up. My mother started to assume that this was a prank/scam & the worst. When she called me 5 minutes later, frantically asking me if I had any knowledge of anyone calling me or trying to reach me. She was clearly upset and I explained to her I did not know but to supply me the phone number that called her. Sure enough, it was someone @ EOS CCA so I immediately call them to inquire on why would they not only call but involve someone else about a private & personal matter. They put an unnecessary worry in my mother ''s mind when they had no right to contact her. This unnecessary aggressive behavior went way too far to my liking & was what I consider harassment to me & my mom. This was done despite the notes the rep. marked in my file not to contact me until I had called back. When I finally reached a representative ( female ) @ the agency, I tried to explain the contact I had with the day prior & to inquire why did they harass my mother in NY, when clearly the file was noted. The lady ( rep. ) gave me attitude, very disrespectful & sighed repeatedly, talking over me during the conversation. I was appalled, so I asked to be transferred to her manager ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-female ). After reviewing my complaint, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the told me she too was going to escalate a complaint clearly stating the egregious errors her staff made & apologized for everything that had occurred. She told me that the internal complaint department would quickly find resolution in the matter. She said that the 1st rep. that I had spoke with, notated the incorrect secondary claim instead of the primary claim screen. This caused the second representative to call me ( in which they did not, instead, harassing my mom ). She said that was not proper protocol and could not tell me where the rep would have called my mom instead of me. She advised me to follow up the next day with the complaints dept. at the same time I explained I would see how they handle situation before I proceeded with any further action. When I did follow up with the complaints dept. ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it seemed like any resolution to the matter would be handled as an internal matter. I asked if they were willing to provide in writing, a document explaining why they took the actions they did in writing & they refused. I asked if I contacted your agency, would they be forthright with providing your agency the information, and she said they may or may not comply depending on the internal investigation. I feel violated, I also feel that contacting my mother who has nothing to do with my personal matters when she demanded to know why were they calling her was harassment. My mother is not well, I do not involve her in my private matters as she is sick, & like any mother would, worry about her son ''s well being.','EOS Holdings, Inc.',2.0,4.0,'a representative on a property tax issue called me on a private line. she asked why she called her line and asked why she called her. she said she was upset and');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3832,'01/20/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Taking out the loan or lease','I would like someone to investigate my vehicle loan with capital chrysler. They financed a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for me in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the amount of {>= $1,000,000}. Payments to begin on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$710.00} a month. We are in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] still oweing {$29000.00}. According to my payment history most of payments have gone to interest and {$260.00} to late fees. We would like to trade the vehicle in, an are not able to as they are showing we still owe what we financed after 2 years alomost 3. They are not appling all payment where should be. They barley contcted me now in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that we missed our 2nd payment. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I made 2 payments to cover the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. they never applied it and continued to move on and apply to next payment. they are showing we are more than 80 days past due which I do not agree with. I have asked the president of chrysler capital to contact me which has not to this day of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to resolve this issue. I feel my money had been robbed from us and we have no clue where it has gone for the past 2.5 years. I feel what they are doing to my money and loan is illegal.','SANTANDER CONSUMER USA HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,2.0,'chrysler capital chrysler financed a vehicle loan for me. they financed a vehicle for me in the amount of >= $1,000,000');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3833,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I completed my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/2008. Since my 10 years For loan forgiveness is coming up I submitted some Documentation from hr supporting the length Of time I had worked as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
I got a reply from the dept of ed stating my loans did n''t Qualify. I began looking for a better loan rate Because navient said I could n''t lower my rate. 
I was about to refinance my loan with a private company with a lower apr Then navient gave me the number to the dep of ed When I called the dept of ed, they walked me through the application and lowered My monthly payment. I called navient back and the y told me that per dept of ed rules I have To wait ten more years for loan forgiveness. I explained That if I knew I had to apply to qualify I would have done it immediately after graduating They said that it was the dept of ed rules and sorry. They are freezing my payments while my loan forgiveness application is pending. 
Approx 2 months. It seems that they deliberately did not tell me about applying for The loan forgiveness until I was about to transfer my loans from navient to a private lender. 
I do n''t feel I sgould have to wait more than ten years for loan forgiveness. They also advised me to take a foreberance on two occasions. I feel taken advantage of and deceived by navient','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'navient said that my loans didn''t Qualify. he gave me the number to the dept of ed. navient');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3834,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','After graduating college in 2011, I discovered that Navient/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had put me on a 10-year repayment plan for each of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans through them that created massive monthly payments of over {$1000.00} per month. When I tried to consolidate the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans I have with Navient/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was told that " the different styles '''' of loans made it so that I was unable to combine all of them under one interest rate. I was also unable to defer the loans until I got a job nor did they allow me to extend my repayment period. They have left me with no options to lower my payments, I ''m currently stuck paying [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] different ( and very high ) interest rates and I was given no option to have an income-based payment plan. I was forced to work [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] jobs at the beginning of my career in order to make payments and even now, six years later, my payments still eat up nearly half of my paycheck every month, making it extremely difficult to live anywhere without roommates.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'a 10-year repayment plan was put on by Navient/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the loans');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3835,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] high interest, private student loans with Navent that have been in default for years due to my inability to repay back the loans. I was a student at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and graduated with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After graduation, I found it very hard to find a job in the field of study. No agency I have applied to accepted my degree from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] education did not meet the educational requirements to obtain a job in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have notified Navent numerous of times and I even attempted to try and repay for 3 or 4 months in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but it was too much of a hardship for me so I had to stop. I explained that I could n''t continue and they kept harassing me at work, at home, etc demanding repayment. I have asked them repeatedly, how am I supposed to pay for a degree which is basically a ''blank piece of paper '', in my field, when I can not even obtain a job in that field? I felt that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should repay back the loan. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is filing bankruptcy and it was announced yesterday that, you, CFPB is suing Navent for illegal practices made it harder and more costly for some borrowers to repay their student loans. And now today, Navent ( their collection company ) decides to call me again, today demanding I repay the private student loans in full. Loans that totaled approximately {$12000.00} when I graduated in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and is now at approximately {$25000.00}. I am currently on the income-based repayment plan for my federal loans that is at $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] monthly payment because I can not afford to repay and yet knowing full well I ca n''t repay, they are demanding I pay in full the Private loans? Why? Because CFPB is suing? I need help.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a student at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] graduated with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONY');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3836,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Can''t repay my loan','I have been on the Income Based plan for years but my monthly bill continues to rise. I appreciate having the ability to pay less but if you get the slightest raise, they increase your payment! I do n''t see how this type of plan will ever help someone like me pay the loans back and be able to live. I have a mortgage, monthly bills, health care, car notes, etc. They do n''t seem to care that you have to live! I have tried multiple times to get my payments lower but despite my efforts, they require your taxes every year to make sure you do n''t make more money. It is n''t fair. The plan should at least allow a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year guarantee of the payments you have before requesting to see your income again. That would be the only way you can ever get ahead! I have always paid and I intend to continue but we need a break and Navient needs to work with us to help make it easier to pay the loans back!','Navient Solutions, LLC.',8.0,8.0,'income Based plan should at least allow a year guarantee of the payments you have before requesting to see your income again. if you get the slightest raise, they increase your payment');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3837,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I fall under thecurrent lawsuit I was only offered a forebearance, late fees, and misapplication of funds. I took out an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan that has costs me over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have complained and nothing.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'i was offered a forebearance, late fees, and misapplication of funds. i have complained and nothing.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3838,'01/20/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Managing the loan or lease','My complaint is on Santander Consumer Bank. XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Santander Consumer bank stated a false and misleading statement. I called stating that I sent a payment in but still have n''t noticed it changing in my Satander consumer account portal and that I did n''t want it to effect my credit. Santander employee stated that he would defer my payment so that the payment can come in heals of stated that he would submit a credit dispute on my behalf and stop any late payment from being reported. I noticed a late payment on my credit report I waited a month and half. Because this employee stated if a late is reported it can take anywhere from 30-45 days to correct. Today is 4 months later and Santander refuses to stand by there statement of removing the late payment.','SANTANDER CONSUMER USA HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Santander Consumer bank stated a false and misleading statement. he said that he would');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3839,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','Last year around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I spoke with my husband about minimizing our debt, of our debt we both had student loans. My loans were private through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; now called Navient, I called them up to see what my options were because I was behind on my payments. My husband had already spoke with his creditor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who agreed to a $ 0 monthly payment based on our monthly income but when I spoke with Navient they first told me the lowest amount would be {$60.00} then cut it down to {$30.00} which may not seem like a lot but with our monthly expenses for childcare and other obligations it was not doable. I then asked for a forbearance which was granted but this has been one of many and during this time the interest has equated to almost 3x what my original student loan was. I now owe close to {$4000.00} when my original loan was only {$1200.00}. I ''m not sure what my options are anymore because when I call to attempt to settle it, they are always recommending a forbearance or to request a hardship to hold off payment while the interest is steady racking up.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'my husband had already spoken with his creditor. he agreed to a $ 0 monthly payment based on our monthly income. when he spoke with him they told me');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3840,'01/20/2017','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','Well i have both federal and private loan. I graduated college only owning [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars. I got out of college and did not get a high paying job and had other bills to pay. Well they steered me towards forbearance on federal loans and gave me low income based repayments plan for my private loans, never telling me that the interest alone would raise my principal by double ... I now pay close to 500 dollars a month for federal and private loans and i now owe around 58000 dollars.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'i have both federal and private loans. i graduated college only owning [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars.');
