INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3903,'01/06/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Managing the loan or lease','I ''ve had excellent credit history and the only late mark on my credit is from Wells Fargo for a misunderstanding. I signed up for auto pay through their website for my payments to come out each month directly from my checking account. But, I must have misssed some fine print about it taking a few days or weeks to actually set up and that my vey next payment would not come out through auto pay. When I received a call from Wells Fargo on the 30th day of being past due I was extremely shocked and asked the representative calling to please make sure this does not affect my credit. I let him know that I was set up on auto pay and he asked if I saw the fine print and/or noticed that a payment had not come out yet and I answered no I signed up and I thought I was good to go. I immediately asked if I could make [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments right on the phone with him so I could actually be a month ahead and never worry about being late again. He accepted my payments and said he would work on making sure it would n''t report late on my credit. I left it at that thinking I was all squared away for the misunderstanding which occurred between XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. A few months later ( around XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) I was applying for a refi for my mortgage and was asked about a 30 day late that was on my credit. The 30 day late mark on my credit actually hurt my chance of receiving the best mortgage rate. I called Wells Fargo and spoke with a supervisor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who said there was nothing that could be done. There is no going back after they report a late payment and I would have to deal with it, that there is no one that I could speak with for this issue. I called back a month or two later and spoke with a female representative that also claimed the same thing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did. So I asked to speak with any supervisor other then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. A gentleman ( I do n''t recall his name ) came on and was very kind, said I could request in writing and send it in via fax. Be ask s me to give it two weeks to a month for the department who handles reporting on credit bureaus to review and see I paid well for a year now and may remove the late payment mark. I did just that. I asked kindly in a letter to please see I ''ve actually paid well and an entire month ahead in payments for the year to prove it was truly a misunderstanding. An entire month later I receive a letter not acknowledging anything on my letter but that there records are correct and no chance will be made on my credit bureaus.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',4.0,4.0,'a representative called me to make sure this does not affect my credit. he accepted my payments and said he would work on making sure it wouldn''t report late ');
