INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3921,'01/02/2017','Debt collection','Medical','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','This is the second time this has happened to me with this company. I fell for the scam the first time. I was mailed a bill from Computer Credit , Inc. on behalf of a medical bill with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I paid the debt of {$84.00} and the check cleared my bank on XX/XX/2016. Computer Credit then sent me a repeat of that same bill on XX/XX/2016. This was sent 4 days after the check cleared. Not received but cleared. This company has done this before and I fell for the scam and was never reimbursed. This is no accident on their part. They will repeatedly re-bill as long as the victim keeps paying. A nice side effect is they ding your credit score while doing this.','Computer Credit, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'this is the second time this has happened to me with this company. I fell for the scam the first time.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3922,'01/01/2017','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Taking out the loan or lease','I purchased a vehicle from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] drive time dealership and was cheated out of my money. I ''ve have had this vehicle for two years and was never provided a title. I have been basically bad mouth, insulted and mistreated by their customer relations department. I have now file a complaint with the state attorney general ''s office as well as the department of motor vehicles and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the CFPB. Your customer relations department never offered me an option and is now trying to settle under the table even though I ''ve requested an arbitrator to have this placed on record. After doing a vin check I found that the title has a lien against it. I have gotten multiple tickets and fines for failure to register the vehicle and was told by the state highway patrol to stop driving the car. Your dealership sold me a car even though my license was revoked and expired, took my down payment and had the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] fraudulently sign off on the deal. Drivetime never offered to put me in another vehicle, or fix the situation and in fact started to become rude as if I was bothering them. It was n''t until I spoke with an Attorney, filed a claim with the state Attorney general ''s office, the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CFPB and the department of motor vehicles thAt your customer relations department contacted me with a bogus offer. The offer was to return the vehicle and they will erase any dealings by removing the tradelines off my credit and any record of the sale. I asked about refunding my down payment and they basically started bad mouthing me as if I was ungrateful. Your company is trying to steal my money by taking the car back, erasing my good payment history, keeping my down payment and basically putting me on the street in a worst situation than I was in before dealing with them. I am asking you in good faith to refund my down payment and I will not pursue any other avenues. This has also been communicated to the local media as well.','DriveTime',2.0,4.0,'a car from a drive time dealership was sold and cheated out of my money. the dealership never offered me an option and was told to stop driving it. the dealership');
