INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3986,'12/12/2016','Mortgage','Reverse mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I applied for and received a reverse mortgage from American Advisors Group in early 2016. My application was handled through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received the attached Good Faith Estimate around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which shows an up front payment of {$4400.00} MIP ( mortgage insurance premium ) to be taken off the top of my loan to secure the property against devaluation which was supposed to be covered by the government. I was told my agent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that this was required as a one time only fee against loss. Yet, on every current statement that I receive from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I am being charged ad additional {$92.00} plus every month for MIP ( mortgage insurance premium. I think that it is extremely deceptive to label MIP in the initial disclosure and then add an additional MIP to the existing mortgage. The use of the same abbreviation MIP for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charges is misleading and not disclosed properly to the consumer. I attended [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] one hour required counseling sessions on Reverse Mortgages and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ongoing MIP was never detailed. These abbreviations are misleading. I am attaching the original Good Faith Estimate and my current bill as documentation.','AMERICAN ADVISORS GROUP',2.0,2.0,'a reverse mortgage was filed by american advisors group in early 2016. my application was handled through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the attached Good Faith Estimat');
