INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3996,'12/09/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','I open a checking Account with Capital One Bank. I received a refund from a merchant for a couple of purchases. The bank put the refund into my account more than once and after they made the mistake, they then charged me over limit fees. I ''m on a fix income of SSI. I refuse to pay these excessive fees. This is a form of swindling. Which I consider a White Collar Crime.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a merchant put the refund into my account more than once. the bank then charged me over limit fees.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3997,'12/08/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I have been negotiating this short sale for years, and it goes in a vicious circle of needing documents, submitting docs, extending the law day, repeat, repeat, repeat. I submitted a complaint in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016, # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but the short sale still has not been approved. I work with all lenders, negotiating short sales, and this lender is hands-down the worst.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,2.0,'short sale is in a vicious circle of needing documents, submitting docs, extending law day. the short sale still has not been approved.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3998,'12/08/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I have notified Equifax back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2016 and even sent them a certified letter, which they received and signed for through the USPS, notifying them that the inquires that were listed on my credit file with their company was never authorized by myself, and that I wanted them removed immediately, if they were unable to justify that I gave these companies permission to pull my credit report with a document baring my signature. Equifax has failed to provided me such valid proof baring my signature that I authorized these companies to pull my credit report, and Equifax has also broken the FDCRA federal laws for reporting such fraud information on my credit profile. I have allowed them nearly three month to rectify this situation and they have refused to correct it. I have also notified each agency/company listed on the letter that I sent them and the companies have also failed to send me the information that I requested. This information is false and was not authorized by me and it ''s affecting my credit rating and I want all of the inquires removed from my credit file associated with my social security number immediately!!!! I am trusting that your government organization will enforce the laws that protect us consumers!!!!','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,4.0,'Equifax has failed to provide me such valid proof that I authorized these companies to pull my credit report. the company has also broken the FDCRA federal laws for reporting such fraud information on');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(3999,'12/08/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I am a victim of an unethical and predatory loan servicer, Ocwen. After years of battling with them it ended up in a court room and an agreement was reached that would allow me to save my home. The agreement required me to make a onetime lump sum payment of {$5200.00} in order to close the deal and I would then resume making regular monthly mortgage payments on my loan. However, after providing Ocwen with the funds they have changed the rules of the game and state that I owe them an ADDITIONAL {$8000.00} in order to pay some other past due fees that were not disclosed ( or clean up bad and shady accounting on their part ). They are holding my modification hostage and I am beyond flabbergasted. I also just became aware that I am being charged an additional $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in deferred interest. This is not what I agreed to. Although I am grateful that we were finally able to find common ground and reach an agreement that would allow me to have my loan modified, I do not appreciate Ocwen changing the terms after we already have reached agreement and then setting a sale date for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
The servicing of this loan has been a comedy of errors. The problem began in 2009 -- the financial markets were failing, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had crashed and been bought out by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I received a notice that I had missed my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2009 payment. I provided proof of the payment and continued making payments, but instead of fixing the problem [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] escalated the matter, refused to give me credit and filed a lis pendens and put me into foreclosure. I tried to resolve the matter but found it impossible to deal with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or the infamous Law Office of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( shut down by Florida [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and could make no progress towards resolving this matter. The loan was transferred to Ocwen, and they tried to move forward with the foreclosure I began requesting documentation and discovered significant irregularities relating to the backdating of documents, altered ledgers, documents that are cut and paste, figures that do n''t match, homeowner ''s insurance that is paid by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] different entities in the same month etc. etc. 
My Attorney and I were able to raise these issues and prove that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Ocwen had engaged in unethical and deceptive servicing practices. That is how we were able to finally come to settlement, because Ocwen did not want their business practices publicized through a legal precedent, and because I wanted to save my home. I never thought that they would renege on the terms of the agreement and demand a larger down payment in order to close on the modification. I also do not agree with or consent to the addition of $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in deferred interest. This figure is not accurate, this was proven in the documents filed with the court. 

Again, I appreciate the fact that Ocwen is willing to work with me and that a resolution was provided. However, after the fact Ocwen has changed the rules of the game. This is a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] owned loan, and there are specific assistance programs available for me through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as well as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or in house Ocwen programs. I am not happy, nor do I agree to a down payment of more than {$5200.00} in order to enter into the modification. I am not happy about, nor do I agree to a deferred balance of $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that is due as a balloon at the end of the loan term. I am not happy about, nor do I agree that 3.875 % should be the rate for this modification. I am not happy nor do I agree to an escrow account. I do n''t want to go back into litigation, I want Ocwen to honor the original initial contribution figure that was agreed to.','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a loan servicer, Ocwen, has changed the rules of the game and owes me a lump sum of $5200.00. the service');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4000,'12/08/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Communication tactics','I obtained a loan thru [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the amount of {$800.00} and was making regular payments to pay back until I loss my job. I was unable to pay back the remaining so in-turn they charged all the fees you can imagine to it and turned it over to a debt collection agency know as Nationwide Debt Management. I initiated a payment plan with them to settle my debt which was then well close to, if not over a {$1000.00}. I began a regular payment plan bi-weekly over several months paying it down to over half of what was owed. Then my bank sent me a new bank card with a chip and a payment did not go thru. So they contacted me and I gave them the new account info and re-established the payments again. However, when a payment did not go thru ( which was over a holiday ), they contacted me again. So I asked them to reschedule the payment again on a specific date which was the following Friday. However, the agent ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) became very rude and told me " we do n''t want your money '''', then hung up the phone. I was left with no other choice at that point. So since then, I have been receiving phone calls day and night at home and now, just today, at my place of employment. The lady ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) told me she was calling to collect a debt and I told her Not to call me at my place of work again and she then told me " Well you are going to pay this back one way or the other so Good luck '''' and hung up. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from all these calls demanding payment. No consumer should have to be treated this way. 

Sincerely -','Nationwide Debt Management Solutions, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a debt collector has been unable to pay back the remaining debt. the debt collectors have re-established the payments again. the agent told me she was calling to collect');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4001,'12/07/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Credit card protection / Debt protection','I have credit card account with Macy ''s in which I keep seeing random interest charges and late fees without any rhyme or reason. 

Even if I pay the amount in full they charge me with finance charges or interest charges. When calling their customer care department they waste a lot of time and then ultimately realize that the interest was incorrectly charged to the account. 

On another occasion, they started charging me interest on a 24-month long interest-free purchase saying they have no previous record of when the amount was charged. They only saw the outstanding balance and started applying the financing and interest charges without any logic. When questioned they reversed the charges but they have been a pain to deal with. It takes 4 hours to get to the actual agent who fixes the issues. It is insane how systematically they are conning their customers without their knowledge.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a credit card account with macy''s charges me interest with finance charges. they charge me interest on a 24-month long interest-free purchase. they only saw the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4002,'12/07/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','Navient is the servicer to my federal student loan. Per their internal policy, they apparently can not process paperwork for loans on autopay if they decide to process two weeks before the date of an autopay. This stands in complete contrast to their stated commitment to process paperwork in five to ten days of submission. 
As an example, my automatic payments are deducted on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of every month from my bank. I filed paperwork showing a change in my income levels on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Despite calling to push the process along on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Navient internally claimed they were ready to process on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However, as XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is within two weeks of the autopay day of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( 13 days, to be precise ), they will not consider the paperwork that has been filed until after XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( and up to five business days after that ). Navient also agreed with me that it could be much later than that, as that " will be the holiday season, and work slows down. '''' I am a responsible lender and have made on-time payments in the Pay as you Earn plan for several years. I am shocked that Navient, a private sector company, can not hold itself to a standard to process critical paperwork for months on end. Its client, the federal government, should take action to stop such incompetence.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',10.0,10.0,'a federal student loan company is not able to process paperwork on autopay. they say they are not able to process paperwork in five to ten days. they say they');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4003,'12/07/2016','Debt collection','Auto','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','The collection firm is Nelson & Kennard operating out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA. 

I initially discovered something was wrong when I logged in to my bank account and discovered that my balances for checking and savings were zero. Upon looking at my transaction history, I discovered that my entire balance on both accounts had been taken out on a legal order. 

Upon contacting my bank, I was given a phone number which led me to the aforementioned firm above. They told me that I owed a debt of around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a car purchased back in 2004. I am only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and would have been [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the time this vehicle was purchased. I tried to explain this to the firm and they asked me to send them images of my driver ''s license, social security card, and to write my signature five times. I did all of this and they still told me that I would have to wait for a fraud packet to be mailed out to my house so that I could fill it out and mail it back before they could take the " next steps. '''' I do n''t understand how they could have pulled all of my money out of checkings and savings for a debt that I have clearly proven that I could not have even accrued. I do share a similar name to my biological father, who left my family when I was young and has been known to try and use my name in the past ; with the only difference being that I have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as my suffix. I do n''t see how it is even legal for this firm to have withdrawn all of my money without even notifying me of it first. 

On top of that, I still have bills due that I am now unable to pay because of this debt that is not mine. My account balance has already been thrown in the negative and on top of that, the firm also appears to have charged a non-refundable {$120.00} legal fee which is absurd. There is no reason for me to not be able to get that fee back when this is not a debt that is mine.','NELSON AND KENNARD',2.0,4.0,'the collection firm is based out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CA. it is a collection firm operating out of the collection firm. the firm has');
