INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4021,'12/02/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Taking out the loan or lease','A long time ago I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to buy a vehicle. I went there because I saw the price reasonable for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was {$2500.00} if it was paid fully cash. So I gave {$1500.00} down agreeing with them that I was going to pay the rest soon. From that point, the confusion and fraud started. That day, we were talking about the vehicle, payments, etc.. they were speaking to me while handing me documents. The documents they gave me agreed with the conversation we were having. Everything that day was great, I even went home with the van and I though it concluded they way it was supposed to.. Then Westlake Financial Services called me about the vehicle, telling me that I had to pay the double of the vehicle original value. I told them to give me an explanation about what was happening but they did n''t tell me much, just that the dealer sent them the purchase documents. I contacted the dealer for an explanation but they did n''t help me either. Then I took all the documents they gave me and I started to review them. The documents I have are the ones with the correct prices but my signatures and initials were n''t there ( I have the documents as prove ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the mistakes is that In the dealer document it says that I gave {$500.00} down payment while Westlake document says I gave {$1500.00} ( which I gave to the dealer ). I contacted Westlake Financial and they told me that they were going to send me the documents the dealer gave them. So I received only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] documents that looked like mine but the information on them was totally different, and I realized that my sign and initials were there! .. So how did they do it? How is that the dealer gave me different documents and Westlake another [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Did they switch it? I