INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4039,'11/26/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was reporting on my credit report that a portion of my student loan, {$22000.00} was included in my bankruptcy therefore showing it 120+ days late and that it was now on a wage earner plan. All of this information is incorrect. Ohio law prohibits student loans from being included in a bankruptcy. These loans were on forbearance during this time. Also, my entire loan for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( a.k.a. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) owed is {$47000.00}. Why would only a portion of it be included on my bankruptcy. Again, all incorrect info. I sent them a letter stating this and the information was removed from my credit report. Within 30 days, the information was put back on my report but now reporting under Navient Solutions on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reports and under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would like this information removed from all credit reports as it is inaccurate information.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'Ohio law prohibits student loans from being included in a bankruptcy. a portion of my student loan, $22000.00 was included in my bankruptcy. a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4040,'11/26/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','A wire was initiated by myself to a customer at Bank of America on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 for {$20000.00}. The account was not able to accept the wired funds. I was notified the next day that the account could not accept the wire, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me to just do a recall request to retrieve the funds. I paid the fee for the recall. I have tried to contact Bank of America, but they will not speak to me. The BofA Customer has taken the wire details and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number into her BofA bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to request that they return my money since it was never deposited into her account, but Bank of America is refusing to return the undelivered funds back to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account from which the funds were sent. The only update that has been seen was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 which said that the request was under investigation. No update has been added since that date. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] wire department has reached out to Bank of America multiple times unsuccessfully to understand why a recall process that takes only 2-3 days has not been completed. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] recall requests from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have been requested in total and as of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016, no funds from Bank of America have been returned to me. Bank of America has essentially stolen {$20000.00} of my money and will not return it to me. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reference number is has been provided for the return recall. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch manager in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where my account and the wire was initiated from, has tried repeated to assist me, but has been unsuccessful. The lack of my funds has created a severe financial burden on me and has negatively impacted my ability to pay my bills now.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'the wire was initiated by a customer at Bank of America on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the account was not able to accept the wired funds ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4041,'11/25/2016','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Making/receiving payments, sending money','My auto loan was purchased from First Niagara by Key Bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have been making my payments online since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no issue before this purchase. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], posted on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I made a payment of {$360.00}, well above the normal {$330.00}, for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. This payment somehow was not recorded correctly as a normal payment, but [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that went directly to the balance. I called on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to have this issue corrected. I was told that an adjustment would be made in 5 business days and thank me for the payment. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I get a statement where I owe {$680.00} which includes a late fee. The phone system does not recognize my payment in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but the website does. I again called customer service to have this issue fixed, which I was told they will immediately. As a good faith measure, I made another payment of {$310.00} for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I get a phone call from collections stating I never made a payment since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], that I was delinquent by over 20 days, and they threatened to take my car and destroy my credit score. Obviously I was rather upset. I gave him all the information and associated emails FROM Keybank recording my payment. They said they noted it but I need to make a payment. 

I again called Key Bank customer service in the afternoon and asked for a Supervisor. After waiting an hour, I got [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I explained to her the situation. She informed me that On Line Payments, the same system we were told to use when Keybank bought First Niagara, did not take normal payments. THIS WAS NEVER TOLD TO ME AT ALL! I told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I made a payment online on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I need to have this adjusted like the payment in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I told her, if you look at my account history, you ''ll see I have made a payment on time or early for the entire life of the loan. I wanted documentation that this issue is their fault and that they are fixing it. They would not do so. I instead got [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] direct number. 

At this point I feel helpless. I am getting punished for making an EARLY payment and worst yet, the only way I can make a normal payment is by sending it by mail as their online banking is n''t capable of accepting the payment. What is this? [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? What bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] not except online payments!? 

I informed them that if this issue is not corrected by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I will contact a lawyer.','KEYCORP',2.0,2.0,'my auto loan was purchased from First Niagara by Keybank. I made a payment of $360.00, well above the normal $330.00. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4042,'11/25/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','Upon reviewing my Transunion credit report ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), I discovered an obsolete account ( creditor name, Navient, account numbers [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], dates opened, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], ). Please delete this account immediately as it is too old to be in my credit file. If for some reason the account is verified, please send me the name of the person who provided the information and the method in which it was investigated. 
In accordance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act, Section 605 [ 15 U.S.C. 1681c ] " Running of Reporting Period '''', as of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], reporting periods only run 7 or 10 years depending on the type of information. In my case, the information in question expired.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a credit report by transunion found an obsolete account. the information in question expired. the information in question expired.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4043,'11/24/2016','Money transfers','Domestic (US) money transfer','Other transaction issues','I was on MoneyGram to send my son money for his tuition. I sent the money, talked to someone to verify that I knew who I was sending it to. It was approved and I had my son go to pick it up. When he got to the Walmart to pick it up, he was told he had to call MoneyGram and then they told him I had to call. I called and was asked all the same questions again, if I knew who it was going to and verified my information. The guy then said that since they had a lot of fraud complaints to that area and that it was not my son who I was sending money to he canceled. Also told me it was a security risk. My son did not get his money like he should have that night. The next day I went on to Walmart MoneyGram and put in a different email address to set up a different account to send him the money. Went through all of the questions again. My son was going to go to Walmart to get the money when I got a call saying that the transaction had been canceled because I was a security risk. That was XX/XX/2016. That Monday I went online to my bank account and found out that even though they canceled the transactions they still took the money out. I had to hound them for over a month, when someone decided yes I was owed the money. I was told one refund would go into my checking account within 3-10 days and the other one I could pick up at a Moneygram location. I went to a Money Gram location and was told the money I was to pick up for a refund was in a different state. I did receive my one refund through my checking account. I have been calling and emailing them about the other complaint since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Finally someone emailed me and said that I was due the refund to take the transaction # they gave me to a MoneyGram location and either the agent could call or I could to get a new #. I got to the location and was told a operator at Money Gram to just use the # I was given. I tried that and still could not get my money. I called Money Gram and was told that it needed to go into my checking account and would take 10 days. After 10 days I called Money Gram to say that I had not gotten my refund. They took all of my information and was going to have someone look into it. I called after a few days to see what they had found out. I was told yes I was due for a refund and they had me talk to someone who processed the refunds that go back into the checking accounts. He told me that it would take 3 to 10 days and I would have it. I asked me more then once if he was sure that it would be in my account after 10 days. He said yes, that was due the refund and it would be in my checking account after 10 days. After 10 days it was not there I called and emailed again. I was told that I was not due the refund and that they would not have taken out money for both of those transactions. Then I was told it was the fault of my credit union that the money was not there. I have show them my emails that said I was really do for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] refund and the money was there waiting for me. They still are saying that they do not owe me a refund, even with it being researched and other people telling me I am owed the refund. I just want my money back. That money was suppose to help me when I had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and had to be out of work. I was to use that money for my bills and food. Now I am behind on my bills.','MONEYGRAM PAYMENT SYSTEMS WORLDWIDE INC',2.0,4.0,'money was sent to my son''s bank account and he was told it was in a different state. he was told he had to call moneyGram and then they');
