Thereby the purchases that were made where made in good faith based on the information that was provided by your customer service rep, that the car payment WOULD NOT BE DEDUCTED On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016, I a beginning day balance of - {$330.00}. Items were presented to my account as follows : Overdraft fee of {$36.00} was refunded and your account available balance increased to - {$300.00} {$25.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid {$36.00} fee and your account available balance fell to - {$360.00} {$5.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid {$36.00} fee and your account available balance fell to - {$400.00} {$17.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid {$36.00} fee and your account available balance fell to - {$450.00} {$0.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid and your account available balance fell to - {$460.00} {$4.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was paid and your account available balance fell to - {$460.00} I contacted the back to see what had happened I was informed they had processed the payment any way and thus all of these items had been assessed a fee. The bank did not have consent to enter the acct and make that deduction, this fact is further affirmed by your customer service rep during the call that took place on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016. 
They now are refusing to refund my money and in essence are attempting to extort funds from be based on your banks " stealing ", my monies by entering my account without consent. This is fraudulent and reprehensible, and at the core of all things illegal. I am unclear on how I can be told a payment will not come out, remove the permission for the bank to enter my account and because I made purchases based on the word of your rep, that the funds where not going to be deducted be assessed additional fees, {$120.00} from me and think this is good business practice. I want my money back.','SUNTRUST BANKS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016, I called to inform Sun Trust that I was resending');
