INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4049,'11/22/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','On or about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 my father instructed and provided his girlfriend with account information to send a quick pay to my account in the amount of {$2000.00}. At this time my father was alive and well, during the course of day on or about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 my father was murdered which was unknown to myself or the girlfriend. The quick pay was sent at some point on or about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 my grandfather became upset that he wasnt listed as a beneficiary and decided to make a fraud claim without in basis. The bank than proceeded to close accounts and send my father funds via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. According to the bank on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 I went to provide death certificates and request rights of survivor-ship and beneficiary information my account was being frozen until the fraud department was finished with an investigation. On or about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I went in back to withdraw funds from direct deposit from my employer and child support when I was notified by a teller that all my funds had been sent back, the remaining funds were sent via mail in form of check on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 to address on file. As of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16, none of the funds have been received and my employer has stated that no notification of returned funds has been received. I have called the customer care and executive office for assistance regarding how Chase JP Morgan has mishandled my funds and account. Chase bank has not provided any instruction on how to handle an account in the event of a death, or rules that states you cant provide another person access to account if the customer wishes engage in such practice. Launching a fraud case without all the facts is bad business practices and causes a disruption in an situation that has no intention of anyone involved committing fraud.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'my father instructed and provided his girlfriend with account information. he sent a quick pay to his account in the amount of $2000.00. the bank then closed accounts');
