INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4060,'11/18/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Using a debit or ATM card','I recently got an account open with pnc bank. Someone was able to get my card information and use it to make an online payment to their orthodontist for {$100.00}. I called pnc bank immediately to tell them about the issue, instead of stopping the payment before it posted they allowed it to go through. Now I am out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] while they take 10 business days to investigate. Most banks show since of urgency when things like this happen. The customer service representatives are rude and show no empathy. I no longer trust my money being in a bank that does n''t protect their account holders accounts and sensitive information.','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'pnc bank has opened an account with pnc bank. it was able to make an online payment to their orthodontist for $100.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4061,'11/18/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Getting a loan','I had a period of medical and financial hardship back between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2014, where I was late through that time period. I got caught up as quickly as I could, and have been on time ever since. Unfortunately, those late payments are now costing me thousands of dollars worth of higher interest rates. I have asked for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] removal of those late payments, but Navient will not budge. I do not feel it is fair to continue to punish me for a period of time I had very little control over. All I am interested in is the removal of those late payments from my Credit Report so that I can move on with my life.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'a period of medical and financial hardship back between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2014. the late');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4062,'11/17/2016','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','This letter is to file a complaint with PayPal as well as the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau concerning PayPal ''s policy of allocating refunds on purchases to the general balance instead of applying directly to the cancelled charge. 

This has happened to my account twice in the last two months. The first incident was on my statement of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 for a charge of {$210.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 that was refunded on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$210.00}. In this instance I was charged {$22.00} in interest on an amount that had been refunded. I would like that {$22.00} refunded as a credit on my account. Note that for some reason the charge is shown as {$210.00} on my Statement, but online it is correctly shown as {$210.00} for both the charge and the refund. 

The second incident was on my statement of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 for a charge of {$230.00} to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 that was immediately refunded that same day by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for {$230.00}. In this instance I was charged {$26.00} in interest on an amount that had been refunded. I would like that {$26.00} refunded as a credit on my account. 

Please note that I ''ve already scheduled a payment of {$620.00} for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 which will alleviate any interest charges as noted on my Statement of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. Of that amount paid, {$340.00} was a charge from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from a charge on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 which was refunded three days later on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] amounts of {$110.00} for a total of {$340.00}. The application of a refund amount to the overall balance is confusing to the client and I believe to be a dishonest and unlawful practice. I believe that when a refund is made on a specific order or payment that it should be credited to that order or payment. What PayPal is doing is deceitful and that is why I have sent a copy of this letter along with the statements and listing of charges to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau as a formal complaint against PayPal. 

I hereby request that you refund a total of {$49.00} in alleged interest charges and case and desist this despicable practice of charging interest on refunded amounts.','PAYPAL HOLDINGS INC.',2.0,2.0,'this letter is to file a complaint with PayPal. it is to file a complaint with the consumer financial protection bureau. the first incident was on my statement of [COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4063,'11/17/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Disputed the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcies showing on my report. Equifax deleted the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcies and later the same day placed them back onto my report. No five day notice received informing me of the lines being added back to my credit report.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax deleted the bankruptcies and later placed them back onto my report. no five day notice received informing me of the lines being added back to my credit report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4064,'11/17/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Making/receiving payments, sending money','I sent money through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] App for my bills which was {$450.00} and {$60.00} to one person & {$310.00} & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] $ to another person. Chase Reversed the money from their accounts by filing a dispute that I never approved. They took the funds out of my account twice and they wo n''t return the funds to the appropriate people or to me. I need them to give them their money back and return the money that they owe to my account. I never approved those disputes. I only dispute an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'Chase Reversed the money from their accounts by filing a dispute that I never approved. I only dispute an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charge.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4065,'11/17/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','False statements or representation','hello, on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 I received a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] time. The caller advised they were a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] representative and were trying to collect a debt in the amount of {$820.00} for a unreturned cable box. The caller was unable to provide any account information in reference to the time warner cable bill she was trying to collect for so I requested to dispute the amount/bill. 

