INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4092,'11/09/2016','Money transfers','Domestic (US) money transfer','Money was not available when promised','Paypal has a policy which states : If you provide tracking information ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and we can confirm delivery, your payment should be available three days after we can confirm the delivery date. 
o Pending payments are generally released three days after we can confirm delivery, but sometimes the delivery information takes a bit longer to update. If it ''s been three days and your payment is still pending, the information is still processing and the payment should be available soon. Please note that pending payments ca n''t be released before you meet these requirements. 

I have entered tracking information and delivery confirmation has been entered by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as of XX/XX/2016. The buyer has not made any complaint or expressed any concern with his delivery. Paypal has not released my funds for transaction ID [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Instead they are saying they may " hold '''' them for up to 21 days!!! For no cause or reason. Just because I ''m new at selling on Ebay. 
How many millions of dollars in customer funds may they be holding and earning interest on despite the fact that the seller delivered a product and the buyer received the product and there is no dispute? This seems completely predatory, arbitrary and lucrative for a company of this size handling as much money as they are. Please address this for me and millions of others.','PAYPAL HOLDINGS INC.',6.0,6.0,'Paypal has a policy which states. pending payments are generally released three days after we can confirm delivery. the information is still processing and the payment should be available soon.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4093,'11/08/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I have [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans through Great Lakes that are in repayment, aquired while a student at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], WI. I have been making regular payments on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of each month for a number of years. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I made an extra payment online. The website clearly stated that after regular payments are made I can specify funds minus outstanding interest to be allocated how I specified. However on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when I logged in to my account I see that the extra payment was divided between my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans. I called the service representative who told me that the " billing cycle '''' starts the day after the regular payment is made and any payments after that day are applied as regular payments first, then the remaining amount it applied as an extra payment. She informed she could not change how my payment was applied. I requested to speak to a supervisor, which I did. The supervisor again reiterated that their policy is that the " billing cycle '''' starts the day after the regular payment is scheduled and any payments made after that day are applied as regular payments first, applied to both loans, then any remainder is applied as an extra payment. Despite my insistence that my regular payment was not due for several more days and so the extra payment should be applied as such she informed that their policy had change recently to reflect the current " billing cycle '''' policy. She informed me " no one can change the policy '''' or change how my payment was applied. She also stated she had received multiple complaints regarding this policy. 

I would like to note I am aware that extra payments are applied to interest first. I am not disputing that the funds were applied to interest, but also applied to principal of the other loan.','GREAT LAKES',2.0,2.0,'aquired while a student at Great Lakes, I made an extra payment online. on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4094,'11/08/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Transunion is improperly and fraudulently verifying information with for an account that does not belong to me. It was opened in 2009 with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I have never even involved with the company. I contacted them and sent them my police report and identity theft report filed with the FTC. And they have closed that account and I can not understand why Transunion is still reporting it. I have included a copy of the letter. I will file another complaint with the FTC with Transunion and seek other legal measures if this is not removed from my account.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,4.0,'transunion is improperly and fraudulently verifying information with for an account that does not belong to me. it was opened in 2009 with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4095,'11/08/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','I contacted Bank of America about how their mobile app does not reflect the current balance. They charged me an overdraft fee for my account when it was not overdrawn. I went through the balance with the representative and she saw the error and still would not refund the fee due to I have already been issued a refund in the past. I advised her that it was due to the same issues. They continuously charge overdraft fees but the account balance online does not reflect the balance within their system. As I was reviewing the charges with the representative she was giving a different balance that what was reflect online. Then I asked the representative how long do you have to pay the account up before the fee hits the account she stated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] eastern time. I advised her that I did not receive an alert until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 and the few was already processed to my account so how am I supposed to review the account and make it current if the fee has already been applied. There is only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank of American and the ATM does not accept cash deposits all the time.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'bank of american charge overdraft fees for account when it was not overdrawn. the account balance online does not reflect the balance within their system.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4096,'11/08/2016','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Managing the loan or lease','XX/XX/2016 To Whom It May Concern : Please note that in XX/XX/2016, I called Fortiva Personal Loans and requested that my due date be changed from the end of the month to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I got an acknowledgment that it was done, yet they have been harassing me and also reported me delinquent on my credit report based on the original due date. I have tried to contact them a few times but there always seems to be a language barrier. I am requesting that my due date be honored for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the month and that my credit reports are corrected. Please see attached documentation that indicates that they are inaccurate for the due dates. 

