INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4109,'11/03/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Settlement process and costs','I submitted a Complete short sale package/Offer for {$28000.00} on XX/XX/2016. Ocwen/servicer for the note for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent a denial on XX/XX/2016 that stated the offer was too low. I sent an Increased offer the same day XX/XX/2016 for {$290000.00} which is closer to the BPO amount of {$330000.00}. On XX/XX/2016 Ocwen sent another denial letter stating the offer was too low and to submit a higher offer. on XX/XX/2016 i submitted an offer of {$310000.00} and then again a full price offer of {$330000.00} the same day in case they denied the higher offer and yet again on XX/XX/2016 they denied the offer due to a confirmed sale date set for XX/XX/2016. I feel that Ocwen has been purposely been delaying this short sale approval as they have been servicing this loan for well over 5 years for the purpose of continuous servicing fees to the note holder. This is unfair and should be looked into and the home owner is in complete shock as to why they would continue with a sale while we are in final stages of negotiations. This truly makes no sense?','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a denial letter from a note holder said the offer was too low. a full price offer of $330000.00 was sent the same day. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4110,'11/03/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Making/receiving payments, sending money','My primary bank is Fifth Third Bank, as it has been for 15 or more years since I opened my first bank account. To my knowledge, I have not disputed charges in the past but did so recently when I made an online order that I canceled within 10 minutes of the order itself. I called Fifth Third ''s [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number and was informed a provisional credit would be made. I offered to provide the email canceling the service but she said it was n''t necessary. The charge was for {$99.00} which caused, partially, my account to be overdrawn and {$110.00} in charges from Fifth Third Bank itself. I recently received a letter saying they denied my dispute because the cancellation must be provided to the merchant before the posting of the item. I am confused because in this instance, it was provided prior to posting.','FIFTH THIRD FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a provisional credit was made by the merchant within 10 minutes of the order itself. the charge was for $99.00 which caused my account to be overdrawn ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4111,'11/03/2016','Money transfers','International money transfer','Other service issues','This complaint is about discriminatory practices and denial of services by MONEYGRAM INTERNATIONAL, INC.. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , Texas On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I initiated a money transfer on MoneyGram site. 
This was a {$1900.00} transfer to my cousin in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The fee, using my bank account was {$5.00}. The transaction authorization number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], obtained using my online account and password, and a security code sent to my email. 
At [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], an email was sent asking to call MoneyGram ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 
Which I did. After verifications ( name, address, date of birth, last [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of SSN ... ), the agent asked my relationship to the transfer ''s beneficiary .I told her it was not their business, but nonetheless answered. 
She then asked the transfer ''s purpose. I questioned the purpose of this question. She decided that the transaction was cancelled and that I should go to a store. 
I asked to speak to a manager on that discriminatory practice, because it was not applied to all users of MoneyGram but selectively based on destination ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), sender perceived or implied origin, or both. 
After narrating the facts as above, the escalation person told me that I was asked these questions because t it was my first transaction ( after telling me it was asked from all ). 
I responded I had used the MoneyGram online to send money to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] during the previous 30 days. As a matter of fact, records available show I did a transfer to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] using the very same service on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ref [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ref [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) ( see attached confirmation emails ). 
In fact I have been using MoneyGram transfer service way back with some archived records showing transfer dating back to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with amount as large if not larger ( see attached receipt emails ) with online account established as early as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if not earlier. 
I indicated to the representative that MoneyGram ''s practice was discriminatory as I was NOT asked these questions when transferring money to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but asked when transferring to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] country. 
She pretended it was for the protection of my account and I asked how the statement about the reason of my transfer which they have no way of verifying, is protecting my account. 
The conversation ended as the representative indicated again that my transaction has been cancelled ( not offering me the opportunity to answer the transfer purpose question ) and I should go to a store to complete the transaction. 
It should be noted that transaction at the store and the online transactions carry different fees. Using the online transaction and a funding from a previously associated bank account -as I did-, the transaction fee is {$5.00}, with a delivery in few days. That option and fee is NOT available in stores and the fee for the same transfer in a store is {$39.00}. This is a significant [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] fee increase. 
The online transaction I initiated does not present any risk profile by any reasonable standard, with the funding is from a bank account in my name and is therefore fully traceable and all security checks listed above. 
As I tried to login into my account later in the early evening and was directed to contact Customer Service again. 
On the call, the representative told me that my account was permanently closed and service was denied by Security, that no reason shall be provided, and that I had to go in stores. 
This is an unacceptable denial of service on a discriminatory basis. 
My wife -[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-did endure the same discriminatory practice but did not complain. 
I would request the agency investigates and take action to prevent the repetition of such discriminatory practices. 
I am requesting that my online account -[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- and that of my wife [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]- be fully re-instated with all transfer privileges according to the fee and rules applicable to all. 
Thanks & Regards [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','MONEYGRAM PAYMENT SYSTEMS WORLDWIDE INC',2.0,2.0,'complaint is about discriminatory practices and denial of services by MONEYGRAM INTERNATIONAL, INC.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4112,'11/03/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Disclosure verification of debt','Ref # : DEBT RECOVERY SOLUTIONS has report this account account as open [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Open Account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$240.00} Balance [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Original Creditor {$240.00} High Balance [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Opened Date - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Last Reported I would like to dispute the item noted above on my credit report I have made every attempt to obtain information related to this item reflected above that is being reported on my credit report under the name Debt Recovery Solutions. Between the original creditor and the agency noted in this dispute the original creditor provided me with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] other companies that they assigned their debt collections too and still no one has any knowledge of this debt. 
