INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4141,'10/26/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','We have been in default and trying to refinance our mortgage for several years now. Our most recent attempt resulted in a letter from Wells Fargo saying they do not have the authority to offer a HAMP modification as servicer to our mortgage. Wells Fargo was the original note holder and transferred it into a trust held by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Both Wells Fargo and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] HAMP are bound by the 2012 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] standards and must under law review our mortgage for a HAMP modification, however we believe they are attempting to use the TRUST to avoid this legal requirement. It is our belief that they intend to wait until HAMP has expired and then release the deed from the trust and then foreclose, circumventing their lawful requirement to offer us a HAMP modification.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'Wells Fargo and HAMP are bound by the 2012 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] standards. they must under law review our mortgage for a HAMP modification');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4142,'10/26/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle lease','Managing the loan or lease','My wife and I are separating and we want to remove my name off her vehicle lease with Ally Financial ; however, Ally wants to impose a {$590.00} fee to do so, albeit this fee or disclosure is not in writing anywhere in the contract. I mentioned this to customer support at Ally and they stated, " yes, it is not in the contract you signed. '''' Since this is not in the contract that both parties agreed to, this is clearly a non-enforceable policy. I find this a breach of their own contract and an illegal attempt to collect money. My ex-wife can qualify on her own and does not need me as a guarantor. The lessee will remain the same with the removal of my name. No one is being added to the lease. I do not see how they can impose this fee.','ALLY FINANCIAL INC.',2.0,2.0,'ally wants to remove my name from her lease. the lessee will remain the same with the removal of my name.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4143,'10/26/2016','Bank account or service','Cashing a check without an account','Deposits and withdrawals','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] First, Assistant VP of Bank of America at their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], MO [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] branch, seized a personal check made payable to me when I tried to cash the check. Refused to give it back to me and said it was their property, not mine, because the check was written by a Bank of America account holder.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a personal check made payable to me was seized by a bank of America account holder. the check was written by a bank account holder.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4144,'10/25/2016','Debt collection','Medical','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','This complaint is against CBM Collections '' collection claim, on behalf of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], as it appears in my credit report. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] collection claim is not valid, since it is demanding payment of monies I never committed myself to pay them. I was billed for almost double the amount I was quoted for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] procedure. In 2014 I paid to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] slightly over {$300.00} for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This amount of slightly over {$300.00} was what I was quoted for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] procedure. I never contracted any responsibility to pay any extra amount [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] may wish to receive. I did not receive any additional service to justify the difference between the amount I was billed for and the amount I was quoted. Therefore, I can not accept nor submit to such claim. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] excuses the discrepancy between the amount quoted and the amount billed, because they alerted the amount quoted had to be prepaid. According to them, that meant the amount quoted was only an initial payment, but the final amount due would be anything over the amount quoted. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] explains their quote does not provide any insight of what would be the final amount due. Instead, I have pointed out that what [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] calls ''prepayment '' is actually generally referred as ''down payment ''. It only takes to look up a dictionary to understand a ''prepayment '' is a payment that needs to be completed before services are rendered. 

If [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] quote is only a statement of an initial, partial payment, but does not provide any insight of what will be the final amount due, then they need to say so. They need to clarify the quote is only a down payment, but the final amount due is undetermined. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has a very obscure and deceiving way of conducting business : they quote a very low amount to get the client ''s business, but then they bill you for a much higher amount. If the client does not submit, they ruin your credit rating. The mismatch between the terms ''prepayment '' and ''down payment '', is not accidental, but absolutely intentional. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] continues its practice of referring what is actually a ''down payment '' as a ''prepayment. 

When [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] submits its collection claim in my credit report is making a statement I am not financially responsible and do not meet my financial commitments and responsibilities. They are alerting lenders and creditors, there is a risk I may not return the money I borrow or may not pay as promised. That statement is false. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claim is false. Plain and simple : I never agreed to pay the amount [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claims I owe them. The truth is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is actually trying to rip me off and is hurting my credit as a way to coerce me. 

Please, find attached my letter of grievance to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','CB1, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'complaint against collection claim against ''compTE_ANONYMISÉ''. ''prepayment'' is a payment that needs to be completed before services are rendered.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4145,'10/25/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','My issue is three : ( 1 ) I do not believe the charges are legitimate. I have receipts indicating payments for service. ( 2 ) The bill that is claimed by the service provider is for service dating back to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014. I paid in full. Also, there were no subsequent notifications that they believed I had an outstanding balance. ( 3 ) The collections agency sent me a letter stating their position with a contact phone number. When I call the phone number, it indicates, " for the states of Texas press [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''''. When I press [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '', the automated voice service says for the state of Texas they are not accepting calls or service is not available. It then provides me a second number to call. When I call this number, the automated voice message indicates that service is not available at this time for the State of Texas and for me to call later.','TRANSWORLD SYSTEMS INC',2.0,2.0,'the collection agency sent me a letter stating their position with a contact phone number. when I call the phone number, it indicates that service is not available for the state of Texas');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4146,'10/25/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','I was redeeming rewards points for airline tickets under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] program and I was charged a {$150.00} fee for booking this travel within 21 days of the flight. At no time during the booking of the flight was I notified that there would be a charge for booking. I contacted them and they informed me that there was nothing they could do and if I failed to pay the charge they would report it on my credit report. I was also billed an additional {$22.00} for this transaction that was disclosed and agreed to.','BARCLAYS BANK DELAWARE',2.0,2.0,'a $150.00 fee was charged for booking this travel within 21 days of the flight. if I failed to pay the charge they would report it on my credit report');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4147,'10/25/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Noticed some fraudulent stuff on my credit reports and did n''t know what to do. Call and asked around everywhere I went, PD, ftc, now here said to file theft affidavit. I ''ve tried to work with this bureau but they wo n''t help. Attached is my file and let me know if you need me to do anything else.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'affidavit shows some fraudulent stuff on credit reports. PD, ftc, now here said to file theft affidavit.');
