INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4181,'10/16/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','My complaint is against Coast Professional , Inc. whom is handling a collection on behalf of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University whom I owe a student loan balance with. I originally contacted them on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 in the late afternoon and left a message at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with no call back. My second call to them was on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I spoke with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I told him that I could afford to pay {$60.00} dollars a month starting on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of each month. Unfortunately there was a problem with my debit card, so on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the payment was rejected by my bank and it was about a few days after that I my bank had notified me that they had n''t process that automatic debit, so on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called and spoke with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and told him that I would n''t be able to do the automatic payment and to cancel it and instead I would be mailing my payments to them. I have made payments on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 credit card payment, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 and mailed another {$60.00} payment on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. Yet on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 they reported me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I ''m wondering why they have done this since I have been paying the agreed upon amount and they have willing accepted my payments. I want that collection taken off my credit report. Also, I have never ever received a call from them nor have they bothered to send me any type of bill within the last two months as to what my current balance is at this time.','COAST PROFESSIONAL INC',2.0,2.0,'coast professional, Inc. is handling a collection on behalf of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] university. a complaint is against Coast Professional, Inc.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4182,'10/15/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Unsolicited issuance of credit card','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016, I received from Amazon.com & partner Chase, an unsolicited " Amazon Rewards VISA '''' credit card. As shown in the uploaded pdf files, this unlawfully issued card had a credit limit of {$6500.00}. I shredded it immediately and called Amazon customer service, who in turn referred me to Chase security. According to them, my personal information was used by a " 3rd party '''' to request the credit card. However, neither was willing to show me any proof of the information used by this so-called " 3rd party ''''. For example, they said the personal information included the answer to my security question asking for my mother ''s maiden name. I asked what the so-called 3rd party ''s answer was to that question and they could only say that it was " my name '''', which is not the established correct answer to that security question. I told each that they should be able to provide me all information used to open a credit card in my name, but they were not able ( or not willing ) to provide me any proof that it was not they who issued this unsolicited credit card. Moreover, I told them that the card came to my address, rather than the address or post office box of a so-called 3rd party ... a fact that makes no sense when a 3rd party had nothing to gain by sending the card to my address. I then contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit reporting agencies, which shared my fraud alert with the other [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit reporting agencies. Each of them provided confirmation of the alert. 
The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] document in the uploaded pdf file, shows another instance of Amazon.com and Chase issuing an unsolicited Amazon Rewards VISA for a credit limit of {$5000.00} to another consumer. Finally, the third document in the uploaded pdf file, is the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] CEO ''s recent admission that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had also been issuing unsolicited credit cards and other services. Perhaps this was an Amazon/Chase attempt to keep up with their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] competition. 
I am requesting that the CFPB require Amazon and Chase to provide to the CFPB, and to me, all information use in requesting and issuing this unsolicited credit card, in a sincere and good-faith effort to convince me that they issued this credit card based on information provided in a request by a 3rd party!','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a " 3rd party '''' asked for the credit card, a " 3rd party ''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4183,'10/15/2016','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Using a debit or ATM card','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 I used Chase " Quick Pay '''' to send {$3400.00} to a relative who is also banks with Chase. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 Chase deducted second ( duplicate ) {$3400.00} which was never authorized. My relative to whom I send the money called me on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 to notify me that a second deposit had been made to her account. 
OnXXXX at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called Chase Private Client Banking in an attempt to rectify the situation. I was told they would contact my private banker and/or branch manager at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] California ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to contact me. As of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 no one has contacted me. 
I called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number a second time and was transferred to the branch phone line which went to an voice message saying to please call back another time. 
I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a third time and was told I need to speak to a debit resolution speciality ( or some title to that effect ). The wait time to speak to said person is in excess of 30-minutes. I am unable to wait on hold that long for them to rectify a debit that was made in error on the part of Chase Bank.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'Chase deducted second ( duplicate ) $3400.00 which was never authorized. my relative called me on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COM');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4184,'10/14/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Advertising and marketing','After loosing my Camera, I call the number on the back on my card. They said my purchase is covered by purchase protection under the " accidental separation '''' clause with my Ink card. Chase They said I must file a claim at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] says under no circumstances are any " accidental separation '''' covered.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'Chase They said my purchase is covered by purchase protection under the " accidental separation '''' clause with my Ink card.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4185,'10/14/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Unsolicited issuance of credit card','I had a temporary account with Chase Bank ( set up in order to receive a payment from another Chase customer ). In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2016 I received a letter saying that a credit card application in my name was submitted on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and denied because it was a duplicate application. I never applied for this credit card. When I called Chase Bank to sort it out, I found out that there was an application submitted on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as well, and that was accepted. Again, I never applied for this. I spoke with a cust. rep and cancelled the card. And told him this was fraud. They said there would be a private investigator who would contact me, and to this day, they have n''t. The cancelled card ( which was apparently already in the mail ) came to my address. I am beginning to think that CHASE bank used my information that was in their system to fraudulently open a credit card. I have n''t had any other instances of a stolen identity or odd things reported on my credit score or in any of my other accounts since that incident.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2016 I received a letter saying that a credit card application in my name was submitted on [COMPTE_ANON');
