I subsequently called Sears/Citicorp and requested to have all the late fees waived. They were unwilling to do so, even after learning of the circumstances ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-year-old cardholder who mailed her payment nine days prior to the due date ). They were willing to waive only one month of fees, leaving me to pay {$62.00} to reduce my mother ''s balance to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
I understand that, technically, Sears/Citicorp has the right to impose these fees under their agreement with cardholders. However, I find their actions unconscionable. They have potentially damaged the credit score of an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] individual who faithfully pays her bills, and have caused her [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about the consequences. 
