INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4213,'10/07/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I own a condo in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NJ that was my primary residence and is now rented for {$1300.00} a month. Last year, there was a period of time where I lost my renter and had to make repairs to the property and I was unable to afford the mortgage payment. I then received " streamline '''' modification documents from Seterus. I met the probationary period making monthly payments of approximately {$1300.00} for three months. I was then sent the final modification documents to sign however in the interim I received a letter from the escrow department stating that my escrow was incorrect and that they would send me a letter with the new amount. I received the letter from the escrow department and it would have reduced my payment to the probationary amount of approximately {$1300.00} rather than {$1400.00} as indicated on the documents. I kindly asked for new modification documents reflecting the corrected escrow amount as that was in line with what I could afford and being they made a mistake I wanted accurate loan documents. This began in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After numerous phone calls and their recommendation to just sign the documents even though the amount was incorrect. As recent as this week, I spoke to someone stating they would look into it and put in a request for updated documents and they would get back to me. I have never gotten a response. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was served with foreclosure papers. I am only trying to have accurate loan documents reflecting the payment with the correct escrow amount that they had originally calculated incorrectly. But as is typical with large financial institutions, the right hand does not communicate with the left. I do not have money to get a lawyer and I just want to fix the situation but they said there is nothing I can do but try to reapply for a new modification which I am completing for form today on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I feel that it is wrong to recommend a borrower to sign documents that they know are incorrect. Also when I make calls I have gotten different answers from different representatives. There was no consistency. I greatly appreciate any assistance you can offer in helping me rectify this situation as I do want to keep the property. I am in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], so I am not nave to the process, however I think the OCC would criticize us if we did n''t have correct documents and the Bank recommended the consumer to just sign the documents knowing the payment is incorrect.','Seterus, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a condo in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is now rented for $1300.00 a month. the condo was my primary residence and was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4214,'10/07/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','My daughter neglected to pay her first three months of her SallieMae student loans that I had co-signed on. Once I became aware of this I immediately called SallieMae to pay the delinquent loans in full and pay them forward until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My credit score has been between [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the past 15 years. The delinquent loans ruined my credit, my score is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I am trying to refinance my home to consolidate these loans at a 3.6 % interest rate, rather than the 9 % current loan rate with SallieMae. I contacted them on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] asking them to send my Credit Union a letter on their letterhead explaining that I immediately paid the delinquent loans off and forward till XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and to note that they were in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] rather than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], delinquent status. They told me that they would be mailing this out to me the following week. I was shocked that it could not be e-mailed to me and that I would have to wait for it to be ''snail mailed! '''' They apologized for the inconvenience but would not email it to me. I made the request over the phone on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I called SallieMea to ask if it had been sent and they said it went out on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 12 days after my request! This absurd " snail mail '''' delay is holding up my opportunity to do a rapid reassessment of my credit score and re-finance my home. I called them again to ask if they would remove the delinquent payments from my records ( because I had paid them immediately once I found out they were delinquent, and paid them up until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). The customer service agent with SallieMae told me to write a letter and send it to them via the postal service i.e. " snail mail '''' then they would have up to 30 days to reply! This is completely unacceptable customer service! I have no recourse but to do this and wait? What if they deny the request? Then I will have waited six weeks ( two weeks for it to get to the appropriate person and up to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to answer and send it back to me ) to see if they will approve this request? What kind of customer service is this? Why ca n''t these requests be expiated by electronic correspondence? I find this antiquated and troubling. I am trying to refinance my home and repay these loans, they are slowing the process to a sloth crawl! This is unacceptable and should be changed. It is XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we do n''t do important time sensitive transactions via snail mail when we have e-mail. Please let me know how you might help. Thanks you','SLM CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'my daughter was unable to pay her first three months of her SallieMae student loans. she called them to pay the delinquent loans in full and pay them forward');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4215,'10/06/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Disclosure verification of debt','I did not receive notification from the debt collector ALLIED COLLECTION SERVICE for a bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This was placed on my credit report without my knowledge or ability to pay before it was reported. I just received my first communication with a debt collector, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. They stated that this debt had not been reported to any credit agency and was not on my credit report. ( I settled the account and paid it in full on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ).','Allied Collection Services, Inc. (Nevada)',2.0,2.0,'debt collector ALLIED COLLECTION SERVICE received a bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. this was placed on my credit report without my knowledge or');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4216,'10/06/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I was called last year informing me that I am eligible for student loan consolidation. posed as a government organization they informed me all of my loans would be consolidated. Instead all they did was get all my information and pay a third party to fill out a student loan consolidation application when I could have done it on my own for free. all in all my loans did not get consolidated and I went on fedloan.gov today and completed the application myself.','Equitable Acceptance Corporation',2.0,2.0,'fedloan.gov gave me information about all of my loans. all in all my loans did not get consolidated.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4217,'10/06/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Experian continues to report a fraudulent & unverifiable account on my credit report. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should be removed from my report. I ''ve disputed this account numerous times with Experian, requested the method of verification & additionally sent a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter to the data furnisher requesting a signed contract/agreement. Neither the data furinsher nor Experian have provided me with a signed contract of my obligation but they continue to claim this has been verified. When reviewing my file here are some facts which question the integrity of their investigation. The address linked to this account is n''t even listed on my credit file. I ''ve requested the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account be removed 3 times but they continue to verify it. Secondly, when I ask them to verify it they always pass the buck & say it ''s the data furnishers responsibility to update their records. This public information which is damaging my name & reputation & I ''m unable to get any financing due to the nature of this issue. This matter is also causing unwanted emotional & financial stress & I ''d like this unverifiable account removed immediately. If Experian continues to claim they ''ve verified this account again without a deeper investigation I will be filing a lawsuit for violations of the FCRA. Please resolve this matter.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'''comPTE_ANONYMISÉ'' should be removed from my report. ''i disputed this account numerous times with Experian, requested the method of verification');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4218,'10/06/2016','Payday loan',NULL,'Can''t contact lender','The company ''s website does not give a clear concise history of principal and interest paid. I did not always get payment confirmations, which is the only way to see how your P & I payment was applied, the customer portal does not provide such details. I made a significant payment ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of outstanding balance ) and my P & I structure did not change. I sent two messages stating this and NEVER received any response. I fear that I was overcharged interest but they will not respond.The company ''s website does not enable consumer to track outstanding balance on a regular basis. I fear that I have been overcharged! It seems that this is on purpose to keep consumer ignorant and make sure we are not able to see any errors or mistakes on the company ''s part. This leave open ample room for fraud! I sent messages to the lender communicating this fear multiple time and no reply in over three months. I believe there maybe fraudulent activity on their part!','CURO Intermediate Holdings',2.0,4.0,'the company''s website does not enable consumer to track outstanding balance on a regular basis. I fear that I have been overcharged interest but they will not respond.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4219,'10/06/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Improper contact or sharing of info','The company IC systems contacted my employer and shared debt information with them. The company is continuing to hit my credit report with hard inquiries each month.','I.C. System, Inc.',10.0,10.0,'IC systems contacted my employer and shared debt information with them. the company is continuing to hit my credit report with hard inquiries each month.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4220,'10/05/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit monitoring or identity protection','I attempted to open an online CD account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ... I had trouble w/their web site, called them ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) got hung up on & locked out of my account before it was established. I was abused w/ " security questions '''' then more by EXPERION ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) these were questions from over 20 years ago ( where did I live 20 years ago ... .street address ) I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] do n''t remember the number, who would? my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sored, I got [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from disbelief on how I was being treated, no other bank/financial ever put me through this ... .and they ask for is your social security # too much!, I had identity theft because of a bank, this is security abuse and out of controll. Experion has WRONG info, OLD, outdated info & are unresponsive, profiteering & should be put out of business, they also make me carry my X-husbands credit info on my report from 20+ years ago! disriminatory/unfair! [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is over kill/abusive in security .... banking/financials/credit reporting/security is OUT of CONTROLL & WRONG! ... [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a bank has a''secure'' info, OLD, outdated info & should be put out of business. experion has''stupid'' info');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4221,'10/05/2016','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Ditech has not paid my town taxes from my escrow account, I have over {$3000.00} due and have had a open claim under investigation since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Have spoke. To [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] seperate supervisors, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and most recently [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'ditech has not paid my town taxes from my escrow account. I have over $3000.00 due and have had a claim under investigation.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4222,'10/05/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letters to Experian ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 30 day apart ) concerning inaccurate information on my report concerning bankruptcy. I ask Experian to provide me with copies of any documentation associated with this account, bearing my signature. In the absence of any such documentation bearing my signature, I formally request that this information be immediately deleted from the credit file you maintain under my Social Security number. I received a letter on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 stating that they have previously processed this dispute and the credit grantor has verified its accuracy. Last but not least, they said that unless you send us additional relevant information to support your claim, WE WILL NOT REINVESTIGATE THIS INFORMATION AGAIN. EXPERIAN has not providing me with copies of documentation bearing my signature in a timely manner. Thank you for your help.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'letters to experian concerning inaccurate information on bankruptcy. I ask Experian to provide me with copies of any documentation associated with this account, bearing my signature. in the absence of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4223,'10/05/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I have written previously and will continue to report JP Morgan Chase until we receive a satisfactory resolution. This is in reference of account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Virginia [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in my father ''s name, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I am authorized to discuss this account. 
JP Morgan Chase is the sorriest excuse for a mortgage company. Several years ago we started the process to obtain a loan modification. Of course we were unsuccessful trying it on our own so we hired an attorney to assist us and JP Morgan Chase had requested the same documents from us over and over again which we have sent EVERY document that was requested of us numerous times and in a timely manner. They told us numerous times that they did not receive them and requested them again and again. Evidently they sat somewhere on someone desk and did not get processed as they should have. This has been reported before by other mortgage holders with them and JP Morgan Chase has even been fined several times for such. 
Then they basically accused me of lying when I told them that after calling in and making several monthly temporary payments in a row, which we were set up for, one month I called to make the next payment and the person told me that she " could not take the payment because our account was under review for a loan modification '''', ( well duh, that is why they were temporary payments ) I even gave them the name of the person that told me that and the telephone number that I called so it can be researched since their calls are " recorded for quality assurance and training '''' but obviously no one even cares to research any of what I have been reporting over and over again. 
They said that my father whose name the loan is under did not reside at the property so that was a reason why they denied the request. That was not true at the time of the request. 
There is no reason why we could not have been approved for a loan modification to safe our home. We even paid off the second mortgage on the property but that did n''t even seem to matter or account for anything. 
The property was scheduled for foreclosure but a representative from JP Morgan Chase told our attorney at the time that the sale was postponed because they were going to review the modification again per the request of our attorney but they still proceeded with the sale anyway. It should have never happened. 
They claim to want to help their customers save their homes but they did not do a single thing to help us save our home and foreclosed on our home leaving me homeless. 
The attached document is a prime example of how they treated us during our request for a simple loan modification. They claim that they did not have the information regarding the account which first of all was in the report and I also sent it twice, I sent it to the addresses that they provided me to send it to. Coincidence that they have not received any of the pertinent documents that they need from me when all I wanted to was for them help me save my home? Why would I have not sent any of this in? 
How ridiculous that they can continue to treat customers like this and remain in business.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage company has been fined several times for a loan modification. the company has been contacted by other mortgage holders. the company has been fined several times for the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4224,'10/05/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Identity theft / Fraud / Embezzlement','I ''m a 20+ year Bank of America credit card holder and have always been in good standing, used my account/card and made payment as agreed. 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was charged {$1800.00} for an online transaction with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] based [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and XX/XX/2020 the transaction was charged back in my favor, first by Claims Dept ( as if a Dispute ), then by Fraud Dept. 
My card ( ended [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) was then cancelled and a number card issued ( ended [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). 
On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Bank of America realized that a " double charge back '''' had taken place and the Claims Dept charged my account {$1800.00} -- therefore my card status was that a fraudulent transaction had taken place and I owned {$0.00} specific to the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] transaction. 
Then twenty days later ( on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), Claims Department charged my new card ( ended [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) the {$1800.00} and mailed me a form letter ( received on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) stating that Bank of America had obtained documentation from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I had ordered and received the subject merchandise, therefore I should be obligated to pay the full {$1800.00}. 
So I contacted the merchant, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], directly on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and learned from Customer Service Representative, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that she found evidence on my account that a remote operator ( supposedly working on behalf of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had made a " alternate delivery request '''' to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] changing the shipping address to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a person in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] network named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had changed the ordering party ''s e-mail address from " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' to my e-mail address " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' ( after I had filed a complaint about a package arriving unexpectedly at my doorstep but for which I had NOT ordered! ) I was e-mailed a copy of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] History where it clearly shows that the XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] item costing {$1800.00} was NOT shipped and delivered to me at my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], California residence. 
To be clear, I have never done business before with this [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] based merchant, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or any subsidiaries and affiliates, they would NOT have my name/billing/credit card information on file, nor am I on their mailing list, etc. 
When I reported all of this updated information to Bank of America, they said nothing could be done by the Claims Department, that this was a matter for Fraud Department to handle. Then I called Fraud and they said this transaction was a valid dispute between two parties and that the Claims Department would have to resolve it! 
In closing, I have never before failed a complaint with the CFPB, nor had reason to complain about what has been a 33+ year relationship with Bank of America . 
In writing this -- I would like to be very clear -- Bank of America ''s Credit Card Customer Service has dramatically deteriorated in recent years and can even been traced to their massive acquisition of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It now takes 20-40+ minutes to speak with live customer representatives, supervisor elevation is no longer real time, and there are unworkable " silos '''' between Credit Card departments ( Claims vs. Fraud ) leaving the consumer account holder at risk and completely unable to resolve. ( I even involved my local Bank of America branch manager and he was told the same thing -- it ''s valid claim, not fraud. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] needs to pay his bills and do n''t get involved, pass on helping him! ) I would like the CFPB to ask Bank of America to resolve this matter and also to investigate in good faith whether the involved merchant, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], knowingly and willfully provided misleading information to Bank of America on or near XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] claiming the subject transaction had been ordered by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and physically received by him when the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] History and internal [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] transaction notes proved otherwise -- even hinting at internal fraud! 
Respectfully Submitted, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'a 20+ year bank of America credit card holder was charged $1800.00 for an online transaction with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] based [');
