Original Balance : {$22000.00} Unpaid Interest : {$1900.00} Current Balance : {$27000.00} ( The balance based on the Original Balance and Unpaid Interest should be {$24000.00} not {$27000.00}. ( Where did this additional {$3000.00} charge come from? ) There are numerous unexplained charges like this. Approximately a year ago my balance was {$150000.00} then it went to {$180000.00} without any actual explanation. 

All this documentation is attached to the complaint. 
I have made all monthly payments, and will continue to do so, but I do not understand how FedLoan Servicing, is racking up phantom charges and interest. I fully intend to pay what is owed, and what I borrowed for school, but there is currently about {$40000.00} of unexplained charges, which interest is being applied to. 

I would appreciate any help CFPB could provide me to ensure that these balances are correct. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a year ago my balance was $150000.00 then it went to $180000.00 without any actual explanation. a year ago my balance was ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4312,'09/14/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my mortgage company received my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mortgage payment. They reversed the payment and applied to the principal because as they explained I could not be ahead due to my bankruptcy. They never notified me of their actions. I continued to pay every month. At the end of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when my bankruptcy was over I get this call asking for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment which I had just paid. As we argued the gentleman stated I had bounced my payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After investigating the matter they found they had not serviced the account correctly however they refused to correct their error. I was not ahead I was on time. I have been charged late fees which they collected from the extra amount I was sending to apply to the principal. Instead of reversing the payment that they applied incorrectly and making current, they now are offering to accept a short sale or I can sign my house to them in lieu of foreclosure. The bank in question is Select Portfolio.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,2.0,'mortgage company received my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] mortgage payment. they reversed the payment and applied to the principal. they now offer to accept a short');
