INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4319,'09/12/2016','Mortgage','Other mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I have recently submitted a compliant about Specialized Loan Servicing purchasing insurance on my behalf ( illegal in New Jersey ) when they already had copies of my insurance dec pages ( both flood and hazard ). SLS responded to CFPB with a letter stating that the insurance they had purchased was cancelled and I would not be charged. I have just received a letter from SLS ( dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 ) giving me notification that my escrow account was being charged for insurance that they already reported to CFPB that was cancelled. They had no right to purchase insurance on my behalf in the first place as they already had proof of insurance on file. So which is it? Is SLS charging my escrow account for insurance or did they cancel? I was told by the CFPB rep to file another complaint as the last compliant ( case # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) was supposedly resolved and obviously is not since SLS is still trying to charge my escrow account for the insurance.','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,2.0,'a compliant has been submitted about specialized loan Servicing purchasing insurance on my behalf. the insurance they had purchased was cancelled and they would not be charged. the esc');
