INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4329,'09/09/2016','Debt collection','Credit card','Disclosure verification of debt','After pulling a copy of my credit report I noticed that Cavalry Portfolio is reporting that I owed them {$1800.00}. I have never done any business with this company and have never owe anyone that amount of money. So on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I mailed a certify letter to Cavalry Portfolio informing them that I am disputing the debt that they say that I owe, provide me with any papers that show that I agree to pay them. I also requested validation of the so called debt and ask them to delete and stop reporting false information to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] major credit reporting agencies. 

On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016, I received a letter from Cavalry Portfolio claiming that my letter is lacking in any specific information and therefore they can not investigate my claim and that I will hear from them within 90 days from the date of their letter. This is a clear FCRA violation, I should get this information within 30 days of my letter. I mailed a second request on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 and its now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016. I have yet to receive any proof from Cavalry Portfolio that I owe any debt to them and the company is still reporting to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] major credit bureaus that I owe them. 

