INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4340,'09/07/2016','Debt collection','Medical','Disclosure verification of debt','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 I was notified through credit monitoring that I had a collection in the amount of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on my credit profile from Fox Collection. Prior to seeing this on my report I had no idea of who this company was and why were they on my report. After I looked the company up and contacted them they advised me that I owed them [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from a past due medical bill that I was not aware of. After a lengthy conversation I was told that they had the right to put it on my report even with me not being aware of the bill. She said that they mailed a bill to me in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I probably did not read it because it was not labeled from an collection agency. I am trying to find out is it fair practice to make only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] attempt to communicate with a customer and then place it on their credit profile. I have no problem paying the bill if they are willing to take it off of my credit profile because truly they made no attempts to contact me to make me aware of the bill.','Professional Recovery Management',2.0,2.0,'a collection of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was mailed to me by a collection agency. the company told me that they had the right to put it');
