INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4348,'09/03/2016','Bank account or service','Cashing a check without an account','Making/receiving payments, sending money','Brother wrote a check for money owed. Went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where he does business to cash the check. They took my license, put my thumb print on the check told me they were going to charge me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for cashing the check. Then refused to cash it with out authorization from the person that wrote the check to me. This is a very unfair practice and I have never been so embarrassed and they were very nasty. Is this the banks normal practice If you have all the I.D . and Thumb print that should be enought.','Synovus Bank',2.0,2.0,'Brother wrote a check for money owed. he did business to cash the check. he refused to cash it with out authorization from the person who wrote it.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4349,'09/03/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','XX/XX/2012 I was offered a Special Direct Consolidation Loan opportunity with the US Dept of Ed for which I accepted. I was promised a lower interest rate with this consolidation which I was eager to do since my lowest loan had a rate below 2 %. However, this consolidation excluded these lower interest rate loans thereby not fulfilling the promise this US Dept of Ed consolidation offered stated here : How this benefits you : One servicer and one payment, rather than multiple bills and multiple payment addresses. 

Potential lower combined payment amount that ''s based on a lower interest rate and the repayment plan selected. 

Up to 0.50 % interest rate reduction! Earn a 0.25 % reduction on the loans you consolidate and another 0.25 % rate reduction if you enroll in automatic debit. 

Lock in a lower fixed interest rate automatically on any of your loans with a variable interest rate. 

Same loan terms and conditions, including your eligibility for the same deferment and repayment relief options. 

Potential for Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program eligibility if you meet specific program requirements. 


Instead, the lower interest rate loans were kept at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], only the higher rated loans were consolidated thereby making me have over {$30000.00} in interest in just 4 years after this consolidation. This offer has actually increased my interest due and NOT HELPED ME AT ALL. 

This is my complaint. Not sure why it was rejected before or why such little time is afforded to respond. Thank you for your help.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'XX/XX/2012 was offered a special direct consolidation loan with the US Dept of Ed. this consolidation excluded these lower interest rate loans.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4350,'09/02/2016','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Problems when you are unable to pay','I had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my car and regretfully, I took out only a small {$400.00} loan with Sunset Finance to help with living expenses. Big mistake. Now, it ''s not so much the money but now the principal of the matter in how this company manages their loans and customer service. Sunset Finance reps have been nothing but a nuisance by contacting me, my friends, colleagues and family excessively, sometimes twice a day triple-dialing my both home and office phones where they had exploited my reference/emergency contact list with unethical collection practices. This happened so much that I was forced to seek legal counsel and they advised me to create a " cease and desist '''' letter. 

I was making payments of $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month to Sunset Finance and 5 of those payments totaling {$470.00} have been paid back despite nearly paying back MORE than double what I borrowed which I came to find out had a ridiculously high interest rate like 86 % or more. I have tried to contact Sunset and emailed them requesting to negotiate a better rate or a reasonable payment but no response or they will not accept a payment other than their choosing versus what I can afford. I even enrolled in Consumer Credit Counseling Service and included Sunset Finance to help pay them back but they DO NOT accept payments from Consumer Credit Counseling which I do not understand. 

Now they have filed a false statement to the court and filed a lawsuit against me stating " defendant received loan on XX/XX/2015 and refuses to pay. '''' and that is not true. I have paid back Sunset over {$400.00} back.','Sunset Management, Inc',2.0,2.0,'Sunset Finance reps have been a nuisance by contacting me, my friends, colleagues and family. they have been contacted by me and their reps. they have filed ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4351,'09/02/2016','Consumer Loan','Title loan','Received a loan I didn''t apply for','onemain is on my credit report as a hardpull i have never applied with them so when i called the place to check on this the man that answered said that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was the one that caused this and he just had another person with the same issue ... i said no matter what your name is on my credit report and i wanted it pulled off ... it got nowhere i called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they do n''t even have me on there records ... funny thing the onemain had my file and i did n''t even apply with them because he brought up a account of mine and asked what that was about ... i just want the hard pull off my report as i already have a id fraud issue going on and have to do all the foot work myself..after 53 years of raising my kids with just a bank account and debit card i apply for credit and see a whole bunch of id fraud..and people wonder why i never wanted credit ... lol here is the info, ONEMAIN FINANCIAL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], TX [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','ONEMAIN FINANCIAL HOLDINGS, LLC.',2.0,4.0,'onemain is on my credit report as a hardpull. i have never applied with them so when i called the place to check on this the man who answered said that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4352,'09/02/2016','Mortgage','VA mortgage','Application, originator, mortgage broker','This letter is to complain about the ill treatment that I ''ve received from US Bank when I applied for a refinance of my original home mortgage that I had with them. I was lied to about how much I could refinance my home for. The original loan was a VA loan which guarantees the loan [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] %. I ''m a service-connected [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] veteran. I was told by US Bank Rep that the VA only allowed a refinance of only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of the market value of my home. I thought this was strange so I contacted the VA and they told me that statement was not true. They gave me a link to go and said share it with the lender. The link stated that VA guarantees [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of new purchase and refinance if the veteran is credit worthy. When I mention this to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at US Bank she then said it was " company policy '''' not to lend more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of the market value on refinances. Yet, the VA was still guaranteeing [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] %. I sacrificed my life for OUR country and was injured in the process. Yet, US Bank felt the need to restrict my benefit and hold me down. For what reason??? The only reason I feel this was down is because of my race, gender, marital status, age, and zip code. When the Rep did not change her position on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % after I reminded her that VA guarantees [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] %, I realized something was not right. I told her that I no longer desired to do business with US Bank. Then I get a letter in the mail which really angered me. It was from US Bank and it stated that they was denying my request to refinance my home loan due to " Lack of Collateral ''''. This made no sense at all. My home is my collateral. Luckily for me, I found a financial institution that refinanced my home loan, a few days ago, at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % and I even received a better interest rate. I did n''t have to pay any additional fees either. They only looked at the market value of my home and my ability to repay the loan. They would have also paid for the appraisal if US Bank had not already made me pay for it. And, they honored my service to this country which I ''ve helped to defend so that they could do business. No one came up with some arbitrary [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % to try to exclude me from a benefit that I earned and deserved.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a letter from the bank rep says the VA only allowed a refinance of only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of the market value of my home');
