INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4358,'08/31/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I was denied a loan due to an erroneous collection on my credit report. My bank informed me of this collection on my credit report from ERC from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the amount of {$410.00}. I was never contacted by phone, mail, or email by them about any money I owed. When I tried to call the number listed on the credit report it was not a valid number. I decided to search on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it showed many claims of fraud. I do not have any outstanding bills for this amount and do not owe them money. As this is causing negative marks on my credit, I would like for this to be completely removed from all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit bureaus, promptly. I have an attorney that is ready to represent me with a law suit if this is not taken care of. These negative marks have caused me to be denied for a loan. I want this taken care! 
I have disputed this account over and over and never get validation or proper documentation. TAKE THIS OFF MY CREDIT!!!','ERC',2.0,4.0,'a bank informed me of this collection on my credit report from ERC. my bank informed me of this collection on my credit report. I was never contacted by phone, mail');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4359,'08/31/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I have unauthorized credit inquiries on my Experian Credit report Experian [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'experian credit report has unauthorized credit inquiries. unauthorized credit inquiries on experian credit report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4360,'08/31/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I have been a cardholder with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for over 10 years. I have never missed a payment. 
I was in the hospital during the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in 2015 and had someone send in my payment. 
Due to an electronic error the payment was never made. I received no email notice, no phone call or no US Mail notice that I was late in making my payment. Previously, if I had been a few days late ( never 30 days ) I was always called by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as the payment date was misleading. I assumed that if you were not 30 days late you were safe. In fact, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] went so far as to reversing late fee ''s that were charged to me due to the fact I paid a couple of days after the due date ( Again, no 30 days ). I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they were insistent that they were right and I was wrong. Again, computer error. I stand by my record as never having had a late payment in 10 years. I am asking them to remove this late payment from my credit report. 

In addition, I was denied a credit limit increase due to this one late payment. In addition I am receiving credit offers from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] regarding approval for a car loan of up to {$35000.00}. Does not make sense ... ... ... ....','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'cardholder was in the hospital during the month of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in 2015. he received no email notice, no phone call or no US Mail');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4361,'08/31/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','There are negative items listed on my credit report that are false. I do not owe these companies ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) any money. I want the negative items removed immediately. I have disputed this information with Experian several times, and they have not removed the false information. They also would not let place a statement on my credit report refuting these lies. Why are credit reporting agencies allowed to lie, and I have no recourse against them?','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'negative items listed on my credit report are false. I do not owe these companies any money.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4362,'08/30/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I took out a {$10000.00} [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan to aid in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] interview travel in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with a payment term of 240 months. I fell behind in repayment in the mid to late residency and fellowship training. Upon completion of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and entry in into the medical work- force, this loan was paid in earnest completing repayment in full XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] well under half of the loan original repayment term. This loan was repaid through the same servicer, Navient, as my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] other federal loans. It was repaid first. I noticed that as I repaid each of the other loans their status on the website changed to " paid in full '''' from " in repayment. '''' The aforementioned [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not make this change. It continues to be listed as in repayment. I have discussed the the customer service representatives from Navient in an effort to determine why this loan was listed as in repayment, furthermore, I have noticed that this loan has been listed in my credit reports as closed as a write off in excess of {$12000.00} dollars whereas all other loans that were subsequently paid in full are listed as closed and paid in full. This is negatively impacting my credit. 

I have contacted the customer service at Navient on multiple occasions each time with the same outcome, the Customer serice representative s ( CSRs ) of Navient for the division that works with the website and federal loans explain that they have no role in private loans and the CSRs in the private loan division state that they have no control over the way the loan is listed on Navient ''s website. On my second attempt to discuss the website listing the loan as ''in repayment, '' the CSR reported to me that both of here supervisors refused to speak to me when I appealed for there assistance with this issue that had proven too complex for the CSRs and then the line suddenly became disconnected. 

As the issue issue above appears on my credit report as a derogatory mark, I have requested the CSRs from Navient ''s private loan division to send a letter documenting what they reported to me the found on the phone -- that the loan repayment was complete and paid in full. When I received the letter it was dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it stated, " On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we received the final payment of {$1.00} for the private student loan referenced above. Once the funds clear, we ''ll consider the loan to be paid in full and will notify the consumer reporting agencies of the updated status. '''' Thus, after 18 months this {$1.00} payment remains pending clearance and despite the assertions by Navient CSRs the the loan is repaid in full their websites, official communications and reports the the credit bureaus are not reflecting this. I do not understand how this {$1.00} payment has remained uncleared and in limbo fo this long and am requesting assistance as this error has impacted me financially in a negative fashion and I have been unable to get it addressed via Navients Customer service system.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a 240-month loan was repaid through the same servicer, Navient. it was repaid in earnest completing repayment in full XX/X');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4363,'08/30/2016','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','I was automatically converted from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Costco card to a Citibank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I received no communication from either company, other than a termination letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and a welcome packed from Citibank. The welcome packet contained the terms of the card, which clearly state that there are 12 months interest free on all purchases. There is no fine print stating that is not the case when the card was converted from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and there was no communication from Citibank that they would not be honoring their own agreement that was sent to their new customers. Talk about starting off a new relationship on the wring foot. As a consumer, I feel cheated and that Citibank purposely misrepresented this information to their customers to incite purchases for which they never intented to honor interest free promotions. This is a classic bait and switch marketing technique that should not be allowed. This is illegal and predatory behavior. I envision a class action suit in the near future for this and other woes encountered when the cards were transferred without consumer consent and any type of honest communication about the terms of the new agreement. Citibank should be ashamed of these practices, did these institutions learn nothing from the collapse they caused barely less than a decade ago??? I contacted customer service of course, and was granted relief on ONE month ''s interest. But that does not help me because I had planned to pay off this balance over the 12 months I was promised. So now I will be incurring interest this entire year that will perpetuate the cycle of debt. Way to go, Citibank! You duped even a responsible financial customer.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'Citibank was automatically converted from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Costco card to a Citibank [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card back');
