INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4376,'08/26/2016','Prepaid card','Other special purpose card','Fees','After successfully using rebates from merchants for years, I recently had the unfortunate experience of receiving several American Express prepaid reward cards as rebates. 

The company is at least misleading in understating that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] monthly service fees will be charged after 5 months from issue. There is no legitimate reason for a monthly fee. All notification of such fees is in minuscule print at page bottom or on the back of the card. It also says funds do not expire immediately after the monthly fee description. Why is that there other than to confuse or mislead consumers? 

I had cards of {$10.00}, {$15.00}, and {$50.00}. After trying to check balances, I learned the first [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] cards were at {$0.00} and the latter was at {$44.00}. So I ultimately used ( received ) {$44.00} of {$75.00} in rebates because I was misled by the obvious expiration date on the cards ( 5 years from issuance ) and the " hidden '''' fees descriptor. 

After checking all the sources I could, it seems these rebates are considered " free '''' money and so there is no recourse that I can detect. 

I feel like AmEx mislead me from fully utilizing my rebates. Maybe it is free money for these unscrupulous banks, but not me. 

I do not believe banks should be allowed to deduct service fees on rebate cards. There is no justification for a passive fee. They are not managing the money. 

If they are deducting monthly service fees as if I had an account with them, then I should be notified as the fees are deducted just as if I were a bank customer. That is how they are treating these prepaid reward cards. 

People should be made aware that there are fees associated with rebate reward cards and these unscrupulous banks should be made accountable.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a rebate card is a rebate card that is not a rebate. the company is misleading in understating that a monthly fee will be charged after 5 months. the company');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4377,'08/25/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Problems when you are unable to pay','I was released from my teniored job last year and informed Navy Federal. I continued to make payments throughout this year as I could. I was then referred to a special collections department who allowed me to make small payments to show effort until my full time job started at the end of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My collections specialist [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was in an accident and a schedule check payment was unable to be stopped but was rectified by an ACH transfer later that week before the returned check. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] our account was placed for repossession and picked up the same night. Tuesday we called into Navy Federal and they explained it was because of bounced payment checks after having our Collections Rep explain the accidental submittal we were directed to another department. That department is Fiance Management. An agent by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] she said in department ) took an application for deferment through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016. We accepted the terms and awaited the Repossession division of Navy Fed to send a release so we can pick up our car at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Two days have passed and they refuse phone calls or to provide documentation of said agreement. The repossession department has told the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] not to even speak to my fianc that I had relinquished rights to speak on my account on every occasion and that they are refusing to release the car even with the deferrement showing a zero balance due and only the repossession fees to be paid at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It is my belief they are intentionally holding my vehicle to either remand custody or to rack up fees as punishment as they have continually reprimanded me as if I was their child and dehumanizing me with their lack of action. I rely on this car and have been very corporative through the whole process even before the repossession. No one at Navy Federal says they have authority to protect my consumer rights I just have to wait it out. This is inexcusable and has put my family in a downward spiral.','NAVY FEDERAL CREDIT UNION',2.0,2.0,'a collection department allowed me to make small payments to show effort. my collection specialist was in an accident and a schedule check payment was unable to be stopped. the repossession');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4378,'08/25/2016','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Managing the loan or lease','Advance Financial has automatically debited my account for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments on another persons account. I helped this person out previously by paying her payment. However, I was never co-signer and I am not responsible for her account. Without my permission they have withdrawn [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments on 1 day for her account. I would like to know if there is anything I can do against this. at this point they are saying they can refund me in 3-5 business days, but in that time i have bills due.','Harpeth Financial Services, LLC',2.0,2.0,'Advance Financial has automatically debited my account for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments on another persons account. without my permission they have withdrawn [COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4379,'08/25/2016','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Deposits and withdrawals','I use the First Data Money Network card for my paycheck to be directly deposited. This card was furnished to me by my work. I am applying for a mortgage and I need to get statements showing the money that I put away as well as my usual cash flow. For the last 2 days, every number that I call gives me a message that they ''re experiencing technical difficulties and to try again later. 

I am running into deadlines and I ca n''t keep pushing this back. I need proof on paper of my money, and I need the people in control of my money to be accessible. There needs to be some recourse. I ''m at my wits end attempting to get ahold of anybody at all at this company.','First Data Corporation',4.0,4.0,'first data money network card is a personal loan application. it is a personal loan and is a mortgage. it is a personal loan.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4380,'08/25/2016','Other financial service','Debt settlement','Fraud or scam','Student loan scam. Signed up after they promised to eliminate my interest, get out of default, and get a fixed payment. Realized after that I was scammed, give credit card info for preliminary payments. Was supposed to receive paperwork in the mail, never got it. They call themselves Student Loan Relief Program, called Manhattan Beach Venture LLC when they tried to withdraw money from my account. Luckily, it did n''t work and I ''m not sure why ... .not sure what to do next.','Manhattan Beach Venture, LLC',2.0,2.0,'student loan scammers promised to eliminate my interest, get out of default, and get a fixed payment. they called themselves Student Loan Relief Program, called Manhattan Beach Venture LLC.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4381,'08/24/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Ditech Financial did not notify me of any change in my required mortgage payment, as required by my mortgage agreement. I sent timely payments in for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] & [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 & these checks were cashed by Ditech. There was an adjustment in my adjustable mortgage ( {$16.00} increase per month ) which Ditech failed to notify me of at any time. Ditech reported these [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments as " 30 days past due '''', thereby ruining my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] score, and failed to correct their error when I requested that they do so. ( Ditech at no time ever sent me any coupon books or monthly mortgage statements, or invoices, despite my request for these ). 
Ditech also refused to refund an over payment I made to them relative to a payment which they deposited some time after my mortgage was paid off in full in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016, and to return these funds which legally belong to me','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'Ditech Financial did not notify me of any change in my required mortgage payment. there was an adjustment in my adjustable mortgage ( $16.00 increase per month. Ditech');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4382,'08/24/2016','Debt collection','Credit card','Improper contact or sharing of info','We represent a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] senior of limited financial means. On his behalf, we sent a letter to this creditor requesting no further contact of any kind. The creditor has continued to send monthly statements and demand letters to our client at his home address. By continuing to communicate with our client directly rather than through us and after receiving his request for no further communication, the creditor is violating Section 805 ( a ) ( 2 ) and Section 805 ( c ) of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'creditor is violating section 805 (a) and section 805 (c) of the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4383,'08/24/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','A branch specialist at Citibank made an unauthorized teller withdrawal on my checking and savings account. I filed a fraud claim with Citibank, but they denied it due to a lack of evidence and said the decision can not be appealed. They also can not further investigate the matter because the branch in question is now permanently closed. If Citibank would pull up the security footage of the incident, it would clearly show that I was n''t present for any teller withdrawal and did n''t withdraw any money. What other options do I have to recover my money?','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'branch specialist at Citibank made an unauthorized teller withdrawal on my savings account. he filed a fraud claim with the branch, but they denied it due to a lack of');
