INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4396,'08/20/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Settlement process and costs','This is just an inquiry about mortgage insurance. I had a financial gift from a friend to purchase a house and in the interest of keeping my monthly payment low, my most important criteria, I opted to pay the mortgage ins up front, lump sum, so it would n''t be added to my monthly bill. I was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and it was my first home purchase, in 2014. I did this solo with no outside assistance, and though my intellect is good, financials make my eyes cross. Aside from that, everything is done so quickly, it ''s hard to grasp what is actually happening. I opted to buy it up front, in the amount of {$4000.00}, thinking this would cover me for a few years until my record was established, and though they did ask me more than once if I was sure I wanted to do this, I do n''t know if consequences of this decision were relayed to me. I do know nobody said this was not a wise decision, that I would likely end up losing more than I was getting. When my mortgage was sold after about a year, that money vanished. I ''m sure my mortgage insurance payments would not have been $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 12-18 months, and mortgage ins never came up with the next mortgage company. When I refinanced with a different company, I was told that money was gone. I ''m just wondering if there ''s any possibility of recouping a portion of these funds. If not, I have to accept that, but it seemed, at least in hindsight, that this was an area in which I was taken advantage of, being a novice in this situation. Thank you.','ACADEMY MORTGAGE CORPORATION',8.0,8.0,'a friend bought a house and paid the mortgage ins up front, lump sum. it wouldn''t be added to my monthly bill, so it would n''');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4397,'08/19/2016','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','I purchased furniture through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It totaled [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was asked if I wanted 12 months financing at 0 % interest. I agreed. I made all payments on time. At the end of 12 months I had a balance. The Wells Fargo credit card did not bill me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month, which, when I calculate it, should have paid off the entire balance in 12 months. Instead they only billed me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month. Now I receive a bill for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which includes interest of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of the balance. If I was informed at the time of purchase that the 0 % interest was deferred and that I had to make higher payments this past 12 months to pay off the balance in 12 months, I would have. There interest rate after 12 months is 28.24 %. I am now subjected to pay this full amount. I have a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit rating and could have paid this off in full to begin with and have several credits cards with lower interest. I was mislead by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Wells Fargo and believe that these fees are fraudulent. This should have been explained to me up front.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a credit card did not bill me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/month. it did not bill me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
