This problem has been going on since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Ditech lacks the competence and knowledge to correct their own problem and the only way I find out they are padding their profits and books is by me closely watching my balance. The amount of {$5200.00} plus the almost {$2000.00} needs to be reapplied back into my account, plus interest since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I also want an written explanation of what caused the problem, what they have done to correct it, why the actual dollar amount ( {$5200.00} ) was added to my balance, where the {$2000.00} escrow payment is, and what are they doing to guarantee this will not occur in the future. 

There should also be fines and fees charged against Ditech. If I owed Ditech over {$7200.00}, plus interest, they would have their lawyers camping at my front door.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'a redistribution was made by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] manager. she said that the missing interest would be calculated and added to the balance ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4400,'08/19/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I fell behind in payments due to my mother passing away, not only I lost her income since she was living with me. I Had to pay for the final services. This caused me a huge financial and emotional struggle. Now my business is doing much better and I am able to start making payments and I have applied for a loan modification but they refuse to open my file and review my loan due to sale being too close. sale date is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'my mother passed away due to her income loss. she was living with me and she was living with me. she was in the financial and emotional struggle. now my business is doing');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4401,'08/18/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Disclosure verification of debt','Paid auto repair service with a check from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card account on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. My check was accepted by the business. I received a written notice via mail from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 that the check had been denied. I contacted the auto repair business to settle the debt but was told that they had been paid. They referred me to Certegy check services along with a case number. I contacted Certegy and found out that my debt had been turn over to Complete Payment Recovery, a collection agent. I paid the debt including the {$40.00} recovery fee. Certegy did not give me any notification of the payment denial or that the debt was being sent to a collection agent.','Fidelity National Information Services, Inc. (FNIS)',2.0,2.0,'my check was accepted by the business. I received a written notice via mail from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].');
