INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4403,'08/18/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','I need to deposit a house insurance check in the amount of {$12000.00} to my Chase account and they are refusing to accept it because they say ( 1 ) the amount is too large, over {$10000.00} and since it was issued to my husband and myself and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] company I hired ) and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and duly endorsed by all parties, Chase ''s internal rule indicates that the check must be deposited to the business account holder in detriment of their own personal clients ( my husband and myself. ) Chase gave me two suggestions : ( 1 ) return the check to the insurance company with the endorsements and ask that they issue a second check only on behalf of my husband and I, or ( 2 ) have the check deposited in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '' banking account. Either of their solution is unacceptable to me as it exposes me to credit risk since ( 1 ) the insurance company may actually reject the check since the money was deposited by a third party and not the insured and ( 2 ) the fee to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is only {$2400.00} for which I already issued and delivered a check. By having the company deposit the check I need to wait for their bank to clear the balance of {$9600.00} which exposes me to the credit risk posed by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] company for a week or so. Additionally, if my bank can stipulate what kinds of checks it can receive in the branches for small amount of dollars or any other internal rule, they are not doing their basic job of clearing checks! I have been a banker all my life, most recently as a Banking Center Manager at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and can not understand how a duly endorsed check, including with a signature guarantee on the part of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bank can not not be processed by the banking system. What woul