Despite the fact that Simon ''s Agency had no record of my residence/address in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( it only lists the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] MD [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as my address in their records ), it now claims that it has sent a legal Collections Notice to me in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The fact is it had not, and could not because according to its '' own records it had no knowledge of my residential and mailing address in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or at any time thereafter, until I sent them the Validation request in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

Multiple attempts ( including filing a complaint via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to resolve this matter with Simon ''s Agency ( third party collection agency ), or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] directly ( allegedly the original creditor ) have failed. 

Simon ''s Agency collection company had failed to produce any evidence to substantiate it ''s claims, or to correct erroneous information. It continues to willfully submit inaccurate and unsubstantiated information to credit bureaus in an attempt to collect the debt while employing deceptive and unconscionable means.','Simon’s Agency, Inc',2.0,2.0,'a complaint is filed against the ''fDCPA'' of the ''fair credit reporting'' act. the ''fcc'' says that the ''fcc');
