INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4419,'08/13/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','I have disputed this several items requesting proof of my signature and the original contract which they fail to provide. I continue to receive the same response each time and within two weeks of each dispute which is " the account has been verified '''' I demand proof of contract and signature or immediate removal from my credit file. Acct # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'i have disputed this several items requesting proof of my signature and the original contract which they fail to provide. I continue to receive the same response each time and within two weeks of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4420,'08/13/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','As a condition of our marriage dissolution my ex-husband was supposed to file our taxes for 2008. He failed to file State taxes & ignored multiple certified letters notifying him of the debt liability, and then the tax lien being placed on us. I no longer resided at that address so I did not receive notification of the lien until it hit my credit report. I contacted the creditor, arranged payment, and made sure the debt was paid, paying the lion-share of the debt. The lien has since been released, but Equifax says it will show on my credit report as a released tax lien for up to 10 years. I want the tax lien information completely removed from my credit report. When I learned of the tax debt, I actively took steps to pay it off, contacting bill collectors and paying what my ex-husband failed to pay. Although it appears as ''released, '' this tax lien threatens to stifle my ability to gain credit, making it even more difficult as a divorced woman to establish myself financially after my divorce. Why must responsible people be made to suffer? Have n''t I suffered enough?','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the lien has since been released, but it will show on my credit report as a released tax lien for up to 10 years. the lien has since been released, but it will show');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4421,'08/13/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Taking out the loan or lease','My husband purchased a car and never received a call from this company for about a year and when he did he was one day late with the payment they immediately threaten to take action and called constantly every hour on the hour when asked to not call on certain days or hours that he was at work. We have filed an insurance claim on our car due to {$800.00} in damage and the day that we left the dealership we had issues with the car they did n''t want it back because it was their car. Now we ''ve had problems ever since. Credit Acceptance has been harassing us since we filed a claim for damage and we have to pay out of pocket for the damage to the car as well as the car payment so now they are threatening to repo it when I purchased the car it was {$7000.00} and I put nearly {$3000.00} down on the car this was XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] it is now XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I still owe over {$5300.00}. Our payments are at {$250.00} a month and my car is only worth about {$2500.00}. I do believe we were scammed out of money at one point because I remember paying a payment one time at the beginning of the month and about halfway into the month they called me saying I did n''t make a payment and I paid the payment twice and they said they did not have it on record what can be done? This company has prevented me trading it in and refinancing a loan. In fact there are multiple recalls on this vehicle which is why I do not understand why the price was so high when I purchased it. The defects were still present when we purchased the car keep in mind it is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Chevrolet HHR and we purchased it in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] those defects were already supposed to be fixed when we purchased the car. I really do not want this car and unfortunately neither the dealer nor credit acceptance would give me back my money for this car when I first purchased it and wanted to take it back the next week. I just want my money back and for the harassment and threats to stop.','CREDIT ACCEPTANCE CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'credit acceptance has been harassing us since we filed a claim for damage. we have to pay out of pocket for the damage to the car and the car payment. now they');
