INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4440,'08/08/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','There are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] accounts reporting with dispute comments. I requested that these accounts remove the dispute comments from all [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bureaus and I had no issues with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but Experian stated that they would have to file a dispute with the companies reporting in order to have the verbiage removed and it could take up to 30 days. Well, it did n''t take 30 days but instead the two companies refusing to remove the comments denied my request even though I stated " I no longer dispute the account and I agreed with the way it was reporting '''' I also contacted both companies and requested for them to remove the dispute comments themselves and both companies stated they would n''t remove the dispute comments " UNLESS THE ACCOUNTS ARE PAID '''' To me this is illegal because these companies are holding me hostage and preventing me from being able to purchase a home by reporting innacurate information on my credit file since I have specifically stated I ''m no longer disputing the accounts. It ''s my right as a consumer to dispute an account and there are mortgage guidelines in place to decide whether or not I am approved for a mortgage and it should n''t be up to anyone deny me this right by reporting inaccurate information in hopes of getting paid. Experian has stated there is nothing they can do unless the creditor reporting the information gives them permission to remove the comment. I had no issues with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and if Experian has to put the account in dispute to remove the dispute comment it ''s extremely contradictory. I have clarified to both experian and the creditor reporting the information that I no longer dispute the information and I agree with the way the account is reporting and still I ca n''t get them to remove the comments from my credit file. This is preventing me from being able to move forward with a mortgage and they are holding me hostage. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are the two accounts.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian and experian have filed a dispute with the accounts reporting. they refused to remove the dispute comments. they said they would have to file a dispute with the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4441,'08/08/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Problems when you are unable to pay','I have had numerous issues with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This particular issue is that as I am working to rebuild my credit following a bankruptcy, I have an auto loan that I had prior to filing my Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcy. I reaffirmed the debt and had to dispute with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that the amount was n''t in bankruptcy. After that was finally resolved, they continue to report that my account is closed. I have disputed this no less than five times, online, by phone and in writing. This is a company whose sole purpose is to fairly report credit and they had done absolutely nothing to confirm that my account is open and current or they would have accurately reported it. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] does n''t seem to do any due diligence in trying to accurately report credit for consumers. Moreover, they have reported payments being made after my account was allegedly closed ( because it is still an open account ). This is just one of the recent problems I have had with Transunion. This is important to me as I am rebuilding my credit and having an open, current car payment loan is good for me and hopefully my next car loan wo n''t be at 12 % interest when current interest rates are 3-4 %.','ALLY FINANCIAL INC.',2.0,2.0,'a company whose sole purpose is to fairly report credit has reported payments being made after my account was allegedly closed. this is just one of the recent problems I have had with Trans');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4442,'08/08/2016','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I currently have a Bank of America first mortgage and I have been trying to refinance my first mortgage. 

Once the refinance process was started and title work was initiated it was discovered that there was a lien on my property as a second note.. Bank of America did do a modification to my loan in 2013 in which the payment and terms were adjusted. During the negotiation of the modification Bank of America never stated that they would be placing a new/2nd lien on my property. 
I have spent over eight months trying to identify who owns & services this lien and how I can achieve a payoff. I have contacted Bank of America, HUD and FHA on numerous occasions and none of them will take ownership of this second lien. Bank of America has told me numerous times that they do not own the lien and do not know anything about it. HUD and FHA have both told me several times that they are not servicer ''s of loans and do not hold notes. 
So at this point I am very frustrated with Bank of America, HUD and FHA because I can not get any answers on this lien on my property. If no one owns this second then how and why is showing on my title??? 
With this Phantom lien on my property I am not able to refinance my mortgage nor would I be able to sell my home if I wanted to or had to. I am stuck and feel scammed.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'bank of America did a modification to my loan in 2013. the payment and terms were adjusted. the lien was discovered on my property as a second note.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4443,'08/08/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','I have contacted experian numerous times in regards to a collection from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that appears on my credit report from Experian. I ''ve tried for the past year, to get this sorted out. Under the FCRA I have the right to ask how my dispute was processed and who they contacted for the information. I have done so, and they always claim they investigated the dispute, and it is accurate. How do they deem that its accurate if they ca n''t even tell me who they spoke to? I disputed this account online in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 and most recently [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would like this account removed as there is no relationship between myself and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',10.0,10.0,'experian disputed account online in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 and most recently in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE');
