INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4446,'08/06/2016','Mortgage','Other mortgage','Credit decision / Underwriting','Official looking mailing received ( from TRU Mortgage, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] , CA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) with a return address of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Inside the mailing is an offer to reduce our monthly mortage payment. We do not have a mortage and have not for years. The mailing claims their information is based on public record sources which probably means credit bureaus or other data providers they pay for information such as names and addresses. Of course, their claim may simply be fabricated.','MOUNT OLYMPUS MORTGAGE COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'mailing received by TRU Mortgage, CA. it claims information is based on public record sources.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4447,'08/05/2016','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Credit decision / Underwriting','I applied for a assumption with Nationstar Mortgage on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 and as of today ''s date they can not tell me whether I ''m approved or declined. I have submitted the documents requested more then once, changed the contract dated per the mortgage lender with Nationstar because it is out dated, and I signed disclosure as of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 which I believe they are out of compliance. I have tried to speak with a supervisor of which no one can give me a name or number at the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number or this mortgage lender. The original mortgage lender is now out of the picture and another person has stepped in. This person has asked for information that I has already given them and they still tell me that the wait time for a approval is 30 days from todays date [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,2.0,'I have submitted the documents requested more then once. they have changed the contract dated per the mortgage lender with Nationstar. they are out of compliance.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4448,'08/05/2016','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Deposits and withdrawals','This is a complaint about transactions denied due to insufficient funds, involving BNY Mellon ( d.b.a. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] provider ). 
On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016, a health care provider ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) attempted to run a charge against my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account via debit card, for more funds than were in the account at the time. The charge was denied, which makes sense. 
Later that day, I looked at my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account online and found that the " denied '''' charge had actually translated to a debit of {$300.00}, which was all the money in the account at the time of the transaction. This transaction number had a unique identifier, Claim # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Eventually, BNY Mellon/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] voided that transaction, and it no longer appears in the customer interface I can see on the web. However, there was a period of approximately six days when this debit remained on the books. 
I called BNY Mellon/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016, and was told by a customer service representative that this is " normal business ''''. I was specifically told that when an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] debit card transaction is denied, the funds in the account may be " in limbo '''' for 3-5 business days while things are straightened out. 
I do n''t know if this practice is in violation of banking law or not, but it seems like it should be. It sounds to me like BNY Mellon/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is processing debits immediately, but delaying credits for 3-5 business days, and possibly benefiting from interest in the mean time. 
This is my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] complaint about BNY Mellon/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the first being Case number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This particular institution seems to be operating on the fringes of legal behavior. I ''d appreciate it if the CFPB could bring their resources to bear on the problem. 

Thanks, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','BNY MELLON, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'a health care provider attempted to run a charge against my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account via debit card. the charge was denied, which makes sense ');
