Then I requested to speak to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Executive Resolution Specialist Customer Care and Recovery Group. I was told he was unavailable. I inquired specifically about proceeds status of my account and the Wells Fargo representative stated that she could not provide me with any information from the Bank ''s internal management information systems ( MIS ). The Bank ''s internal MIS did not contain any new information on my loan file. Then the representative transferred me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who stated he did not know where the proceeds were for my loan number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He did not know if FHA received the excess proceeds from the wrongful foreclosure sale of my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] residence in the amount of {$270000.00} and Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] lien position has not been paid as of Friday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] why the accounts have not been paid since the Bank wrongfully foreclosed on my owner occupied [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] residence more than 115 calendar days ago. I thought my question was simple since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is an " Executive Resolution Specialist Customer Care and Recovery Group. '''' Surprisingly, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] responded to my question by " stating my complaints never focus on this issue. '''' He would have to contact the settlement area to find out where the proceeds are because my account has not settled. This clearly demonstrates Wells Fargo Home Mortgage inability to adequately maintain ongoing and accurate records which further illustrate management ''s in ability to comply with federal financial laws and written federal mandates that have been instituted against the Bank since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after the financial meltdown.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'liens on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] residence have not settled. both liens on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]