INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4457,'08/03/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','I had rented a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Even though the transaction was paid for in cash, there was an unauthorized holding/pending charge placed on my US Bank debit card which overdrafted my account. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ONLY had my credit card information because it was required to reserve the rental. The charge pended on my bank account, then disappeared, as it was NOT legitimately authorized and ran mistakenly, unbeknownst to me. As a result of the charge pending, several overdraft charges ( I believe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), were charged to my account. I contacted staff at US Bank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Ohio to contest the fees, as I DID NOT authorize the charge which then disappeared, leaving nothing but the fees. 
The fact that I did indeed have money in the account is observable due to the fact that the overdraft fees alone totalled MORE than the amount which my account had gone negative. ( IE : I DID NOT overdraft, the pending, unauthorized charge which then DISAPPEAERED, overdrafted me ). 
I was advised by US Bank employees that I should just keep a better eye on my account, and that the only employee who could help me was on leave for another 3 weeks. 
Honestly, I have better things to do with my time than argue with banks over fees which I did not incur through any fault of my own. 
I am now in the " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' for a negative account which was solely the fault of the financial institution itself, and by them not honoring their policies for unauthorized charges causing fees.','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,4.0,'a charge placed on my US Bank debit card overdrafted my account. the charge pended on my bank account, then disappeared. the charge was pending, and it was');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4458,'08/03/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Taking out the loan or lease','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I applied for a loan with Chase Auto Finance. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a phone call from the Chase loan representative named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] indicating the loan was approved with an interest rate of 6.9 %. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated she would need the sale documentation from the dealership to finalize the loan and release funds. Due to not finalizing the purchase price of the 2015 Chevrolet Sonic Lt we stated we would proceed tomorrow to close the loan. I called on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to finalize the loan and was told the interest rate now has changed from 6.9 % to 8.24 %. This is deceptive unethical business practice. I was told the call was being recorded when the initial offer was made with the 6.9 % interest rate for the used auto. The loan representative did not give me a clear answer as to why the interest rate has changed.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I applied for a loan with Chase Auto Finance. the loan representative');
