INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4493,'07/25/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','For two months ditech Financial LLC has failed to apply our mortgage payments to our account. This payment transaction is an automatic bank transfer from my checking account to ditech. There have been no problems with the transfers as my bank statement clearly indicates they ''ve taken the money on time every month. Two months ago I called and spoke with a service representative after my monthly billing indicated that I was behind on my payments. The rep explained that apparently their system had an issue but that we were current on our payment and not to worry the system would " catch up '''' before our next billing period. My wife and I came home last week to find a notice on our front door instructing us to call ditech about a problem with our account. We called and talked to another service representative who, after some discussion, told us the system had a coding issue and while we were current it was n''t being applied to our account correctly but had been corrected on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016. Today in our mail there was a notice from ditech claiming we owed them {$500000.00} and a second notice from a collection agency. So the long and the short of my problem is that I ''ve been sent to collection by ditech for mmoney I do n''t owe them. A call to ditech again ended with me being told there is no problem. So my question is how do I fix the damage done to my credit scores by a company that seems to have no interest in repairing their problem and what do I do next month when this happens again? 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'ditech Financial LLC has failed to apply our mortgage payments to our account. the payment transaction is an automatic bank transfer from my checking account to ditech. the company has no interest in');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4494,'07/25/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','Transworld sent over several student loans to a collection law firm to collect on even though I never purchased or signed any paperwork with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which I complained about to them twice. Per FDCPA, the owner of the debt must show proof that they own it before they demand any money for it. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to send me the proof of ownership that I asked for but instead they decided to send it to a law firm where it could be sued on. I also spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they acknowledged they had the loan before but none of the information was on the paperwork I received which is unacceptable. I never signed any paperwork or borrowed any money from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] either which they said to deal with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because they no longer have the loans. I do see any ownership information from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a promissory note that states [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and then letters from the law firm that states owner was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but no explanation as to how they own this debt which is a requirement and I sent a letter asking for this information but I only received a promissory note and bills, nothing else and I asked for several issues to be resolved in the validation of debt that I sent to the law form on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. I did speak to a FDCPA attorney and was advised this debt is uncollectible without proof of ownership and no one can take legal action against me on this debt and it will need to be removed from my credit report. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Transworld are trying to commit fraud against me. I have the copies of all of the complaints I have against Transworld as proof. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] can not collect on this debt without ownership and that information must predated the day it was sent to the collections law firm.','TRANSWORLD SYSTEMS INC',2.0,4.0,'transworld sent over several student loans to a collection law firm to collect on. owner must show proof that they own it before they demand any money for it. owner must show proof');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4495,'07/24/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Rewards','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16, Citibank close my AT & T Access More Credit Card account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] without explanation and refused to respond to my inquires. This account is an new account I opened XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I paid the {$95.00} annual fee in order to enjoy the benefits of this account. Since this account was unilaterally closed by Citibank, I would like Citibank to refund me the {$95.00} annual fee I paid. 

Furthermore, the sign up bonus for this account included a {$650.00} credit towards a purchase of a new AT & T smartphone after spending {$2000.00}. Although I met the spending requirement very quickly I was not able to purchase the phone through the Citi online portal due to the Citi website ''s technical difficulties. I contacted Citi Customer Service with this issue and the Customer Service Representative I spoke with advised me to purchase the phone directly from AT & T and faxed in the receipts to be reimbursed. I purchase the phone on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and faxed in the receipt to Citi Rewards Department @ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on the same day. Since the {$650.00} credit was still processing when the account was unilaterally closed by Citi, I suffered detrimental reliance since I purchased the phone with the expectation that I would be reimbursed up to {$650.00} by Citi. I would like Citi to follow through with the agreement of reimbursing me {$650.00} for the phone I purchased. I attached the fax I sent to Citi Rewards Department on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'Citibank closes my account on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. I paid the $95.00 annual fee');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4496,'07/24/2016','Debt collection','I do not know','Taking/threatening an illegal action','This company has called my work issued phone threatening to file with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Court on a Saturday. When I asked for what, the gentleman got extremely rude and defensive. I have since blocked the calls. Now they have made several calls to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year old mother. She has told them each time to stop calling her and to remove her from the list. She decided to call and the gentleman she spoke to was rude and told her that she can not tell him how to do his job and that there is nothing stating to stop the calls.','Lionstone Holdings Group',2.0,2.0,'company called my work issued phone threatening to file with the court. the gentleman got extremely rude and defensive. she has since blocked the calls.');
