INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4535,'07/12/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','Wells Fargo ''s last letter to me stated that I willingly put a check in online and it somehow appeared in a specific branch. Upon speaking with a customer service agent of another bank, that is impossible. When a customer takes a picture of their checks, they still have the check itself in their possession. So if you take a picture of your paycheck, and upload it to us bank. It does n''t show up in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if you deposit it online or via mobile in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When it ''s a picture taken online or via mobile app, it is still visible to you. Unlike when you go to an actual branch, it is taken from you. But mobile banking and online banking both do n''t have any way to put the check in any specific branch. I did not willingly put anything anywhere. Knowing that I have told their representatives I only get ssi, and knowing that nobody gets {$15000.00} in ssi, that would be logical that my account was highjacked. The most one person may get in ssi, may be about {$2500.00} to {$3000.00}, but no more than that. As well as they stated that if you report that funds were put into your account as an unauthorized access to the account, then as long as you report it within 60 days, it should be resolved. If they think willingness, is about giving permission, it is not. If I willingly put {$15000.00} in that account, and making only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a month in ssi, I doubt I willingly put anything anywhere. How can I come up with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], when at most, one could only get {$1300.00} from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payday loan companies? {$730.00} + {$1300.00}, equals nothing close to {$15000.00}, and the person who put it in there is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I do n''t think that ''s logical. And also, they state that in their funds availability policy, that any amount over {$5000.00}, is to have the first {$200.00} available the first business day after that was deposited, well then if that be the case, mine were available the first day they were put in. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is the check issuer, but that check holder is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. And by federal law, he should be in prison for committing a purposeful fraud against wells Fargo. But wells Fargo looks at me for fault, when the last time I ''ve travelled outside of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], is when I was a very going minor child. The check was unclear to me online. I do not know any [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Willingness is not permission. If what they state is true, then why was the check from an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] address. And what about the check being from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], in the fact, that they refused to hand over certain information that would have prevented me from being held liable.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'if you deposit a check online, it is still visible to you. it doesn''t show up in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] if you deposit');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4536,'07/12/2016','Mortgage','VA mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Our mortgage is through Freedom Mortgage. When I stopped working, my husband and I fell on hard times. When I called freedom to ask about how late I can make my payment. They connected me to a dept to help customers in need. They set me up on a payment plan. I would skip the first month then pay a little extra for the next 4 months to catch up with my mortgage. They said to disregard all letters because they are system automated. They then transferred my loan to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I was done with the payment plan they transferred my loan back to Freedom along with {$600.00} dollars worth of fees accrued by late charges. Freedom refuses to help me because they say that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] charged me those fees not them. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] will not help me because they say they do not have our file anymore and we are no longer their client.','FREEDOM MORTGAGE COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'freedom mortgage is through Freedom Mortgage. when I stopped working, my husband and I fell on hard times. they connected me to a dept to help customers in need.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4537,'07/11/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Customer service / Customer relations','I ''ve had my Citi Thankyou card since 1996. Never had any problems until this year. I was 2 days late making the payment to completely pay off my balance in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I knew I would be charged interest on my next statement. I paid the complete balance in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. However, when I received my statement for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], there was another interest charge of {$240.00}, so I called customer service. They said they could n''t help me, but would have a supervisor contact me. I missed the call when the supervior called back and she left a message saying that I should call the number on the back of my card. I have called 4 more times and each time I get the same response, that they will have a supervisor contact me. To date, I have n''t received a return call from the supervisor. It ''s very frustrating to received no response at all.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'I paid the balance in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was 2 days late. I called customer service and they said they couldn''t help me ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4538,'07/11/2016','Debt collection','Federal student loan','Communication tactics','EDUCATIONAL CREDIT MANAGEMENT CORP calls my cell phone and home phone multiple times a day. They call from multiple phone numbers. The last time I spoke with them, I provided my home address and told them I only wish to communicate by letter. 

This defaulted student loan debt is already in involuntary repayment through tax offset. 

I know that repayment options negotiated at this point will not stop the tax offset I want to stop the phone calls.','ECMC Group, Inc.',2.0,4.0,'student loan debt is already in involuntary repayment through tax offset. a defaulted student loan debt is already in involuntary repayment through tax offset.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4539,'07/11/2016','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Taking out the loan or lease','My fianc and I came in to Jared jewelry store and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told us that he could put a diamond stone on a band they had in store ( which would make the ring custom ) and if I did n''t '' like it, I did n''t have to keep it as long as I returned it within 30 days. According to their pamphlet, anything custom can not be returned. He lied to us about this. I did n''t want to return my ring. I loved it, but I ''m informing you about this to show a pattern. When he talked to us about financing, I told him that I do n''t like to finance because I do n''t want to pay interest. He said that they had a program right now for 0 % interest for 12 months. He never mentioned a down payment and he stated if we needed a little more time we could go with an 18 month loan that was 0 % for the first 12 months and 9.99 % for the last 6 months. We were at the store for quite some time and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated it was taking longer because he was trying to make it so we would n''t have to put any money down. Had he told us at any point we would have to put money down, we would have been out of the store empty handed. However, that was n''t the case, so we thought and we ordered our rings believing we were getting 0 % for 12 months. I received the first bill due [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 but no payment was due on the paper statement. I made an account online because I pay all my bills online. When I did that, it stated I needed to make a payment of {$690.00}, which I paid by the due date. The amount was about right, in store the calculation was about {$700.00} a month. However, when I got the next months statement, it stated I had {$270.00} in interest. I called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at ext [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that I did not have the account for 0 % for 12 months, I had a regular account with an interest rate of 24.99 %. I told her that is not what [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told us. She said she could change it to 0 % but my monthly payment would be {$1100.00} per month. I told her that I could n''t afford that much per month and that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] never told us that. She stated she would call [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the store. She came back on the phone and stated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would be calling me because he wanted to handle this since we were his customer. We called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and he told us that he did n''t sign us up for the 0 % but that we could change it to 0 % for 12 months for {$900.00} and change per month or 18 months, etc. I told [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that he did not tell us this in store and he misled us. I hung up. I called Jared [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # back and asked to be set up for the 18 month plan. She stated that we would have to put 20 % down in order to do that. I was appalled, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had not informed us of this either. I looked through my paperwork and I was not given a copy of the credit application or any information regarding the credit agreement. On my receipt it merely states reg credit plan. I take responsibility for not reading thoroughly and making sure the verbal information given to us matched the written, but we were misled. Also, when I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I told him I just wanted to return the rings. He said I could not because the 30 days had passed. Perhaps that is the reason no bill is due until 60 days after a purchase. It ''s not that I do n''t want to pay for the rings, it ''s just that we were misled with the credit terms. I can email you all the documents I have.','STERLING JEWELERS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a ring was custom made by a friend who had a diamond stone on it. he told us that he could put it on a band they had in store');
