INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4545,'07/08/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Hello I have a complaint against Transunion. I was a victim of identity theft. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 I noticed that I had items on my credit that was n''t me. So I stared a dilute with TransUnion. When it came to the inquiries I was told by TransUnion that they will not dispute my inquiries and I neede to contact the creditors myself. I did that I wrote letter to the creditors. I did get letters back from the creditors either stating that the inquiries was not a hard check and should not be showing I also got letters saying that they did n''t have me in the system and I even got inf back from the postal service stamped insufficient address. Now these are the address that the bureau have. I sent the copies to TransUnion however they still say they are going to remove them. I did what they ask of me and still did n''t get any results!! Please help me because I ''m out of options.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'id theft victim of identity theft. id theft victim of identity theft.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4546,'07/08/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Settlement process and costs','Chase promised us outstanding customer service and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loan issues as Private Clients. We went through the application process and had everything set for closing. Our loan officer was a nice guy who tried his best to help us but our closing was awful. It was a 7.5 hr closing with our final CD only issued about 2-3 hours into closing instead of 3 business days before. We ended up wiring a substantial amount of money to an escrow account prior to closing based on the verbal instructions from our loan officer. We were not provided with the final CD as required by Fed law. The sellers attorney left after a few hours for another closing. Chase [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] up the titling on our mortgage which affected our deed. Chase had our closing date wrong which would have meant a dry close on Monday instead of Friday. The title company officially closed at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The closer stayed until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to try to get the loan done. Chase ''s closer and loan department stopped picking up our calls or responding to emails and voicemails. Our IL closing was handled in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We ended up having to reschedule our move, we had to hire a dog walker since we couldnt leave the title company. We ended up having to take the entire day off work instead of the 2 hours allocated for the close. Chase didnt bother to send a representative to the closing. We ended up dialing everyone we could think of at Chase. I had a Chase branch manager try to get hold of someone to help us figure out how to get the correct info submitted. We had to sign the mortgage docs without very much time to review because of the time deadline and the pressure from the title company closing. The sellers were irate. We submitted a formal complaint the Monday after closing and didnt hear back from the Customer resolutions team until today. She hadnt bothered to review the file. I submitted phone records, copies of emails and a narrative statement to our branch manager who forwarded it to the loan officer and his superior. I would be happy to share those with your department. I could not paste that here due to the character limit.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'the title company officially closed at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the closing was handled in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the title');
