INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4581,'06/28/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Unable to get credit report/credit score','Experian will not allow me to dispute information in my credit file that is incorrect because they say they are unable to verify my identity but yet I was able to retrieve my credit report from them. I had previously filed a dispute with them and upon completing the investigation there were still errors on my credit file. However now they are saying they can not verify my identiy and I need to submit my request by mail. I disagree with that because I just got a copy of my Experian credit report and I should be able to submit my disputes on line as well. I have included proof of my current credit report and experians rejections of my disputes.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',4.0,4.0,'experian will not allow me to dispute information in my credit file that is incorrect. they say they are unable to verify my identity but yet I was able to retrieve my credit');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4582,'06/27/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','I signed up for a promotion for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after completing specific requirements. 

" Within 60 days after account opening : you spent the required minimum amount ( {$1000.00} ) using the Citibank Debit Card Completed 1 qualifying bill payment to the new checking account during a calendar month and during the following calendar month " I have completed this and never got my points, I have requested twice for reviews and nothing has happened.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a promotion for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was launched within 60 days. you spent the required minimum amount using the Citibank Debit Card.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4583,'06/27/2016','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Equifax has a poor site for correcting errors. I have misinformation listed in my report that indicates a negative public record judgment against me. It is not against me, it is against someone else. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had the misinformation listed also, but quickly removed the error ... upon request from me. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not list this misinformation, apparently they are more careful. What recourse does the public have with Equifax and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]? They have filed false information about me and this has cost me credit, and I have had my credit levels lowered by several of my credit card companies ... this could also have cost me an employment opportunity. I have been financially and emotionally injured, and spent a lot of wasted time. It seems to me that we the public, are victims of their casual yet powerful business practices. It is irresponsible of them to post negative information in our reports without at least advising us that they will be doing it. I am glad that there is this opportunity to pull up the annual credit report. If I had not been able to, who knows how much longer this misinformation would have been listed ... 7 plus years? It seems to me that we should be able to have access to our credit reports, without charge, every day. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a poor site for correcting errors has been posted by the public. it is irresponsible of them to post negative information in our reports. it seems to me that');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4584,'06/27/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014 our loan was sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], OK. Shortly after purchasing the home, we put in over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of updates and remodel costs. I wrote to the company and was told that I had to have the loan for TWO YEARS before the PMI could be removed. It has now been two years and I am trying to request an appraisal so that I can meet the loan to value amount of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % that the company requires. I just got off the phone with their customer service, and they have told me that they can not tell me the price of the appraisal ( even though I have to use an appraiser in their system ). I have to submit a letter requesting an appraisal, and then be bound to pay for it, without knowing how much it will cost me. I was told a supervisor can call me within 48 hours. It appears to me that the company is making it very difficult to remove the PMI and not disclosing appraisal rates. In addition, this year they paid my home insurance LATE out of the escrow account which created problems with my insurance company. My request is that I be given a cost for the appraisal before I request one from the company. I do not believe that their practice of requiring a commitment without knowing the cost is ethical.','BOK FINANCIAL CORP',2.0,2.0,'in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014 our loan was sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of [COMPTE_ANONY');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4585,'06/27/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','This charge is for my son ''s lease on an apartment while he was in college. We hired an attorney to get him out of the lease because of proven mold issues and negligence. This lease was only signed by him at the time of termination. He indeed turned his key into the office but they are saying that he did not so they are charging him {$100.00}. I was a co-signer on the previous year lease but was not on this second year lease, that is how they have my information. This is direct retaliation for them having to terminate the lease agreement.','National Credit Systems,Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a co-signer on the previous year lease was not on this second year lease. he was not on this second year lease, that is how they have my information.');
