INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4597,'06/22/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Cash advance fee','Wells fargo Visa card and checking account - demanded over numerous years that all overdraft protection be removed and was assured it was not. each time I overdrafted it, it took from my credit card, allowing me to continue using my debit with no clue I had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance. what should have been a one time fee and my card decline on the next purchase turned into multiple " lower fees meant to save me money and help me continue shopping ''''. these added up to far more than the one time fee. sure enough, happened again. only this time, the overdraft fee turned into a fee hitting me from the checking account AND credit card side multiple times, then hitting me with cash advance fees. A soda , drive thru and gum purchased totalled all of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bucks, which has now cost me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and climbing as the cash advance fees rack up. apparently, they stick the cash advance debt behind your running balance, preventing you from ever freeing yourself. three separate times now I have called and been assured it was removed.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'overdraft protection was removed from wells fargo Visa card and checking account. the one time fee turned into a fee hitting me multiple times, then hitting me with cash advance fees');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4598,'06/22/2016','Bank account or service','Savings account','Problems caused by my funds being low','Wells Fargo bank discriminantly assesses fees and fails to adequately notify consumers of changes in their fee structures. My savings and checking accounts are being charged fees if I do not set up AUTOMATIC transfers, even if I make sufficient deposits to these accounts for the sums allowed for monthly fee protection. Banks should be required to recognize savings deposits whether made automatically or directly during a statement cycle and should provide more notice to consumer of upcoming changes in account terms beyond a checklist always included in monthly statements.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',4.0,4.0,'wells Fargo bank discriminantly assesses fees and fails to adequately notify consumers of changes in their fee structures. banks should be required to recognize savings deposits whether made automatically or');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4599,'06/22/2016','Bank account or service','Savings account','Problems caused by my funds being low','Capital One Direct Banking claims they never received a deposit of {$170.00} money order by mail which was sent a week again and I did another moneyorder for {$170.00} priority mail, now they are returning my items but they are affecting my credit. The post office advised it was received but the bank now claims they do not have it. I need to be able to pay my bills but according to the the person I speak today advised no deposits since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but I received a direct deposit to the account on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16, I do not believe, I have been a customer for 10 years but they are causing my credit rating with the return items. The money orders have not been cashed yet but that does not mean they did not receive them. I want all return checks fees plus my {$340.00} credited to my account otherwise I file fraud charges against them.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,4.0,'capital one Direct Banking claims they never received a deposit of $170.00 money order by mail which was sent a week again. they are returning my items but they are');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4600,'06/22/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Other fee','I mistakenly paid {$70.00} less than the statement balance on my Chase Freedom credit card -- ~ {$2200.00} rather than {$2200.00}. So, their tactic is that the ENTIRE balance is subject to the borrowing interest rate ( that is, the usual grace period is null and void for the credit card ) - not only for the previous statement period but for the following statement period until the payment is received. So, I had interest charges of approximately {$10.00} apiece for two consecutive months ( by which time the balance was completely paid ). Essentially, {$70.00} borrowed for 2 or 3 weeks resulted in {$20.00} interest charge which would amount to an effective annual interest rate of almost 400 %. I hope there could be some reform in the laws so that only the UNPAID portion of the credit debt could be subject to interest assessment.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'$70.00 borrowed for 2 or 3 weeks resulted in $20.00 interest charge. the ENTIRE balance is subject to the borrowing interest rate ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4601,'06/21/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Transaction issue','I received and activated Citi Costco Visa card. It was supposed to replace [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card. My [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card stopped working and Citi Visa although activated successfully - is being declined by all merchants. All calls to Citi result in the message : " We experience a large volume of calls. Call us back some other time ''''. I tried calling and emailing Citi for last 24 hours to no avail. I am traveling today and unable to pay for food, transportation, lodging or basic necessities as I traveled with only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Citi cards.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citi Visa was activated successfully. my card stopped working and Citi Visa is being declined.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4602,'06/21/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','Recently TD Bank change the way they process transactions. I am a customers that lives check by check. My work checks are direct deposit on fridays each week. I pay my car every other week and now I have incurred in more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] overdraft fees of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They said this change was because customers wanted it like that. What customers rich customers? I ca n''t not afford this and certainly I ca n''t not afford loosing {$35.00} dollars just like that. The only reason why have n''t close my account is because I have to many payments linked to my account. I feel this NEW thinks is not only afftecting me is affecting people like me and we are getting excesive overdrafts fees. We are being robbed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the little money we make.','TD BANK US HOLDING COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'TD Bank recently change the way they process transactions. a customer who lives check by check has incurred in more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] overd');
