INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4634,'06/10/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Rewards','I received a letter on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was dated from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Wells Fargo. It stated, " we reviewed and found an unusual volume of purchases and/or payments made using this card. '''' And it continued to say, " if it continues beyond the receipt of this notice we will close your account and your rewards balance will be forfeited. '''' I completely stopped using the card altogether. At this point, I had {$3500.00} in rewards that were earned during this billing cycle and I did not want to risk losing them so I did not use the card again. My credit card balance was more than {$24000.00} at this time with a total limit of {$25000.00}. I was basically maxed out and absolutely needed to make a payment so I did not risk adverse action from other creditors if I allowed the total balance of {$24000.00} to report on my credit reports. So I made a payment to get the balance down and this payment was the only activity on the card after receiving the letter. 

Wells Fargo closed my account anyway and I received a letter dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that stated, " per the warning notice we sent, we closed your account on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. You can no longer make transactions with this account and your rewards balance has been forfeited '''' Wells Fargo clawed back rewards that I earned legitimately after sending out a warning letter, to which I obeyed, and cited the warning letter as the reasoning behind the closure. 

I have read some of Wells Fargo ''s responses to other complaints and Wells Fargo does not need to inform me that my CURRENT rewards balance is {$0.00}. I know that it is {$0.00} as of today. It was {$3500.00} before my account was closed and Wells Fargo forfeited them.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a letter on ''comPTE_ANONYMISÉ'' was sent to Wells Fargo. it stated that "we reviewed and found an unusual volume of purchases and');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4635,'06/10/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','For the second time in 6 years I am being forced to defend my property pro se. 
It does n''t seem to matter that the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] foreclosure was FIRST a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Aurora, Aurora [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], robosigned MERS, mortgage, that was thrown out of court in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. And I guess the 5 year statue of limitations law in Florida, means [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is above the law to have to refile the foreclosure now, claiming this time, ownership of a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] securitization by blatently altering the records. 

Their fraudulent actions, killed my marriage of 15 years, stripped my 50 year ''s net worth and has frozen my ability to work as a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] figure [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] while conducting my own forensic audit, I found that DeutcheBank is and ALWAYS WAS the bad actor here and served a QWR to NationStar servicer, that never responded to it.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,4.0,'a 5 year statue of limitations law in Florida means [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is above the law to have to refile the foreclosure now, claiming ownership of');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4636,'06/10/2016','Debt collection','Federal student loan','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I applied for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] discharge through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to have my student loans forgiven. A debt collection company called Pioneer sent me a letter they were taking over my loans and they were adding a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] collection fee.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a debt collection company called Pioneer sent me a letter they were taking over my loans. they were adding a collection fee to my loans.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4637,'06/10/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2005, I purchased a town house a few months before the housing market collapsed. After the collapsed, the house depreciated about 60 % of the purchase value. Two years later, I received [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) orders. I was unable to sell the town house and forced to find a tenant. Eleven years later, the market has not recover enough for me to be able to sell the property. I had been thru numerous tenants which either leave the property without noticed/paying the rent or I have to requested legal assistance to evict of them from the property. In addition, every time the property is left in a complete mess with me responsible for all the repairs. 
At this point, I have concluded that it is better for me to find a permanent solution to this situation. I started doing some research and learned about the different federal mortgage programs available for people in my specific situation. After reading the program criteria I was certain I qualified to receive help. Therefore, I contacted Navy Federal and requested assistance. I was directed to complete the Uniform Borrower Assistance Form and return it to them. Since I am currently station in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I requested to have all the documents forward to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Navy Federal banks in the area in order for me to expedite the process. However, Navy Federal refused. Instead, they used the postal mail service to send me all the require documents. I explained to them, by the time the letters or documents get to me in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I am always late for the bank requested submission due date on the package. I have tried in different occasions to get the documents either fax or scan to me directly or to a Navy Federal branch in the area. However, Navy Federal refused. As a result, my application process was delayed for approximately 5 months utilizing these tactics. 
Once the package was completed, I requested a deed in lieu of foreclosure. However, I was explained over the phone, first " you need to place the house in the market for short-sale and intent to sell the property ''''. Therefore, I agreed. Navy Federal approved the short sale and I immediately listed the property in the market. The property was on the market for 90 days as requested. In the processed, my realtor explain to me a few issued with the location of my property. The area have a higher rate of renters in comparison with owners. Therefore, it is almost impossible for any potential buyers to get finance to purchase the property. We contacted Navy Federal and after explaining the situation asked, " if they were willing to finance a potential buyers to sale the house ''''. They said no. Therefore, in order for me to sell this property I need to do a cash sale. 
On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the short-sale time frame expired and I was unable to sale the town house. I contacted Navy Federal requesting further instructions to process with the deed in lieu of foreclose. The agent told me, " the town house was not approved for deed in lieu and I need it to reapply for short-sale to place the house back in the market, a package will be mail to you soon ''''. Again, I was indirectly explained, " as long as you are making your payments on time, you are not demonstrating you have a financial issue ''''. I am told over and over, " you are not qualify for the Home Affordable Modification Program ( HAMP ), Home Affordable Refinance Program ( HARP ) or any refinance option available and I had been indirectly suggested to miss payments ''''. However, it is my understanding, I do not need to miss any payments in order to qualify for refinance programs. 
During the last ten months, the Loss Mitigation Department with Navy Federal Credit Union, has intentionally delayed my mortgage modification requested. They have continuously denial me all federal refinance options available without providing detail explanation.','NAVY FEDERAL CREDIT UNION',2.0,2.0,'a town house was purchased in 2005 by a bank in the area. the market has not recovered enough for me to sell the house. the market has not recovered enough for me');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4638,'06/09/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','My mortgage was sold to Green Tree Services LLC/now Ditech in 2014. Since then my monthly mortgage payments that I make on a timely basis have not been applied correctly, they have been misappropriated into a " Funds In Suspense Balance account ''''. Because the funds are not applied correctly, I receive multiple harassing phone calls from Ditech on a daily basis to bring my account current. When I speak to the representatives that call me, they scream, holler and belittle me. When I try to contact someone at Ditech ( each week they give you a new account manager and they have no idea who you talked to previously or what the problem is with your account so you have to start all over again and explain to them what the problem is ), you are put on hold for long periods of time, directed to someone ''s voicemail who has no idea what is going on with your account, and disconnected. My account is current and paid up to date yet notices have been put on the door of my property from a company called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that is contracted out by Ditech to check on " their property '''' to make sure it is being maintained. No legitimate mortgage company takes these kind of actions to ensure that they get their monthly payments.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'my mortgage was sold to green Tree Services LLC/now Ditech in 2014. since then my monthly mortgage payments have not been applied correctly. they have been misappropriated into a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4639,'06/09/2016','Debt collection','Medical','False statements or representation','Describe what happened so we can understand the issue ... 
XX/XX/2015 I was contacted by ATG credit in reference to a Medical debt totaling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for numerous accounts. I was advised that it had not reported to the Credit Bureau as of yet and in order to hold the account from further action I needed to pay the balance. I agreed to a one time payment of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over the phone and advised that I would try to make a large payment the following month. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ATG withdrew [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of my checking account. I called them immediately and was advised they had me on record authorizing this amount. I told them that it was untrue. They advised me they would review the recording and call back When the representative called back she advised me it was valid. I asked her directly if the recording stated I agreed to this amount or did I say that I would make arrangements for the amount. She stated I agreed to it which is a blatant lie. 

I filed a fraud complaint with my bank and the BUREAU OF CONSUMER FINANCIAL PROTECTION ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) for the funds which were returned ... .. 

Today I received a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the same debt for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I explained to her they have already reported to my credit bureau which she states they have not. She said they have sent numerous letters no letters have been received from ATG credit since their violation of EFTA. She demanded a payment arrangement and advised me it would be reported the following week. The previous payment arrangements were for the same hospital stay I believe they are finding a reason to contact me again by misinforming of the number of accounts/balance and I feel harassed and confused about what I actually owe. I will not give them any payment information based on the fraudulent abusive and unscrupulous actions previously. 

[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ATG Credit LLC said : Explanation of closure We have reviewed the account and determined that the complainant did agree to the payments but asked us to hold them until she contacted us back. The payments should not have been processed. We have placed the account on hold and as a courtesy have removed from reporting on credit. The account is still outstanding but we have pulled future payments and removed from credit. It appears the payments did not clear so the balance does remain outstanding but as a courtesy we have removed from credit for the time being.','ATG Credit, LLC',6.0,8.0,'XX/XX/2015 I was contacted by ATG credit in reference to a Medical debt totaling [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for numerous accounts');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4640,'06/09/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Billing statement','For my monthly statement with the due date [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2016 ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), the new balance was {$3000.00}. However, Capital One then reported my balance being {$3100.00} without notice and added a {$59.00} membership fee also without notice, seemingly attempting to put my card greatly over the limit, which brought my credit score down from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] within the FICO reporting months of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016. I have paid {$100.00} and the minimum was {$97.00}. These are unfair practices by Capital One. The should at least warn me when they will add a membership fee.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'capital one reported my balance to be $3100.00 without notice. but the new balance was $3100.00. the minimum was $97.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4641,'06/09/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015, I came across an offer stating that if I applied for a citigold checking account using a promotional code, I would be eligible to receive [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] AAdvantage Miles if I met the following conditions : a. Spent {$1000.00} of money in the checking account. 
b. Made two qualifying bill payments in consecutive months. 

I decided to call Citibank to confirm that this was not a scam. I called and spoke to a Customer Service Representative who assured me that I was in fact eligible for this promotion and that If I opened an account over the phone, with her, and met the stipulated conditions, I would in fact receive [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Miles. She also told me that there would be a $ 30 monthly fee for the account, and that I should only proceed if I was ok with those terms. I agreed, since I would be receiveing a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mile sign up bonus, it would be worth it. I listened to her instructions carefully, and followed them to the letter to meet the conditions stipulated. However, it has been 6 months, and I ''ve had multiple monthly fees deducted from the account, however I have not received any miles. When I called customer service, I was assured that I had in fact met all of the requirements for the miles with my checking account, however Citibank would not be honoring the terms of the promotion as I had been misled by the customer service agent who spoke to me, and that I was not in fact eligible for the promotion as I was not targeted. This is despite the assurances i took care to get from the customer service agent before opening the account. This is an unfair practice, because as a result of being misled, I opened the account under false pretenses and will incur more than {$60.00} in monthly fees as a result. 
How','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'if I applied for a citigold checking account using a promotional code, I would be eligible to receive [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] AAdvantage Mile');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4642,'06/08/2016','Payday loan',NULL,'Charged fees or interest I didn''t expect','I took out a loan from them thinking it was legal. After looking into my state laws they could only charge me 10 % they were charging me over 600 %. Violation in state law. I am protected under state and federal law. I do n''t have to listen to no Indian tribe. I went to an attorney and they did n''t respond to his request so he advised me that it is illegal and I do n''t have to pay it.','Green Trust Cash, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a loan from them was a way to charge me 10 %. they were charging me over 600 %.');
