INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4644,'06/08/2016','Debt collection','Medical','Improper contact or sharing of info','I was sent summons information about someone else from a collection company. They filed incorrect information regarding someone else ''s debt in my case and Certified that I had been served while providing Name and Address of entirely different person. They additionally sent critical court date and appearance information to an old address, despite that all other correspondence addressed to current address. They are suing me even though I am paying on a debt that I have disputed.','Credit Bureau of Carbon County',2.0,2.0,'a collection company has a summons information about someone else. they filed incorrect information regarding someone else''s debt. they also sent critical court date and appearance information to an old');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4645,'06/08/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','I have attempted to contact Discover for over 3 months about an issue their website and the calculations of the current balance. Multiple times I have went to my activity and it computes my current balance with the following formula. Last Statement Balance - Payments and Credits + Transactions = Current Balance. However, many of the times when I review this information the math does not add up. Everyone of these times it has show that my current balance is more that it really can when you do the math. It makes it seem that Discover is simply taking this additional money and hoping that I do n''t catch it. I have informed Discover of this multiple time over the course of 3 months. Every time I was told they were working on this issue but do not have an exact date as to when this problem with be fixed. Well, I have given them over 3 MONTHS to fix this issue and it still is not fixed. I feel that the company is not telling me the truth and actually are not working on the issue. This seems like a very unethical practice for a financial institution. How can a large company not resolve a simple IT issue?','DISCOVER BANK',4.0,4.0,'multiple times I have gone to my activity and it computes my current balance. the math does not add up when you review this information. Discover has given them over 3 MONTHS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4646,'06/07/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Using a debit or ATM card','I am an account holder at TD Bank. I requested a withdrawal from my brokerage account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to be credited to my debit card at TD Bank. I spoke to a customer service representative at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I was shown evidence that the withdrawal and instantaneous deposit to my checking account was completed. I went to the TD Bank branch office on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Streets and they told me they have nothing in pending transactions or otherwise to reflect that fact. Also, I write to complain about TD Bank ''s policy of not abiding by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] standards in accounting which specify First-In, First-Out accounting or First-In Last-Out accounting, but rather by the " size of the transaction, '''' in overdraft protection. This practice is unacceptable because the balances on ATM receipts do not reflect the balance by their method and the result is a charge of {$35.00} every time the consumer withdraws from the account. For example, an ATM receipt may reflect a {$20.00} balance, and the consumer may withdraw {$10.00} based on that statement only to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that TD Bank ''s " records '''' do not match their statement and the consumer is defrauded out of {$35.00} each time a withdrawal down to {$0.00} occurs. I will attach proof of my withdrawal from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and instantaneous credit to my TD Bank debit card as well as proof of such fraudulent charges as associated with overdraft protection, known as " Debit Card Advance ''''.','TD BANK US HOLDING COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a withdrawal from my brokerage account was requested to be credited to my debit card. a customer service representative at TD Bank said the withdrawal was completed. a consumer is');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4647,'06/07/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','WHAT DOES RACIALLY DISCRIMINATION MEAN TO A BANK / SERVICER / LENDER AND EVEN THE ATTORNEYS THAT REPRESENTS THESE AGENCIES? 
