The forbearance plan was supposed to last for six months, until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. At that point I would enter into a repayment agreement with LenderLive according to the plan. Instead, LenderLive reported on my credit as if I was missing payments during the forbearance plan. I noticed the negative reporting in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was looking at my credit because I was going up for security clearance for a job. When I called LenderLive about it they refused to fix the credit reporting. They had previously been ridiculously rude to me over the phone -- they even insulted me for being a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] veteran. 

In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] LenderLive transferred my loan to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not have any information about the forbearance plan. As far as they were concerned, I was six months behind on my mortgage. After the transfer, LenderLive refused to talk to me about the issue or to fix it. They just directed me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did n''t have the records and did n''t know what I was talking about. 

