rch Department within 10 days.','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'faxed a copy of the " Request for PMI Cancellation Review '''' to OCWEN Mortgage. it has been more than 15 business days since I ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4704,'05/19/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Other','I had a secured Discover IT card, and I fell behind with payments due to education expenses. My account was closed and permanently revoked in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and this was not something I was aware of. I reached out on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 by a message, and I asked if I made a full payment would it enable me to have spending privileges again. I was hasty, and I initiated a live chat with an Account Manager. We had an extensive chat, and in the end, I ended up making a payment for the full balance. Well, during this chat, this manager did n''t say anything about my account being essentially inactive. I scheduled the payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016. I received a response on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016 informing me that my account was revoked and closed. I immediately sent a message and asked them to stop the payment having been told of that new information. To this day, I have not received a response to that message. I finally decided [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hours had passed, so I reached out to a live agent and asked for the payment to be reversed on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016. She told me that it would take about 15 business days for it to go thru the proper channels. I waited that much time and a bit over because on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016, I reached out again and I was informed that due to my payment history a partial or full refund could n''t be issued. I did n''t let it rest. Since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have been fighting constantly. I reached out to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and about an hour ago, I rejected Discover ''s decision and issued a rebuttal. Discover has given me the runaround tirelessly for almost three months. I have talked to Account Managers, Supervisors, and this [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] person who was a representative of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] division. It went from a 15 day refund to talking to the bank wire department to everything in between. I even offered to allow them to a portion to show good faith. They rejected that citing company policy and my payment history. At any rate, this payment was made without having all of the facts. I do n''t know if the agent assumed that I knew my account was revoked or what, but all I wanted to do was get back on track. I ''m a college student, and I do n''t have a lot of money or a cushion so to speak. {$5500.00} tuition every [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] weeks and the cost of supplies for school means my money is low. I was trying to do the right thing, but I would have preferred to pay the balance down overtime. I ''ve been more than patient. I realize my payment history was n''t as strong as it could have been but work with me not rail against me and make me pay for a miscommunication. It ''s bad enough that I asked 24 hours after the payment was scheduled to be taken for someone to please stop it and no one responded. It was a gross error and a huge mistake. One that I have been fighting hard to amend since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2016.','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'my account was closed and permanently revoked in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I reached out to the account manager and asked for the payment to be reverse');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4705,'05/19/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','I have cancelled a creditcard issued by Bank of America the year of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], for fraudulent issue, I have requested it closed since then and have not used the card. Last year [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was suprise to see a charge of {$99.00} on that closed account. I called the BA credit card nos. and dispute about such transactions and question them about why was there a charge on my account and it was closed .They answered it came from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and I told them so what the card was closed why would you allow it to be used. The person I spoke to said in that time said they will take care of it. 
I never had access to that account anymore for it was closed, it was also never connected to my online banking, at that time. 
Today I discovered through the email message from that bank sent to me, that the original {$99.00} charge was now incurring an interest and they kept the account open even if requested it closed for 2 years now.Again I called the Credit Card nos./company and dispute about it, and I was informed as long as there is a recurring charges, even if the account was closed by the customer, it will still incur charges.I called the company that keep charging my account and informed them to stopped those charges for the account was closed, I was told that they were never informed the account was closed, because the charges kept going through. 
