INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4730,'05/11/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Rewards','Citi closed my credit card account without warning. Customer service said they could not tell me why my account was closed and I had to write directly to Citi Bank. I wrote Citi Bank asking for an explanation and for them to reinstate my account. They responded via mail quickly, but the said they would not reconsider their decision but still would not offer an explanation for why my account was closed. As of the final billing cycle, I had accrued {$150.00} in cash back rewards and Citi deems these points to be forfeited due to the status of the account. If I had been warned of a shutdown, but did not heed the warning, then I could understand the forfeiture. However have my account was always in good standing and involuntarily closed by Citi without warning and my earned rewards involuntarily forfeited without explanation. This is not acceptable. Citi earns money per each transaction and promises rewards on these transactions to their consumers. If I had known I would not receive rewards for these transactions I would have taken my business to a competitor instead. Citi may have chose to cut ties with me, which is their right, but to not pay the accrued rewards I earned is extra revenue to Citi, directly at my expense. I sincerely ask Citi to pay the rewards due to me and to reconsider my business.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citi closed my credit card account without warning. customer service said they could not tell me why my account was closed. they responded via mail quickly, but the said they would not reconsider their');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4731,'05/11/2016','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Managing the loan or lease','I had an equity loan with Bank of America that was paid off on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. I have requested NUMEROUS times for them to send me an accounting of the figures closing out the loan. I believe it is call the Truth and Lending statement. They have continually refused and previously I complained to you because they refused to give me any information on this loan other than charging me an outrageous amount of interest that they did not break down or define at how it was arrived at. My prior case with you is, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I received a letter from Bank of America today from their department that handles loans discharged in bankruptcy and has to do with my default. My loan has been paid in full. All I want is an accurate accounting of the end figures on that loan and now they have it in the resolution department in discharging a debt. I DEMAND FROM THEM A TRUTH AND LENDING STATEMENT AS TO WHAT HAPPENED AFTER MY LAST MONTHLY PAYMENT OF THE LOAN. i HAVE NOT DEFAULTED ON ANY LOAN AND IT HAS BEEN PAID IN FULL AND ACTUALLY HAS BEEN OVERPAID. I would also like to know Bank of America ''s usual practices when a loan is paid off and how many [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] people they are ripping off. Thank you for looking into this matter for me. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'i had an equity loan with Bank of America that was paid off on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. i have requested NUMEROUS times for them');
