Despite my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] consolidation with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I have been contacted by Navient, which claims that I owe Navient a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] student loan debt of approximately {$4700.00} and say that I am late in making monthly payments to Navient ( which I have never made ). I exchanged several messages, and spoke at length by phone, with a Navient agent, but Navient can not explain what this alleged federal " student loan '''' debt is from -- and can not explain why ( if it was actually a legitimate student loan ) it was not included in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] consolidation that took all of my student loan debt from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and brought it to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
Now, Navient has sent me a letter saying that they have reported my late status to the credit bureaus and is beginning the process of suing me in court to obtain a judgement against me for the alleged student loan debt. So, despite my countless efforts to get an answer from Navient explaining what this alleged debt is from, and ( if hypothetically it was legitimate ), why it was not consolidated along with the rest of my student loan debt with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], now I am forced to bring this matter to your attention and to beg your assistance in 1 ) stopping Navient from pursuing me for a debt that appears to be a mistake of some kind, and 2 ) stopping Navient from ruining my status with the credit bureaus, 3 ) stopping Navient from suing me in court. 

I await your help, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( ps : Navient has given me an account number : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] )','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'despite my college college student loan debt, I consolidated with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] all of my student');
