h was supposed to be recorded as paid in full by us - as demonstrated by attached cancelled check in attachments, but was NOT reflected by SPS as paid by us, These fees, after our check should have reflected payment in full by us - but was not reflected as paid by us by SPS -- included the following after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - date of our check for payment in full to SPS, and included fees up until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], for -- ( Codes included ) -- " 745 - restricted repayment, '''' " 601 - Disbursement to Servicer, " " 631- property preservation disbursements, " " 170 - Pre-distributed interest, escrow, payment, '''' " 173 - Custom Payment manual or max, '''' 766- Misc. Repayment, " and most important - " 633- Misc . [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Disbursement. '''' In addition, code 181 is not reflected on transaction code listing. However, a servicer advance - in the amount of {$35000.00} is reflected as " servicer advanced '''' on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- just prior to our refinance ( loan paid in full, on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. '''' Internal Revenue Service documents for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Mortgage Interest Statement reflect no delinquency, or default, at any time, and can be provided to the CFPB upon request. In the meantime, given SPS ''s newly recorded assignment, and discharge, on behalf of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank recorded in our County Registrar ''s Office in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it is apparent that any Statute of Limitations for diverted monies, is no longer an issue. We request an accounting in full, to us, to the CFPB, to the IRS, and to our County Registrar ''s Office, and request that the CFPB forward this request to these appropriate authorities, as authorized under law.. 
Thank You.','SELECT PORTFOLIO SERVICING, INC.',2.0,2.0,'SPS attached incomplete " payment history history '''' that does not reflect the entity to which our mortgage payments, and mortgage payoff were forwarded to on our behalf. ''''');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4796,'04/21/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','Our daughter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] six years ago and the bank has been trying to foreclose on her apartment for the last six years. The first foreclosure was dismissed due to fact they had used [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the robo-signing attorney to try to steal the apartment and could not produce the original note. We have maintained the property over the last six years. We are the heirs to our daughter ''s Estate. The case was refiled and was at issue. We were never served by the court my wife and I. We located the attorney ad litem that was supposed to defend our interest [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He referred us to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Suite [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] where we met with both attorneys. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told us he could not defend us and recommended his friend [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We asked [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] our attorney ad litem to inform the court that we wanted to defend or position as heirs of the estate and he refused. Instead [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] insisted we needed to hire his friend [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to represent us. When we failed to give [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the business due to lack of funds. It seems [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] took retaliatory action against us and got the trial moved to an earlier date then the original docket stated and allowed the court to foreclose on the apartment in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2015 for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sale date, knowing we wante