INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4848,'04/06/2016','Student loan','Federal student loan servicing','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I took out a student loan to send my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] daughters through college at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] graduated from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ; the other in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Just as I was starting to pay the {$110000.00} loan back ; my husband ( who was a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and main bread winner, as I am a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) had a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] over the course of a year and a half - and had to go on social security [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The loans are in my name alone, so we could not qualify for loan forgiveness. We lost our cars, our home, everything - and of course my loans went directly into forebearance. Fast forward to today. My loans have ballooned into an insermountable amount of almost {$200000.00}. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old. I ca n''t understand why a serious medical happening would not allow me to " freeze '''' my accounts ( so as not to accumulate so much interest and penalties ). This seems almost illegal and if not, definitely unfair. How can I ever climb out of this hole - a hole that through no fault of mine I fell into that I can not get out of. My credit is ruined. I ca n''t even buy a small house or condo because of that. It seems that there should be medical exceptions to loan forgiveness ( if you can show proof - which we of course can. ) It hangs over my head daily - and it keeps growing and growing, because I ca n''t even afford [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of hwat the minimum monthly amount is. I am stuck, lost and scared to death. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Ohio','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a student loan from a compte_anonyMISÉ student has ballooned into $200000.00. my loans are in my name');
