INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4874,'03/29/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I have a private student loan with Sallie Mae called the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When my time to make the first payment was approaching, I contacted Sallie Mae in several occasions requesting help and/or deferment because due to financial hardships and low income. In every single time, they said there was nothing that could be done, not even lowering my monthly payments. Upon my first due date, I was unable to make the payment. They also advised they would not accept a lower payment. Different representatives handled my issue at different occasions, they even did a financial statement, and still, they were firm in that I had to pay the minimum monthly payment as it was. My credit score and report have been SERIOUSLY affected. In the last two months, after constant threats that my loans where going to default, they finally realized I could n''t make payments and ALL OF A SUDDEN, there was a program for which I qualified. They lowered my payment about {$75.00} only. I told them the minimum payment was still too high and compromising to that amount would be irresponsible. However, they said that was the best they could do. Upon agreement, I expressly noted that the amount was extremely high for me to comply on an ongoing basis. They required for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] set payments for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] following months in order to " officially '''' enter the program. While in the meantime, my credit is still being affected. Nonetheless, the payments were scheduled. For the next continuing month, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] continued to make collecting calls, they continued to send " final '''' emails advising me to take action, etc. Many times I called to make sure everything was set and to make sure there was nothing pending, since I was still getting calls, emails, mail ... and I never received a written confirmation of the agreement I had entered with them, even though I requested it. Every time I call Sallie Mae, a representative provides different information from the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I ad previous received. More than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] persons have " changed '''' the terms to which I apparently agreed. They provide misguided information to students ; provide unreliable information ; they are extremely disrespectful ; every week I get a new " account manager '''' even though my letters say my account Manager is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

They have not acted in good faith at all. They waited months to finally provide help, affecting my credit report, when they could have provided help before defaulting on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of my payments. Their inconsistency with the information is not only misleading but misguided. They do n''t even provide accurate information on the online account service, therefore, I do n''t even know how my payments are being applied, etc. The minimum amount reflected online does not represent the correct amount ; the due date is not accurate ; the balance is not accurate. Their treatment is simply abusive. There should be oversight on how this company manages the students and student loans. Summerizing : - I cant repay my loan ; ca n''t decrease my monthly payments ; ca n''t temporarliy postpone payments ; and ca n''t get flexible payment options. 
- Dealing with Sallie Mae service : impossible with how payments are handled ; they are not clear or accurate as to what is the balance and what are the terms ( since every single person in that office says something different ) ; kept getting calls about my loan ; customer service personnel are rude and disrespectful.','SLM CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a student loan with Sallie Mae was lowered to $75.00. the loan was due to be a private loan. the loan was due to be ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4875,'03/28/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','My wife and I took out [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We were under the same belief that many have that these loans would fund the education that would lead to the higher paying jobs, thus enabling us to repay the loans and have the life we had worked hard to create. After graduation we were told our repayment plans would be more than the income we were making and opted for a hardship forbearance. Once this expired we were still within the same financial structure and unable to pay the requested amount. Navient was formed and our loans were transferred to them for servicing. They were even more difficult to deal with! My wife had her parents cosign on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of her [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans and, as a result, Navient refused to offer income based assistance due to the income her parents bring home. We explained to Navient that these are out loans and we are happy to repay them but we need to be within a reasonable payment. They are requesting over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of our gross monthly income in the form of payments and are unwilling to budge. We were told that these are private loans and are not eligible for any assistance outside of what they feel we should have. This is extremely frustrating because we are already paying them {$370.00} for my wife ''s loans and mine are in an educational forbearance. Once these come out, they want an additional {$1000.00} per month. That does n''t include the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans they are unwilling to include in the consolidation for my wife due to the consigned. They want an additional {$800.00} for those [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans- more than the combined total for all the other loans! When all is said and done, they want {$2200.00} per month from us. Our monthly income is only $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That means over half of it would go to them. That does n''t include the Federal loans we pay. Navient has been completely unwilling to work with us despite multiple attempts. The worst part is we have been paying on them for nearly 6 years and the total amount due today is actually more than when we took the loans out due to the ''interest only '' repayment plans and the fact that interest continued to accrue during forbearance. It is almost criminal that these companies are able to lock students in to these loans with no chance of assistance!','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a couple of friends took out their loans from XX/XX/XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. they were told');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4876,'03/28/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','My payment on my credit card was received by Bank of America 4 days after the due date, generating a late fee as well as interest. The interest charged to me was an overcharge. In the next month, another interest payment was assessed to me. This was incorrectly charged. Bank of America was unable to specify what that interest charge pertained to. With respect to that month, our bill was timely paid early and in full, plus a large overpayment. Our overpayment to Bank of America occurred because its bill was incorrect because it failed to credit our previous month ''s payment, continuing to bill it as a charge still due. So we paid the previous month ''s bill twice. Interest was then assessed, twice, on entirely wrong amounts, none of which were owed.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'my payment was received by bank of America 4 days after the due date. the interest charged to me was an overcharge. in the next month, another interest payment was assessed to me');
