PS : I asked Customer Relations to look over the recorded information between me and the loan officer. Customer Relations replied the tape was erased.','AMERISAVE MORTGAGE CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'amerisave mortgage officer asked me to prequalify me before incurring expenses. he asked me a good number of questions about my income, assets and liabilities.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4921,'03/14/2016','Debt collection','I do not know','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','Received repeated calls and voice mails from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] about an alleged debt of a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year old relative who lives in another state and who is not my financial responsibility and who has never been my financial responsibility. Nor have I ever co-signed for any of her debts. When I called back to tell the company to stop calling me they said they were " not customer service '''' - suggesting that they did not have to deal with irate callers and could use whatever tactics they chose to collect debts.','Clear Debt Solutions, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a relative who lives in another state is not my financial responsibility. she is not customer service.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4922,'03/14/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','In order to attend [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University for the 2 years I did, I was subject to using [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] loans to cover the costs of attending [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My loans are up to {$81000.00} from over {$100000.00} because of military reasons. They are currently forcing me to pay them {$880.00} PER MONTH, which take a whole paycheck every month. I do not know who Navient is, but it seems that now I must pay through them at this time, due to some unknown transfers of loans before a certain period of time. I still feel they are blatantly stealing money from me and others, plus forcing people who get paid under minimum wage to pay nearly {$900.00} per month is completely absurd. The company also told me, in the last forbearance conversation, that there are a limited number of times I can postpone my payments, and I am on my last one.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',4.0,4.0,'my loans are up to $81000.00 from over $100000.00 because of military reasons. they are currently forcing me to pay $880.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4923,'03/13/2016','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','I contacted Citibank Customer service on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and spoke to a representative and an account manager with regard to having my account reviewed to have interest rate lowered. I am currently paying [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance on the card and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on another balance on the same card. The account has been closed for several years and I am getting frustrated in the fact that even though I pay more than minimum due the account balance seems to continually increase. I have a letter from their Office of the President, dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that states that the account would be automatically reviewed every six months for a lower APR with no reference as to whether the account was open or closed. That is what I called and requested today and was very bluntly and rudely told by the account manager that because the account was closed, there would be no review. His response was the letter was from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and things have changed. So, just because my account is closed and I am continually making payments not only on time, but also more than the minimum due, I get penalized for review because the account is no open. The only remedy that was offered was to reopen the account at a higher rate! Please I am not a stupid consumer, all I ask is that I ''m treated the same as an account holder that has an open account.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'account manager told me that because account was closed, there would be no review. he said that because account was closed, there would be no review. he said that because account');
