INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4964,'02/29/2016','Debt collection','Credit card','Communication tactics','Several years ago I had taken out a credit card through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). I fell on hard financial times and was unable to pay off the debt. I made payments of {$50.00} when I could but was still not enough and they sent it to collections. After [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] other companies had the debt ( which I did not know about ) midland credit management picked up the debt. I ''ve attempted to work with them for the past month and have continuously spoke to a woman named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After realizing she was unwilling to help or answer any questions I had I requested to speak with her supervisor. A woman named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( who I believe is still [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/same voice ) begins telling me that they can no longer work with me because I have failed to make any attempt to solve the debt which is not true. I explained everything to her and nothing was said other than I can solve this debt today or I will be sued over this. They are rude and have tried bullying me for the last month. What do I do? 
