INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4975,'02/25/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','False statements or representation','FMS Financial Management Solutions, through its representative, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], has a false claim that I, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and my wife, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], owe a debt that we do not owe. They have filed this on our credit reports, despite the evidence that their claims are inaccurate. This is a clear violation of the law by their false representation of an amount and legal status of a so-called debt they are claiming. We provided them the information and evidence that they are in error, but they have since failed to correct their error. 

Originally, a dispute had arisen with a potential landlord that was settled in court. When a significantly reduced judgment was entered in court, we satisfied the judgment, since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015. However, FMS Financial Solutions has continued to negatively affect our credit score since that time by insisting that we owed an amount which is simply false and inaccurate. 

FMS Financial Solutions refused to correct their records, despite the fact that they were made aware that they are in violation of the Fair Debt Collections Practices Act ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), especially section [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( false or misleading representation of " A ) the character, amount, or legal status of any debt '''' ). We provided them the evidence of the notice of satisfied judgment, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], their representative, refuses to correct this information. 

We provided proof of the satisfied judgment amount and closed legal status, which was significantly less judgment than their client was claiming. We notified them that further delay requires further action provided by the laws of the United States.','Financial Management Solutions',2.0,2.0,'a dispute with a potential landlord was settled in court. the dispute was settled in court. they have filed this on our credit reports.');
