INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4981,'02/23/2016','Mortgage','Home equity loan or line of credit','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','This is a summarized version of the events that took place. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I paid off my Home Equity Line of Credit with Wells Fargo Bank. The amount paid to them was {$32000.00} plus a {$12.00} filing fee. I made the payment at the branch at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], GA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a letter from Wells Fargo ( see attached ) stating that I would be entitled to {$500.00} in liquidated damages if the lien holder failed to release the lien within 60 days of full payment. I never heard anything further until I contacted the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Court Clerk ''s office on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to see if the lien was released. It had not been. Bear in mind the 60 days were up on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I did some research and found out that I would have to demand the {$500.00} liquidated damages from the bank for failure to release the lien within the time limit set by Georgia Law. I wrote a letter to the bank which I mailed, faxed and also hand delivered to my local branch ( where I had paid the account off ). The branch employee refused to accept my letter and so I left it on his desk for him to hand to the branch manager when he got out of his meeting. I videotaped myself leaving the letter on the employees desk. When I returned to work I got a call from that employee stating he had handed my letter to the Branch Manager and that it would be forwarded to the appropriate department. I also contacted Wells Fargo Home Equity Department by telephone numerous times and on numerous occasions and no one seemed able to find the request sent by Wells Fargo to the Clerks office, although they insisted it was sent on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I finally got to speak to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who is an Executive Resolution Specialist in the Customer Care and Recovery Group in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], IA. We spoke on a number of occasions and finally the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Court Clerks office received the request to release the lien on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I then received the attached letter from Wells Fargo admitting that there was a delay in the lien release and they had requested a check in the sum of {$500.00} for me and it would be sent out within 7-14 days. I then received a phone call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stating that I needed to complete a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] form for the IRS BEFORE they could send me a check. I completed the form and immediately faxed it back to them. As of this writing, I have still not received the check I was promised. I feel like I am getting the run around. Wells Fargo are one of the biggest banks in the country and I would have thought that they would be REQUIRED to do their job PROPERLY, just as I have had to do. I got the payment to them and all the documentation that was required to be filled out to complete the process and they have completely FAILED to do what is REQUIRED BY GEORGIA LAW in the specified time. I am sure that there are others out there who have had the same experience and they should also be aware of the compensation rules that are NOT told to you by the banks. They tell you that you are entitled to these liquidated damages but they do NOT tell you that you have to DEMAND those damages if they fail to do their job. They might be paying out more of those {$500.00} checks if they did they because they can not seems to get it right.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I paid off my Home Equity Line of Credit with Wells Fargo Bank ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4982,'02/23/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Communication tactics','I have been called numerous times a day for over 2 months from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Callers on my work cell phone. They would not tell me what it was regards to until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15. Before this date, they would only tell me they were collecting a debt for {$43.00}. I have spoke with them on countless occasions and asked to please send me information in the mail in regards to this and I would be happy to pay it ( if it was legit. ) They told me on many occasion they would send me something in the mail. After being told this over a two week period of numerous calls, I finally asked to please stop calling if they were not going to send me anything in the mail. They continue to call and have become very rude and harassing. Tonight I was harassed by an employee by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I tried to nicely tell him to send me something in the mail. I stated they sent something in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and " there is no point to send anything else because I obviously do not pay me bills. '''' He also stated I " should have paid my debts and he would not have to call me. '''' When I asked to speak to his supervisor he told me '''' NO, you are going to stop talking and listen to him! '''' He would not give me his information until I argued with him for over 5 minutes. I finally was transferred to his supervisor, I explained the situation and she told me my number would be removed from their call list.','CONTRACT CALLERS INC',2.0,2.0,'a caller called me from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] calls for 2 months. they would not tell me what it was about until [COMPTE_');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4983,'02/23/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','BAYVIEW IS ENGAGING IN DECEPTIVE LOAN SERVICING PRACTICES BY NOT PROVIDING UPDATED AND CORRECT FINANCIAL STATEMENTS, PROVIDING INCORRECT ACCOUNT INFORMATION IN ORDER TO CREATE A DEFAULT LOAN SCENARIO, NOT ABIDING BY THE TRUTH IN LENDING ACT, NOT PROCESSING/APPLYING MORTGAGE PAYMENTS IN ACCORD WITH THE SPECIFIED ACCOUNT SCHEDULE, NOT PROVIDING CORRECT PAYMENT INFORMATION WHEN REQUESTED, THEREBY CREATING A DEFAULT STATUS, NOT COMPLYING WITH THE FEDERAL REGULATED ACTS, THAT GOVERN LOANS AND PROCESS, AND THREATENING TO MAKE THE MORTGAGE LOAN IN DEFAULT STATUS, REVOKING A MODIFICATION AGREEMENT PREVIOUSLY AGREED TO BY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], UNLESS PAYMENT IS MADE IMMEDIATELY ON [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 ON THE TELEPHONE, WITH NO PROOF OR REQUESTED DOCUMENTATION PROVIDED PRIOR TO PAYMENTS BEING MADE. ADDITIONALLY THREATENING TO CANCEL THE MODIFICATION AGREEMENT [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] HAS SIGNED WITH NO NOTIFICATION PERIOD OR GRACE PERIOD AS PER FEDERAL LAW, IF PAYMENT NOT MADE ON [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 VIA THE PHONE BY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], DESPITE [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] DISAGREEMENT AND REQUEST FOR PROOF OR STATEMENTS TO BETTER CLARIFY THE SITUATION','BAYVIEW LOAN SERVICING, LLC',2.0,2.0,'BAYVIEW ENGAGS IN DECEPTIVE LOAN SERVICING PRACTICES BY NOT PROVIDING UPDATED AND CORRECT FINANC');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4984,'02/23/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I applied twice for a loan modification and was stringed along for over 6mos and encouraged to apply twice to have the same outcome. Now I am currently facing foreclosure and losing my home. Chase just does n''t care I am just another number in foreclosure.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'i applied twice for a loan modification and was stringed along for over 6mos. now I am facing foreclosure and losing my home.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4985,'02/22/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Customer service / Customer relations','We received an email from our credit card company, Capital One, on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 Friday asking us to confirm recent purchases. We called on Monday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 to confirm, and they said it was too late, that one of our merchant ''s systems had been compromised and they may be collecting sensitive account information, so they were turning off the credit card. We asked which merchant, and they would n''t tell us. We asked them to please not turn off the card because it is used for business expenses, but they said they could n''t do that. They said they would send us a new card. We have waited two weeks, and still no card. Today, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16, Monday we called to ask what the status was. They said the card was still in effect, but had just been labeled to restrict use. They never told us a new card was n''t coming in the mail. We asked them to turn the existing card back on, and they finally agreed to that. Two weeks ago we asked them the same thing, and they would n''t do it. This has caused an interruption in our ease of business, as the owner of the company has not had his business credit card to use for the past two weeks. Very disappointed in Capital One ''s lack of communication and lack of customer service to service our needs.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'we received an email from our credit card company, Capital One. they said it was too late that one of our merchant''s systems had been compromised. they said they would ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4986,'02/22/2016','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Improper contact or sharing of info','We have a loan with One Main Financial that is partially secured by a vehicle that we own. Recently, we experienced a bit of financial hardship and fell about a month behind. We received several calls and a few letters from the creditor. I finally spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at the OMF branch that is closest to us and scheduled an appointment to refinance the loan. She said she ''d call me before the appointment to confirm but she never called. The following week someone from the company contacted my brother, a reference listed on our loan, and told him that they were going to repossess the vehicle if I did not pay on the account. We scheduled another meeting with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and went in to discuss the loan and what happened regarding the contact with my brother. She said that they determined that the person who made this call was terminated as they found that she had done several other things that were not permitted. At this point, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that they could remove our vehicle from the loan as collateral and refinance the loan without it. We told her that we wanted to confer with an attorney regarding our rights surrounding the violation of the FDCPA. The attorney suggested that we go ahead and refinance the loan with OMF since they were willing to remove the vehicle as collateral. I contactded [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] again to advise of the findings from our meeting with the attorney and she advised me that they would not be removing the vehicle from the loan and could only refinance the loan with the vehicle still listed as collateral. I have a recording of our full discussion where [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said they would remove the vehicle as collateral as well as the conversation about the employee who was terminated for the violations that were discovered.','ONEMAIN FINANCIAL HOLDINGS, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'one main financial loan is partially secured by a vehicle that we own. the loan is partially secured by a vehicle that we own. the creditor has received several calls and letters');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(4987,'02/22/2016','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','I paid my credit card balance of {$970.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16 due within the due date of the statement cycle and was charged interest of {$4.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16. They stated that the interest was charged because i had a previous statement cycle that was not paid off. Why would I get charged interest for paying the balance due for that month. My understanding is that this is not allowed under Regulation Z. Thanks','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'i paid my credit card balance of $970.00 on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/16');
