INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5049,'02/01/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','I signed up for a free bank account with PNC back in 2007 and just recently they said that my account was no longer free and I have a {$7.00} a month fee to maintain my account. I was grandfathered into the old terms which PNC and myself are bound.','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a free account with PNC was signed up in 2007. I have a $7.00 a month fee to maintain my account.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5050,'02/01/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','Hi my name is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Iam writing because I have medical issues that interfere with me constantly checking my account. I signed up with email and text notifications to alert me of any, including overdrafts I may incur due to the banks inaccurate online statements of available balances. Well Friday I was highly upset due to not knowing I had insufficient funds in my account. Yes I am now aware that merchants do n''t necessarily take funds out according to the order in which they were made. So at the time, I thought I had a balance in my account. The problem is the transaction happened Wednesday and I did n''t receive an overdraft notification until Friday at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the morning. If the notification was sent at a more accurate time to allow me time to cover the funds, I would have done so before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the prior day which is what a bank representative told me, would prevent the overdraft, but clearly if my balance is showing overdrawn not to my knowledge, the reason for signing up for notifications is pointless. Please help in this matter as I am never able to make resolve with my bank. I was charged an iverdraft fee and would like a refund due to the lack if the bank not notifying me or allowing me enough time to cover the fee like their policies state. Thank you','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'iverdrafts are a problem with my account. the bank has not been notified of the overdrafts. the bank has not been notified of the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5051,'01/31/2016','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Managing the loan or lease','This is a supplement to Case No. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : We have since received responses from the credit bureaus that Ditech said the credit reporting information was correct. Today, we received certified notices for homeowner counseling with a PAST DUE AMOUNT OF {$7400.00}. Ditech is obviously not recognizing the new contract that was put in place during bankruptcy and filed with the Court, and acknowledged by the Court. The credit reports now have " Charged Off '''' and {$0.00} past due. A [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2015 statement also states charged off, and {$0.00} past due, and now a new statement showing {$7400.00} past due. This is truly unbelievable. Do I need to take my savings and sue this company? They are in breach of contract, and have obviously violated FTC rules, wrong reporting on my credit report as Charged Off, rather than Included in Bankruptcy, and states {$0.00} due. So, technically it looks like on the credit reports we do n''t owe anything. How can a company do this to people. They depend on their attorneys to have political clout within the court system, but hopefully I can locate someone to sue them in Federal Court where the playing fields are somewhat more level. I feel sorry for people that dont understand their rights, but unfortunately to exercise your rights, it takes a lot of money, which I do n''t have obviously having gone through bankruptcy. Please advise the status of any assistance you can provide.','Ditech Financial LLC',2.0,2.0,'credit bureaus have responded to the claims that Ditech said the information was correct. the credit reports now have " Charged Off '''' and $0.00 past due ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5052,'01/30/2016','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I have a student loan with Wells Fargo that unfortunately became one of many bills that I was unable to keep up with due to a layoff experienced in late [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was laid off and unable to gain employment until late [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( 11 months 300+ days ) and nearly lost my home, vehicle, and dignity, due to my inability of upholding my end of the bargain. Along with these issues and losing nearly $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] per year in income, I also was unable to continue making student loan payments. As a result, my student loan charged off just weeks before obtaining a new job and receiving my first paycheck to avoid charge off. After re-establishing myself financially by saving my home through foreclosure prevention programs offered by the state, I ''ve been able to consistently make my payments as agreed. Wells Fargo has processed and performed a transaction on my account without any notice, knowledge, authorization or communication in the amount of {$2100.00}. This again was unauthorized. When I contacted Wells Fargo on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they advised me that they were unaware of unsure of why this occurred. I spoke to a supervisor by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said he would file a claim that could take up to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] business days and could not be reversed immediately because the Student Loan department was closed. I advised that I had made a recent transfer and that money that was deposited was to pay the mortgage of {$1700.00}. Wells Fargo has seen these recent payments from my account, because they are categorized utilizing THEIR VERY OWN Bill Pay Service, and they still would rather my family suffer the consequences of living on the street because they were unwilling and or unable to accept a student late payment to prevent a charge off. Not only was unemployment not a good enough reason to prevent charge-off and credit sufferings, they want me to lose my house as well. I thought I could trust Wells Fargo to allow me to regain my financial well being, not contribute to its demise.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a layoff in late [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] caused me to lose my home, vehicle, and dignity. a student loan charged off just weeks before');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5053,'01/30/2016','Debt collection','Credit card','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','Had Identity theft around or during time frame of said account. midland collections will not what so ever send any forms /paperwork to me when said account was open with credit [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with my signature that can prove that I did such a thing.','ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.',2.0,2.0,'midland collections will not send any forms /paperwork to me when said account was open.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5054,'01/29/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Rewards','PNC bank mailed me a physical letter advertising my pre-approval a new credit card with a promotional bonus of {$100.00} upon meeting certain requirements. After meeting the requirements no {$100.00} bonus was received. I spoke to a PNC bank escalation representative who asked for a copy of the offer, which I provided. I was then told by the representative that the {$100.00} credit would not be given because I was not eligible for the offer because I had previously received an unrelated bonus for an unrelated banking product. I still have the mailed printed offer explicitly outlining the terms of the disputed offer, and it contains no terms describing that I would be disqualified by receiving bonuses for unrelated banking products. 

If not for the bonus offer I would not have opened the line of credit which harms my credit score, affecting loan rates, and costing me time managing the credit line..','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a pc bank escalation representative mailed me a physical letter advertising my pre-approval a new credit card with a promotional bonus of $100');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5055,'01/29/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','I bank with BB & T. Recently they have overdraft my account when the funds are there. This has occurred on several occasions in the past few months and the trend is that this happens overnight when I have a paycheck pending electronic deposit. While in some cases I may not have the funds to cover all charges BB & T tends to push all charges through immediately. At other times pending charges may take days to process. The example below shows what I mean. I spoke with a representative at BB & T about the overdraft charges and I was told their system accounts for all charges pending or otherwise. So BB & T can make money off customers regardless of circumstances and that funds like a pending paycheck that will cover all charges is not counted. Mind you that they consider pending charges against the ledger but not pending paychecks. 

