INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5096,'01/16/2016','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','Earlier in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] someone changed my address and received my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] check then deposited it into her sole bank account at which time she was credited the money. The bank was made aware of the situation and still in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the bank has not returned my funds to me.','M&T BANK CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'the bank has not returned my funds to me.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5097,'01/15/2016','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Managing the loan or lease','Good morning, this is my third complaint about this company. My last complain number is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This company is a master of deception. Our first complain was in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. they said they would help us with the repairs of the car, and now their offering to pay us [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] out of a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollar tab. Than i offered them to accept if they would finance the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and they said no. And then i offered them to help me with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and i would buy my own engine, and i would have my own mechanic put it in and they said no. And then the representative claims we drove [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] miles when the claim clearly states the problems were present before we bought the vehicle. They are unwilling to work with me.','DriveTime',2.0,2.0,'a representative claims we drove [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] miles before we bought the vehicle. the representative claims the problems were present before we bought the vehicle.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5098,'01/15/2016','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','I opened an account with Synchrony Bank with a " promotional offering '''' of No Interest if Paid in Full within promotional period which ends [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016. This credit card was opened to purchase art work through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 billing charged {$470.00} interest on what appears to be a portion of {$1100.00} of the amount owned. An amount that is over 43 % interest. The amount due on account, to be paid in full without interest by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 is {$2000.00}.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'credit card opened to purchase art work through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2016 billing charged $470.00');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5099,'01/15/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I got a loan through The Money Source in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a primary residence. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] they sent me a letter stating that there was an escrow shortfall. I had to come up with another [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to cover the shortfall and even with this additional money my mortgage payments increased by ~ {$500.00}. In the meantime I was granted a 5 year property tax abatement by my township which effectively reduced my mortgage payments by ~35 %. I just received another letter from The Money Source stating that I had another escrow shortfall. They have now instructed me to pay another {$2400.00} and that my mortgage will increase, yet again, by another {$400.00}. I then went to the tax office in my township and requested a copy of the property taxes I paid last year. When I called the representative who handled my case back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we went through the numbers and there is some mysterious amount of over {$7000.00} that is listed as an " actual '''' payment that does not match up in any way with the document I received from the township. The statement The Money Source sent is very confusing and has " actual '''' payments and disbursements listed. What ''s the difference? Either they are guilty of gross negligence in calculating my property taxes not once, not twice, but three times ( because they also got it wrong prior to my closing ) or they are a predatory lender. The way the conversation ended was I was told that I had to pay the new mortgage amount, which now represents an ~ {$900.00} increase from the amount I was originally quoted I would have to pay, by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The statement I received is dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but I just received it today, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','MONEY SOURCE, THE',2.0,2.0,'the money source sent me a letter stating that there was an escrow shortfall. the letter was sent to me by the money source. the money source has now instructed');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5100,'01/14/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','From conference calls XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ],XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ],XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it became clear - because Wells mentioned it -- Wells ran a 3rd appraisal they never told us about, once again drive-by though I requested many times an on-site appraisal. I need to see this appraisal and I have 30 days to examine and/or dispute it - not only under Dodd-Frank, but the FCRA Fair Credit Reporting Act { 15 U.S.C. 1681 } as outlined by the Comptroller of the Currency, Administrator of National Banks holds that if adverse action was taken against the consumer, the consumer has 60 days from discovery of this information to " obtain and examine the details of the negative information so that if erroneous, the consumer can correct it. '''' Adverse action is defined as " an action in connection with an account that is adverse to the consumer ''s interests. '''' Furthermore, Section 615 ( b ) ( 1 ) states that if the adverse action taken was based on information obtained from a third party ( such as a third party appraiser ) then this information must be provided to the consumer within a reasonable period of time. That being said, please send me this third appraisal you mentioned on our phone call as required by law. 
( 3 ) But perhaps the most surprising and unfortunate revelation from our last phone call was Wells mention of the possibility of a " partial reinstatement '''' for an amount less than our full arrears - proving that, all along, going back to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] offers to bring the loan current in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments before we even entered the mod process - Wells can and does accept payment arrangements - as mentioned in their Notice of Default - they just do n''t offer these arrangements in a timely manner because it is their preference ( more profitable ) for Wells to foreclose. 
Further problems with Wells servicing include asking me to enumerate my concerns with their modification, then leaving me a subsequent phone message - about a whole new raft of items ( pay stubs, etc ) they would like to see from me, " moving forward. '''' The problem with this is they are picking and choosing which banking laws they ''re going to comply with and which not as they go along, what the deadlines are and even if there are any, asking me to jump through hoops they are arbitrarily creating, when in fact there is much federal and state law that defines how you should have handled my modification already and should be handling it now. 
Under the Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act ( RESPA ) as administered by the Department of Housing & Urban Development, Wells has established a " pattern of non-compliance, '''' for which there are civil penalties. This is Title 12 Chapter 27 US Code 2605 section F " pattern of non-compliance. '''' By pattern of non-compliance I mean every step of the way, Wells has not abided by how Dodd-Frank demands a modification must be run -- the consumer ''s right to see and dispute my NPV data inputs, my right to dispute your shoddy drive-by appraisals, and so forth. As recently as XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the Wells servicing associate [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said in a recorded phone conversation : " Why do we need to re-run your NPV with the corrected inputs - it ''s not going to make a difference so long as there ''s equity in your home you ''ll never get modified anyway. '''' This is like saying " we ''re not going to read this guy his [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because we ''ve already decided the verdict. '''' But Dodd-Frank is the law, I have numerous times requested my NPV be re-run with my thorough appraisal, and Wells has yet to comply. However they have established a very thorough pattern of non-compliance. Last thing : Wells put an underwriter on the phone with me who said, " We DID our job, got you your keys and got you in your house. '''' I had to point out I never applied for a Wells loan, my loan was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but it ''s a good indicator of how little Wells servicers actually understand or care.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'if adverse action was taken against the consumer, the consumer has 60 days to examine the details. if adverse action was taken against the consumer, the consumer can correct it. Well');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5101,'01/14/2016','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Credit decision / Underwriting','Capital One is processing a mortgage application for a condominium and demanding a totally irrational level of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] insurance. The association master policy provides cover for unit interior to original plans and specs. The master policy excludes improvements and betterments, which the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] policy should cover. The unit being purchased has no improvements and betterments ; it is the unit as conveyed to the original purchaser by the developer. Capital One ''s requirement for {$290000.00} of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] coverage is completely baseless because there is not property of even a fraction of that value to insure. It is more than three times the coverage I would purchase that would include the value of personal property. Appropriate coverage would cost me about {$500.00} per year, not $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$1500.00}.','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'association master policy provides cover for unit interior to original plans and specs. the unit being purchased has no improvements and betterments. the unit being purchased has no improvements and betterments.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5102,'01/14/2016','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Settlement process and costs','LenderFi, Inc. created multiple delays in processing our loan documents, eventually necessitating a rate lock extension with a {$780.00} fee. At one point we were told that documents faxed in by our agent had mistakenly been sitting on someone ''s desk for 3 weeks. In addition, the morning the appraisal was scheduled we received an email stating that we failed to qualify, and so we delayed the appraisal over a weekend, by which time they had reversed this position and we were able to have the appraisal immediately performed. 
LenderFi President [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told us that they would only pay half of the {$780.00} fee due to our role in delaying the appraisal, which we agreed to. He stated on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( via text message to our real estate agent ) that he was mailing a check for {$390.00}. We have yet to receive this check, and have been unable to contact him since.','Lenderfi, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a rate lock extension with a $780.00 fee was due to delay. a faxed in email was sent to us stating that we failed to');
