INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5146,'12/29/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','Equifax is violating my rights to an honest and true credit report by reporting to the public records section of my file and outdated and inaccurate tax lien that was made in error many years ago. The filed date is incorrect and the item does not include the lien removal slip which was granted by the judge following my attorney adamant appeal at the debt placed against me by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] board of California. I have asked this information to be verified and have forwarded my tax removal slip to the bureau to be propeller verified and I requested a full and complete report domineering their pruderies and desciprtion during this reinvestigation process nearly 6 months ago and have been provided with ABSOLUTELY NOTHING! I am infuriated and disgusted by this poor attempt at a reinvestigation in my part and have become utterly anxious at the way my credit report is currently being reflected. It is not 100 % accurately because of this tax liens and the mis information it contains and i have been denied a lawful investigation. I have waited past the 30 day mark threefold of a time an don longer will wait for anything to be verified. I will not give this bureau anymore chanced to validate or verify anything. I have had enough and they are required by law, to follow the law, an removed tax lien ... [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from my records. It is their responsibility to validate this and they have NOT and it is their responsibility to provide me procedures and the descriptions and they have NOT. Why do i have NOTHING from this company and yet they are allowed to still report this? Why is it that i have mailed them every piece of document i can and the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] recorders office claims that they have receive don calls or validation requests from this bureau? What is it that has validated this? No one and nothing! They claim to use a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] party vendor and REFUSE to disclose anything about who they are and how they operate and validate consumer information. I will NOT rely on a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] party vendor with my financial life on the line, that is insane and not fair nor is this acceptable. Is this vendor certified? Is this vendor in the United States? Is this vendor knowledgable in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] court systems? DO they have full and complete access to my report and all of my appeals and court records? When was this Vendor last certified and is their software up to date and FCRA certified and compatible with the law and guidelines? I WOULD NOT KNOW BECAUSE THIS VENDOR IS A MYSTERY AND THIS VENDOR IS RUINING MY LIFE!','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'i have been denied a lawful investigation by the federal court. i have had enough and they are required by law to follow the law. they have NOT. ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5147,'12/29/2015','Payday loan',NULL,'Charged fees or interest I didn''t expect','I opened a payday loan with Speedy Cash in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014 and was charged extremely high loan fees. I filed Chapter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bankruptcy in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014 and reported all of my debts to the attorney. This account is still open and this pay day loan company located in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Texas ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) refuses to acknowledge that I am in bankruptcy. I have filed a dispute with the credit reporting agencies but I have not received a satisfactory judgement.','CURO Intermediate Holdings',2.0,2.0,'payday loan company in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Texas refuses to acknowledge that I am in bankruptcy.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5148,'12/29/2015','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Settlement process and costs','Hello, I am contacting you regarding a loan modification agreement that I received. Due to the mortgage crisis my home is severely under water. Further, due to the increased amount of crime in the area and the need for more space I opted to apply for a short sale versus walking away from my home. I initially had contact with Relationship Manager, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], at U.S. Bank Home Mortgage regarding a short sale. She informed me that my paperwork was reviewed and I qualified for a loan modification instead of a short sale. I agreed to the loan modification because I wanted to take the best path to protect my credit as much as possible. Additionally, I would be in a better position to find a renter if the payments were lower without me having to make up the difference between the rent payments received and my mortgage payment. She also informed me that the terms of the agreement would remain the same ( 13 years remaining on my mortgage ) ; however, the monthly payments would be reduced. She further stated that I would have to undergo a 90 day trial period and after the trial my payments would remain the same, decrease or increase slightly ; however, the number of years remaining on the loan would remain the same. I agreed to the terms and entered the trial period. 

I received a telephone call indicating that I successfully completed the trial period and that I would be receiving the final modification package in the mail. I received the paperwork for my final modification and the information appeared to be different from what I agreed to. I contacted my current relationship manager, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and was informed that the terms of the loan would be 30 years. I informed him that that information was different from what I was given by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I requested to speak with his manager, and I was informed that she was on vacation. I was transferred to another supervisor who informed me that the notes clearly state that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] informed me that the terms of my loan would remain the same and I only had 13 years remaining on the loan and would have 13 years remaining after the modification. She stated that she does not know where [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] got that information from and that she was sorry for her giving me that incorrect information because she should have known better. She informed me that she no longer works for the company. 

It should be noted that the terms of the mortgage agreement is not listed on the original paperwork that I received in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Therefore, I agreed to the program based on the expertise of your employee. 

Further, I do n''t fell like I should be penalized based of the incorrect information provided by the bank ''s employee. I tried to do the correct thing by contacting the bank in an attempt to mitigate the damages instead of walking away from the home like many others have done. Further, a review of my credit reveals that it has been reported to the credit reporting agency that I was late on my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s payment ; however, I made all of the payments as agreed. I was not informed that being on a trial payment plan would result in a negative credit report. Nor would I have signed up for the program if I had known that my mortgage would be extended 30 years and not remain at the current terms with lower payments. This entire ordeal has been extremely stressful based on the fact that I was informed that if I wanted to apply for a short sale now I have to decline the modification and start the entire process over again. I think that the original terms should be honored as the notes clearly state that that was the information that was provided to me. I would appreciate it if a manager would review the account to see if anything can be done regarding this matter. 

Thank you in advance for your attention to this matter. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a short sale is a loan modification agreement that I received from a relationship manager. the agreement would remain the same, but the monthly payments would be reduced. the terms of');
