INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5197,'12/09/2015','Debt collection','Credit card','Disclosure verification of debt','I received a notice this year from the IRS stating that Discover sent them a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for an old collection where pmts had not been made since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I did not settle this debt nor did I receive a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from the to file on my XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] taxes. Also, Discover still shows that I owe the full amount of this debt as a collection on my credit report and is still updating with no mention of settlement for less than balance. The IRS says I owe them {$1000.00} and wants me to consent to changing my return. This debt has exceeded the Statute of Limitations and is set to be removed from my credit report XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have disputed this with the IRS and sent them a copy of my credit report showing this but they just keep sending me the same letter. I think it is wrong for them to side with Discover. Can you help me?','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'the IRS says I owe the full amount of this debt as a collection on my credit report. I did not settle this debt nor did I receive a [COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5198,'12/08/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Other','I honestly believe Citi Bank and Sears set out to defraud me. I was lied to by Sears Salesman to get me to buy a poor quality home improvement product which was poorly installed at an overly inflated price. I question the fact it was too high priced {$11000.00} for just the gable ends and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] lean to wall. I was told I was getting perks for example lifetime wholesale buying on any Sears product. I found out a month later this was a lie when I went to buy a washer at Sears. I called Citi Bank Sears Card complaining that I did not get what I paid for. I would be placed on hold or forward to another customer service in another part of the world. I never got to talk to the dispute dept until I stopped paying on the card this past [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015. I tried writing and calling two years but continue to make payments until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2015. I paid {$4800.00} which I want refunded. The siding is falling apart after year and half. I would have never bought this if I was n''t made false promises to lure me in. Citi is constantly calling me telling me I owe over {$10000.00}. This is a joint corporate scam. Sears card should be shutdown. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on a fixed income and was taken advantage of. I want my money back please and no blemish on my credit. Please help me.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,4.0,'Citi Bank and Sears lied to me to buy a poor quality home improvement product. a month later, a customer service service in another part of the world was ');
