I called DFS again on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15, explained again and was told that I had to pay. I told them I refused to pay and asked again to cancel my account, which they agreed to do. 
On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sent a notice that they consider the transaction valid and would notify the credit reporting agencies of my refusal to pay the disputed charge. 

My dispute is with DFS : How can they expect me to pay a charge from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had already canceled? This is after DFS resolved the dispute in my favor and closed the investigation. This is DFS case number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have copies of all statements and relevant documents. I will contact the credit reporting agencies to notify them that I refuse to pay [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a service they did not provide and I refuse to pay DFS for failure to recognize an improper charge. I feel that DFS has abused the credit card relationship.','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'my Discover card bill dated [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 reinstated the charge. the service person');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5204,'12/06/2015','Debt collection','Non-federal student loan','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','American Education Services is calling me every day about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] missed payment, the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment. According to my bank records a check was sent to them on XX/XX/2015 and cashed on XX/XX/2015. They say they have no record of the payment. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who verified that the payment was made on XX/XX/2015. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has attempted to contact AES by telephone but received busy Signals. 

