INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5234,'11/24/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Other','We accidentally overpaid our Discover bill by approximately {$15000.00}. We called more than a week ago and we were assured that a check would be sent to us in a day. After not receiving the check after about a week, we called and spoke with a customer service representation who assured us that the check had been mailed " that day ''''. We doubted the veracity of this claim and asked to speak with a supervisor who said the check had not been mailed ( admitted that they had lied to us on two occasions ), and the could n''t tell us when we could expect a refund.','DISCOVER BANK',2.0,2.0,'we overpaid Discover bill by approximately $15000.00. we called and spoke with a customer service representation who assured us that the check had been mailed "that day ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5235,'11/24/2015','Debt collection','I do not know','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','This company has called me regarding debt that belongs to someone else. I do not have, nor have I ever had, business or an account with Wells Fargo. I have asked them repeatedly to cease and desist calling me regarding someone else''s debt. I even had someone fill out a cease and desist form. They have called me every two to three days since XX/XX/2015, sometimes leaving a message or, using a robo-dialer, leaving a message with no content. These attempts are in violation of the Fair Credit Reporting Act and in violation of the do not call list, as I have no debt owed to them and have not given them permission to contact me in any form.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'company has called me regarding debt that belongs to someone else. they have called me every two to three days since XX/XX/2015. they have called me every two');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5236,'11/23/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] program sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] e-mails to us in two days with our account number, but someone else ''s name, indicating that they are suspending our mortgage payment program. They indicated that their banks have stopped handling the mortgage deductions. They did take payments [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments on our first and second mortgages. We are told that we must make the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payments ourselves. We called the company and asked about fee refunds. They said the account is only suspended and not closed, so they are not refunding fees. We feel that we have been scammed and given only part of the story. We want to protect ourselves in this situation. What action of the CFPB caused the banks to stop supporting the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] program? Will the program be resuming as indicated in our call to them? If it will resume, when might that happen? Can we trust the information coming from the company?','Nationwide Biweekly Administration, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'e-mails sent to us in two days with account number, but someone else''s name'' they indicated that their banks have stopped handling the deductions. they did take');
