INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5297,'11/02/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','I am filing this complaint because Equifax has ignored my request to provide me with the documents that their company has on file that was used to verify the accounts I disputed. Being that they have gone past the 30 day mark and can not verify these accounts, under Section 611 ( 5 ) ( A ) of the FCRA-they are required to " promptly delete all information which can not be verified '''' that I have disputed. Please resolve this manner as soon as possible. Thank You','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'Equifax has ignored my request to provide me with the documents that they have on file that was used to verify the accounts I disputed. they are required to delete all information which can not');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5298,'11/02/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','I went to my local credit union and applied for a checking account. I was denied for a traditional checking account and was offered a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] chance checking account. Once you have had the checking account active for 12 months you can request a review to be considered for a regular checking account. Coming up XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] will be 12 months that I have had the account open. I was advised by the bank rep that it came up in their system that I owe Wells Fargo and that they submitted information to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that shows I mismanaged an account with them. The concern is that if I mismanaged an account with them. Then why would they allow me to open another account with them after reporting this information. Basicly its telling other banks not to do business with me, but it ''s ok for me to do business with them after they have reported this negative information. They are also reporting a balance after I paid the account off in 2014. The information they are reporting remains in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for 7 years and will limit you from obtaining a standard checking account instead of a second chance checking account.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a bank rep told me that it came up in their system that I owe Wells Fargo. the bank rep said they submitted information to [COMPTE_ANON');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5299,'11/01/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','After this issue had been resolved with a collection agency for an agreed amount on behalf of the creditor [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the file is again reopened for a third time after this had already been settled. These people are seeking a vendetta against me and seemingly are continuing to resubmit these derogatory credit filings to the agencies to reap their revenge for what I do n''t know.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'the file is again reopened for a third time after this had already been settled. the files are reopened for a third time after this had been resolved.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5300,'11/01/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Customer service / Customer relations','For over month citi bank financial websites have been down for my Macys credit card and my best buy credit card. I ''m unable to track my spending, check when my bills or due, or make payments. Not only are there websites down but when I call there are really long waits to talk to someone. I should be able to monitor my activities and keep track of my account at any moment to make sure that I ''m using my cards responsibility. Citi bank is making tracking/monitoring difficult.','CITIBANK, N.A.',4.0,4.0,'citi bank financial websites have been down for my Macys credit card. I''m unable to track my spending, check when my bills or due'' and make payments.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5301,'10/31/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','First Merit Bank and its employee [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] committed fraud by lying to me on more than one occasion. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2015, in response to the Bank ''s advertisement for free checking, I inquired in person at its [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Ohio branch. The ad stated " no minimum balance '''' and " no monthly maintenance fee ''''. I asked about transfer of money and was told by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I could transfer the money anywhere without a fee. I and my husband, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], spent considerable time asking questions, including " whether there were any hidden fees ''''. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] repeatedly stated that the account was totally free. He also told me that I would be given a {$150.00} bonus if I set up direct deposit. Based on his extensive information and answers, I opened a checking account. The person who handled the opening, under the direction of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], is identified on the receipt as " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''''. I was given a receipt for the deposit, but NO schedule of fees, which I did not expect because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] told me that there were no fees. 
I then went through the timely effort of switching my direct deposit instructions with my employer. 
Shortly afterwards, when I tried to transfer money from this account, I learned that there would be a fee. I complained in person to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He then told me that only transfers to another account at First Merit Bank are free ( which he knew I did not have ) and that transfers to other institutions required payment of fees. I, with my husband present during this discussion, requested that my account be closed because he, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], had given me wrong information at the time I opened the account. To cover his earlier lies, he said that there would be a fee if I closed the account within 90 days. I was never informed of this when I opened the account, being told that there were no fees whatsoever. He refused to give me the full balance in my account. 
So, based on his advice to " wait at least three months to get ALL of your money back '''', I did not withdraw any money. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], never told me that by waiting I would be charged an inactivity fee. Again, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] committed fraud by misleading me. 
Shortly afterwards because I could not transfer my money out to another institution without being charged a fee on the " free '''' checking promised by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I went through additional effort to change my direct deposit of salary from First Merit Bank back to my previous bank. 
I was never credited {$150.00} for setting up direct deposit with First Merit Bank. 
Today, I went to the same branch to withdraw the balance of my money and close the not useful account. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] failed to give me the full amount I had deposited, but kept {$28.00} of my money. When I asked him why he had not given me the full amount of my deposit, he stated that there was an inactive account fee. I was never informed of this, either at the time of opening the account or when I complained about his lying about free transfers. 
When my husband complained to him about the lousy service and asked to have the branch manager informed, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with a mean look on his face and a shouted voice, threatened to " escort ( him ) outside '''', saying that he, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], did not want any other customer to hear a complaint. 
First Merit Bank employee [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] repeatedly misled me and lied to me. He did not once indicate that there were any fees, but repeatedly stated that there were none. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should be fired for purposely deceiving a consumer and First Merit Bank should both be fined for its fraud upon the public and institute a mandatory retraining of all its employees regarding not lying to, but informing, potential and actual customers of fees. 
Furthermore, First Merit Bank should refund to me {$28.00} plus interest and pay me {$150.00} for setting up direct deposit based upon its fraud.','HUNTINGTON NATIONAL BANK, THE - FIRSTMERIT BANK, N.A. BRANCH',2.0,4.0,'first Merit Bank and its employee committed fraud by lying to me. ad stated " no minimum balance '''' and " no monthly maintenance fee ''''. a');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5302,'10/31/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Unable to get credit report/credit score','why should I have to write a letter to get my information, what is the problem it is telling me I need to write a letter to get it. this is time consuming not realistic today, people use the computer for everything and phones and email. now I have wasted time and more time because I need my credit information now! there should not be any issue with getting it online, and it does not tell me the reason. no security issue should not be handled that way because I still do n''t know the issue. I do n''t have time for this. this needs to be fixed and better convenient for people. we have to be systemized to do anything! is unfair!','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a letter to get my information is telling me why should I have to write. a letter to get my information is a problem. it is time consuming and not realistic');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5303,'10/30/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I was taken to small claims court for a parking lot accident that the law enforcement rules " no fault ''''. The other party involved sued me for damages to his vehicle because he only had liability. My insurance counter sued him and the courts ruled in my favor. I even got my deductible back. I do n''t understand why I have a negative mark on my credit report when the courts ruled in my favor and I won court lawsuit. This unnecessary negative mark is hurting my credit and I would like it resolved.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',4.0,6.0,'insurance counter sued me for damages to his vehicle because he only had liability. my insurance counter sued him and the courts ruled in my favor.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5304,'10/30/2015','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Application, originator, mortgage broker','We called to begin the loan process XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and signed our application docs right away. Once requested, we handed in all of our underwriting docs within a few days. We requested an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] closing date. Because we were unsure if our builder would be ready on that date ( new construction ) they decided to use the date of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We were fine with that. They ensured they would do their best to beready by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] just in case. As we got closer the builder informed us the house would be ready to close on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We relayed that informaion to the broker. The broker then told us the lender ( another company ) was working towards an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] date. We had never heard [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] previously and were confused. The broker said they would try to move quicker but the appraisal was not done. Not only not done, but the appraiser had n''t even been out to see the house. In the meantime, the appraisal had been ordered over ten days prior and our credit card already charged. The appraiser did not go out to our new property until Monday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Later that day the broker emailed us a list of new conditions required to close. Example, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for a previous rented apartment that came up on our credit report. Another item was a 2014 EOY paystub because my VOE and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was off. We were again confused because our broker had told us they had eveyrthing they needed from us and wondered why did they not ask for these items earlier. I would like to mention we began being frustrated since missing the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] date ( however that one was somewhat understandable ). Missing an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] closing ( the date on our application docs ) was even more disappointing. We were still counting on an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] closing but then guess what, more things came up. We continued to hand in everything the broker asked for right away. Today is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Clealy I am not closing. We had to ask for an extension from our landlord to stay in our current residence - we were given only 4 extra days at a high daily rate. We were thankful to not be without anywhere to go and were told we would be closing Monday or Tuesday of next week. Still this is cutting it very close because we need to close, move, and clean our old place in one or two days. All of our things have been packed and we ''ve been living out of boxes since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] thinking anyday we ''d be closing. Today we were notified the Tax Cert is incorrect and the broker said " it should have been fixed weeks ago. '''' This could add additional days. Now we are scheduled to close Wednesday XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] " at best. '''' That gives us ONE day to close, move, and clean if we even get to close that day. In my prespective we have missed [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] closing dates. We went into a whole other month ( changing pre-paids, and many other scheduled peices ). I am about to have no where to go and no where for my belongings if we do n''t close by Wednesday and it feels like no one seems to care. The appraisal being late is not our fault. The Tax Cert being incorrect and not fixed on time is not our fault. Yet we will be the ones to suffer. By contract, the builder will be allowed to take the home away from us that we have been building for the last ten months if we are not ready to close by Tuesday. The market price on our new construction home is already up $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which we cant afford so we can not lose this house! The broker claims to be doing all her can yet does n''t sound like he can do anything but relay messages. The lender, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], has made too many errors that are greatly affecting us and we feel no one is being held accountable. This is unacceptable to us, but it seems the lender and broker are just going along as if everything is fine and it ''s okay to continue pushing our closing date again and again.','HOMEBRIDGE FINANCIAL SERVICES, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the broker told us the house would be ready to close on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_');
