INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5311,'10/28/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I received a final bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that was not correct. I disputed the charges and after almost 2 weeks of email correspondences with their collections manager, I finally received notification from their accounting department stating that they found their error and they would be sending a refund check on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15. Included in this email was a notice from the accountant to the collection manager to remove my name from their collection agency. On Friday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I received a phone call from the National Credit Audit Corporation threatening to report my disputed balance if full payment was n''t received by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15. I tried to explain the situation and that I had an email confirming that this had been resolved to which he responded that unless he received something directly from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] he would pursue collections. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] properties collections department, who I was directly reporting to, is closed on Fridays so I emailed them explaining the situation and then have tried to call them repeatedly on Monday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Tuesday ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and can not get a response even after leaving multiple messages to multiple staff. When I could n''t get a hold of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I contacted the collection agency to update them on my actions and at that time the representative working my account implied that I was being untruthful and again threatened to pursue collection if I did n''t pay the account balance immediately. I feel that this has been turned over to collection in error. My final bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I was originally disputing was n''t due until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 so even if I did n''t have an email from them telling me that they found their error, I still would n''t be delinquent to the point of being turned over for collection and having it reported to the credit bureau. As of this date, I have not received any mail correspondence from the collection agency which I feel does n''t qualify as proper notification of a debt due. If [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] would respond to my emails and numerous phone messages I feel this would be resolved quickly and easily by a call to the collection agency informing them that I have a zero balance due.','First Advantage LNS Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a final bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was not correct. the accounting department found the error and sent a refund check. the bill was ');
