INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5384,'10/06/2015','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] have been trying to make additional loan payments to principal since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014. Navient has continually made processing errors ( including not making payments recurring as directed and promised and not making payments in the proper amount ) and providing incorrect information regarding manually making additional payments. This has resulted in a continual halt on progress in paying down my student loans, which the company takes no responsibility for. The representatives will apologize for previous errors, but will not take actions to retroactively correct them ; although they promise to " personally monitor '''' future payments, I never receive the in-writing confirmation that they promise. I have also requested documentation including my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and loan disclosures be sent, which I ''m told has a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day delivery window via USPS. To date, I have not received these documents and have just made another request for them today. 

Most recently, I was advised that if my billing due date is on a weekend, I should schedule an additional principal payment for the first business day following as their online system does not allow scheduling payments on a Saturday or Sunday. Following the representative ''s instruction resulted in two days of accrued interest taken out of my additional payment ( due date Saturday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. payment scheduled for Monday [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). The supervisor I spoke with today sent in a request that my payment be made effective on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as I was given faulty information, but can not guarantee that any action will be taken. I was advised instead to schedule additional payments on the Friday before any weekend due date, although this may still result in accrued interest charges. 

Each time I have to call Navient I can count on at least 45 minutes to an hour or more of my life wasted. Navient engages in shady business practices that not only waste my time and money, but also appear to be illegal ( if not absolutely immoral ). I have no recourse other than to continue wasting my time and energy with a customer service department that is inept, uninformed and makes " promises '''' and " guarantees '''' that they do not keep. 

I have a record of most of my calls since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014, including names and promises made.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a supervisor sent in a request that my payment be made effective on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as a result of faulty information. the supervisor who');
