INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5389,'10/04/2015','Debt collection','Credit card','Taking/threatening an illegal action','A collection attorney named Forster & Garbus is trying to sue me for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card account that is no longer on my credit report. The credit card account is from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which is more than seven years ago. I live in New York [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the statue of limitation is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years on credit card accounts. I do not want this collection attorney to try to seize my checking account because I am barely living above the poverty rate. I can not afford to pay this debt and plus the debt is more than seven years ago and it is no longer on my credit report. The debt is pass the statue of limitations in New York State.','Forster & Garbus LLP',2.0,2.0,'collection attorney is trying to sue me for a credit card account. the debt is passed the statue of limitations in new york state.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5390,'10/03/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Billing statement','I applied for and received a credit card from american express. I have just received my first bill and no where on it is found my account number with the company. This is the first time I have ever experienced this ; in my opinion it should be illegal. No other credit card company I know of does this. I thought I had misplaced the card as I attempted to setup a bank payment for the bill for which the account number is of course required ; it took me some period of time, but I finally found it. I should not have been put to this trouble ; this is security taken a step too far - I should like to see this stopped before it becomes a fashion among the credit card issuers.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'american express has just received my first bill and nowhere on it is found my account number. this is the first time I have ever experienced this.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5391,'10/02/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','Once I refinanced my mortgage in 2013, Wells Fargo opened a checking account for me. I have no active recollection of agreeing to that, but I assume the paperwork was among the massive volume of papers to sign with the mortgage. The account was never used and dormant until two months ago when [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] started to charge me a $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] monthly fee for this account. 
