INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5400,'09/30/2015','Payday loan',NULL,'Received a loan I didn''t apply for','There is a loan on my credit report for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and a duplicate for Ad Astra for the same debt. I did not apply for this loan. I have requested documentation to prove that this loan was applied for by me and the debt collection agency gave me a checking account and said the money had been deposited into this account. I have not used the checking account for more than 5 years prior to the date of when the debt collector said I applied for the loan. I attempted to speak with the debt collector and I have on a recorded phone file where the debt collector threatened to have me arrested at my place of employment. The debt collector also told me that they would call my HR department and garnish my wages. On another day, the debt collector called and stated he was a police officer. I made a police report and the Police Dept in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that there was a scam going on and that this had occurred to many people where there identity had been compromised. My identity was compromised during an employment layoff XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] by the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and this is the only way they could have gotten my information. I have contacted the credit bureau more than 10 times, my attorney [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] firm has requested documentation and neither of us have received documentation nor updates for more than 2 years.','Ad Astra Recovery Services Inc',2.0,2.0,'debt collector threatened to have me arrested at my place of employment. he called police and said he was a police officer. he said he was a police officer');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5401,'09/30/2015','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','Made a purchase on my Best Buy credit card ( Citibank ) a little over 2 years ago that was approx. {$1000.00}. Have made regular on-time payments to date. I am a regular Best Buy customer so I periodically make small purchases for office needs and put on same card. The {$1000.00} ( 2-years ago ) purchase should have been paid off long ago. However, I was just notified I am being charged $ 700+ ( 29.9 % ) interest on that particular purchase because it had not been paid off. When I inquired where had all my payments been going for the past 2 years, I discovered they had been applying them to my ongoing purchases instead of the large purchase from 2 years ago. I now have a {$700.00} interest penalty on a {$1000.00} purchase. 
I thought the new credit laws were enacted to protect the consumer? This is not only completely unethical, but discourages customers to continue doing business with a retailer after a promotional purchase. 
I want my payments to apply to my promotional purchases first, or oldest purchase, not to ones with highest interest rate, such as current purchases.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a little over 2 years ago, I made a purchase on my Best Buy credit card. the $1000.00 purchase should have been paid off long ago. but');
