INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5426,'09/22/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 I received an email that my account was overdrawn. When I opened up my account, I had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$36.00} overdraft fees. I immediately started reviewing the account and could not find where it was overdrawn. I contacted PNC Bank to inquire about the fees. In the chat with the representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it was stated that the check I deposited was n''t cleared until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On the online tool that they provide it clearly states that my check was cleared on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and all of the transactions were posted after the check was cleared. The representative said that the check was not cleared until XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. PNC bank provides this tool for consumers to to keep track of their spending, but are now telling me that it is not accurate. I have attached a copy of my transcript, a screenshot of the transactions which do not show my account in the negative, and a previous overdraft which does show my account in the negative. If the tool is inaccurate, then it should not be made available to the consumers.','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a representative said that my check was cleared on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and all of the transactions were posted after the check was');
