INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5430,'09/21/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Identity theft / Fraud / Embezzlement','GECRB/AMAZON PLCC has been reporting an account to which is NOT mine. Following it ''s discovery I submitted a demand for validation of debt and following their failure to do so, I sent the a motion to bring complaint under [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for unfair and deceptive practices and acts, to that they have also failed to respond appropriately. The company has violated multiple State and Federal laws in regards to FACTA and FDCPA regulations and suggest strongly that they are held accountable for said actions and sited for all violations in accordance with Federal Statutes.','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'the company has violated multiple state and federal laws in regards to FACTA and FDCPA regulations. the company has also failed to respond appropriately.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5431,'09/20/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Deposits and withdrawals','I am trustee for my mother ''s insurance trust account. I have a Wells Fargo checking account [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I use [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a year to pay the premium for the insurance policy set up in this trust.. I have never had a debit card for this account. I keep over {$1500.00} in the account so that fees will not be charged. Once a year I make [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] large deposit and write [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] large check. 
I had a balance of {$2000.00} in the account after the check was written in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for that year ''s premium. The bank does not mail statements to me nor do I access the account online. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], as I was preparing to make a deposit and write a check, I discovered that the balance had dwindled to almost nothing. I immediately contacted bank officials, met with a bank official at my local branch bank and filed Claim # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] requesting full restitution of the balance of {$2000.00} that was in the account.. Somehow someone had accessed the card number..[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] assigned to this account and since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was using the card number to make automatic payments to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. All of these charges were coming out of my checking account. Of course I expected either Wells Fargo or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or both to reimburse the money that was stolen from my account. Bottom line, Wells Fargo is responsible as far as I am concerned. Banks are responsible for having adequate security systems so that clients '' money is not stolen while it is in the bank. Banks should not expect clients to be responsible for poor security when the client has done nothing to cause a security breach. That is the bank ''s responsibility. 
However, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Senior Vice President of Claims Assistance Center of Wells Fargo, wrote a letter to me refusing to pay the entire amount stolen from the account - he agreed to pay {$1000.00}, which he said was the amount charged in the 60 days prior to my complaint - for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He claims that I should have been monitoring the account constantly and should have reported the discrepancy within 60 days. Because {$2000.00} was stolen, then {$2000.00} should be returned by Wells Fargo. They owe me the other {$1000.00} plus monthly service fees that they have charged due to a less than {$1500.00} balance. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter stated that they had removed any service fees, but that had not been done as of XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Of course because of their refusal to replace the stolen money, the account balance is below {$1500.00} although it should be {$2000.00}. Surely they will not charge me service fees because they have refused to bring my account balance up to what it should be..','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,4.0,'a year ago, a balance of $2000.00 was written in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the balance');
