INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5444,'09/16/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I have a serious problem with disconnects between credit scores. I recently obtained my fico scores from my fico. The scores reported were Equifax [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I thought these scores were n''t great but the were high enough for me to qualify for a mortgage. Wrong. I find that they have a separate score foe mortgages that were about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] points LOWER than the scores given to me. How can this be? So here I am excited at the prospect of owning my home and I come to find out that probably will never be. Yes I have had some credit problems 6 years ago! I would like to know how these scores are derived. Something has to be amiss. I am a single mother and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] veteran and because of these faulty scores I ca n''t even use my va loan benefit. It appears that this whole credit reporting thing is a scam. In the past 2 weeks I ''ve spent about {$100.00} to get faulty information. These people are not regulated properly and people with mistakes that the credit bureaus refuse to fix pay the price.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a single mother and a veteran of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] veteran, I have had some credit problems 6 years ago. I have spent about ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5445,'09/15/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','A dispute was submitted to Equifax on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] due to an account being inaccurately reporting on my Consumer Credit Report. Supporting documents were submitted from the data furnisher that I received to support my claim that the account was being inaccurately reported on my Consumer Credit Report. Equifax failed to investigate the matter properly in addition to disregarding the supporting evidence. A Consumer Reporting Agency ''s reinvestigation obligation is to verify the accuracy of its original source of information. This duty may include going beyond the original source. Whether the credit reporting agency must go beyond the original source depends on a number of factors, including : ( 1 ) whether the consumer has alerted the CRA that the original source may be unreliable ; ( 2 ) whether the CRA itself knows or should know that the original source is unreliable ; and ( 3 ) the comparative costs of verifying the accuracy of the original sources versus the potential harm the inaccurate information may cause the consumer. See : [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Experian Information Solutions , Inc., [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). Please be advised that under Section 611 ( 5 ) ( A ) of the FCRA - you are required to ( A ) promptly DELETE all information which can not be verified. Pursuant to the FCRA in 609 ( c ) ( 2 ) ( E ) ; " A consumer reporting agency is not required to remove accurate derogatory information from a consumer ''s file, unless the information is outdated and or can not be verified. I request my private right of action pursuant but not limited to 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2, 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2b and 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( 6 ) ( A ) ( B ) and ( 15 U.S.C. 1692g ). Account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting inaccurate.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a dispute was submitted to Equifax on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the account was being inaccurately reported on my Consumer');
