Chase will end my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Chase card but Chase intends to convert my Chase [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account into a Chase Freedom account without my permission and against my will. They are imposing a new credit card on me - the Chase Freedom card. They say they have the right to change the terms of the card per the cardmember agreement but they are not simply changing the terms. They are forcing me into an entirely new credit card against my wishes. 

I want them to let my Chase/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card fade out of existence when [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Chase end their relationship but I do not want to actually close the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Chase account myself. I also do not want Chase to force me into their Chase Freedom card without my permission and against my wishes. 

You see, I plan to apply for a Chase Freedom card on my own in the near future and if I do that then I would get a signing bonus of a 15 month ZERO percent interest rate for the first 15 months PLUS {$100.00} for spending {$500.00} in the first 3 months, but I only get that if I apply for the card on my own. If, on the other hand, they forcefully convert me into the Chase Freedom card ( from the Chase [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card ) then I do not get that ZERO percent for 15 months and I do not get the {$100.00} for spending {$500.00} in the first 3 months I have the Chase Freedom card. 

