INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5515,'08/23/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I had a non contract account, which means I was not required to pay a fee for closing my account. One month later they sent me an bill with cancellation fees attach to my last bill. I was instructed to dispute the bill ... which I sent in my request to review the bill. I have been getting the run around on the status. Received [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letter that they were still working on my request, as of today no word. My thought was it has been removed and account closed.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a month later they sent me an email with cancellation fees attached to my last bill. I was instructed to dispute the bill.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5516,'08/23/2015','Debt collection','I do not know','Disclosure verification of debt','Through several rounds of correspondence ( beginning XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and ending XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) with Portfolio Recovery Associates , LLC ( a debt collector ), I have insisted on the verification of a debt they are trying to collect. Despite the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( specifically 15 U.S.C. 1692g ) giving me the rights to 1 ) the names *and addresses* of original/current creditors and 2 ) *a copy of the verification or judgment against me by the original creditor*, Portfolio Recovery Associates , LLC has failed to properly validate this debt. As such, Portfolio Recovery Associates , LLC is breaking the law. 

In addition, Portfolio Recovery Associates , LLC lists the date they purchased this account as XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In my last correspondence, on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I requested a full payment history since they have purchased the account ( which, on each of their identical form letters, they invite me to request - but did not provide in their last correspondence on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in response to my request ). According to the statute of limitations on debt collection in Nevada ( where I live ), the maximum time a debt collector has to collect a debt is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years, depending on the type of debt ( NRS 11.190 ). Even if the debt were mine ( which I am not admitting to, as it has not been properly validated ), Portfolio Recovery Associates , LLC is deliberately refusing to allow me to prove that the statute of limitation on debt collection has been passed on this account - and that by attempting to collect it, they are breaking the law.','PORTFOLIO RECOVERY ASSOCIATES INC',2.0,2.0,'portfolio recovery Associates, LLC has failed to properly validate a debt. despite the fair debt collection practices act, they are breaking the law. despite the fair debt collection practices');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5517,'08/22/2015','Payday loan',NULL,'Can''t stop charges to bank account','Due to a medical crisis, I used poor judgement and took out an online loan with 500FastCash.com on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012 in the amount of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This amount was deducted from my checking account and it was my understanding that this matter was resolved as this was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years ago. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] weeks ago, I began receiving threatening phone calls from this company saying I owe them [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have since moved out of state thus closing my account. I requested a statement from this company and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] weeks later I received a statement by email showing ridiculous charges for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years. Although my balance was paid in full, I am told that additional interest was incurred. Additionally, as I had closed my account and transferred to an out of state bank, this company has continued to attempt to deduct funds and when denied as account closed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank, I am being charged for each transmission that was rejected for the last [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years.','Red Cedar Services, Inc',2.0,2.0,'500FastCash.com loaned me a loan on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. this amount was deducted from my checking account');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5518,'08/22/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Problems caused by my funds being low','I have not been using my account for over 6 months. When I checked the account it had occurred over {$630.00} in overdraft fees alone. There were over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$35.00} fees from where one company tried to take money out of the account.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,2.0,'a company tried to take money out of the account. there were overdraft fees.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5519,'08/21/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Rewards','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2015, I received an unsolicited written offer from American Express to apply for their " Blue Cash '''' credit card and, if used for over {$500.00} in the first three months, I would receive a reward bonus of {$100.00}. I have been an excellent AMEX card customer for 15+ years and have never missed making all payments in a timely manner. I used the new card for $ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the first month, but did not receive the {$100.00} bonus reward. Over the last two months, I have made [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] inquiries and have been told they were making a 6-8 week " investigation '''' of the issue. Now they said they will not honor the offer I received but would give me a {$50.00} credit because I have been a " good '''' customer. I refused this offer based on the principle of them not honoring the original offer that was extended to me to open the new card account.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'if used for over $500.00 in the first three months, I would receive a reward bonus of $100.00. if used for over ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5520,'08/21/2015','Debt collection','Federal student loan','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','This fraudulent debt appeared on my credit file. I am a victim of identity theft. So I notified the company ''s and they refused to show original contracts so I can better investigate the fraud.','United Student Aid (USA) Funds',2.0,4.0,'debt appeared on credit file. notified company''s and refused to show original contracts.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5521,'08/21/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Application, originator, mortgage broker','I recently closed a loan with Prospect Mortgage. I received my initial disclosures indicating that I have a 3.99 % interest rate. Once I signed and return the initial package. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 my loan officer emailed my saying that the interest rate went up to 4.125 %. and said he would like to lock the 4.125 % rate to provide us the security of rates getting any higher, but still having the free float down option of lowering the rate if the market gets better by 1/8 % up until closing. I agreed to the 4.125 since he said the interest rate were risingassuming I was getting new disclosure, however I never got a revised disclosure and the next thing I know we were closing the loan at 4.125 %. At the time it went by so fast I end up signing documents. Now thinking back, I wish I was given a revised disclosure showing my new rate, what my amortization would have looked like prior to me closing loan. Does TILA and RESPA require a lender to redisclosuse if the interest rate is higher than the initial disclosure? If so, doesnt this mean Prospect violated these regulations. Can someone assist me. Thanks [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]','Prospect Financial Group, Inc',2.0,2.0,'I recently closed a loan with Prospect Mortgage. I received my initial disclosures indicating that I have a 3.99 % interest rate. the loan officer said he would');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5522,'08/21/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Billing disputes','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2015, when I went to my credit card ''s website to pay the monthly bill, on the date it was due, the website was down, and I was not able to pay my bill until the next day. This made my payment [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day late. 
The credit card company then added a late fee to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill. 
In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I payed the monthly bill on time, paying the minimum amount that would have been due without the late fee, because I believed that the company should not have charged a late fee, when their website had been down at the time that I tried to pay my bill in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I expected the credit card company to have realized that their website was down, and to drop the late fee. 
Now, the credit card company is claiming that my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment is past due, because the wrongly assessed late fee is past due. And they are adding [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] late fees to my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill. 
My complaint is Twofold : A ) The credit card company charged me a late fee for a bill that I was unable to pay on the due date because their website was down ; B The credit card company is charging me a late fee on a late fee, when I paid the regular minimum amount due on time in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2015.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'credit card company adds late fee to bill that I was unable to pay on due date. in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my payment was late, and');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5523,'08/20/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Improper contact or sharing of info','About a year ago I had to break the lease at my apartment complex, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], due to work related issues. This resulted in a balance due on my account which I was unable to pay by the deadline and as a result my account was referred to a debt collector, National Credit Systems. When my account was referred to this debt collector the apartment complex provided them with my contact information. I know this because I have been receiving communications from National Credit Systems for a few months now. Today I received a text message from an ex-boyfriend/friend whom I have n''t spoken to in about a year stating an [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called his cell phone and left a message looking for me. Upon calling the number that was left in the message I realized the call had come from National Credit Systems and was in regards to the debt from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Even though this company has ALL of my contact information, they somehow felt the need to reach out to the individual I listed as my emergency contact on my rental application in an attempt to locate me. This not only blew my mind, but was rather confusing to me being that they already have my contact information. The phone number they have for me is in service and always has been and they have contacted me on that number before. The mailing address they have is a good address and they are aware of this because I continue to receive mail from them. I ''m not sure if this is normal practice but when I listed an emergency contact on my rental application I was under the impression that individual would ONLY be contacted in the event of an emergency while I was a resident at the complex. I was not aware that this individual would be subject to receive calls from debt collectors attempting to locate me a year after I vacated the property. I ''m not even sure why the apartment complex provided my emergency contact person ''s information to the debt collector in the first place.','National Credit Systems,Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a year ago, a debt collector had to break the lease at my apartment complex. this resulted in a balance due on my account which I was unable to pay');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5524,'08/20/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','an insurance company issued payment for flood damage to a home, and listed tthe mortgage holder on the draft. after endorsing the draft and sending it tothe mortgage holder ( seterus / [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), the mortgage holder has committedintentional fraud, and will not refund the money to complete the flood repairs. 
they continually change criteria for release of the funds, indicate that we haveto complete repairs from money out of our pocket, and has caused loss ofuse of our property.','Seterus, Inc.',2.0,4.0,'insurance company listed tthe mortgage holder on the draft. the mortgage holder committedintentional fraud. the mortgage holder will not refund the money to complete flood repairs ');
