INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5526,'08/19/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Communication tactics','Unannounced, they came into our place of business and started taking pictures. We are not a public-facing company. We are a private call center. They startled my employees. Would n''t leave when asked. One girl went home crying. We threatened to call police and they said they had the right to be here. We started calling police and they left real fast.','VeriCore, LLC',2.0,2.0,'they started taking pictures of our place of business. they started calling police and left real fast.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5527,'08/19/2015','Debt collection','Auto','Communication tactics','After my atuo loan provider contacted me at work I told them not to contact me at work again they threatened to make deductions to my pay and made me a offer of payment. The colecter demanded " when I will I be payed my money '''' then threated that if paper work or payment was n''t receaved by the end of the month that they will proceed with garnishment. Because I did n''t know what my rights where I told them to email mail me the paper work. I also have receaved multiply phone calls in a day from this corperation.','BB&T CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'atuo loan provider threatened to make deductions to my pay. colecter threatened to garnish if paper work or payment wasn''t receaved by the end');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5528,'08/19/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Late fee','My payment date is due on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They are are charging a {$38.00} late fee to my balance if not paid on or before the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is not my due date. I have moved to another state almost [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year ago and have had financial slow downs while getting re- established. I did not realize the were charging this outrageous late fee after the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In my industry ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) the deadlines dates are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that night as this is within the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hour day. My account is has a {$150.00} balance with a {$500.00} limit. No warnings on my paper statement disclose payments should be received on the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I happened to see it on line when I made my payment this evening. I have been running late due to difficulty but when I pay on the due date, I should not be charged a late fee no matter what time of day it is. The bank can draft out funds from our accounts in real time so our payments should be able to count in real time within the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hour due date time frame. This is robbery and should not be allowed even if posted in all caps and Bold on the statements. It ''s even worse as it ''s not clarified on the paper statements at all. This means that those who do not have internet access have no way of knowing before they see the charge that this is happening or why if they are paying on their due date. The 26.99 % APR rate and the {$38.00} late fee is thievery and the sneaky way they are getting it is criminal!','SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL',2.0,2.0,'the deadlines dates are [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that night. my account is has a $150.00 balance with a $');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5529,'08/19/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Unable to get credit report/credit score','I used www.annualcreditreport.com to request a free credit report from TransUnion on XX/XX/2015. Due to internet issues, I never saw my report nor had a chance to save that report. When I finally connected [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes later, I received this message, " You have already received your free Personal Credit Report from TransUnion ; therefore, you are not eligible to receive an additional TransUnion report at this time. " Does the law not require that I can " request and **obtain** all the information about [ me ] in the files of a consumer reporting agency? '''' I do not want an updated report, but access to the report I allegedly " received '''' on XX/XX/2015. As the consumer reporting agencies already maintain a record of my most recent date of " file disclosure, '''' it is nearly costless to them to allow me to obtain my XX/XX/2015 report until I am eligible to " receive '''' an updated report. Does the FCRA law allow these agencies to seal my " free disclosure file '''' for one year due to a failed online attempt at " disclosure ''''? I would like CFPB to help enforce substantive " disclosure '''' or the " right to obtain a copy '''' -- can you help me?','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a consumer reporting agency has already received a free credit report. the law allows the agency to seal my " free disclosure file '''' for one year.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5530,'08/18/2015','Debt collection','Medical','Disclosure verification of debt','Received a call on my answering machine announcing that I needed to call back a number about a debt issue. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day later I received a collection notice for {$78.00} for date of service [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 from Arcadia Recovery Bureau for a doctor charge from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of 2015. 
Checked my EOB/Medical file to find that I never received a bill from the provider. 
I contacted the provider University [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They told me that they had sent a bill on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 that was returned from the PO stating " temporary out of town and can not deliver ''''. At that point they told me their policy was to flag the account for that invoice and future invoices for collection. 
1. I do not understand how that policy can be legal. The creditor must do due diligence to make an attempt to collect the debt before turning it over to a collection agency. Automatically flagging an account does not constitute due diligence. 
2. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] further told me that they have so many patients that is the only way they can handle the billing process. Just because they do not have the proper man power does not mean they have the right to put a persons credit record in jeopardy. They have my home number, my cell phone number, my email address and a messaging system from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in place to contact me. 
3. Flagging an account because of a temporary mail delivery issue is not the patient ''s fault. On the hospital side I still receive bills and process them for payment. They have access to all those records and should be able to determine if the mailing address is correct. 
4. The message left by the collection agency disclosed debt collection information and my name on an answering machine that is available to other individuals. That can not be legal. 
5. I believe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ''s billing system is flawed, prejudicial and illegal and I need help to shut it down.','Arcadia Holdings, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a collection notice for a doctor charge from a provider was sent. the provider said they had sent a bill on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5531,'08/18/2015','Debt collection','Credit card','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I paid off my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card thru Credit Control, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], Mo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but it still show ''s as in collection on my credit report. How ca this be removed? [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','JH Portfolio Debt Equities, LLC',2.0,2.0,'credit card was paid off through Credit Control. it still shows''s as in collection on my credit report.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5532,'08/18/2015','Consumer Loan','Installment loan','Problems when you are unable to pay','This is about a collection company for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was in the hospital in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years. The phone number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me on the hour every hour. When I was released from the hospital they called me last me last night. I asked what company this was. I explained I had been in the hospital over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] times in the last [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days and when I got settled, I would review the situation. I got another call from them [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes later and then again in an hour.','EXPERT GLOBAL SOLUTIONS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'a collection company for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was called on the hour every hour. when released from the hospital they called me last night.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5533,'08/18/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I am an attorney. I represent homeowners in foreclosure. I normally advise my client to submit legitimate complaints here, and I think my client has in this matter, but this case is so gut wrenching and the consequences so dire, that I want to make sure it gets the full attention of the CFPB. Bottom line, my clients have lost their homestead property AND NEARLY {$300000.00} IN EQUITY because of a gross and well documented case of dual tracking. My client has very good and very detailed records of correspondence from JPMorgan who confirmed they had a completed application in. My client next confirms that while she knew a foreclosure sale was set, JPMorgan advised that it would be cancelled. My client confirmed with the attorney for JPMorgan that they were cancelling the sale. I personally spoke with the attorney for JPMorgan chase who confirms that they moved to cancel the sale. The problem is, the court refused to cancel the sale and now their home has been sold to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] party at an auction. I am trying everything I can procedural to undo this sale, but our options are limited. This case illustrates a serious problem in lack of enforcement of CFPB protections. I urge you to read the Order issued by the judge in this case and I especially urge CFPB to pay particular attention to the well-documented facts that judges in circuit courts are refusing to recognize CFPB protections. This case represents very harsh consequences of this refusal and I implore you to intervene in this case and use this case for larger enforcement purposes.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',4.0,4.0,'a bad case has been uncovered by the CFPB. my client has a complete application in. the case illustrates a serious problem in lack of enforcement of ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5534,'08/18/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I spoke with a representative at Experian after a dispute of the incorrect information was made, then not changed, and to date I have not receive a response after the call was made. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting that a total of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was written off, but in fact my insurance company paid them [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because the car was totaled. I have sent in the documentation, but they refuse to change it due to the fact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is reporting it this way. I had a short sale in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2012, and Experian is reporting it as a foreclosure. I have disputed this item also. I have a great deal of student loans, that I have disputed also, but are still being reported incorrectly. I have been denied a mortgage due to inaccurate reporting on my credit reporting from all of the reporting agencies, but because I spoke directly with Experian, they are at the forefront.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian representative spoke with me after dispute of incorrect information was made. a total of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was written off, but my insurance company');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5535,'08/17/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','THIS IN REGARDS TO A COLLECTION ACCOUNT ON MY CREDIT REPORT LISTED AS [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for the amount of {$620.00} that has been disputed in the pass ... the experian did not properly verify this account ... .due to the fact that the company itself has no imformation regarding this account accept the original creditor. when i disputed the validity of the debt .... experian will not inform me of their verification methods .... ..','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian did not properly verify this account. the company itself has no imformation regarding this account accept the original creditor.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5536,'08/17/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I had filed for loss mitigation assistance in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and was approved based on the successful completion of my trial period payments. I then made my trial period payments from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was sent modification documents and advised that I had to sign and return these. This is the typical process. I called in and advised the company that the link that was sent to me would not open and would not allow for me to download the documents. This delayed the process. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I asked for my daughter to get involved because she worked in loss mitigation at that time, and now works in bankruptcy, and is familiar with the processes, their timelines, and how to get things done from the creditor perspective. The documents were sent to her by a representative who identified herself as a supervisor on an escalated call, ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] we later found out was a " team lead '''', not a person in management ). After discussing the issues we had with my daughter, she advised she would resend the docs, and once received, would ensure that my modification would be boarded, as their had been an extension placed on my file allowing time for me to turn in the documents. The documents were notarized and sent via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the following day. From [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], several phone calls were made to follow up on the status of the my pending modification and each time, we were advised that the modification had not been boarded, to not make a payment on the account, but rather to " hang on '''' to the funds until everything was updated to my account. I did as I was advised. My daughter became concerned and called to ask why the process was taking so long, as boarding an approved modification should not have this kind of delay. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] she escalated the call to a supervisor in that department and was advised within [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hours that the modification had never been approved, and that it was denied on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because the documents had not been received on time. At this point, she requested a review of the notation on the account as on many occasions, she was the one who called and spoke with representatives of the bankruptcy department. She was advised by this manager that on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the modification package had been received, however, the deadline or extension to have them in ended on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we called and were advised the modification had not been booked. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], when she called, both times she was advised the modification was still pending and to have me wait until everything was boarded to resume payments. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she was advised there was no sale date related to the foreclosure, and that the modification was still pending. Upon calling at the end of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and then finally getting answers on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from the manager she had been speaking with, the only thing I was left with was the notice that I now had no modification, and I was even more past due than before. My daughter spoke at length with this manager with me on the phone, and after having Nationstar review the calls from XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to date, and reviewing the notes on my file, asked what options I had. The manager advised Nationstar would be willing to honor my modification if I brought the account current and covered [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] monthly payments. When I called to make my payment we were unable to speak with the manager who had become our single point of contact and rather got a representative who assured us he had been with the company for five years and could assist. He quoted a figure different from what the manager had advised my daughter of and then stated he could validate the actual figure and have the manager follow up. Upon asking for something in writing stating if paid, the modification would be honored, we were advised that documentation stating this could not be provided. And now, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], we have not received a follow up in this matter.','NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE',2.0,4.0,'a representative sent the documents to her and advised her to sign and return them. the documents were notarized and sent via [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the');
