INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5554,'08/11/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I have an account that is fraudulent that have been listed with your agency and have been listed with various credit reporting agencies with this false information. ... that needs to be removed i have gone through alot of trouble to get this taken care of I have filed a police report and a ftc id theft affidavit ...','FirstPoint Collection Resources',2.0,4.0,'ftc id theft affidavit filed by a police report and a ftc id theft affidavit.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5555,'08/11/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Other','Citi [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] : Harassment calls several times a day, for days after making a payment. 
I received a phone call that I missed a payment. It was in fact numerous phone calls thoughout a day. When I called in the automated system to make a payment ( almost [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] times the amount requested ), I continued to receive the annoying computer generated calls throughout the day. For the day I made the payment, and three days later. Three days later of up to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] calls a day each and every day, including Sunday evening, at random times. 
This same thing happned a few months before, were even after making a payment I received numerous calls each day for a few days after my payment was made. After calling in both times to speak to a customer service rep, they acknowledged my payment, and apologized that there system does not recognize payments made on certain days, until some days later. I informed them this is harrassment and no excuse. 

I would like to see that Citi is prevented from harrassing people that have made the proper payment, and calls immediately cease once a satisfactory payment is made. Their calls have interrupted my family and business time, and have been harrassing in nature with the frequency and time both on Sunday and in evenings each night. 

I would like to see this investigated and fined to prevent this from happening to others.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'Citi calls several times a day, for days after making a payment. harrassment calls are harrassing in nature with the frequency and time ');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5556,'08/11/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] i purchased a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] computer, made payments on it for several years, I fell behind, the interest rate was extremely high andI couldnt get to the balance. I stopped making payments in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Its been over 10 years and the negative response is still on my credit report. The original company, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] sells it off to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] a while back then it gets sold to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] company and they say the origianal creditor is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. That is false they keep selling it off and repeating it over and over, and do this over 10 years, and keeping it current. Please look into this.','TRANSUNION INTERMEDIATE HOLDINGS, INC.',2.0,2.0,'i stopped making payments in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for several years. the original company sells it off to [COMPTE_ANONYMIS');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5557,'08/10/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Credit card protection / Debt protection','I received an email from Bank of America notifying me that my credit card information has been compromised. They alerted me that a new card was in the mail. I then received a call from Bank of America ''s fraud protection department. I asked which store or vendor had compromised my account information. They informed me that they can not tell me this information due to an on-going investigation. They then informed me that even after the investigation, I would not be able to find out who or which vendor compromised my credit card information. This information secrecy is atrocious and unacceptable. Consumers should have the right to know which companies are protecting their consumer data and which companies are not. Consumers should have the right to chose which vendors we do business with based on their ability to protect our security.','BANK OF AMERICA, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION',2.0,4.0,'bank of America contacted me to tell me which store or vendor compromised my credit card information. they told me that they can not tell me this information due to an investigation. this information');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5558,'08/10/2015','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','I am trying to get a modification on my home. I was first working with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had all the documents needed to start the underwriting process. My loan was then transferred to Rushmore Loan Management [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2015. When first contacting Rushmore in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was told they had none of my information from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] but was told it can take some time to get the documentation. When I called I was told that they were only given parts of the documents and the best thing to do was resend ALL information which I did. My case manager with Rushmore Loan Management has given me false information many times regarding my loan. Also when I spoke to her she said she needed more information faxed. I asked her to review the documents she did have and come to find out they already had the documents. I was then told that I needed {$20000.00} for a down payment if I wanted to save my home. If I had the {$20000.00} I would n''t be having to try and get a modification in the first place. Also I asked her if she could please leave a voicemail if I do n''t answer and leave me the information that they need. This has only happened once and she did n''t leave a message with documentation needed she just left me her name and number. I am extremely frustrated and feel as if I am being mistreated by this company. I did not receive notice from Rushmore Loan Management that my house was being foreclosed on. I was notified by they trustee note taped to my door that my house is going into auction on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15','RUSHMORE LOAN MANAGEMENT SERVICES LLC',4.0,4.0,'a loan was transferred to Rushmore Loan Management in 2015. when she called she was told they had no information from me. she said she needed $20000.00 for');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5559,'08/10/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','We took out our house loan XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The loan was with Homecomings Financial - Loan # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and Account # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for around {$160000.00}. Sometime later it changed to GMAC Mortgage. Again sometime later OCWEN took over. Account # with them is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I would say [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of the payments I also paid extra principal. I started out just paying extra towards the principal and then I got a copy of the Amortization schedule and paid the principal applied for the the upcoming month. We had it figured and was told by our mortgage officer that if we got a 30 year loan and paid the extra that our house would pay off in 12 years instead of 30 years. We are right at the 12 years and OCWEN is saying that we still owe {$83000.00} and our loan will not pay off until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have sent OCWEN numerous letters informing them of this and all they send me is a printout of what we have paid. I know what we have paid. I am the one that paid it. I CAN NOT understand their people on the phone because they do not speak very good English. I have plenty of documents from Ocwen and to Ocwen. I sent my last letter certified mail to the attention of the Manager of the Servicing Department at Ocwen with copies of payments I have made which included additional principal paid throughout the years. They sent a letter explaining where they post the payments too. They have sent me this letter many times. I am going to try and attach my certified letter, their certified letter and printout of my payments.','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a mortgage officer told us that if we got a 30 year loan and paid extra, our house would pay off in 12 years instead of 30 years. the mortgage officer told me');
