INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5561,'08/09/2015','Money transfers','Domestic (US) money transfer','Other transaction issues','Dear [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I spoke with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 in regards to a missing wire transfer that I have yet to receive or returned back to my original [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account. He said that he would open back up a ticket to have the Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] research team investigate further into the funds that I am still missing. He also asked if I could forward you a copy of any information that I have that would aid in this process. With that said, I have attached a screen shot copy of the Record of my Wire Transfer, as well as the Federal Reference Number of the wire transfer which is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Please keep in mind that the letter [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] could be a zero in the Federal Reference Number but either way, both [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank as well as the regular Wells Fargo Bank, were both able to show that the funds were wired to Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 

To bring you up to speed, I wired {$2900.00} from my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank account to my Wells Fargo Bank CHECKING account on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] EST, or so I thought. When I did not see the money in my CHECKING account the next day, I immediately checked my records and saw that I accidentally put my Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] credit card account number ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] instead. I immediately called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Bank to inform them of my error and the bank representative informed me that it should not be a problem because the receiving bank will see that it went to a credit card and will just need to reject it. I was told that it would be back into my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bank account in two business days. Well [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it ''s been two weeks and I still have not received my transfer money, nor does your bank seem to know where it is either. I spoke with a personal banker at Wells Fargo Bank by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) more than a week ago about the missing wire transfer. He told me as instructed by someone from Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] or Wells Fargo Bank, to get the federal reference number and call [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I did as instructed and spoke to a representative by the name of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He was able to use the the Federal Reference number to see that the {$2900.00} did in fact go to Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and that I would have to call them to rectify the matter. I did as instructed and spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] representative [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who transferred me to Team Lead [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], who transferred me to Manager [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. All of whom were not able to do anything as far as locating my missing wire transfer. They said there screen would only let them look into the matter so far but that the Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] research team was looking into it. 

Feeling very frustated to my surprise, I finally received a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who said they will reopen the research with the evidence that I have just presented you. 1. A screen shot of my wire transaction sent to Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] card ending in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 2. ) The Federal Reference number that shows where the money went. 3. ) The wire identifier number from my wire transfer receipt which is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 4. ) The transaction number which is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 5. ) The Routing/ABA Number which was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 6. ) The account number that it was sent to which is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 7. ) The day the wire was created which was on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 but it officially went out the next business day which was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/15 in the amount of {$2900.00}. 

In closing, I am highly frustrated that a bank as large a Wells Fargo and as long as they have been around, can not find funds from a simple wire transfer. Whether it ''s Wells Fargo Bank or Wells Fargo [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], to me it ''s still under the Wells Fargo umbrella and I ''m highly disappointed with the company as a whole. I do n''t know how you all communicate with each other but I need this situation resolved.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a wire transfer that I have yet to receive or return back to my original account is missing. a screen shot copy of the record of my Wire Transfer is attached. the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5562,'08/09/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Billing statement','We carried an ongoing balance on an American Express Credit Card. Each billing statement, indicates the statement balance to pay and the total balance to pay. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], which was the payment due date, we paid the Total balance in full. Now a new statement has come in and they have charged me some type of fees and more interest. We had {$8.00} in charges and {$130.00} in fees and interest. Their explanation is that in the fine print of the agreement it states that they can charge fees and more interest on balances or payments that were made late in the past. I asked them, based on this, how would one ever be able to pay off a balance if they were allowed to tack on fees and interest for the past AFTER the balance was paid in full. They said it was in the agreement and totally legal. I said, even if it is legal, is it right? I paid off the balance in full, there should be no new charges.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a new statement has come in and they have charged me fees and more interest. they said it was in the agreement and totally legal.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5563,'08/08/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','A few months ago I ended up filing some disputes because there was incorrect and incomplete information on my credit report. So I prepared a nice letter and sent it with a copy of my driver ''s license, proof of my social security number and proof of my mailing address so that Experian would be able to verify my identity. 
It has been at least [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] months since I mailed my letter and I have n''t heard back. When I try calling their [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] number they want a report number before I speak with an agent and since I do n''t have one I ca n''t speak to anyone. 
I thought that the credit companies had to respond back to me within [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days otherwise they are supposed to remove things from my credit report?! 
Well it ''s been way more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days and all of the stuff I disputed is still there. I know I can go online and buy a credit monitoring service and try to dispute things online but I thought that Experian is supposed to help me for free! 
I ''m at the point where I ''m done wasting time and need to get this fixed immediately.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'a few months ago I filed some disputes because there was incorrect information on my credit report. I sent a nice letter and sent it with a copy of my driver''s license');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5564,'08/08/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I made a payment of {$1200.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 which, as of today ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 ) still has not been applied to my account. The payment is being held in suspense. My mortgage payments are up to date ( next payment due [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 ) and the payment is not a partial payment ( normal monthly payment is {$950.00} ).','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'payment is being held in suspense. the payment is not a partial payment.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5565,'08/07/2015','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Application, originator, mortgage broker','We were trying to apply for a mortgage. Since my credit is locked they refused to use only my wifes credit and because we do n''t have any recurring credit were not approved. This part was fine. 

The problem is that we are staying with our kids at their house, and we told them to use our mailing address and to NOT send anything to our kids address. They ignored their own application that shows a mailing address on it. We told them we do n''t use our kids address for anything, and they used it during my wifes credit check, and then also against our request they also sent their credit documents to our kids address ignoring our request to ONLY use our mailing address. Now we will start to get things mailed to our kids address against our will and promise to them to never use their address for anything.','FIRST MORTGAGE COMPANY',4.0,4.0,'we were trying to apply for a mortgage because my credit is locked. they refused to use only my wifes credit and because we don''t have any recurring credit were');
