INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5567,'08/07/2015','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I have tried for months to get my monthly private student loan payment through Citibank lowered. I have explained I am not working and have not been working for over a year and unemployment ran out. They agreed to let me defer one month ( because they said that ''s all I had available to me [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They have called me at all hours of the day and night, sometimes 5 times a day if my payment is late. When I ask for help they have told me time and time again that they can not do anything and it will just have to go to collections and I can just deal with them. They have no compassion, no understanding and could care less that I am not working ... they asked me how I plan to pay my monthly payment and I told them I will have to start selling my personal property and their response was well you have to do what you have to do. I have never been more disappointed in my life with a financial institution. I am just asking for my payment to be lowered, I am not asking them to pardon me from paying back my debt. I went to the University [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] online and completed my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Degree.','CITIBANK, N.A.',2.0,2.0,'i have tried for months to get my monthly private student loan payment lowered. they agreed to let me defer one month because they said that''s all I had available to');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5568,'08/07/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I had a phone contract with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. When I signed up for services in store XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was told by the customer service representative in the store that I had 30 days in which to cancel my contract if I was unhappy with service. By the end of the first week it was clear that the very costly services ( around {$350.00} a month for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] phones ) were not providing good reception, the internet did not even WORK on the phones ( these were brand new models!!! ) and even when calling between the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] lines or sending texts there were often delays of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes or more. I called on day [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] after giving their services a chance, feeling I was well within the time limit of 30 days. I was told, I am sorry you only have ten days to cancel. I went into the store to try to talk to someone, they apologized that I was given incorrect information by the sales representative but told me that indeed I had ten days to cancel NO EXCEPTIONS. So now I was locked into a horrible cell phone service that barely worked and I did not want. We did not even use one of the phones because the internet service on it was so poor ( even when on a Wifi connection! ) that it was rendered worthless. We had to buy another phone with a different ( and much cheaper! ) provider that worked great. I continued to pay the outrageous $ 350+ monthly charges ( keep in mind this is for only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] phones with minimum packages ) for six months. In early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] my house was robbed, my car was stolen, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of the phones was stolen. I called and reported the phone stolen and requested to cancel service on that phone. A few days later the other phone was broken beyond repair and I did not have the funds ( after being robbed of nearly all my belongings ) to purchase a new phone through [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I requested they terminate my account. My father offered to call and pay via credit card because I could not afford termination fees. He did this in early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. A year and a half later and I am getting letters and calls from a collection agency ( including [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] calls after [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on a weeknight which I have reported them for ) asking for {$930.00} that they say I owe to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] says my father never completed payment, even though when I called them to confirm the accounts were closed and everything was settled I was told, " Yes everything has been taken care of and you have nothing to worry about and will not be getting a bill from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in the future. '''' They are requesting a whopping {$580.00} for termination fees, despite the fact that I was duped into a contract and had made their outrageous payments each month for non-working cell phones and had been robbed and was therefore not at fault for the need to cancel contract. I am currently expecting my first child any day now, and I am single and a student with no income. I do not have the time to deal with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the collection agency harassment as I try to finish my degree and move forward in my life. These charges are beyond excessive, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has already lost a court case in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County ( where I was residing ) in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for excessive termination fees, and recently lost a nationwide case for bill cramming that occurred during the time I had service with them. Furthermore, my father paid these charges in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I was told by a representative that my account was closed, no more billing, no problems. Now I am being harassed by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and their collection agency with calls being placed at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in an attempt to collect this so-called debt. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] customer service lies and says they want to speak with me to resolve and address my issues then claim they never got payment from my father and yell that I owe them money and they will send me the bill. A total waste of my time and harassment on all levels!','ERC',2.0,4.0,'a customer service representative told me that he had 30 days to cancel my contract. he said that the service was not providing good reception, the internet did not even WORK on');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5569,'08/06/2015','Mortgage','Home equity loan or line of credit','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','I am a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year old widow who was mislead and convinced Ineeded a home equity loan by Washington Mutual Bank inXXXX of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. From that point until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] when Chasemodified loan. Approximately forty percent of my monthlyincome was being spent to satisfy loan. Then Chase reducedmy interest rate and escrowed my taxes and insuranceinto [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment making my payments easier. HoweverI discovered that for from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] until week [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Chase had not applied any of my monthly paymentstoward principal. Balance stayed same for seven years. 
I read and reread loan agreement many times and had mychildren examine loan documents. The original loan and nowmodified loan is not interest only agreement! Its principalinterest and escrow. I have many documents supportingmy case of mortgage fraud against Washington Mutualand now continuing fraud by Chase. By Chase not applying mypayments to principal it increases my interest rate much higher thanwhat was written in instrument of mortgage. That ''s mortgage fraud! In ten yearsof making payments of approximately [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] dollars my principalbalance is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Again I have maybe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] documents proving this fraud. 
When I contact Chase and make inquires regarding this fraud they justhang up the phone or place me on hold for hours. Last week alone [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hoursphone. Total time in eight weeks more than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] hours. Everyday a differentanswer. I have also gone in person to many Chase banks to have employeesclaim they have no access to information regarding loan. I have proof by chasesown letters of fraud. From monthly statements to original loan document. 
This is my last effort before I file a lawsuit against Chase for mortgage fraud. 
Any assistance you could provide would be helpful because cost of anattorney maybe too high? Again I have documented proof of mortgage fraud.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,4.0,'a widow who was mislead and convinced I needed a home equity loan. a banker escrowed my taxes and insurance to pay my monthly income.');
