INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5572,'08/06/2015','Debt collection','Credit card','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I had a collection account at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I owed to Capital One for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They reported the account on my credit bureau the same day they received the account. I did n''t find out about it until months later when I pulled my free credit report. Before I paid it I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and asked them when it would be reported to the bureau as paid. A lady told me if they received it before the end of the month if would take no less than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days. I paid the account in full on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called cavalry today ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015 ) to make sure they were going to show it as paid in full and now they are telling me its going to take [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days????? Why does it take [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days?? They did n''t take [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days before reporting it. I paid with a debit card and the money had cleared my bank. It should be reported immediately. I felt that they were deceptive, they just wanted the money before the end of the month and so they lied about when it was going to be reported to the bureau. They want the money right away, but they drag their feet when its on them to update it to the bureau!','CAPITAL ONE FINANCIAL CORPORATION',2.0,2.0,'a lady told me if they received it before the end of the month if would take no less than [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] days. they did');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5573,'08/05/2015','Bank account or service','Other bank product/service','Account opening, closing, or management','I am writing this letter on behalf of my daughter. My daughter had gotten into a financial bind. She is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and has always tried to be independent. Feeling ashamed of her situation, made the decision to seek help from her bank, Wells Fargo, instead of coming to myself for assistance. 
She has attended school part-time for the last two years to be accepted to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] program. We found out in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that a spot had been secured for her at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] University. This is the same school she attended and received a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She is intelligent, hardworking, and motivated. Unfortunately, she is not well educated in the world of finances or banking. I found out about her finances when I was trying to organize a budget for us when she returns to school in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. 
The help that Wells Fargo gave her left her in a position that she would not be able to get out of for the rest of her life. This started when they told her she had to keep a balance of {$1500.00} in her checking account. This would be impossible for her and seems it would be quite evident by her ongoing banking with them. Wells Fargo ''s help consisted of a loan at 12.25 %, a personal line of credit at 11.25 %, and a credit card that carries a 17 % on purchases and a 23.99 % on cash advances. The accounts she was signed up for also carry an annual fee of {$25.00}. She makes her minimum payments. The interest being charged every month is more than her payment. I realize she signed these agreements, but did so reluctantly. The person helping her even stated to her that she " looked uncomfortable doing this ''''. She had no idea what any of the interest rates meant or of the charges that went along with cash advances. I tried going into the bank with her and was told there was nothing they could do since she signed the agreements already. However, they were willing to run her credit again to see if they could get her yet another loan. 
I went on their website and not even being a customer ( which she has been since it was owned by Wachovia ) ; I can get a credit card with a balance transfer at 0 % interest and accounts that have no annual fee. They advertise all kinds of help for students. I am wondering why she was not offered any of that help. I do n''t even know of a bank that does n''t offer free checking and savings accounts ( well, now I do ). 
I have now exhausted all my avenues and put my credit in an unsatisfactory light trying to get her out of this mess. She is unable to get any other financial help in terms of loans for school due to the fact her credit is now maxed out. I am appalled and beside myself that a bank would do this to someone. I feel an obligation to let every unsuspecting and unaware individual know that this financial institution is not there to help anyone, but only for their own gain.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'she has always tried to be independent, says robert mccartney. she has attended school part-time to be accepted to a [COMPTE_');
