INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5614,'07/24/2015','Mortgage','Conventional adjustable mortgage (ARM)','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','OCWEN has been mismanaging my foreclosure for almost [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years now. After filing for bankruptcy my foreclosure hearing was suddenly dismissed without prejudice, which means they can refile at any time. Currently I am in conversation with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] different people, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the Trustee and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at OCWEN. I ''m asking to speak with someone who has the authority to dismiss the lien now that the note has been discharged and the property is a liability rather than an asset to either the bank or to me. Ultimately I would like the lien discharged or for the foreclosure court ( Maine ) to simply dismiss the case with prejudice so that I can get on with managing the property at a loss because it has sentimental value. The first step would be to identify someone at either OCWEN or [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who has the authority to make that decision, if in fact they agree with my cost benefit analysis and simply want to close this case. Otherwise, I want them to discuss options with me. 

