INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5659,'07/11/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Settlement process and costs','We received pre-approval for a mortgage from CitiBank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. During the pre-approval process, they were very responsive. However, once we had a ratified contract for a house, our loan officer because very slow to respond to questions. We asked for specific details on the timeline but our questions were frequently ignored. We communicated early that they would need to coordinate with our second trust lender, but they failed to do so. In the week leading up to our originally scheduled settlement ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), we could not get anyone on the phone or to answer our emails to coordinate the final part of the process. Finally, I called the Citibank national helpline and got connected via email to the manager or our loan officer. The manager was similarly unresponsive after an initial email and we ended up missing our settlement date. We had arranged settlement for this Friday before [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] weekend so we would have time to move into our new house. We had family coming in from out of town to help and movers scheduled to arrive. We failed to even get anyone on the phone to explain to us what was happening. Finally, the following Tuesday night ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ), our realtor was able to find out from the loan officer ''s manager that our loan officer had quit the day before our scheduled settlement. When we still could n''t get this manager on the phone, I had to call the Citibank national hotline again. Eventually, they connected me to the regional manager who finally told me our loan settlement would be delayed until at least Friday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. We rescheduled our movers again, but Citibank again could not close. At that point, we were already required to be out of our apartment. We finally closed on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but at that point, my wife and I had to take 3 days off work trying to coordinate the constantly shifting timeline and move and we had to remain in our apartment past the day we were allowed to. We ended up having to move everything with only one person to help because the timeline shifted from a weekend to a weekday. Throughout this process, Citibank was dismissive, unresponsive, and only got back to us after we called their national helplines or escalated to supervisors.','CITIBANK, N.A.',4.0,4.0,'we received pre-approval for a mortgage from Citibank in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. the manager was unresponsive after an initial email and we ended');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5660,'07/10/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Arbitration','I would like to file a complaint against American Express Credit Card. I used them to make a purchase with floorstoyourhome.com, in the amount of {$1800.00}. 
American Express does n''t stand behind their customers. We installed the flooring, but it buckles up. The retailer sent out his inspector who said the reason, because the subfloor is not even. When their inspector was here he never removed the floor to check out the subfloor. Did n''t remove any moldings and came back with a false report. I hired [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] independent contractors to do inspection. Both said the problem is not the subfloor. It is the merchandise, because the locking mechanism is defected. Finally I could talk to a customer service representative at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( the manufacturer of the wood floor ) who said the reason we are having a problem, because the underlayment what the retailer sold us is not compatible with the floor. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] even e-mailed me out the installation requirements, what they provide to all retailers. I forwarded that document along with the purchase receipt to Amex, which shows that floorstoyourhome.com sold me the wrong underlayment. I sent all the documents to American Express and they denied the dispute. They told us they are not even going to look at the proofs, pictures and documentations from our side. They are only talking to the retailer. The retailer only provided his inspector ''s report and American Express accepted it as is. They did n''t honor the other [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] professionals inspection reports, the pictures and the manufacturer ''s letter with the installation requirement. This is not fair that I have to pay for defected merchandise with the wrong underlayment. Also this cost me more since the floor had to be installed, I had to pay for the inspectors, we need to pick up the floor and underlayment and reinstall everything with the right underlayment. I did n''t even counted the precious time I had to spend to arrange everything, communicate with Amex, all the letters, pictures, phone calls. 
Please look into this very serious and delicate matter!','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'american Express sent out inspector who said the subfloor is not even. he never removed the floor to check out the subfloor. he sent me a false report to the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5661,'07/10/2015','Mortgage','FHA mortgage','Loan modification,collection,foreclosure','To The reviewer of all my complaintsCFPBMy name is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I was the owner of the HUD located at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], GA [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], the house was sold at the steps of the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] house. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Georgia. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Wells Fargo requested the sale to be rescinded after my complaint. On XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she advised that the sale can not be rescinded. and it was final. Last week, XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County Water Authority called me to tell me a company wanted to establish an account with them. Since my name is the legal owner of the property, they did n''t open an account in their name. The same company locked me out of the property and took ownership of the property without an eviction letter. Again prior to the dismissal of the rescinded request. I was locked out of the house. 
The same [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Wells Fargo told me the HAMP application submitted on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was not reviewed, but the one on XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was reviewed. Therefore, this is a violation of Federal Law. I further asked her if I was not qualified for any other Federal program in order to keep my house. She responded " No ''''. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of Wells Fargo advised in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to have a letter of a permanent job offer in order for her to continue with the modification. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] applications were submitted to Wells Fargo for review and an appeal form to continue with the modification. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] said that nothing was reviewed. Since XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] promised to give me the information about the third party purchaser of the house. She did not respond to her phone call. This is an illegal possession of the house and a wrongful eviction. I hope someone can look at this complaint and act upon it. Wells Fargo has received the bailout money from the US Government but violated the law for modification and put a barrier to minorities to get loans to keep their house. This is pure discrimination for denying me due process.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a reviewer of all my complaints said that the sale of the house can not be rescinded. the same company locked me out of the house without an e');
