INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5730,'06/18/2015','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','I realized [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day after a payment was due that I had not paid my card. I went online to pay the balance and noticed that they had already put a late fee and interest on my account. I always pay the balance due. I called them to see if they would waive the fees and they said they would waive the late fee but not the interest. Although I was not really satisfied I realized I made a mistake and accepted that I had to pay the interest. I paid the balance the day after it was due. I then signed up for autopay to pay the future balances so I would not be late again. My following month was paid then when I received another bill there was interested on the bill again. I called for an explanation and they said that since it was late the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] time then the interest charge was automatically placed again. I explained that even if they wanted to claim that, the balance I paid was {$570.00} and the interest being charged for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day was {$10.00}. That would come to 54 % interest. She claimed there was a basic interest charge regardless. I also spoke to her Supervisor and she also refused to budge. I told them that if the {$10.00} was not waived I would cancel the card, which I intend to do after I pay the current balance. I still disagree with their practices and told them I was going to file a complaint.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'I paid the balance the day after it was due and paid the balance. they said they would waive the late fee but not the interest. they said they would waive the late fee and');
