Thank you,','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'Chase student loan customer care explained why the balance is not reduced with every payment. the payments are applied first towards the interest, then fees and other charges if any, and then the principal');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5820,'05/19/2015','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I recently filed for bankruptcy. I was current with my Navient STudent Loans, paid [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] off and was on auto pay. last month, Navient cut off my auto pay and disconnected me from using the webpage to log in and pay my bill. I noticed it was not paid, so was going to use the website and make sure I was still set up on auto pay. 
I called and a rep told me that she could not help me and I would get a notice in the mail due to my bankruptcy which was final [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I called back a few days later, worried they were trying to stop my payments and garnish my spouse wages. I was able to make them reset up my payments that were not late and Due [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Relieved, I was able to stop my anger and get on. 
Yesterday, I was called by a Navient collector and he said that the payment did not go thought because I was not late, Now I was late and had to pay late fees. Then I could go through the process of setting up on auto pay. 
I was cut of from my account, and make late with interest, all the while current on my student loans. They kept telling me that they could not find my account and my spouse was made primary on the loans even though were current. The bankruptcy did not disolve my loans, why was I harrassed, blocked from payments, and made to answer an recording about being in forbearance. I was forced to answer that I was in forberance in order to get back on auto pay. It is humiliating enough to have a college degree and no stable income. To be treated in this manor has caused me undue stress. 
I have other student loan providers, who did not do this to my when I was in bankruptcy. I need help getting back my interest that I had to pay. the collectors on the phone will not stop until I paid the late fees and was put in forberance. I also got a letter that I needed to update my email address, or some benefits would be stopped. I had unsubscribed to emails since I was on auto pay. I did not want monthly notices from them. They had my email address already. Nothing has changed. 
I never got a good job since going to college an never had the money to pay back loans, I work several jobs to make ends meet. Recently started my own business to get work.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,2.0,'a friend called me and said that the payment did not go thought because I was not late. he said that the payment did not go thought because I was not late. ');
