INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5822,'05/19/2015','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','I received a student loan from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. It was my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] year and I had run out of money to attend and exhausted all of my choices. I was told by the school that I would be able to roll this loan into my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Also, the rep from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] stated that that would be the best way to handle my loans. Well, I graduate, start on the paperwork and found out that I can not do this. What really caught me off guard is that this loan is basically treated like a credit card, with a variable rate. I am [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old, divorced with a child ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years old ), and XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] is my payoff date! I do not know what to do. I ''m trying to by a home, but need to take care of my family. The job I have does not even come close to paying my loans off. I do work for a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and have over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years in the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I qualified for loan forgiveness on my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], but not on my private loan. I did not even know I was receiving this type of loan. Any help or advice would be appreciated.','AES/PHEAA',2.0,2.0,'a student loan from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was received by [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. it was my [COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5823,'05/18/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Using a debit or ATM card','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]/2015, at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]., I attempted to use an ATM owned by Navy Federal Credit Union ( located at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], FL [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) to make a deposit to my account at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. ( This ATM accepts deposits for other institutions. ) I put in my ATM card, entered the PIN and selected cash deposit. I was then prompted to enter the cash ( {$130.00} ) and the ATM took the money. Suddenly, the machine " blinked out '''' like a power surge occurred. The screen read " error - unable to complete transaction or return deposit - contact Navy Federal Credit Union. The atm then released my ATM card and I made another transaction to determine if my deposit had been credited to my account and was shocked to learn that it had not. I then contacted Navy Federal Credit Union, and was pushed off from one person to another for 45 minutes and could not be helped. Finally, I was told to contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and was told that the ATM failure was Navy Federal Credit Union ''s fault and that I was to contact them for a refund. I attempted to contact Navy Federal Credit Union 3 more times and was told that they could not do anything and that I was to contact [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I contacted [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] again and as informed that nothing was documented on their records and Navy Federal had my money. I then called Navy Federal again and spoke to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at Navy Federal Credit Union in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She was rude and belligerent. She had me do a conference call with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and she was no help at all and there was no resolution. After 4 hours of this, I gave up and still do not have my money.','NAVY FEDERAL CREDIT UNION',2.0,2.0,'a ''''mist