INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5828,'05/16/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I am currently experiencing extreme difficulty with the credit bureaus. Experian, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are all reporting my [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Accounts as a revolving debt. The definition of revolving debt is- Revolving debt is debt that typically has a variable interest rate, an open-ended term and payments that are based on a percentage of the balance. Revolving debt has a pre-determined limit, agreed upon by the lender and borrower. 
Revolving debt is the kind of debt that credit cards offer and is usually an easy way to get credit. It can be a useful tool when used with discipline. This is damaging my score and affecting my lively hood. My revolving accounts such as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Credit Card, First Premiere, and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] are all in good standing. I have been paying about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]-[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] % of my balance charged every single month. My credit score should be much high than it is. The credit reporting agencies are in direct violation of The Fair Credit Reporting Act where it states, '''' Consumer reporting agencies must correct or delete inaccurate, incomplete, or unverifiable information. Inaccurate, incomplete or unverifiable information must be removed or corrected, usually within 30 days. However, a consumer reporting agency may continue to report information it has verified as accurate ''''. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should be reporting as UTILITY not revolving. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] acct number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should have a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] balance and account number [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] should have a balance of {$160.00} not {$380.00} reported. Due to the erroneous reporting since [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] 2014, my credit score has suffered tremendously. Revolving accounts reporting as past due or late can damage a consumer ''s credit report and in this case I have suffered severely.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,4.0,'revolving debt is debt that typically has a variable interest rate, an open-ended term and payments that are based on a percentage of the balance. revol');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5829,'05/15/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','I would like to know the reason why Experian declined my request to remove an item that was inaccurately placed on my credit report. An apartment management company sent my final move out statement to a collection agency and the collection agency reported the account as delinquent to all the CRA ''s before I was aware of any amount due. In essence the collection agency dinged my credit report before I received any notice of an amount due from the original creditor. Not to mention that the original creditor failed to properly apply all my credits and payments and thus reported inaccurate information to the collection agency. According to my accounting I had no money due to the apartment complex and I should be receiving a return of my deposit.I received, from the original creditor, a move out statement in the mail on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012, the envelope had a date stamp of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012. The Move Out Statement states that I have 15 days to respond or my account may be forwarded to a collection agency. I responded to the original creditor the day I received the move out statement. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012 the collection agency had already reported my account as delinquent to the CRA ''s, please note that the collection agency reported on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012 that they had properly notified me of a delinquent account and that they have, in good faith, verified the accuracy of a delinquent account. Yet the collection agency did not generate an " initial letter '''' of a reported delinquent account to me until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012, and according to the date stamp on the envelope they did n''t mail it until [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2012. It is blatantly clear that this whole scenario is a violation of my right to Fair Credit Reporting Practices. In my dispute to Experian I clearly stated that, if not in federal law, in California state law, where I reside, there are credit reporting accuracy laws that have been violated. This item should have never been reported to the CRA ''s. I can not fathom why such a clear violation of my rights has been shoved aside. I would like Experian to give my a legal explanation of why this item will continue on my credit report.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'experian declined to remove an item that was inaccurately placed on my credit report. the collection agency dinged my credit report before I received any notice of an amount due. the');
