INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5854,'05/07/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I attended court after being subpeoned for a break of a lease by my roommate while i lived there and was forced to move out. The owners of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], MI did not attend court. They did not attend court because they dropped all charges [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] There was no judgement possession made because the possession of the apartment was immediately returned to the owners. They also leased the same apartment within a week of moving out. We ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) and I immediately moved out of the apartment with in a week of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] breaking the lease. I have been informed that this should not be on my credit and that I do not have to pay any of the rent from the lease being broke back to the owners. I also know that the property has been sold a couple times so the original owners do not own the property anymore. I have been trying to resolve this with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who represents National Credit Systems. He has been rude and uncooperative, demanding and bullying that I owe this money and pay it immediately. He refuses to discuss that I have been to court for this and the case and charges were dropped and closed. I am trying to obtain housing for me and my son and unable to do so because this is on my credit and been unable to get this removed after a couple of attempts of disputing it. it just got renewed to be on my credit even longer.','National Credit Systems,Inc.',2.0,2.0,'the owners of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] did not attend court. they dropped all charges and dropped all charges');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5855,'05/07/2015','Consumer Loan','Vehicle loan','Managing the loan or lease','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I sold back my vehicle to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], it was purchased on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They gave me 46k for it but took off 1k due to minor rim damage, some scratches on rims. At the time of purchase in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] several warranties were also purchased including, rim/tire, theft, environment, etc. The dealer should have known about the rim/tire warranty as they sold it to me back in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], this would have covered damage. Instead, they took off 1k off the selling price of 46k. 
The warranties were never canceled by the dealer, I was referred back to them by the issuing companies for cancellation. Please note, this is not the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] negative experience with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was advised by my sales rep, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I was approved for 25k by the bank. When I went in two days later on Monday, their business manager called and told me I was not approved after I left my car there to trade in. They pulled this stunt in order to get my car in, which they were very interested in with low miles, so they could buy it. My sales rep had sent me home thinking I had a bank approval. 
I spoke with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in their corporate office yesterday, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she stated if a claim had been submitted with warranty that would have lowered the refund amount when canceled. The cost of warranty is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], there is no way they would take 1k off that for damage, maybe pro-rate it if anything. Either their math is off or they are just lying, more than likely lying so they do not have to pay me back 1k. 
Please advise them I will need a check for 1k to cover the difference from what I should have gotten, the rim/tire coverage should have covered the damage. Their address is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] # [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], NY [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. My address is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], CT [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ].','BMW Financial Services NA, LLC',2.0,2.0,'dealer gave me 46k for it but took off 1k due to minor rim damage. dealer should have known about the rim/tire warranty as they sold it back in [COM');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5856,'05/07/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Incorrect information on credit report','I had [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] as my provider. I wanted to change my plan, so I brought the account current and when I update my plan I was quoted {$180.00} a month. The [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bill I received they charged me over {$240.00}. I called and let them know that that is not what I was quoted. They said they would fix it. I received the next bill and I was overcharged again. I called and they stated that they would again fix the issue. I told them that I planned to terminate my service and that we needed to settle the dispute. I send them a history of my payments, I did so with no response. I then discontinued my account with them. They contacted me and told me it was a remaining balance. I sent in again my payment history and they said again, they would contact me with an update. It has now been reported on my credit report. I disputed the charges and they were removed. I checked back later and they are back on my credit report.','EQUIFAX, INC.',2.0,2.0,'the bill I received was over $240.00 a month. I called and let them know that that is not what I was quoted. they said they would fix the issue');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5857,'05/06/2015','Debt collection','Credit card','Communication tactics','I got home from work on XX/XX/2015 and my wife gave me a message that a debt collector named [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called my mother in laws house. She had told my mother in law that she needed to talk to me about repossessing something. I called the number immediately and left a message saying i was very upset about her phone call and to give me a call a.s.a.p. I got a call from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] the next day around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], she was instantly hostile towards me about the message I had left and called it " [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] '''' and then proceeded to harass me about my debt that I owe on a jewelry credit card. she told me i was a loser for not paying for my wife ''s jewelry and asked me sarcastically " how old are you ''''. She also told me that she was going to get a police escort, find me and take back my wife ''s jewelry, she said she already had my mother in laws contact information and was going to start there. she continued to belittle me and after trying to explain that I had lost my job and gone through some major family issues she told me she did not care and to start paying my bills before the cops come looking for me. After hanging up on me I called back to see what I could do to not have some weird people or the cops knocking on my Mother in laws door. she told me she had already submitted the claim for repossession but she might be able to work out something and she would call me back. when she called me back she gave me some options that I could not do and I said " i guess you have to do what you have to do ''''. After that I called my mother who has been in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] for almost [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] years and told her what had happened. She immediately told me she had broken all sorts of laws ( ex. not telling me that the call was being recorded, abusive language, talking to a third party about my case ) and that I should call the jeweler to make sure that it was not a scam because [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Summit Receivables was very unprofessional and if it was not a scam that I need to file complaint with the CFPB. I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from Summit Receivables and asked her for her name and other information about her company, she refused so I told her I was filing a complaint with the CFPB and she proceed to laugh at me and tell me to just shut up and pay my bills then she hung up on me again. I called the jeweler and the sent me to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] who was taking over the debt. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was very helpful and filed a complaint with his company and agreed that what had happened was very unprofessional and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had broken alot of the guidelines debt collectors have to follow. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] also told me that the whole " repossessing '''' thing was a lie and the companies name was Summit Receivables and not [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Repossessions like [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] had told me. My biggest thing in all this is I understand I have a debt that is unpaid but alot of uncontrollable circumstances went into me not being able to pay that debt. if you look at my past payment history it was flawless. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] was abusive and humiliated me to my mother in law with lies about taking jewelry away from my wife. people like this should not be allowed to have jobs like this if they have 0 people skills and 0 selfcontrol','GMA Investments, LLC',2.0,2.0,'a debt collector called her mother in laws house and called her. she told her she needed to talk to her about repossession. she called her mother and told her she had broken');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5858,'05/06/2015','Debt collection','I do not know','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','Dynamic Solutions has been calling my house # and once even called my cell. These people called my house using local phone numbers such as [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. The calls come in at any time and they even leave voice messages asking me to return the calls at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( of course I never did ).','Dynamic Recovery Solutions, LLC',2.0,2.0,'Dynamic Solutions has called my house # and once even called my cell. the calls come in at any time and they leave voice messages asking me to return the calls at [COMPTE');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5859,'05/06/2015','Prepaid card','Gift or merchant card','Fraud or scam','In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], my friend purchased a {$300.00} MasterCard gift card ( plus {$5.00} in " fees '''' ) at a local grocery store ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ). According to the packaging, it was issued by the US Bank National Association. She gave it to me later in the month or early [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. In [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I decided to use it. The instructions said to to register it online prior to making an online purchase. I attempted to do so at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] - the site listed on the packaging. The site told me they could n''t find the card so I called the customer service number - [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. According to customer service, the card was not activated at the point of purchase and I was directed back to the store. I went to the store ( WITH the receipt for the gift card ) where the baffled manager said he could n''t help me and HE called the customer service number and they advised him I should call back with instructions. I returned home, called the number, and the rep told me I would have to fax the receipt, along with a copy of the gift card ( front and back ) to the attention of " Gift Card Activation '''' at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. She said it would take 7-10 BUSINESS DAYS to activate the card. I did this on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. On the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] day, the card was STILL not activated. I called AGAIN and the rep told me they would " escalate '''' the matter -- but refused to find out if even the fax was received as that was a " different department. '''' When transferred to a supervisor - she told me the same thing. ( But how can you " escalate '''' something that is ALREADY late on your part?! ) She took my phone number ( which was already on the fax I had sent ) and said someone would call me back in 24-48 hours. After 48 hours passed without a call, I called them. The supervisor then explained that it was n''t 24-48 hours in day time -- it was 24-48 hours -- BUSINESS HOURS. ( Have you EVER heard THAT? ) Which, he told me, would be five more days before I would hear about ANYTHING. This is OUTRAGEOUS! I asked him for the name of the company he worked for and he said, " Card Services. '''' I asked for the physical address so I could put it on the complaint form to the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Attorney General. He refused to give it to me and could only tell me that the business was located in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. So, after being told the card would be activated in 7-10 business days, it was n''t. Now I am " lucky '''' enough to have this matter " escalated '''' so it MAY be five MORE days before a single person calls me and will probably tell me " they never received anything. ''''','U.S. BANCORP',2.0,2.0,'a friend bought a $300.00 card at a local grocery store. she gave it to me later in the month or early. the card was not activate');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5860,'05/06/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Closing/Cancelling account','I closed my Chase mileage card last year. At the time the service rep told me the annual member fee will be refunded, and I have no other balance on the card. I did not hear from Chase until earlier this year. I got a letter from Chase saying that my account was in significant delinquency, and was about to be charged off. 
After receiving the letter I called Chase, the service rep was able to see that the membership fee never got refunded, and meanwhile late payment fees was incurring. The service rep then told me that he would clear the account and also contact credit agencies. 
I check my credit score this morning ( a few months after the call ), the entry from Chase is still on my credit report. I call Chase and they told me they have to open another investigation for this matter. It seems like nothing gets done and meanwhile my credit score took a big hit. I am very disappointed in Chase.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',2.0,2.0,'service rep told me membership fee will be refunded. service rep told me that my account was in significant delinquency. service rep told me that the membership fee never');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5861,'05/05/2015','Credit card',NULL,'Other fee','I was in a debt repayment program with a set amount that I paid each month to the credit card company. The final payment was an over payment. When I saw that I had a two dollar credit, I wrote and asked that I receive a refund check for this amount. I sent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] letters, as I thought that the first did not reach them. About three weeks later I did receive a check. 
I went to my bank and cashed the {$2.00} check, so you can imagine my surprise when I received a copy of the check from my bank with a stop payment order. I was also accessed a {$12.00} fee for the stop payment on my account. 
I have attempted to contact American Express. I even went on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to try and get this resolved. I just keep having to try and explain it over and over .... 
If the money owed had been on my side, they would not have hesitated to demand that I pay up immediately. 
When I tried to call them, I was switched to a different extension, and after about [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] minutes the line went dead. I ''m tired of going through this and re explaining everything to American Express. I ''m tired of having to go back in the long line to get someone to talk to. 

I want a refund of the original credit along with reimbursement of the fee that my account was charged. I do n''t think a {$2.00} check will break the bank for AmEx, but I am aggravated that not only do I not get money owed me, but have been accesses an additional fee as well - for their mistake.','AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a credit card company has a set amount that I paid each month. the final payment was an over payment. the company has a refund check for the amount.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5862,'05/05/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Our homeowners insurance was not paid by Carrington from our escrow account, resulting in the cancellation of our policy. We were not made aware of the cancellation until we received a letter today from our insurance company.','CARRINGTON MORTGAGE SERVICES, LLC',2.0,2.0,'homeowners insurance was not paid by Carrington from our escrow account. the cancellation was not made aware until we received a letter from our insurance company today.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5863,'05/05/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','Fidelity Creditor Services out of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Ca., has erroneously charged a debt to me stemming from a rental agreement which a relative signed and I did not. I advised them of this. However, instead of taking me out of that claim, they filed with the [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Superior Court a complaint against me for nearly {$5000.00}. The debt shows on my credit score and it has negatively impacted my score and my financial reputation as I have in the last 12 months refinanced my home and am about to do so again. As a result of their tactics, my FICO score went from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This has made lenders unable to provide me with lower loan rates thus negatively financially impacting me.In addition, they have provided details about my debt to third parties without my authorization.','FIDELITY CAPITAL HOLDINGS, INC',2.0,2.0,'the debt shows on my credit score and negatively impacted my score. the debt has negatively impacted my score and my financial reputation.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5864,'05/04/2015','Debt collection','Medical','Communication tactics','I received a notice from Transworld Systems Inc. that threatens to report me to all national credit bureaus. It also gave me a phone number to call, which I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] times. Each time I called I was placed on hold for several minutes and then the phone would just hang up. This is a very rude and deplorable way to conduct their business.','TRANSWORLD SYSTEMS INC',2.0,2.0,'Transworld Systems threatened to report me to all national credit bureaus. it gave me a phone number to call, which I called [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5865,'05/04/2015','Credit reporting',NULL,'Credit reporting company''s investigation','Reporter to credit agency is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They inaccurately report rental property addresses on property that I own to be personal residences of mine. Makes me look like I have lived in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] different places, many times simultaneously. Have tried to dispute with Experian, and update failed to address the disputes. possible [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] issue is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] reporting utility billings as loans, where credit limit is {$0.00} and balances are listed as greater than loan limit. 
At this time, these uncorrected errors are costing me thousands of dollars per year in property insurance costs as insurance companies ( [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ) have begun incorporating credit score into premium rates.','Experian Information Solutions Inc.',2.0,2.0,'reporter to credit agency is [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. they incorrectly report rental property addresses on property. they are reporting utility billings as loans,');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5866,'05/04/2015','Credit card',NULL,'APR or interest rate','I have had my Chase card since XX/XX/1987 They raised my rate to 27.24 % prior to the advent of the Dodd Frank Act and the creation of your agency. I spoke to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in customer service and she indicated there was nothing Chase could do to lower my rate. She indicated that Chase was not lowering rates right now. I spoke to her about the need review and lower rates according to Regulation Z. She answered that Chase was only required to review not lower rates. My account is in good standing and been so for many years. I would like you to investigate and see why after 5 years of required rate re-evaluation there has been no reduction in my rate.','JPMORGAN CHASE & CO.',10.0,10.0,'my rate was raised to 27.24 % prior to the advent of the dodd Frank Act. she indicated that Chase was not lowering rates right now.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5867,'05/03/2015','Debt collection','I do not know','Cont''d attempts collect debt not owed','I recently pulled my credit report and discovered that this company has reported that I owe them several debts to my knowledge I received not prior notification that I owed them any debt. My rights under the FDCPA have been violated as I was not granted the right of validation','National Credit Systems,Inc.',2.0,2.0,'i recently pulled my credit report and discovered that this company has reported that I owe them several debts to my knowledge I received not prior notification that I owed them any debt ');
