INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5895,'04/23/2015','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Dealing with my lender or servicer','I went to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and I graduated with a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Degree I graduated in 2006. Getting an education at this school was the worst decision of my life. My debt is so bad and I struggled getting work when I [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] got out of school which just compounded my debt. I also found out that my degree is pretty much worthless and does n''t transfer to any other college, I digress. I ''ve been doing everything in my power to pay down this enormous debt. My current interest rate is at 8.75 % thru Navient/ [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] which they increased my interest last year. I pay over {$2000.00} a month and still owe around {$200000.00}. Do I have any options, anything at all, that can help me pay more towards my principle or bring down my monthly payment. I ''m not trying to skip out on paying what I borrowed but the amount that was added on top of what I borrowed is insane. I feel that I ''m a slave to this debt it will be for most of my life. My advise to others is do n''t ever follow your dreams if it involves going to a college like [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] because in my case it was the exact thing that prevented me from achieving it.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,4.0,'a student at a college in california graduated with a degree in 2006. he was a slave to this debt and he ''do');
