INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5937,'04/08/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','False statements or representation','This is just a general complaint. a utility company says I owe [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and sold the debt to a collection agency. The collection agency tacked on fees and put {$140.00} as a negative remark on my credit. 

I have never received any service from the collection agency, I never entered into any contract with them either, so why should I pay for services rendered to a creditor/utility company, when the utility company has agreed to a payment from the credit agency? 

I do n''t think the agency should be able to represent that I owe them the {$45.00}. A consumer should only be responsible for the debts that they make. Any fees a collection agency thinks they deserve should be dealt with between the collection agency and the original creditor. Passing these fees on to a consumer only digs deeper holes for consumers for services they never wanted nor received. 

I think legislation should be enacted that 1 ) a company can only report to a credit bureau to collect the original debt, and 2 ) a collection agency can not collect extra fees from the consumer.','Credit Service of Logan, Inc.',2.0,2.0,'utility company says I owe collection agency and sold debt to collection agency. collection agency put $140.00 as a negative remark on my credit. consumer');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5938,'04/08/2015','Mortgage','Home equity loan or line of credit','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','We had a HELOC with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bank which was to mature at the end of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] We applied for and received a modification for a fixed rate of 4.75 % for 300 months. Letter is attached. We ratified this modification with a payment on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and continued to pay the required amount, {$830.00} on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. See attached statements and [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment letter from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. Specialized Loan Service, LLC took over the servicing of the loan on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. See attached letter. We sent our [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] payment due on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. See attached check with date stamp of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] at SLS. They returned our check and never cashed it. I called and was told they had no information of our loan modification and could only accept the full balloon payment of {$140000.00}. See attached statement. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] I was advised that I should fax them the information of my modification and then I could make payment. I did so and authorized them to withdraw the payment directly from my account. See attached [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] notification of payment on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I set my payment for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to be sent from bill pay from my bank. It is now [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] and the payment has not cleared. On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], I received a check from SLS on their check stock for the amount of my payment which they withdrew On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. See attached. I have not cashed this check. I called them again of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], and they are again stating that they can only accept the full amount of the balloon payment and informed me that I am 36 days in arrears. I am making this complaint to document that I have attempted to comply with my loan agreement as established by the previous loan servicer. I am not getting any help from SLS at this point and am worried about what they may do to my credit. Other complaints about this company have a similar story.','Specialized Loan Servicing LLC',2.0,2.0,'we had a HELOC with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] bank which was to mature at the end of [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5939,'04/07/2015','Student loan','Non-federal student loan','Can''t repay my loan','Navient has tried to re-open a private student loan account that has been " charged off '''' AND " closed '''' on my credit report. I have not made a payment in 7 years exactly this month. They re notified the credit bureau trying to say this is an open account and it is not. It has passed its 7 year date of non payment. I believe they are just trying to still receive payment after transferring from [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. They were rude on the phone stating my account '''' never closed, it is open and you are currently accuring interes. '''' They wont work out a repayment plan I can afford stating i had to " Give {$1000.00} down then [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] {$100.00} payments and only then will they tell the credit bureau I am in good standing. '''' Or I could '''' pay {$290.00} for the next 8 months '''' before they put me in good standing. The would not accept less. Dont they have to work with me? However, this account is closed and charged off. Is it not illegal to put its status back into repayment and start charging me interes again after its been closed. Its been 7 years ... I found all of this out because I tried applying for a mortgage loan and they company told me what Navient reported to them. Can you please help. I have heard and read nothing good about Navient. This account originally went to collections because I got a divorce and lost my job and just had a baby I had to support. All my other federal student loans I have made good one. Please help me correct this. 
