to a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. He stated he was calling in regards to a check fraud situation regarding [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] ( my bank from 7 years ago ). After further conversation, he stated he represented Advance America and was going to file charges against me and take me to court on check fraud charges. I stated to [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] that I was aware of my rights and that I would be filing a complaint against him for threatening me in the attempts to collect this debt. Also, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] has a time barr of 6 years. I stopped payment on this debt XX/XX/[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. After our conversation, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] company contacted my sister in CA at around [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] Pacific CT and made an attempt to embarrass me in order to get me to cooperate. A message was left accusing me of fraud on my sister ''s cell phone. They then proceeded to call my husband ''s cell phone at work at [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to leave messages accusing me of check fraud and that they are beginning court action against me.','Advance America, Cash Advance Centers, Inc.',2.0,4.0,'agent [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] called me again and threatened to have me arrested. she called me again and threatened to have me arrested at work. she called');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5990,'03/20/2015','Bank account or service','Checking account','Account opening, closing, or management','On [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2014, I went into a Wells Fargo Branch in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] to open a new Business Checking Account ( I have been a customer of Wells Fargo for almost 30 years ). I had opened another business account with Wells earlier that year ( even though I never applied for a credit card with that account -- they sent me one -- claiming I had applied ). As a result of that previous issue, when I went into the branch on [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], 2014, I specifically advised the banker, that I did not want any credit cards, and only wanted a Business Checking account -- and nothing more. I spent close to an hour discussing the account with the Banker ( his name was [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- his family were attorneys in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ], with his grandfather having been a [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -the Federal Building bears his name ). [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] fully understood I did n''t want any credit cards. 
Two or three weeks after opening the account, I received a notice from Wells Fargo that my business had been approved for a {$15000.00} credit card. I immediately went into the Wells Branch and met with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] -- he advised me he had learned of the credit card and had reason to believe that an employee within his branch had forged my signature -- as he did not submit a credit card application. He further advised me that upon learning of the credit card he told the branch manager that I did not apply for a credit card nor did I sign any authorization for a credit card. [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] suggested that I should request all documents from the Bank regarding my business account -- which I did ; the documents I received -- contained [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] signatures -- only [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] of those signatures is mine. The other signature is a forgery. 
I have brought this to the attention of Wells Fargo ; they have told me they would investigate -- I sent a follow-up email to the person supposedly handling the matter at Wells Fargo -- yesterday she responded that she would ignore all of my emails and not provide me with any response -- it was as though this person was covering up for the person that forged my signature.','WELLS FARGO & COMPANY',2.0,2.0,'a customer of Wells Fargo has opened a new business checking account. he told the banker that I did not want any credit cards. he told the');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5991,'03/19/2015','Bank account or service','Cashing a check without an account','Deposits and withdrawals','I have a contract with a guy whom has an account at PNC Bank, I ''ve been cashing my check here for over a year with my drivers license and pre-paid bank card. They are no longer cashing my check that ''s on their back unless I have a major credit card? Or they said I can use a work Id I work for myself do n''t have one, or a passport, it cost {$100.00} ''s of dollars I do n''t have that kind of money and lastly they said a car registration I do n''t have a car. this is oppression to the poor, If I can ; t qualify for a major credit card how can I pay my bills? This should not be allowed because not everyone can qualify, if my drivers license and debit card is ok to drive and use my debit card everywhere major credit cards are accepted I do n''t see how this is not an acceptable form of ID for PNC','PNC Bank N.A.',2.0,2.0,'a guy who has an account at PNC Bank has an account. he says he can use a work Id I work for myself don''t have one');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5992,'03/19/2015','Debt collection','Other (i.e. phone, health club, etc.)','False statements or representation','I received a letter from Pioneer Credit Recovery claiming I owed NY State {$1500.00} in income tax. I called to tell them this was incorrect. They " transferred '''' me to a NY State tax official, but it was someone impersonating a government official. I stupidly gave them my SSN and maybe my DOB. I fear that they will use this information for future fraudulent action.','Navient Solutions, LLC.',2.0,4.0,'I called to tell them this was incorrect. they "transfer '''' me to a government official, but it was someone impersonating a government official.');
INSERT INTO "reclamations" VALUES(5993,'03/19/2015','Mortgage','Conventional fixed mortgage','Loan servicing, payments, escrow account','Ocwen loan servicing is the servicer of my loan. 
1. They refuse to talk to about anything. 
2. They refuse to send me any papers. 
3. They will not send me my statements4. They will not send payment statement. 
5. They will not return any letters or phone calls. 
6. They refuse to let me know what owed on loan. 
7. They refuse to let me know if they received my payments. 
8. They refuse to let me know what my payments are. 
9. They but forced insurance on this property when I have insurance on the property. They refused to take it off after 3 months of sending them proof and calling them over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] times. 
10. They double charged me for insurance. 
11. The only thing that they will say when I call, is that they were told not to talk or send anything to me due to I filed litigation against them. 
[COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. I have over [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] documented calls to Ocwen and copy ''s of letters sent to prove this. 
I believe they are doing this because I filing a lawsuit and complaints against them in an unrelated mortgage that they are servicing for [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. ( Case, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] in [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ] County ). This has noting to do with this loan which is owned by you, [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. There is no reason for there conduct in the servicing of this loan. I have no complaints or lawsuits against you. I have not missed any mortgage payments. Its not in foreclosure. I want to make payments on time and have been making payments for the last 4 months not knowing what my payments are, and if they were even credited ect. 
I believe they are going to to try to foreclose on this loan even though I have proof of all of this, just like they illegally did on the loan with [COMPTE_ANONYMISÉ]. This is the loan I filed the lawsuit on. This letter will be sent along with complaints to other agency ''s including the press. 
The nation is in a foreclosure crisis and the courts are full of foreclosure cases. There is no excuse for this conduct by Ocwens loan servicing. They may cause this loan to go in foreclosure for no reason what so ever.','OCWEN LOAN SERVICING LLC',2.0,2.0,'a lawsuit filed against the servicer of a mortgage that is owned by you. the nation is in a foreclosure crisis and the courts are full of foreclosure cases.');
